ns', 'value': 'ARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-01T00:10:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Energy & Environment ', 'byline': {'original': 'By Henry Fountain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Henry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fountain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6a08450-71b4-5ce4-9e1f-5e13c8203123', 'word_count': 546, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6a08450-71b4-5ce4-9e1f-5e13c8203123'}, {'abstract': 'Readers say a good credit score may or may not tell you something about a potential partner.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/01/opinion/new-old-dating-tip-if-youve-got-it-flaunt-it.html', 'snippet': 'Readers say a good credit score may or may not tell you something about a potential partner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/01/opinion/0101LETTERS/0101LETTERS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 610, 'width': 555, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/01/opinion/0101LETTERS/0101LETTERS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 610, 'width': 555, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Old Dating Tip: If You’ve Got It, Flaunt It', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Old Dating Tip: If You&#8217;ve Got It, Flaunt It', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Scores', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Ratings and Credit Rating Agencies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dating and Courtship', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-01T00:12:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/a65de2ca-d333-542a-aab8-7880cca267be', 'word_count': 371, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a65de2ca-d333-542a-aab8-7880cca267be'}, {'abstract': 'New Year’s Day is the only holiday devoted to acknowledging, if not precisely celebrating, time itself. And there is nothing stranger than time.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/01/opinion/crossing-into-2013.html', 'snippet': 'New Year’s Day is the only holiday devoted to acknowledging, if not precisely celebrating, time itself. And there is nothing stranger than time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here we are again, getting squared away in the New Year. Some of us take comfort in its resemblance to the Old Year, and some of us wish it were newer than it’s likely to be — a more radical departure, an unfamiliar train boarding at an unfamiliar station and headed who knows where. Make of this holiday what you will, but it is the only one in the calendar devoted to acknowledging, if not precisely celebrating, time itself. And there is nothing stranger than time. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Crossing Into 2013', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Crossing Into 2013', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New Year', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Time', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-01T00:13:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/610dfa35-fdf2-5ea6-a1dc-df3941da2cc4', 'word_count': 285, 'uri': 'nyt://article/610dfa35-fdf2-5ea6-a1dc-df3941da2cc4'}, {'abstract': 'A useful federal program intends to help graduates who walked right into a recession and faced lower earnings and higher unemployment rates.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/01/opinion/relief-for-student-borrowers-in-pay-as-you-earn.html', 'snippet': 'A useful federal program intends to help graduates who walked right into a recession and faced lower earnings and higher unemployment rates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'College graduates who began their careers during the Great Recession faced several long-term economic obstacles. These included lower earnings, higher unemployment rates and greater career instability — all of which made it more difficult to buy homes and save for retirement. It also made it harder to pay off student loans. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Relief for Student Borrowers', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Relief for Student Borrowers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Student Loans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-01T00:17:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/23ad8af2-3623-5971-9604-e763dcefba33', 'word_count': 409, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23ad8af2-3623-5971-9604-e763dcefba33'}, {'abstract': 'Wreaths become a blank canvas for artists in the city parks department’s 30th annual exhibition.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/12/31/the-many-ways-a-wreath-can-turn/', 'snippet': 'Wreaths become a blank canvas for artists in the city parks department’s 30th annual exhibition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wreaths have existed for thousands of years, imbued with meaning by different societies and religions. In ancient times, they were symbols of success and importance. Pagan cultures created wreaths as reminders of spring’s approach, with the circular shape evoking the turning of the seasons. And in modern times, of course, the wreath is a Christian symbol of eternal rebirth.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Many Ways a Wreath Can Turn', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Reimagining Christmas Wreaths, Artists Ignore the Evergreen Bough', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Waste Materials and Disposal', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kuhn, Jonathan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Parks and Recreation Department (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fifth Avenue (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-01T00:18:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa W. Foderaro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Foderaro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/63c2528b-3168-55e7-9299-823fb836a310', 'word_count': 555, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63c2528b-3168-55e7-9