1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f40014c7-4c23-58ae-8bf1-9beb7e4aa649', 'word_count': 906, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f40014c7-4c23-58ae-8bf1-9beb7e4aa649'}, {'abstract': 'Since Coach Gregg Popovich gave his three stars a game off, resulting in a $250,000 fine, they have led the San Antonio Spurs to 12 wins in 16 games.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/01/sports/basketball/controversial-rest-day-has-not-hurt-spurs.html', 'snippet': 'Since Coach Gregg Popovich gave his three stars a game off, resulting in a $250,000 fine, they have led the San Antonio Spurs to 12 wins in 16 games.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN ANTONIO — On the first play of the second half of the Spurs’ blowout victory over the Nets on Monday night, Coach Gregg Popovich ran a play that had Deron Williams chasing Tony Parker around a Tim Duncan screen, only for Parker to turn and reroute Williams around Duncan again. Duncan scored on a short bank shot off a feed from Parker, who had exploited the Nets’ defense throughout the first half.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/01/sports/subSPURS/subSPURS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 819, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/01/sports/subSPURS/subSPURS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1638, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Vindication for Popovich: Spurs Are Playing With Vigor', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Vindication for Popovich: Spurs Are Playing With Vigor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Appleman, Jake', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basket