': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/02/dining/02STUFF_BROWNIESPAN/02STUFF_BROWNIESPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 434}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/dining/02STUFF_BROWNIESPAN/02STUFF_BROWNIESPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/dining/02STUFF_BROWNIESPAN/02STUFF_BROWNIESPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1499, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/dining/02STUFF_BROWNIESPAN/02STUFF_BROWNIESPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/02/dining/02STUFF_BROWNIESPAN/02STUFF_BROWNIESPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/dining/02STUFF_BROWNIESPAN/02STUFF_BROWNIESPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Brownie Bites, Served Crisp', 'kicker': 'Food Stuff', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Brownies for Those Who Can’t Commit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chocolate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bakeries and Baked Products', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-01T01:09:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0555f19-eebd-54e0-b4b3-7c4ae967dfb1', 'word_count': 250, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0555f19-eebd-54e0-b4b3-7c4ae967dfb1'}, {'abstract': 'Cheryl Perry, who sells in the New Amsterdam Market, has opened a pie shop in Brooklyn.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/02/dining/from-market-stand-to-new-shop.html', 'snippet': 'Cheryl Perry, who sells in the New Amsterdam Market, has opened a pie shop in Brooklyn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s starting to become a familiar pattern: an artisanal food-maker goes from market stand to opening his or her own store. So it’s no surprise that Cheryl Perry a pie baker who sells in the New Amsterdam Market in the South Street Seaport, has opened a shop, Pie Corps, in Greenpoint, Brooklyn. Ms. Perry, a professional chef, had also been selling wholesale, but said she wanted more personal contact with retail customers. “I needed a more permanent physical space for that,” she said. With her partner, Felipa Lopez, she is producing flaky pies and turnovers, filling them with ingredients that are locally sourced and organic whenever possible. There are savories, like chicken potpies, all thick with chunky ingredients, and rectangular turnovers, which she calls hand pies, in flavors like Moroccan beef, and red wine mushrooms. These deserve to be warmed. Irresistible pies like coconut custard, s’mores (with a marshmallow glaze and graham-cracker crust), and rich pecan spiked with rye whiskey are on the sweet side of the menu.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/dining/02STUFF_PIESSPAN/02STUFF1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 375, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/