dren, but will not be subject to any penalties if family coverage is unaffordable to workers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/01/health/employers-must-offer-family-health-care-affordable-or-not-administration-says.html', 'snippet': 'The Obama administration said Monday that employers must offer health insurance to employees and their children, but will not be subject to any penalties if family coverage is unaffordable to workers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — In a long-awaited interpretation of the new health care law, the Obama administration said Monday that employers must offer health insurance to employees and their children, but will not be subject to any penalties if family coverage is unaffordable to workers.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Employers Must Offer Family Care, Affordable or Not', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Employers Must Offer Family Care, Affordable or Not', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pear, Robert', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Internal Revenue Service', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-01T01:28:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Pear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pear', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0382ca33-9009-5ded-8d23-1cecf04aa264', 'word_count': 791, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0382ca33-9009-5ded-8d23-1cecf04aa264'}, {'abstract': 'Marginally talented and usual