stricts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Glint-eyed and with a practiced amiability, the House Appropriations Committee chairman, Harold Rogers, would have us know that his heart is heavy at our suffering, even as he applies a little Kentucky common sense to New York and New Jersey. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Discussing Disaster Relief Costs, and Changing Tone When It’s Closer to Home', 'kicker': 'Gotham', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Discussing Disaster Relief Costs, and Changing Tone When It’s Closer to Home', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Powell, Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Aid (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Staten Island (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Legal Services Corp', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rogers, Harold Dallas', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coats, Dan', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-01T01:49:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Powell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Powell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7f50efc-d3d1-55e4-bf8e-4a89e991e281', 'word_count': 827, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7f50efc-d3d1-55e4-bf8e-4a89e991e281'}, {'abstract': 'The national birthrate is now about half what it was during the late 1950s, as Hispanic women, who have generally had the highest fertility rates in the country, are choosing to have fewer children.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/01/health/us-birthrate-dips-especially-for-hispanics.html', 'snippet': 'The national birthrate is now about half what it was during the late 1950s, as Hispanic women, who have generally had the highest fertility rates in the country, are choosing to have fewer children.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ORLANDO, Fla. — Hispanic women in the United States, who have generally had the highest fertility rates in the country, are choosing to have fewer children. Both immigrant and native-born Latinas had steeper birthrate declines from 2007 to 2010 than other groups, including non-Hispanic whites, blacks and Asians, a drop some demographers and sociologists attribute to changes in the views of many Hispanic women about motherhood.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/01/us/BIRTHRATE/BIRTHRATE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/01/us/BIRTHRATE/BIRTHRATE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/01/us/BIRTHRATE/BIRTHRATE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/01/us/BIRTHRATE/BIRTHRATE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hispanic Pregnancies Fall in U.S. as Women Choose Smaller Families', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Birthrate Dips as Hispanic Pregnancies Fall', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saulny, Susan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Rates', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Childbirth', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-01T01:49:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Saulny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saulny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/231767a5-e290-5085-a094-b59bcc640689', 'word_count': 1188, 'uri': 'nyt://article/231767a5-e290-5085-a094-b59bcc640689'}, {'abstract': 'In a service that adapted elements of a traditional Hindu rite, friends said goodbye to Sunando Sen, who was pushed onto elevated tracks in Queens.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/01/nyregion/victim-of-fatal-subway-push-is-given-a-fond-farewell.html', 'snippet': 'In a service that adapted elements of a traditional Hindu rite, friends said goodbye to Sunando Sen, who was pushed onto elevated tracks in Queens.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sunando Sen had no close relatives still living, nor had he started a family in his adopted home of New York. So it was the close circle of friends whom he had come to call his family in the United States that gathered to pray for his soul and cremate his body on Monday, four days after he was pushed onto subway tracks in Queens and crushed by a train.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': N