sing ethnic, political and sectarian troubles that showed little sign of easing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BAGHDAD — At least three dozen people were killed in a string of attacks on Monday in Iraq, the police said, signaling a bloody end to a year of rising ethnic, political and sectarian troubles that showed little sign of easing.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Violence in Iraq Swells at Year’s End, Leaving at Least 3 Dozen Dead', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Violence in Iraq Swells at Year’s End, Leaving at Least 3 Dozen Dead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ghazi, Yasir', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Attacks on Police', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civilian Casualties', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Talabani, Jalal', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shiite Muslims', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sunni Muslims', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-01T04:26:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Yasir Ghazi and Christine Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Yasir', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ghazi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5630abb5-565c-5066-afdb-2a29df326e9d', 'word_count': 626, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5630abb5-565c-5066-afdb-2a29df326e9d'}, {'abstract': 'How the former slaves along the South Carolina coast celebrated Emancipation Day, 1863.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/12/31/the-grove-of-gladness/', 'snippet': 'How the former slaves along the South Carolina coast celebrated Emancipation Day, 1863.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As dawn broke across a cloudless New Year’s Day sky over the South Carolina Sea Islands, Charlotte Forten, a black Pennsylvania missionary who had come south to teach local freed people, set out for Camp Saxton, a waterside settlement on Port Royal Island, near the town of Beaufort. After a short ride on an old carriage that was pulled by “a remarkably slow horse,” Forten boarded a ship for the trip up the Beaufort River. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Grove of Gladness', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emancipation Proclamation (1863)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New Year', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Slavery', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Higginson, Thomas Wentworth', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Carolina', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-01T04:31:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Blain Roberts and Ethan J. Kytle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Blain', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roberts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstnam