': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8af644a-40ed-5822-8f3a-cf26be213e04', 'word_count': 43, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8af644a-40ed-5822-8f3a-cf26be213e04'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on January 1, 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/01/pageoneplus/corrections-january-1-2013.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on January 1, 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRONT PAGE', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: January 1, 2013', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-01T05:39:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/182e510d-a884-575e-8762-24bd5dc220c5', 'word_count': 544, 'uri': 'nyt://article/182e510d-a884-575e-8762-24bd5dc220c5'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/01/arts/television/whats-on-tuesday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '4 P.M. (TMC) SERENITY (2005) A small crew aboard a spaceship, led by Capt. Malcolm Reynolds (Nathan Fillion, left), tries to scrape together a living smuggling cargo from one fringe of the universe to the next in this film written and directed by Joss Whedon. But the crew members’ off-the-radar existence is threatened when an agent (Chiwetel Ejiofor) of an oppressive government tracks them down. Writing in The New York Times, Manohla Dargis compared this science-fiction adventure with the “Star Wars” movies by George Lucas. “Scene for scene, ‘Serenity’ is more engaging and certainly better written and acted than any of Mr. Lucas’s recent screen entertainments,” she wrote. “Mr. Whedon isn’t aiming to conquer the pop-culture universe with a branded mythology; he just wants us to hitch a ride to a galaxy far, far away and have a good time.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Tuesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-01T06:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/10206455-dcb6-5373-a13d-f7b5a0d38440', 'word_count': 744, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10206455-dcb6-5373-a13d-f7b5a0d38440'}, {'abstract': 'Kim Jong-un, who called for an end to the “confrontation” with South Korea, also laid out broad policy guidelines for the new year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/02/world/asia/north-koreas-leader-kim-jong-un-makes-overture-to-south.html', 'snippet': 'Kim Jong-un, who called for an end to the “confrontation” with South Korea, also laid out broad policy guidelines for the new year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — The North Korean leader, Kim Jong-un, called for an end to the “confrontation” with rival South Korea on Tuesday in what appeared to be an overture to the incoming South Korean president as she was cobbling together South Korea’s new policy on the North.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/global-home/2korea-image/2korea-image-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 700, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank'