'word_count': 996, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7bbd6361-939f-59d9-b2c2-851716ec7394'}, {'abstract': 'Fears are growing that the Chinese mainland is slowly engulfing democratic Taiwan through ever-deepening economic integration and purchases of the island republic’s free media by Taiwanese businessmen with large financial stakes in China.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/01/as-taiwans-links-with-mainland-grow-so-do-concerns/', 'snippet': 'Fears are growing that the Chinese mainland is slowly engulfing democratic Taiwan through ever-deepening economic integration and purchases of the island republic’s free media by Taiwanese businessmen with large financial stakes in China.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAIPEI — The 188-second flurry of fireworks that shot out at midnight from Taipei 101, the world’s second-tallest building, drew a crowd of 800,000 and announced the start of 2013 on the island republic.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/01/global-home/01taiwan_rdv/01taiwan_rdv-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 842, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/01/global-home/01taiwan_rdv/01taiwan_rdv-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1684, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/01/global-home/01taiwan_rdv/01taiwan_rdv-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/01/global-home/01taiwan_rdv/01taiwan_rdv-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/01/global-home/01taiwan_rdv/01taiwan_rdv-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'As Taiwan’s Links With Mainland Grow, So Do Concerns', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antitrust Laws and Competition Issues', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chiang Kai-shek', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lai, Jimmy', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'APPLE DAILY', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Next Media Ltd', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Radio Free Asia', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Post', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beijing (China)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Taipei (Taiwan)', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Taiwan', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tiananmen Square (Beijing)', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-01T06:37:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Didi Kirsten Tatlow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Didi', 'middlename': 'Kirsten', 'lastname': 'Tatlow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/20649f9e-7e0f-522e-8a93-4e1a6e4b7142', 'word_count': 809, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20649f9e-7e0f-522e-8a93-4e1a6e4b7142'}, {'abstract': 'The results of a closely watched survey underline the view that the world’s second-largest economy has settled into a mild rebound that is likely to extend into 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/02/business/global/chinese-manufacturing-sector-expanded-in-december.html', 'snippet': 'The results of a closely watched survey underline the view that the world’s second-largest economy has settled into a mild rebound that is likely to extend into 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An important gauge of China’s giant manufacturing sector published Tuesday showed a third successive month of expansion in December and underlined the view that the world’s second-largest economy has settled into a mild rebound that is likely to extend into 2013.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chinese Manufacturing Sector Expands for a 3rd Month', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-01T07:04:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bettina Wassener', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bettina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wassener', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ff26cd0-c90b-5a6d-b504-b96a3f116f0b', 'word_count': 431, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ff26cd0-c90b-5a6d-b504-b96a3f116f0b'}, {'abstract': 'Taraf, a rare brave and independent voice in the Turkish media, is in trouble.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/01/the-travails-of-the-turkish-newspaper-taraf/', 'snippet': 'Taraf, a rare brave and independent voice in the Turkish media, is in trouble.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISTANBUL — That the editor-in-chief of Taraf — a cash-strapped Turkish newspaper that struggles to sell more than 50,000 copies — should resign after falling out with its proprietor might seem like a humdrum story worthy only of an inside page. But in the gloomy landscape that is Turkish journalism, where self-censorship and kowtowing to the government are the norm, recent news that several of the paper’s leading lights were throwing in their pens made headlines: Taraf has been a rare brave and independent voice. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Requiem for a Newspaper', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of the Press', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Erdogan, Recep Tayyip', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-01T07:23:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Finkel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Finkel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a964122-9b26-5f6c-ba16-de3b6a5da400', 'word_count': 733, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a964122-9b26-5f6c-ba16-de3b6a5da400'}, {'abstract': 'The Senate easily passed the measure, which also put off cuts in spending, early on Tuesday after the deadline on the so-called fiscal cliff had passed. Republican House aides said a vote Tuesday was possible.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/02/us/politics/senate-tax-deal-fiscal-cliff.html', 'snippet': 'The Senate easily passed the measure, which also put off cuts in spending, early on Tuesday after the deadline on the so-called fiscal cliff had passed. Republican House aides said a vote Tuesday was possible.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Senate, in a predawn vote two hours after the deadline passed to avert automatic tax increases, overwhelmingly approved legislation on Tuesday that would allow tax rates to rise only on affluent Americans while temporarily suspending sweeping, across-the-board spending cuts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/01/us/01fiscal3_cnd/01fiscal3_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 374, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/01/us/01fiscal3_cnd/01fiscal3_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 374}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/01/us/01fiscal3_cnd/01fiscal3_cnd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 639, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/01/us/01fiscal3_cnd/01fiscal3_cnd-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1277, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/01/us/01fiscal3_cnd/01fiscal3_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 's