e': 'Tannenbaum, Mike', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-01T10:00:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Kurylo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kurylo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1480697-8fd5-5f89-894f-5cdaad43a089', 'word_count': 498, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1480697-8fd5-5f89-894f-5cdaad43a089'}, {'abstract': 'It’s difficult for members of Congress to agree to take a political hit for raising taxes and cutting into popular programs when the benefits will be realized only by their successors, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/01/when-the-deficit-will-be-fixed/', 'snippet': 'It’s difficult for members of Congress to agree to take a political hit for raising taxes and cutting into popular programs when the benefits will be realized only by their successors, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bruce Bartlett held senior policy roles in the Reagan and George H.W. Bush administrations and served on the staffs of Representatives Jack Kemp and Ron Paul. He is the author of “The Benefit and the Burden: Tax Reform – Why We Need It and What It Will Take.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When the Deficit Will Be Fixed', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Bonds', 'rank': 4