f Leung Chun-ying, the city’s chief executive, have accused him of misleading the public on a controversial real estate issue, but he has appeared to retain the support of Beijing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — Thousands of demonstrators in rival marches crowded through Hong Kong’s main shopping district on Tuesday to praise or condemn the city’s chief executive, who appears to retain the confidence of leaders in Beijing despite facing criticism here over a series of actions.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Hong Kong, Rival Protests Are Divided Over Leader', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Political Rift\r\nUnderlined\r\nBy Protests\r\nIn Hong Kong', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bradsher, Keith', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hong Kong', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leung Chun-ying', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-01T13:05:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Keith Bradsher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Keith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bradsher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b26b0383-49ae-573b-99af-8ff4f2db7f41', 'word_count': 884, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b26b0383-49ae-573b-99af-8ff4f2db7f41'}, {'abstract': 'The Shell Oil rig, which is carrying about 139,000 gallons of diesel fuel, broke free from tow ships in rough seas in the Gulf of Alaska, officials said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/02/business/energy-environment/shell-oil-rig-runs-aground-in-alaska.html', 'snippet': 'The Shell Oil rig, which is carrying about 139,000 gallons of diesel fuel, broke free from tow ships in rough seas in the Gulf of Alaska, officials said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An enormous Shell Oil offshore drilling rig ran aground on an island in the Gulf of Alaska on Monday night after it broke free from tow ships in rough seas, officials said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/01/us/RIG/RIG-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 410, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/01/us/RIG/RIG-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 410}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/01/us/RIG/RIG-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 699, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/01/us/RIG/RIG-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1399, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/01/us/RIG/RIG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/01/us/RIG/RIG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/01/us/RIG/RIG-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Breakaway Oil Rig, Filled With Fuel, Runs Aground', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Shell Oil Rig Runs Aground in Alaska', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Offshore Drilling and Exploration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal Dutch Shell Plc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALASKA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-01T13:26:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Energy & Environment ', 'byline': {'original': 'By Henry Fountain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Henry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fountain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b7e6c8e-8954-5424-b739-01460b41e672', 'word_count': 673, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b7e6c8e-8954-5424-b739-01460b41e672'}, {'abstract': 'What the fiscal cliff bargain means for the long-term liberal project.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/01/liberalisms-400000-problem/', 'snippet': 'What the fiscal cliff bargain means for the long-term liberal project.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If the tax debate could be simplified to a liberal desire to make sure the tax burden is borne by those who can most easily afford it and a conservative desire to keep taxes as low as possible on as many people as possible, the fiscal-cliff bargain that was struck between Mitch McConnell and Joe Biden over the last 48 hours — a bargain that could still fail to pass the House, but probably won’t — seems to offer something credible to both sides. One the one hand, it includes a real Democratic concession, which substitutes a top income rate threshold of $400,000 for the $250,000 threshold that President Obama had long insisted on. But at the same time, for liberals seeking progressivity and fairness, that should be the easiest possible concession to make. The $400,000 threshold still puts the top bracket close to where it was under Bill Clinton when you adjust for inflation, and that Clintonian definition of “rich” wasn’t an implausible one: While the whining of the upper upper middle class (or, if you prefer, the not-that-rich rich) can be unseemly, there really is a big difference between a taxpayer making six figures annually and a taxpayer making seven or eight, and setting the top rate in the mid rather than low six figures is a way of acknowledging that the near-rich and super-rich do not occupy the same financial universe.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Liberalism’s $400,000 Problem', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-01T13:32:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea8002d5-290d-5d5a-8cad-e91c2f3f380d', 'word_count': 1093, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea8002d5-290d-5d5a-8cad-e91c2f3f380d'}, {'abstract': 'The economy, elections, and how to deal with a new Islamist threat: as politicians make their New Year resolutions, these are a few items on Europe’s agenda for 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/01/what-to-watch-for-in-europe-in-2013/', 'snippet': 'The economy, elections, and how to deal with a new Islamist threat: as politicians make their New Year resolutions, these are a few items on Europe’s agenda for 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — New Year’s predictions, like New Year’s resolutions, are probably best avoided.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/01/b