d Notre Dame have proven one thing: at the highest level, the battle in the trenches still matters. The Crimson Tide and the Irish each reached the B.C.S. title game with dominant line play, and in the buildup to Monday’s game, many analysts have focused on the clash between Alabama’s huge offensive line and Notre Dame’s dominating defensive line. But the flip side of that matchup will go just as far in determining which team hoists the crystal football.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The View From Notre Dame: Offensive Line Is Key', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'BCS National Championship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Golson, Everett', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Alabama', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Notre Dame', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-01T15:00:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Joseph', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Joseph', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/736a989d-84a5-5cbe-9475-55c3943e9ab2', 'word_count': 541, 'uri': 'nyt://article/736a989d-84a5-5cbe-9475-55c3943e9ab2'}, {'abstract': 'Meat plays an outsize role in the demented behavior in Mo Yan’s novel “Pow!”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/02/books/pow-by-mo-yan.html', 'snippet': 'Meat plays an outsize role in the demented behavior in Mo Yan’s novel “Pow!”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mo Yan, the controversial Chinese winner of the 2012 Nobel Prize in Literature, is a demented poet of the appetites. His novels have a lurid, greasy sheen.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/books/02book/02book-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 739, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/books/02book/02book-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1479, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/books/02book/02book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/02/books/02book/02book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/books/02book/02book-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Meaty Tale, Carnivorous and Twisted', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Meaty Tale, Carnivorous and Twisted', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garner, Dwight', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mo Yan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-01T15:19:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dwight Garner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dwight', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a5549a9-674a-5bc1-bb03-fa91c8ff8d98', 'word_count': 970, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a5549a9-674a-5bc1-bb03-fa91c8ff8d98'}, {'abstract': 'Officials say the emphasis will now be on salvage.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/01/shells-drilling-rig-runs-aground/', 'snippet': 'Officials say the emphasis will now be on salvage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a big setback for Shell Oil, Coast Guard officials say that the Kulluk, a big offshore drilling rig, has run aground on an island in the Gulf of Alaska, Henry Fountain reports. A Coast Guard helicopter that flew over the rig Monday night spotted no detectable oil sheen from the rig, which is carrying about 139,000 gallons of diesel fuel and 12,000 gallons of lubricating oil and hydraulic fluid, officials said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shell’s Drilling Rig Runs Aground', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-01T15:52:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b42d286-d382-5eee-818b-bd3389476a2b', 'word_count': 72, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b42d286-d382-5eee-818b-bd3389476a2b'}, {'abstract': 'Continuing a militant campaign of violence against aid workers in Pakistan, gunmen on Tuesday killed seven Pakistani teachers and health workers, six of them women.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/02/world/asia/pakistani-militants-gun-down-7-aid-workers.html', 'snippet': 'Continuing a militant campaign of violence against aid workers in Pakistan, gunmen on Tuesday killed seven Pakistani teachers and health workers, six of them women.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISLAMABAD, Paki