Feared for 2013: Iceland. And not by some crackpot reality show; by PBS.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/arts/02VOLCANO/02VOLCANO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/02/arts/02VOLCANO/02VOLCANO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/arts/02VOLCANO/02VOLCANO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 628, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/arts/02VOLCANO/02VOLCANO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 1223, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/arts/02VOLCANO/02VOLCANO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/02/arts/02VOLCANO/02VOLCANO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/arts/02VOLCANO/02VOLCANO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Put Iceland, Cold but Seething Hot, on Your 2013 Anxiety Barometer', 'kicker': 'Television Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Put Iceland, Cold but Seething Hot, on Your 2013 Anxiety Barometer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iceland', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Volcanoes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Nova (TV Program)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-01T22:11:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/14dbcd9b-04d3-5259-93e2-532117194289', 'word_count': 549, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14dbcd9b-04d3-5259-93e2-532117194289'}, {'abstract': 'Probably no mayor of New York City except Edward I. Koch came close to writing as many letters to constituents as William J. Gaynor, who served from 1910 to 1913 and dictated missives filled with philosophical touches.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/01/the-mayor-of-sarcastic-witty-and-candid-letters/', 'snippet': 'Probably no mayor of New York City except Edward I. Koch came close to writing as many letters to constituents as William J. Gaynor, who served from 1910 to 1913 and dictated missives filled with philosophical touches.', 'lead_paragraph': 'John V. Lindsay often delivered homespun advice to ordinary constituents, and Edward I. Koch claims to have answered every letter or e-mail he has received. But a century ago, few elected officials were more prolific or perspicacious in their correspondence than William J. Gaynor, who became New York City’s mayor 103 years ago on Tuesday, and served until 1913.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/29/nyregion/28cityroom-gaynor/28cityroom-gaynor-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 39