ation': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c28ce121-7445-5f10-bb78-af86fc8c4737', 'word_count': 715, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c28ce121-7445-5f10-bb78-af86fc8c4737'}, {'abstract': 'The presence of M.I.T. and Harvard, along with several hospitals, is attracting drug developers happy to draw on a large pool of scientists.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/02/realestate/commercial/biotech-players-lead-a-boom-in-cambridge.html', 'snippet': 'The presence of M.I.T. and Harvard, along with several hospitals, is attracting drug developers happy to draw on a large pool of scientists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAMBRIDGE, Mass. — Anyone who knows the history of this town would be surprised to find a fashionable coffee shop on Third Street, with dozens of people walking by. The lattes and chai teas are being sold on a Kendall Square site that had been empty for most of the last 40 years — since factories with names like American Rubber and the Badger Company were razed for a NASA facility that was never built. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/business/CAMBRIDGE/CAMBRIDGE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 637, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/business/CAMBRIDGE/CAMBRIDGE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1274, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Biotech Players Lead a Boom in Cambridge', 'kicker': 'Square Feet', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Biotech Players Lead a Boom in Cambridge', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cambridge (Mass)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate (Commercial)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Harvard University', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Massachusetts Institute of Technology', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-01T22:21:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'subsection_name': 'Commercial Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Weintraub', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weintraub', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/853560aa-181c-57d8-aeef-feddd428c09e', 'word_count': 977, 'uri': 'nyt://article/853560aa-181c-57d8-aeef-feddd428c09e'}, {'abstract': 'Artek went to unusual lengths on Saturday to present “Mozartean Masterpieces” in a manner inspired by accounts from Mozart’s day.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/02/arts/music/artek-an-early-music-orchestra-at-immanuel-lutheran-church.html', 'snippet': 'Artek went to unusual lengths on Saturday to present “Mozartean Masterpieces” in a manner inspired by accounts from Mozart’s day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No drinks were quaffed nor meals consumed during a performance by the early-music ensemble Artek on Saturday night at Immanuel Lutheran Church on the Upper East Side. Conversation ceased when music was played. Applause came almost exclusively at the end of each work. It was almost a shame — given that the performers, billed as the Artek Orchestra, went to unusual lengths to present “Mozartean Masterpieces” in a manner inspired by accounts from Mozart’s day, you almost wanted the audience to respond in kind.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/arts/02ARTEK/02ARTEK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 822, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/arts/02ARTEK/02ARTEK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1643, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/arts/02ARTEK/02ARTEK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/02/arts/02ARTEK/02ARTEK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/arts/02ARTEK/02ARTEK-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Recreating Fragile Sounds With an 18th-Century Configuration', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Recreating Fragile Sounds With an 18th-Century Configuration', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Artek Early Music Ensemble', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-01T22:32:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Smit