: 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-01T23:21:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b5a0059-0364-52cd-9796-9e4cc9e2c09c', 'word_count': 161, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b5a0059-0364-52cd-9796-9e4cc9e2c09c'}, {'abstract': 'Ninety-three percent of all income growth in the U.S. in 2010 went to the top 1 percent. And just 15,000 households received 37 percent of all of those gains.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/01/is-america-still-the-land-of-opportunity/', 'snippet': 'Ninety-three percent of all income growth in the U.S. in 2010 went to the top 1 percent. And just 15,000 households received 37 percent of all of those gains.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Millions of immigrants head to the United States each year. And millions more would if they could get a visa. Yet, more and more Americans complain of a sense that the cards are stacked against the middle class — and, more devastatingly, its children. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/01/blogs/01rdv-us-income-inequality/01rdv-us-income-inequality-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/01/blogs/01rdv-us-income-inequality/01rdv-us-income-inequality-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/01/blogs/01rdv-us-income-inequality/01rdv-us-income-ineq