pe': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mayy El Sheikh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mayy', 'middlename': 'El', 'lastname': 'Sheikh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9644248-f198-590d-9bed-3d7b7650ac1a', 'word_count': 169, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9644248-f198-590d-9bed-3d7b7650ac1a'}, {'abstract': 'President Omar al-Bashir of Sudan has agreed to meet with President Salva Kiir Miyardeit of South Sudan on Friday in Ethiopia to discuss border security and oil sharing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/02/world/africa/sudan-and-south-sudan-leaders-agree-to-meet.html', 'snippet': 'President Omar al-Bashir of Sudan has agreed to meet with President Salva Kiir Miyardeit of South Sudan on Friday in Ethiopia to discuss border security and oil sharing.', 'lead_paragraph': ' President Omar al-Bashir of Sudan has agreed to meet with President Salva Kiir Miyardeit of South Sudan on Friday in Ethiopia to discuss border security and oil sharing, the official Sudanese news agency reported Tuesday. In New Year’s speeches, both presidents promised increased cooperation. On Tuesday, Mr. Bashir said he was committed to achieving peace with South Sudan, which seceded from Sudan in 2011 and became an independent state. The two countries signed an agreement last September to end hostilities and work on resolving issues, including how to share the oil wealth and contested border areas. “The call now is for establishing good neighborly relations, cooperation and implementing all items of the agreement,” Mr. Bashir said. Mr. Kiir, in a speech on New Year’s Eve, said he would withdraw troops from border areas, though he did not specify when. “To be able to establish the border monitoring mission, we are temporarily withdrawing our forces from the immediate border areas,” he said, according to Reuters. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sudan and South Sudan Leaders Agree to Meet', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Africa', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sudan and South Sudan Leaders Agree to Meet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kiir Mayardit, Salva', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "Kushkush, Isma'il", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bashir, Omar Hassan Al-', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sudan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Sudan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-02T00:38:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': "By Isma'il Kushkush", 'person': [{'firstname': "Isma'il", 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kushkush', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/f28caa57-145f-5643-a828-b8beefd011ba', 'word_count': 164, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f28caa57-145f-5643-a828-b8beefd011ba'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Pat Quinn is seeking to take advantage of the lame duck legislative calendar to fix the state’s underfinanced pension systems in a matter of days, after decades of failure and frustration.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/02/us/illinois-governor-seeks-fast-vote-on-states-long-troubled-pension-systems.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Pat Quinn is seeking to take advantage of the lame duck legislative calendar to fix the state’s underfinanced pension systems in a matter of days, after decades of failure and frustration.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — As Illinois lawmakers head back to work this week, Gov. Pat Quinn is seeking to use the practical advantages of a lame-duck legislative calendar to fix the state’s pension systems — the most underfinanced in the nation — in a matter of days.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/us/ILLINOIS/ILLINOIS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 662, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/us/ILLINOIS/ILLINOIS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1324, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/us/ILLINOIS/ILLINOIS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/02/us/ILLINOIS/ILLINOIS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/us/ILLINOIS/ILLINOIS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Illinois Governor Seeks Fast Vote on State’s Long-Troubled Pension Systems', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Illinois Governor Seeks Fast Vote on State’s Long-Troubled Pension Systems', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Illinois', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quinn, Patrick J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Employees', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-02T00:48:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Monica Davey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Monica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8cca3eed-d6fa-5c1a-a532-f7244a6cf065', 'word_count': 839, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8cca3eed-d6fa-5c1a-a532-f7244a6cf065'}, {'abstract': 'The companies making the narcotic painkillers OxyContin and Opana have introduced tamper-resistant pills, hoping to slow adoption of the drugs’ generic versions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/02/health/drug-makers-losing-a-bid-to-foil-generic-painkillers.html', 'snippet': 'The companies making the narcotic painkillers OxyContin and Opana have introduced tamper-resistant pills, hoping to slow adoption of the drugs’ generic versions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Public officials have long urged makers of powerful painkillers to do more to make the medications harder to crush and abuse. But now that some companies have done so, they want something in return — a ban on generic versions of the drugs they make that do not have such tamper-resistant designs.\xa0 ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/business/PAIN/PAIN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 675, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/business/PAIN/PAIN-sup