71da858', 'word_count': 770, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79a074ca-3776-5cec-bdad-2747171da858'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Carey Jr. was considered the last surviving member of a group known informally in Hollywood as the John Ford stock company.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/02/movies/harry-carey-jr-boyish-sidekick-to-john-wayne-dies-at-91.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Carey Jr. was considered the last surviving member of a group known informally in Hollywood as the John Ford stock company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Harry Carey Jr., an actor who made his mark as a boyish sidekick to John Wayne in John Ford westerns like “She Wore a Yellow Ribbon” (1949), “Wagon Master” (1950) and “The Searchers” (1956), and later became one of the most ubiquitous character actors in American television and movie westerns, died on Thursday in Santa Barbara, Calif. He was 91.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/arts/CAREY-obit/CAREY-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/02/arts/CAREY-obit/CAREY-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/arts/CAREY-obit/CAREY-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 764, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/arts/CAREY-obit/CAREY-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1529, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/arts/CAREY-obit/CAREY-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 