: 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c35eb55-f76d-5f67-a47b-dc2c6b2d0c2b', 'word_count': 898, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c35eb55-f76d-5f67-a47b-dc2c6b2d0c2b'}, {'abstract': 'Nearly 20 years later, the Bills’ record-setting 32-point rally against the Oilers is still debated as both the greatest comeback and choke.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/02/sports/football/bills-oilers-game-in-1993-is-greatest-comeback-that-ever-was-and-was-not.html', 'snippet': 'Nearly 20 years later, the Bills’ record-setting 32-point rally against the Oilers is still debated as both the greatest comeback and choke.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It seemed like a logical decision at the time. It was a cold, windy day at Rich Stadium in suburban Buffalo in 1993, and the hometown Bills were behind, 35-3, in the second half of a first-round playoff game against the Houston Oilers. With the outcome seemingly no longer in question and the weather rather uninviting, many fans simply chose to go home.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/sports/COMEBACK/COMEBACK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/02/sports/COMEBACK/COMEBACK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/sports/COMEBACK/COMEBACK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/sports/COMEBACK/COMEBACK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image'