'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/02/opinion/haitis-long-road.html', 'snippet': 'Three years after the earthquake, recovery is distant and progress slow.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the eve of the third anniversary of the earthquake that devastated Haiti in January 2010, the country remains in a fragile state. Billions of dollars in aid and lofty promises to “build back better” have brought it only so far. A recent article by Deborah Sontag of The Times showed, in disheartening detail, the distance between hope and reality. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Haiti’s Long Road', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Haiti’s Long Road', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Haiti', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Aid', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Earthquakes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-02T01:57:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2e3577c-5d17-5094-8ec3-46e5caceb2be', 'word_count': 616, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2e3577c-5d17-5094-8ec3-46e5caceb2be'}, {'abstract': 'Ricky Tibbs and his daughter, Alexis, have struggled to cope with the separate deaths of Mr. Tibbs’s wife and his 1-year-old son in 2010.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/02/nyregion/with-broken-hearts-a-father-and-daughter-press-on.html', 'snippet': 'Ricky Tibbs and his daughter, Alexis, have struggled to cope with the separate deaths of Mr. Tibbs’s wife and his 1-year-old son in 2010.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most of the memories Ricky Tibbs has of his son, Kevin, were forged inside hospitals. Even though Kevin was just a year old when he died in late 2010, Mr. Tibbs said that he was blessed by what his son was able to teach him in such a short time.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/nyregion/NEEDIEST/NEEDIEST-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/02/nyregion/NEEDIEST/NEEDIEST-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/nyregion/NEEDIEST/NEEDIEST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/nyregion/NEEDIEST/NEEDIEST-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/nyregion/NEEDIEST/NEEDIEST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/02/nyregion/NEEDIEST/NEEDIEST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/nyregion/NEEDIEST/NEEDIEST-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Father and Daughter Press On With Broken Hearts', 'kicker': 'The Neediest Cases', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Father and Daughter Press On With Broken Hearts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Otis, John', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federation of Protestant Welfare Agencies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Alternatives for Children', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times Neediest Cases Fund', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-02T01:58:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Otis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Otis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebd05040-965c-58e5-b09d-2d2e27422d78', 'word_count': 770, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebd05040-965c-58e5-b09d-2d2e27422d78'}, {'abstract': 'More lawmakers and voters are facing up to the costs and mistakes of capital cases.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/02/opinion/americas-retreat-from-the-death-penalty.html', 'snippet': 'More lawmakers and voters are facing up to the costs and mistakes of capital cases.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the Supreme Court reinstated the death penalty in 1976, it said there were two social purposes for imposing capital punishment for the most egregious crimes: deterrence and retribution. In recent months, these justifications for a cruel and uncivilized punishment have been seriously undermined by a growing group of judges, prosecutors, scholars and others involved in criminal justice, conservatives and liberals alike. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'America’s Retreat From the Death Penalty', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'America’s Retreat From the Death Penalty', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations