'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b057935-6820-5be5-a8e2-4d6f2eff44b9', 'word_count': 662, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b057935-6820-5be5-a8e2-4d6f2eff44b9'}, {'abstract': 'Regardless of what research shows, people seem enamored of their own theories about the origin of the phrase “the whole nine yards.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/02/the-whole-nine-yards-continued/', 'snippet': 'Regardless of what research shows, people seem enamored of their own theories about the origin of the phrase “the whole nine yards.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week’s article about recent discoveries relating to the origins of the mysterious phrase “the whole nine yards” drew a huge number of online comments, most of them from people whose certainty about their own pet theories was matched only by their total lack of supporting evidence.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Whole Nine Yards, Continued …', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'English Language', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Language and Languages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cooper, Bradley', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shapiro, Fred R', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Van Buren, Martin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Eagle', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kentucky', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Scotland', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-02T15:31:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original'