of “Argo,” discusses her process.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/02/below-the-line-the-sets-of-argo/', 'snippet': 'Sharon Seymour, the production designer of “Argo,” discusses her process.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The production designer Sharon Seymour has collaborated with Ben Affleck on all three films he has directed, creating gritty contemporary Boston sets for “Gone Baby Gone” and “The Town.” But “Argo,” Mr. Affleck’s\xa0 thriller set amid the 1979 Iranian hostage crisis, presented a new challenge for the team. She and Mr. Affleck wanted to recreate the looks of the period, without drawing attention to them and making the film feel like an episode of “That ’70s Show.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/01/movies/argo-design1/argo-design1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/01/movies/argo-design1/argo-design1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/01/movies/argo-design1/argo-design1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/01/movies/argo-design1/argo-design1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Below the Line: The Sets of ‘Argo’', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'AFFLECK, BEN', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Seymour, Sharon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-02T16:41:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/85f08ae4-ec04-5469-9ebf-445f8095193e', 'word_count': 602, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85f08ae4-ec04-5469-9ebf-445f8095193e'}, {'abstract': 'At first glance, the river may seem a near-wilderness. On closer inspection, the Mekong and its banks are more like an unruly linear farm.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/02/beyond-the-myth-the-bounteous-mekong/', 'snippet': 'At first glance, the river may seem a near-wilderness. On closer inspection, the Mekong and its banks are more like an unruly linear farm.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Seventy-two hours after leaving Cleveland, I slipped away from Christmas Eve dinner with my family, walked down a dimly lighted path and crossed a rickety bamboo bridge to an island. I knelt down and dipped my hand into the Mekong River.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/blogs/mekong1/mekong1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/blogs/mekong1/mekong1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/blogs/mekong1/mekong1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/02/blogs/mekong1/mekong1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/blogs/mekong1/mekong1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Beyond the Myth: The Bounteous Mekong', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Light and Power', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish and Other Marine Life', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Levees and Dams', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rivers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nature Conservancy', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Laos', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mekong River', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-02T16:41:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Opperman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Opperman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b0c9c98-cd5f-55ef-9757-6488c7822e66', 'word_count': 1421, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b0c9c98-cd5f-55ef-9757-6488c7822e66'}, {'abstract': 'For Jacqui Rosshandler, the decision came down to this question: Isn’t 25 percent of something better than 100 percent of nothing?', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/02/should-a-cash-poor-entrepreneur-give-up-control-to-keep-her-start-up-alive/', 'snippet': 'For Jacqui Rosshandler, the decision came down to this question: Isn’t 25 percent of something better than 100 percent of nothing?', 'lead_paragraph': 'We just published a case study about Eatwhatever, a recent entrant in the crowded, billion dollar breath mint industry. Begun by Jacqui Rosshandler in 2008 when she was in her mid-20s, her one-woman start-up took off quickly. Her energy and youthful slogan — 2 Steps for Kissable Breath — helped land a buzz-building mention on Daily Candy’s main page. She talked her way into New York retail outlets like C.O. Bigelow, Ricky’s, Joe Coffee and the specialty department store Zitomer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Should a Cash-Poor Entrepreneur Give Up Control to Keep Her Start-Up Alive?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venture Capital', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-02T16:45:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Grossmann', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grossmann', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4da08f1-159a-5bb4-8396-9597e8287317', 'word_count': 747, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4da08f1-159a-5bb4-8396-9597e8287317'}, {'abstract': 'A number of recent deals offer a variation on the takeunder theme: takeovers for less than the initial public offering price. Avis, for example, is buying Zipcar at a 32 percent discount from the I.P.O.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/01/02/long-after-the-i-p-o-deals-at-a-discount/', 'snippet': 'A number of recent deals offer a variation on the takeunder theme: takeovers for less than the initial public offering price. Avis, for example, is buying Zipcar at a 32 percent discount from the I.P.O.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the mergers and acquisitions world, they are called “takeunders,” acquisitions at a price that is less than the target company’s stock market value. Now, a number of recent deals for companies that have gone public in recent years offer a variation on the theme: takeovers for less than the initial offering price. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Long After the I.P.O., Deals at a Discount', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Duff & Phelps Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Starbucks Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ZipCar', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-02T16:51:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e1da273-c415-5476-a6df-4eb4728d140e', 'word_count': 247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e1da273-c415-5476-a6df-4eb4728d140e'}, {'abstract': 'The depth of the anger that followed the House’s refusal to take up a package of assistance for Hurricane Sandy victims was extraordinary and exceedingly personal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/03/nyregion/congressional-members-blast-house-for-ignoring-storm-aid-bill.html', 'snippet': 'The depth of the anger that followed the House’s refusal to take up a package of assistance for Hurricane Sandy victims was extraordinary and exceedingly personal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Northeastern Republicans, long outnumbered and overshadowed in their own party nationally, erupted in fury on Wednesday after the Republican-controlled House of Representatives blocked a measure that sought to provide billions of dollars in aid to New York, New Jersey, Connecticut and other states pummeled by Hurricane Sandy.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/03/nyregion/Sandy/Sandy-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 440, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/03/nyregion/Sandy/Sandy-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 440}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/03/nyregion/Sandy/Sandy-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 751, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/03/nyregion/Sandy/Sandy-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1502, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/03/nyregion/Sandy/Sandy-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnai