'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/sports/20130102photoreplay-slide-2HEJ/20130102photoreplay-slide-2HEJ-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Photo Replay: Jan. 2', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hopman Cup (Tennis)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Scottish Premier League', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-02T16:54:25+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/a0dd91b7-c198-55d8-8c7b-8a1a15f591a2', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/a0dd91b7-c198-55d8-8c7b-8a1a15f591a2'}, {'abstract': 'New light vehicle registrations in the United States in 2013 are expected to rise 6.6 percent over 2012 levels to 15.3 million vehicles.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/02/polk-forecasts-increased-u-s-vehicle-sales-and-production-in-2013/', 'snippet': 'New light vehicle registrations in the United States in 2013 are expected to rise 6.6 percent over 2012 levels to 15.3 million vehicles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The auto industry is expected to continue to recover in 2013 and 2014 in a positive sign for the American economy, according to Polk, a global automotive market intelligence firm.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Polk Forecasts Increased U.S. Vehicle Sales and Production in 2013', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ford Motor Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toyota Motor Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-02T16:54:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cheryl Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cheryl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6718191-a87e-5f85-9dd7-a82b0fcbe5cb', 'word_count': 308, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6718191-a87e-5f85-9dd7-a82b0fcbe5cb'}, {'abstract': 'The actor, who appears in “Killing Them Softly” and “Argo,” talks to T about his “slow, slow break”', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/02/asked-answered-scoot-mcnairy/', 'snippet': 'The actor, who appears in “Killing Them Softly” and “Argo,” talks to T about his “slow, slow break”', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Scoot McNairy’s voice first came over the phone, I was startled to hear a Texan accent. I should not have been — I had read that he grew up outside of Dallas — but I had just watched him act in two films, “Killing Them Softly” and “Argo,” in which he disappears so fully into two very different characters, I had all but forgotten he came from anywhere. You don’t expect a chameleon to speak with a twang. In “Killing Them Softly,” directed by Andrew Dominik and starring Brad Pitt, McNairy plays one of three guys who rob a mob-protected card game. In “Argo,” directed by and starring Ben Affleck, and based on real events, he plays one of six American diplomats who were extracted out of revolutionary Iran in an outlandish C.I.A. scheme that had them pretending to be a Canadian film crew. McNairy, 34, shifts shapes again in “Promised Land,” a Gus Van Sant movie that opened Dec. 28, and, if these films are any indication, he’ll do so again in “Twelve Years a Slave,” directed by Steve McQueen and due out this year. But don’t call him an overnight success. Between long days of shooting yet another major feature, “Non-Stop,” starring Julianne Moore and Liam Neeson, McNairy spoke to T about muddying accents, the art of riding mechanical bulls and what he terms his “slow, slow break.”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Asked & Answered | Scoot McNairy', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At Last, All Over the Screen  Scoot McNairy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-02T17:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abby Aguirre', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Aguirre', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/74fef40c-8406-52b3-b126-b661f688526e', 'word_count': 1275, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74fef40c-8406-52b3-b126-b661f688526e'}, {'abstract': 'The Times’s Michael D. Shear talks about the deal that averted spending cuts and tax increases for most Americans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/us/politics/100000001983526/house-passes-fiscal-legislation.html', 'snippet': 'The Times’s Michael D. Shear talks about the deal that averted spending cuts and tax increases for most Americans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Times’s Michael D. Shear talks about the deal that averted spending cuts and tax increases for most Americans.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/us/politics/video-tc10-130102-deal/video-tc10-1301