er.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/02/dueling-weinstein-films-and-other-subplots-in-the-foreign-film-race/', 'snippet': 'The foreign-language Oscar shortlist includes two films backed by the Weinstein Company as well as an entry by a director famously snubbed by the Academy once before. Who will make the final five?', 'lead_paragraph': 'With little more than a week to go before the shortlist of nine films in contention for the Academy Award for best foreign-language film is trimmed to five official nominees, Michael Haneke’s “Amour” remains the clear front-runner. But the question of what four other films will also qualify is less clear, and the likelihood of some surprises is high, in part because of the strong field, but also because of the Academy’s unusual voting procedures in this category.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/arts/intouchables/intouchables-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/08/arts/intouchables/intouchables-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/arts/intouchables/intouchables-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 770, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/arts/intouchables/intouchables-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/08/arts/intouchables/intouchables-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dueling Weinstein Films and Other Subplots  in the Foreign Film Race', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headl