ad_paragraph': 'MENDRISIO, Switzerland — The Swiss like to think their country is to gold what Bordeaux, France, is to wine. Thanks to a dark red merlot produced in the hills surrounding this town in the south of Switzerland, it has both, the real gold and the wine.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/03/world/03switzerlandweb1/03switzerlandweb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/03/world/03switzerlandweb1/03switzerlandweb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 345}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/03/world/03switzerlandweb1/03switzerlandweb1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 590, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/03/world/03switzerlandweb1/03switzerlandweb1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1179, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/03/world/03switzerlandweb1/03switzerlandweb1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/03/world/03switzerlandweb1/03switzerlandweb1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/03/world/03switzerlandweb1/03switzerlandweb1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Swiss Region Where the Gold Comes in Solid and Liquid Forms', 'kicker': 'Mendrisio Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Swiss Region Where the Gold Comes in Solid and Liquid Forms', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Switzerland', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tagliabue, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mendrisio (Switzerland)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gold', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-02T19:45:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Tagliabue', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tagliabue', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/73191cc5-2509-5ad4-82d7-9716df6b8e05', 'word_count': 1011, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73191cc5-2509-5ad4-82d7-9716df6b8e05'}, {'abstract': 'How the breakout star (and daughter of David) turned “Girls” from a show about a trio to one about a quartet.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/06/magazine/zosia-mamet-is-still-getting-used-to-being-your-new-best-friend.html', 'snippet': 'How the breakout star (and daughter of David) turned “Girls” from a show about a trio to one about a quartet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Zosia Mamet was in upstate New York shooting a movie in 2010 when she received a call: the producers of “Girls,” a new TV series on HBO, created by some up-and-coming writer-director type, were eager to have her read for a part on the show. The series was going to be about three 20-something women — a lost and awkward aspiring writer named Hannah (who would be played by the show’s creator, Lena Dunham); her strait-laced, perfectionist roommate Marnie; and her saucy, libertine friend Jessa — all trying to make it in New York.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/magazine/06mamet-1/06mamet-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/06/magazine/06mamet-1/06mamet-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/magazine/06mamet-1/06mamet-1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/magazine/06mamet-1/06mamet-1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1500, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/magazine/06mamet-1/06mamet-1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/06/magazine/06mamet-1/06mamet-1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/magazine/06mamet-1/06mamet-1-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Zosia Mamet Is Still Getting Used to Being Your New Best Friend', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘I Am a Private Human’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mamet, Zosia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Girls (TV Program)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-02T19:47:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Taffy Brodesser-Akner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Taffy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brodesser-Akner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0646189d-0ef9-5dd7-a5c3-edaa2a111290', 'word_count': 3003, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0646189d-0ef9-5dd7-a5c3-edaa2a111290'}, {'abstract': '“Americans are the only people in the world known to me whose status anxiety prompts them to advertise their college and university affiliations in the rear windows of their automobiles,” Paul Fussell once wrote.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/02/what-those-college-stickers-on-the-rear-window-say-about-america/', 'snippet': '“Americans are the only people in the world known to me whose status anxiety prompts them to advertise their college and university affiliations in the rear windows of their automobiles,” Paul Fussell once wrote.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A lot of college applications are being submitted this week. To mark (but not make light of, no!) the occasion, I went back to look up a recollected passage from “Class,” by Paul Fussell, who was memorialized in last weekend’s “Lives They Lived” issue. About the author and that book in particular, Dwight Garner had this to say:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/magazine/02-fussell1/02-fussell1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 776, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/magazine/02-fussell1/02-fussell1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1553, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/magazine/02-fussell1/02-fussell1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/02/magazine/02-fussell1/02-fussell1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/magazine/02-fussell1/02-fussell1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Those College Stickers on the Rear Window Say About America', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fussell, Paul', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-02T19:52:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dean Robinson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dean', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robinson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1827f76-4250-5e55-a64b-f6cbe838c82a', 'word_count': 386, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1827f76-4250-5e55-a64b-f6cbe838c82a'}, {'abstract': 'City Room offers a sampling of views from more than 1,000 online comments on The Journal News’s efforts to present handgun permit information online.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/02/readers-divided-on-news-sites-map-of-gun-permit-holders/', 'snippet': 'City Room offers a sampling of views from more than 1,000 online comments on The Journal News’s efforts to present handgun permit information online.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When a newspaper in Westchester County, N.Y., published a map online last month showing the names and addresses of local pistol permit holders, a flood of nationwide criticism (and a counter-flood of support) ensued. Many gun owners objected to the information being published, though it is publicly available, and now, officials in Putnam County, N.Y., are refusing to release pistol-permit records to the paper, The Journal News.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Readers Divided on News Site’s Map of Gun Permit Holders', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Publishing of Gun Data Elicits Strong Opinions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gannett Company Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Westchester County (NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-02T19:55:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/980db007-514e-5705-a065-2f05fde1426d', 'word_count': 1403, 'uri': 'nyt://article/980db007-514e-5705-a065-2f05fde1426d'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Page was known for hits like “Tennessee Waltz,” “Old Cape Cod” and “(How Much Is) That Doggie in the Window.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/03/arts/music/patti-page-singer-dies-at-85.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Page was known for hits like “Tennessee Waltz,” “Old Cape Cod” and “(How Much Is) That Doggie in the Window.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Patti Page, the apple-cheeked, honey-voiced alto whose sentimental, soothing, sometimes silly hits like “Tennessee Waltz,” “Old Cape Cod” and “(How Much Is) That Doggie in the Window” made her one of the most successful pop singers of the 1950s, died on Tuesday in Encinitas, Calif. She was 85.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/03/us/03pageweb1/03pageweb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 792, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/03/us/03pageweb1/03pageweb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 792}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/03/us/03pageweb1/03pageweb1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 777, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/03/us/03pageweb1/03pageweb1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1553, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/03/us/03pageweb1/03pageweb1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/03/us/03pageweb1/03pageweb1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/03/us/03pageweb1/03pageweb1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {