the last few years, connoting an eco-friendly ethos among the business set, “community” is now a favorite of the nonprofit world. But if oil companies could be suspected of not being quite as green as their advertising claims, cultural institutions claiming to act on behalf of the community can raise similar alarms. A cynical thought, perhaps, but appropriate when considering “Go: a community-curated open studio project” at the Brooklyn Museum.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/03/arts/GO/GO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/03/arts/GO/GO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/03/arts/GO/GO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/03/arts/GO/GO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 858, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/03/arts/GO/GO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/03/arts/GO/GO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/03/arts/GO/GO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Crowdsourced Exhibition Looks Kind of Familiar', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Crowdsourced Exhibition Looks Kind of Familiar', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Museum', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-02T23:18:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Schwendener', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwendener', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a71f73aa-b412-598b-940e-4cc93b5554c7', 'word_count': 740, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a71f73aa-b412-598b-940e-4cc93b5554c7'}, {'abstract': 'Spurred by her children, an urbanite tests four garbage-eating devices.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/03/garden/a-city-dweller-tests-four-composters.html', 'snippet': 'Spurred by her children, an urbanite tests four garbage-eating devices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN my oldest son returned from a first-grade field trip last year insisting that our family start composting, my heart did not exactly soar. After six years of changing diapers, I wasn’t looking to take on additional waste-management responsibilities. I switched the subject, and our melon rinds and abandoned cheese sticks continued their steady march into the trash. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/03/garden/03COMPOST_SPAN/03COMPOST_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 368, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/03/garden/03COMPOST_SPAN/03COMPOST_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 368}}, {'