sh-empire.html', 'snippet': 'Each Jan. 1 the reigning British monarch announces an honors list. British and Commonwealth subjects are recognized for especially meritorious achievement in almost any field.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Each Jan. 1 the reigning British monarch announces an honors list. British and Commonwealth subjects are recognized for especially meritorious achievement in almost any field. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/arts/card/card-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 361, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/arts/card/card-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 361, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Andrew Robson Given Order of the British Empire', 'kicker': 'Bridge', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cards and Card Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bridge (Card Game)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Robson, Andrew', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-02T23:38:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'subsection_name': 'Bridge', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phillip Alder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phillip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d9d1e63-df09-5e17-84e1-f848da042f23', 'word_count': 505, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d9d1e63-df09-5e17-84e1-f848da042f23'}, {'abstract': 'Patricia Urquiola’s Tatou lamps for Flos are named after the French word for armadillo.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/03/garden/patricia-urquiolas-tatou-lamps-for-flos.html', 'snippet': 'Patricia Urquiola’s Tatou lamps for Flos are named after the French word for armadillo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Designing a new lighting collection for Flos, Patricia Urquiola began with a vision of strength and security. “In the beginning, I was inspired by Japanese armor,” said Ms. Urquiola, the Milan-based designer. “I was looking at modules of metal crossed with fiber and making a really powerful and emotional suspension lamp.”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/03/garden/03CURR_SPAN/03CURR_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/03/garden/03CURR_SPAN/03CURR_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/03/garden/03CURR_SPAN/03CURR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 813, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/03/garden/03CURR_SPAN/03CURR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1627, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/03/garden/03CURR_SPAN/03CURR_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/03/garden/03CURR_SPAN/03CURR_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/03/garden/03CURR_SPAN/03CURR_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Gentle Creature, Illuminated', 'kicker': 'Currents | Lighting', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Gentle Creature, Illuminated', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Urquiola, Patricia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McKeough, Tim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lamps and Lampshades', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Flos SpA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-02T23:39:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim McKeough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McKeough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d69cf1b-28b1-57bd-b4b8-a7f97ffb89d8', 'word_count': 138, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d69cf1b-28b1-57bd-b4b8-a7f97ffb89d8'}, {'abstract': 'The Avalon chair and bench, designed in 1950 by William Haines, an actor turned interior designer, have been reissued.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/03/garden/hollywood-chairs-make-an-encore.html', 'snippet': 'The Avalon chair and bench, designed in 1950 by William Haines, an actor turned interior designer, have been reissued.', 'lead_paragraph': 'William Haines, a film actor turned interior designer who left the movie business after refusing to deny his homosexuality and who acquired a glittering clientele of Hollywood stars, created the Avalon chair and bench in 1950 for the lanai of the Sidney and Frances Brody House in Los Angeles. Those designs have now been reissued — down to the chair’s distinctive hand-grip, with its brass spiral-wrap detail. “Haines had a unique, well-honed design sensibility, which still looks fresh today,” said Greg Bianchini, production manager of William Haines Designs. A powder-coated steel base and an array of weather-resistant upholstery fabrics (like the hemp-and-acrylic textile shown here, from the company Perennials) make the chair suitable for outdoors. Customers can also choose indoor-only fabrics. Prices vary based on material. The chair below is $8,080; the bench, $6,280. Available through Profiles New York, (212) 689-6903 or info@williamhaines.com.\xa0', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/03/garden/03CURR4_SPAN/03CURR4_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/03/garden/03CURR4_SPAN/03CURR4_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/03/garden/03CURR4_SPAN/03CURR4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/03/garden/03CURR4_SPAN/03CURR4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/03/garden/03CURR4_SPAN/03CURR4_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/03/garden/03CURR4_SPAN/03CURR4_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url':