': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6dfb496-4d54-5bc9-bc45-f22c4882341d', 'word_count': 1111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6dfb496-4d54-5bc9-bc45-f22c4882341d'}, {'abstract': 'Speaker John Boehner failed the thousands devastated by the storm when the relief package that passed the Senate was ignored in the House.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/03/opinion/dereliction-of-duty-hurricane-sandy-aid.html', 'snippet': 'Speaker John Boehner failed the thousands devastated by the storm when the relief package that passed the Senate was ignored in the House.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is a lot of finger-pointing in Washington about who is responsible for the mess made of the so-called fiscal-cliff negotiations, but there is no doubt about who failed thousands of residents and businesses devastated by Hurricane Sandy and still waiting for help: Speaker John Boehner.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hurricane Sandy Aid', 'kicker': 'Editorial | Dereliction Of Duty', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'House speaker kills vote on Hurricane Sandy aid', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Aid (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', '