hat-a-good-quarterback-means/', 'snippet': 'Do you have a top quarterback or not? Everything in the N.F.L. can change based on that question.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Hey, Tony. I just wanted to say to you: Don’t listen to what anybody else is saying about you. You’re a great quarterback, man. And this game doesn’t mean anything.” Robert Griffin III to Tony Romo, as captured by a microphone for Showtime’s “Inside the NFL,” via Michael David Smith, ProFootballTalk.com', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Robert Griffin III: What a Good Quarterback Means', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Griffin, Robert III', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Redskins', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-03T13:35:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f86e8a60-bca3-5abc-819b-0b7a280008e7', 'word_count': 454, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f86e8a60-bca3-5abc-819b-0b7a280008e7'}, {'abstract': 'Psychologist who studied sexual offenders in India says there is no fear of rule of law among them.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/03/psychologist-who-works-with-sexual-offenders-in-india-explains-motives/', 'snippet': 'Psychologist who studied sexual offenders in India says there is no fear of rule of law among them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dr. Rajat Mitra, a clinical psychologist, is the director of the Swanchetan Society for Mental Health, a nongovernmental organization in India that provides counseling and support services to survivors of violence, abuse and trauma. He is one of the few people in the country who has closely studied sex offenders to understand the motivation behind their attacks, interviewing hundreds of them in Tihar Jail in Delhi over several years.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Conversation With: Psychologist Rajat Mitra', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tihar Jail', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-03T13:45:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Malavika Vyawahare', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Malavika', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vyawahare', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a965ec4e-b613-5e62-9f43-161fb11965cf', 'word_count': 1428, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a965ec4e-b613-5e62-9f43-161fb11965cf'}, {'abstract': 'The $500 million acquisition of Zipcar by the Avis Budget Group represents a perhaps inevitable evolution for a company that has been more successful as a collectivist concept than as a profit-making venture.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/03/daily-report-avis-also-buys-zipcar-ethos/', 'snippet': 'The $500 million acquisition of Z