17ee-500b-8dd1-ced92c7cf509'}, {'abstract': 'While their building remains closed, Sandy Hook Elementary students headed back to class at a different Connecticut school that was transformed into a “very cheerful and nurturing” environment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/04/nyregion/sandy-hook-students-return-to-class-in-new-building.html', 'snippet': 'While their building remains closed, Sandy Hook Elementary students headed back to class at a different Connecticut school that was transformed into a “very cheerful and nurturing” environment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MONROE, Conn. — On the first day back, Sean Murray said, his 9-year-old son, Brendan, was eager to return to school and see his friends, but he was nervous at the same time.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/us/04school_span/04school_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/04/us/04school_span/04school_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/us/04school_span/04school_span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 602, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/us/04school_span/04school_span-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1204, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/us/04school_span/04school_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/04/us/04school_span/04school_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/us/04school_span/04school_span-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Children of a Tragedy Are Returned to School Life', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Children Of a Tragedy Are Returned To School Life', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newtown, Conn, Shooting (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Applebome, Peter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sandy Hook Elementary School (Newtown, Conn)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Newtown (Conn)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-03T14:21:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Applebome', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Applebome', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b42b465e-e74c-5030-a1fb-a0a20f3b4435', 'word_count': 762, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b42b465e-e74c-5030-a1fb-a0a20f3b4435'}, {'abstract': 'The closely watched experimental drug, dexpramipexole, failed to work in a late-stage clinical trial, disappointing medical experts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/04/business/company-gives-up-on-drug-for-lou-gehrigs-disease.html', 'snippet': 'The closely watched experimental drug, dexpramipexole, failed to work in a late-stage clinical trial, disappointing medical experts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A closely watched experimental drug to treat Lou Gehrig’s disease failed to work in a late-stage clinical trial, the drug’s developer, Biogen Idec, said Thursday, disappointing medical experts who had hoped it might be a useful tool against the poorly understood and fatal illness. The company said it would discontinue work on the drug.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Biogen Idec Gives Up on Drug for Lou Gehrig’s Disease', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Biogen Idec Gives Up on Drug for Lou Gehrig’s Disease', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pollack, Andrew', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AMYOTROPHIC LATERAL SCLEROSIS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Clinical Trials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Biogen Idec Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-03T14:39:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Pollack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pollack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef083cda-87b9-5a65-88e7-13997bac173c', 'word_count': 602, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef083cda-87b9-5a65-88e7-13997bac173c'}, {'abstract': 'In the past year, Google has been repeatedly criticized on privacy issues. Is that why the search giant seems to be having a hard time finding enough participants for an ambitious new tracking venture?', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/03/data-dump-are-potential-panelists-scorning-google/', 'snippet': 'In the past year, Google has been repeatedly criticized on privacy issues. Is that why the search giant seems to be having a hard time finding enough participants for an ambitious new tracking venture?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Suppose a stranger showed up at your house, a shiny new modem under his arm. He says he wants to attach the device to your computer so he can see everything you do online — how you update your Facebook friends with news about your cats, how you use Twitter to flatter your boss, how you single-handedly are keeping the cult of Kim Kardashian alive. He says he will use the information to help make the Internet run more smoothly. All mankind will benefit.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/technology/02bits-letter/02bits-letter-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 219, 'width': 592, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/technology/02bits-letter/02bits-letter-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 219, 'width': 592, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/technology/02bits-letter/02bits-letter-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/02/technology/02bits-letter/02bits-letter-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/technology/02bits-letter/02bits-letter-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 99, 'width': 99, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Data Dump: Are Potential Panelists Scorning Google?', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Google Seeks\r\nVolunteers\r\nFor Web Tracking', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-03T14:47:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Streitfeld', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Streitfeld', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71803292-02cd-5581-b984-446db1d4cc27', 'word_count': 759, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71803292-02cd-5581-b984-446db1d4cc27'}, {'abstract': 'Also, Andrew Sullivan strikes out on his own and a federal judge rejects an information request on the United States military’s drone program.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/03/the-breakfast-meeting-al-jazeeras-deal-for-current-tv/', 'snippet': 'Also, Andrew Sullivan strikes out on his own and a federal judge rejects an information request on the United States military’s drone program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Al Jazeera, the Arab news giant financed by the government of Qatar, announced its plans to buy Current TV, the failing progressive network co-founded by Al Gore. The deal will give Al Jazeera a much bigger footprint in the United States, reaching 40 million households. After the acquisition was announced, Time Warner Cable said that it would no longer carry Current TV. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: Al Jazeera’s Deal for Current TV', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drones (Pilotless Planes)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Awlaki, Anwar al-', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gore, Al', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sullivan, Andrew', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL JAZEERA', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BuzzFeed Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Current TV', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Time Warner Cable Inc', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-03T14:59:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editors', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editors'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/683238c6-176f-5459-8ecd-dd0a99c6e61a', 'word_count': 162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/683238c6-176f-5459-8ecd-dd0a99c6e61a'}, {'abstract': 'After decades of journeyman work, Reed Birney has translated his recent Off Broadway success into his return to Broadway, in “Picnic.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/06/theater/reed-birney-back-on-broadway-in-picnic.html', 'snippet': 'After decades of journeyman work, Reed Birney has translated his recent Off Broadway success into his return to Broadway, in “Picnic.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN Reed Birney’s big break finally came, after 30 years as a journeyman actor in New York, he nearly let it pass him by. Like many performers who had seen dream role after dream role go to bigger stars, Mr. Birney had lost faith in himself. Supporting parts and forgettable guests spots on “Law & Order” were cold comfort as he watched, at home in pajamas, as former classmates like Sigourney Weaver and Mercedes Ruehl walked Hollywood red carpets. Mr. Birney even started to believe what an anonymous poster once wrote on a blog about his performances in countless nice-guy parts. That he was a lightweight.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/arts/06BIRNEY_SPAN/06BIRNEY_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 406, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/06/arts/06BIRNEY_SPAN/06BIRNEY_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 406}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/arts/06BIRNEY_SPAN/06BIRNEY_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 693, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/arts/06BIRNEY_SPAN/06BIRNEY_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1386, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/arts/06BIRNEY_SPAN/06BIRNEY_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/06/arts/06BIRNEY_SPAN/06BIRNEY_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/arts/06BIRNEY_SPAN/06BIRNEY_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Actor Ages Into His Broadway Comeback', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Actor Ages Into His Broadway Comeback', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Birney, Reed', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-03T15:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70e3113a-c902-5e23-b256-9a01c452703f', 'word_count': 1686, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70e3113a-c902-5e23-b256-9a01c452703f'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/03/what-were-reading-599/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Slate: The chicken nugget: a biography. Small, salty, spongy and reviled by food purists, the lowly nugget can now be tracked to its little-known but likely progenitor: a Cornell University poultry-science professor named Robert C. Baker, who proposed the nugget in 1963, way before McDonald’s introduced its wildly popular McNuggets in 1980. — Glenn Collins', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-03T15:03:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6f158dd-70c6-536e-84e1-34f659542e88', 'word_count': 302, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6f158dd-70c6-536e-84e1-34f659542e88'}, {'abstract': 'President Vladimir V. Putin of Russia signed a decree making the French actor, who has been fighting high taxes in his home country, a Russian citizen.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/04/world/europe/putin-makes-gerard-depardieu-a-citizen-of-russia.html', 'snippet': 'President Vladimir V. Putin of Russia signed a decree making the French actor, who has been fighting high taxes in his home country, a Russian citizen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — At the time, it seemed like a joke. President Vladimir V. Putin of Russia, at his annual news conference before more than 1,000 journalists last month, declared with a mixture of braggadocio and magnanimity that if one of the world’s best-known Frenchmen, the actor Gérard Depardieu, really wanted to renounce his French citizenship, he would find the doors to Russia wide open — with a residency permit and Russian citizenship his for the asking. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/world/04Depardieuweb1/04Depardieuweb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 407, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/04/world/04Depardieuweb1/04Depardieuweb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 407}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/world/04Depardieuweb1/04Depardieuweb1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 695, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/world/04Depardieuweb1/04Depardieuweb1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1389, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/world/04Depardieuweb1/04Depardieuweb1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/04/world/04Depardieuweb1/04Depardieuweb1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/world/04Depardieuweb1/04Depardieuweb1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'That Russian Movie Star, Gérard Depardieu', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'French Star’s New Role: Being a Russian Citizen', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Depardieu, Gerard', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Belgium', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizenship and Naturalization', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-03T15:03:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By David M. Herszenhorn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/470421cc-0fc9-58ae-b956-fc637021b35b', 'word_count': 924, 'uri': 'nyt://article/470421cc-0fc9-58ae-b956-fc637021b35b'}, {'abstract': 'Sportswriters regard Ray Lewis, who will retire after the playoffs, as a hero and a villain — a symbol of today’s N.F.L.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/04/sports/the-many-sides-of-ray-lewis-leading-off.html', 'snippet': 'Sportswriters regard Ray Lewis, who will retire after the playoffs, as a hero and a villain — a symbol of today’s N.F.L.', 'lead_paragraph': "When Ray Lewis announced his impending retirement from the Baltimore Ravens on Wednesday, it fell neatly in line with the dichotomy that has been Lewis’s entire career. Was his idea to do this before the Ravens’ first playoff game an invaluable emotional boost to his teammates, or a look-at-me moment at a team-focused time? Was Lewis merely the game’s greatest middle linebacker, or the kind of head-wrecking force that necessitated the N.F.L.'s making the game safer, a campaign, fittingly, Lewis has put his face to? Was he a great statesman, or the shady guy the N.F.L. once fined a substantial sum for his involvement in a murder?", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/sports/04leading/04leading-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/04/sports/04leading/04leading-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/sports/04leading/04leading-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/sports/04leading/04leading-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/sports/04leading/04leading-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/04/sports/04leading/04leading-thumb