cle', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Glenn Collins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Glenn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c3e9b09-b2ba-50b0-9fbd-faad4cf1cb39', 'word_count': 248, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c3e9b09-b2ba-50b0-9fbd-faad4cf1cb39'}, {'abstract': 'The first in a month of Townies essays from Washington, D.C.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/03/arianna-huffington-and-me/', 'snippet': 'The first in a month of Townies essays from Washington, D.C.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This month, Townies goes out of town, to Washington, D.C.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Arianna Huffington and Me', 'kicker': 'Townies', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huffington, Arianna', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-03T17:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Alter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/02ab7a08-280b-5cf6-82f3-d02f1c6be663', 'word_count': 1052, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02ab7a08-280b-5cf6-82f3-d02f1c6be663'}, {'abstract': 'No one mines his own life in the service of understanding the American experience better than Walter Kirn.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/03/looking-into-a-mothers-bible/', 'snippet': 'No one mines his own life in the service of understanding the American experience better than Walter Kirn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No one mines his own life in the service of understanding the American experience better than Walter Kirn. He has written about his Mormonism and his college education, and, for this magazine, he has written (among many other topics) about meeting his girlfriend via Facebook friending, taking Adderall and being fired. Now Kirn, the author of “Up in the Air” and other novels, has written about discovering his mother’s Bible, or more precisely discovering her marginalia in the Bible. (And for more thoughts on marginalia, see Sam Anderson’s first Riff column.)\xa0“My Mother’s Bible,” which appears on Byliner, is hard to categorize. It is at once an exegesis of Genesis and Exodus and a wail of mourning for his mother, who died suddenly, from a strep infection of the brain. In his musing on Rebekah helping her son Jacob to conspire against his brother, Esau, Kirn writes:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/magazine/02-bible/02-bible-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/magazine/02-bible/02-bible-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1365, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/magazine/02-bible/02-bible-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/02/magazine/02-bible/02-bible-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/02/magazine/02-bible/02-bible-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': '