1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/140dbdba-bc5c-5cc9-893e-365f0adf2505', 'word_count': 1289, 'uri': 'nyt://article/140dbdba-bc5c-5cc9-893e-365f0adf2505'}, {'abstract': 'David O. Russell on how he came to rethink the kind of films he wanted to make.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/03/david-o-russell-part-2-the-uses-of-enchantment/', 'snippet': 'David O. Russell on how he came to rethink the kind of films he wanted to make.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David O. Russell is keen to talk about his silver linings. Five years ago, after foundering earlier with “I ♥ Huckabees,” he was invited (by Sydney Pollack, no less) to adapt the novel “Silver Linings Playbook,” and he leapt at the chance. “I had to work,” he said. “It makes you squeeze the toothpaste out of the tube – you can’t overthink it, you have to just write the script, write it now, turn the draft around now.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/03/movies/russell-bagger/russell-bagger-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/03/movies/russell-bagger/russell-bagger-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1368, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/03/movies/russell-bagger/russell-bagger-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/03/movies/russell-bagger/russell-bagger-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2