.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the second year in a row, President Obama has signed a military budget bill with odious provisions that further entrench the practice of indefinite military detention for terrorist suspects, make it nearly impossible to close the Guantánamo Bay prison camp, and actually leave open the possibility that the military could arrest and detain an American citizen without due process.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Odious Provisions in the Defense Bill', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Signing Statements', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feinstein, Dianne', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-03T20:05:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea5f3dba-ecd5-5155-b7d8-a176377c1d70', 'word_count': 335, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea5f3dba-ecd5-5155-b7d8-a176377c1d70'}, {'abstract': 'Time Warner Cable dropped Current TV after the company announced it was being sold to the pan-Arab news network.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/03/time-warner-cable-says-it-will-keep-open-mind-on-reinstating-al-jazeera/', 'snippet': 'Time Warner Cable dropped Current TV after the company announced it was being sold to the pan-Arab news network.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Time Warner Cable minced no words when it announced on Wednesday night that it was dropping Current TV, just hours after Al Jazee