otos, Sequencing Passages and More', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-03T20:15:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Ferlazzo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ferlazzo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9aa4867c-45d0-5370-8148-4218c420dcfc', 'word_count': 1172, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9aa4867c-45d0-5370-8148-4218c420dcfc'}, {'abstract': 'The School of Life, a new Picador series, includes self-help books by Alain de Botton and Philippa Perry.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/04/books/alain-de-botton-on-sex-and-philippa-perry-on-sanity.html', 'snippet': 'The School of Life, a new Picador series, includes self-help books by Alain de Botton and Philippa Perry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the drawbacks of working in a bookstore, something I did for many years, is that it can be like working in a small-town pharmacy: You learn things about people you might rather not know. What sort of face do you put on when your new girlfriend’s mother comes to the counter with a Newt Gingrich novel, a scented candle and a copy of “The Herpes Survival Guide”? ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/arts/04BOOK2/04BOOK2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 749, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/arts/04BOOK2/04BOOK2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1498, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/arts/04BOOK2/04BOOK2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/04/arts/04BOOK2/04BOOK2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/arts/04BOOK2/04BOOK2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Nerdy-Dirty Primer on Primal Urges', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Nerdy-Dirty Primer on Primal Urges', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garner, Dwight', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Botton, Alain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Philippa', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-03T20:16:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dwight Garner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dwight', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d849d90-22c2-54ce-9f99-6db783ba6840', 'word_count': 972, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d849d90-22c2-54ce-9f99-6db783ba6840'}, {'abstract': 'Eric Bledsoe’s shooting percentage and assists are down, and his turnovers are up, after a hot start in which he was seen as an early contender for most improved player.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/03/bledsoe-cools-but-clippers-will-need-him-come-playoffs/', 'snippet': 'Eric Bledsoe’s shooting percentage and assists are down, and his turnovers are up, after a hot start in which he was seen as an early contender for most improved player.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the most entertaining stories of the first 20 games of this season was the Clippers backup guard Eric Bledsoe. Not only were his statistics astounding — he held the second highest Player Efficiency Rating among point guards at 24.4 through Dec. 14 (only his teammate Chris Paul had a higher PER) — but he was also a thrill to watch. You did not want to miss any of Bledsoe’s 18 minutes a night because each moment held the potential for one of the fantastically athletic plays which only he was capable of making. Bledsoe seemed primed to fulfill a crucial role on a very strong team.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bledsoe Cools, but Clippers Stay Hot for Now', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bledsoe, Eric', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Clippers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-03T20:18:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Beckley Mason', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Beckley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mason', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2cca8efc-b633-5184-8b7d-e159f8d1249e', 'word_count': 551, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2cca8efc-b633-5184-8b7d-e159f8d1249e'}, {'abstract': 'Lez Zeppelin, a Led Zeppelin tribute band, will play at First Saturdays at the Brooklyn Museum, while the dance ensemble Saung Budaya will perform works from Indonesia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/04/nyregion/in-weekend-miser-lez-zeppelin-and-saung-budaya.html', 'snippet': 'Lez Zeppelin, a Led Zeppelin tribute band, will play at First Saturdays at the Brooklyn Museum, while the dance ensemble Saung Budaya will perform works from Indonesia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Led Zeppelin has been enjoying quite the victory lap lately, being lauded at the 35th Kennedy Center Honors last month and releasing a concert film of its triumphant 2007 reunion in the fall.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lez Zeppelin at the Brooklyn Museum', 'kicker': 'Weekend Miser', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Museum', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-03T20:22:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By A. C. Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/66180e70-d502-530f-9e9b-f95ccce2b789', 'word_count': 403, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66180e70-d502-530f-9e9b-f95ccce2b789'}, {'abstract': 'By working out with kettlebells, cast-iron weights with handles, some exercisers are able to meet their fitness goals in a few hours a week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/04/nyregion/kettlebell-fitness-classes-in-manhattan.html', 'snippet': 'By working out with kettlebells, cast-iron weights with handles, some exercisers are able to meet their fitness goals in a few hours a week.', 'lea