ct', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fitness Cell Collective', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-03T20:32:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shivani Vora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shivani', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fe175d1-5f51-55a2-b3a1-57d316e83611', 'word_count': 517, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fe175d1-5f51-55a2-b3a1-57d316e83611'}, {'abstract': 'This and that on an off day.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/03/short-takes/', 'snippet': 'This and that on an off day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sorry about the failure to post anything earlier. It was a combination of family responsibilities and, to be frank, sheer weariness over the folly of our public life. And I really don’t feel up to any extended discussion even now. Instead, just a few short takes on things that caught my eye:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Short Takes', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-03T20:36:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a1f8b10-7751-518c-81f3-559a3ece285e', 'word_count': 338, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a1f8b10-7751-518c-81f3-559a3ece285e'}, {'abstract': 'Gotham Extra: After Gov. Chris Christie of New Jersey lashed Republicans for blocking a measure to provide storm aid, his national prospects could prove tenuous.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/03/christie-takes-a-swing-at-his-party-possibly-hurting-his-political-future/', 'snippet': 'Gotham Extra: After Gov. Chris Christie of New Jersey lashed Republicans for blocking a measure to provide storm aid, his national prospects could prove tenuous.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Chris Christie admirably threw himself upon the shoals of national Republican Party politics this week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Christie Takes a Swing at His Party, Possibly Hurting His Political Future', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-03T20:40:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Powell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Powell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a8d300d-7c8c-59cc-ab93-49aa24dfc7e3', 'word_count': 1001, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a8d300d-7c8c-59cc-ab93-49aa24dfc7e3'}, {'abstract': 'The Japanese artist’s first solo exhibition in New York is now on view in Williamsburg, Brooklyn.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/03/aki-sasamotos-lines-of-reasoning/', 'snippet': 'The Japanese artist’s first solo exhibition in New York is now on view in Williamsburg, Brooklyn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Aki Sasamoto sees the world, an object is never merely its humble self. It may be, as the artist has written, her grandmother, who became a kimono belt after her death. Or her music teacher, who became a wig worn after chemotherapy. In other words, objects exist within a web of associations and relationships that are utterly personal, but also — at times — bewilderingly universal. Sasamoto, whose work was included in the 2010 Whitney Biennial, makes these connections visible through networks of cords and cables that demarcate lines across spaces and between repeated motifs like lemons and doughnuts. In her performances, she frequently wields a thick marker to draw whirlwind diagrams of coincidence or alliances, as if she were an unusually aggressive math teacher (the field in which she began her studies). The relentless pace of her narration is matched in her nimble and mercurial movements; her installations often act as room-size jungle gyms, from which she effortlessly folds, wraps or dangles her body, navigating around her audience.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Aki Sasamoto’s Lines of Reasoning', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Artist Is In', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-03T21:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lumi Tan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lumi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/59a0c3a2-e26e-576a-af6c-3032d4be98b0', 'word_count': 462, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59a0c3a2-e26e-576a-af6c-3032d4be98b0'}, {'abstract': 'A song for a terrible travel day.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/03/friday-night-music-the-head-and-the-heart/', 'snippet': 'A song for a terrible travel day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yes, I know that it’s only Thursday afternoon. But I’m off to dinner with friends now, and I have a nightmare travel day tomorrow — three different flight segments, almost 12 hours from first takeoff to final landing. So it’s now or never.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Friday Night Music: The Head and the Heart', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-03T21:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d4de1bc-7683-5af8-8c58-7c594c97b0f2', 'word_count': 101, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d4de1bc-7683-5af8-8c58-7c594c97b0f2'}, {'abstract': 'Northeast Republicans erupted in anger after a Hurricane Sandy relief bill stalled in the House.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/nyregion/100000001985632/backlash-after-stalled-sandy-bill.html', 'snippet': 'Northeast Republicans erupted in anger after a Hurricane Sandy relief bill stalled in the House.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Northeast Republicans erupted in anger after a Hurricane Sandy relief bill stalled in the House.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/03/nyregion/video-tc-pol-130103-sandy/video-tc-pol-130103-sandy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/03/nyregion/video-t