ia and Elsewhere', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-03T23:02:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1d76603-d262-5254-9803-57fa2c28b812', 'word_count': 14, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1d76603-d262-5254-9803-57fa2c28b812'}, {'abstract': 'A selected guide to classical music and opera performances in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/04/arts/music/classical-music-and-opera-listings-for-jan-4-10.html', 'snippet': 'A selected guide to classical music and opera performances in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Classical', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Classical Music and Opera Listings for Jan. 4-10', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Listings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-03T23:03:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9eeed24-a97b-5fa1-8bdf-0d81c5e58436', 'word_count': 1518, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9eeed24-a97b-5fa1-8bdf-0d81c5e58436'}, {'abstract': 'Led by the saxophonist Oscar Noriega, the quintet Background Music foraged through in the fluid catalog of Lennie Tristano at Barbès on Wednesday night.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/04/arts/music/background-music-at-barbes.html', 'snippet': 'Led by the saxophonist Oscar Noriega, the quintet Background Music foraged through in the fluid catalog of Lennie Tristano at Barbès on Wednesday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s still residual energy in the music of the pianist Lennie Tristano’s circle from the late 1940s and 1950s. The tunes are beautiful and charged: breezy on the surface but almost scarily focused within themselves, with their strange phrase lengths, metrical games over steady 4/4 time, long lines of straight eighth notes intermittently flicking into double time, harmonic elasticity, constant invention. They can easily be reimagined, because they were themselves reimaginings — of standards, of bebop phrasing, of what rhythm sections should do and not do. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/arts/04BARBES_SPAN/04BARBES_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/04/arts/04BARBES_SPAN/04BARBES_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/arts/04BARBES_SPAN/BARBES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/arts/04BARBES_SPAN/BARBES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/arts/04BARBES_SPAN/04BARBES_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/04/arts/04BARBES_SPAN/04BARBES_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/arts/04BARBES_SPAN/04BARBES_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Improvisational Cosmology, Vibrations Ever Expanding', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Improvisational Cosmology, Vibrations Ever Expanding', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-03T23:05:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Ratliff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ratliff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e74a4f19-a381-5f31-8a6e-afb7e0807e3c', 'word_count': 565, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e74a4f19-a381-5f31-8a6e-afb7e0807e3c'}, {'abstract': 'A selected guide to dance performances in the New York area.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/04/arts/dance/dance-listings-for-jan-4-10.html', 'snippet': 'A selected guide to dance performances in the New York area.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dance', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dance Listings for Jan. 4-10', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Listings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-03T23:07:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/bab2351b-22dd-588d-a627-65f8b4f43a22', 'word_count': 1302, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bab2351b-22dd-588d-a627-65f8b4f43a22'}, {'abstract': 'While John Cage’s centenary year is over, the pianist Conor Hanick gave a performance of Cage’s Sonatas and Interludes for Prepared Piano that was notable for its virtuosity and focus.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/04/arts/music/conor-hanick-performing-john-cage-at-the-stone.html', 'snippet': 'While John Cage’s centenary year is over, the pianist Conor Hanick gave a performance of Cage’s Sonatas and Interludes for Prepared Piano that was notable for its virtuosity and focus.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the joyous, overwhelmingly busy John Cage centenary celebrations of 2012 now at an end, adherents might worry that the musicians who trotted out all manner of Cage scores last year might be ready to shelve them now. It felt doubly fortunate, then, to encounter a performance of Cage’s seminal Sonatas and Interludes for Prepared Piano on Wednesday evening at the Stone, the spartan East Village music laboratory founded and maintained by the composer John Zorn: doubly not only because the account, by Conor Hanick, was a marvel of poetic concentration, but also because it was not even planned until a few days ago.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/arts/04STRING1_SPAN/04STRING1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/04/arts/04STRING1_SPAN/04STRING1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/arts/04STRING1_SPAN/STRING1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/arts/04STRING1_SPAN/STRING1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/arts/04STRING1_SPAN/04STRING1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/04/arts/04STRING1_SPAN/04STRING1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/arts/04STRING1_SPAN/04STRING1_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Last-Minute Performance Extends a Centenary', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Last-Minute Performance Extends a Centenary', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cage, John', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hanick, Conor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-03T23:09:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/605ed63e-980c-59bc-a984-04f3f3f65302', 'word_count': 488, 'uri': 'nyt://article/605ed63e-980c-59bc-a984-04f3f3f65302'}, {'abstract': 'The significance of Monteverdi’s 1610 Vespers was not lost in the Green Mountain Project’s Wednesday performance of the work at the Church of St. Mary the Virgin.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/04/arts/music/monteverdis-1610-vespers-at-the-church-of-st-mary-the-virgin.html', 'snippet': 'The significance of Monteverdi’s 1610 Vespers was not lost in the Green Mountain Project’s Wednesday performance of the work at the Church of St. Mary the Virgin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Green Mountain Project, an outgrowth of the New York-based early-music group Tenet, presented Monteverdi’s 1610 Vespers at the Church of St. Mary the Virgin in Times Square on Wednesday evening. It was the group’s third New Year’s performance of this work in four years. (Last year’s was dedicated to the 1640 Vespers.) And to judge from the capacity crowd and the enthusiastic reception, the tradition is taking root as a sequel to the glut of pre-Christmas “Messiah” performances.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Celebrating Monteverdi’s Vespers With Attention to 400-Year-old Details', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Celebrating Monteverdi’s Vespers With Attention to 400-Year-old Details', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'da Fonseca-Wollheim, Corinna', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Green Mountain Project', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-03T23:10:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Corinna da Fonseca-Wollheim', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd4a9e8b-159b-56fd-a4d7-cfcc98f64835', 'word_count': 536, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd4a9e8b-159b-56fd-a4d7-cfcc98f64835'}, {'abstract': 'Martin Sorrell, chief executive of the British advertising giant WPP, says he sees growth prospects in Latin America. The firm has taken a 20 percent stake in an information technology services company based in Argentina.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/01/03/seeing-opportunity-wpp-adds-to-its-investments-in-latin-america/', 'snippet': 'Martin Sorrell, chief executive of the British advertising giant WPP, says he sees growth prospects in Latin America. The firm has taken a 20 percent stake in an information technology services company based in Argentina.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Martin Sorrell, chief executive of the British advertising giant WPP, is not deterred by the political tension in Argentina or economic setbacks in Brazil. Far from it: his firm is still investing in Latin America.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Seeing Opportunity, WPP Adds to Its Investments in Latin America', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Online Advertising', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sorrell, Martin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WPP Group Plc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-03T23:11:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vinod Sreeharsha', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vinod', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sreeharsha', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News',