atasuna, already illegal in Spain, announced Thursday that it would dissolve itself in France as well. The party was banned in Spain for its connections to the armed Basque separatist group ETA, for which it acted as its political wing. Two members of the party, Maite Goyenetxe and Jean Claude Aguerre, speaking in Bayonne, the center of the Basque region in France, announced the dissolution of Batasuna, but said they would continue to press for an independent Basque nation. In 2011, ETA announced that it had abandoned violence after a four-decade campaign for an independent homeland that claimed more than 800 lives. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France: Basque Party to Disband', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France: Basque Party to Disband', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Erlanger, Steven', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basques', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Batasuna', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ETA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-04T00:42:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Erlanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erlanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a6e1b6d-93d9-54a9-b64f-dd7181f95e5e', 'word_count': 107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a6e1b6d-93d9-54a9-b64f-dd7181f95e5e'}, {'abstract': 'A 2011 bill required Texas law enforcement agencies to report the number of untested rape evidence kits on their shelves. The next question is how to pay to get all of that testing done.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/04/us/hefty-cost-to-testing-texas-huge-backlog-of-rape-evidence-kits.html', 'snippet': 'A 2011 bill required Texas law enforcement agencies to report the number of untested rape evidence kits on their shelves. The next question is how to pay to get all of that testing done.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are some 20,000 untested rape kits sitting on evidence shelves in police departments across Texas, the state Department of Public Safety estimates. Each box with samples of hair, skin and clothing represents one of the worst moments of the victim’s life, a crime that was followed by hours in a doctor’s office submitting the most personal evidence.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/us/04ttrapekits/04ttrapekits-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/04/us/04ttrapekits/04ttrapekits-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/us/04ttrapekits/04ttrapekits-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 642, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/us/04ttrapekits/04ttrapekits-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1283, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Testing State’s Huge Backlog of Rape Evidence Kits Comes With Hefty Price Tag', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Testing State’s Huge Backlog of Rape Evidence Kits Comes With Hefty Price Tag', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forensic Science', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Wendy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DNA (Deoxyribonucleic Acid)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-04T00:43:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brandi Grissom', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brandi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grissom', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c783ede-17bf-576f-972b-bfc4eafb3336', 'word_count': 626, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c783ede-17bf-576f-972b-bfc4eafb3336'}, {'abstract': 'For nuclear talks with Iran, President Obama should learn two Persian words: maslahat and aberu.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/04/opinion/how-to-talk-to-iran.html', 'snippet': 'For nuclear talks with Iran, President Obama should learn two Persian words: maslahat and aberu.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IF there are any two words in Persian that President Obama should learn, they are “maslahat” and “aberu.” Maslahat is often translated as expediency, or self-interest. Aberu means face — as in, saving face. In the nearly 34 years since the Islamic revolution in Iran, expediency has been a pillar of decision making, but within a framework that has allowed Iranian leaders to save face. If there is to be any resolution of the nuclear standoff, Western leaders must grasp these concepts. \xa0', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Talk to Iran', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributors', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How to Talk to Iran', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': 