e made available to defense lawyers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOUNT OLIVE, W.Va. — Convicted of robbing and raping an 83-year-old woman, Joseph A. Buffey at 19 was no one’s idea of a choirboy. A marijuana smoker and high school dropout, he was out thieving on the night in question 11 years ago and broke into the Salvation Army near the woman’s home to steal the bell-ringing money.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/us/JP-WESTVIRGINIA-1/JP-WESTVIRGINIA-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 725, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/us/JP-WESTVIRGINIA-1/JP-WESTVIRGINIA-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1104, 'width': 782, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/us/JP-WESTVIRGINIA-1/JP-WESTVIRGINIA-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lawyers, Saying DNA Cleared Inmate, Pursue Access to Data', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lawyers, Saying DNA Cleared Inmate, Pursue Access to Data', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bronner, Ethan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forensic Science', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'False Arrests, Convictions and Imprisonments', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DNA (Deoxyribonucleic Acid)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Virginia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Buffey, Joseph A', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-04T02:15:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ethan Bronner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ethan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bronner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/82d7a0d6-a689-541d-b3a3-dd94fe80faf4', 'word_count': 1393, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82d7a0d6-a689-541d-b3a3-dd94fe80faf4'}, {'abstract': 'Former Gov. Bill Richardson of New Mexico and Google’s executive chairman, Eric E. Schmidt, were advised against a visit to the country, though an expert says it might aid in the discussion of a detained American citizen.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/04/world/asia/bill-richardson-and-googles-eric-schmidt-are-advised-not-to-visit-north-korea.html', 'snippet': 'Former Gov. Bill Richardson of New Mexico and Google’s executive chairman, Eric E. Schmidt, were advised against a visit to the country, though an expert says it might aid in the discussion of a detained American citizen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The State Department said Thursday that it had advised against a visit to North Korea by the former governor of New Mexico, Bill Richardson, and Google’s executive chairman, Eric E. Schmidt. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '2 Americans Are Advised Not to Visit North Korea', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '2 Americans Are Advised Not to Visit North Korea', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Richardson, Bill', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gordon, Michael R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schmidt, Eric E', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bae, Kenneth', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-04T02:22:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael R. Gordon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Gordon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bdaf8469-b2f2-5fd7-a5e6-f316a760b3dc', 'word_count': 445, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bdaf8469-b2f2-5fd7-a5e6-f316a760b3dc'}, {'abstract': 'Doubts about the independence of Al Jazeera do not justify removing it from cable and satellite systems.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/04/opinion/al-jazeera-in-america.html', 'snippet': 'Doubts about the independence of Al Jazeera do not justify removing it from cable and satellite systems.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Al Jazeera, the pan-Arab news network, has long wanted to gain a bigger American television audience, and it may have finally found a way to do that by buying Current TV. But as the deal was being signed, Time Warner Cable announced it would immediately stop carrying Current, a struggling channel partly owned by former Vice President Al Gore. While the cable company has the legal right to cut off Current, the decision is unfortunate and could block access to an important news source.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Al Jazeera in America', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Al Jazeera in America', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL JAZEERA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Current TV', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Time Warner Cable Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Qatar', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-04T02:23:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/97bbcd47-fcfc-5720-8bdb-efa37e70d70d', 'word_count': 498, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97bbcd47-fcfc-5720-8bdb-efa37e70d70d'}, {'abstract': 'Five weeks ago, Coach Gregg Popovich was fined for sitting his top players for the Spurs’ fourth game in five days. Against the Knicks, after a similar stretch, Popovich opted to keep his lineup intact.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/04/sports/basketball/after-long-stretch-of-games-spurs-stars-dont-get-a-night-off.html', 'snippet': 'Five weeks ago, Coach Gregg Popovich was fined for sitting his top players for the Spurs’ fourth game in five days. Against the Knicks, after a similar stretch, Popovich opted to keep his lineup intact.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The San Antonio Spurs arrived in New York at 2 a.m. Thursday after playing in Milwaukee on Wednesday night. They had played Sunday and Monday as well. That left Coach Gregg Popovich in a familiar predicament.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/sports/y-spurs/y-spurs-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 344, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/04/sports/y-spurs/y-spurs-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 344}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/sports/y-spurs/y-spurs-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 588, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/sports/y-spurs/y-spurs-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1176, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/sports/y-spurs/y-spurs-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/04/sports/y-spurs/y-spurs-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/sports/y-spurs/y-spurs-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Spurs’ Stars Play, but Sit by the End', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spurs’ Stars Play, but Sit By the End', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Antonio Spurs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Popovich, Gregg', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-04T02:24:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zach Schonbrun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zach', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schonbrun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a141e80-5732-5339-a240-2af6776c3b90', 'word_count': 625, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a141e80-5732-5339-a240-2af6776c3b90'}, {'abstract': 'Al Gore used the same arm-twisting he employed to build up Current TV to persuade cable distributors to keep showing it after it was sold to Al Jazeera.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/03/gore-went-to-bat-for-al-jazeera-and-himself/', 'snippet': 'Al Gore used the same arm-twisting he employed to build up Current TV to persuade cable distributors to keep showing it after it was sold to Al Jazeera.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Al Gore’s Current TV was never popular with viewers, but it was a hit where it counted: with cable and satellite providers. When he co-founded the channel in 2005, Mr. Gore managed to get the channel piped into tens of millions of households — a huge number for an untested network — through a combination of personal lobbying and arm-twisting of industry giants.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gore Went to Bat for Al Jazeera, and Himself', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gore Went to Bat for Al Jazeera, and Himself', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beck, Glenn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gore, Al', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hyatt, Joel Z', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL JAZEERA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Current TV', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'DirecTV', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News Corporation', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-04T02:24:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c289130-9793-5939-8a67-39671e9d2743', 'word_count': 1071, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c289130-9793-5939-8a67-39671e9d2743'}, {'abstract': 'The first day of the 113th Congress brought a new diversity to the Capitol, including a record number of women and various firsts for the numbers of Latinos and Asians.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/04/us/first-day-of-113th-congress-brings-more-women-to-capitol.html', 'snippet': 'The first day of the 113th Congress brought a new diversity to the Capitol, including a record number of women and various firsts for the numbers of Latinos and Asians.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — As the 113th Congress opens, the Senate and the House are starting to look a little bit more like the people they represent.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/us/SCENE/SCENE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 293, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/04/us/SCENE/SCENE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 293}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/us/SCENE/SCENE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 499, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None,