m California to Hawaii, totally alone and unsupported.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For much of last year, kayaking enthusiasts around the world were keeping tabs on Wave Vidmar, who said he was planning to kayak from California to Hawaii — totally alone and unsupported. The 48-year-old Mr. Vidmar expected the journey over the rolling Pacific Ocean would take between 45 and 65 days. And the 3,100-mile odyssey would rank among the longest of its kind, if successful.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/14/arts/14iht-athlete14-pic1/14iht-athlete14-pic1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/07/14/arts/14iht-athlete14-pic1/14iht-athlete14-pic1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/14/arts/14iht-athlete14-pic1/14iht-athlete14-pic1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/14/arts/14iht-athlete14-pic1/14iht-athlete14-pic1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1356, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/14/arts/14iht-athlete14-pic1/14iht-athlete14-pic1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/07/14/arts/14iht-athlete14-pic1/14iht-athlete14-pic1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/14/arts/14iht-athlete14-