down.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/04/tom-coughlin-chip-kelly-and-moneyball-football/', 'snippet': 'Some of what we’re reading this morning: The agony of the Giants’ coach, possible landing spots for Oregon’s coach and the value of statistical analysis in football.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Morning links for your consideration, a day before wild-card weekend opens:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tom Coughlin, Chip Kelly and ‘Moneyball’ Football', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coughlin, Tom', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelly, Chip', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-04T12:45:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4308e93-0ffb-5440-9c7f-fee91d4e0606', 'word_count': 607, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4308e93-0ffb-5440-9c7f-fee91d4e0606'}, {'abstract': 'Malala Yousafzai, the 15-year-old Pakistani schoolgirl who survived an assassination attempt by Taliban militants, was discharged from a hospital in Birmingham, England, on Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/04/malala-yousafzai-discharged-from-hospital/', 'snippet': 'Malala Yousafzai, the 15-year-old Pakistani schoolgirl who survived an assassination attempt by Taliban militants, was discharged from a hospital in Birmingham, England, on Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Malala Yousafzai, the 15-year-old Pakistani schoolgirl who survived an assassination attempt by Taliban militants, was discharged from Queen Elizabeth Hospital in Birmingham, England, on Thursday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Malala Yousafzai Discharged From Hospital', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yousafzai, Malala', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'England', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-04T12:50:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d79bf0e-e7e1-5f12-97a5-d0f61a7e230c', 'word_count': 255, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d79bf0e-e7e1-5f12-97a5-d0f61a7e230c'}, {'abstract': 'A straightforward spot demonstrating the capacity of a French-door refrigerator from Samsung received the highest score for any of the almost 6,000 commercials that Ace Metrix evaluated last year.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/04/top-commercial-for-2012-was-really-big-ace-metrix-says/', 'snippet': 'A straightforward spot demonstrating the capacity of a French-door refrigerator from Samsung received the highest score for any of the almost 6,000 commercials that Ace Metrix evaluated last year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The commercial that received the highest average score last year from viewers of national television ads in a closely followed survey was not a glitzy Super Bowl spot or an emotional Olympics spot. Nor was it a commercial that was sexy, snarky or stuffed with celebrities.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Top Commercial for 2012 Was Really ‘Big,’ Ace Metrix Says', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-04T13:00:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d82e760-55b0-59d4-838f-728a053ec36f', 'word_count': 479, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d82e760-55b0-59d4-838f-728a053ec36f'}, {'abstract': 'Twelve House Republicans did not vote for John A. Boehner’s re-election as speaker. Is that really so bad? Judging by recent history, it is.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/04/were-the-g-o-p-votes-against-boehner-a-historic-rejection/', 'snippet': 'Twelve House Republicans did not vote for John A. Boehner’s re-election as speaker. Is that really so bad? Judging by recent history, it is.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The holiday season hasn’t been kind to House Speaker John A. Boehner. He was sharply criticized by fellow Republicans for failing to pass legislation providing aid to those affected by Hurricane Sandy. Earlier, he was sidelined in the negotiations to resolve the so-called fiscal cliff. And before that, he failed to garner enough support from his own caucus for “Plan B,” Mr. Boehner’s own bill to avert the fiscal crisis.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Were the G.O.P. Votes Against Boehner a Historic Rejection?', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Small but Significant Number of Defections in the Vote on Boehner as Speaker', 'name': None, 'seo'