o be appointed as an interim senator to fill John Kerry’s seat until a special election later this year.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/04/barney-frank-seeks-short-stint-in-senate/', 'snippet': 'Barney Frank would like to be appointed as an interim senator to fill John Kerry’s seat until a special election later this year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Barney Frank is finding it hard to say goodbye to Congress.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Barney Frank Seeks Short Stint in Senate', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-04T13:55:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By John H. Cushman Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'H.', 'lastname': 'Cushman', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1e7493a-d609-50f9-b44e-baeb19b791fc', 'word_count': 196, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1e7493a-d609-50f9-b44e-baeb19b791fc'}, {'abstract': 'An anonymous donor gives $500,000, and the Andrew W. Mellon Foundation gives $100,000 as the museum seeks help from damaged caused by the hurricane.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/04/a-life-raft-for-seaport-museum-500000-gift/', 'snippet': 'An anonymous donor gives $500,000, and the Andrew W. Mellon Foundation gives $100,000 as the museum seeks help from damaged caused by the hurricane.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Having called out for help after Hurricane Sandy, the South Street Seaport Museum has received $500,000 from an anonymous donor and $100,000 from the Andrew W. Mellon Foundation. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Life Raft for Seaport Museum: $500,000 Gift', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A $500,000 Gift For Seaport Museum', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Susan Henshaw', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mellon Foundation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum of the City of New York', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'South Street Seaport Museum', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-04T14:04:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Pogrebin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogrebin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b5ba452-b77d-5067-a0f6-5c3e25f80a78', 'word_count': 128, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b5ba452-b77d-5067-a0f6-5c3e25f80a78'}, {'abstract': 'The Federal Trade Commission exonerated Google from accusations that it violated antitrust statutes, and Al Gore used his considerable negotiating skills to smooth the way for the sale of Current TV to Al Jazeera.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/04/breakfast-meeting-victories-for-gore-and-google-but-not-barnes-noble/', 'snippet': 'The Federal Trade Commission exonerated Google from accusations that it violated antitrust statutes, and Al Gore used his considerable negotiating skills to smooth the way for the sale of Current TV to Al Jazeera.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Al Gore used his considerable lobbying and negotiating skills when he started Current TV in 2005, and he used them again last month in arranging the sale of the channel to Al Jazeera, Brian Stelter reports on Friday in The New York Times. He used persuasive legal arguments with cable and satellite providers to convince them that Al Jazeera, like Current, offered news content and that they were obligated to carry the new channel run by the Middle Eastern news organization. In the process, Mr. Gore, already estimated to be worth about $100 million, assured himself some $100 million more from the sale. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Breakfast Meeting: Victories for Gore and Google, but Not Barnes & Noble', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antitrust Laws and Competition Issues', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gore, Al', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL JAZEERA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Barnes & Noble Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Current TV', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-04T14:06:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Brink', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brink', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5177d0f-e5fc-506b-9691-6de478d561b9', 'word_count': 225, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5177d0f-e5fc-506b-9691-6de478d561b9'}, {'abstract': 'It appears that the past four years had a net gain of just 28,000 jobs. Private-sector jobs were up, but government employment was down.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/04/four-years-later-28000-more-jobs/', 'snippet': 'It appears that the past four years had a net gain of just 28,000 jobs. Private-sector jobs were up, but government employment was down.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For jobs, the past four years have been a wash.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Four Years Later, 28,000 More Jobs', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bureau of Labor Statistics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-04T14:16:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Floyd Norris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Norris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/11973888-ea9c-58ca-8079-1b7a7f9e6c3a', 'word_count': 325, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11973888-ea9c-58ca-8079-1b7a7f9e6c3a'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/04/what-were-reading-600/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Elizabeth Minchilli in Rome: Don’t be afraid of cardoons. — Jeff Gordinier ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-04T14:27:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Time