', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicia R. Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicia', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb2e9709-4932-5f03-af12-a363a5beb3f9', 'word_count': 989, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb2e9709-4932-5f03-af12-a363a5beb3f9'}, {'abstract': 'A new promo shows the Golden Globes hosts at the top of their game, or someone’s game.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/04/tina-fey-and-amy-poeher-know-its-avatars-year/', 'snippet': 'A new promo shows the Golden Globes hosts at the top of their game, or someone’s game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Celebrity interviewers, time to step your game up. Tina Fey and Amy Poehler, hosts of the Golden Globes on Jan. 13 and everyone’s favorite ladies of all time – or maybe just ours – have released a video of themselves answering the usual kind of questions they’ll get as they prepare for the ceremony.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tina Fey and Amy Poehler Know: It’s ‘Avatar’s’ Year', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golden Globes (Awards)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fey, Tina', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Poehler, Amy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-04T15:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d04de86-54ae-5edb-bac6-d93372a04b73', 'word_count': 134, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d04de86-54ae-5edb-bac6-d93372a04b73'}, {'abstract': 'Oregon fans chanted, “We want Chip,” after Chip Kelly’s Ducks won the Fiesta Bowl, but N.F.L. teams are also interested.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/05/sports/everyone-wants-oregon-coach-chip-kelly-leading-off.html', 'snippet': 'Oregon fans chanted, “We want Chip,” after Chip Kelly’s Ducks won the Fiesta Bowl, but N.F.L. teams are also interested.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Now that Oregon has won its Fiesta Bowl game, everyone’s retinas have recovered from encountering the Ducks’ latest uniform and the crowd in Arizona has finally stopped chanting, “We want Chip,” the frenzy can truly begin. In fact, by the time you finish Leading Off, Ducks Coach Chip Kelly might have been hired by the Eagles. Or the Browns. Or the Bills. Even the Chiefs might stop their fire-breathing pursuit of Andy Reid and hire Kelly instead. Listen hard enough and you may even hear that the Lakers believe he can bring out the best in Kobe Bryant. Yes, Kelly is hot, eyebrow-searing hot.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/sports/ncaafootball/04leading1/04leading1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/sports/ncaafootball/04leading1/04leading1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/sports/ncaafootball/04leading1/04leading1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/