ization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ba8358f-2928-5ec2-aee1-eccdd8ef6f92', 'word_count': 1495, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ba8358f-2928-5ec2-aee1-eccdd8ef6f92'}, {'abstract': 'New controversies erupt over are reactions to “Les Miz,” “Django Unchained” and even whether controversy helps or hurts an Oscar campaign.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/04/debating-films-audiences-epithets-and-even-debate-itself/', 'snippet': 'New controversies erupt over are reactions to “Les Miz,” “Django Unchained” and even whether controversy helps or hurts an Oscar campaign.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From trembling uvulas to spewing epithets, this awards season has not been without controversy. (It’s not every day that the Senate Intelligence Committee gets into the Oscar game.) At The New Yorker, David Denby shares some thoughts on “Les Miz.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Debating Films, Audiences, Epithets and Even Debate Itself', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-04T16:30:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a3f3e77-722d-51c2-9767-fff36fc619e2', 'word_count': 444, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a3f3e77-722d-51c2-9767-fff36fc619e2'}, {'abstract': 'Under a proposal, the Food and Drug Administration would shift from taking action after contamination occurred to requiring measures to prevent it in the first place.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/05/business/fda-offers-rules-to-stop-food-contamination.html', 'snippet': 'Under a proposal, the Food and Drug Administration would shift from taking action after contamination occurred to requiring measures to prevent it in the first place.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Food and Drug Administration on Friday proposed two sweeping rules aimed at preventing the contamination of produce and processed foods, which has sickened tens of thousands of Americans annually in recent years. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/05/business/Food/Food-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 701, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/05/business/Food/Food-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1401, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'F.D.A. Offers Broad New Rules to Fight Food Contamination', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'F.D.A. Proposes Broad New Rules On Food Safety', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strom, Stephanie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Contamination and Poisoning', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taylor, Michael R', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-04T16:34:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Strom', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Strom', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f127ee3-b50c-5ee3-93e0-abd22cb8cfe3', 'word_count': 1203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f127ee3-b50c-5ee3-93e0-abd22cb8cfe3'}, {'abstract': 'A onetime leader of the anti-GMO movement now embraces that technology as a planet saver.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/04/new-shade-of-green-stark-shift-for-onetime-foe-of-genetic-engineering-in-crops/', 'snippet': 'A onetime leader of the anti-GMO movement now embraces that technology as a planet saver.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In case you missed the coverage and commentary yesterday (the Twitter flow is here), you can now watch Mark Lynas, the British writer and environmentalist who once helped drive Europe’s movement against genetically engineered crops, apologize for those actions and embrace this technology as a vital tool for ending hunger and conserving the environment. He spoke yesterday at the\xa0Oxford Farming Conference\xa0at Oxford University. (Many other fascinating presentations are now online.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Shade of Green: Stark Shift for Onetime Foe of Genetic Engineering in Crops', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biotechnology', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetic Engineering', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetics and Heredity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organic Foods and Products', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Population', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sustainable Living', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kloor, Keith', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lomborg, Bjorn', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Monsanto Company', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oxford (England)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-04T16:40:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/811513e8-6427-52b6-9efc-c289deea3e4a', 'word_count': 1420, 'uri': 'nyt://article/811513e8-6427-52b6-9efc-c289deea3e4a'}, {'abstract': 'A look at the relationship between dogs and people.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/06/books/review/whats-a-dog-for-by-john-homans.html', 'snippet': 'A look at the relationship between dogs and people.', 'lead_paragraph': '“We wanted another family member, someone to fill out the cast, a supporting actress,” John Homans, the executive editor at New York magazine, writes in his engaging and informative book that is both a survey of the latest research on canine cognition and a memoir of his years with his Lab mix, Stella. As a puppy, Stella found her way from Tennessee to an animal shelter near New York City. Even at 12 weeks old and locked in a cage, she seemed “self-possessed, happy for attention but not demanding it,” the author recalls. The Homans family took to her immediately and adopted her to be a companion for their soon-to-be 10-year-old son — thereby bringing the comedic and mysterious presence of canine intelligence into their lives. ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image',