 is the host.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2013/01/04/books/review/06books_pod.html', 'snippet': 'This week, John Homans talks about “What’s a Dog For?”; Leslie Kaufman has notes from the field; Allan Kozinn discusses Kurt Weill and Lotte Lenya; and Gregory Cowles has best-seller news. Sam Tanenhaus is the host.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week, John Homans talks about “What’s a Dog For?”; Leslie Kaufman has notes from the field; Allan Kozinn discusses Kurt Weill and Lotte Lenya; and Gregory Cowles has best-seller news. Sam Tanenhaus is the host.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Book Review Podcast', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Podcasts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-04T17:05:42+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/4a181381-9938-5566-9605-9ca294f19ce1', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/4a181381-9938-5566-9605-9ca294f19ce1'}, {'abstract': 'Isabel Wilkerson’s history of the Great Migration, “The Warmth of Other Suns,” was published only two years ago, but it shows every indication of becoming a classic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/06/books/review/up-front.html', 'snippet': 'Isabel Wilkerson’s history of the Great Migration, “The Warmth of Other Suns,” was published only two years ago, but it shows every indication of becoming a classic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Isabel Wilkerson’s history of the Great Migration, “The Warmth of Other Suns,” was published only two years ago, but it shows every indication of becoming a classic, winning a National Book Critics Circle Award and receiving numerous Best Book citations from such sources as Newsday, The New York Times and The New Yorker. This week, Wilkerson reviews the first novel by Ayana Mathis, “The Twelve Tribes of Hattie,” which traces the fortunes of a woman and her children after she left Jim Crow Georgia for Philadelphia in the 1920s.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/books/review/0106-Upfront/0106-Upfront-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 630, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/books/review/0106-Upfront/0106-Upfront-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1260, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Up Front', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Up Front', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-04T17:06:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editors', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editors'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/96c72487-7558-5d9b-89cb-284ae001f574', 'word_count': 272, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96c72487-7558-5d9b-89cb-284ae001f574'}, {'abstract': 'The hit series is popular all over the world.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/arts/100000001986979/downton-in-french.html', 'snippet': 'The hit series is popular all over the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The hit series is popular all over the world.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/multimedia/video-down-french/video-down-french-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/04/multimedia/video-down-french/video-down-french-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/multimedia/video-down-french/video-down-french-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/04/multimedia/video-down-french/video-down-french-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': "'Downton' in French", 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-04T17:06:58+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'NBCU', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nbcu', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/33554b6f-b052-527e-9842-7f53e3f6bf70', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/33554b6f-b052-527e-9842-7f53e3f6bf70'}, {'abstract': 'Thirty years ago on the best-seller list, James Michener’s “Space” was one of several books grappling with the final frontier.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/13/books/review/inside-the-list.html', 'snippet': 'Thirty years ago on the best-seller list, James Michener’s “Space” was one of several books grappling with the final frontier.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE FINAL FRONTIER: Thirty years ago this week, outer space was the dominant theme on the hardcover fiction list. All four of the top sellers kept an eye on the stars — or, in the case of James Michener (inset), the moon — and a fifth space novel, Douglas Adams’s “Life, the Universe and Everything,” also touched down in the top 10. The nonfiction list was moony in its own way, with books by Leo Buscaglia and Helen Gurley Brown, but probably the most notable title was Robert A. Caro’s “Path to Power: The Years of Lyndon Johnson,” described here as “the first 33 years of the life of the 36th president.” Three decades later, Caro’s life of Johnson is rivaling Boswell’s in its magisterial sweep, and still going strong. Here are the complete lists for Jan. 9, 1983:', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/books/review/13list-img/13list-img-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 275, 'width': 270, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/books/review/13list-img/13list-img-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 275, 'width': 270, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/books/review/13list-img/13list-img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/13/books/review/13list-img/13list-img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/books/review/13list-img/13list-img-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside the List', 'kicker': 'Tbr', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Inside the List', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '