}, {'abstract': 'Thom Andersen’s film “Reconversão,” coming to the Museum of the Moving Image’s First Look series, examines buildings by the Portuguese architect Eduardo Souto de Moura.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/06/movies/thom-andersens-reconversao-at-the-first-look-series.html', 'snippet': 'Thom Andersen’s film “Reconversão,” coming to the Museum of the Moving Image’s First Look series, examines buildings by the Portuguese architect Eduardo Souto de Moura.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOR the Portuguese architect Eduardo Souto de Moura, the 2011 winner of the Pritzker Prize for architecture, there are two potential responses to the presence of a ruin in a landscape. The first is the default Romantic expression of bittersweet wonder. The second, and more intriguing, is to ask: “What can I do here? What does this suggest to me that I am able to build?” Mr. Souto de Moura is the subject of “Reconversão,” a new film by the Los Angeles filmmaker Thom Andersen, who could be the architect’s cinematic doppelgänger.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/arts/06ANDERSEN_395/06ANDERSON1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/arts/06ANDERSEN_395/06ANDERSON1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1080, 'width': 1920, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/arts/06ANDERSEN_395/06ANDERSON2_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/06/arts/06ANDERSEN_395/06ANDERSON2_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, '