tle': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Habib', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zahori', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e42ae8dd-ab43-525a-a27e-bb21913d044b', 'word_count': 989, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e42ae8dd-ab43-525a-a27e-bb21913d044b'}, {'abstract': 'Though this was the first the eponymous host wasn’t part of “Dick Clark’s New Year’s Rockin’ Eve,” viewers flocked to the countdown special.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/04/record-ratings-for-new-years-rockin-eve/', 'snippet': 'Though this was the first the eponymous host wasn’t part of “Dick Clark’s New Year’s Rockin’ Eve,” viewers flocked to the countdown special.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Television viewers and party hosts have been given more programming options on New Year’s Eve in recent times, but on Monday night most of them still chose to ring in the new year with an old, reliable standby: “Dick Clark’s New Year’s Rockin’ Eve With Ryan Seacrest” on ABC. According to Nielsen, that countdown special attracted its largest prime-time audience ever – with 13.3 million total viewers tuning in during the 10 p.m. hour – and its highest rating in the 18-to-49-year-old demographic in 12 years. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Record Ratings for ‘New Year’s Rockin’ Eve’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clark, Dick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Seacrest, Ryan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-04T19:22:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6fa29795-bb76-582a-b887-29a6723b2c64', 'word_count': 176, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6fa29795-bb76-582a-b887-29a6723b2c64'}, {'abstract': 'The Writers Guild of America releases its nominations, giving momentum to “Zero Dark Thirty” and “Moonrise Kingdom.”', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/04/writers-guild-gives-flight-looper-and-master-a-little-help/', 'snippet': 'The Writers Guild of America releases its nominations, giving momentum to “Zero Dark Thirty” and “Moonrise Kingdom.”', 'lead_paragraph': '3:48 p.m. | Updated  If anybody appreciates the power of revision, it’s the members of the Writers Guild, which today announced its screenplay nominations, a day after they were originally due. In the original category, the guild selected John Gatins for “Flight,” Rian Johnson for “Looper,” Paul Thomas Anderson for “The Master,” Wes Anderson and Roman Coppola for “Moonrise Kingdom,” and Mark Boal for “Zero Dark Thirty.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Writers Guild Gives ‘Flight,’ ‘Looper’ and ‘Master’ a Little Help', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Film Nominations From Writers Guild', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Writers Guild of America', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-04T19:24:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material':