{'firstname': 'Glenn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eed0c542-72c7-54fd-b251-ef1c0e3bc368', 'word_count': 264, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eed0c542-72c7-54fd-b251-ef1c0e3bc368'}, {'abstract': 'An agreement with American authorities about antitrust laws is unlikely to sway European regulators, who are pursuing assertions that the company rigs results to favor its own businesses.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/05/technology/europe-likely-to-be-harder-on-google-over-search.html', 'snippet': 'An agreement with American authorities about antitrust laws is unlikely to sway European regulators, who are pursuing assertions that the company rigs results to favor its own businesses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — By some accounts, the United States let Google off the hook when it found that the technology giant had not abused its dominance in the Internet search market.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/05/technology/05google-webSUB/05google-webSUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 702, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/05/technology/05google-webSUB/05google-webSUB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1404, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/05/technology/05google-webSUB/05google-webSUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/05/technology/05google-webSUB/05google-w