t may be. Call it the real estate cure.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/06/realestate/relocation-therapy.html', 'snippet': 'There are events in life — a breakup, a death, an illness — that make a change of address good medicine, wrenching and expensive as it may be. Call it the real estate cure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALMOST four years ago, Marilyn Kotcher suddenly became a widow. And the large — 2,250-square-foot — condominium in Fort Lee, N.J., that she and her husband had bought together and lovingly remodeled no longer seemed like home.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/realestate/06COVER1_SPAN/06COVER1_SPAN-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/06/realestate/06COVER1_SPAN/06COVER1_SPAN-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 403}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/realestate/06COVER1_SPAN/06COVER1_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/realestate/06COVER1_SPAN/06COVER1_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1376, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/realestate/06COVER1_SPAN/06COVER1_SPAN-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/06/realestate/06COVER1_SPAN/06COVER1_SPAN-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/realestate/06COVER1_SPAN/06COVER1_SPAN-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Relocation Therapy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Relocation Therapy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Therapy and Rehabilitation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-04T20:46:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanne Kaufman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaufman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1f1ceaa-858e-5724-8a56-672d69c6e890', 'word_count': 1731, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1f1ceaa-858e-5724-8a56-672d69c6e890'}, {'abstract': 'When bloggers and readers of SBNation’s Posting & Toasting got together for the first time this season, their night was brightened by the Knicks’ victory over the Spurs.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/04/knicks-online-community-keeps-it-real-for-a-night/', 'snippet': 'When bloggers and readers of SBNation’s Posting & Toasting got together for the first time this season, their night was brightened by the Knicks’ victory over the Spurs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Full Circle is a congenially bonkers sports-and-beer bar on Grand Street in Williamsburg, Brooklyn, where the menu features 60 or so canned beers, 5 on draft, no bottles, a modest liquor selection, free soft pretzels and hot dogs, and nothing else. The house sport is brewskee ball — the bar is owned by the creators of the first national brewskee ball league, and the décor is given over entirely to brewskee paraphernalia — but on Thursday night Full Circle belonged to the Knicks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Knicks’ Online Community Keeps It Real for a Night', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-04T20:47:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brandon K. Thorp', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brandon', 'middlename': 'K.', 'lastname': 'Thorp', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c9a9614-8703-54d4-a1c0-266ee79a454b', 'word_count': 988, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c9a9614-8703-54d4-a1c0-266ee79a454b'}, {'abstract': 'I grew up in a duplex lined with old newspapers, videocassettes and a Tetris puzzle of cobwebbed credenzas. Determined to not to become my mother, I organized and cleaned fiercely — until I realized that the mess wasn’t the only part of my past that I didn’t want to repeat.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/04/a-hoarders-daughter-yields-to-a-little-mess/', 'snippet': 'I grew up in a duplex lined with old newspapers, videocassettes and a Tetris puzzle of cobwebbed credenzas. Determined to not to become my mother, I organized and cleaned fiercely — until I realized that the mess wasn’t the only part of my past th...', 'lead_paragraph': 'I grew up in a Montreal duplex lined with old newspapers, videocassettes and a Tetris puzzle of cobwebbed credenzas. My mother, born on my grandparents’ flight from Nazi-occupied Poland, had formative years filled with loss. She saved everything, but in doing so, created physical and emotional barriers between us. Her kitchen was not used for family meals, but to host fortresses of molding tuna cans and bags of insect-infested flour. The path to her bed was so covered with files and clothes that I could not reach her if I had a nightmare. I was an anxious child who feared intimacy. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Hoarder’s Daughter Yields to a (Little) Mess', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hoarding', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hygiene and Cleanliness', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-04T20:48:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judy Batalion', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Batalion', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/59e11395-3ecb-5832-b7ce-96871e6cc7e4', 'word_count': 860, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59e11395-3ecb-5832-b7ce-96871e6cc7e4'}, {'abstract': 'The new Accord is a remarkable return to form for Honda, both as bread-and-butter sedans and the dessert course of coupes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/06/automobiles/autoreviews/rarely-spotted-but-ready-for-flight.html', 'snippet': 'The new Accord is a remarkable return to form for Honda, both as bread-and-butter sedans and the dessert course of coupes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TESTED 2013 Honda Accord EX-L Coupe', 'print_section': 'AU', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'm