, 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d917bd04-197e-5118-96ec-40abba7441f7', 'word_count': 1239, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d917bd04-197e-5118-96ec-40abba7441f7'}, {'abstract': 'Jean S. Harris’s trial marked differences in attitudes between generations: some of us who watched it had disapproved of how our own mothers had handled their dependence on men.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/06/fashion/jean-harriss-cautionary-tale.html', 'snippet': 'Jean S. Harris’s trial marked differences in attitudes between generations: some of us who watched it had disapproved of how our own mothers had handled their dependence on men.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN I read that Jean S. Harris had died, I immediately texted my friend Anita in Seattle to ask if she’d heard. How to put this? Anita and I were Jean Harris groupies back in 1981, when the 57-year-old former Madeira School headmistress went on trial for shooting to death her philandering lover of 14 years, the 69-year-old cardiologist and Scarsdale Diet guru Herman Tarnower. We got up at dawn one cold winter morning the week Ms. Harris was on the stand and drove to the small White Plains courthouse hoping to get seats in the courtroom. We didn’t drive there in any official capacity. We were ordinary young New York working women. Divorced and never married, respectively. We were former English majors. We read. We knew a thing or two about bad love. We were in therapy. We were sixth in line. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/fashion/06REFLECTIONS/06REFLECTIONS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 758, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/fashion/06REFLECTIONS/06REFLECTIONS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1812, 'width': 1342, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/fashion/06REFLECTIONS/06REFLECTIONS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/06/fashion/06REFLECTIONS/06REFLECTIONS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/fashion/06REFLECTIONS/06REFLECTIONS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'No Longer a Cautionary Tale', 'kicker': 'Reflections', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Longer a Cautionary Tale', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harris, Jean S', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clayburgh, Jill', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Bette', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hearst, Patricia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trilling, Diana', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bates, Alan', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALEXANDER, SHANA', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Friedan, Betty', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'An Unmarried Woman (Movie)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Scarsdale (NY)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-04T21:45:24+0000