er than you can say Pandora. ', 'print_section': 'AU', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Digital Connections Will Increase as a Selling Point, Study Says', 'kicker': 'Technology', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Digital Connections Will Increase as a Selling Point, Study Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ford Motor Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Business Machines Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chevrolet Division of General Motors Corp', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mercedes-Benz', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-04T23:00:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Automobiles', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By John R. Quain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Quain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b023123d-6e39-531b-95b5-56cb252831eb', 'word_count': 558, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b023123d-6e39-531b-95b5-56cb252831eb'}, {'abstract': 'Peter Magistro, who runs a company that builds, renovates and manages affordable housing in the Bronx, details what’s good about living there — and what still needs work.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/06/realestate/debriefing-whats-great-about-living-in-the-bronx.html', 'snippet': 'Peter Magistro, who runs a company that builds, renovates and manages affordable housing in the Bronx, details what’s good about living there — and what still needs work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AS the founder and president of the Bronx Pro Group, a family-run, neighborhood-based company in Morris Park that builds, renovates and manages low- and moderate-income housing in the Bronx, Peter Magistro, 63, has seen the borough struggle and come back to life. A Bronx native and longtime resident who now lives on the Upper West Side, he has an intimate knowledge of local housing trends. He knows where the Bronx has been and where it’s headed. ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/realestate/06DEBRIEF_SPAN/06DEBRIEF_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 355, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/06/realestate/06DEBRIEF_SPAN/06DEBRIEF_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 355}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/realestate/06DEBRIEF_SPAN/debriefcircle-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/realestate/06DEBRIEF_SPAN/debriefcircle-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/realestate/06DEBRIEF_SPAN/06DEBRIEF_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/06/realestate/06DEBRIEF_SPAN/06DEBRIEF_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thu