eared to show fresh airstrikes near the historic medieval castle Krak des Chevaliers, in Qalaat al-Hosn, west of the city of Homs near the Lebanese border.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video Shows Airstrikes Near Crusader Castle in Syria', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-04T23:16:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a872437-fa87-595e-8448-e976d23a38e4', 'word_count': 200, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a872437-fa87-595e-8448-e976d23a38e4'}, {'abstract': 'A roundup of news from Afghanistan this week includes more revelations about insider killings and proposals for NATO’s exit in 2014.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/04/as-plans-for-afghan-exit-are-sketched-hope-turns-to-hatred/', 'snippet': 'A roundup of news from Afghanistan this week includes more revelations about insider killings and proposals for NATO’s exit in 2014.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many of the insider attacks for which the Taliban take responsibility actually start off as offers by enraged Afghan soldiers and police officers, Matthew Rosenberg reported in The Times on Thursday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Plans for Afghan Exit Are Sketched, Hope Turns to Hatred', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pentagon Building', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'St John, Allen', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-04T23:22:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/383e2db8-1af3-5599-b2a7-7a44a2d2626a', 'word_count': 421, 'uri': 'nyt://article/383e2db8-1af3-5599-b2a7-7a44a2d2626a'}, {'abstract': 'Top-ranked Victoria Azarenka pulled out of her Brisbane semifinal against Serena Williams, citing an infection in her right big toe.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/04/azarenka-withdraws-after-pedicure-injury/', 'snippet': 'Top-ranked Victoria Azarenka pulled out of her Brisbane semifinal against Serena Williams, citing an infection in her right big toe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The most anticipated match of the young 2013 season was called off on Friday, when top-ranked Victoria Azarenka pulled out of her Brisbane International semifinal against third-ranked Serena Williams, citing an infection in her right big toe. It would have been a rematch of the dramatic United States Open final between the two, which Williams won, 7-5, in the third set after Azarenka had served for the championship.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Azarenka Withdraws After Pedicure Injury', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Azarenka Withdraws', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-04T23:30:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By BEN ROTHENBERG', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'ROTHENBERG', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f13ed86-72f0-5a48-98ea-e54cb0bfd536', 'word_count': 617, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f13ed86-72f0-5a48-98ea-e54cb0bfd536'}, {'abstract': 'Alexandra Daddario, Scott Eastwood and Tremaine Neverson (a k a the singer Trey Songz) star in “Texas Chainsaw 3D,” the generic sixth installment of the horror series.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/05/movies/texas-chainsaw-3d-with-alexandra-daddario.html', 'snippet': 'Alexandra Daddario, Scott Eastwood and Tremaine Neverson (a k a the singer Trey Songz) star in “Texas Chainsaw 3D,” the generic sixth installment of the horror series.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Let’s see, how many name actors have enrolled in the “Texas Chainsaw Massacre” school of hard blows over that horror franchise’s history? There are Viggo Mortensen (class of 1990); Matthew McConaughey and Renée Zellweger (1994); Jessica Biel (2003); and Matt Bomer of “White Collar” (2006). Now add Alexandra Daddario (of “Percy Jackson & the Olympians”), Scott Eastwood (yes, Clint’s son) and Tremaine Neverson (a k a the singer Trey Songz), who graduate with flying limbs in the new, generic sixth installment, “Texas Chainsaw 3D.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/05/arts/05TEXASCHAIN/05TEXASCHAIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/05/arts/05TEXASCHAIN/05TEXASCHAIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None,