': 'Sessions at American Historical Association conference look at storytelling, used goods, and the relationship between horses and humans across three continents.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/04/historians-look-back-and-inward-at-annual-meeting/', 'snippet': 'Sessions at American Historical Association conference look at storytelling, used goods, and the relationship between horses and humans across three continents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW ORLEANS — Some 4,000 historians descended on New Orleans on Thursday for the American Historical Association’s four-day annual meeting, replacing the chants of departing Sugar Bowl revelers with more sober talk of job interviews, departmental politics, and — at least in the official panels — the past itself. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Historians Look Back, and Inward, at Annual Meeting', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cronon, William', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pfund, Niko', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pollan, Michael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN HISTORICAL ASSN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Orleans (La)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-04T23:52:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Schuessler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schuessler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/39aa7d16-50a9-57f4-8a8f-2b3b29254f3a', 'word_count': 973, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39aa7d16-50a9-57f4-8a8f-2b3b29254f3a'}, {'abstract': 'A 2012 law loosened limits on consumption and sales at microbreweries and brew pubs in New Jersey, allowing consumers to imbibe on the premises.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/06/nyregion/new-rules-loosen-the-tap-at-microbreweries-and-brew-pubs-in-new-jersey.html', 'snippet': 'A 2012 law loosened limits on consumption and sales at microbreweries and brew pubs in New Jersey, allowing consumers to imbibe on the premises.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAMBERTVILLE, N.J. — When Sean Hanrahan and Nina Sassano, both of Freehold, bought tickets to the River Horse Brewing Company’s oatmeal milk stout release party here last month, they noticed on Facebook that it was the first time the brewery was holding such an event, Ms. Sassano said. But they did not realize that a change in New Jersey law governing microbreweries had made such gatherings possible.', 'print_section': 'NJ', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/nyregion/06DINENJ1_SPAN/06DINENJ1_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/06/nyregion/06DINENJ1_SPAN/06DINENJ1_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/nyregion/06DINENJ1_SPAN/06DINENJ1_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/nyregion/06DINENJ1_SPAN/06DINENJ1_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/nyregion/06DINENJ1_SPAN/06DINENJ1_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'h