nistration officials cautioned that President Obama had not made a final decision or offered Chuck Hagel the job as defense secretary, but those who know the former senator said all signs point to his selection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Chuck Hagel appears to have weathered a concerted and vocal campaign to derail his chances for defense secretary, with President Obama likely to nominate him as early as next week, administration and Congressional officials said Friday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nomination of Hagel Could Come Next Week', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nomination Of Hagel Could Come Next Week', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Landler, Mark', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hagel, Chuck', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-05T01:36:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bbfa5800-c61d-58c3-bddf-b01f04f4f119', 'word_count': 471, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bbfa5800-c61d-58c3-bddf-b01f04f4f119'}, {'abstract': 'The end of smartphone patent lawsuits is by no means near, but legal experts say an F.T.C. settlement signals progress in clarifying the rules in high-tech patent battles, and thus could ease them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/05/technology/in-google-patent-case-ftc-set-rules-of-engagement-for-battles.html', 'snippet': 'The end of smartphone patent lawsuits is by no means near, but legal experts say an F.T.C. settlement signals progress in clarifying the rules in high-tech patent battles, and thus could ease them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Federal Trade Commission’s antitrust investigation of Google focused mainly on the company’s lucrative search business, while its inquiry into the tech giant’s handling of patents seemed an afterthought.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Google, F.T.C. Set Rules of War Over Patents', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On Google, F.T.C. Set Rules of War Over Patents', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abelson, Reed', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Trade Commission', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antitrust Laws and Competition Issues', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inventions and Patents', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tablet Computers', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Motorola Mobility LLC', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-05T01:37:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Lohr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lohr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d8917d4-89ef-5a1f-98f0-cd1f0e36f6b0', 'word_count': 823, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d8917d4-89ef-5a1f-98f0-cd1f0e36f6b0'}, {'abstract': 'The authorities say that a New Jersey mechanic offered to pay an officer, now accused of planning to cook and eat women, to kidnap a woman on his behalf.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/05/nyregion/man-accused-of-conspiring-with-officer-to-kidnap-woman.html', 'snippet': 'The authorities say that a New Jersey mechanic offered to pay an officer, now accused of planning to cook and eat women, to kidnap a woman on his behalf.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When federal prosecutors accused a New York City police officer in October of planning to abduct, rape, cook and eat women, they said the officer had plotted with others who shared his impulses.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Man Accused of Conspiring to Kidnap a Woman', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Man Accused of Conspiring With Officer to Kidnap Woman', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kidnapping', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Valle, Gilberto', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cannibalism', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vanhise, Michael', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-05T01:41:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph Goldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1648c621-b8d4-5d5c-bb6d-671cee05462f', 'word_count': 502, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1648c621-b8d4-5d5c-bb6d-671cee05462f'}, {'abstract': 'Showered with racist taunts, a player at an Italian exhibition led his team off the field — a first — and many hope that will have wide repercussions in sports.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/05/world/europe/pro-patria-fans-racism-prompts-ac-milan-walkout-and-outrage.html', 'snippet': 'Showered with racist taunts, a player at an Italian exhibition led his team off the field — a first — and many hope that will have wide repercussions in sports.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — Italians reacted forcefully Friday to a racist incident that led players with the powerful A.C. Milan club to abandon a soccer match this week, taking a strong stand in a country where racist episodes in sporting events are generally underplayed. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/05/world/italy/italy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 786, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/05/world/italy/italy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1573, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/05/world/italy/italy-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/05