 '_id': 'nyt://article/ceb5a269-b0f7-5bb9-9bbf-926a03fcef54', 'word_count': 1003, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ceb5a269-b0f7-5bb9-9bbf-926a03fcef54'}, {'abstract': 'An exhibition called “Long Island at Work and at Play,” at the Society for the Preservation of Long Island Antiquities, presents photos of life in the early 20th century.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/06/nyregion/a-photo-exhibition-of-the-way-new-yorkers-lived-a-century-ago.html', 'snippet': 'An exhibition called “Long Island at Work and at Play,” at the Society for the Preservation of Long Island Antiquities, presents photos of life in the early 20th century.', 'lead_paragraph': 'COLD SPRING HARBOR, N.Y. — A boy gripping his baseball bat stares out at us from a photograph with the solemn determination of any young slugger. A family poses proudly for a portrait in its French-made automobile, perhaps before taking it for a spin. A fish peddler, seemingly oblivious of a camera nearby, peers into the cart from which he sells his wares to residents of the homes lining a wide, unpaved road.', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/nyregion/06ARTSLI2_SPAN/06ARTSLI2_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 425, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/06/nyregion/06ARTSLI2_SPAN/06ARTSLI2_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 425}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/nyregion/06ARTSLI2_SPAN/06ARTSLI2_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 726, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/nyregion/06ARTSLI2_SPAN/06ARTSLI2_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1451, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/nyregion/06ARTSLI2_SPAN/06ARTSLI2_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/06/nyregion/06ARTSLI2_SPAN/06ARTSLI2_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/nyregion/06ARTSLI2_SPAN/06ARTSLI2_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Frozen in Time, With Hints of What Was to Come', 'kicker': 'Arts | Long Island', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Frozen in Time, With Hints of What Was to Come', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Society For the Preservation of Long Island Antiquities', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-05T02:39:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karin Lipson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lipson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/efc2f86c-8c97-59e8-bf2b-4fcca0b7025d', 'word_count': 782, 'uri': 'nyt://article/efc2f86c-8c97-59e8-bf2b-4fcca0b7025d'}, {'abstract': 'Ireland’s Great Hunger Museum in Hamden displays accounts from the time of the potato famine of 1845-1852, but its strongest works are modern.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/06/nyregion/a-review-of-irelands-great-hunger-museum-in-hamden.html', 'snippet': 'Ireland’s Great Hunger Museum in Hamden displays accounts from the time of the potato famine of 1845-1852, but its strongest works are modern.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most museums that bear witness to a nightmare, like Yad Vashem in Jerusalem or the Peace Memorial Museum in Hiroshima, are hard to visit. Caught between our need to understand the history and our wish to turn away from the horror, we don’t quite know where or how to look.', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/nyregion/06ARTSCT1_SPAN/06ARTSCT1_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/06/nyregion/06ARTSCT1_SPAN/06ARTSCT1_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/nyregion/06ARTSCT1_SPAN/06ARTSCT1_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/nyregion/06ARTSCT1_SPAN/06ARTSCT1_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/nyregion/06ARTSCT1_SPAN/06ARTSCT1_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/06/nyregion/06ARTSCT1_SPAN/06ARTSCT1_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype