ions-january-5-2013.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on January 5, 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': 'INTERNATIONAL', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: January 5, 2013', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-05T03:01:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/5cd009d1-e35c-5f87-8f13-ab306f45d661', 'word_count': 285, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5cd009d1-e35c-5f87-8f13-ab306f45d661'}, {'abstract': 'Climate change has forced arena managers in the northernmost reaches of Canada to forgo relying on natural ice for the entire skating season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/05/sports/hockey/more-rinks-in-far-north-find-need-for-cooling-systems.html', 'snippet': 'Climate change has forced arena managers in the northernmost reaches of Canada to forgo relying on natural ice for the entire skating season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Winter has come to the vast, northernmost reaches of Canada, the sparsely populated area surrounding the Arctic Circle historically characterized by severely cold weather. But these days refrigeration systems are needed to keep the ice cold at hockey arenas.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/05/sports/y-jp-ice/y-jp-ice-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 409, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/05/sports/y-jp-ice/y-jp-ice-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 409}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/05/sports/y-jp-ice/y-jp-ice-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 698, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/05/sports/y-jp-ice/y-jp-ice-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1397, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rinks in Canada’s Arctic Turn to Cooling Systems', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rinks in Canada’s Arctic Turn to Cooling Systems', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klein, Jeff Z', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ice', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stadiums and Arenas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-05T03:01:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b988adcf-c417-5e79-9987-956578b1a351', 'word_count': 902, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b988adcf-c417-5e79-9987-956578b1a351'}, {'abstract': 'A new arena at Flushing Meadows-Corona Park in Queens could help rejuvenate the aging park.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/05/opinion/a-soccer-stadium-but-where.html', 'snippet': 'A new arena at Flushing Meadows-Corona Park in Queens could help rejuvenate the aging park.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A tour of the old World’s Fair grounds in Queens on a recent weekday felt a little like walking through an aging Hollywood stage set. In the 1930s, superbuilder Robert Moses converted what had been a miserable ash heap covering more than 1,300 acres into a suitable site for the 1939-40 World’s Fair — complete with grand pools, fountains and boulevards. The 140 feet high Unisphere, built for the 1964-65 World’s Fair, languishes at one end of what is now known as Flushing Meadows-Corona Park, a vast, overused and underfinanced public space and the largest city park in Queens. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Soccer Stadium, but Where?', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Soccer Stadium, but Where?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Flushing Meadows-Corona Park (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stadiums and Arenas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Soccer', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Area Planning and Renewal', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-05T03:01:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/661e3676-9048-52b9-86f1-cdc4d713e504', 'word_count': 422, 'uri': 'nyt://article/661e3676-9048-52b9-86f1-cdc4d713e504'}, {'abstract': 'The writings of Philip Chlanda provide a rare, firsthand account of an officer’s encounter with an emotionally disturbed person but were not an indication of\xa0his future.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/05/nyregion/a-police-officers-journal-cited-his-use-of-restraint.html', 'snippet': 'The writings of Philip Chlanda provide a rare, firsthand account of an officer’s encounter with an emotionally disturbed person but were not an indication of\xa0his future.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A rookie police officer returned to his parents’ Manhattan apartment after his overnight tour of duty and sat at the computer in the bedroom where he had grown up. The officer, Philip Chlanda, then 24, kept an online journal that he shared with friends, and on this morning, he had a story to tell about his night in Times Square. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/05/nyregion/CRIMESCENE/CRIMESCENE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 896, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/05/nyregion/CRIMESCENE/CRIMESCENE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1792, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/05/nyregion/CRIMESCENE/CRIMESCENE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/05/nyregion/CRIMESCENE/CRIMESCENE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/05/nyregion/CRIMESCENE/CRIMESCENE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Rookie’s Online Jou