eque in the East Village, which recently opened a restaurant and offers slow-cooked meats using two types of techniques.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the opening of Mighty Quinn’s Barbeque in the East Village in December, barely a month after BrisketTown opened in Williamsburg, Brooklyn, the artisanal smoked meat wars are officially on. Both enterprises started ad hoc — Quinn’s as the stand with the longest line at the outdoor Smorgasburg bazaar, BrisketTown as a series of one-off events — and both promise long, slow cooking by mostly traditional methods. At Quinn’s, on Second Avenue at Sixth Street, the back wall and tables are made from century-old wood salvaged from the Puck Building in SoHo.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/nyregion/06TABLE_SPAN/06TABLE_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 353, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/06/nyregion/06TABLE_SPAN/06TABLE_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 353}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/nyregion/06TABLE_SPAN/06TABLE_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 602, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/nyregion/06TABLE_SPAN/06TABLE_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1204, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/nyregion/06TABLE_SPAN/06TABLE_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/06/nyregion/06TABLE_