 None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f3fd46f-0ccc-56e4-b0e3-20198ac5a1a3', 'word_count': 4227, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f3fd46f-0ccc-56e4-b0e3-20198ac5a1a3'}, {'abstract': 'The former space shuttle astronaut on poker, Porsches and kale.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/06/opinion/sunday/catching-up-with-the-astronaut-mark-kelly.html', 'snippet': 'The former space shuttle astronaut on poker, Porsches and kale.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Capt. Mark Kelly is a former Navy pilot and NASA astronaut and is the husband of the former congresswoman Gabrielle Giffords, who survived an assassination attempt in 2011. The couple has formed a political action committee, Gabby PAC, to promote civil political discourse and the election of moderates to Congress. Captain Kelly is also the author of “Mousetronaut,” a recently published children’s book loosely based on a mouse that accompanied him on one of his space shuttle missions. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/sunday-review/06download/06download-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 513, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/sunday-review/06download/06download-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 513, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/sunday-review/06download/06download-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/06/sunday-review/06download/06download-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/sunday-review/06download/06download-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 149, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Capt. Mark Kelly', 'kicker': 'Download', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Capt. Mark Kelly', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murphy, Kate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Aeronautics and Space Administration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelly, Mark E (1964- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-05T17:45:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/93b0b963-564a-55e9-8b26-34bba8a0dadd', 'word_count': 468, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93b0b963-564a-55e9-8b26-34bba8a0dadd'}, {'abstract': 'On Jan. 1, the government began depositing pension and scholarship payments directly into the bank accounts of about 245,000 people — to prevent corrupt officials from diverting the money.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/06/world/asia/india-takes-aim-at-poverty-with-cash-transfer-program.html', 'snippet': 'On Jan. 1, the government began depositing pension and scholarship payments directly into the bank accounts of about 245,000 people — to prevent corrupt officials from diverting the money.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — India has more poor people than any nation on earth, but many of its antipoverty programs end up feeding the rich more than the needy. A new program hopes to change that.', 'p