my, which analysts estimate grew just 0.1 percent last year and had an unemployment rate of 10.7 percent in October. But Mr. Hollande has so far done little to turn things around. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reviving the French Economy', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Reviving the French Economy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hollande, Francois', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-05T18:17:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/017b1c07-4bbe-5044-b12b-1baf94ebb492', 'word_count': 525, 'uri': 'nyt://article/017b1c07-4bbe-5044-b12b-1baf94ebb492'}, {'abstract': 'The Knicks’ forward commemorated the death of his brother, Hazell, who died in a traffic accident, by inviting 30 children to a game against the Orlando Magic.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/05/stoudemire-commemorates-brothers-death/', 'snippet': 'The Knicks’ forward commemorated the death of his brother, Hazell, who died in a traffic accident, by inviting 30 children to a game against the Orlando Magic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ORLANDO, Fla. – Amar’e Stoudemire will commemorate the death of his brother, Hazell, by inviting 30 children from his hometown of Lake Wales, Fla. to attend the Knicks’ game against the Orlando Magic on Saturday. Stoudemire purchased the tickets and will bring the children to the game on a charter bus.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stoudemire Commemorates Brother’s Death', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "Stoudemire, Amar'e", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Orlando Magic', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-05T18:18:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8129d45f-8493-5ce5-8573-7d2270984623', 'word_count': 330, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8129d45f-8493-5ce5-8573-7d2270984623'}, {'abstract': 'We’ve had lots of deal-making in Washington lately, but hardly any displays of courage from anyone.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/06/opinion/sunday/friedman-more-risk-taking-less-poll-taking.html', 'snippet': 'We’ve had lots of deal-making in Washington lately, but hardly any displays of courage from anyone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE U.S. military trains its fighter pilots on a principle called the “OODA Loop.” It stands for observe, orient, decide, act. The idea is that if your OODA Loop is faster and more accurate than the other pilot’s, you’ll shoot his plane out of the sky. If the other pilot’s OODA Loop is better, he’ll shoot you down. Right now, our national OODA Loop is broken. We’re are doing something crazy — taking the country back and forth to the financial brink to produce suboptimal, midnight compromises without any overall plan for how this will lead to growth in the world in which we’re living. We’re doing the worst thing a country can do — cutting taxes and spending without a plan. Maybe you can grow without a plan. But if you want to ensure that every scarce dollar gets the biggest bang, you can’t cut without a plan. It’s deciding and acting without observing and orienting. It’s how fighter pilots get shot down.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'u