iving-charge/', 'snippet': 'Senator Michael D.Crapo, Republican of Idaho, pleaded guilty on Friday to a drunken-driving charge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Republican senator who has said in the past that he does not drink alcohol because of his Mormon faith is headed to rehab after he pleaded guilty to a drunken-driving charge on Friday in Alexandria, Va.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Idaho Senator Pleads Guilty to Drunken-Driving Charge', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-05T18:34:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Southall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Southall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7acf5db6-bffa-50d3-be57-4c79285fc697', 'word_count': 254, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7acf5db6-bffa-50d3-be57-4c79285fc697'}, {'abstract': 'The Social Security system uses antiquated and unreliable methods of forecasting how long beneficiaries will live.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/01/06/sunday-review/social-securitys-flawed-forecasting.html', 'snippet': 'The Social Security system uses antiquated and unreliable methods of forecasting how long beneficiaries will live.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Social Security system uses antiquated and unreliable methods of forecasting how long beneficiaries will live.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Social Security’s Flawed Forecasting', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Security (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Social Security Administration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Payroll Tax', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-05T18:34:54+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Sunday Review', 'section_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/f566021f-3a90-5d92-bd6c-46783d3223b4', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/f566021f-3a90-5d92-bd6c-46783d3223b4'}, {'abstract': 'The Social Security Administration underestimates how long Americans will live. As a result, the trust funds will run out two years earlier than the government has predicted.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/06/opinion/sunday/social-security-its-worse-than-you-think.html', 'snippet': 'The Social Security Administration underestimates how long Americans will live. As a result, the trust funds will run out two years earlier than the government has predicted.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CONGRESS and President Obama have pushed through a relatively modest stopgap measure to avoid the “fiscal cliff,” but over the coming years, the United States will confront another huge cliff: Social Security. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/opinion/sunday/06social-graphic/06social-graphic-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 1541, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/06/opinion/sunday/06social-graphic/06social-graphic-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1541}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/opinion/sunday/06social-graphic/06social-graphic-jumbo-v2.pn