se about breath tests.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Fourth Amendment prohibits the police from searching individuals without a warrant, but the Supreme Court allows exceptions to that rule for “exigent circumstances” — when the police believe that the delay involved in getting a warrant would lead to destruction of evidence.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is the Driver Drunk?', 'kicker': 'Editorial | Week Ahead', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Is the Driver Drunk?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drunken and Reckless Driving', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fourth Amendment (US Constitution)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search and Seizure', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Missouri', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests (Sobriety)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-05T19:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lincoln Caplan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lincoln', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6c8f867-1d54-58ea-ad87-aa70472f287d', 'word_count': 259, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6c8f867-1d54-58ea-ad87-aa70472f287d'}, {'abstract': 'Beyoncé Knowles is renting her image to a product that may one day be ranked with cigarettes as a killer we were too slow to rein in.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/05/why-do-stars-think-its-o-k-to-sell-soda/', 'snippet': 'Beyoncé Knowles is renting her image to a product that may one day be ranked with cigarettes as a killer we were too slow to rein in.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Beyoncé Knowles would presumably refuse to take part in an ad campaign that showed her carrying a semiautomatic rifle. But she’s eager, evidently, to have the Pepsi logo painted on her lips and have a limited-edition Pepsi can bearing her likeness.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/sunday-review/06BITTMAN/06BITTMAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 613, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/sunday-review/06BITTMAN/06BITTMAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1226, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/sunday-review/06BITTMAN/06BITTMAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/06/sunday-review/06BITTMAN/06BITTMAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/sunday-review/06BITTMAN/06BITTMAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Do Stars Think It’s O.K. to Sell Soda?', 'kicker': 'Mark Bittman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Why Do Stars Think It’s O.K. To Sell Soda?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKE