he New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Step Toward Gay Marriage', 'kicker': 'Editorial | Week Ahead', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Step Toward Gay Marriage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Illinois', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Downes, Lawrence', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-05T19:01:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lawrence Downes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lawrence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Downes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/82aae46d-9e5a-5563-93c7-47749c28d899', 'word_count': 248, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82aae46d-9e5a-5563-93c7-47749c28d899'}, {'abstract': 'Connecticut lawmakers will weigh ideas for reducing gun violence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/06/opinion/sunday/preventing-the-next-shooting.html', 'snippet': 'Connecticut lawmakers will weigh ideas for reducing gun violence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The shooting deaths of 20 elementary-school children and seven adults in Newtown will dominate the agenda of the Connecticut General Assembly as lawmakers open their five-month session Wednesday in Hartford. Gov. Dannel Malloy has appointed a 15-member advisory committee to study and recommend needed changes in public safety, mental health services and the control of gun violence. But lawmakers are already offering a raft of separate proposals, including an outright ban of the Bushmaster AR-15 rifle and 30-round magazine used in the massacre last month.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/sunday-review/06EDITORIAL/06EDITORIAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/06/sunday-review/06EDITORIAL/06EDITORIAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 403}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/sunday-review/06EDITORIAL/06EDITORIAL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 688, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/sunday-review/06EDITORIAL/06EDITORIAL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1376, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/sunday-review/06EDITORIAL/06EDITORIAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/06/sunday-review/06EDITORIAL/06EDITORIAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/sunday-review/06EDITORIAL/06EDITORIAL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Preventing the Next Shooting', 'kicker': 'Editorial | Week Ahead', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Preventing the Next Shooting', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newtown, Conn, Shooting (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Malloy, Dannel P', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-05T19:01:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Francis X. Clines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Francis', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Clines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d54431f-cc99-5614-8cce-a3d941a564db', 'word_count': 305, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d54431f-cc99-5614-8cce-a3d941a564db'}, {'abstract': 'Alabama’s Jesse Williams, the man they call Tha Monstar, has taken an interesting journey from Australia to football stardom in the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/06/sports/ncaafootball/alabamas-jesse-williams-takes-improbable-path-to-stardom.html', 'snippet': 'Alabama’s Jesse Williams, the man they call Tha Monstar, has taken an interesting journey from Australia to football stardom in the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TUSCALOOSA, Ala. — The man they call Tha Monstar walked into Alabama’s football complex last month as if bound for a biker bar. Tattoos covered most every inch of his wide frame. He wore his hair carved down the center, into a Mohawk. He carried an Oakland Raiders knitted cap.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'captio