, a high-achieving student who had a strong commitment to playing sports, was shot about a block from his mother’s apartment in the Baruch housing project on Friday night.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/05/on-lower-east-side-corner-mourning-young-athlete-killed-by-a-gunman/', 'snippet': 'Raphael Ward, 16, a high-achieving student who had a strong commitment to playing sports, was shot about a block from his mother’s apartment in the Baruch housing project on Friday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Raphael Ward was known in the projects of the Lower East Side for his lanky frame, his easy laugh and his devotion to nearly every form of sports, especially baseball. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On a Lower East Side Corner, Mourning a Young Athlete Killed by a Gunman', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Teenager Fatally Shot In New York', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lower East Side (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-05T22:12:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Colin Moynihan and Daniel Krieger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Colin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moynihan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krieger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c73d064-8bbb-50de-9a75-cd0864b7741a', 'word_count': 569, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c73d064-8bbb-50de-9a75-cd0864b7741a'}, {'abstract': 'Even though regulators are required by the new health care law to review requests for a large rate increases, many states have not given the overseers any authority to deny or roll back rates that are deemed excessive.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/06/business/despite-new-health-law-some-see-sharp-rise-in-premiums.html', 'snippet': 'Even though regulators are required by the new health care law to review requests for a large rate increases, many states have not given the overseers any authority to deny or roll back rates that are deemed excessive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Health insurance companies across the country are seeking and winning double-digit increases in premiums for some customers, even though one of the biggest objectives of the Obama administration’s health care law was to stem the rapid rise in insurance costs for consumers.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/us/JP-RATES/JP-RATES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 448, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/06/us/JP-RATES/JP-RATES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 448}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/us/JP-RATES/JP-RATES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 765, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/us/JP-RATES/JP-RATES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1293, 'width': 1731, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Health Insurers Raise Some Rates by Double Digits', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Health Insurers Raise Some Rates By Double Digits', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abelson, Reed', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-05T22:30:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Reed Abelson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Reed', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abelson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5016ed92-dd4a-54f1-82bf-065dfa9824f2', 'word_count': 1482, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5016ed92-dd4a-54f1-82bf-065dfa9824f2'}, {'abstract': 'Are you jealous that Dan Feyer and Andrea Carla Michaels thought of this theme first?', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/05/puzzle-envy/', 'snippet': 'Are you jealous that Dan Feyer and Andrea Carla Michaels thought of this theme first?', 'lead_paragraph': 'SUNDAY’S PUZZLE — You’ve patted yourself on the back when you’ve solved a tough puzzle, and you’ve congratulated yourself when you’ve solved a puzzle fairly quickly, haven’t you? Don’t be shy; there are those who feel that solving the New York Times crossword puzzle is in itself a formidable feat.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Puzzle Envy', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-05T23:00:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/195988e3-77ce-5b6c-8d08-f02f4cd32677', 'word_count': 664, 'uri': 'nyt://article/195988e3-77ce-5b6c-8d08-f02f4cd32677'}, {'abstract': 'Sascha Stone Guttfreund is 23 and a 2011 University of Texas graduate, but his company, ScoreMore, already regularly produces hip-hop concerts across the state.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/06/us/sascha-guttfreund-of-scoremore-rubs-elbows-with-texas-hip-hop-stars.html', 'snippet': 'Sascha Stone Guttfreund is 23 and a 2011 University of Texas graduate, but his company, ScoreMore, already regularly produces hip-hop concerts across the state.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In November, at the first Formula 1 United States Grand Prix in Austin, Bun B, a rap superstar from Houston, talked with Sascha Stone Guttfreund, a budding promoter for the state’s hip-hop scene, about the feasibility of a plan Mr. Guttfreund was considering: how to promote two shows by the rapper Kendrick Lamar on the same night in competing Houston locations. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27B', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/us/06ttCulture/06ttCulture-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/06/us/06ttCulture/06ttCulture-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/us/06ttCulture/06ttCulture-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 710, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/us/06ttCulture/06ttCulture-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1420, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rubbing Elbows With Hip-Hop Royalty', 'kicker': 'Texas Monthly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rubbing Elbows With Hip-Hop Royalty', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rap and Hip-Hop', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ScoreMore', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wiz Khalifa', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bun B', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-05T23:03:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Langer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Langer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1fc78a9-3abb-56f8-9ff5-ae65149172dd', 'word_count': 771, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1fc78a9-3abb-56f8-9ff5-ae65149172dd'}, {'abstract': 'The Senate minority leader, Mitch McConnell, and the House minority leader, Nancy Pelosi, are among the members of Congress who join the Sunday shows this week to weigh in on whether the new Congress can break the gridlock.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/05/sunday-breakfast-menu-jan-6/', 'snippet': 'The Senate minority leader, Mitch McConnell, and the House minority leader, Nancy Pelosi, are among the members of Congress who join the Sunday shows this week to weigh in on whether the new Congress can break the gridlock.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 112th Congress reached an agreement to avert a fiscal crisis and adjourned for a final time last week. Now that the 113th Congress has been sworn in, can the incoming members help break the gridlock before lawmakers must find consensus on raising the debt ceiling?\xa0Senator Mitch McConnell of Kentucky, the Senate minority leader, and Representative Nancy Pelosi of California, the House minority leader, are among the members of Congress who join the Sunday shows this week to weigh in.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sunday Breakfast Menu, Jan. 6', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-05T23:14:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emmarie Huetteman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emmarie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Huetteman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6c7dd3b-a435-5e35-944d-18fda9438074', 'word_count': 544, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6c7dd3b-a435-5e35-944d-18fda9438074'}, {'abstract': 'With improving fiscal conditions and redistricting mostly in the rearview mirror, the 2013 Texas legislative session will face pressing policy questions on education, health care and transportation projects.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/06/us/texas-legislature-faces-a-new-set-of-priorities.html', 'snippet': 'With improving fiscal conditions and redistricting mostly in the rearview mirror, the 2013 Texas legislative session will face pressing policy questions on education, health care and transportation projects.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The last time Texas lawmakers convened in Austin, they were absorbed with numbers and boundaries: how to make ends meet with a deflated state budget and draw new district maps the courts would approve.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/us/06ttLegislatureFloater1/06ttLegislatureFloater1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/06/us/06ttLegislatureFloater1/06ttLegislatureFloater1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/us/06ttLegislatureFloater1/06ttLegislatureFloater1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 715, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/us/06ttLegislatureFloater1/06ttLegislatureFloater1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1430, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Legislature Faces a New Set of Priorities', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Legislature Faces a New Set of Priorities', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-05T23:19:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Texas Tribune', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Texas Tribune'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ecfb1ab0-1a53-5998-a03e-513d83aeb5ee', 'word_count': 2481, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ecfb1ab0-1a53-5998-a03e-513d83aeb5ee'}, {'abstract': 'Thirty years after Britain and Argentina fought over the Falkland Islands, the same questions of sovereignty that led to that conflict are being voiced again.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/06/world/americas/argentinas-call-for-return-of-falkland-islands-causes-a-stir.html', 'snippet': 'Thirty years after Britain and Argentina fought over the Falkland Islands, the same questions of sovereignty that led to that conflict are being voiced again.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — They have barely 3,000 inhabitants and far more sheep than people. They are more than 8,700 miles from London. For much of the year, they are bitterly cold and wind-swept, with only open sea and ice between them and Antarctica. President Ronald Reagan, who tussled with Margaret Thatcher over them as he rarely did on any other issue that engaged the two leaders, described them once as “that little ice-cold bunch of land down there.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/world/bull-falklands1/bull-falklands1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 363, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/06/world/bull-falklands1/bull-falklands1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 363}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/world/bull-falklands1/bull-falklands1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 620, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumb