section_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By John F. Burns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Burns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0cfcd5c5-f4a4-5550-ab65-eafe161d8451', 'word_count': 1161, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0cfcd5c5-f4a4-5550-ab65-eafe161d8451'}, {'abstract': 'The Red Bulls are two weeks away from opening training camp but have yet to hire a coach to replace Hans Backe.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/05/red-bulls-coaching-mystery-solved/', 'snippet': 'The Red Bulls are two weeks away from opening training camp but have yet to hire a coach to replace Hans Backe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The news release from the Red Bulls landed Friday morning, but it was not that news release.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Red Bulls’ Coaching Mystery Solved?', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Henry, Thierry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Soccer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Red Bulls (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-05T23:49:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Bell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/880d0f27-74a9-5c7f-8300-8bcfd2f348bc', 'word_count': 980, 'uri': 'nyt://article/880d0f27-74a9-5c7f-8300-8bcfd2f348bc'}, {'abstract': 'Two days before the B.C.S. title game, Alabama Coach Nick Saban had a chance to talk about one of his favorite things: his process.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/05/saban-is-keen-to-explain-process/', 'snippet': 'Two days before the B.C.S. title game, Alabama Coach Nick Saban had a chance to talk about one of his favorite things: his process.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MIAMI GARDENS, Fla. — Alabama Coach Nick Saban climbed atop a stage on Saturday morning and spent an hour in one of his least favorite places on the planet: in front of the news media, obliged to answer any and all questions. He looked as if he would have preferred to run through a blizzard in a Speedo.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Saban Is Keen to Explain ‘Process’', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'BCS National Championship', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saban, Nick', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Alabama', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Notre Dame', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-05T23:51:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Greg Bishop', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Greg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bishop', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7db2eab7-40c8-538c-8778-cb3a86067c85', 'word_count': 511, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7db2eab7-40c8-538c-8778-cb3a86067c85'}, {'abstract': 'Readers comment on my column about Xi Jinping, China’s new leader, and about my suggestions for reducing the risk of war between China and Japan over disputed islands.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/05/chinas-new-leader-and-the-islands-dispute/', 'snippet': 'Readers comment on my column about Xi Jinping, China’s new leader, and about my suggestions for reducing the risk of war between China and Japan over disputed islands.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My Sunday column, probably the last from this China trip, looks at the new Chinese paramount leader, Xi Jinping, and offers a pretty optimistic take about what may happen in the next 10 years under his leadership. I should acknowledge that plenty of Chinese disagree with me and think that Xi will be another drip like President Hu Jintao. But let me cling to my optimism as long as I can — and I welcome your views as well.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China’s New Leader, and the Islands Dispute', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-05T23:54:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c192d6b6-3a38-576b-a98e-875244ebaca8', 'word_count': 1046, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c192d6b6-3a38-576b-a98e-875244ebaca8'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Jones, who loved to play the music of stars like Sinatra and Ellington, was known for sprinkling his WNEW-AM broadcast with details about the singers and composers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/06/nyregion/bob-jones-new-york-dj-heard-on-milkmans-matinee-dies-at-70.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Jones, who loved to play the music of stars like Sinatra and Ellington, was known for sprinkling his WNEW-AM broadcast with details about the singers and composers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bob Jones, a mellow-voiced New York radio personality who was the last regular host of the historic WNEW-AM show “Milkman’s Matinee,” playing the music of Frank Sinatra, Ella Fitzgerald and Duke Ellington as it slowly became harder to find on the dial, died on Dec. 29 in Manhattan. He was 70.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bob Jones, New York D.J. Heard on ‘Milkman’s Matinee’, Dies at 70', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bob Jones, 70, New York D.J. Heard on ‘Milkman’s Matinee’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Bob (1942-2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radio', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-05T23:58:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel E. Slotnik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Slotnik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f674463-5b86-5331-9498-90ba91deb58c', 'word_count': 357, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f674463-5b86-5331-9498-90ba91deb58c'}, {'abstract': 'Commentary and live analysis of Saturday night’s N.F.C. wild-card game between the Minnesota Vikings and the Green Bay Packers at Lambeau Field.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/05/live-analysis-vikings-at-packers/', 'snippet': 'Commentary and live analysis of Saturday night’s N.F.C. wild-card game between the Minnesota Vikings and the Green Bay Packers at Lambeau Field.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Read on to relive The Fifth Down’s commentary and live analysis of Saturday night’s N.F.C. wild-card game between the Minnesota Vikings (10-6) and the Green Bay Packers (11-5). The best part? You can enjoy the game snuggled up next to your favorite source of warmth while 73,000 fans at Lambeau Field were left to wonder what their toes used to feel like. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Final: Packers 24, Vikings 10', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Green Bay Packers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Minnesota Vikings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-06T00:13:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Das', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Das', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/821678d8-0831-5f12-aa4e-ad7cc33cb945', 'word_count': 2035, 'uri': 'nyt://article/821678d8-0831-5f12-aa4e-ad7cc33cb945'}, {'abstract': 'When Geewon Anderson, a South Korean immigrant, bought Charlie’s Main Street Cafe in Minot, N.D., she not only embraced the tradition the cafe represented, she also worked to bolster it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/06/us/down-home-american-food-korean-style.html', 'snippet': 'When Geewon Anderson, a South Korean immigrant, bought Charlie’s Main Street Cafe in Minot, N.D., she not only embraced the tradition the cafe represented, she also worked to bolster it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MINOT, N.D. — Charlie’s Main Street Cafe in the heart of downtown here is a monument to small-town Americana.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multime