: None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aedb912e-3190-58a3-9252-e4e61b3f077c', 'word_count': 590, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aedb912e-3190-58a3-9252-e4e61b3f077c'}, {'abstract': '“The Hobbit: An Unexpected Journey” had been expected by some analysts to repeat for a fourth week as the most popular movie in North American theaters.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/06/texas-chainsaw-3d-leads-at-the-box-office/', 'snippet': '“The Hobbit: An Unexpected Journey” had been expected by some analysts to repeat for a fourth week as the most popular movie in North American theaters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A chainsaw finally pried the Hobbits out of first place at the North American box office. “The Hobbit: An Unexpected Journey” was expected by some analysts to repeat for a fourth week as the most popular movie in the land, but “Texas Chainsaw 3D” (Lionsgate) beat projections and took in an estimated $23 million for No. 1. (“Massacre” was dropped from the title after the Colorado movie theater shootings last summer.) ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Texas Chainsaw 3D’ Leads at the Box Office', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Texas Chainsaw 3D’ Leads at the Box Office', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hollywood.com', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-06T17:37:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/60ab8d60-6eb9-5903-920d-17075267d705', 'word_count': 170, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60ab8d60-6eb9-5903-920d-17075267d705'}, {'abstract': 'A $10 billion settlement to resolve claims of foreclosure abuses by major lenders could be announced on Monday, several people with knowledge of the discussions said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/07/business/lenders-said-to-be-near-deal-of-foreclosure-claims.html', 'snippet': 'A $10 billion settlement to resolve claims of foreclosure abuses by major lenders could be announced on Monday, several people with knowledge of the discussions said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A $10 billion settlement to resolve claims of foreclosure abuses by 14 major lenders was expected to be announced as early as Monday, several people with knowledge of the discussions said on Sunday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Deal in Foreclosure Case Is Imminent, Officials Say', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Regulators and 14 Banks Are Said to Be Near a Deal on Foreclosure Claims', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Silver-Greenberg, Jessica', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreclosures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-06T17:46:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jessica Silver-Greenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jessica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver-Greenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1f52c8f-a9e2-5ae2-9e8a-6f8361fcdaa0', 'word_count': 701, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1f52c8f-a9e2-5ae2-9e8a-6f8361fcdaa0'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/06/arts/television/whats-on-sunday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '9 P.M. (13, 49) DOWNTON ABBEY The Great War has ended, and preparations are being made for the society event of the season — the long-awaited wedding of Lady Mary (Michelle Dockery) and Matthew Crawley (Dan Stevens) — as a third installment of this “Masterpiece Classic” soap opera begins, chronicling the lives of masters and servants at the twilight of the British Empire. But all is not tranquil as this English country estate is gripped by social change, romantic intrigue and personal crises. Shirley MacLaine, above, joins the cast as Martha Levinson, the American mother of Cora, Countess of Grantham (Elizabeth McGovern). “This series about British aristocrats and their servants is ‘Fifty Shades of Grey’: soft-core pornography, but fixated on breeding and heritage rather than kinky sex,” Alessandra Stanley wrote in The New York Times. “\xa0‘Downton Abbey’ is a fantasy that gets sillier in prolongation, and as is the case with ‘Fifty Shades of Grey,’ there is a huge audience that cannot get enough.” ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Sunday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Sunday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-06T17:54:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/43622da2-a8d1-5d66-b003-e2f4fe12714e', 'word_count': 751, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43622da2-a8d1-5d66-b003-e2f4fe12714e'}, {'abstract': 'The Senate Republican leader, Mitch McConnell, made clear in three television appearances that he would oppose any effort by the Obama administration to further increase tax revenue and that he remained focused on finding ways to cut spending as the government grapples with debilitating debt.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/06/g-o-p-senate-leader-says-no-to-more-tax-revenue/', 'snippet': 'The Senate Republican leader, Mitch McConnell, made clear in three television appearances that he would oppose any effort by the Obama administration to further increase tax revenue and that he remained focused on finding ways to cut spending as t...', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Senate Republican leader, Mitch McConnell, made clear on Sunday that he would oppose any effort by the Obama administration to raise more tax revenue and that he remained focused on finding ways to cut spending as the government grapples with its debt.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'G.O.P. Senate Leader Says No to More Tax Revenue', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McConnell, Mitch', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-06T18:19:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Knowlton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Knowlton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b18ab170-0dd4-565a-b58b-9e669124e902', 'word_count': 551, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b18ab170-0dd4-565a-b58b-9e669124e902'}, {'abstract': 'The White House is betting that opposition to Chuck Hagel, a maverick Republican former senator nominated for defense secretary, won’t stop his confirmation in the Senate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/07/us/obama-expected-to-select-hagel-for-defense-post.html', 'snippet': 'The White House is betting that opposition to Chuck Hagel, a maverick Republican former senator nominated for defense secretary, won’t stop his confirmation in the Senate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — When President Obama nominates Chuck Hagel, the maverick Republican and former senator from Nebraska, to be his next secretary of defense, he will be turning to a trusted ally whose willingness to defy party loyalty and conventional wisdom won his admiration both in the Senate and on a 2008 tour of war zones in Iraq and Afghanistan.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/07/us/07hagel_2/07hagel_2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/07/us/07hagel_2/07hagel_2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/07/us/07hagel_2/07hagel_2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0