 Monday’s regular weekly auction of new three- and six-month bills and an auction of four-week bills on Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Treasury Auctions Set for This Week', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Treasury Auctions Set for This Week', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-06T23:04:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/449b1d66-a016-5ec6-a49b-0dd2da2ac5cc', 'word_count': 222, 'uri': 'nyt://article/449b1d66-a016-5ec6-a49b-0dd2da2ac5cc'}, {'abstract': 'A reader recalls a Japanese brochure that glosses over World War II.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/07/opinion/an-elided-history-of-japan.html', 'snippet': 'A reader recalls a Japanese brochure that glosses over World War II.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor: ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Elided History of Japan', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Elided History of Japan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-06T23:04:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f8e8679-a572-5390-9b87-86ded3e95ddb', 'word_count': 110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f8e8679-a572-5390-9b87-86ded3e95ddb'}, {'abstract': '“Deception” on NBC employs an increasingly hoary prime-time dramatic premise: an outsider goes undercover in a wealthy social circle.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/07/arts/television/deception-with-meagan-good-on-nbc.html', 'snippet': '“Deception” on NBC employs an increasingly hoary prime-time dramatic premise: an outsider goes undercover in a wealthy social circle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week’s television trend: law enforcement officers who aren’t what they seem. On Friday, Cinemax brings us “Banshee,” a new series about a former convict who assumes the identity of a dead sheriff. But first comes NBC’s almost-as-improbable “Deception,” in which a police detective trying to solve a murder goes undercover to get the skinny on a wealthy family with all sorts of wickedness in its DNA.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/07/arts/deception/deception-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 359, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/07/arts/deception/deception-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 359}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/07/arts/deception/deception-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 612, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/07/arts/deception/deception-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1223, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/07/arts/deception/deception-thumbStandar