ay, “At the E.R., Bearing Witness to Gun Violence.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Guns: A Public Health Issue', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Guns: A Public Health Issue', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newtown, Conn, Shooting (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emergency Medical Treatment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-06T23:08:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/35ebc21f-67ff-551b-b338-bb234ac93514', 'word_count': 224, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35ebc21f-67ff-551b-b338-bb234ac93514'}, {'abstract': 'Primary Stages is to announce on Monday that the world premiere of a new play written by and starring Charles Busch will be among the productions in the 2013-14 season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/07/theater/primary-stages-announces-season.html', 'snippet': 'Primary Stages is to announce on Monday that the world premiere of a new play written by and starring Charles Busch will be among the productions in the 2013-14 season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Primary Stages is to announce on Monday that the world premiere of a new play written by and starring Charles Busch will be among the productions in the 2013-14 season. Mr. Busch’s untitled comedy, scheduled to have its premiere next January, sounds as if it will fit among the rest of a farcical oeuvre that includes “The Tale of the Allergist’s Wife” and “You Should Be So Lucky.” He will play an unemployed female impersonator who steals the identity of his recently deceased landlord to remain in her Greenwich Village town house. Primary Stages will also mount the New York premiere of “Harbor,” a comedy by Chad Beguelin (“The Wedding Singer”) and directed by Mark Lamos (“Black Tie”), from July through September 2013. And the world premiere of “The Yankees,” written and directed by Eric Simonson (“Lombardi”), following the career of Yogi Berra, will run this September and October.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Primary Stages Announces Season', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Primary Stages Announces Season', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Primary Stages Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beguelin, Chad', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Busch, Charles', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lamos, Mark', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Simonson, Eric', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-06T23:09:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b335f86-c576-55f7-ae70-2f849771ea67', 'word_count': 149, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b335f86-c576-55f7-ae70-2f849771ea67'}, {'abstract': 'As new trends come to libraries, a reader fondly recalls a childhood memory of one.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/07/opinion/library-as-enduring-memory.html', 'snippet': 'As new trends come to libraries, a reader fondly recalls a childhood memory of one.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Library as Enduring Memory', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Library as Enduring Memory', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Libraries and Librarians', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-06T23:09:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/3974a469-c082-5d29-aeae-e83620ca7095', 'word_count': 150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3974a469-c082-5d29-aeae-e83620ca7095'}, {'abstract': 'The Center for the Theater Commons at Emerson College in Boston is set to announce a program to award 14 theater residencies to playwrights in 11 communities across the country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/07/theater/theater-residencies-from-emerson-college.html', 'snippet': 'The Center for the Theater Commons at Emerson College in Boston is set to announce a program to award 14 theater residencies to playwrights in 11 communities across the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Center for the Theater Commons at Emerson College in Boston is set to announce on Monday a program to award 14 theater residencies to playwrights in 11 communities across the country, to increase the presence of playwrights at theater companies. The three-year-long, full-time residencies will be paid for by grants from the Andrew W. Mellon Foundation. Among the artists are David Adjmi, at Soho Rep in New York; Dan LeFranc,  at Playwrights Horizons, also in New York; Andrew Saito at the Cutting Ball Theater in San Francisco; and Pearl Cleage at the Alliance Theater in Atlanta.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Theater Residencies From Emerson College', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'cont