 already tense negotiations on an evaluation system.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/07/education/michael-bloomberg-compares-teachers-union-to-the-nra.html', 'snippet': 'Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg’s comparison of the United Federation of Teachers to the National Rifle Association might have further damaged the already tense negotiations on an evaluation system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Of all the polarizing things Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg has said and done over the years, from banning large sugary drinks to supporting congestion pricing, few have generated the sort of viral backlash that has unexpectedly mounted after his weekly radio show on Friday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Teachers Irate as Bloomberg Likens Union to the N.R.A.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Teachers Irate As Bloomberg Likens Union To the N.R.A.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Rifle Assn', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN FEDERATION OF TEACHERS', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Federation of Teachers', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-07T05:01:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Al Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Al', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/796dc2b5-1573-554a-890c-8f56e4116962', 'word_count': 489, 'uri': 'nyt://article/796dc2b5-1573-554a-890c-8f56e4116962'}, {'abstract': 'With 11 states branded with an F, StudentsFirst, led by the former schools chancellor in Washington, D.C., would seem to be building a reputation as a harsh grader.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/07/education/studentsfirst-issues-low-ratings-on-school-policies.html', 'snippet': 'With 11 states branded with an F, StudentsFirst, led by the former schools chancellor in Washington, D.C., would seem to be building a reputation as a harsh grader.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In just a few short years, state legislatures and education agencies across the country have sought to transform American public education by passing a series of laws and policies overhauling teacher tenure, introducing the use of standardized test scores in performance evaluations and expanding charter schools.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/07/us/STUDENT/STUDENT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 755, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/07/us/STUDENT/STUDENT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1510, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/07/us/STUDENT/STUDENT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/07/us/STUDENT/STUDENT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type':