'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/07/indias-rape-and-sexual-assault-laws-under-scrutiny/', 'snippet': 'Outdated concepts like “outraging the modesty of a woman” and unclear guidelines about punishment need to be changed, activists say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The death of a young rape victim in from Delhi has reopened a debate in India about the country’s sexual assault and rape laws, as sweeping changes are being demanded to improve women’s rights in the country. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'India’s Rape and Sexual Assault Laws Under Scrutiny', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Castration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sexual Harassment', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tharoor, Shashi', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Human Rights Watch', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indian National Congress', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court of India', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-07T05:43:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neha Thirani and Anjani Trivedi',