u-brigitte-bardot-and-russia/', 'snippet': 'A few days into each New Year, Russia’s haze of smoke, alcohol and overindulgence makes it difficult to distinguish between truth and fact, reality and a fever dream.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — The first week of January is always a week out of time and space in Russia: all business shuts down, many people flee to more temperate climes, and those who remain, drink, eat and then drink some more. A few days into the year, the haze of smoke, alcohol and overindulgence makes it difficult to distinguish between truth and fact, reality and a fever dream. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russian Holiday', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizenship and Naturalization', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bardot, Brigitte', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Depardieu, Gerard', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-07T10:41:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Masha Gessen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Masha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gessen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/19cc425a-7a10-5f3d-8357-8d980e036ff3', 'word_count': 642, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19cc425a-7a10-5f3d-8357-8d980e036ff3'}, {'abstract': 'Two college counselors provide customized advice and next steps to high school seniors who are applying to college, including a reminder to avoid senioritis.', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.co