media', 'news_desk': 'Fashion & Style', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/4f28dfe3-2940-52b4-a705-847fe2cf1c20', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/4f28dfe3-2940-52b4-a705-847fe2cf1c20'}, {'abstract': 'The actor will receive the Eugene O’Neill Theater Center’s annual Monte Cristo Award.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/07/oneill-theater-center-honors-christopher-plummer/', 'snippet': 'The actor will receive the Eugene O’Neill Theater Center’s annual Monte Cristo Award.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Eugene O’Neill Theater Center announced on Monday that Christopher Plummer would receive its 13th\xa0 Monte Cristo Award in recognition of his theater career, which includes two Tony-winning performances on Broadway — in the 1997 play “Barrymore” and in the 1973 musical “Cyrano.” Mr. Plummer, 83, also won the Academy Award for best supporting actor last year for the film “Beginners.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'O’Neill Theater Center Honors Christopher Plummer', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'O’Neill Theater Center  Honors Plummer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Plummer, Christopher', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "O'Neill, Eugene, Theater Center", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Waterford (Conn)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-07T14:43:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93f5a4a0-6042-50c6-8cd6-5c859f1d60cf', 'word_count': 162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93f5a4a0-6042-50c6-8cd6-5c859f1d60cf'}, {'abstract': 'India has the world’s single largest population lacking electricity, but many argue that dam-building is not the solution.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/07/hobbled-on-energy-india-ponders-a-multitude-of-dams/', 'snippet': 'India has the world’s single largest population lacking electricity, but many argue that dam-building is not the solution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As we noted here last week, over 600 million people lost power in India last summer, setting a modern record for the number of people affected by a blackout. Well before that, though, India’s government was grappling with growing pressure to increase the dependability of its electricity service — for the growing numbers who have intermittent power and the 400 million who live without it. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hobbled on Energy, India Ponders a Multitude of Dams', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Light and Power', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hydroelectric Power', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Power Outages and Blackouts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Conservation Biology (Journal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Himalayas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-07T14:51:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Nuwer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nuwer', 'qualifier': Non