media': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Illumina Buys Maker of Down Syndrome Test', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Diagnostics Push, Illumina to Buy Maker of Down Syndrome Test', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DNA (Deoxyribonucleic Acid)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Down Syndrome', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetics and Heredity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests (Medical)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Illumina Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roche Holding A G', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Verinata Health Inc', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-07T15:16:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Pollack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pollack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a5d86bd-3131-56a1-a9ed-b8b88d2a0fc2', 'word_count': 674, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a5d86bd-3131-56a1-a9ed-b8b88d2a0fc2'}, {'abstract': 'The Supreme Court agrees to decide whether the water authority serving Fort Worth and its growing suburbs can take water from within Oklahoma’s borders.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/07/supreme-court-to-decide-on-texans-bid-for-oklahomas-water/', 'snippet': 'The Supreme Court agrees to decide whether the water authority serving Fort Worth and its growing suburbs can take water from within Oklahoma’s borders.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was largely overlooked last year when Fort Worth, now boasting a population of 758,000, moved closer to overtaking San Francisco in population. Yet in some ways, the Texas city’s early-21st-century growth spurt recalls the issues that San Francisco faced a century ago: if Fort Worth doesn’t get more water, its opportunities for growth will diminish rapidly.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Supreme Court to Decide on Texans’ Bid for Oklahoma’s Water', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fort Worth (Tex)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hetch Hetchy Reservoir', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oklahoma', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-07T15:23:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicity Barringer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicity', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barringer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/917c479f-7e16-5f9c-945b-32f3ec98b05e', 'word_count': 464, 'uri': 'nyt://article/917c479f-7e16-5f9c-945b-32f3ec98b05e'}, {'abstract': 'The power of compound interest is on display only after decades of persistent saving. Don’t let that keep you from starting today, though.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/07/investing-money-plus-lots-of-time-equals-excitement/', 'snippet': 'The power of compound interest is on display only after decades of persistent saving. Don’t let that keep you from starting today, though.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carl Richards is a financial planner in Park City, Utah, and is the director of investor education at the BAM Alliance. His book, “The Behavior Gap,” was published last year. His sketches are archived on the Bucks blog. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Investing: Money Plus (Lots of) Time Equals Excitement', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How to Build a Nest Egg', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Savings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-07T15:47:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Richards', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Richards', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/12f58c4e-f6c4-5524-8abc-4026d509d624', 'word_count': 726, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12f58c4e-f6c4-5524-8abc-4026d509d624'}, {'abstract': 'The author of this week’s cover article tells us what it was like to get to know the man who wrote “Tenth of December.”', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/07/behind-the-cover-story-joel-lovell-on-the-short-story-genius-george-saunders/', 'snippet': 'The author of this week’s cover article tells us what it was like to get to know the man who wrote “Tenth of December.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Joel Lovell, deputy editor at The Times Magazine, wrote this week’s cover story about the writer George Saunders. He last wrote for the magazine about the playwright Kenneth Lonergan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/magazine/04-joel-headshot/04-joel-headshot-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 731, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/magazine/04-joel-headshot/04-joel-headshot-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1463, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/magazine/04-joel-headshot/04-joel-headshot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/04/magazine/04-joel-headshot/04-joel-headshot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/magazine/04-joel-headshot/04-joel-headshot-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Behind the Cover Story: Joel Lovell on the Short-Story Genius George Saunders', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lovell, Joel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saunders, George', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-07T15:53:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Nolan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nolan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/803e876f-7c6d-5394-9cf4-4ee66340384c', 'word_count': 1462, 'uri': 'nyt://article/803e876f-7c6d-5394-9cf4-4ee66340384c'}, {'abstract': 'The author reflects on the small world that is Savile Row, just as the Fall 2013 men’s collections shows begin in London.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/07/on-savile-row-a-tale-of-two-tailors/', 'snippet': 'The author reflects on the small world that is Savile Row, just as the Fall 2013 men’s collections shows begin in London.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I was a young man and finally got a teaching job and some money of my own I was determined to have a Savile Row suit. (The Porsche speedster, Purdy shotgun, Renoir etching or a first edition of Pope’s “Homer” were still all beyond my ken.) I had seen all the films of Fred Astaire, Gary Cooper and Cary Grant, and the print media had been enamored by the Duke of Windsor — the most photographed man of his time — and the other elegant habitués of the Row long enough.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Savile Row | A Tale of Two Tailors', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-07T16:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Boyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Boyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e3ea3726-4c3c-58d0-b9a0-0326fadfbee9', 'word_count': 1006, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3ea3726-4c3c-58d0-b9a0-0326fadfbee9'}, {'abstract': 'The suspected gunman, James E. Holmes, was described as being eerily calm and detached from the chaos he had created.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/08/us/hearing-expected-to-offer-details-of-plotting-before-colorado-massacre.html', 'snippet': 'The suspected gunman, James E. Holmes, was described as being eerily calm and detached from the chaos he had created.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CENTENNIAL, Colo. — The movie theater was a blood-soaked nightmare that night in July. Wounded moviegoers screamed for help and tried to crawl for the exits. Bodies lay in the aisles. The floor was a carpet of shell casings, the air stung with the smell of tear gas, and dozens of abandoned cellphones bleated incessantly.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/us/AURORA-2/AURORA-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/08/us/AURORA-2/AURORA-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/us/AURORA-2/AURORA-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 729, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/us/AURORA-2/AURORA-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1458, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/us/AURORA-2/AURORA-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/08/us/AURORA-2/AURORA-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At Hearing, Police Recall Details of Horror at Colorado Movie Theater', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline'