rganizations', 'value': 'Port Authority of New York and New Jersey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jersey City (NJ)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-07T16:35:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5525d828-bafb-5520-ad77-3b27578c9441', 'word_count': 133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5525d828-bafb-5520-ad77-3b27578c9441'}, {'abstract': 'All that glitters need not be platinum.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/07/moral-obligation-coupons/', 'snippet': 'All that glitters need not be platinum.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Don’t like the platinum coin option? Here’s a functionally equivalent alternative: have the Treasury sell pieces of paper labeled “moral obligation coupons”, which declare the intention of the government to redeem these coupons at face value in one year. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Moral Obligation Coupons', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-07T16:37:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99a7966b-8f22-57cb-bae1-9d329e019a3f', 'word_count': 385, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99a7966b-8f22-57cb-bae1-9d329e019a3f'}, {'abstract': 'Legal advocates said an announcement fueled hopes that the draconian system of labor camps, established in the 1950s, would be significantly modified.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/08/world/asia/china-says-it-will-overhaul-re-education-system.html', 'snippet': 'Legal advocates said an announcement fueled hopes that the draconian system of labor camps, established in the 1950s, would be significantly modified.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — China will start overhauling its draconian system of re-education through labor in the coming year, according to the state news media, signaling the incoming leadership’s determination to alter one of the government’s more widely despised cudgels for punishing petty criminals, religious dissidents, petitioners and other perceived social irritants. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/world/china/china-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/13/world/china/china-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/world/china/china-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/world/china/china-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/world/china/china-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/13/world/china/china-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/world/china/china-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'China Says It Will Overhaul Sprawling System of Re-education Through Labor', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China Says It Will Overhaul Sprawling System of Re-education Through Labor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jacobs, Andrew', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forced Labor', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Xinhua', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-07T16:46:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Jacobs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jacobs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/76b08f59-a50f-5c90-b791-5c82c9d9f4a4', 'word_count': 763, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76b08f59-a50f-5c90-b791-5c82c9d9f4a4'}, {'abstract': 'TV executives are speculating that Monday’s Bowl Championship Series title game could challenge the ratings record. But if you strip away the uniforms and the back story, the game looks only average by B.C.S. championship standards.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/07/a-marquee-b-c-s-matchup-to-be-determined/', 'snippet': 'TV executives are speculating that Monday’s Bowl Championship Series title game could challenge the ratings record. But if you strip away the uniforms and the back story, the game looks only average by B.C.S. championship standards.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Monday’s Bowl Championship Series title game is attracting a significant amount of attention from fans and the news media. Google searches for the terms “BCS Championship Game” and “BCS Title Game” are on pace to be about twice as high as they were last year. Senior executives at ESPN, which will televise the game, are openly speculating that the contest could challenge ratings records — perhaps matching the mark set in 2006, when the game between Texas and U.S.C. attracted a 21.7 Nielsen rating.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Marquee B.C.S. Matchup? To Be Determined', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'BCS National Championship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ratings (Audience Measurement)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Alabama', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Notre Dame', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-07T16:46:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a9151eb-9e9f-5f8a-b686-769a08385575', 'word_count': 894, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a9151eb-9e9f-5f8a-b686-769a08385575'}, {'abstract': 'Chuck Hagel, a Republican from Nebraska, was elected to the Senate in 1996 and retired in 2008. Following are some of his recent statements on issues he is likely to confront if he is con