tag buzzed about on the Internet in November may have been a hoax. But the American Dialect Society has given the Twitter-inspired term a boost by christening “hashtag” the word of the year.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tweet This: ‘Hashtag’ Named Word of the Year', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Hashtag’ Is Word of Year', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'English Language', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zimmer, Ben', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Dialect Society', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-07T17:33:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Schuessler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schuessler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af8fab73-b505-5dca-99d1-3972b1298c1a', 'word_count': 324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af8fab73-b505-5dca-99d1-3972b1298c1a'}, {'abstract': 'All the public tickets to President Obama’s official inaugural ball and parade were snapped up Sunday – a day before they were scheduled to go on sale – after Ticketmaster inadvertently sent out e-mails announcing they were available, inaugural officials said on Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/07/after-ticketmaster-glitch-inaugural-ball-and-parade-tickets-sell-out-early/', 'snippet': 'All the public tickets to President Obama’s official inaugural ball and parade were snapped up Sunday – a day before they were scheduled to go on sale – after Ticketmaster inadvertently sent out e-mails announcing they were available, inaugural of...', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON – All the public tickets to President Obama’s official inaugural ball and parade were snapped up Sunday – a day before they were scheduled to go on sale – after Ticketmaster inadvertently sent out e-mails announcing they were available, inaugural officials said on Monday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Ticketmaster Glitch, Inaugural Ball and Parade Tickets Sell Out Early', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inaugurations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ticketmaster', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-07T17:34:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sheryl Gay Stolberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sheryl', 'middlename': 'Gay', 'lastname': 'Stolberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97be9430-d365-5c9e-82e8-b151f095cf70', 'word_count': 371, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97be9430-d365-5c9e-82e8-b151f095cf70'}, {'abstract': 'What the near-impossibility of a major deal on entitlements and taxes should mean for Republican strategy.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/07/a-world-without-grand-bargains/', 'snippet': 'What the near-impossibility of a major deal on entitlements and taxes should mean for Republican strategy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In my Sunday column defending John Boehner’s record as Speaker of the House, I make the point that for all the talk about how much more bipartisan and effective Congress used to be, there really isn’t a modern historical precedent for the kind of “everybody hurts”\xa0bargain on taxes and entitlements that would actually be required to bring our projected spending in line with our projected revenue. The most plausible recent example of such a bargain is the deal that George H.W. Bush struck with Congressional Democrats in 1990, which brought him so much grief and helped inspire a generation of Republican resistance to tax increases: That compromise promised to cut $500 billion from the deficit over five years, which (per my back-of-the-envelope adjustments for inflation) is the equivalent of about $2.5 trillion in deficit reduction over ten years today. $2.5 trillion is\xa0a big number … but it’s only slightly more than the combined deficit reduction promised by last year’s debt-ceiling deal and this month’s tax increases combined — and that combination, of course, has only put a very modest dent in our long-term deficit problem.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A World Without Grand Bargains', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-07T17:35:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c7fb5aac-d7a7-519b-bf0c-05a775973c88', 'word_count': 1076, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c7fb5aac-d7a7-519b-bf0c-05a775973c88'}, {'abstract': 'TimesCast: President Obama picks new chiefs for the C.I.A. and Defense Department. | A look at how more guns means more killing. | Peruvian village forced to make way for a giant mine.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/us/100000001990366/obama-fills-top-security-posts.html', 'snippet': 'TimesCast: President Obama picks new chiefs for the C.I.A. and Defense De