3d84-6b01-55aa-95b1-6c99cf667e93'}, {'abstract': 'TerraCycle’s sales have grown every year for the past nine years, but the company earned its first profit in 2011.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/07/the-role-of-profit-in-a-social-business/', 'snippet': 'TerraCycle’s sales have grown every year for the past nine years, but the company earned its first profit in 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As I reflected on the end of 2012, I decided to write a letter to our more than a hundred employees around the world to discuss the role profits play at TerraCycle.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Role of Profit in a Social Business', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recycling of Waste Materials', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "BEN & JERRY'S HOMEMADE INC", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TerraCycle', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-07T18:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Szaky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Szaky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fac38a44-6e64-5c1c-9665-bfa4e1e004e4', 'word_count': 926, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fac38a44-6e64-5c1c-9665-bfa4e1e004e4'}, {'abstract': 'A look back at Numberplay in 2012.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/07/2012-review/', 'snippet': 'A look back at Numberplay in 2012.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As we begin the new year (our puzzle for this week — a trapezoidal challenge from Joshua Zucker — is already up in a separate post), let’s also pause for a moment to reflect on the adventures we had in 2012.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Numberplay 2012: A Year in Review', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mathematics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Puzzles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-07T18:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gary Antonick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Antonick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4b34b4c-fa84-5822-9fd3-c8ba51d37863', 'word_count': 958, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4b34b4c-fa84-5822-9fd3-c8ba51d37863'}, {'abstract': 'Ewan McGregor recounts what it was like to work with very young actors for “The Impossible.”', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/07/ewan-mcgregor-on-acting-with-youngsters/', 'snippet': 'Ewan McGregor recounts what it was like to work with very young actors for “The Impossible.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Though Ewan McGregor is up for a Golden Globe on Sunday for his performance in “Salmon Fishing in the Yemen,” he’s been making the rounds in support of a higher-profile film, “The Impossible,” the based-on-a-true-story tale of a vacationing family torn apart by a tsunami. Mr. McGregor plays the father (opposite Naomi Watts), and if he knew the adage about never working with children, he didn’t acknowledge it in this talk with the Carpetbagger, in which he recounts filming a scene with the young actors — Tom Holland, Samuel Joslin and Oaklee Pendergast — who play his sons.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ewan McGregor on Acting With Youngsters', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golden Globes (Awards)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGregor, Ewan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-07T18:01:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9d8745d-0348-5335-bf41-a1ee0ca49599', 'word_count': 98, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9d8745d-0348-5335-bf41-a1ee0ca49599'}, {'abstract': 'Sony Music has released a very limited album of early Bob Dylan recordings to retain its copyright on them under the provisions of a new European law.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/08/arts/music/sony-issues-bob-dylan-recordings-to-keep-european-copyright.html', 'snippet': 'Sony Music has released a very limited album of early Bob Dylan recordings to retain its copyright on them under the provisions of a new European law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In an unusual response to provisions in a new European copyright law, scheduled to take effect by 2014, Sony Music has released a compilation of early Bob Dylan recordings that is bound to become one of his most collectible albums. “The 50th Anniversary Collection,” which carries a subtitle — “The Copyright Extension Collection, Vol. 1” — that explains its purpose, was rushed to only a handful of record shops in Germany, France, Sweden and Britain just after Christmas. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/arts/08DYLANjp/08DYLANjp-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 598, 'width': 598, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name'