major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nose', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Temperature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-07T19:18:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By C. Claiborne Ray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'C.', 'middlename': 'Claiborne', 'lastname': 'Ray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/f027283e-5bec-546e-87cd-2ac55dbd3c94', 'word_count': 244, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f027283e-5bec-546e-87cd-2ac55dbd3c94'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Midler will star in the one-character play “I’ll Eat You Last: A Chat With Sue Mengers,” about the powerful Hollywood agent whose clients included Barbra Streisand, Steve McQueen, Faye Dunaway and Michael Caine.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/07/bette-midler-to-play-super-agent-sue-mengers-on-broadway/', 'snippet': 'Ms. Midler will star in the one-character play “I’ll Eat You Last: A Chat With Sue Mengers,” about the powerful Hollywood agent whose clients included Barbra Streisand, Steve McQueen, Faye Dunaway and Michael Caine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The recipe for a successful one-character play would, at minimum, seem to call for two things: a powerful person to base it upon and a powerful person to play her. And a newly announced theater project surely has both: Bette Midler will perform on Broadway for the first time in more than 30 years in a play about the Hollywood superagent Sue Mengers, its producers said on Monday. The play, called “I’ll Eat You Last: A Chat With Sue Mengers,” is written by John Logan and will be directed by Joe Mantello. It is scheduled to open on April 24 at a Shubert theater still to be determined.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None,