e', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f26a6191-1480-5e6f-b574-2d7d24f033ba', 'word_count': 513, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f26a6191-1480-5e6f-b574-2d7d24f033ba'}, {'abstract': 'Our weekly look at what our writers and editors are reading.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/07/walkabout-17-swiping-through-disney-and-learning-how-to-survive-avalanches/', 'snippet': 'Our weekly look at what our writers and editors are reading.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Big, Magical Data In the coming months, Disney plans to introduce a vacation management system called MyMagic+ that will allow visitors to buy Mickey Mouse ears with a swipe of a rubber bracelet encoded with credit card information. (The New York Times)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Walkabout — 1/7: Swiping Through Disney, and Learning How to Survive Avalanches', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-07T19:35:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff6f1c55-fed0-5f4f-983f-fef821f43ea5', 'word_count': 151, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff6f1c55-fed0-5f4f-983f-fef821f43ea5'}, {'abstract': 'The primates’ willingness to help out and interact with strangers, a trait not shared by chimpanzees, offers clues about the origins of similar impulses in humans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/08/science/the-unexpected-altruism-of-bonobos.html', 'snippet': 'The primates’ willingness to help out and interact with strangers, a trait not shared by chimpanzees, offers clues about the origins of similar impulses in humans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bonobos will happily share their food with a stranger, and even give up their own meal — but only if the stranger offers them social interaction, evolutionary anthropologists at Duke University report in the journal PLoS One. The researchers, Jingzhi Tan and Brian Hare, say their findings may shed light on the origins of altruism in humans. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/science/08OBAPE/08OBAPE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/08/science/08OBAPE/08OBAPE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/science/08OBAPE/08OBAPE-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/science/08OBAPE/08OBAPE-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1333, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/science/08OBAPE/08OBAPE-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/08/science/08OBAPE/08OBAPE-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/science/08OBAPE/08OBAPE-thumbLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 