ners that read: “Get rid of censorship. The Chinese people want freedom.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'As my colleague Edward Wong reports, hundreds of protesters gathered outside the headquarters of a newspaper office in southern China on Monday to register their anger at the censorship of a recent editorial.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video of Chinese Censorship Protest', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Censorship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guangzhou (China)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-07T19:53:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8cadfcc0-1ce1-52fc-92c7-060d8461ccde', 'word_count': 205, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8cadfcc0-1ce1-52fc-92c7-060d8461ccde'}, {'abstract': 'Bev Kearney, Texas’s longtime women’s track and field coach, resigned after admitting to an affair with an athlete 10 years ago.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/07/texas-track-coach-resigns-after-admitting-10-year-old-affair/', 'snippet': 'Bev Kearney, Texas’s longtime women’s track and field coach, resigned after admitting to an affair with an athlete 10 years ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On one hand, the story of Bev Kearney, the longtime women’s track and field coach at the University of Texas, sounds just like the disappointing stories about a lot of coaches. She was found to have had an affair with a student and was pressured to resign by the school, which she did on Saturday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/sports/08kearney/08kearney-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 709, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/sports/08kearney/08kearney-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1417, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/sports/08kearney/08kearney-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/08/sports/08kearney/08kearney-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/sports/08kearney/08kearney-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Texas Track Coach Resigns After Admitting 10-Year-Old Affair', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Track and Field', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Texas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-07T19:54:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b06a687-6d8f-5a54-aa58-f83d3b7c185f', 'word_count': 328, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b06a687-6d8f-5a54-aa58-f83d3b7c185f'}, {'abstract': '“Le Jardin,” valued at $1 million, will go back to the Museum of Modern Art in Stockholm.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/07/stolen-matisse-to-be-returned-to-swedish-museum/', 'snippet': '“Le Jardin,” valued at $1 million, will go back to the Museum of Modern Art in Stockholm.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Twenty-five years ago, a burglar smashed his way into Stockholm’s Museum of Modern Art and took a Matisse oil painting called “Le Jardin.” Now the work, valued at $1 million, has been recovered and will be returned to the museum.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/07/arts/artsspecial/07MATISSE/07MATISSE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 682, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/07/arts/artsspecial/07MATISSE/07MATISSE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1363, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/07/arts/artsspecial/07MATISSE/07MATISSE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/07/arts/artsspecial/07MATISSE/07MATISSE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type'