en shutter shows right after the new year, when the profitable holiday season gives way to the reliably coldest months – January and February – on the Broadway calendar.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cold Spell Hits Broadway Box Office', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Wicked (Play)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Butz, Norbert Leo', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holmes, Katie', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-07T21:26:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d31fdcf-7fec-5452-b974-34b02c7e44f6', 'word_count': 244, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d31fdcf-7fec-5452-b974-34b02c7e44f6'}, {'abstract': 'The excellent condition of a newly discovered 13th-century chapel has stirred hopes among archaeologists that an entire city may be largely intact underground.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/08/science/under-turkish-mud-well-preserved-byzantine-chapel.html', 'snippet': 'The excellent condition of a newly discovered 13th-century chapel has stirred hopes among archaeologists that an entire city may be largely intact underground.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DEMRE, Turkey — In the fourth century A.D., a bishop named Nicholas transformed the city of Myra, on the Mediterranean coast of what is now Turkey, into a Christian capital. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': Non