firstname': 'Sophie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brickman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fcd0419-76a6-55a2-8040-cee11331fc65', 'word_count': 1182, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fcd0419-76a6-55a2-8040-cee11331fc65'}, {'abstract': 'The band is in negotiations with a number of subscription services for the right to stream “Whole Lotta Love,” “Stairway to Heaven” and the rest of the band’s classic catalog. Among the services in potential competition are Spotify, Rhapsody and Rdio.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/07/coming-soon-to-online-streaming-led-zeppelin/', 'snippet': 'The band is in negotiations with a number of subscription services for the right to stream “Whole Lotta Love,” “Stairway to Heaven” and the rest of the band’s classic catalog. Among the services in potential competition are Spotify, Rhapsody and R...', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the 1960s and ’70s, Led Zeppelin’s tough negotiations with record companies and concert promoters helped transform the music industry. Now the band is poised to make a change to the industry’s latest hot sector: online subscription services.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Coming Soon to Online Streaming: Led Zeppelin', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Audio Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Swift, Taylor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deezer', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Led Zeppelin', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rdio', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rhapsody.com', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Spotify', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-07T21:31:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4bda0bdf-c87b-561e-9b68-8eeb7f539d51', 'word_count': 460, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4bda0bdf-c87b-561e-9b68-8eeb7f539d51'}, {'abstract': 'The Buffalo Bills joined the trend of N.F.L. teams hiring a college coach, but the choice of Doug Marrone wasn’t the expected one.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/07/marrone-nabs-unlikely-seat-in-coaching-musical-chairs/', 'snippet': 'The Buffalo Bills joined the trend of N.F.L. teams hiring a college coach, but the choice of Doug Marrone wasn’t the expected one.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is no stretch to say this year’s coaching carousel has gone a little off-kilter, which was perhaps inevitable when there were seven openings at once in the N.F.L. It produced the twin curiosities of Bill O’Brien being briefly in the mix after one whole season as a head coach at Penn State and Oregon’s Chip Kelly making the interview rounds before reportedly retreating back to the land of the Ducks, where N.C.A.A. troubles may or may not await him. And the college-coach craze may continue with either Alabama’s Nick Saban or Notre Dame’s Brian Kelly after the B.C.S. title game Monday night.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Marrone Nabs Unlikely Seat in Coaching Musical Chairs', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Buffalo Bills', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Syracuse University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-07T21:32:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b547ca6-50b6-597e-887d-a91f4734b3f5', 'word_count': 398, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b547ca6-50b6-597e-887d-a91f4734b3f5'}, {'abstract': 'Researcher video shows how an infant may recognize his mother’s accent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/health/100000001991101/baby-recognizess-mothers-accent.html', 'snippet': 'Researcher video shows how an infant may recognize his mother’s accent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Researcher video shows how an infant may recognize his mother’s accent.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/07/science/video-baby/video-baby-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/07/science/video-baby/video-baby-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/07/science/video-baby/video-baby-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/07/science/video-baby/vi