jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Today’s Scuttlebot: Game Wreckers and a Changing C.E.S.', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-07T21:36:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d61e1790-e6ef-50a6-be89-695284272a13', 'word_count': 133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d61e1790-e6ef-50a6-be89-695284272a13'}, {'abstract': 'Why a structural-deficit stalemate currently looks like a plausible American future.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/07/deficits-forever/', 'snippet': 'Why a structural-deficit stalemate currently looks like a plausible American future.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Okay, smart guy, I can imagine a reader of the preceding post saying, you’ve just explained why you don’t think a grand bargain is going to resolve our fiscal dilemma any time soon. But just last week, you were explaining why the Democrats’ willingness to define “rich” upward made it seem less likely that they would be able to raise tax rates high enough to pay for the government they want, and in the same post you noted\xa0the conservative, entitlement-reforming path to fiscal sustainability also has “an air of fantasy about it.” So if liberals can’t win, conservatives can’t win, and the two sides can’t strike a deal, how are we actually going to get our fiscal house in order?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Deficits Forever?', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-07T21:40:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/49d25de2-2abc-5bec-826a-3e389d556ebe', 'word_count': 639, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49d25de2-2abc-5bec-826a-3e389d556ebe'}, {'abstract': 'Officials could not say for sure whether the low growth reflected the start of a trend or the continuing effects of the recession.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/08/us/health-spending-growth-stays-low-for-third-straight-year.html', 'snippet': 'Officials could not say for sure whether the low growth reflected the start of a trend or the continuing effects of the recession.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — National health spending climbed to $2.7 trillion in 2011, or an average of $8,700 for every person in the country, but as a share of the economy, it remained stable for the third consecutive year, the Obama administration said Monday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Growth of Health Spending Stays Low', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Growth of Health Spending Stays Low', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pear, Robert', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Health Affairs (Journal)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-07T21:48:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Pear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pear', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e916636-a47a-5d0a-9f59-54ea2df457f8', 'word_count': 786, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e916636-a47a-5d0a-9f59-54ea2df457f8'}, {'abstract': 'Analysts say the consolidation of the car rental business may not affect prices in the short term, but they are less certain about the long-term implications.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/08/business/avis-and-hertz-expand-raising-questions-over-future-rates.html', 'snippet': 'Analysts say the consolidation of the car rental business may not affect prices in the short term, but they are less certain about the long-term implications.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The car rental business is consolidating, with Hertz’s acquisition of Dollar Thrifty in November and the Avis Budget Group’s announcement last week that it planned to buy the car-sharing company Zipcar. Does this mean that consumers will have fewer options and end up paying more to rent a car? ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/business/RENTAL/RENTAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/08/business/RENTAL/RENTAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/business/RENTAL/RENTAL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 650, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/business/RENTAL/RENTAL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1300, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/business/RENTAL/RENTAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/08/business/RENTAL/RENTAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/business/RENTAL/RENTAL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Avis and Hertz Acquisitions Raise Questions Over Rate Trend', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Car Rental Shuffle', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Renting and Leasing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Business Travel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Avis Budget Group Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Zipcar Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hertz Global Holdings Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-07T21:52:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harriet Edleson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harriet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Edleson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/52b60c07-88ce-54bf-b074-bf54e3ca211d', 'word_count': 1094, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52b60c07-88ce-54bf-b074-bf54e3ca211d'}, {'abstract': 'After the March 3 closing, the New Amsterdam Theater will be renovated over several months before “Aladdin” moves in.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/07/mary-poppins-to-fly-off-as-aladdin-lands-on-broadway/', 'snippet': 'After the March 3 closing, the New Amsterdam Theater will be renovated over several months before “Aladdin” moves in.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Broadway musical “Mary Poppins” will close on March 3 at the New Amsterdam Theater to make way for extensive renovations of the Disney-owned house before its expected next tenant: A musical adaptation of the company’s 1992 animated film “Aladdin,” according to two Broadway theater executives. The two executives spoke on condition of anonymity to discuss production plans that remain confidential. A Disney spokesman did not immediately return a phone message seeking comment on Monday.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Mary Poppins’ To Fly Off as ‘Aladdin’ Lands on Broadway', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Mary Poppins’ to Close, Ceding to ‘Aladdin’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beguelin, Chad', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mackintosh, Cameron', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Menken, Alan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rice, Tim', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Walt Disney Company', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-07T21:52:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c7a185af-bee1-5412-bd21-e7eb6f7f22aa', 'word_count': 270, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c7a185af-bee1-5412-bd21-e7eb6f7f22aa'}, {'abstract': 'Carne cruda, or raw beef like steak tartare, is a classic accompaniment for dolcetto in Piedmont in Italy', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/dining/with-dolcetto-a-dish-of-raw-beef.html', 'snippet': 'Carne cruda, or raw beef like steak tartare, is a classic accompaniment for dolcetto in Piedmont in Italy', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the panel members tasted the earthy yet elegant dolcettos, we were unanimous in suggesting crudo to go alongside. And we did not mean raw fish. Carne cruda, or raw beef like steak tartare, is a classic accompaniment for dolcetto in Piedmont in Italy. As prepared in Alba, fillet of beef is hand cut and dressed with olive oil, lemon and maybe anchovies and shavings of white truffle. But the evening before the tasting, I had a different type of carne cruda, also perfect with dolcetto, at Commerce, in the West Village. Harold Moore, the chef and a partner, seared beef deckle and served thin slices, still raw in the center, over charred mushrooms, with a light salad garnish, a shot of spice and a drizzle of ponzu, a citrus-flavored soy sauce. He calls the dish “toro” because it’s similar to his preparation for seared tuna. Can’t find a butcher who sells tasty beef deckle, the rib cap? A hunk of fillet will do just fine. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/dining/09PAIR/09PAIR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 33