aph': 'A new study suggests that babies learn bits of their native languages even before they are born.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/24/health/well_perceptions/well_perceptions-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 219, 'width': 219, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/24/health/well_perceptions/well_perceptions-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 219, 'width': 219, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/24/health/well_perceptions/well_perceptions-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/24/health/well_perceptions/well_perceptions-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/24/health/well_perceptions/well_perceptions-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Babies Seem to Pick Up Language in Utero', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Perceptions: Babies Seem to Pick Up Language in Utero', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Language and Languages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-07T22:15:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Bakalar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakalar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c4e8100-ef76-50ef-ae11-b7b66301fd34', 'word_count': 279, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c4e8100-ef76-50ef-ae11-b7b66301fd34'}, {'abstract': 'Nearly 200 comments resulted from an article about subway operators whose trains fatally struck people; some commenters sought preventive steps, but others described their own experiences or those of loved ones.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/07/readers-share-own-stories-of-death-on-the-tracks/', 'snippet': 'Nearly 200 comments resulted from an article about subway operators whose trains fatally struck people; some commenters sought preventive steps, but others described their own experiences or those of loved ones.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A front-page article last week by our colleague Matt Flegenheimer about subway operators whose trains fatally struck people drew nearly 200 comments. Some called for installing sliding barriers on the platforms, a proposal that transit officials said would be “both expensive and extremely challenging,” though not out of the question. Some readers wondered why trains did not simply slow down sooner, even if it meant delaying commutes.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Readers Share Own Stories of Death on the Tracks', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Readers Share Stories Of Deaths on the Tracks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Railroad Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subways', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suicides and Suicide Attempts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-07T22:21:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37e607a8-64d1-5875-b81b-ad227d414a7b', 'word_count': 1574, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37e607a8-64d1-5875-b81b-ad227d414a7b'}, {'abstract': 'Boys need to understand and learn how to care for their genitals, including getting regular exams if they had undescended testes at birth.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/07/needed-more-attention-to-boys-development/', 'snippet': 'Boys need to understand and learn how to care for their genitals, including getting regular exams if they had undescended testes at birth.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When you learn how to examine the female reproductive system in medical school, you generally work with a professional surrogate patient, and there is often a humiliating moment when you try to palpate the ovaries only to be told, in no uncertain terms, that you are way off-target. At such a moment, the male reproductive system seems quite simple and accessible.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/science/08KLAS/08KLAS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 838, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/science/08KLAS/08KLAS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1925, 'width': 1575, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/science/08KLAS/08KLAS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/201