cs to sports psychology concepts like leadership, consistency and minimizing errors shows Alabama has the edge over Notre Dame.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carlton J. Chin, a portfolio strategist and fund manager, and Jay P. Granat, psychotherapist, are authors of “Who Will Win the Big Game? A Psychological & Mathematical Method.” They have previously written about the N.C.A.A. men’s basketball tournament, the N.B.A. finals and the Super Bowl.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Keeping Score: Characteristics of a Champion', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'BCS National Championship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Alabama', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Notre Dame', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-07T22:45:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By CARLTON J. CHIN and JAY P. GRANAT', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carlton', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'CHIN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jay', 'middlename': 'P.', 'lastname': 'GRANAT', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7593e27-1803-5328-b122-b82a25d13731', 'word_count': 674, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7593e27-1803-5328-b122-b82a25d13731'}, {'abstract': 'The fourth season of “Cougar Town,” which begins on Tuesday night, finds it at a new network — TBS — and without its creators, Bill Lawrence and Kevin Biegel, at the helm.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/08/arts/television/cougar-town-begins-fourth-season-with-new-show-runner.html', 'snippet': 'The fourth season of “Cougar Town,” which begins on Tuesday night, finds it at a new network — TBS — and without its creators, Bill Lawrence and Kevin Biegel, at the helm.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The whole point of having a child is to love it and to nurture it and to worry about it,” Courteney Cox’s character, Jules, says in the second episode of the new season of “Cougar Town.” “And eventually, if you’ve done your job right, the child doesn’t need you anymore.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/arts/08COUGAR/08COUGAR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/08/arts/08COUGAR/08COUGAR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/arts/08COUGAR/08COUGAR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/arts/08COUGAR/08COUGAR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/arts/08COUGAR/08COUGAR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/08/arts/08COUGAR/08COUGAR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/arts/08COUGAR/08COUGAR-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Dawn for a Flo