nd General Motors aim to create applications that customers can upload to their smartphones.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/07/ford-and-g-m-battle-to-win-wired-drivers/', 'snippet': 'By providing an open platform for developers to create new software, Ford and General Motors aim to create applications that customers can upload to their smartphones.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Automakers began rolling out heavy artillery in the infotainment war, as the Ford Motor Company and General Motors introduced on Monday at the Consumer Electronics Show in Las Vegas open platform software kits that would enable developers to create applications for use in vehicles.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ford and G.M. Battle to Win Wired Drivers', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Consumer Electronics Show', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Software', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ford Motor Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Highway Traffic Safety Administration', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Las Vegas (Nev)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-08T00:00:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Stenquist', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stenquist', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72b47490-d7f9-5f5b-9c0f-7b