 and it went viral. Since then, I have received a deluge of messages from people expressing their support.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/opinion/0108OPEDwilliamson/0108OPEDwilliamson-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 585, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/08/opinion/0108OPEDwilliamson/0108OPEDwilliamson-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 585}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/opinion/0108OPEDwilliamson/0108OPEDwilliamson-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/opinion/0108OPEDwilliamson/0108OPEDwilliamson-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/opinion/0108OPEDwilliamson/0108OPEDwilliamson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/08/opinion/0108OPEDwilliamson/0108OPEDwilliamson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/opinion/0108OPEDwilliamson/0108OPEDwilliamson-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'I Was Wounded; My Honor Wasn’t', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'I Was Wounded; My Honor Wasn’t', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's Rights", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-08T01:08:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sohaila Abdulali', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sohaila', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abdulali', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e370812-24c6-5e35-af88-e3f0299cff37', 'word_count': 913, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e370812-24c6-5e35-af88-e3f0299cff37'}, {'abstract': 'The Crohn’s and Colitis Foundation of America has started a new series of advertisements to help make the public aware of inflammatory bowel disease.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/08/business/media/crohns-and-colitis-foundation-begins-new-campaign.html', 'snippet': 'The Crohn’s and Colitis Foundation of America has started a new series of advertisements to help make the public aware of inflammatory bowel disease.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A NEW print ad by the Crohn’s and Colitis Foundation of America shows a closed bathroom stall, with the gap below the door revealing the enormous clown shoes of the occupant. “I.B.D. is no laughing matter,” says the headline.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/business/Adco/Adco-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 761, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/business/Adco/Adco-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1521, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Finding a Way to Talk About a Disquieting Condition', 'kicker': 'Advertising', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Finding a Way to Talk About a Disquieting Condition', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Newman, Andrew Adam', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Crohn's Disease", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colitis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Digestive Tract', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bowels', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Crohn's and Colitis Foundation of America", 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-08T01:12:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Adam Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'Adam', 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4e898da-e485-5b8d-8d3f-30607f2ce9cf', 'word_count': 799, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4e898da-e485-5b8d-8d3f-30607f2ce9cf'}, {'abstract': 'The deans of the nation’s top public health schools sent a letter to President Obama condemning the use of a vaccination campaign ruse that has caused a severe backlash in Pakistan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/08/us/deans-condemn-vaccine-ruse-used-in-bin-laden-hunt.html', 'snippet': 'The deans of the nation’s top public health schools sent a letter to President Obama condemning the use of a vaccination campaign ruse that has caused a severe backlash in Pakistan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The deans of the nation’s top public health schools sent a letter to President Obama on Monday condemning the Central Intelligence Agency’s use of a vaccination campaign ruse in the hunt for Osama bin Laden. The letter was signed by deans at Columbia, Harvard, Johns Hopkins and nine other universities. The C.I.A. has admitted hiring a Pakistani doctor to give out hepatitis B vaccine, apparently in an effort to get DNA samples from the compound that it suspected was Bin Laden’s hide-out. That has caused a severe backlash against vaccination in Pakistan. Nine polio vaccinators have been shot dead, and the effort to fight polio there was halted for weeks. Deaths from measles also soared in 2012, to 306 from 64 the year before. Resistance to measles vaccine in the populous Sindh province was blamed. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Deans Condemn Vaccine Ruse Used in Bin Laden Hunt', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Deans Condemn Vaccine Ruse Used In Bin Laden Hunt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McNeil, Donald G Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Intelligence Agency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DNA (Deoxyribonucleic Acid)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-08T01:14:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Donald G. McNeil Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Donald', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'McNeil', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/fbb9a408-9192-5da1-ba4f-d4aedec25075', 'word_count': 135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fbb9a408-9192-5da1-ba4f-d4aedec25075'}, {'abstract': 'Justices raised concerns that a federal law meant to address abuses in class-action cases might harm rather than help corporate defendants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/08/business/supreme-court-weighs-a-limit-on-class-action-filings.html', 'snippet': 'Justices raised concerns that a federal law meant to address abuses in class-action cases might harm rather than help corporate defendants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Supreme Court struggled on Monday to determine whether plaintiffs’ class-action lawyers can avoid having their cases heard in federal court by stipulating that they will seek less than the $5 million threshold set in a 2005 federal law.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Justices Weigh Intent of a Class-Action Law', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Justices Weigh Intent Of a Class-Action Law', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-08T01:17:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Liptak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liptak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e0aad64-0537-5a0b-8c6a-9f9956843c68', 'word_count': 810, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e0aad64-0537-5a0b-8c6a-9f9956843c68'}, {'abstract': 'A judge ruled that the Roman Catholic Archdiocese of Los Angeles must release the names of church officials included in confidential records about priests accused of sexually abusing children.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/08/us/california-archdiocese-loses-ruling-on-records.html', 'snippet': 'A judge ruled that the Roman Catholic Archdiocese of Los Angeles must release the names of church officials included in confidential records about priests accused of sexually abusing children.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Los Angeles judge ruled Monday that the Roman Catholic Archdiocese of Los Angeles must release the names of high-ranking church officials included in some 30,000 pages of confidential records about priests accused of sexually abusing children. The decision reverses a ruling by a judge who said he worried that including the names could further embarrass the church. But in her ruling Monday, Judge Emilie H. Elias said the public’s right to know how the nation’s largest archdiocese handled molesting charges outweighed other concerns. The records include reports of abuse, letters to the Vatican and psychiatric reports and are likely to be released in the next several weeks, lawyers said. The Los Angeles Times and The Associated Press had filed an objection to the previous ruling that all names of church employees, including Cardinal Roger M. Mahony, would be blacked out. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California: Archdiocese Loses Ruling on Records', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | West', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'California: Archdiocese Loses Ruling On Records', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 3, 'major'