h tabloid owned by Rupert Murdoch.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — In the first of a number of high-profile trials expected this year in cases of alleged criminal wrongdoing at Britain’s freewheeling newspapers, a high-ranking Scotland Yard officer went on trial on Monday, charged with seeking to sell confidential police information to a tabloid that Rupert Murdoch ordered shut 18 months ago as the phone-hacking scandal erupted around his British newspaper empire. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trial Begins for Scotland Yard Officer in Phone-Hacking Scandal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trial Begins for Scotland Yard Officer in Phone-Hacking Scandal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burns, John F', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wiretapping and Other Eavesdropping Devices and Methods', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Casburn, April', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News of the World', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Scotland Yard (Metropolitan Police Service)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sun, The (British Newspaper)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News Corporation', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-08T02:06:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By John F. Burns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Burns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/60cb4a76-35f2-507b-922c-9d3e942f180e', 'word_count': 787, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60cb4a76-35f2-507b-922c-9d3e942f180e'}, {'abstract': 'Young undocumented immigrants who are allowed to work legally should be allowed to drive legally, too.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/08/opinion/dreaming-and-driving.html', 'snippet': 'Young undocumented immigrants who are allowed to work legally should be allowed to drive legally, too.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Young undocumented immigrants who are allowed to work legally in the United States should be allowed to drive legally, too. It makes perfect sense, if only for public-safety reasons: people need to drive to work, and they should follow the law and be demonstrably competent, registered and insured. But with the politics of immigration, nothing is ever that simple.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dreaming and Driving', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dreaming and Driving', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drivers Licenses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deferred Action for Childhood Arrivals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dream Act (Development, Relief and Education for Minors Act)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-08T02:08:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/fdc94f2a-8d05-5f40-9f63-c107a10f9326', 'word_count': 385, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fdc94f2a-8d05-5f40-9f63-c107a10f9326'}, {'abstract': 'Devices like tablets and smartphones have transformed the way people use the Internet, making the dominance of a company like Google potentially more precarious than it seems.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/08/business/mobile-apps-drive-rapid-changes-in-search-technology.html', 'snippet': 'Devices like tablets and smartphones have transformed the way people use the Internet, making the dominance of a company like Google potentially more precarious than it seems.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — When the Federal Trade Commission decided last week to close its antitrust investigation of Google without charges, one important factor, though hardly mentioned, was just beneath the surface: the mobile revolution. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/business/Googlejp/Googlejp-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 764, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/business/Googlejp/Googlejp-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1529, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/business/Googlejp/Googlejp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/08/business/Googlejp/Googlejp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/business/Googlejp/Googlej