01/08/nyregion/cuomo-to-order-hospitals-to-use-new-sepsis-procedures.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo will announce in his State of the State Message this week that all New York hospitals must adopt aggressive procedures for identifying sepsis in patients.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo will announce in his State of the State Message this week that every hospital in New York must adopt aggressive procedures for identifying sepsis in patients, including the use of a countdown clock to begin treatment within an hour of spotting it, a state official said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cuomo Plans New Rules in Fight Against Sepsis', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cuomo Plans New Rules In Fight Against Sepsis', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dwyer, Jim', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sepsis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests (Medical)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York University Langone Medical Center', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Staunton, Rory', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-08T03:09:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Dwyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dwyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4ab2d8d-321d-51c8-b43a-6648772975bd', 'word_count': 510, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4ab2d8d-321d-51c8-b43a-6648772975bd'}, {'abstract': 'Linebacker Manti Te’o (Big Five) and quarterback Everett Golson (Little Five) wear the same number and are both stars for Notre Dame.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/08/sports/ncaafootball/irishs-teo-and-golson-share-a-number-and-the-spotlight.html', 'snippet': 'Linebacker Manti Te’o (Big Five) and quarterback Everett Golson (Little Five) wear the same number and are both stars for Notre Dame.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MIAMI GARDENS, Fla. — Manti Te’o was 5, on a drive around his hometown, Laie, Hawaii, when his father turned to him and asked, “Son, when you play football, what number do you want to be?”', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/sports/FIVE2/FIVE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 624, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/08/sports/FIVE2/FIVE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 624}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/sports/FIVE2/FIVE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 985, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/sports/FIVE2/FIVE2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1417, 'width': 1362, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/sports/FIVE2/FIVE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/08/sports/FIVE2/FIVE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/sports/FIVE2/FIVE2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sharing a Number, and the Spotlight', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sharing a Number, And the Spotlight', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Notre Dame', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "Te'o, Manti", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Golson, Everett', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-08T03:10:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Rohan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef1ea0fb-d638-5be1-9c71-ffd4998fd34b', 'word_count': 739, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef1ea0fb-d638-5be1-9c71-ffd4998fd34b'}, {'abstract': 'In a complaint filed on Monday, a group said that the Chicago Public Schools have repeatedly failed to evaluate children with disabilities and move them into special education preschool programs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/08/education/chicago-public-schools-faulted-on-assessing-learning-disabilities.html', 'snippet': 'In a complaint filed on Monday, a group said that the Chicago Public Schools have repeatedly failed to evaluate children with disabilities and move them into special education preschool programs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Rashaan Payne was 2 years old, his pediatrician noticed that he was not talking at the level of most children his age. After autism was diagnosed, Rashaan began receiving speech therapy once a week at his home on the South Side of Chicago, paid for by the federal and state governments.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/us/SPECIAL/SPECIAL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/us/SPECIAL/SPECIAL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chicago Faulted on Learning Disabilities', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chicago Faulted on Learning Disabilities', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Special Education', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (Pre-School)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-08T03:12:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Motoko Rich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Motoko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f3f958e-9466-534a-9bc8-ea91af33cd2c', 'word_count': 801, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f3f958e-9466-534a-9bc8-ea91af33cd2c'}, {'abstract': 'It has taken 32 years for Jamal Crawford, the best shooter on the N.B.A.’s highest-scoring bench, to find a true home with the resurgent, out-from-under-the-rock Los Angeles Clippers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/08/sports/basketball/clippers-jamal-crawford-is-still-firing-away.html', 'snippet': 'It has taken 32 years for Jamal Crawford, the best shooter on the N.B.A.’s highest-scoring bench, to find a true home with the resurgent, out-from-under-the-rock Los Angeles Clippers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Chicago was great for Jamal Crawford’s first four N.B.A. seasons, with adoring fans and lots of shot opportunities, even if his Bulls went 89-239.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/sports/YCRAWFORD/YCRAWFORD-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 514, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/08/sports/YCRAWFORD/YCRAWFORD-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 514}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/sports/YCRAWFORD/YCRAWFORD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 877, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/sports/YCRAWFORD/YCRAWFORD-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1753, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/sports/YCRAWFORD/YCRAWFORD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/08/sports/YCRAWFORD/YCRAWFORD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/sports/YCRAWFORD/YCRAWFORD-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Still Firing Away', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Still Firing Away', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Clippers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crawford, Jamal', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-08T03:14:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Heisler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Heisler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/69fb3eba-b845-5168-a234-495072638baf', 'word_count': 933, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69fb3eba-b845-5168-a234-495072638baf'}, {'abstract': 'The Trust for Public Land, a nonprofit group, has joined with local residents to promote the idea of a park for Queens, like Manhattan’s High Line, where unused train tracks lie.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/08/nyregion/queens-wants-to-transform-an-abandoned-railway-into-a-park.html', 'snippet': 'The Trust for Public Land, a nonprofit group, has joined with local residents to promote the idea of a park for Queens, like Manhattan’s High Line, where unused train tracks lie.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It has been abandoned for five decades, a railway relic that once served Queens passengers on the old Rockaway Beach branch of the Long Island Rail Road. For all those years, no one paid much notice to the ghostly tracks, long overgrown with trees and vines, as they ran silently behind tidy houses in Rego Park, dipped through ravines in Forest Park and hovered above big-box stores in Glendale.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/nyregio