do the striking journalists want?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/08/journalists-go-on-strike-in-southern-china/', 'snippet': 'What outcome do the striking journalists want?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In “Supporters Back Strike at Newspaper in China,” Edward Wong reports on a growing demand for press freedom in southern China. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/world/asia/08china2-LN/08china2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/08/world/asia/08china2-LN/08china2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/world/asia/08china2-LN/08china2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/world/asia/08china2-LN/08china2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/world/asia/08china2-LN/08china2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/08/world/asia/08china2-LN/08china2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/world/asia/08china2-LN/08china2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Journalists Go on Strike in Southern China', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-08T09:30:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Gonchar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonchar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a8d7fd6-7ada-5b2d-bf04-cafee08aa28f', 'word_count': 112, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a8d7fd6-7ada-5b2d-bf04-cafee08aa28f'}, {'abstract': 'A bipartisan club of economists might have a way to solve traffic jams. (And to get your neighbor to pick up after the dog.)', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/13/magazine/should-we-tax-people-for-being-annoying.html', 'snippet': 'A bipartisan club of economists might have a way to solve traffic jams. (And to get your neighbor to pick up after the dog.)', 'lead_paragraph': 'Driving home during the holidays, I found myself trapped in the permanent traffic jam on I-95 near Bridgeport, Conn. In the back seat, my son was screaming. All around, drivers had the menaced, lifeless expressions that people get when they see cars lined up to the horizon. It was enough to make me wish for congestion pricing — a tax paid by drivers to enter crowded areas at peak times. After all, it costs drivers about $16 to enter central London during working hours. A few years ago, it nearly caught on in New York. And on that drive home, I would have happily paid whatever it cost to persuade some other drivers that it wasn’t worth it for them to be on the road.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/magazine/13economy/13economy-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 736, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/13/magazine/13economy/13economy-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 736}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/magazine/13economy/13economy-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 835, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/magazine/13economy/13economy-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1500, 'width': 1223, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/magazine/13economy/13economy-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/13/magazine/13economy/13economy-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/magazine/13economy/13economy-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Should We Tax People for Being Annoying?', 'kicker': 'It’s the Economy', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Tax on Annoying Behavior?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gasoline Tax (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sales and Excise Taxes', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-08T10:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Davidson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davidson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e196706-82bb-52b5-bf5b-5fc91e04b1f2', 'word_count': 1229, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e196706-82bb-52b5-bf5b-5fc91e04b1f2'}, {'abstract': 'Does publishing the names of handgun permit holders provide a public service in any way?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/08/did-a-newspaper-act-irresponsibly-by-publishing-the-addresses-of-gun-owners/', 'snippet': 'Does publishing the names of handgun permit holders provide a public service in any way?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Journal News, a newspaper serving the northern suburbs of New York City, published the names and addresses of handgun permit holders in two counties in New York State. The interactive map received more views than any other article in the paper’s history and generated significant outrage across the nation. Calls and e-mails to the newspaper became so threatening that it decided to hire armed security guards to protect the safety of its employees.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/26/nyregion/26gunmap-cityroom-LN/26gunmap-cityroom-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 542, 'width': 887, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/26/nyregion/26gunmap-cityroom-LN/26gunmap-cityroom-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 542, 'width': 887, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/26/nyregion/26gunmap-cityroom-LN/26gunmap-cityroom-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/12/26/nyregion/26gunmap-cityroom-LN/26gunmap-cityroom-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/26/nyregion/26gunmap-cityroom-LN/26gunmap-cityroom-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 149, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Did a Newspaper Act Irresponsibly by Publishing the Addresses of Gun Owners?', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-08T10:00:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Gonchar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonchar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/faa367da-28c3-5474-9413-6bdc9cfe2b53', 'word_count': 551, 'uri': 'nyt://article/faa367da-28c3-5474-9413-6bdc9cfe2b53'}, {'abstract': 'For the Magnum photographer Alex Webb, how a picture turns out isn’t always up to him.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/08/alex-webb-rendering-a-complex-world-in-color-and-black-and-white/', 'snippet': 'For the Magnum photographer Alex Webb, how a picture turns out isn’t always up to him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For someone who says 99 percent of street photography is about failure, Alex Webb has had a notably successful career. From his early work in Haiti and along the United States-Mexico border, to recent projects in the United States Rust Belt, Mr. Webb, a member of Magnum Photos, had produced a deep archive of images rich in color and complexity. James Estrin recently discussed with him how his work has evolved over the last four decades. Their interview has been edited.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Alex Webb: Rendering a Complex World, in Color and Black-and-White', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Color', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Webb, Alex', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'APERTURE FOUNDATION', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Magnum Photos', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Haiti', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Istanbul (Turkey)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rochester (NY)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-08T10:00:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Estrin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Estrin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab894de4-4b06-5c2b-b5c6-4257680fe8bc', 'word_count': 1508, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab894de4-4b06-5c2b-b5c6-4257680fe8bc'}, {'abstract': 'A graying population and revised policies determining who gets priority for donated organs have led to a rising proportion of older adults receiving transplants.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/08/who-should-receive-organ-transplants/', 'snippet': 'A graying population and revised policies determining who gets priority for donated organs have led to a rising proportion of older adults receiving transplants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Joe Gammalo had been contending with pulmonary fibrosis, a scarring of the lungs, for more than a decade when he came to the Cleveland Clinic in 2008 seeking a lung transplant.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Should Receive Organ Transplants?', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Age, Chronological', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lungs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organ Donation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transplants', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cleveland Clinic', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Michigan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-08T10:42:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paula Span', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paula', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Span', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e665df4-37f8-55e7-8ea0-109133e71673', 'word_count': 869, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e665df4-37f8-55e7-8ea0-109133e71673'}, {'abstract': 'Jessie Brumfiel, a director of college counseling at Dunn School in California, advises juniors on how to jump-start their college searches in 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/08/counselors-calendar-january-juniors/', 'snippet': 'Jessie Brumfiel, a director of college counseling at Dunn School in California, advises juniors on how to jump-start thei