e president and general manger of the Lexus Division. “Our vision is a car equipped with an intelligent, always-attentive co-pilot whose skills contribute to safer driving.”', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/08/lexus-aims-gadgets-at-increasing-vehicle-safety/', 'snippet': '“For Toyota and Lexus, a driverless car is just a part of the story,” said Mark Templin, Toyota group vice president and general manger of the Lexus Division. “Our vision is a car equipped with an intelligent, always-attentive co-pilot whose skill...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Among the panoply of gizmos and gadgets taking bows this week at the Consumer Electronics Show in Las Vegas, relatively few are intended to keep you safe in an automobile — even in an automobile that’s driving itself.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lexus Aims Gadgets at Increasing Vehicle Safety', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Consumer Electronics Show', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lexus Division of Toyota Motor Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toyota Motor Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-08T11:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5561fcc0-2d0b-585e-a685-9a0b0a0d48fe', 'word_count': 338, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5561fcc0-2d0b-585e-a685-9a0b0a0d48fe'}, {'abstract': 'Political news from today’s Times and around the Web, plus a look at the latest happenings in Washington.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/08/the-early-word-legacy/', 'snippet': 'Political news from today’s Times and around the Web, plus a look at the latest happenings in Washington.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Today’s Times', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Early Word: Legacy', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-08T11:00:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jada F. Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jada', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71ed08b1-6fab-54d3-be7a-f402bacf2abf', 'word_count': 209, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71ed08b1-6fab-54d3-be7a-f402bacf2abf'}, {'abstract': 'Richard McCarthy, the new executive director, co-founded the Crescent City Farmer’s Market in New Orleans.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/08/new-leader-for-slow-food-usa/', 'snippet': 'Richard McCarthy, the new executive director, co-founded the Crescent City Farmer’s Market in New Orleans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Slow Food USA, the American chapter of the global Slow Food organization based near Turin, Italy, has hired a new executive director. The group has been without a national leader since Josh Viertel left in May, after a period filled with internal strife over its mission. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Leader for Slow Food USA', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'val