kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-08T13:16:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f9225b3-fdc1-5a9e-b7cc-3f3e5708bfa1', 'word_count': 77, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f9225b3-fdc1-5a9e-b7cc-3f3e5708bfa1'}, {'abstract': 'After paying back its bailout, A.I.G. is now considering whether to sue its government rescuers. | Bank of America continues a retreat from the home mortgage market. | Edward S. Lampert, chairman of Sears Holdings, is set to become its chief too. | In relaxing rules for liquidity, bank regulators acknowledged a reality, Andrew Ross Sorkin writes.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/01/08/a-i-g-weighs-suing-the-government/', 'snippet': 'After paying back its bailout, A.I.G. is now considering whether to sue its government rescuers. | Bank of America continues a retreat from the home mortgage market. | Edward S. Lampert, chairman of Sears Holdings, is set to become its chief too. ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'After paying back its $182 billion bailout, the American International Group is now considering whether to sue the government agencies that rescued it during the financial crisis. A.I.G.’s board is meeting on Wednesday to weigh joining a $25 billion lawsuit filed by Maurice R. Greenberg, the company’s former chief executive, claiming that the bailout cheated shareholders, DealBook’s Ben Protess and Michael J. de la Merced report.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A.I.G. Weighs Suing the Government', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-08T13:22:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c9a0ef1-fd93-5f6e-9425-c846a6af2387', 'word_count': 1901, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c9a0ef1-fd93-5f6e-9425-c846a6af2387'}, {'abstract': 'The actress performs a scene from Quiara Alegría Hudes’s Pulitzer Prize-winning play “Water by the Spoonful.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/08/in-performance-zabryna-guevara-of-water-by-the-spoonful/', 'snippet': 'The actress performs a scene from Quiara Alegría Hudes’s Pulitzer Prize-winning play “Water by the Spoonful.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Quiara Alegría Hudes’s play “Water by the Spoonful,” winner of the 2012 Pulitzer Prize for drama, is about the intersecting lives of a group of people struggling with issues of addiction, family resentment and forgiveness. In this scene Yazmin, an adjunct professor of music played by Zabryna Guevara, talks about how different she is from her soon-to-be ex-husband and other family members. The play continues through Jan. 27 at Second Stage Theater.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Performance: Zabryna Guevara of ‘Water by the Spoonful’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Guevara, Zabryna', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hudes, Quiara Alegria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Second Stage Theater', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-08T13:30:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'n