8dc3c14c-3727-568a-b17e-83c79f18cdff'}, {'abstract': 'Affluent immigrants are giving generously to universities, museums, concert halls and hospitals, as well as to groups focused on their own diasporas or homelands.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/nyregion/as-asian-americans-numbers-grow-so-does-their-philanthropy.html', 'snippet': 'Affluent immigrants are giving generously to universities, museums, concert halls and hospitals, as well as to groups focused on their own diasporas or homelands.', 'lead_paragraph': 'About 800 people gathered in November in a ballroom in Midtown Manhattan for one of the year’s more elegant galas. They dined on beef tenderloin with truffle butter, bid on ski and golf vacations in a charity auction, and gave more than $1 million to a nonprofit group based in New York. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/nyregion/08philan1_cnd/08philan1_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 418, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/08/nyregion/08philan1_cnd/08philan1_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 418}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/nyregion/08philan1_cnd/08philan1_cnd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 714, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/nyregion/08philan1_cnd/08philan1_cnd-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 961, 'width': 1378, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/nyregion/08philan1_cnd/08philan1_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/08/nyregion/08philan1_cnd/08philan1_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/nyregion/08philan1_cnd/08philan1_cnd-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Asian-Americans Gain Influence  in  Philanthropy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Asians in U.S. Gain Influence In Philanthropy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Semple, Kirk', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Asian-Americans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Korean-Americans', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chinese-Americans', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-08T15:56:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kirk Semple', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kirk', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Semple', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2a9b162-b243-59a0-b269-8457e65c974e', 'word_count': 1058, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2a9b162-b243-59a0-b269-8457e65c974e'}, {'abstract': 'After a dud of a championship game, critics ask why the bowl system endures.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/sports/is-there-a-cure-for-the-bcs-hangover.html', 'snippet': 'After a dud of a championship game, critics ask why the bowl system endures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For everyone but the true Alabama believers — and all the college football and Southeastern Conference powers that be who get stinking rich no matter what transpires in the actual sport — today feels like the cleanup from a very bad party. As we pick our way through the discarded golden streamers and trampled leprechaun hats and try to remember why exactly the bowl system survives several eons past its defensible existence, the day-after B.C.S. hangover has nothing to do with alcohol. You could try to put a positive spin on Alabama’s overwhelming victory by joining the raging “Nick Saban for Emperor” parade, but unless you were already one of those true Alabama believers, well, Saban does not make this easy, being roughly as huggable as a dyspeptic porcupine.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/sports/ncaafootball/09leadingpic/09leadingpic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/sports/ncaafootball/09leadingpic/09leadingpic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/sports/ncaafootball/09leadingpic/09leadingpic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/09/sports/ncaafootball/09leadingpic/09leadingpic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/sports/ncaafootball/09leadingpic/09leadingpic-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Is There a Cure for the B.C.S. Hangover?', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Alabama', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Notre Dame', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Southeastern Conference', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saban, Nick', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Griffin, Robert III', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-08T15:58:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37f0fa92-9f9e-5ade-b68f-ec15ae2046a6', 'word_count': 673, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37f0fa92-9f9e-5ade-b68f-ec15ae2046a6'}, {'abstract': 'Judy Battista, the N.F.L. reporter for The Times, will answer questions from readers.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/08/have-an-n-f-l-question-judy-battista-has-answers-6/', 'snippet': 'Judy Battista, the N.F.L. reporter for The Times, will answer questions from readers.', 'lead_paragraph': '10:45 a.m. | Updated How good are the Falcons? And the Seahawks? Can the Ravens beat the Broncos? Is Colin Kaepernick experienced enough to beat the Packers? Judy Battista, the N.F.L. reporter for The Times, will answer questions from readers about the playoffs and other football news. Use the comment field below for your questions. Answers will appear Friday on The Fifth Down.Comments for this fea