un Control', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-08T16:42:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Hulse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hulse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d332d660-e2f0-59e3-b30b-b87c62dac940', 'word_count': 831, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d332d660-e2f0-59e3-b30b-b87c62dac940'}, {'abstract': 'Expectations among investors and others are high for change under Xi Jinping, but he appears to be facing his first major test with the public blowup over the censoring of the liberal newspaper Southern Weekend.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/01/08/a-bull-in-stocks-but-a-bear-for-free-speech/', 'snippet': 'Expectations among investors and others are high for change under Xi Jinping, but he appears to be facing his first major test with the public blowup over the censoring of the liberal newspaper Southern Weekend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Shanghai stock market is officially in bull territory, having climbed just over 20 percent since early December. Economists’ forecasts for 2013 economic growth are for the most part cautiously positive, though heavy with caveats about calls for economic reforms. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Bull in Stocks, but a Bear for Free Speech', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank':