’s co-chief executives vowed in September to strengthen the bank’s finances without tapping shareholders. But American capital rules, noncore losses and a looming Libor settlement have raised the ante.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Raising Capital Makes Sense for Deutsche Bank', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deutsche Bank AG', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-08T16:44:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dominic Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dominic', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/365f3612-7c64-5ab7-9c49-9ea1980b00a3', 'word_count': 425, 'uri': 'nyt://article/365f3612-7c64-5ab7-9c49-9ea1980b00a3'}, {'abstract': 'Barry Bonds and Roger Clemens will almost certainly not be elected to the Baseball Hall of Fame in Cooperstown on Wednesday. But the way writers vote on them could provide a useful benchmark for how they are handling the steroids issue.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/08/suspicion-of-steroid-use-could-keep-bagwell-and-piazza-out-of-hall/', 'snippet': 'Barry Bonds and Roger Clemens will almost certainly not be elected to the Baseball Hall of Fame in Cooperstown on Wednesday. But the way writers vote on them could provide a useful benchmark for how they are handling the steroids issue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Barry Bonds and Roger Clemens, eligible to be elected to the Baseball Hall of Fame for the first time, will almost certainly not be named when the next choices for Cooperstown are announced on Wednesday. Instead, tallies of sportswriters who have publicly announced their ballots suggest that they may only get 40 to 50 percent of the vote, despite having statistical records that rank them as among the best players in history. A player must be named on 75 percent of the ballots to be elected to the Hall of Fame.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Suspicion of Steroid Use Could Keep Bagwell and Piazza Out of Hall', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-08T16:48:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8cb9752-7f19-53f7-a4ec-e7b7736ecc8b', 'word_count': 1694, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8cb9752-7f19-53f7-a4ec-e7b7736ecc8b'}, {'abstract': 'Couples perform a ritual for the long lives of their spouses, in Allahabad, Uttar Pradesh.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/08/image-of-the-day-jan-8/', 'snippet': 'Couples perform a ritual for the long lives of their spouses, in Allahabad, Uttar Pradesh.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Image of the Day: Jan. 8', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-08T16:49:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b45074d4-25aa-54e9-a7e3-aa71068c60c8', 'word_count': 1, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b45074d4-25aa-54e9-a7e3-aa71068c60c8'}, {'abstract': 'The Chilean director Pablo Larraín explains how he come to make three films about the Pinochet era even though he never set out to make a trilogy at all.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/08/pablo-larrain-and-his-unintentional-trilogy/', 'snippet': 'The Chilean director Pablo Larraín explains how he come to make three films about the Pinochet era even though he never set out to make a trilogy at all.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2008, the Chilean director Pablo Larraín made a splashy international debut with “Tony Manero,” a chilling portrait of a serial killer obsessed with John Travolta’s character in “Saturday Night Fever” and operating seemingly unhindered at the height of Gen. Augusto Pinochet’s dictatorship. A few years later, Mr. Larraín was back with “Post-Mortem,” another character study of a deviant personality, but set during the 1973 military coup that brought Pinochet to power.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pablo Larraín and His Unintentional Trilogy', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Larrain, Pablo', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chile', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-08T16:53:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Rohter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/10092afc-3720-58df-ac91-deefb23b2304', 'word_count': 1195, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10092afc-3720-58df-ac91-deefb23b2304'}, {'abstract': 'A writer suggests a way to enable voters to really know their representatives. Readers are invited to reply.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/