: 1027, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d56cf1c5-b399-5e29-b997-4ae491bd0036'}, {'abstract': 'The artist Max Mulhern has cast two huge dice — each 8 feet to a side — adrift in the waters of the Atlantic, in a project designed to turn its own fate over to chance.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/08/an-artists-game-of-chance-on-the-high-seas/', 'snippet': 'The artist Max Mulhern has cast two huge dice — each 8 feet to a side — adrift in the waters of the Atlantic, in a project designed to turn its own fate over to chance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dice have been around a long time, at least since man first carved bone, and are one of the most potent symbols we have of the vicissitudes of dumb luck. Which is part of their fascination for the artist Max Mulhern — he is endlessly interested in the role of chance in life — and one big reason he was inspired to create “Aqua Dice.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Artist’s Game of Chance on the High Seas', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boats and Boating', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Positioning System', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Navigation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Arp, Jean', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Le Corbusier', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Le Bateau Ivre', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canary Islands', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chesapeake Bay', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Las Vegas (Nev)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'ra