ount': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/64133b8f-ef24-5b1f-9b18-d731b0bb98e2'}, {'abstract': 'John Lithgow and Joshua McGuire in a scene from “The Magistrate” at the National Theater in London.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/theater/100000001992628/excerpt-the-magistrate.html', 'snippet': 'John Lithgow and Joshua McGuire in a scene from “The Magistrate” at the National Theater in London.', 'lead_paragraph': 'John Lithgow and Joshua McGuire in a scene from “The Magistrate” at the National Theater in London.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/arts/video-magistrate2/video-magistrate2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/08/arts/video-magistrate2/video-magistrate2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/arts/video-magistrate2/video-magistrate2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/08/arts/video-magistrate2/video-magistrate2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Excerpt: ‘The Magistrate’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lithgow, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-08T17:59:27+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'National Theater', 'person': [{'firstname': 'National', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Theater', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/855fc6b6-6758-5a57-98a3-095eee444616', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/855fc6b6-6758-5a57-98a3-095eee444616'}, {'abstract': 'I told one of my managers that I feel good about our prospects for next year, and she reminded me that I say that every year.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/08/can-i-afford-to-be-optimistic/', 'snippet': 'I told one of my managers that I feel good about our prospects for next year, and she reminded me that I say that every year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is time to complete the budget for 2013. I now have the final numbers from 2012 to help in the planning/forecasting/guessing game that I have been playing for 35 years. My comptroller reminds me that every year, for as long as she can remember, she has had to reduce my projections by midyear. Great. Is it a shortcoming to be optimistic if you own a company? The answer is yes, and no. At the moment, more yes.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Can I Afford To Be Optimistic?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Can I Afford\r\nTo Be Optimistic?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-08T18:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jay Goltz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goltz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/766be58e-78ff-57fc-9337-4d7d25f935f7', 'word_count': 750, 'uri': 'nyt://article/766be58e-78ff-57fc-9337-4d7d25f935f7'}, {'abstract': 'What happens when Guantanamo justice and the actual rule of law come into contact.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/08/material-support-for-terrorism/', 'snippet': 'What happens when Guantanamo justice and the actual rule of law come into contact.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When President George W. Bush established a prison at Guantánamo Bay on land rented from the Cuban dictatorship, held detainees without charge, often without evidence, and then concocted a system of “military tribunals” to try those detainees, he effectively created a separate justice system. One with only a passing resemblance to the “real,” constitutional system that functions fairly well on American soil.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Material Support for Terrorism’', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Military Tribunals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hamdan, Salim Ahmed', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-08T18:01:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa0b836e-9e20-5c17-a098-c66d43fddef5', 'word_count': 399, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa0b836e-9e20-5c17-a098-c66d43fddef5'}, {'abstract': 'Total spending on film and television in home entertainment formats rose slightly in 2012 to about $18 billion, according to the Digital Entertainment Group, a trade association.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/08/streaming-lifts-home-entertainment-spending/', 'snippet': 'Total spending on film and television in home entertainment formats rose slightly in 2012 to about $18 billion, according to the Digital Entertainment Group, a trade association.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Total spending on film and television in home entertainment formats rose ever so slightly in 2012, to about $18 billion, up 0.23 percent from $17.96 billion a year earlier, the Digital Entertainment Group, a trade association, said on Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Streaming Lifts Home Entertainment Spending', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Slight Spending Rise On Home Film and TV', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Digital Entertainment Group', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-08T18:04:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cieply', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cieply', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f75040bb-ea7d-573f-9c63-a97b19cc4c3b', 'word_count': 125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f75040bb-ea7d-573f-9c63-a97b19cc4c3b'}, {'abstract': 'The play will be directed by Ms. Shaw’s longtime collaborator, Deborah Warner.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/08/fiona-shaw-to-star-in-the-testament-of-mary-on-broadway/', 'snippet': 'The play will be directed by Ms. Shaw’s longtime collaborator, Deborah Warner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The acclaimed actress Fiona Shaw and her longtime collaborator, the director Deborah Warner, will return to Broadway this spring for the first time since their “Medea” in 2002 with another play about an emotionally vivid and vulnerable woman: “The Testament of Mary.” Ms. Shaw will play the Virgin Mary, struggling to come to grips with the life of her son some 20 years after the crucifixion. The play is scheduled to begin preview performances on March 26 at the Walter Kerr Theater and open on April 22.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fiona Shaw to Star in ‘The Testament of Mary’ on Broadway', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Play About Virgin Mary Is Headed to Broadway', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christians and Christianity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mary, Mother of Jesus', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mengers, Sue', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Metcalf, Laurie', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Midler, Bette', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rudin, Scott', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shaw, Fiona', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Toibin, Colm', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Warner, Deborah', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dublin (Ireland)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ireland', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-08T18:06:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f0fd564-b0bf-5edf-a1b7-e05fd28006b4', 'word_count': 730, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f0fd564-b0bf-5edf-a1b7-e05fd28006b4'}, {'abstract': 'Scott Shane, a Times national security reporter, was referred to in the government’s prosecution of a former C.I.A. official.', 'web_url': 'https://publiceditor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/08/was-a-reporters-role-in-a-government-prosecution-a-reason-to-recuse-him/', 'snippet': 'Scott Shane, a Times national security reporter, was referred to in the government’s prosecution of a former C.I.A. official.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s a generally accepted rule in journalism that if you’re involved in a newsworthy situation, you shouldn’t cover it. Most of the time that makes excellent sense.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Was a Reporter’s Role in a Government Prosecution a Reason to Recuse Him?', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-08T18:08:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1946b022-53b0-5df4-941c-f0bfe61666f2', 'word_count': 681, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1946b022-53b0-5df4-941c-f0bfe61666f2'}, {'abstract': 'The comedian Jeff Garlin will be the host of a podcast featuring conversations with other comics, like his “Curb Your Enthusiasm” co-star Larry David.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/08/jeff-garlin-joins-the-podcast-fray/', 'snippet': 'The comedian Jeff Garlin will be the host of a podcast featuring conversations with other comics, like his “Curb Your Enthusiasm” co-star Larry David.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Earwolf, which runs an extensive lineup of podcasts including the popular “Comedy Bang Bang” and “Professor Blastoff,” is adding another big name. “By the Way, In Conversation With Jeff Garlin” will be a biweekly series of talks with famously funny people led by Mr. Garlin, a Second City veteran perhaps best known for his role as Larry David’s pal on “Curb Your Enthusiasm.” It starts Thursday with a chat with Mr. David.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jeff Garlin Joins the Podcast Fray', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Podcasts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garlin, Jeff', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-08T18:15:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Zinoman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinoman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4fbdda8f-a77b-5fcd-9fa5-c7095fefbf99', 'word_count': 148, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4fbdda8f-a77b-5fcd-9fa5-c7095fefbf99'}, {'abstract': 'A map showing which parts of the country were warmest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/01/08/science/earth/record-setting-heat-across-the-us-in-2012.html', 'snippet': 'A map showing which parts of the country were warmest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A map showing which parts of the country were warmest.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Record-Setting Heat Across the U.S. in 2012', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': 