lifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 5}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/52ac893b-b7b7-57d1-bc36-045215ba63be', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/52ac893b-b7b7-57d1-bc36-045215ba63be'}, {'abstract': 'El Toro Blanco in the West Village conjures a midcentury modern, California ambience, where the centerpiece of a fun and stylish night on the town can be a plate of tamales.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/dining/reviews/restaurant-review-el-toro-blanco-in-the-west-village.html', 'snippet': 'El Toro Blanco in the West Village conjures a midcentury modern, California ambience, where the centerpiece of a fun and stylish night on the town can be a plate of tamales.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ONCE you plow your way through the crowds struggling in vain to catch a bartender’s eye at El Toro Blanco, you emerge into a dining room that might be in Santa Barbara during the last days of the Nixon administration. Ridged orange backs on half-moon banquettes stand up like a wall of Cheetos. Glazed brick walls in red and black flank curvy 1960s plywood chairs, dangling tangerine-colored pendant lights, and matadors painted on black velvet. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/dining/09REST1_SPAN/09REST1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/09/dining/09REST1_SPAN/09REST1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/dining/09REST1_SPAN/09REST1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit':