0821ca25-30e0-5433-a899-4d552f0637aa'}, {'abstract': 'The United States spends much more on health care than other advanced nations with public health care systems. By most objective measures, it gets no better results.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/01/08/business/costly-medicine.html', 'snippet': 'The United States spends much more on health care than other advanced nations with public health care systems. By most objective measures, it gets no better results.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The United States spends much more on health care than other advanced nations with public health care systems. By most objective measures, it gets no better results.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Costly Medicine', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-08T21:43:14+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/468d6065-7571-51f6-9d65-5af3d176a518', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/468d6065-7571-51f6-9d65-5af3d176a518'}, {'abstract': 'A government tax-return pilot program did show promise for helping the unbanked, an analysis finds.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/08/despite-promise-federal-tax-refund-debit-cards-a-no-go/', 'snippet': 'A government tax-return pilot program did show promise for helping the unbanked, an analysis finds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Giving consumers who lack accounts at a bank or credit union the option of getting tax refunds on multiuse, prepaid debit cards may help bring them into the financial mainstream, a report from the Urban Institute finds. But the accounts must be low-cost, easy to use and available early in the tax season to encourage their use.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Despite Promise, Federal Tax-Refund Debit Cards a No Go', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Green Dot Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Urban Institute', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-08T21:44:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9bea546f-1456-5de1-a1e6-9413c796c026', 'word_count': 702, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9bea546f-1456-5de1-a1e6-9413c796c026'}, {'abstract': 'Many items on the menu for the lunch after the presidential inaugural on Jan. 21 are from New York State.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/dining/lobster-bison-and-wine-at-lunch-after-inauguration.html', 'snippet': 'Many items on the menu for the lunch after the presidential inaugural on Jan. 21 are from New York State.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WITHOUT a single filibuster or even a cross word, the bipartisan Congressional committee responsible for the lunch after the presidential inaugural on Jan. 21 has agreed on a menu featuring sustainable, artisanal and local ingredients. And many are from New York State.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': N