3-7246-5d82-a658-d52dc80f5281'}, {'abstract': 'No one at PBS guessed that the opening episode of Season 3 of “Downton Abbey” would surpass the viewer numbers for some networks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/arts/television/downton-abbey-audience-swells-for-seasons-first-episode.html', 'snippet': 'No one at PBS guessed that the opening episode of Season 3 of “Downton Abbey” would surpass the viewer numbers for some networks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The producers of the PBS series “Masterpiece” had an office pool going to guess the premiere ratings for Season 3 of “Downton Abbey,” the British period drama that has improbably become one of America’s most-buzzed-about shows.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/arts/09ABBEY/09ABBEY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 705, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/arts/09ABBEY/09ABBEY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1410, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/arts/09ABBEY/09ABBEY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/09/arts/09ABBEY/09ABBEY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/arts/09ABBEY/09ABBEY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'No Savior Needed for This Old House', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Savior Needed for This Old House', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stelter, Brian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Public Broadcasting Service', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ratings (Audience Measurement)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Downton Abbey (TV Program)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fellowes, Julian', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-08T23:08:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3c9727f-bdeb-5054-84fc-ac63990d16e1', 'word_count': 868, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3c9727f-bdeb-5054-84fc-ac63990d16e1'}, {'abstract': 'The memorial for the saxophonist David S. Ware on Monday at St. Peter’s Church was a bittersweet confirmation of his legacy, in words and images but especially in music.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/arts/music/memorial-service-for-david-s-ware-jazz-saxophonist.html', 'snippet': 'The memorial for the saxophonist David S. Ware on Monday at St. Peter’s Church was a bittersweet confirmation of his legacy, in words and images but especially in music.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At one point during the memorial service for David S. Ware, at St. Peter’s Church in Midtown Manhattan on Monday night, a slide show provided a visual record of his commanding presence. It opened with a black-and-white snapshot from when he was 5, sometime in 1955, and ran chronologically up to his final performances, in 2011. Most images showed him with a saxophone, either at the ready or held aloft, in midcry. In almost all of them he looked intensely self-possessed, exuding gravity even in repose.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/arts/09WARE1/09WARE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/arts/09WARE1/09WARE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/arts/09WARE1/09WARE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/09/arts/09WARE1/09WARE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/arts/09WARE1/09WARE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Free Improvisation at a Memorial Helps Affirm a Saxophonist’s Legacy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Free Improvisation at a Memorial Helps Affirm a Saxophonist’s Legacy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ware, David S', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-08T23:13:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6af0e344-93aa-5122-a536-bb95448059c3', 'word_count': 634, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6af0e344-93aa-5122-a536-bb95448059c3'}, {'abstract': 'The Emerson String Quartet, including the soon-to-depart cellist David Finckel, played a Brahms program at Carnegie Hall on Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/arts/music/the-emerson-string-quartet-at-carnegie-hall.html', 'snippet': 'The Emerson String Quartet, including the soon-to-depart cellist David Finckel, played a Brahms program at Carnegie Hall on Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the cellist David Finckel played a bittersweet melody in the first movement of Brahms’s String Sextet No. 2 in G at Carnegie Hall on Monday evening, it was hard not to recall that this is the last season he will perform with the Emerson String Quartet. Mr. Finckel announced last year that he would leave the ensemble, which he joined in 1979, to dedicate more time to his other substantial endeavors, which include the artistic directorship of the Chamber Music Society of Lincoln Center with his wife, the pianist Wu Han. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/arts/09EMERSON/09EMERSON-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/09/arts/09EMERSON/09EMERSON-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/arts/09EMERSON/09EMERSON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 628, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'im