eople who used them.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/08/ada-louise-huxtables-new-york/', 'snippet': 'As the first full-time architecture critic for a daily newspaper, Ada Louise Huxtable, who began writing for The Times in 1963, believed that the best buildings served the people who used them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a rule, there are few things as stale in literature as yesterday’s news columns anthologized. A 1,000-word essay prepared for immediate consumption usually doesn’t read very well years later.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/blogs/20130108Huxtable1/20130108Huxtable1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/08/blogs/20130108Huxtable1/20130108Huxtable1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/blogs/20130108Huxtable1/20130108Huxtable1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/blogs/20130108Huxtable1/20130108Huxtable1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/blogs/20130108Huxtable1/20130108Huxtable1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/08/blogs/20130108Huxtable1/20130108Huxtable1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'ur