mes', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Voting Process Overdue for Reform', 'kicker': 'On Baseball', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Voting Process Overdue for Reform', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kepner, Tyler', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baseball Hall of Fame', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baseball Writers Assn of America', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-08T23:26:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/11cc7449-d33c-5f60-9971-ba1b5ad7a468', 'word_count': 922, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11cc7449-d33c-5f60-9971-ba1b5ad7a468'}, {'abstract': 'The owner of the popular Chelsea Market in Manhattan, which is planning to add office towers to its squat structure, first wants to expand by including eight new retail outlets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/realestate/commercial/before-building-towers-chelsea-market-plans-to-add-vendors.html', 'snippet': 'The owner of the popular Chelsea Market in Manhattan, which is planning to add office towers to its squat structure, first wants to expand by including eight new retail outlets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The owner of Chelsea Market, a popular food marketplace in West Chelsea, recently ignited a public furor when the city approved plans to add office towers to the squat structure. But before construction on the towers begins, the market now plans to expand by