ration said Tuesday that it was open to a so-called zero option when the NATO combat mission there ends.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/world/asia/us-is-open-to-withdraw-afghan-force-after-2014.html', 'snippet': 'On the eve of a visit by President Hamid Karzai of Afghanistan, the Obama administration said Tuesday that it was open to a so-called zero option when the NATO combat mission there ends.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — On the eve of a visit by President Hamid Karzai of Afghanistan, the Obama administration said Tuesday that it was open to a so-called zero option that would involve leaving no American troops in Afghanistan after 2014, when the NATO combat mission there comes to an end.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Is Open to Withdraw Afghan Force After 2014', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Is Open To Withdraw Afghan Force After 2014', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Landler, Mark', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gordon, Michael R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karzai, Hamid', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'North Atlantic Treaty Organization', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Center for Strategic and International Studies', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Afghan National Army', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}