nd-rhinos.html', 'snippet': 'The Wildlife Conservation Society responds to “The Price of Ivory” news series.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Poaching of Elephants and Rhinos', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Poaching of Elephants and Rhinos', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poaching (Wildlife)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ivory', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elephants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rhinoceroses', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-09T01:35:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b9792de-e0f1-5ea4-81df-cc3da3b240bd', 'word_count': 197, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b9792de-e0f1-5ea4-81df-cc3da3b240bd'}, {'abstract': 'The Obama administration rejected Gov. Paul R. LePage’s request to drop thousands of people from Medicaid rolls.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/us/maine-medicaid-purge-is-rejected.html', 'snippet': 'The Obama administration rejected Gov. Paul R. LePage’s request to drop thousands of people from Medicaid rolls.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Obama administration rejected Gov. Paul R. LePage’s request to drop thousands of people from Medicaid rolls. Mr. LePage, a Republican, had sought to eliminate Medicaid coverage for nearly 15,000 parents with incomes between the federal poverty level ($23,050 for a family of four last year) and 133 percent of that level ($30,657 for a family of four). He also wanted to end coverage for more than 6,000 19- and 20-year-olds. Marilyn Tavenner, the acting administrator of the Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services, told Mr. LePage in a letter that the cuts would violate a provision of President Obama’s health care law requiring states to maintain Medicaid eligibility levels. But Ms. Tavenner did approve a separate plan to end Medicaid coverage for Maine parents earning more than 133 percent of the poverty level. Mr. LePage had hoped to save more than $20 million from the cuts. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Maine: Medicaid Purge Is Rejected', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | New England', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Maine: Medicaid Purge Is Rejected', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicaid', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'LePage, Paul R', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tavenner, Marilyn B', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maine', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-09T01:41:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abby Goodnough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goodnough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/a319563d-f9aa-5d18-96ee-a993ca26d5ef', 'word_count': 147, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a319563d-f9aa-5d18-96ee-a993ca26d5ef'}, {'abstract': 'All Indians have a stake in fair trials and a stronger judicial system.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/opinion/justice-for-indias-rape-victims.html', 'snippet': 'All Indians have a stake in fair trials and a stronger judicial system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Influenced by extraordinary street protests, Indian authorities have moved swiftly to try the men accused of gang-raping a 23-year-old physiotherapy student in New Delhi. Clearly, justice must be served, but there are disturbing aspects to the way the case is being handled.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Justice for India’s Rape Victims', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Justice for India&#8217;s Rape Victims', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Delhi (India)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-09T01:42:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a89744f-c833-5748-8a7e-9598d66b1535', 'word_count': 494, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a89744f-c833-5748-8a7e-9598d66b1535'}, {'abstract': 'Peace has eased safety concerns in Helmand Province, but there is little faith in the Afghan government’s ability to maintain the security gains won by American and British troops.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/world/asia/in-old-taliban-strongholds-qualms-on-what-lies-ahead.html', 'snippet': 'Peace has eased safety concerns in Helmand Province, but there is little faith in the Afghan government’s ability to maintain the security gains won by American and British troops.', 'lead_paragraph':