all', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judy Battista', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Battista', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/567ba91b-e037-5d90-8c00-29a779a5cbd8', 'word_count': 695, 'uri': 'nyt://article/567ba91b-e037-5d90-8c00-29a779a5cbd8'}, {'abstract': 'Former Representative Gabrielle Giffords and her husband unveiled a campaign against gun violence on the second anniversary of the shooting that killed six people and left Ms. Giffords critically injured.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/us/arizona-giffords-and-husband-start-campaign-against-gun-violence.html', 'snippet': 'Former Representative Gabrielle Giffords and her husband unveiled a campaign against gun violence on the second anniversary of the shooting that killed six people and left Ms. Giffords critically injured.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Former Representative Gabrielle Giffords and her husband, Mark E. Kelly, unveiled a campaign against gun violence on Tuesday, the second anniversary of the shooting in a Tuscon shopping center that killed six people and left Ms. Giffords critically injured. In an op-ed article published in USA Today, Ms. Giffords, a Democrat, and Mr. Kelly, a former astronaut, explained that the effort, called Americans for Responsible Solutions, was intended to counter the influence of the powerful gun lobby. They said they wanted to encourage elected officials “to prevent gun violence and protect responsible gun ownership by communicating directly with the constituents that elect them.” They emphasized that they are strong supporters of the Second Amendment. “We don’t want to take away your guns any more than we want to give up the two guns we have locked in a safe at home,” the couple wrote. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Arizona: Giffords and Husband Start Campaign Against Gun Violence', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Southwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Arizona: Giffords and Husband Start\r\nCampaign Against Gun Violence', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giffords, Gabrielle', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Preston, Jennifer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelly, Mark E (1964- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tucson Shooting (2011)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'USA Today', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-09T01:51:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/36e39522-96b8-55ee-b2ed-3543e4043707', 'word_count': 144, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36e39522-96b8-55ee-b2ed-3543e4043707'}, {'abstract': 'CBS, which will broadcast the Super Bowl on Feb. 3, sold all the available commercial time — unless a marketer wants so much to be included that money is no object.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/business/media/a-sellout-for-super-bowl-commercial-time.html', 'snippet': 'CBS, which will broadcast the Super Bowl on Feb. 3, sold all the available commercial time — unless a marketer wants so much to be included that money is no object.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JUST as the playoff results are making it clearer which teams will play in Super Bowl XLVII, the lineup of advertisers buying commercials in the game is also becoming clearer.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/business/ADCO/ADCO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 535, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/business/ADCO/ADCO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 535, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/business/ADCO/ADCO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/09/business/ADCO/ADCO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/business/ADCO/ADCO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Super Bowl Commercial Time Is a Sellout', 'kicker': 'Advertising', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Super Bowl Commercial Time Is a Sellout', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Elliott, Stuart', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Super Bowl', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-09T01:55:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/be933c1c-2704-5b3d-b496-4f252c3808c9', 'word_count': 886, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be933c1c-2704-5b3d-b496-4f252c3808c9'}, {'abstract': 'A.I.G.’s board should keep the history of the bailout in mind and decide not to join a misguided lawsuit against the government.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/opinion/a-mind-boggling-claim-over-aigs-bailout.html', 'snippet': 'A.I.G.’s board should keep the history of the bailout in mind and decide not to join a misguided lawsuit against the government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The board of the American International Group will meet on Wednesday to consider joining a misguided lawsuit against the government, which spent $182 billion to save the insurance giant from near certain failure. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Mind-Boggling Claim', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Mind-Boggling Claim', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN INTERNATIONAL GROUP INC', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greenberg, Maurice R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emergency Economic Stabilization Act (2008)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Treasury Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve Bank of New York', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-09T02:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4568c3d-ed00-52bd-bb67-af6dca8378da', 'word_count': 499, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4568c3d-ed00-52bd-bb67-af6dca8378da'}, {'abstract': 'Why the United States needs to cut both debt and carbon emissions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/opinion/friedman-the-market-and-mother-nature.html', 'snippet': 'Why the United States needs to cut both debt and carbon emissions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Whenever I hear the word “cliff,” I am reminded of something that President Obama’s science adviser, John Holdren, used to say about how we need to respond to climate change because no one can predict when it might take a disruptive, nonlinear turn. “We are driving toward a cliff in a fog,” said Holdren about the climate, and that’s always a good time “to start tapping on the brakes.” Indeed, when you think about how much financial debt we’ve built up in the market and how much carbon debt we’ve built up in the atmosphere, the wisest thing we could do as a country today is to start tapping on the brakes by both emitting less carbon to bend the emissions curve down and racking up less debt to bend our debt-to-G.D.P. curve down. Unfortunately, we are still doing neither.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'ima