said an assessment could halt or scale back Shell’s program to open Alaska’s Arctic waters to oil exploration.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Interior Department on Tuesday opened an urgent review of Arctic offshore drilling operations after a series of blunders and accidents involving Shell Oil’s drill ships and support equipment, culminating in the grounding of one of its drilling vessels last week off the coast of Alaska.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/us/ARCTIC/ARCTIC-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 387, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/09/us/ARCTIC/ARCTIC-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 387}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/us/ARCTIC/ARCTIC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 660, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/us/ARCTIC/ARCTIC-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1320, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/us/ARCTIC/ARCTIC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/09/us/ARCTIC/ARCTIC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/us/ARCTIC/ARCTIC-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Interior Dept. Expedites Review of Arctic Drilling After Accidents', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Interior Dept. Expedites Review of Arctic Drilling After Accidents', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal Dutch Shell Plc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Broder, John M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Offshore Drilling and Exploration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Interior Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Salazar, Ken', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Odum, Marvin E', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALASKA', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-09T02:05:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By John M. Broder and Clifford Krauss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/52188143-11fd-5818-93fa-5154d37401f4', 'word_count': 959, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52188143-11fd-5818-93fa-5154d37401f4'}, {'abstract': 'Dustin Johnson ran away from the winners-only field in Kapalua, Hawaii, posting a 54-hole score of 16-under 203 to win by four strokes over Steve Stricker.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/sports/golf/dustin-johnson-wins-tournament-of-champions-easily.html', 'snippet': 'Dustin Johnson ran away from the winners-only field in Kapalua, Hawaii, posting a 54-hole score of 16-under 203 to win by four strokes over Steve Stricker.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KAPALUA, Hawaii — Only someone as athletic and powerful as Dustin Johnson could take the hilly, 7,411-yard, par-73 Plantation Course and turn it into a par-3 contest. And only someone like Johnson, whose personality is as placid as the west Maui winds are not, could describe as “nice” the blustery conditions that delayed the start of the Tournament of Champions for three days.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/sports/GOLF/GOLF-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 365, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/09/sports/GOLF/GOLF-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 365}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/sports/GOLF/GOLF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 624, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/sports/GOLF/GOLF-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1248, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/sports/GOLF/GOLF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/09/sports/GOLF/GOLF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/sports/GOLF/GOLF-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Displaying Skill and Composure, Johnson Wins Tournament of Champions Easily', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Displaying Skill and Composure, Johnson Wins Easily', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Dustin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stricker, Steve', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-09T02:06:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7fd2ae59-8cce-54ae-a1a1-3bd5b99dee6a', 'word_count': 857, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7fd2ae59-8cce-54ae-a1a1-3bd5b99dee6a'}, {'abstract': 'Gen. Stanley A. McChrystal said the United States still needs to keep forces in Afghanistan to help stabilize the country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/world/asia/q-and-a-with-gen-stanley-mcchrystal.html', 'snippet': 'Gen. Stanley A. McChrystal said the United States still needs to keep forces in Afghanistan to help stabilize the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — As the Obama administration weighs how many troops to keep in Afghanistan after 2014, Gen. Stanley A. McChrystal cautioned that the United States still needs to keep forces there to help stabilize the country and urged a continued effort to advise the Afghan military that appears to be more extensive than the White House has in mind.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/world/asia/09mcchrystal/09mcchrystal-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge':