ake place at a later date. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/world/americas/09CHAVEZ1/09CHAVEZ1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/09/world/americas/09CHAVEZ1/09CHAVEZ1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/world/americas/09CHAVEZ1/09CHAVEZ1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/world/americas/09CHAVEZ1/09CHAVEZ1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/world/americas/09CHAVEZ1/09CHAVEZ1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/09/world/americas/09CHAVEZ1/09CHAVEZ1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/world/americas/09CHAVEZ1/09CHAVEZ1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chávez, Too Ill to Return to Venezuela, Will Be Sworn In Later, Official Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chávez, Too Ill to Return to Venezuela, Will Be Sworn In Later, Official Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chavez, Hugo', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inaugurations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venezuela', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-09T02:11:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Neuman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Neuman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8171f410-14af-51cc-9994-59eacde00be3', 'word_count': 697, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8171f410-14af-51cc-9994-59eacde00be3'}, {'abstract': 'Five Americans and two Peruvians were killed Monday when the helicopter they were in crashed in the jungle near Pucallpa, in the central part of the country, soon after takeoff.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/world/americas/peru-5-americans-and-2-peruvians-die-in-copter-crash.html', 'snippet': 'Five Americans and two Peruvians were killed Monday when the helicopter they were in crashed in the jungle near Pucallpa, in the central part of the country, soon after takeoff.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Five Americans and two Peruvians were killed Monday when the helicopter they were in crashed in the jungle near Pucallpa, in the central part of the country, soon after takeoff. The victims were employees of Columbia Helicopters, an Oregon-based company that operated the cargo helicopter, a two-rotor Boeing Model 234 Chinook. They were on their way to deliver materials to an oil exploration site, the company said. There was no immediate indication of what caused the crash, which is being investigated by Peruvian transportation officials. Witnesses told local news media that the helicopter appeared to have exploded after hitting the ground. Photographs showed the aircraft’s charred and flattened remains in a marshy area. The company said the Americans on board were from Washington, Florida, Utah, Tennessee and Oregon. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Peru: 5 Americans and 2 Peruvians Die in Copter Crash', 'kicker': 'Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Peru: 5 Americans and 2 Peruvians Die in Copter Crash', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Helicopters', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aviation Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Peru', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-09T02:14:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrea Zarate', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zarate', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/98de0e87-fc55-5bb2-93d1-8cb711d9b5bc', 'word_count': 128, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98de0e87-fc55-5bb2-93d1-8cb711d9b5bc'}, {'abstract': 'The N.H.L. Board of Governors is expected to approve the deal Commissioner Gary Bettman reached with Donald Fehr and the N.H.L. Players’ Association.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/sports/hockey/official-vote-on-nhl-agreement-unofficial-one-on-gary-bettman.html', 'snippet': 'The N.H.L. Board of Governors is expected to approve the deal Commissioner Gary Bettman reached with Donald Fehr and the N.H.L. Players’ Association.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The N.H.L. Board of Governors will convene Wednesday in New York to vote on a new collective bargaining agreement with the league’s players’ association. But another important item will be under consideration, even though it will not be on the official agenda: whether Gary Bettman will keep his job as commissioner.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Official Vote, and an Unofficial One', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Official Vote, and an Unofficial One', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bettman, Gary', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klein, Jeff Z', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "National Hockey League Players' Assn", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lockouts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-09T02:15:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/88634e82-3def-5ce5-82d8-0b1d838b78ec', 'word_count': 922, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88634e82-3def-5ce5-82d8-0b1d838b78ec'}, {'abstract': 'The director of United Nations emergency relief implored the Security Council on Tuesday to find ways to ensure his aid teams can gain access to two isolated southern states of Sudan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/world/africa/sudan-top-un-aid-official-warns-of-food-crisis-in-2-southern-states.html', 'snippet': 'The director of United Nations emergency relief implored the Security Council on Tuesday to find ways to ensure his aid teams can gain access to two isolated southern states of Sudan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The director of United Nations emergency relief implored the Security Council on Tuesday to find ways to ensure his aid teams can gain access to two isolated southern states of Sudan. Hundreds of thousands of civilians are trapped there because of a conflict between rebels and the Sudanese government, which has accused the newly independent country of South Sudan of abetting an insurgency. The relief director, John Ging, told reporters afterward that he feared that many residents in the isolated states, South Kordofan and Blue Nile, might be dying of malnutrition and disease, while others were subsisting on roots and leaves. “This is 2013, and to think that tens of thousands, hundreds of thousands of people are living in such desperate and deplorable circumstances, and we can’t get in to help them as humanitarian organizations, it’s just not acceptable,” Mr. Ging said. The United Nations and aid groups have accused Sudan of denying them access to the two states. Sudan’s United Nations ambassador, Daffa-Alla Elhag Ali Osman, told reporters that rebels were responsible for any impediments to aid. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sudan: Top U.N. Aid Official Warns of Food Crisis in 2 Southern States', 'kicker': 'Africa', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sudan: Top U.N. Aid Official Warns of Food Crisis in 2 Southern States', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sudan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Security Council (UN)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-09T02:19:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1d5f66c-9359-50e2-b2bd-cab045a68da1', 'word_count': 178, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1d5f66c-9359-50e2-b2bd-cab045a68da1'}, {'abstract': 'Ayatollah Ali Khamenei, Iran’s supreme leader, said its enemies would most likely try to sabotage the presidential election scheduled for June.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/world/middleeast/iran-ayatollah-discourages-talk-of-votes-fairness.html', 'snippet': 'Ayatollah Ali Khamenei, Iran’s supreme leader, said its enemies would most likely try to sabotage the presidential election scheduled for June.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Ayatollah Ali Khamenei, Iran’s supreme leader, said its enemies would most likely try to sabotage the presidential election scheduled for June. He warned citizens and prospective candidates to avoid discussion about the fairness of the vote, suggesting that such talk was subversive and would discourage turnout. “Where on earth have elections been so free as in Iran?” he said in a speech in the holy city of Qom, reported by the state-run press. “Watch out for your words not to dissuade people.” His statement, coming five months before the vote for a successor to President Mahmoud Ahmadinejad, appeared to reflect the ayatollah’s concern about repeating the chaotic aftermath of the 2009 election, in which Mr. Ahmadinejad, his favored candidate, won by a suspiciously lopsided margin that opponents said was fraudulent. Postelection protests escalated into the most serious challenge that the Islamic government had faced since it took power in the 1979 revolution. Mr. Ahmadinejad’s two challengers have remained under house arrest for the past few years. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iran: Ayatollah Discourages Talk of Vote’s Fairness', 'kicker': 'MIddle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iran: Ayatollah Discourages Talk of Vote’s Fairness', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khamenei, Ali', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'AHMADINEJAD, MAHMOUD', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-09T02:20:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/f44ce20e-56ea-5b83-9899-4824f2e9af4a', 'word_count': 166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f44ce20e-56ea-5b83-9899-4824f2e9af4a'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Cramer, a Pulitzer Prize-winning journalist, was the author of “What It Takes,” an intimate, deeply reported account of the 1988 presidential election.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/us/richard-ben-cramer-writer-on-large-topics-dies-at-62.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Cramer, a Pulitzer Prize-winning journalist, was the author of “What It Takes,” an intimate, deeply reported account of the 1988 presidential election.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It took time for “What It Takes” to become a classic.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/us/CRAMER-obit/CRAMER-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 906, 'width': 627, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/us/CRAMER-obit/CRAMER-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 906, 'width': 627, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 