e most-viewed program was the 2011 B.C.S. title game, Auburn’s 22-19 win over Oregon, which was seen by 27.3 million viewers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Title Game Draws Second Biggest Cable Audience', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Title Game Draws Second Biggest Cable Audience', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'BCS National Championship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Alabama', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Notre Dame', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ESPN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cable Television', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-09T02:42:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03b2f292-b73c-503f-835d-3bfeaf5eaba9', 'word_count': 172, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03b2f292-b73c-503f-835d-3bfeaf5eaba9'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the day for Wednesday, Jan. 9, 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/pageoneplus/quotation-of-the-day-for-wednesday-jan-9-2013.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the day for Wednesday, Jan. 9, 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The heat was remarkable. It was prolonged. That we beat the record by one degree is quite a big deal.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day for Wednesday, Jan. 9, 2013', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-09T02:44:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/beed5234-d413-550d-ad3e-05304014f282', 'word_count': 46, 'uri': 'nyt://article/beed5234-d413-550d-ad3e-05304014f282'}, {'abstract': 'The office of the Special Commissioner of Investigation handled 4,173 complaints, more than double the amount received during the first year of the Bloomberg administration.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/nyregion/record-number-of-misconduct-allegations-made-against-new-york-school-employees.html', 'snippet': 'The office of the Special Commissioner of Investigation handled 4,173 complaints, more than double the amount received during the first year of the Bloomberg administration.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A record number of allegations of wrongdoing against teachers and other Department of Education workers were received last year by the office that investigates misconduct in New York City schools, according to a report released on Tuesday. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Record Number of Misconduct Complaints Are Made Against City School Employees', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Record Number of Misconduct Complaints Are Made Against City School Employees', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child A