/pageoneplus/corrections-january-9-2013.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on January 9, 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRONT PAGE', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: January 9, 2013', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-09T03:00:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4192c72-676c-539c-973b-a48a51421ebe', 'word_count': 700, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4192c72-676c-539c-973b-a48a51421ebe'}, {'abstract': 'The winning lottery numbers for New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/nyregion/lottery-numbers-for-new-york-new-jersey-and-connecticut.html', 'snippet': 'The winning lottery numbers for New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jan. 8, 2013', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lottery Numbers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lottery Numbers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lotteries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-09T03:02:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/eed35331-5328-5893-bb56-6f0ba226e9b2', 'word_count': 171, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eed35331-5328-5893-bb56-6f0ba226e9b2'}, {'abstract': 'Justices from across the ideological spectrum seemed to reject arguments by the government that discounted statutes of limitations on certain kinds of civil lawsuits.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/business/justices-assail-governments-case-in-a-fraud-suit.html', 'snippet': 'Justices from across the ideological spectrum seemed to reject arguments by the government that discounted statutes of limitations on certain kinds of civil lawsuits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — A Supreme Court argument that started on Tuesday as a routine consideration of the time limits for filing some kinds of securities fraud suits turned by its conclusion into a broad attack from justices across the ideological spectrum on what they said was government overreaching with the potential to do away with statutes of limitations whenever the government seeks civil penalties for any kind of fraud.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Argument Is Assailed by Justices in Fraud Case', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Argument Is Assailed By Justices in Fraud Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Statutes of Limitations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-09T03:03:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Liptak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liptak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9823a7ed-1595-5587-9bb0-474b169fa690', 'word_count': 710, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9823a7ed-1595-5587-9bb0-474b169fa690'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama’s selection of a new national security team appears to have ended, at least for now, many of the internal debates about military interventions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/us/politics/obama-nominees-in-step-on-light-footprint.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama’s selection of a new national security team appears to have ended, at least for now, many of the internal debates about military interventions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — With the selection of a new national security team deeply suspicious of the wisdom of American military interventions around the world, President Obama appears to have ended, at least for the moment, many of the internal administration debates that played out in the Situation Room over the past four years.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/world/americas/09team-2/09team-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/09/world/americas/09team-2/09team-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/world/americas/09team-2/09team-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 621, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/world/americas/09team-2/09team-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1242, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'cr