oped, and not everyone is celebrating. And Deacon (Charles Esten) reconnects with an old love.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Wednesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-09T06:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b55493a-9644-5f05-92f9-de82b2d1a054', 'word_count': 722, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b55493a-9644-5f05-92f9-de82b2d1a054'}, {'abstract': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/news-quiz-january-9-2013/', 'snippet': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'See what you know about the news below. To prepare, you might scan the articles or summaries on today’s paper. Good luck!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Quiz | January 9, 2013', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-09T06:30:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anastasia Economides', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anastasia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Economides', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8d1e0de-f61c-5629-8ed7-62fc21147968', 'word_count': 22, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8d1e0de-f61c-5629-8ed7-62fc21147968'}, {'abstract': 'Peace without optimism in Afghanistan’s south; euro-zone unemployment hits a new high; Obama’s increasingly male inner circle; a slapdash post-Fukushima cleanup.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/iht-quick-read-jan-9/', 'snippet': 'Peace without optimism in Afghanistan’s south; euro-zone unemployment hits a new high; Obama’s increasingly male inner circle; a slapdash post-Fukushima cleanup.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEWS In Helmand Province in southern Afghanistan, places that were once Taliban strongholds have been transformed by the American troop surge that brought tens of thousands of marines three years ago. But there is little faith in the government’s ability to maintain those security gains once the Americans leave, and many assume that the Taliban will return. Alissa J. Rubin reports from Loy Bagh, Afghanistan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/blogs/helmand-rdv/helmand-rdv-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/blogs/helmand-rdv/helmand-rdv-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/blogs/helmand-rdv/helmand-rdv-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/09/blogs/helmand-rdv/helmand-rdv-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/blogs/helmand-rdv/helmand-rdv-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'IHT Quick Read: Jan. 9', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-09T07:25:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By The International Herald Tribune', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The International Herald Tribune'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d9008ce-e763-587c-acea-f7c820f77673', 'word_count': 434, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d9008ce-e763-587c-acea-f7c820f77673'}, {'abstract': 'Two players with fathers who played for Brazil’s 1994 World Cup champions will represent the country at this month’s South American Youth Championship.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/sons-of-94-lead-brazil-into-south-american-youth-championship/', 'snippet': 'Two players with fathers who played for Brazil’s 1994 World Cup champions will represent the country at this month’s South American Youth Championship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the iconic images of the 1994 World Cup captures Bebeto, Mazinho and Romário celebrating Bebeto’s 62nd-minute goal against the Netherlands at the Cotton Bowl.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sons of ’94 Lead Brazil Into South American Youth Championship', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-09T07:57:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jerrad Peters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jerrad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aad6785b-b019-51ef-9eb3-c2ae6e17d56a', 'word_count': 637, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aad6785b-b019-51ef-9eb3-c2ae6e17d56a'}, {'abstract': 'If given the percentage of 2011 high school graduates enrolled in college in October 2011 and the total number of college students, can you calculate the number of people who graduated high school that year?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/test-yourself-math-jan-9-2013/', 'snippet': 'If given the percentage of 2011 high school graduates enrolled in college in October 2011 and the total number of college students, can you calculate the number of people who graduated high school that year?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Test your math skills with this question created by Scott Matthews at Math for America from the Economix blog post “Degree Inflation? Jobs That Newly Require B.A.’s.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Test Yourself | Math, Jan. 9, 2013', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-09T09:21:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb9f6c54-b420-54ac-93d9-3a84d06fac17', 'word_count': 55, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb9f6c54-b420-54ac-93d9-3a84d06fac17'}, {'abstract': 'What is a digital globe, and what can it do that makes it useful to both scientists and students?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/our-world-on-a-sphere/', 'snippet': 'What is a digital globe, and what can it do that makes it useful to both scientists and students?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Digital Globes Offer a Dynamic Vision, Mark Vanhoenacker reports on an educational tool that can animate complex phenomena. The questions below are based on the article, but watching the video, above, will give students a good sense of the power of this technology.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Our World on a Sphere', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-09T09:50:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ecce89b2-5e18-5df3-bb8e-5b16b826c844', 'word_count': 154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ecce89b2-5e18-5df3-bb8e-5b16b826c844'}, {'abstract': '“Obama would like to reach peace in the Middle East and has to be convinced that Israel agrees with this,” Shimon Peres says. “Of course, he’s not convinced.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/13/magazine/shimon-peres-on-obama-iran-and-the-path-to-peace.html', 'snippet': '“Obama would like to reach peace in the Middle East and has to be convinced that Israel agrees with this,” Shimon Peres says. “Of course, he’s not convinced.”', 'lead_paragraph': '“This part of the conversation is highly sensitive,” said the spokeswoman for Israel’s president. “I want all cellphones taken out of the room.” It was July 25, 2012, and I was interviewing Shimon Peres in a wood-paneled suite at the King David Hotel in Jerusalem. I handed my phone to one of the guards standing at the door, and Peres swiftly opened a scathing monologue against a potential Israeli attack on Iran’s nuclear sites. “Israel cannot solve the problem alone,” he said. “There is a limit to what we can do.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/magazine/13peres/13peres-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 540, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/13/magazine/13peres/13peres-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 540}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/magazine/13peres/13peres-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 922, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/magazine/13peres/13peres-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1335, 'width': 1483, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/magazine/13peres/13peres-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/13/magazine/13peres/13peres-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/magazine/13peres/13peres-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Shimon Peres on Obama, Iran and the Path to Peace', 'kicker': 'From the Archives', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Conversation with President Shimon Peres of Israel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bergman, Ronen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Peres, Shimon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netanyahu, Benjamin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Middle East', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-09T10:00:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ronen Bergman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ronen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bergman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f7f8ecc-af92-5376-82f2-2e3b934b8489', 'word_count': 3977, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f7f8ecc-af92-5376-82f2-2e3b934b8489'}, {'abstract': 'How often do you try new things? Read one Op-Ed columnist’s advice about choosing a college that challenges the safe world you know, then tell us to what extent that resonates with you.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/how-often-do-you-leave-your-comfort-zone/', 'snippet': 'How often do you try new things? Read one Op-Ed columnist’s advice about choosing a college that challenges the safe world you know, then tell us to what extent that resonates with you.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a recent column, Frank Bruni suggests choosing a college that will take you out of the comfortable world you have known and “expand your universe.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/sunday-review/06BRUNI-LN/06BRUNI-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/06/sunday-review/06BRUNI-LN/06BRUNI-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/06/sunday-review/06BRUNI-LN/06BRUNI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 673, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_n