come a symbol for India’s youth.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Groups of women huddled around makeshift fires on a wet mud-lane, surrounded by partially constructed houses on both sides, in Mahavir Enclave Part II in Delhi. They winced as the smoke went in to their eyes, and glanced towards the locked house with a green steel door, a barred window and white brick walls, as they remembered the young woman from their neighborhood, who has suddenly become a symbol of India’s dire treatment of women.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Ambitious Woman From a Delhi Neighborhood of Migrants', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Youth', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Uttar Pradesh State (India)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-09T10:24:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anjani Trivedi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anjani', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Trivedi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/375d0b9c-e3fd-5c70-975b-c82e1970cbc7', 'word_count': 832, 'uri': 'nyt://article/375d0b9c-e3fd-5c70-975b-c82e1970cbc7'}, {'abstract': 'The recently enacted budget compromise, which increased taxes and extended unemployment benefits, is unlikely to help the labor market this year, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/the-labor-market-post-cliff/', 'snippet': 'The recently enacted budget compromise, which increased taxes and extended unemployment benefits, is unlikely to help the labor market this year, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Casey B. Mulligan is an economics professor at the University of Chicago. He is the author of “The Redistribution Recession: How Labor Market Distortions Contracted the Economy.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Labor Market Post-Budget Deal', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment Insurance', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tax Policy Center', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-09T11:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Casey B. Mulligan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Casey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4df604fb-3796-519e-bbcf-1c687a17d7e2', 'word_count': 697, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4df604fb-3796-519e-bbcf-1c687a17d7e2'}, {'abstract': 'Amritsar and Delhi offices of the manufacturer of India’s low-cost computer.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/indside-datawinds-india-operations/', 'snippet': 'Amritsar and Delhi offices of the manufacturer of India’s low-cost computer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a nondescript neighborhood of Amritsar known as Ghee Mandi, a nod to the area’s past as a clarified butter wholesale market, a three-story building with blue glass windows has displayed a prominent sign: “DataWind Makers of Aakash Tablets.” Below the sign hangs a portrait of a Sikh saint, Baba Deep Singh, after whom the building has been named.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside DataWind’s India Operations', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customer Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tablet Computers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tuli, Suneet Singh', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'DataWind Ltd', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Montreal (Quebec)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-09T11:04:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pamposh Raina', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pamposh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Raina', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bfd25818-1915-584e-87ae-5a8a599e73fc', 'word_count': 1157, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bfd25818-1915-584e-87ae-5a8a599e73fc'}, {'abstract': 'More than 2,000 prisoners held by the Syrian authorities were being released in return for 48 Iranians held by rebels for months, Turkish and Iranian news reports said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/10/world/middle