+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dorothy J. Samuels', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dorothy', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Samuels', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99032fd8-b76f-5d2a-8a79-0a30be12d884', 'word_count': 292, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99032fd8-b76f-5d2a-8a79-0a30be12d884'}, {'abstract': 'Scenes from the London fashion week photo diary of Kasia Bobula.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/photos-of-the-moment-christopher-shannon-2/', 'snippet': 'Scenes from the London fashion week photo diary of Kasia Bobula.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Photos of The Moment | Christopher Shannon', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'London Fashion Week', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-09T15:30:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kasia Bobula', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kasia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bobula', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c71e2a74-5800-547f-92bd-715286797fd2', 'word_count': 36, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c71e2a74-5800-547f-92bd-715286797fd2'}, {'abstract': 'Reaction to the spate of news conferences announcing hirings and firings, including the one Tuesday by the Jets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/10/sports/jets-miss-playoffs-and-go-straight-to-the-news-conferences-leading-off.html', 'snippet': 'Reaction to the spate of news conferences announcing hirings and firings, including the one Tuesday by the Jets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The sports calendar tells us it is football playoff season, the time of year we get to focus on only the good teams, the teams that won important games and comported themselves in a relatively professional fashion, at least well enough to escape the regular season with Super Bowl dreams intact. In reality, January is football news conference season, with barely a day going by when a coach or an owner is not sitting in front of some backdrop sponsored by a doughnut company or a health care clinic (fine bedfellows at that), explaining how his championship season morphed into something that resembled the remake of a Three Stooges movie. There are hirings and firings, coordinators axed, fresh starts and do-overs, mediocrity and calamity all cued up for the cameras.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Explaining Season', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Woody', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Rex', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Musburger, Brent', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCarron, A J', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANTHONY, CARMELO', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garnett, Kevin', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nash, Steve', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-09T15:32:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/04ddd3f9-ef1e-54fd-917b-d49d67aab8e8', 'word_count': 705, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04ddd3f9-ef1e-54fd-917b-d49d67aab8e8'}, {'abstract': 'In her annual report to Congress, Nina E. Olson suggested repealing the alternative minimum tax and reducing so-called tax expenditures — income exclusions, deductions and credits.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/business/irss-taxpayer-advocate-calls-for-a-tax-code-overhaul.html', 'snippet': 'In her annual report to Congress, Nina E. Olson suggested repealing the alternative minimum tax and reducing so-called tax expenditures — income exclusions, deductions and credits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lawmakers need to overhaul the tax code completely to reduce the “significant, even unconscionable, burden” placed on taxpayers just to file a tax return, the Internal Revenue Service’s ombudsman told Congress on Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'I.R.S.’s Taxpayer Advocate Calls for a Tax Code Overhaul', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'I.R.S.’s Taxpayer Advocate\r\nCalls for Overhaul of Code', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALTERNATIVE MINIMUM TAX', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Internal Revenue Service', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-09T15:32:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4555ad41-52a4-55a4-b51a-3aa613b8be22', 'word_count': 667, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4555ad41-52a4-55a4-b51a-3aa613b8be22'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Yurick’s best-known work, the 1965 gang novel “The Warriors,” was based on his experiences in the New York City Welfare Department, and was turned into a movie in 1979.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/10/arts/sol-yurick-novelist-dies-at-87.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Yurick’s best-known work, the 1965 gang novel “The Warriors,” was based on his experiences in the New York City Welfare Department, and was turned into a movie in 1979.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sol Yurick, a writer whose best-known work, the 1965 novel “The Warriors,” recast an ancient Greek battle as a tale of warring New York street gangs and earned a cult following in print, on film and eventually in a video game, died on Saturday in Manhattan. He was 87.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/arts/YURICK1-obit/YURICK1-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 709, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/arts/YURICK1-obit/YURICK1-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1806, 'width': 125