 policy in the second.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/continuity-on-obamas-economic-team/', 'snippet': 'Jacob J. Lew is part of a small circle of economic advisers who have ascended to prominent roles in the first term of the Obama presidency and will shape policy in the second.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After President Obama took office in 2009, Jacob J. Lew became a deputy secretary of state within days. Gene Sperling was serving as an adviser to the Treasury secretary. Austan Goolsbee, a longtime Obama adviser, was serving on Mr. Obama’s Council of Economic Advisers. Alan B. Krueger would become an assistant secretary of the Treasury within a few months.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Continuity on Obama’s Economic Team', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goolsbee, Austan D', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Krueger, Alan B', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lew, Jacob J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sperling, Gene', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'White House Council of Economic Advisers', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-09T17:46:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt and Kitty Bennett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Kitty', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bennett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0fe94d3-a795-51ff-9701-45cf91382f87', 'word_count': 540, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0fe94d3-a795-51ff-9701-45cf91382f87'}, {'abstract': 'Liberals and conservatives both seem to avoid looking in the mirror when facing certain challenges.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/on-budget-deficits-co2-binges-and-wise-investments/', 'snippet': 'Liberals and conservatives both seem to avoid looking in the mirror when facing certain challenges.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here’s a post, once again, on the human habit of kicking the can down the road — sometimes very different cans, depending on the person and the problem at hand.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Budget Deficits, CO2 Binges and Wise Investments', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carbon Dioxide', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Liberalism (US Politics)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Libertarianism (US Politics)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Friedman, Tom', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-09T17:47:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename':