ark-thirty/', 'snippet': 'Greig Fraser, the cinematographer of “Zero Dark Thirty,” discusses shooting the raid sequence for the film.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the many challenges\xa0 of making\xa0 “Zero Dark Thirty,” Kathryn Bigelow’s drama about the hunt for Osama bin Laden, involved\xa0 how to shoot one of the\xa0 climactic scenes: the SEAL team raid on Osama Bin Laden’s compound. The moment would be low in light, yet high in tension, so securing a cinematographer who could effectively shoot in near darkness was essential for Ms. Bigelow. She decided on Greig Fraser, an Australian director of photography who shot two other 2012 releases: “Snow White and the Huntsman” and “Killing Them Softly.” Those films also used darkness and light in interesting ways but were\xa0 more stylized in their approach. Mr. Fraser was recently honored by the New York Film Critics Circle\xa0 for his work on “Zero Dark Thirty.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Below the Line: The Light and Dark of ‘Zero Dark Thirty’', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bigelow, Kathryn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-09T18:06:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2deccd83-1738-5e83-999f-5ec1253efafc', 'word_count': 521, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2deccd83-1738-5e83-999f-5ec1253efafc'}, {'abstract': 'The Pacers, who will host the Knicks on Thursday night, have kept winning without their leading scorer, Danny Granger, thanks to defense and a favorable schedule.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/keeping-score-pacers-lead-central-despite-offensive-woes/', 'snippet': 'The Pacers, who will host the Knicks on Thursday night, have kept winning without their leading scorer, Danny Granger, thanks to defense and a favorable schedule.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 2011-12 N.B.A. season was an unqualified success for the Indiana Pacers, who finished with the third best record in the Eastern Conference and put a scare into the Miami Heat before bowing out of the conference semifinals in six games.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Keeping Score: Pacers Lead Central Despite Offensive Woes', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Granger, Danny', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indiana Pacers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-09T18:09:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Justin Kubatko', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kubatko', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c04d2f8b-51e0-59bc-a6a6-67aed74ccba1', 'word_count': 489, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c04d2f8b-51e0-59bc-a6a6-67aed74ccba1'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo’s 2013 State of the State address can be viewed here.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/gov-cuomos-state-of-the-state/', 'snippet': 'Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo’s 2013 State of the State address can be viewed here.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 4:08 p.m. | Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo, rewriting his agenda in the wake of Hurricane Sandy and the Newtown, Conn., school massacre, proposed measures in his State of the State address on Wednesday intended to limit the damage from future storms and to reduce the scourge of gun violence. (Mr. Cuomo begins his speech about 34 minutes into the video.) ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video: Cuomo’s State of the State Address', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the State Message (NYS)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-09T18:10:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7690f1a-27ab-53df-beb8-7e79738d8e59', 'word_count': 70, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7690f1a-27ab-53df-beb8-7e79738d8e59'}, {'abstract': 'Although the Obama administration has a stated goal of buying only alternative-technology vehicles for the federal government’s fleet of vehicles by 2015, the number of hybrid and electric vehicles bought by the government dropped by a third last year, according to Bloomberg News.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/wheelies-the-not-so-green-car-edition/', 'snippet': 'Although the Obama administration has a stated goal of buying only alternative-technology vehicles for the federal government’s fleet of vehicles by 2015, the number of hybrid and electric vehicles bought by the government dropped by a third last ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'In which we bring you motoring news from around the Web:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Whe