s and flexibility cry out to be used?', 'lead_paragraph': 'You know what’s kind of wild? We can identify products by their container designs. You’d know a ketchup bottle, even if it was empty and unlabeled, no matter what the brand. You’d know a pickle jar, or a milk jug, or a bottle of salad dressing, or a cereal box just by their container shapes.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/19/business/pogue-75/pogue-75-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/04/19/business/pogue-75/pogue-75-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bringing the Calendar Up to Date', 'kicker': 'State of the Art', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bringing The Calendar Up to Date', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pogue, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Calendars', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-09T19:47:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Pogue', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogue', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f42ed62b-09a8-5c44-aba5-b5804460b5b9', 'word_count': 1322, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f42ed62b-09a8-5c44-aba5-b5804460b5b9'}, {'abstract': 'After three incidents in three days, the aircraft’s maker says its record is comparable to that of other new planes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/10/business/boeing-defends-safety-of-787.html', 'snippet': 'After three incidents in three days, the aircraft’s maker says its record is comparable to that of other new planes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Boeing defended the safety of its 787 Dreamliner airplane on Wednesday after three incidents in three days, saying it had “extreme confidence” in the innovative design and technology used in the plane.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/10/business/Air/Air-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 305, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/10/business/Air/Air-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 305}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/10/business/Air/Air-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 521, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/10/business/Air/Air-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1042, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/10/business/Air/Air-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/10/business/Air/Air-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/10/business/Air/Air-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Boeing Says 787 Is Safe Despite Recent Problems', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Boeing Says 787 Is Safe Despite Recent Problems', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boeing Company', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aviation Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-09T19:55:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jad Mouawad', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mouawad', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d16c538d-d8db-5230-9fda-fd40dd19b03a', 'word_count': 597, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d16c538d-d8db-5230-9fda-fd40dd19b03a'}, {'abstract': 'Carl Berner, who was thought to be New York City’s oldest man, once said of his longevity: “I have no secret. I live a normal life.”', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/queens-man-dies-just-shy-of-111th-birthday/', 'snippet': 'Carl Berner, who was thought to be New York City’s oldest man, once said of his longevity: “I have no secret. I live a normal life.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carl Berner, a former toolmaker, toy-maker, factory owner and civic activist who achieved his greatest fame for simply staying alive, died at his home in Middle Village, Queens, on Monday, 20 days shy of his 111th birthday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/nyregion/09berner-cityroom/09berner-cityroom-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 314, 'width': 480, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/nyregion/09berner-cityroom/09berner-cityroom-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 314, 'width': 480, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/nyregion/09berner-cityroom/09berner-cityroom-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/09/nyregion/09berner-cityroom/09berner-cityroom-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/09/nyregion/09berner-cityroom/09berner-cityroom-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 0, 'width': 0, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Queens Man Dies Just Shy of 111th Birthday', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Age, Chronological', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Middle Village (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-09T20:00:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b507963a-5b78-59b6-a289-f53842cc673a', 'word_count': 193, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b507963a-5b78-59b6-a289-f53842cc673a'}, {'abstract': 'OKeh Records, the label that released historic early recordings by Louis Armstrong, King Oliver and Duke Ellington, is being revived under the corporate umbrella of Sony Masterworks.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/a-historic-jazz-label-gets-a-new-life/', 'snippet': 'OKeh Records, the label that released historic early recordings by Louis Armstrong, King Oliver and Duke Ellington, is being revived under the corporate umbrella of Sony Masterworks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The major-label landscape hasn’t been hospitable to jazz in recent years, but there’s a bit of good news on the horizon: OKeh Records, the label that released historic early recordings by Louis Armstrong, King Oliver and Duke Ellington, is being revived under the corporate umbrella of Sony Masterworks. The new OKeh roster will feature contemporary artists, including the guitarist Bill Frisell, the saxophonist David Sanborn and the pianist and keyboardist Bob James; its first release will be “A Different Time,” by the pianist John Medeski, on April 9.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Historic Jazz Label Gets a New Life', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'OKeh Jazz Label Gets a New Life', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blues Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mitchell, Chuck', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sony Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-09T20:05:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2cc27f43-c946-554b-bf68-d2b3bf639e43', 'word_count': 504, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2cc27f43-c946-554b-bf68-d2b3bf639e43'}, {'abstract': 'Dreamliners this week have been dogged by glitches.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/nightmare-week-for-dreamliner/', 'snippet': 'Dreamliners this week have been dogged by glitches.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Glitches on Boeing’s Dreamliner airplanes have surfaced every day since Monday, our colleagues in the Business section report. That includes an All Nippon Airways aircraft at Yamaguchi Ube Airport in Japan whose on-board computer on Wednesday erroneously showed problems with its brakes; a plane operated by Japan Airlines at Boston’s Logan Airport that had a fuel leak on Tuesday; another Japan Airlines plane at Logan that had an electrical fire on Monday. None of the problems occurred in-flight and none caused injuries. “While the problems so far do not point to serious design flaws with the airplane,” Jad Mouawad and Bettina Wassener write, “they represent an embarrassment to Boeing’s manufacturing ability.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nightmare Week for Dreamliner', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boeing Company', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-09T20:06:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ffe6b39-bc7d-5ee6-a660-4bb73952296c', 'word_count': 111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ffe6b39-bc7d-5ee6-a660-4bb73952296c'}, {'abstract': 'Most changes will have to come through legislation. But President Obama can do some work on his own.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/executive-action-on-guns/', 'snippet': 'Most changes will have to come through legislation. But President Obama can do some work on his own.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At a White House meeting about gun control this morning, Vice President Joe Biden said his boss was fully prepared to take executive action to reduce gun violence, an important but limited way to bypass the inevitable Congressional roadblocks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Executive Action on Guns', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco and Firearms', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-09T20:08:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Firestone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Firestone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebcc9836-b9fd-5a3a-82c2-ccd5f949dc41', 'word_count': 433, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebcc9836-b9fd-5a3a-82c2-ccd5f949dc41'}, {'abstract': 'In a slow sales week it edges out “Babel” by Mumford & Sons.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/les-misrables-soundtrack-storms-to-no-1/', 'snippet': 'In a slow sales week it edges out “Babel” by Mumford & Sons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The soundtrack to the film “Les Misérables” is No. 1 on the latest Billboard album chart, beating out Mumford & Sons by a hair in the sleepy sales week after Christmas.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Les Misérables’ Soundtrack Storms to No. 1', 'kicker': 'ArtsB