= {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Photos of The Moment | J.W. Anderson', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-09T22:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kasia Bobula', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kasia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bobula', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf8c14a8-38fe-512c-b411-30308848ef5e', 'word_count': 36, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf8c14a8-38fe-512c-b411-30308848ef5e'}, {'abstract': 'Predictions by veteran Oscar watchers are all over the map — the perfect time for you to tell us who you’d nominate.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/its-anybodys-guess-now-so-who-would-you-nominate/', 'snippet': 'Predictions by veteran Oscar watchers are all over the map — the perfect time for you to tell us who you’d nominate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With only hours to go until the Academy bigwigs, telecast host Seth MacFarlane and actress Emma Stone announce the nominees, the race is still not settled. Even veteran prognosticators are split on what will make the cut for best picture – “Lincoln”? “Argo”? “Zero Dark Thirty”? “Les Miz”? “Life of Pi” is creeping up in the game too, with its DGA nomination for Ang Lee, and the Bagger keeps hearing raves for “Silver Linings Playbook.” Other indicators, like the cinematography society nominations, are only muddying the field, at least when it comes to handicapping. If you’ve got money in the game on the nominations tomorrow, check some of the round-up sites here and here, and otherwise, prepare to be surprised. Who do you want to see on the list of nominees tomorrow morning?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'It’s Anybody’s Guess Now, So Whom Would You Nominate?', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-09T22:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1eda3c33-ccd8-534f-a762-bb0deaa271e2', 'word_count': 135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1eda3c33-ccd8-534f-a762-bb0deaa271e2'}, {'abstract': 'As a sign of the shows’ importance, creative directors attended, as did store chiefs, editors and a few celebrities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/10/fashion/prefall-fashion-shows-easygoing-tailoring-and-tweeds.html', 'snippet': 'As a sign of the shows’ importance, creative directors attended, as did store chiefs, editors and a few celebrities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE prefall collections resumed this week after a holiday break (we heard about people’s trips to St. Barth and the Bahamas), with presentations by European brands. A sign of how important these showings are, creative directors were in attendance: Peter Copping of Nina Ricci, Clare Waight Keller of Chloé, Alber Elbaz of Lanvin. Store chiefs turned up as well, along with editors and a few celebrities.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/10/fashion/10PREFALL_SP