 viewers see an interactive, 3-D, “virtual reality” representation of the city through the ages.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — In a 1789 painting of the Bastille, the French artist Hubert Robert portrayed that Paris fortress as a huge, seemingly impregnable structure and the Parisian revolutionaries who razed it as small, vulnerable human beings. More than two centuries later, thanks to 3-D modeling software, a different picture of the Bastille emerges. In its recreated setting it is the Bastille that seems small, even vulnerable. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/10/arts/10BASTILLE/10BASTILLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/10/arts/10BASTILLE/10BASTILLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/10/arts/10BASTILLE/10BASTILLE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 573, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/10/arts/10BASTILLE/10BASTILLE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1074, 'width': 1918, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/10/arts/10BASTILLE/10BASTILLE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/10/arts/10BASTILLE/10BASTILLE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/10/arts/10BASTILLE/10BASTILLE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Taking in Paris Any Day, Any Century', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Taking In Paris Any Day, Any Century', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pfanner, Eric', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Virtual Reality (Computers)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dassault Systems', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-09T22:25:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Pfanner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pfanner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb632e44-220c-5c28-b0fa-0b6eea198221', 'word_count': 946, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb632e44-220c-5c28-b0fa-0b6eea198221'}, {'abstract': 'Sprint Nextel will make local FM radio signals available on some of its smartphones, the first such deal with a carrier after years of pressure from the major radio broadcasters.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/fm-radio-on-cellphones-long-sought-by-broadcasters-comes-to-sprint/', 'snippet': 'Sprint Nextel will make local FM radio signals available on some of its smartphones, the first such deal with a carrier after years of pressure from the major radio broadcasters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For years, the radio industry has watched with worry as consumers snap up all kinds of electronic gadgets\xa0— from cellphones to tablets to set-top TV boxes\xa0— that deliver seemingly every kind of media but that old standby, terrestrial radio.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'FM Radio on Cellphones, Long Sought by Broadcasters, Comes to Sprint', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radio', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Emmis Communications Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sprint Nextel Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-09T22:27:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8313833f-6ee0-53a8-9c38-e8eec8379696', 'word_count': 488, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8313833f-6ee0-53a8-9c38-e8eec8379696'}, {'abstract': 'Smartphone and tablet users can choose from an array of mobile chargers for times when a wall socket is unavailable or inconvenient.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/10/technology/personaltech/mobile-devices-provide-power-for-smartphones-and-tablets.html', 'snippet': 'Smartphone and tablet users can choose from an array of mobile chargers for times when a wall socket is unavailable or inconvenient.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You undoubtedly know people so smitten with their smartphones and tablets that they experience separation anxiety when asked to put them away, even if it’s just long enough to get through dinner. But that is nothing compared with the angst they feel when their devices’ batteries are getting low. Think tremors and rending of garments.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/10/business/10TOOLKIT_SPAN/10TOOLKIT_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/10/business/10TOOLKIT_SPAN/10TOOLKIT_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/10/business/10TOOLKIT_SPAN/10TOOLKIT_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/10/business/10TOOLKIT_SPAN/10TOOLKIT_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/10/business/10TOOLKIT_SPAN/10TOOLKIT_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/10/business/10TOOLKIT_SPAN/10TOOLKIT_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/10/business/10TOOLKIT_SPAN/10TOOLKIT_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mobile Chargers Ease That Feeling of Powerlessness', 'kicker': 'Tool Kit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mobile Chargers Ease That Feeling of Powerlessness', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murphy