he form of satirical television ads for two parties at opposite ends of the political spectrum, have been stifled by the country’s Central Election Committee, which deemed them too offensive to broadcast. Despite those rulings, however, both ads have attracted tens of thousands of views online this week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Israeli Election Ads Ruled Too Offensive for Broadcast Rack Up Views on YouTube', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lieberman, Avigdor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yosef, Ovadia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shas Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-10T00:31:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1dff7035-1cd7-5d46-a54a-03de8f937e3e', 'word_count': 1207, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1dff7035-1cd7-5d46-a54a-03de8f937e3e'}, {'abstract': 'The injury to Robert Griffin III has cast doubt over his availability next season and also called into question whether his dynamic style of play can, or should, be continued when he returns.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/10/sports/football/redskins-robert-griffin-iii-has-knee-surgery-amid-questions-on-future.html', 'snippet': 'The injury to Robert Griffin III has cast doubt over his availability next season and also called into question whether his dynamic style of play can, or should, be continued when he returns.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Washington Redskins quarterback Robert Griffin III had two knee ligaments surgically repaired Wednesday — including a reconstruction of the anterior cruciate ligament and a repair of a tear in the lateral collateral ligament — the result of a knee injury he sustained during Sunday’s playoff loss to the Seattle Seahawks. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/10/sports/RG3/RG3-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/10/sports/RG3/RG3-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/10/sports/RG3/RG3-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/10/sports/RG3/RG3-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/10/sports/RG3/RG3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/10/sports/RG3/RG3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/10/sports/RG3/RG3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Questions of Strategy as Griffin Has Surgery', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Questions of Strategy As Griffin Has Surgery', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Griffin, Robert III', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Redskins', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-10T00:34:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judy Battista', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Battista', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2d46943-89de-526f-8bef-58fe45fb08fd', 'word_count': 635, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2d46943-89de-526f-8bef-58fe45fb08fd'}, {'abstract': 'The governor offered many ambitious plans for New York, but he should start with real gun control, a minimum-wage increase and campaign finance reform.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/10/opinion/gov-cuomos-wish-list.html', 'snippet': 'The governor offered many ambitious plans for New York, but he should start with real gun control, a minimum-wage increase and campaign finance reform.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Andrew Cuomo vowed on Wednesday that New York would soon enact the “toughest gun assault weapon ban in the nation. Period.” New Yorkers should hold him to that promise. He made stronger gun laws an urgent priority in his annual State of the State address, but he will need to present the specifics quickly to a divided Legislature and push lawmakers to act. The supporting documents for his speech suggest that he plans to tighten the ban on large magazines and require all gun owners to reapply for a permit every few years, replacing the lifetime permits allowed in some counties. He also wants mental health professionals to be able to report if someone is dangerous, allowing law enforcement to confiscate the individual’s firearms. And he would make the process of licensing guns more efficient while increasing penalties for use of guns illegally.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gov. Cuomo’s Wish List', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gov. Cuomo’s Wish List', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minimum Wage', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the State Message (NYS)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-10T00:41:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/e3caf520-8ff8-503c-85f6-fc8cf6406b7d', 'word_count': 412, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3caf520-8ff8-503c-85f6-fc8cf6406b7d'}, {'abstract': 'Houses with secluded gardens and courtyards were widely demolished to make way for glassed apartment blocks, but some Iranians are beginning to reverse the trend.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/10/world/middleeast/restoring-irans-majestic-homes-in-a-high-rise-era.html', 'snippet': 'Houses with secluded gardens and courtyards were widely demolished to make way for glassed apartment blocks, but some Iranians are beginning to reverse the trend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KASHAN, Iran — A petite woman in gray boots and a checkered scarf, Shanaz Nader had spent much of her adult life abroad, with long stretches in Tokyo, London and New York. But here she was braving a cold wind in this desert city three hours south of Tehran, making her way through a maze of high mud-brick walls. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/10/world/kashan1/kashan1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/10/world/kashan1/kashan1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/10/world/kashan1/kashan1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/10/world/kashan1/kashan1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/10/world/kashan1/kashan1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/10/world/kashan1/kashan1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/10/world/kashan1/kashan1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Restoring Iran’s Heritage of Magnificent Hom