, 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36725711-f998-5bdb-9632-8492724a682d', 'word_count': 914, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36725711-f998-5bdb-9632-8492724a682d'}, {'abstract': 'Mike Piazza hit more home runs as a catcher than any player in baseball, but suspicion about performance-enhancing drugs may have prevented him from being elected to the Hall of Fame.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/10/sports/baseball/mike-piazza-falls-short-in-hall-of-fame-voting.html', 'snippet': 'Mike Piazza hit more home runs as a catcher than any player in baseball, but suspicion about performance-enhancing drugs may have prevented him from being elected to the Hall of Fame.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Voters roundly rejected some of the most accomplished baseball players in the history of the game Wednesday, denying them entry into the Hall of Fame because of their documented association with performance-enhancing drugs. Caught in the middle was Mike Piazza, who hit 396 home runs as a catcher, more than any other player at the position, but who was never directly linked to steroids or human growth hormone.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/10/sports/piazza/piazza-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 659, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/10/sports/piazza/piazza-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 659}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/10/sports/piazza/piazza-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 933, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/10/sports/piazza/piazza-superJumbo.jpg', 'hei