'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c65063c4-26b8-59c7-84c4-acc06eb10fae', 'word_count': 623, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c65063c4-26b8-59c7-84c4-acc06eb10fae'}, {'abstract': 'Forty years after the Supreme Court handed down the great abortion rights decision, Americans remain permanently uncomfortable with the issue.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/10/opinion/collins-the-woes-of-roe.html', 'snippet': 'Forty years after the Supreme Court handed down the great abortion rights decision, Americans remain permanently uncomfortable with the issue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Forty years ago this month, the Supreme Court handed down the great abortion rights decision Roe v. Wade. To be honest, you’re not going to be seeing a whole lot of cake and Champagne. Time magazine recognized the occasion with a downbeat cover story. (“They’ve Been Losing Ever Since.”) Gallup polls suggest support for abortion rights is fading, particularly among young Americans, and that more people now regard themselves as “pro-life” than “pro-choice.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-su