'', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d055d347-3f45-5144-95b6-ddcdd95a8142', 'word_count': 623, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d055d347-3f45-5144-95b6-ddcdd95a8142'}, {'abstract': 'Morgan Stanley has been shrinking its business of trading bonds, commodities and other investments, leaving that to be dominated by its Wall Street rivals.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/deep-cuts-raise-questions-about-morgan-stanley/', 'snippet': 'Morgan Stanley has been shrinking its business of trading bonds, commodities and other investments, leaving that to be dominated by its Wall Street rivals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Morgan Stanley’s top executives gathered in mid-September at the Gramercy Park Hotel in Manhattan to discuss strategy, some participants complained that the room was too small.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Deep Cuts Raise Questions About Morgan Stanley', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Slimming Wall Street Giant', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gorman, James P', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hadden, Edward Glenn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Morgan Stanley', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-10T02:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susanne Craig', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Craig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5ead53a-cf9c-502e-b5fa-8163138e3bcb', 'word_count': 1341, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5ead53a-cf9c-502e-b5fa-8163138e3bcb'}, {'abstract': 'Judge Bork was a tragic figure, not because he was dealt an unjust hand when he was rejected for the Supreme Court — he wasn’t — but because of his inability to understand what had happened.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/09/robert-borks-tragedy/', 'snippet': 'Judge Bork was a tragic figure, not because he was dealt an unjust hand when he was rejected for the Supreme Court — he wasn’t — but because of his inability to understand what had happened.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Even before Robert Bork died last month, he had achieved something close to martyrdom. In the quarter-century since the Senate rejected his Supreme Court nomination, successive generations of conservative lawyers and activists have carried the torch, depicting his defeat as an injustice of historic proportion. Following his death at the age of 85, liberals mostly maintained a respectful silence while conservatives dusted off old complaints about the conduct of the confirmation hearing and the unfairness, in their view, of the “borking” the nominee received. Clearly, the Bork Battle survives Bork.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Robert Bork’s Tragedy', 'kicker': 'Linda Greenhouse', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitution (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bork, Robert H', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Specter, Arlen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate Committee on the Judiciary', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-10T02:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Linda Greenhouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Linda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenhouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/401a347c-857c-51a6-9309-cf44ac6ed065', 'word_count': 1646, 'uri': 'nyt://article/401a347c-857c-51a6-9309-cf44ac6ed065'}, {'abstract': 'President Hugo Chávez’s health crisis and decision to proceed on Thursday with a quasi-presidential inauguration that he is unable to attend is producing national angst about who is in charge.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/10/world/americas/would-be-inauguration-in-venezuela-for-chavez.html', 'snippet': 'President Hugo Chávez’s health crisis and decision to proceed on Thursday with a quasi-presidential inauguration that he is unable to attend is producing national angst about who is in charge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CARACAS, Venezuela — President Hugo Chávez’s supporters have not ruled out swearing him in from his hospital in Havana. His detractors are calling for government investigators to go check his pulse themselves. The justices whom Mr. Chávez’s allies have named to the Supreme Court have decided that he can continue to govern in absentia.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chávez, or at Least His Sash, Is Set for Venezuela Inauguration', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chávez, or at Least His Sash, Is Set for Venezuela Inauguration', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chavez, Hugo', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venezuela', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inaugurations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-10T02:01:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Neuman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Neuman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d4a3ff2-9f08-5572-8b02-89d27c601e0b', 'word_count': 1225, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d4a3ff2-9f08-5572-8b02-89d27c601e0b'}, {'abstract': 'The Supreme Court considered a request by Missouri prosecutors and the federal government to rule that warrants are not needed to obtain blood samples in drunken-driving cases.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/10/us/supreme-court-weighs-drunken-driving-blood-tests.html', 'snippet': 'The Supreme Court considered a request by Missouri prosecutors and the federal government to rule that warrants are not needed to obtain blood samples in drunken-driving cases.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Prosecutors in Missouri, supported by the federal government, came to the Supreme Court on Wednesday with a big request: They wanted the justices to rule that the police do not need warrants to obtain blood samples in drunken-driving investigations.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Justices Look at Legality of Drunken-Driving Test', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Justices Look at Legality Of Drunken-Driving Test', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests (Sobriety)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drunken and Reckless Driving', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Missouri', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-10T02:02:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Liptak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liptak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b92692d6-11e0-5d22-a45b-ebe341377e1a', 'word_count': 814, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b92692d6-11e0-5d22-a45b-ebe341377e1a'}, {'abstract': "How can Indian women gain power so they would not only be safe, but also have more say in their nation's future?", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/roomfordebate/2013/01/09/power-for-the-women-of-india/', 'snippet': "How can Indian women gain power so they would not only be safe, but also have more say in their nation's future?", 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Power for the Women of India', 'kicker': 'Room for Debate', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-10T02:03:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0222c9a4-6261-5b53-9aae-68d697ea4d19', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0222c9a4-6261-5b53-9aae-68d697ea4d19'}, {'abstract': 'The Obama administration said that the 2008 conviction of a Guantánamo Bay prisoner was valid even though charges against him were not war crimes under international law.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/10/us/us-to-press-fight-of-detainees-appeal.html', 'snippet': 'The Obama administration said that the 2008 conviction of a Guantánamo Bay prisoner was valid even though charges against him were not war crimes under international law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Obama administration, after a high-level debate among its legal team, told a federal appeals court on Wednesday that the conviction of a Guantánamo Bay prisoner by a military commission in 2008 was valid even though the charges against him — including “conspiracy” and “material support for terrorism” — were not recognized as war crimes in international law.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. to Press Fight of Detainee’s Appeal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. to Press Fight of Detainee’s Appeal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Savage, Charlie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holder, Eric H Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guantanamo Bay Naval Base (Cuba)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-10T02:04:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b881ddc-8b7b-56d6-bc0e-edd5d17f3a3f', 'word_count': 536, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b881ddc-8b7b-56d6-bc0e-edd5d17f3a3f'}, {'abstract': 'This time, something must be done about gun laws. And it looks as if something will.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/10/opinion/blow-reframing-the-gun-debate.html', 'snippet': 'This time, something must be done about gun laws. And it looks as if something will.', 'lead_paragraph'