r dives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Diving apps were this week’s subject for the App Smart column. If that seems a little unseasonal then you should remember that some great diving locations are in sunny spots, and a winter getaway vacation doesn’t have to be about skiing!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'App Smart Extra: More Options for Divers', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-10T13:00:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kit Eaton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kit', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eaton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c262aee-c8c1-55ca-900f-f83e8df96831', 'word_count': 432, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c262aee-c8c1-55ca-900f-f83e8df96831'}, {'abstract': 'Europe’s sovereign debt crisis originated in a sclerotic Balkan polity — not the legendary Athenian city-state of yore.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/11/opinion/global/reversing-greeces-free-fall.html', 'snippet': 'Europe’s sovereign debt crisis originated in a sclerotic Balkan polity — not the legendary Athenian city-state of yore.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Regarding “Greece’s rotten oligarchy” (Views, Jan. 7): In citing the mendacity, corruption and avarice overrunning Athens, Kostas Vaxevanis describes a country whose political establishment has betrayed its citizenry. But the notion that modern-day Hellas can be revivified by a return to “Greece’s ancient democratic heritage” is a chimera.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reversing Greece’s free fall', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker'