'pub_date': '2013-01-10T13:08:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3cf58d24-85e3-599c-a21e-6ac9ddabad5c', 'word_count': 93, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3cf58d24-85e3-599c-a21e-6ac9ddabad5c'}, {'abstract': 'Paul Schrader, Bret Easton Ellis, Lindsay Lohan and a porn star named James Deen try to make a movie for $250,000 that will save all of their careers. What could go wrong?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/13/magazine/here-is-what-happens-when-you-cast-lindsay-lohan-in-your-movie.html', 'snippet': 'Paul Schrader, Bret Easton Ellis, Lindsay Lohan and a porn star named James Deen try to make a movie for $250,000 that will save all of their careers. What could go wrong?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lindsay Lohan moves through the Chateau Marmont as if she owns the place, but in a debtor-prison kind of way. She’ll soon owe the hotel $46,000. Heads turn subtly as she slinks toward a table to meet a young producer and an old director. The actress’s mother, Dina Lohan, sits at the next table. Mom sweeps blond hair behind her ear and tries to eavesdrop. A few tables away, a distinguished-looking middle-aged man patiently waits for the actress. He has a stack of presents for her.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/magazine/13lohan1/13lohan1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 423, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/13/magazine/13lohan1/13lohan1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 423}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/magazine/13lohan1/13lohan1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 722, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/magazine/13lohan1/13lohan1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1057, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/magazine/13lohan1/13lohan1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/13/magazine/13lohan1/13lohan1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/magazine/13lohan1/13lohan1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Here Is What Happens When You Cast Lindsay Lohan in Your Movie', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Mistfits', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Canyons (Movie)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodrick, Stephen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lohan, Lindsay', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schrader, Paul', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ellis, Bret Easton', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Deen, James', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pope, Braxton', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-10T13:09:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Rodrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rodrick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0de56a4f-bb6a-5d05-aeec-3ec20a9ba398', 'word_count': 7640, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0de56a4f-bb6a-5d05-aeec-3ec20a9ba398'}, {'abstract': 'William A. Ackman and Daniel S. Loeb became business rivals on Wednesday, with hundreds of millions of dollars in play over Herbalife. | Diminished profits have forced Morgan Stanley to cut back its trading desk, raising questions about the firm. | Jacob J. Lew, President Obama’s chief of staff and former budget director, has been tapped to be the secretary of the Treasury. | Amid criticism, the board of the American International Group decided not to join a lawsuit against the federal government.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/01/10/battle-lines-drawn-over-herbalife/', 'snippet': 'William A. Ackman and Daniel S. Loeb became business rivals on Wednesday, with hundreds of millions of dollars in play over Herbalife. | Diminished profits have forced Morgan Stanley to cut back its trading desk, raising questions about the firm. ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'BATTLE LINES DRAWN OVER HERBALIFE \xa0|\xa0 The clash of the hedge fund titans has been set, and the financial world is eagerly watching. William A. Ackman and Daniel S. Loeb, two of the most prominent hedge fund managers in Manhattan, became business rivals on Wednesday, with hundreds of millions of dollars in play over Herbalife, a nutritional supplements company.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Battle Lines Drawn Over Herbalife', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-10T13:16:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/39afb4fa-734f-5f35-9709-961f601a0209', 'word_count': 1949, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39afb4fa-734f-5f35-9709-961f601a0209'}, {'abstract': 'Metropolitan Diary: A subway commuter on a packed stairway witnessed an unusual method of being inconsiderate.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/10/gambling-on-a-crowded-subway-platform/', 'snippet': 'Metropolitan Diary: A subway commuter on a packed stairway witnessed an unusual method of being inconsiderate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dear Diary:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gambling on a Crowded Subway Platform', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Commuting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lotteries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subways', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Midtown Area (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-10T13:30:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sharon Lowenheim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sharon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lowenheim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7952606e-3dfe-59bb-a9de-827f7f95a614', 'word_count': 126, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7952606e-3dfe-59bb-a9de-827f7f95a614'}, {'abstract': 'French police investigating the murder of three Turkish-Kurdish women activists may have to look for clues in the murky politics of a Kurdish guerrilla movement with links to Syria, Iraq and Iran.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/10/theories-link-paris-murders-to-kurdish-peace-moves/', 'snippet': 'French police investigating the murder of three Turkish-Kurdish women activists may have to look for clues in the murky politics of a Kurdish guerrilla movement with links to Syria, Iraq and Iran.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The overnight discovery in Paris of the  bodies of three Kurdish women activists prompted instant speculation that the execution-style triple killing was linked to an attempt to disrupt peace talks between Turkey and a jailed Kurdish guerrilla leader.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/10/blogs/10rdv-kurd/10rdv-kurd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/10/blogs/10rdv-kurd/10rdv-kurd-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1370, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/10/blogs/10rdv-kurd/10rdv-kurd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/10/blogs/10rdv-kurd/10rdv-kurd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/10/blogs/10rdv-kurd/10rdv-kurd-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Theories Link Paris Murders to Kurdish Peace Moves', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kurds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ocalan, Abdullah', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Kurdistan Workers' Party", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-10T13:51:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Morris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b566e99-7026-5571-8c0c-ae8513b4bd8f', 'word_count': 618, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b566e99-7026-5571-8c0c-ae8513b4bd8f'}, {'abstract': 'Herbalife executives made a presentation to analysts and its investors to respond to accusations by the investor William A. Ackman that their company operates a pyramid scheme.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/01/10/live-blog-herbalife-responds-to-accusations-from-hedge-fund/', 'snippet': 'Herbalife executives made a presentation to analysts and its investors to respond to accusations by the investor William A. Ackman that their company operates a pyramid scheme.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Herbalife found itself in a public relations nightmare in December when the hedge fund manager William A. Ackman called the company a pyramid scheme, announcing he was short-selling its shares. Since then, the stock has rebounded somewhat, and it got a lift on Wednesday when another hedge fund manager, Daniel S. Loeb, said he was bullish on Herbalife, which sells nutritional supplements and skin-care products through a network of independent distributors.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Herbalife Responds to Accusations From Hedge Fund', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hedge Funds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ackman, William A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Loeb, Daniel S', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Herbalife Ltd', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-10T13:56:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d6fc5e7-bd82-587b-b9d5-ce841d041bdf', 'word_count': 1451, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d6fc5e7-bd82-587b-b9d5-ce841d041bdf'}, {'abstract': 'Political news from today’s Times, plus a look at what’s happening in Washington.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/10/the-early-word-fight-prep/', 'snippet': 'Political news from today’s Times, plus a look at what’s happening in Washington.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Today’s Times:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Early Word: Fight Prep', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-10T13:59:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Southall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Southall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aeea3a38-bf2f-504d-882b-2948dfa4fa7d', 'word_count': 392, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aeea3a38-bf2f-504d-882b-2948dfa4fa7d'}, {'abstract': 'Mercier’s new eyeliner glides on, is easy to use and offers a soft golden glow at cocktail hour.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/10/vain-glorious-laura-merciers-caviar-stick-eye-color/', 'snippet': 'Mercier’s new eyeliner glides on, is easy to use and offers a soft golden glow at cocktail hour.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For those of us who didn’t snare any rose gold jewelry for the holidays, consider Laura Mercier’s new Caviar Stick Eye Color in rose gold as a consolation prize. Called “Caviar” because it glides on and is easy to use, the eyeliner has warm tones that seem to work on any skin color. I’ve been wearing it during the day (it’s a total mood lifter) and when the sun goes down, adding a little extra, for a soft golden glow at cocktail hour. A luxe treat for $24.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vain Glorious | Laura Mercier’s Caviar Stick Eye Color', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beauty', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sephora', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-10T14:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Earle-Levine', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Earle-Levine', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f626d11b-f884-5792-bbb3-e25f85567062', 'word_count': 104, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f626d11b-f884-5792-bbb3-e25f85567062'}, {'abstract': 'Michael Kimmelman views architecture in terms of public policy as well as aesthetics.', 'web_url': 'https://publiceditor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/10/in-the-spirit-of-ada-louise-huxtable-a-times-critic-reinvents-his-role/', 'snippet': 'Michael Kimmelman views architecture in terms of public policy as well as aesthetics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Michael Kimmelman’s piece on Ada Louise Huxtable, who died this week at age 91, in Tuesday’s Arts section is tagged “An Appraisal,” but it could easily have been called something more enthusiastic: an appreciation. For by his own eager admission, Mr. Kimmelman – who took over as architecture critic in September 2011 — owes much to Ms. Huxtable, whom he calls a role model.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In the Spirit of Ada Louise Huxtable, a Times Critic Reinvents His Role', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-10T14:02:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d8313e6-1fa0-5664-a31f-d9a175a0f2e9', 'word_count': 605, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d8313e6-1fa0-5664-a31f-d9a175a0f2e9'}, {'abstract': 'Steven Spielberg’s film starring Daniel Day-Lewis was nominated for 12 Academy Awards, including best picture, best director (for Mr. Spielberg) and best actor (for Mr. Day-Lewis).', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/10/lincoln-leads-academy-award-nominations/', 'snippet': 'Steven Spielberg’s film starring Daniel Day-Lewis was nominated for 12 Academy Awards, including best picture, best director (for Mr. Spielberg) and best actor (for Mr. Day-Lewis).', 'lead_paragraph': '“Lincoln,” Steven Spielberg’s film starring Daniel Day-Lewis as the president of the United States who grappled with the scourge of slavery and the Civil War, was nominated for 12 Academy Awards on Thursday morning, including best picture, best director (for Mr. Spielberg) and best actor (for Mr. Day-Lewis). The other films nominated for best picture were “Beasts of the Southern Wild,” “Silver Linings Playbook,” “Zero Dark Thirty,” “Les Misérables,” “Life of Pi,” “Amour,” “Django Unchained” and “Argo.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/arts/oscar-lincoln/oscar-lincoln-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 264, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/08/arts/oscar-lincoln/oscar-lincoln-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 264}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/arts/oscar-lincoln/oscar-lincoln-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 451, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/arts/oscar-lincoln/oscar-lincoln-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 902, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/arts/oscar-lincoln/oscar-lincoln-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/08/arts/oscar-lincoln/oscar-lincoln-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/08/arts/oscar-lincoln/oscar-lincoln-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Lincoln’ Leads Academy Award Nominations', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Day-Lewis, Daniel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lincoln, Abraham', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spielberg, Steven', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-10T14:06:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c512732-7d45-5f93-a6d1-43fcd816bbc3', 'word_count': 95, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c512732-7d45-5f93-a6d1-43fcd816bbc3'}, {'abstract': 'An investor group led by Cerberus Capital Management agreed on Thursday to buy a number of grocery chains from Supervalu, including Albertsons, for about $3.3 billion. The Cerberus-led group will also buy up to 30 percent of Supervalu itself, paying $4 a share in a tender offer.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/01/10/cerberus-to-buy-albertsons-grocery-chain-from-supervalu/', 'snippet': 'An investor group led by Cerberus Capital Management agreed on Thursday to buy a number of grocery chains from Supervalu, including Albertsons, for about $3.3 billion. The Cerberus-led group will also buy up to 30 percent of Supervalu itself, payi...', 'lead_paragraph': 'An investor group led by Cerberus Capital Management agreed on Thursday to buy a number of grocery chains from Supervalu, including Albertsons, for about $3.3 billion.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cerberus to Buy Albertsons Grocery Chain From Supervalu', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ALBERTSONS INC', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cerberus Capital Management', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SUPERVALU INC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-10T14:14:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/16af50c0-d192-59ee-9b28-12d92f256920', 'word_count': 160, 'uri': 'nyt://article/16af50c0-d192-59ee-9b28-12d92f256920'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/10/what-were-reading-604/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Esquire: McDonald’s versus Italian pizza: is this war? — Jeff Gordinier', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-10T14:55:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/053e48fb-a48d-5b97-b0e3-8ddbb9b5cce9', 'word_count': 422, 'uri': 'nyt://article/053e48fb-a48d-5b97-b0e3-8ddbb9b5cce9'}, {'abstract': 'The surprise omissions of Thursday suggest a replay of the 1999 race when a favored epic (“Saving Private Ryan”) was beat by a heartwarming romance (“Shakespeare in Love”).', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/10/director-snubs-point-to-a-threeway-race-lincoln-vs-playbook-and-pi/', 'snippet': 'The surprise omissions of Thursday suggest a replay of the 1999 race when a favored epic (“Saving Private Ryan”) was beat by a heartwarming romance (“Shakespeare in Love”).', 'lead_paragraph': 'An Oscar race that could have gone in almost any direction suddenly has a shape, and it’s not one that anyone was expecting. The shutout of Kathryn Bigelow and Ben Affleck for best director – though their movies, “Zero Dark Thirty” and “Argo,” were nominees for best picture and screenplay as well as for performances – will cause much hand-wringing around Hollywood, where both were considered locks, especially after they earned nods from the Directors Guild. Tom Hooper, the director of “Les Misérables,” was skipped over too, though his film had a high number of nominations.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Director Snubs Point to a Threeway Race: ‘Lincoln’ vs. ‘Playbook’ and ‘Pi’', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-10T15:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1cc19905-3403-51d2-ac8e-3be7c551f88e', 'word_count': 326, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1cc19905-3403-51d2-ac8e-3be7c551f88e'}, {'abstract': 'If the author of the Patrick Melrose novels could meet any character from literature, he would choose Isabel Archer. And then he’d propose marriage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/13/books/review/edward-st-aubyn-by-the-book.html', 'snippet': 'If the author of the Patrick Melrose novels could meet any character from literature, he would choose Isabel Archer. And then he’d propose marriage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If the author of the Patrick Melrose novels could meet any character from literature, he would choose Isabel Archer. And then he’d propose marriage.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/books/review/0113-BTB/0113-BTB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 721, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/books/review/0113-BTB/0113-BTB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1441, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/books/review/0113-BTB/0113-BTB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/13/books/review/0113-BTB/0113-BTB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/books/review/0113-BTB/0113-BTB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Edward St. Aubyn: By the Book', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'By the Book: Edward St. Aubyn', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'St Aubyn, Edward', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-10T15:15:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a9207f9-4314-5362-a772-37cbfb6b9525', 'word_count': 1028, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a9207f9-4314-5362-a772-37cbfb6b9525'}, {'abstract': 'In his state of the state address, he never mentioned guns. Unlike the other tri-state area governors.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/10/what-chris-christie-didnt-say/', 'snippet': 'In his state of the state address, he never mentioned guns. Unlike the other tri-state area governors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'All three tri-state area governors gave their annual state of the state speeches this week. Two of them – Democrats Andrew Cuomo of New York and Dannel Malloy of Connecticut – discussed the weapons epidemic that was brought into such ghastly focus by the shootings in Newtown, Conn. Mr. Cuomo actually called for major legislation –to restrict ownership of assault-style weapons and high-capacity magazines.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Chris Christie Didn’t Say', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newtown, Conn, Shooting (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'},