spect little girls by letting them go first? For starters, it perpetuates millenniums of sexism.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/10/i-dont-want-my-preschooler-to-be-a-gentleman/', 'snippet': 'What’s the harm in teaching little boys to respect little girls by letting them go first? For starters, it perpetuates millenniums of sexism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My 4-year-old son, Emmett, swallows a spoonful of cereal and asks me if I know what a gentleman is. Surprised, I tell him I have some idea; then I ask what the word means to him.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'I Don’t Want My Preschooler to Be a ‘Gentleman’', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs, Etiquette and Manners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (Pre-School)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Title IX (Gender Discrimination Legislation)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-10T15:22:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Messina', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Messina', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fae3b49c-eb99-5711-bb9d-7c46f27642d1', 'word_count': 764, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fae3b49c-eb99-5711-bb9d-7c46f27642d1'}, {'abstract': 'This week’s Poetry Pairing matches “Bleak Weather,” a poem by Ella Wheeler Wilcox, with “A Cool Glid