ount': 36, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ef74701-8484-587e-b89e-e714e4f4cd37'}, {'abstract': 'Hall of Fame voting would be criticized no matter what because baseball never actually dealt with the steroids era.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/11/sports/a-statement-on-steroids-but-what-does-it-say.html', 'snippet': 'Hall of Fame voting would be criticized no matter what because baseball never actually dealt with the steroids era.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Perhaps the most remarkable thing about the great Hall of Fame shutout of 2013 is, no matter which way the election voting had gone on Wednesday, the outrage would have sounded remarkably similar. Today’s injustice — that the Hall of Fame path of some of the game’s greatest players, led by Barry Bonds and Roger Clemens, was blocked at least for now in the name of protesting the steroids era — would have been replaced by the injustice of ignoring the steroids era. The Hall’s credibility, now under attack for omitting such obvious superstars, would have been assailed for welcoming players everyone believes cheated the game on a massive scale.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/11/sports/baseball/11leadingpic/11leadingpic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 702, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/11/sports/baseball/11leadingpic/11leadingpic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1404, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/11/sports/baseball/11leadingpic/11leadingpic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/11/sports/baseball/11leading