h John Hawkes and Marion Cotillard were seen as likely contenders for Oscars, both were shut out.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pity poor John Hawkes. Mr. Hawkes endured weeks of discomfort – and perhaps permanent back damage – to play the polio-stricken writer Mark O’Brien in “The Sessions,” only to be snubbed by the Academy for best actor. His co-star Helen Hunt, playing a sex therapist in a deeply felt performance that has her frequently naked, did earn the attention of the Academy, though. (Mr. Hawkes may get a chance to go to the ceremony though: he appears in “Lincoln”; then again so do hundreds of other actors.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Apologies to John Hawkes and Marion Cotillard', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-10T16:52:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/13dc2dc7-b3d1-56c5-a8fc-bfc911a464e0', 'word_count': 437, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13dc2dc7-b3d1-56c5-a8fc-bfc911a464e0'}, {'abstract': 'In the Rockaways, truckloads of sand containing debris from Hurricane Sandy are emptied into huge sand-sifting machines. The sand is filtered, then returned to build up damaged seafronts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/nyregion/100000001996799/sifting-out-sandy.html', 'snippet': 'In the Rockaways, truckloads of sand containing debris from Hurricane Sandy are emptied into huge sand-sifting machines. The sand is filtered, then returned to build up damaged seafronts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the Rockaways, truc