 Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By now, you’d think that Oscar nominations would be all in a good night’s sleep for Amy Adams. After earning best supporting actress nods for “Junebug” (2005), “Doubt” (2008) and “The Fighter” (2010), Ms. Adams has received another shout-out, this time for Paul Thomas Anderson’s film “The Master,” playing Peggy Dodd, the submissive wife of a charismatic religious leader (Philip Seymour Hoffman) who eventually shows her husband who’s boss with a rather steely hand.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Amy Adams, Scared by Her Own Character', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adams, Amy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-10T17:44:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dda7a8a2-15a6-574a-a7c8-ae1a09524985', 'word_count': 331, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dda7a8a2-15a6-574a-a7c8-ae1a09524985'}, {'abstract': 'Pilgrims on their way to the Gangasagar mela in West Bengal.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/10/image-of-the-day-jan-10/', 'snippet': 'Pilgrims on their way to the Gangasagar mela in West Bengal.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Image of the Day: Jan. 10', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-10T17:45:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World',