enhouse gases.\xa0The scientists were\xa0Peter C. Frumhoff, an ecologist who directs science and policy for the Union of Concerned Scientists, and\xa0Kerry Emanuel, a veteran climate and hurricane researcher at the Massachusetts Institute of Technology. (Emanuel has a new edition of his short everyman’s guide to global warming, by the way.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More On a Quest for Common Ground on Climate Change', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carbon Dioxide', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservatism (US Politics)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Energy Efficiency', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Liberalism (US Politics)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Emanuel, Kerry', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ATMOSPHERE', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Massachusetts Institute of Technology', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Academy of Sciences', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Union of Concerned Scientists', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'YouTube.com', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-10T19:47:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/137c2687-8301-5d8b-bd6c-f8ce417fe371', 'word_count': 699, 'uri': 'nyt://article/137c2687-8301-5d8b-bd6c-f8ce417fe371'}, {'abstract': 'Three male stars of “Girls” — Alex Karpovsky, Adam Driver and Christopher Abbott — talk about their characters and how the show has changed their lives.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/13/arts/television/adam-driver-christopher-abbott-alex-karpovsky-of-girls.html', 'snippet': 'Three male stars of “Girls” — Alex Karpovsky, Adam Driver and Christopher Abbott — talk about their characters and how the show has changed their lives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOR a show that is, down to its title, about women, “Girls” pays a lot of attention to its boys. The male characters — boyfriends, exes, bosses, frenemies — are fleshed out in a way that’s unusual for an ensemble comedy, especially one aimed at the other gender. (How long did audiences have to wait for Mr. Big’s mere name on “Sex and the City”?)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/arts/13GIRLS_SPAN/13GIRLS_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 368, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/13/arts/13GIRLS_SPAN/13GIRLS_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 368}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/arts/13GIRLS_SPAN/13GIRLS_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 628, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_n