 None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/251b66b0-83f3-5a4d-bfbe-7bfdf3fbd11f', 'word_count': 1755, 'uri': 'nyt://article/251b66b0-83f3-5a4d-bfbe-7bfdf3fbd11f'}, {'abstract': 'Andrew Rannells, a cast member of “The New Normal,” also plays Elijah, the ex-boyfriend of Lena Dunham’s character in “Girls.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/13/arts/television/andrew-rannells-of-girls-and-the-new-normal.html', 'snippet': 'Andrew Rannells, a cast member of “The New Normal,” also plays Elijah, the ex-boyfriend of Lena Dunham’s character in “Girls.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'NOT all of the boys of “Girls” fit in with the Brooklyn crew. Andrew Rannells, a longtime New York theater actor, plays Elijah, Hannah’s gay ex-boyfriend. Mr. Rannells, 34, who lives in the East Village, also stars in “The New Normal,” the NBC sitcom about a gay couple trying to have a child via surrogate. He saw his career blossom after he appeared on Broadway in “The Book of Mormon.” These are excerpts from his conversation with Melena Ryzik.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/arts/13BGIRLS/13BGIRLS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/arts/13BGIRLS/13BGIRLS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A ‘New Normal’ Star Thrives in the TV Ensemble', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A ‘New Normal’ Star Thrives in the TV Ensemble', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 