 appeal to smartphone-addicted buyers.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/10/portable-navigation-learns-some-new-moves-at-c-e-s/', 'snippet': 'One company that is taking a page from built-in car systems to appeal to smartphone-addicted buyers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Portable navigation devices aren’t dead yet — at least not at the Consumer Electronics Show in Las Vegas. Several makers are promoting their wares this week, including one company that is taking a page from built-in car systems to appeal to smartphone-addicted buyers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Portable Navigation Learns Some New Moves at C.E.S.', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Positioning System', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Consumer Electronics Show', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Navigation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Garmin Ltd', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Magellan's", 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TomTom NV', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-10T21:40:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By John R. Quain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Quain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/11a53021-48f7-5aec-8d45-6f26884b2409', 'word_count': 678, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11a53021-48f7-5aec-8d45-6f26884b2409'}, {'abstract': 'A Google+ Hangout on modern slavery with Somaly Mam, Rachel Lloyd and Nick Kristof.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/10/a-google-hangout-on-modern-slavery/', 'snippet': 'A Google+ Hangout on modern slavery with Somaly Mam, Rachel Lloyd and Nick Kristof.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Today I participated in a Google+ Hangout with two of my heroes, Somaly Mam of the Somaly Mam Foundation, and Rachel Lloyd of GEMS Girls. Both have devoted their life’s work to fighting sex trafficking, and here’s our discussion. Let me know what you think in the comments section. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Google+ Hangout on Modern Slavery', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-10T21:42:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/759ac53f-3db1-5c54-bec1-68bd8fd70b86', 'word_count': 50, 'uri': 'nyt://article/759ac53f-3db1-5c54-bec1-68bd8fd70b86'}, {'abstract': 'The publication Southern Weekend appeared on newsstands, but the newspaper remains at the forefront of the dispute over government control.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/11/world/asia/as-protest-ends-chinese-censorship-battle-remains.html', 'snippet': 'The publication Southern Weekend appeared on newsstands, but the newspaper remains at the forefront of the dispute over government control.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GUANGZHOU, China — The demonstrations have died down, and the reporters and editors are back to work at China’s most prominent weekly newspaper. Its latest issue was published more or less on schedule. But the paper, Southern Weekend, is sure to remain a crucial battleground over Communist Party censorship.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chinese Newspaper Protests End, but Battle Over Censorship Is Unresolved', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chinese Newspaper Protests End, but Battle Over Censorship Is Unresolved', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Censorship', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Southern Weekend (Chinese Newspaper)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of the Press', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tuo Zhen', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-10T21:47:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong and Chris Buckley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/57ed927f-64cc-5dc6-b576-84ec082e3416', 'word_count': 1093, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57ed927f-64cc-5dc6-b576-84ec082e3416'}, {'abstract': 'New research suggests that prunelike wrinkles on fingers and toes may have evolved to give early humans an advantage in wet conditions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/15/science/wrinkled-fingers-get-better-grip-on-wet-objects.html', 'snippet': 'New research suggests that prunelike wrinkles on fingers and toes may have evolved to give early humans an advantage in wet conditions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The prunelike wrinkles that result from a long, hot bath may have an evolutionary purpose, researchers say. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/15/science/15OBWATER/15OBWATER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/15/science/15OBWATER/15OBWATER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Wet Wrinkled Fingers Evolved for Better Grip', 'kicker': 'Observatory', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wet Wrinkled Fingers Evolved for Better Grip', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Touch (Sense)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Biology Letters (Journal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTHROPOLOGY', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hands', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Feet', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biology and Biochemistry', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-10T21:50:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sindya N. Bhanoo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sindya', 'middlename': 'N.', 'lastname': 'Bhanoo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4087482f-a79c-51ba-9410-59cdb9383a9d', 'word_count': 238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4087482f-a79c-51ba-9410-59cdb9383a9d'}, {'abstract': 'Wednesday would have been his 100th birthday.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/10/richard-nixons-reputation/', 'snippet': 'Wednesday would have been his 100th birthday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yesterday, on the occasion of what would have been Richard Nixon’s 100th birthday, many journalists rehearsed an argument that goes something like this: To one generation of Americans (who grew up, as I did, in the 60s and 70s), Nixon was the personification of political evil. But his achievements, and his liberalism by the standards of today’s Republican Party, may ultimately prove more significant than his failings.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Richard Nixon’s Legacy', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nixon, Richard Milhous', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-10T21:53:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/64f71efb-44d5-5774-89d9-94a3d0893c27', 'word_count': 526, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64f71efb-44d5-5774-89d9-94a3d0893c27'}, {'abstract': 'Stuart Frank, a curator at the New Bedford Whaling Museum, has written a book detailing the scrimshaw carvings of sailors on 19th-century whale ships.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/11/arts/design/scrimshaw-in-new-book-from-new-bedford-whaling-museum.html', 'snippet': 'Stuart Frank, a curator at the New Bedford Whaling Museum, has written a book detailing the scrimshaw carvings of sailors on 19th-century whale ships.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sailors on 19th-century whale ships faced oppressive boredom, interrupted by occasional life-threatening storms and hunting expeditions. As a kind of distracting therapy, they carved whale teeth and bones into everything from dominoes to bird cages, pieces that are collectively known as scrimshaw.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '38', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/11/arts/ANTIQUES2/ANTIQUES2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 588, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/11/arts/ANTIQUES2/ANTIQUES2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1176, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/11/arts/ANTIQUES2/ANTIQUES2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/11/arts/ANTIQUES2/ANTIQUES2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/11/arts/ANTIQUES2/ANTIQUES2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Making Scrimshaw a Sea Companion', 'kicker': 'Antiques', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Making Scrimshaw A Sea Companion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTIQUES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-10T21:55:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_