logs.nytimes.com/2013/01/10/daulerio-is-leaving-as-gawker-editor/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Daulerio moved up from the sports site Deadspin to take over Gawker in November of 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': '5:49 p.m. | Updated Gawker Media is getting a change in leadership. A.J. Daulerio, who became the editor of Gawker just over a year ago, is leaving and will be replaced by the writer John Cook. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Daulerio Is Leaving as Gawker Editor', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Daulerio, A J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Denton, Nick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deadspin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gawker Media', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-10T22:27:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Haughney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haughney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc987a93-eb45-5536-b3b6-d55cce83dfd8', 'word_count': 406, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc987a93-eb45-5536-b3b6-d55cce83dfd8'}, {'abstract': 'Benjamín Ávila’s film is a semiautobiographical story about a 12-year-old being raised in the late 1970s in Argentina by activists opposed to the ruling military junta.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/11/movies/clandestine-childhood-directed-by-benjamin-avila.html', 'snippet': 'Benjamín Ávila’s film is a semiautobiographical story about a 12-year-old being raised in the late 1970s in Argentina by activists opposed to the ruling military junta.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In “Clandestine Childhood” a 12-year-old Argentine boy is forced into playing a dangerous game of pretend. It’s 1979, three years after a military coup d’état at home and exile in Cuba with his family. Now the boy, Juan (Teo Gutiérrez Moreno), who will go by Ernesto, is returning to Argentina with his parents, Charo (Natalia Oreiro) and Daniel (César Troncoso), and his baby sister, Victoria. “We think,” Charo tells Juan, “it’s the right time to carry on fighting.” In between changing diapers she and Daniel will soon be fighting Argentina’s right-wing military dictatorship in the name of freedom and country — and saluting fallen compañeros with rousing cries of “Perón or death!”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/11/arts/11CLANDESTINE_SPAN/11CLANDESTINE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/11/arts/11CLANDESTINE_SPAN/11CLANDESTINE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/11/arts/11CLANDESTINE_SPAN/CLANDESTINE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/11/arts/11CLANDESTINE_SPAN/CLANDESTINE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/11/arts/11CLANDESTINE_SPAN/11CLANDESTINE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/11/arts/11CLANDESTINE_SPAN/11CLANDESTINE_SPAN-thum