t of Wisdom,’ his show at Jack Shainman Gallery.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/11/arts/design/el-anatsui-pot-of-wisdom.html', 'snippet': 'El Anatsui expands his color palette while remaining true to his signature material in ‘Pot of Wisdom,’ his show at Jack Shainman Gallery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jack Shainman Gallery', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '37', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'El Anatsui: ‘Pot of Wisdom’', 'kicker': 'Art In Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'El Anatsui: ‘Pot of Wisdom’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Anatsui, El', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-10T22:40:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roberta Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roberta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/0568ff9d-f046-56de-bec3-1418dd07a883', 'word_count': 293, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0568ff9d-f046-56de-bec3-1418dd07a883'}, {'abstract': 'Two men plunged off a ski slope while strapped into a zorb, an inflatable ball, earlier this month. The accident has generated concern over unlicensed attractions on Russia’s ski slopes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/11/world/europe/zorbing-accident-kills-1-man-and-injures-another-in-russia.html', 'snippet': 'Two men plunged off a ski slope while strapped into a zorb, an inflatable ball, earlier this month. The accident has generated concern over unlicensed attractions on Russia’s ski slopes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — It is called a zorb, an outsize inflatable ball in which people strap themselves, then bounce down a ski slope and, presumably, have a good time doing so. But when a zorb veered off a ski run high in Russia’s Caucasus Mountains earlier this month, there was little anyone could do but watch as the two men inside careened along a jagged ridge and then plunged over a precipice.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Man in Plastic Ball Dies on Russian Ski Slope', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Man in Plastic Ball Dies on Russian Ski Slope', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roth, Andrew', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skiing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rescues', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-10T22:40:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Roth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/30b967c0-1d0f-573b-bf73-b21d67829172', 'word_count': 475, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30b967c0-1d0f-573b-bf73-b21d67829172'}, {'abstract': 'A selected guide to stand-up and improv performances  in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/11/arts/comedy-listings-for-jan-11-17.html', 'snippet': 'A selected guide to stand-up and improv performances  in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Comedy', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Comedy Listings for Jan. 11-17', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Listings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-10T22:40:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/9da78959-7ee9-5ab3-bc7b-f1bc9fd876d7', 'word_count': 498, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9da78959-7ee9-5ab3-bc7b-f1bc9fd876d7'}, {'abstract': 'In Tom O’Brien’s “Fairhaven,” three old friends from a Massachusetts fishing village are reunited for a funeral.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/11/movies/fairhaven-with-tom-obrien-chris-messina-sarah-paulson.html', 'snippet': 'In Tom O’Brien’s “Fairhaven,” three old friends from a Massachusetts fishing village are reunited for a funeral.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There isn’t a dishonest moment in “Fairhaven,” Tom O’Brien’s piercing, wistful portrait of three longtime buddies in their mid-30s who reunite around a funeral in a southeastern Massachusetts fishing community. It is the dead of winter, and Peter Simonite’s exquisite cinematography captures the bluish snow light with such acute sensitivity to atmosphere that even in the warmth of a theater you may shiver. A line of sea gulls hovers above a red-gold ribbon of a sunset on the horizon, signaling the distant promise of spring. But for now Fairhaven (a town of about 15,000 near New Bedford) is a place of hibernation.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/11/arts/11FAIRHAVEN1_SPAN/11FAIRHAVEN1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/11/arts/11FAIRHAVEN1_SPAN/11FAIRHAVEN1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 