: None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ec790a4-6e68-55aa-bd4f-135213156b93', 'word_count': 896, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ec790a4-6e68-55aa-bd4f-135213156b93'}, {'abstract': 'A 16-year-old boy with a shotgun at a Central California high school shot a fellow student on Thursday; he was taken into custody after staff members talked him into putting down the gun.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/11/us/california-teenager-held-in-shooting-at-high-school.html', 'snippet': 'A 16-year-old boy with a shotgun at a Central California high school shot a fellow student on Thursday; he was taken into custody after staff members talked him into putting down the gun.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A 16-year-old boy with a shotgun shot a fellow student on Thursday and was taken into custody after staff members talked him into putting down the gun, law enforcement officials said. The teenager walked into a classroom at Taft Union High School just before 9 a.m. and shot a male student in the chest, then fired at another student and missed, said Ray Pruitt, a spokesman for the Kern County Sheriff’s Office. A teacher who began to evacuate students through a rear door in the room and a campus supervisor persuaded the teenager to put down the gun. The victim was in critical condition in a hospital. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California: Teenager Held in Shooting at High School', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | West', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'California: Teenager Held In Shooting at High School', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'School Shootings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-11T01:01:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Lovett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lovett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/362df298-e91b-51e3-9031-24ea1f6031f6', 'word_count': 107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/362df298-e91b-51e3-9031-24ea1f6031f6'}, {'abstract': 'The Archdiocese of Boston told priests that they could make changes to church services to prevent the spread of flu, one day after Mayor Thomas M. Menino declared a public health emergency.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/11/us/massachusetts-archdiocese-is-guarding-against-flu.html', 'snippet': 'The Archdiocese of Boston told priests that they could make changes to church services to prevent the spread of flu, one day after Mayor Thomas M. Menino declared a public health emergency.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Archdiocese of Boston told priests on Thursday that they could suspend distributing communion wine from a shared chalice and suggested that they ask parishioners to bow instead of shaking hands to wish one another peace to curb the spread of flu. Auxiliary Bishop Robert P. Deeley also said communion ministers should sanitize their hands before and after giving communion and try not to touch parishioners’ hands or tongues when distributing communion. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Massachusetts: Archdiocese Is Guarding Against Flu', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | New England', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Massachusetts: Archdiocese Is Guarding Against Flu', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bidgood, Jess', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Influenza', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epidemics', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Menino, Thomas M', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Priests', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-11T01:03:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jess Bidgood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jess', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bidgood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/0bd1a9cf-3a76-58b4-8a01-2277de29c0d6', 'word_count': 72, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0bd1a9cf-3a76-58b4-8a01-2277de29c0d6'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Jerry Brown declared that “the deficit is gone,” and he projected that his state would post surpluses beginning next year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/11/us/california-balances-its-budget.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Jerry Brown declared that “the deficit is gone,” and he projected that his state would post surpluses beginning next year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SACRAMENTO — California has been Exhibit A for the fiscal upheaval that has rocked states throughout the recession. Year after year, California officials reported bigger and bigger deficits and sought to respond with spending cuts that left the state reeling.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/11/us/CALIFORNIA/CALIFORNIA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge',