 York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/10/blogs/curved-tv/curved-tv-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 663, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/10/blogs/curved-tv/curved-tv-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1326, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/10/blogs/curved-tv/curved-tv-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/10/blogs/curved-tv/curved-tv-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/10/blogs/curved-tv/curved-tv-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'C.E.S. 2013: What’s New in TVs', 'kicker': 'Pogue&#039;s Posts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television Sets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Samsung Group', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sony Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Las Vegas (Nev)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-11T01:20:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Pogue', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogue', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b57ce996-10c8-50a8-825f-7caab0a5bc70', 'word_count': 423, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b57ce996-10c8-50a8-825f-7caab0a5bc70'}, {'abstract': 'Defense Secretary Leon E. Panetta announced the money-saving steps, which are designed to be reversible should a compromise be reached on federal spending.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/11/us/pentagon-acts-to-limit-spending-in-case-cutbacks-begin-in-march.html', 'snippet': 'Defense Secretary Leon E. Panetta announced the money-saving steps, which are designed to be reversible should a compromise be reached on federal spending.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Fearing that Congress and the president may not reach a deal on spending and the deficit, the Pentagon’s leadership is freezing civilian hiring, limiting maintenance work and delaying approval of some contracts.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pentagon Acts to Limit Spending in Case Cutbacks Begin in March', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pentagon Acts to Limit Spending In Case Cutbacks Begin in March', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shanker, Thom', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Panetta, Leon E', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-11T01:24:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thom Shanker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shanker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8938602-60f0-536c-95de-3ee3cda16bec', 'word_count': 249, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8938602-60f0-536c-95de-3ee3cda16bec'}, {'abstract': 'Guantánamo Bay should stay open, at least for the short term, because the alternatives are worse.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/11/opinion/dont-close-guantanamo.html', 'snippet': 'Guantánamo Bay should stay open, at least for the short term, because the alternatives are worse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Don’t Close Guantánamo', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Don’t Close Guantánamo', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guantanamo Bay Naval Base (Cuba)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Daskal, Jennifer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-11T01:28:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Daskal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Daskal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/7471552e-d621-55f5-8b02-a2ff80daa683', 'word_count': 816, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7471552e-d621-55f5-8b02-a2ff80daa683'}, {'abstract': 'A weighty new book is an acknowledgement of the need for public policy to pay more attention to behavioral research. Just waiting on the politicians.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/11/opinion/brooks-beware-stubby-glasses.html', 'snippet': 'A weighty new book is an acknowledgement of the need for public policy to pay more attention to behavioral research. Just waiting on the politicians.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you want to deter crime, it seems that you’d want to lengthen prison sentences so that criminals would face steeper costs for breaking the law. In fact, a mountain of research shows that increases in prison terms have done nothing to deter crime. Criminals, like the rest of us, aren’t much influenced by things they might have to experience far in the future. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-thumbLarge-v2.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 's