1223e5ec6'}, {'abstract': 'The captain of the commuter vessel that slammed into a Manhattan dock said that he tried to make the boat go into reverse, but it did not respond as anticipated.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/11/nyregion/focus-is-on-crashed-ferrys-control-system.html', 'snippet': 'The captain of the commuter vessel that slammed into a Manhattan dock said that he tried to make the boat go into reverse, but it did not respond as anticipated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One day after a New Jersey commuter ferry slammed into a Lower Manhattan dock, injuring scores of passengers, the vessel’s captain trained investigators’ attention on problems with the control system, which he said did not respond as he tried to put the boat in reverse near shore.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Day After Crash, Focus Is on Ferry’s Control System', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Day After Crash of Ferry, Focus Moves to Control System', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maritime Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Transportation Safety Board', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transit Systems', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Seastreak LLC', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ferries', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-11T02:09:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Flegenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flegenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4d0511b-7c5b-535a-8149-96012c6646e7', 'word_count': 412, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4d0511b-7c5b-535a-8149-96012c6646e7'}, {'abstract': 'In a stunning rejection of the steroid era, no players were elected into the Baseball Hall of Fame.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/11/opinion/shutout-in-cooperstown.html', 'snippet': 'In a stunning rejection of the steroid era, no players were elected into the Baseball Hall of Fame.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Barry Bonds and Roger Clemens were not voted into the Baseball Hall of Fame on Wednesday. The rejection was hardly surprising but is still a stunning thing. Two of baseball’s all-time best — Bonds, the home-run king, and Clemens, the pitcher with the most Cy Young awards — were shunned by baseball writers in what Tyler Kepner of The Times called “the most resounding referendum yet on the legacy of steroids in baseball.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shutout in Cooperstown', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Shutout in Cooperstown', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Steroids', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baseball Hall of Fame', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clemens, Roger', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bonds, Barry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doping (Sports)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-11T02:18:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f58812c-e4ed-519d-a32a-fa0ce8757085', 'word_count': 351, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f58812c-e4ed-519d-a32a-fa0ce8757085'}, {'abstract': '“My Best Enemy,” a World War II drama, follows the closely linked fortunes of two childhood friends: the heir of a Jewish gallery owner and a newly minted Nazi.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/11/movies/my-best-enemy-directed-by-wolfgang-murnberger.html', 'snippet': '“My Best Enemy,” a World War II drama, follows the closely linked fortunes of two childhood friends: the heir of a Jewish gallery owner and a newly minted Nazi.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An awkward blend of anti-Semitic atrocities and identity-swapping absurdity, the World War II drama “My Best Enemy” struggles to find a convincing tone. Sidling around the violence with a plot that juggles class resentment, counterfeit art and a limp love triangle, the film wobbles between high-stakes adventure and high-tone caper.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/11/arts/11RDP_MYBEST_SPAN/11RDP_MYBEST_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/11/arts/11RDP_MYBEST_SPAN/11RDP_MYBEST_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/11/arts/11RDP_MYBEST_SPAN/11RDP_MYBEST_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 661, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/11/arts/11RDP_MYBEST_SPAN/11RDP_MYBEST_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 661, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'ima