’ Andray Blatche, his lawyer said, insisting he would not be charged.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/11/sports/basketball/nets-andray-blatche-focuses-on-job-as-police-investigate-sexual-assault-claim.html', 'snippet': 'A woman’s allegation of an assault at a Philadelphia hotel was not linked to the Nets’ Andray Blatche, his lawyer said, insisting he would not be charged.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST RUTHERFORD, N.J. — Two days after a woman said she was sexually assaulted in Nets forward Andray Blatche’s hotel suite in Philadelphia, Blatche said he was not worried about an investigation.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Blatche Focuses on Job as Inquiry Continues', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Blatche Focuses on Job As Inquiry Continues', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Nets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blatche, Andray', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assaults', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philadelphia (Pa)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-11T02:40:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zach Schonbrun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zach', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schonbrun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d82c9cb-9d22-5fbd-9e97-ada7d06ccb17', 'word_count': 525, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d82c9cb-9d22-5fbd-9e97-ada7d06ccb17'}, {'abstract': 'Abreham Zemedagegehu, who finds solace in his faith,  communicates with the help of an iPad, which was bought with Neediest Cases funds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/11/nyregion/technology-makes-life-a-little-easier-for-homeless-and-deaf-ethiopian-immigrant.html', 'snippet': 'Abreham Zemedagegehu, who finds solace in his faith,  communicates with the help of an iPad, which was bought with Neediest Cases funds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some of the problems Abreham Zemedagegehu faces as a homeless person in New York, like cold weather and lack of sleep, are fairly predictable. Some are less so: the police have gotten angry with Mr. Zemedagegehu because they did not realize that he could not hear their instructions. He was born with no hearing in one ear and only a little in the other.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/11/nyregion/NEEDIEST/NEEDIEST-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 388, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/11/nyregion/NEEDIEST/NEEDIEST-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 388}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/11/nyregion/NEEDIEST/NEEDIEST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/11/nyregion/NEEDIEST/NEEDIEST-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/11/nyregion/NEEDIEST/NEEDIEST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/11/nyregion/NEEDIEST/NEEDIEST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/11/nyregion/NEEDIEST/NEEDIEST-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For a Homeless Deaf Man, an iPad Makes Life Easier', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For a Homeless Deaf Man, An iPad Makes Life Easier', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times Neediest Cases Fund', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wheaton, Sarah', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deafness', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Housing and Urban Development Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homeless Persons', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-11T02:40:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Wheaton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wheaton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7567b863-32bd-5dd9-b3f1-0a26e772f337', 'word_count': 747, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7567b863-32bd-5dd9-b3f1-0a26e772f337'}, {'abstract': 'In a sudden escalation of longstanding tensions this week, each side has bitterly accused the other of violating the de facto border in Kashmir, which both sides claim in its entirety.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/11/world/asia/pakistan-a-new-clash-in-kashmir.html', 'snippet': 'In a sudden escalation of longstanding tensions this week, each side has bitterly accused the other of violating the de facto border in Kashmir, which both sides claim in its entirety.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Pakistani Army said Thursday that Indian troops had killed another Pakistani soldier in the latest round of clashes in Kashmir, the disputed Himalayan region. In a sudden escalation of longstanding tensions this week, each side has bitterly accused the other of violating the de facto border in Kashmir, which both sides claim in its entirety. In recent days, India said two of its soldiers had been killed by the Pakistanis, and Pakistan had earlier accused India of killing one of its soldiers. The clashes have occurred amid tentative steps by the two nations to improve relations. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pakistan: A New Clash in Kashmir', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pakistan: A New Clash in Kashmir', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kashmir and Jammu (India)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-11T02:41:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Salman Masood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Salman', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Masood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/e953ce85-23fb-599e-9a43-e264623a65c6', 'word_count': 97, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e953ce85-23fb-599e-9a43-e264623a65c6'}, {'abstract': 'Nearly 200 firefighters battled the five-alarm blaze that spread through a five-story apartment building in Manhattan’s NoLIta neighborhood Thursday night.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/11/nyregion/one-is-found-dead-and-2-others-are-injured-in-manhattan-fire.html', 'snippet': 'Nearly 200 firefighters battled the five-alarm blaze that spread through a five-story apartment building in Manhattan’s NoLIta neighborhood Thursday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After arguing with the mother of his child, a man set a fire in the second-floor hallway of his Manhattan apartment building on Thursday night, igniting a rapidly spreading, five-alarm blaze that killed one person and injured at least nine, the authorities said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/11/nyregion/FIRE/FIRE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 356, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/11/nyregion/FIRE/FIRE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 356}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/11/nyregion/FIRE/FIRE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 696, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/11/nyregion/FIRE/FIRE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1392, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/11/nyregion/FIRE/FIRE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/11/nyregion/FIRE/FIRE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/11/nyregion/FIRE/FIRE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Man Sets Fire, Killing One Person, Police Say', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Man Sets Fire in Building, Killing One, the Police Say', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fire Department (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'NoLIta (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARSON', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-11T02:52:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ravi Somaiya and Colin Moynihan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ravi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Somaiya', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Colin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moynihan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d61f8f66-13d1-50b2-a339-13916da7811a', 'word_count': 401, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d61f8f66-13d1-50b2-a339-13916da7811a'}, {'abstract': 'An order of Cistercian monks have rebuilt a 12th-century chapter house whose stones lay for decades after being brought from Europe by William Randolph Hearst in the 1930s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/11/us/monks-in-california-reconstruct-monastery-building-from-spain.html', 'snippet': 'An order of Cistercian monks have rebuilt a 12th-century chapter house whose stones lay for decades after being brought from Europe by William Randolph Hearst in the 1930s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VINA, Calif. — The rebirth of a medieval Cistercian monastery building here on a patch of rural Northern California land was, of course, improbable. William Randolph Hearst, the newspaper tycoon, brought the dismantled Santa Maria de Óvila monastery from Spain but failed to restore it. The City of San Francisco, after some fitful starts at bringing the monastery back to life, left its stones languishing for decades in Golden Gate Park. The Great Depression, World War II and lethargy got in the way.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/11/us/MONK-1/MONK-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/11/us/MONK-1/MONK-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/11/us/MONK-1/MONK-1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/11/us/MONK-1/MONK-1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/11/us/MONK-1/MONK-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/11/us/MONK-1/MONK-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2