': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/31918741-cbd8-55db-ab48-731d3705c60d', 'word_count': 755, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31918741-cbd8-55db-ab48-731d3705c60d'}, {'abstract': 'In denying the request for a preliminary injunction, Judge Naomi Reice Buchwald said the health risks of a religious ceremony involving oral contact with blood were clear.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/11/nyregion/parental-consent-rule-may-proceed-for-a-circumcision-ritual-a-judge-says.html', 'snippet': 'In denying the request for a preliminary injunction, Judge Naomi Reice Buchwald said the health risks of a religious ceremony involving oral contact with blood were clear.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York City health officials may proceed temporarily with a plan to require parental consent before an infant may undergo a particular Jewish circumcision ritual, a federal judge ruled Thursday. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Consent Rule May Proceed for a Circumcision Ritual', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Consent Rule May Proceed For a Circumcision Ritual', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Religion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Circumcision', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Herpes Viruses', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-11T04:24:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sharon Otterman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sharon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Otterman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f515a31c-8e91-558c-8fbb-46f9078ecbde', 'word_count': 292, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f515a31c-8e91-558c-8fbb-46f9078ecbde'}, {'abstract': 'This year’s Oscar nominees, led by Steven Spielberg’s “Lincoln,” are an indication that mainstream movies for grown-ups may not be on the way out.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/11/movies/awardsseason/lincoln-and-other-serious-films-top-oscar-nominee-list.html', 'snippet': 'This year’s Oscar nominees, led by Steven Spielberg’s “Lincoln,” are an indication that mainstream movies for grown-ups may not be on the way out.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the past few years, the Oscars have been haunted by the fear that the pictures, to paraphrase Norma Desmond, had gotten small. Or at least that the kind of pictures worthy of Academy Awards no longer operated at a scale demanded by a worldwide broadcast. The box office numbers of best picture nominees seemed to be shrinking as the movie business split in two. At one end was a specialized boutique outfit, at the other a franchise factory geared to the international mass market. Between those poles was a hole where the serious mainstream movies used to be.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/19/movies/lincoln8/lincoln8-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 377, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/12/19/movies/lincoln8/lincoln8-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 377}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/19/movies/lincoln8/lincoln8-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 643, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, '