ame': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2cb8af4-4bd3-562e-98cc-7335559ed8e1', 'word_count': 765, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2cb8af4-4bd3-562e-98cc-7335559ed8e1'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Connell’s diverse writing included two books, “Mrs. Bridge” and “Mr. Bridge,” that ended up being made into a film starring Paul Newman and Joanne Woodward.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/11/arts/evan-connell-88-novelist-in-multiple-genres.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Connell’s diverse writing included two books, “Mrs. Bridge” and “Mr. Bridge,” that ended up being made into a film starring Paul Newman and Joanne Woodward.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Evan S. Connell, a versatile writer praised for his spare portrayal of the frost and repression within a fictional upper-class Midwestern family as well as for his account of the very real and bloody battle that was Custer’s Last Stand, was found dead early Thursday in an assisted-living facility in Santa Fe, N.M. He was 88.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/11/arts/CONNELL-obit/CONNELL-obit-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/11/arts/CONNELL-obit/CONNELL-obit-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 480}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/11/arts/CONNELL-obit/CONNELL-obit-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 820, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/11/arts/CONNELL-obit/CONNELL-obit-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 13