w Guinea', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Snakes on a Plane (Movie)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-11T05:14:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gerry Mullany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gerry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mullany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8cac43cd-8ea1-5bca-a876-9835e82709eb', 'word_count': 157, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8cac43cd-8ea1-5bca-a876-9835e82709eb'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Howser roamed the highways of the Golden State as the host of “California’s Gold,” perhaps the most popular public television show in the state.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/11/arts/television/huell-howser-folksy-public-tv-host-is-dead-at-67.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Howser roamed the highways of the Golden State as the host of “California’s Gold,” perhaps the most popular public television show in the state.', 'lead_paragraph': 'He interviewed painters on the Golden Gate Bridge and sat atop the H of the Hollywood sign. He followed Julie Nixon Eisenhower up the stairs to her father’s tiny boyhood bedroom in Yorba Linda, Calif. He profiled an 88-year-old white woman who proudly remained in her South Central Los Angeles home after all her white neighbors fled to make way for black residents. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/11/obituaries/11howser/11howser-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/11/obituaries/11howser/11howser-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'typ