ts digital service, code-named Daisy; and Axe, the men’s grooming brand, is promoting a new line of products called Apollo by sending 22 consumers into space.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/11/the-breakfast-meeting-oscar-picks-music-by-beats-and-a-space-age-ad-promotion/', 'snippet': 'The 85th Academy Awards season got underway on Thursday with the annual Oscar nominations; Beats Electronics announced that Ian Rogers of Topspin Media would be the chief executive of its digital service, code-named Daisy; and Axe, the men’s groom...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 85th Academy Awards season got under way on Thursday as the heaviest number of Oscar nominations — including nods for best picture — went to “Lincoln,” about a president’s struggle with the Civil War; “Life of Pi,” about a shipwreck survivor and a tiger; “Silver Linings Playbook,” a comedy, of sorts, about a man with bipolar disorder; and “Les Misérables,” filled with songs of the oppressed. Close behind were “Argo,” about political captivity; “Amour,” a French-language film about aging and dying; and “Django Unchained,” a tale of slavery and retribution. “Beasts of the Southern Wild,” which chronicles a child’s encounters with rising floodwaters in the bayou, and “Zero Dark Thirty,” about the murky pursuit of a national enemy, also received best picture nominations. As Michael Cieply and Brooks Barnes report, the shocker was a triple snub in the best director category: Kathryn Bigelow (“Zero Dark Thirty”), Ben Affleck (“Argo”) and Quentin Tarantino (“Django Unchained”) were passed over despite widespread expectations that one or all of them would be nominated. Instead, the nominations went to Steven Spielberg (“Lincoln”), Ang Lee (“Life of Pi”), Michael Haneke (“Amour”), David O. Russell (“Silver Linings Playbook”) and Benh Zeitlin (“Beasts of the Southern Wild,” his first film). In all, nine films received best picture nominations in a field that can include as many as 10 or as few as 5, depending on how voters from the Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences spread their hand.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: Oscar Nods, Music by Beats, and a Space Age Ad Promotion', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'AFFLECK, BEN', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bigelow, Kathryn', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Haneke, Michael', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Ang', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reznor, Trent', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rogers, Ian', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Russell, David O', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spielberg, Steven', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tarantino, Quentin', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zeitlin, Benh', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ACADEMY OF MOTION PICTURE ARTS AND SCIENCES', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Beats Electronics', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mog', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nine Inch Nails', 'rank': 18, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rhapsody.com', 'rank': 19, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Spotify', 'rank': 20, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Unilever NV', 'rank': 21, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'XCOR Aerospace', 'rank': 22, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Curacao', 'rank': 23, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-11T13:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editors', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editors'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2e3d5d1-62da-5752-944d-c925b80abfff', 'word_count': 564, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2e3d5d1-62da-5752-944d-c925b80abfff'}, {'abstract': 'The retirement of the boss of one of Somalia’s biggest pirate gangs is the latest indication that the world’s navies may be winning the war against a scourge plaguing Indian Ocean waters.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/11/top-pirate-quits-as-tide-turns-against-somali-raiders/', 'snippet': 'The retirement of the boss of one of Somalia’s biggest pirate gangs is the latest indication that the world’s navies may be winning the war against a scourge plaguing Indian Ocean waters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — A notorious Somali sea raider known as Big Mouth is a pirate with a retirement plan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/11/blogs/11rdv-pirates/11rdv-pirates-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/11/blogs/11rdv-pirates/11rdv-pirates-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/11/blogs/11rdv-pirates/11rdv-pirates-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'imag