would retire in 2014 at the completion of his fifth term in the Senate.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/11/senator-rockefeller-is-said-to-be-retiring/', 'snippet': 'Senator John D. Rockefeller IV of West Virginia, the scion of the Rockefeller family who established himself as a liberal voice in Congress, said he would retire in 2014 at the completion of his fifth term in the Senate.', 'lead_paragraph': '11:22 p.m. | Updated  A revised version of this post is available here.Senator John D. Rockefeller IV of West Virginia, the scion of the Rockefeller family who established himself as a liberal voice in Congress, said on Friday that he would retire in 2014 at the completion of his fifth term in the Senate.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Senator Rockefeller Is Retiring After Five Terms', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-11T15:40:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Weisman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weisman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a82a873-9b9a-5e6b-bb4e-5e1e41671185', 'word_count': 439, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a82a873-9b9a-5e6b-bb4e-5e1e41671185'}, {'abstract': 'In this week’s installment, students can write argumentative pieces about a mining town in Peru; create poems in honor of the poet chosen for this year’s presidential inauguration; and summarize why many countries are concerned with Syria’s possible production of chemical weapons.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/11/common-core-practice-a-mining-village-in-peru-weapons-in-syria-and-inaugural-poetry/', 'snippet': 'In this week’s installment, students can write argumentative pieces about a mining town in Peru; create poems in honor of the poet chosen for this year’s presidential inauguration; and summarize why many countries are concerned with Syria’s possib...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Each Friday we collaborate with a classroom in New Jersey to test and publish three short writing ideas that address Common Core Standards and that are grounded in New York Times content. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Common Core Practice | A Mining Village in Peru, Weapons in Syria and Inaugural Poetry', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-11T15:45:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Olsen, Sarah Gross and Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Olsen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gross', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0fb2102a-1e41-52f7-94df-5b51c383fb83', 'word_count': 908, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0fb2102a-1e41-52f7-94df-5b51c383fb83'}, {'abstract': 'Playoff excitement is reaching a fever pitch, but it’s getting harder to fend off the sobering impact of stories about head trauma in football.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/11/leading-off-the-n-f-l-s-collision-course-with-itself/', 'snippet': 'Playoff excitement is reaching a fever pitch, but it’s getting harder to fend off the sobering impact of stories about head trauma in football.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The two sets of football stories keep rolling along, as if on different sets of train tracks, not yet crossing but getting closer, their impending collision bringing something no one can yet imagine.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Leading Off: The N.F.L.’s Collision Course, With Itself', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Seau, Junior', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-11T15:51:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6aeb94b6-0715-5356-ad33-686f99786f00', 'word_count': 704, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6aeb94b6-0715-5356-ad33-686f99786f00'}, {'abstract': 'Seth MacFarlane’s performance at the announcement of the Oscar nominations on Thursday morning raised questions about his coming turn as host of the awards ceremony.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/11/seth-macfarlane-already-under-fire-and-he-hasnt-even-hosted-yet/', 'snippet': 'Seth MacFarlane’s performance at the announcement of the Oscar nominations on Thursday morning raised questions about his coming turn as host of the awards ceremony.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Seth MacFarlane’s unusual foray into the Oscar nominations morning — it’s not common for a host to help with the announcement — left a lot of people worrying about his coming turn as host of the telecast. “Is Seth MacFarlane already a terrible Oscar host?” wondered Slate. ', 'source'