-person-who-said-once-upon-a-time.html', 'snippet': 'A good narrator, in books and in life, is the guide who makes sense of the story. So why have so many storytellers given up on narration?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good morning. My name is Steve Almond. I’ll be your narrator for today. I felt duty bound to introduce myself because the following essay is actually about narrators, and it begins with what we in the narrating business call a “triggering anecdote.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '44', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/magazine/13riff/mag-13Riff-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 90, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/13/magazine/13riff/mag-13Riff-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 90}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/magazine/13riff/mag-13Riff-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 154, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/magazine/13riff/mag-13Riff-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 309, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/magazine/13riff/13riff-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/13/magazine/13riff/13riff-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/magazine/13riff/13riff-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Once Upon a Time, There Was a Person Who Said, ‘Once Upon a Time’', 'kicker': 'Riff', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Once Upon a Time, There Was a Person Who Said, ‘Once Upon a Time’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Almond, Steve', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-11T16:21:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Almond', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Almond', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/890a3c24-8549-54dc-a841-16d0a0ae93a0', 'word_count': 1800, 'uri': 'nyt://article/890a3c24-8549-54dc-a841-16d0a0ae93a0'}, {'abstract': 'When party to a dark secret that may be false, all of your options are bad.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/13/magazine/is-a-rumor-enough-to-go-on.html', 'snippet': 'When party to a dark secret that may be false, all of your options are bad.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A few years ago, the daughter of a family friend had twins. Shortly afterward, one twin died. Recently I heard that the twins’ father, who is now estranged from the mother, accidentally smothered the baby with his body as he slept, almost certainly while intoxicated. I asked if the father had been charged, perhaps with negligence or something similar. I was told that the mother of the children lied to investigators to prevent the father from being charged. Of course, the accusation could be gossip; though I don’t think it is. What is the best thing to do in this situation? NAME WITHHELD', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/magazine/13ethicist/13ethicist-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 402, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/magazine/13ethicist/13ethicist-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 402, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/magazine/13ethicist/13ethicist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/13/magazine/13ethicist/13ethicist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/magazine/13ethicist/13ethicist-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Is a Rumor Enough to Go On?', 'kicker': 'The Ethicist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Secondhand Secret', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Personal)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klosterman, Chuck', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rumors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-11T16:21:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chuck Klosterman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chuck', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Klosterman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad635d90-1f9a-5f4e-acab-71066d384206', 'word_count': 539, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad635d90-1f9a-5f4e-acab-71066d384206'}, {'abstract': 'The comedian on his new sketch show, getting in touch with his emotions and the difference between him and Dave Chappelle.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/13/magazine/nick-kroll-takes-a-hike.html', 'snippet': 'The comedian on his new sketch show, getting in touch with his emotions and the difference between him and Dave Chappelle.', 'lead_paragraph': ' To talk to you, I had to track you down in Peru, where you were hiking in the mountains. Don’t take this the wrong way, but you don’t seem like the hiking type.  I thought I would pull a reverse Chappelle and leave the country before my show even came out. In high school I went to a place called the Mountain School. It’s on a farm in Vermont, and I read Emerson and Thoreau and ran around the woods. Now I go hiking with a bunch of my comedy buddies. We talk about our emotions. I also do a lot of writing on hikes, just to get the blood flowing and the ideas moving.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/magazine/13talk/13talk-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 390, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/magazine/13talk/13talk-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1303, 'width': 495, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/magazine/13talk/13talk-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 7