e.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The four stars of “Sex and the City” discuss their characters and the process of turning the hit television show into a movie.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Talking About ‘Sex’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'MOTION PICTURES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Sex and the City (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-11T16:31:27+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Movies', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/a067fc38-b912-559d-9529-7da0ac3c71ce', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/a067fc38-b912-559d-9529-7da0ac3c71ce'}, {'abstract': 'The Brady Campaign to Prevent Gun Violence wants the push to reduce gun violence to be broader than a possible ban of assault weapons.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/12/us/politics/gun-control-group-urges-expanded-background-checks.html', 'snippet': 'The Brady Campaign to Prevent Gun Violence wants the push to reduce gun violence to be broader than a possible ban of assault weapons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Brady Campaign to Prevent Gun Violence, one of the nation’s leading gun control groups, said on Friday that it wanted the White House to focus its attention on expanded background checks for gun buyers as part of a broad push to reduce gun violence in the wake of the school attack in Connecticut last month.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gun Control Group Urges Expanded Background Checks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organization