', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/business/james-stewart/james-stewart-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1333, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/business/james-stewart/james-stewart-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/25/business/james-stewart/james-stewart-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/business/james-stewart/james-stewart-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'They Got 2012 Right. What About 2013? ', 'kicker': 'Common Sense', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'They Got 2012 Right. What About 2013?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forecasts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-11T16:34:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By James B. Stewart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e787ae13-9f18-548b-ac4f-055a845d1559', 'word_count': 1546, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e787ae13-9f18-548b-ac4f-055a845d1559'}, {'abstract': 'As a combat medic in Afghanistan, Brandon Caro learned that keeping troops away from the enemy was as much a part of his role as keeping them away from contaminated water.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/11/when-preventive-medicine-involves-guns/', 'snippet': 'As a combat medic in Afghanistan, Brandon Caro learned that keeping troops away from the enemy was as much a part of his role as keeping them away from contaminated water.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Prevention is the surest form of medicine. This is a fact. It is with clean hands from strenuous, frequent washing and the habitual application of hand sanitizer that we are able to restrict the diffusion of bacterial and viral nasties, of parasitic organisms and interloping, malevolent fungi. With these simple measures, we are able to arrest potentially hazardous threats to our health and well-being before they have had the chance to infiltrate us. Prevention. Any doctor, nurse practitioner, lab coat or orderly will attest to this. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Preventive Medicine Involves Guns', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emergency Medical Treatment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Geneva Conventions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hygiene and Cleanliness', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Marine Corps Base Camp Lejeune (SC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-11T16:35:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brandon Caro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brandon', 'midd