 'word_count': 292, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99d18063-3435-57a2-a0ce-07e7a1f94e44'}, {'abstract': 'Big banks worked through more of their postcrisis hangovers and investors gathered more confidence in them, the author writes, but there’s little sign of a noticeably brighter future.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/01/11/uncertainty-hangs-over-wall-street-in-2013/', 'snippet': 'Big banks worked through more of their postcrisis hangovers and investors gathered more confidence in them, the author writes, but there’s little sign of a noticeably brighter future.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Big American banks have plenty to prove in 2013. Wells Fargo aside, their valuations have languished below book value. After a strong 2012 for stock markets and with fourth-quarter earnings reports imminent, JPMorgan and Goldman Sachs are again near that level. But when they get there, it will be a relief rather than anything to crow over.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Uncertainty Hangs Over Wall Street in 2013', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bank of America Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JPMorgan Chase & Company', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Morgan Stanley', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wells Fargo & Company', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-11T18:06:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Agnes T. Crane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Agnes', 'middlename': 'T.', 'lastname': 'Crane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb56340a-2ce1-5067-99db-b58a72fcda47', 'word_count': 405, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb56340a-2ce1-5067-99db-b58a72fcda47'}, {'abstract': 'The short but pitched battle between the Hatteras and the Alabama was unique, and had long-lasting military consequences.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/11/a-strange-sail/', 'snippet': 'The short but pitched battle between the Hatteras and the Alabama was unique, and had long-lasting military consequences.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the year 1862 ended, Union naval forces had consolidated effective control of much of the Texas Gulf Coast. From Sabine Pass in the North to the mouth of the Rio Grande, almost all of the roughly 450 miles of Texas coastline were safely in their hands. During that year, minor engagements at Corpus Christi, Galveston and Sabine Pass had effectively secured the coastline from most Confederate shipping. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Strange Sail', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Farragut, David Glasgow', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Navy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-11T18:10:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jed Morrison', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jed', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morrison', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d0a70f8-95b6-564d-b8ef-d328370526a3', 'word_count': 2033, 'uri': 'nyt