atement on Thursday the company said it had come up with the questions “in collaboration with” the philosopher Slavoj Zizek, and will ask the composers to write works responding to them. The questions are: “What preoccupies us today? How can we today stage ourselves? What are the collective myths of our present and future?” The operas are expected to be presented in 2020.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Opera Meets Philosophy', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Opera Meets Philosophy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ades, Thomas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cairns, Tom', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Haas, Georg Friedrich', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hwang, David Henry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saariaho, Kaija', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Turnage, Mark-Anthony', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weir, Judith', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zizek, Slavoj', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Finland', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-11T18:55:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/199979d1-8dd8-5372-939f-c61a64d597b9', 'word_count': 221, 'uri': 'nyt://article/199979d1-8dd8-5372-939f-c61a64d597b9'}, {'abstract': 'Bucks readers share tips on getting their wills, powers of attorney, accounts and other estate planning matters in order.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/11/getting-your-will-and-estate-plans-together/', 'snippet': 'Bucks readers share tips on getting their wills, powers of attorney, accounts and other estate planning matters in order.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this weekend’s Your Money column, I pay a visit to Chanel Reynolds, a widow who has built a site whose name cannot be mentioned here (though I can give you a link to it). It encourages you to get your will, living will and power of attorney done. And it urges you to collect all of your financial and other account information in one place and let a few trusted people know where to find it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Getting Your Will and Estate Plans Together', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Living Wills and Health Care Proxies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wills and Estates', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-11T18:56:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Lieber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lieber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ee6f0f1-eafa-53ac-a92c-3c26c53a825d', 'word_count': 261, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ee6f0f1-eafa-53ac-a92c-3c26c53a825d'}, {'abstract': 'A. O. Scott and David Carr talk about free speech and the gun issue — and when violence veers “too close to what is real.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.