g-started-assessing-the-value-of-a-home.html', 'snippet': 'A challenging task in New York City, where similar apartments a few blocks from one another can have varying values; the same can hold true for homes on different floors and with different views.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEFORE anyone can buy a house with a loan from a bank or refinance a mortgage, the lender needs an objective assessment of the property’s value — after all, the home is the bank’s collateral for the loan. Assessing the value is the job of the appraiser.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/realestate/13GETTINGSTARTED/geting-started-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 855, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/realestate/13GETTINGSTARTED/geting-started-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1710, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/realestate/13GETTINGSTARTED/13GETTINGSTARTED-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/13/realestate/13GETTINGSTARTED/13GETTINGSTARTED-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/realestate/13GETTINGSTARTED/13GETTINGSTARTED-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Understanding the Home Appraisal Process', 'kicker': 'Getting Started', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Understanding the Home Appraisal Pro