middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1d72d45-a9c3-5fcf-a962-f33c485c48b8', 'word_count': 344, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1d72d45-a9c3-5fcf-a962-f33c485c48b8'}, {'abstract': 'The Sundance Film Festival has created a growing family of directors whose movies weren’t accepted for a screening there.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/13/movies/a-talk-with-directors-rejected-by-sundance-festival.html', 'snippet': 'The Sundance Film Festival has created a growing family of directors whose movies weren’t accepted for a screening there.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE first-time feature-film director Stacy Sherman was on the edge of her seat in a Los Angeles movie theater, watching “Silver Linings Playbook,” when she received the e-mail she’d been waiting for. Ms. Sherman had been repeatedly checking her BlackBerry in those days leading up to Thanksgiving, and at last she scanned the words: “Sundance,” “\xa0‘Claire’s Cambodia’\xa0” (the name of her movie) and, finally, “we are sorry.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/arts/13SUNDANCE3/13SUNDANCE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/13/arts/13SUNDANCE3/13SUNDANCE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/arts/13SUNDANCE3/13SUNDANCE3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/arts/13SUNDANCE3/13SUNDANCE3-superJum