umentarians Audrey Ewell and Aaron Aites were watching live online as Occupy Wall Street started its ill-fated march over the Brooklyn Bridge. It was October 2011, and “there was this crazy drama unfolding,” Ms. Ewell said. “All of a sudden everybody is being arrested — and then the guy who was filming it said his batteries were running low, and the screen went black.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/arts/13OCCUPY1_SPAN/13OCCUPY1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/13/arts/13OCCUPY1_SPAN/13OCCUPY1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 390}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/arts/13OCCUPY1_SPAN/13OCCUPY1_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/arts/13OCCUPY1_SPAN/13OCCUPY1_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/arts/13OCCUPY1_SPAN/13OCCUPY1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/13/arts/13OCCUPY1_SPAN/13OCCUPY1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Messy Work of Examining Disorganizations', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Messy Work Of Examining Disorganizations', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 