': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mercedes-Benz', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-11T21:37:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Automobiles', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'subsection_name': 'New Cars', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ezra Dyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ezra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/6fb482e4-8b60-5fa0-8755-955d5666d70d', 'word_count': 1119, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6fb482e4-8b60-5fa0-8755-955d5666d70d'}, {'abstract': 'A list of films made by women in 2012.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/13/movies/listing-of-films-of-2012-by-female-directors.html', 'snippet': 'A list of films made by women in 2012.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Of the 250 top films at the box office last year, 9 percent were made by female filmmakers. Most were working on their own, a few had partners. Here are their films, in alphabetical order:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Listing of Films of 2012 by Female Directors', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-11T21:38:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/9906277b-8883-52ce-838e-f13c675031f6', 'word_count': 229, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9906277b-8883-52ce-838e-f13c675031f6'}, {'abstract': 'The XP-819 is a one-of-a-kind Corvette developed as a research vehicle by General Motors in the 1960s. The car is now being brought back to life at a restoration shop on Long Island.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/13/automobiles/collectibles/the-rear-engine-corvette-that-was-never-to-be.html', 'snippet': 'The XP-819 is a one-of-a-kind Corvette developed as a research vehicle by General Motors in the 1960s. The car is now being brought back to life at a restoration shop on Long Island.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ON Sunday evening, just ahead of two press preview days for the 2013 North American International Auto Show in Detroit, Chevrolet will unveil the seventh generation of the Corvette. While the two-seat sports car accounts for a small fraction of Chevy’s total sales, it is a vital element of the brand’s image — and, in fact, its longest-running passenger-car nameplate.', 'print_section': 'AU', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/automobiles/13VETT1/13VETT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 187, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/13/automobiles/13VETT1/13VETT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 187}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/automobiles/13VETT1/13VETT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 321, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/automobiles/13VETT1/13VETT1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 596, 'width': 1899, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/automobiles/13VETT1/13VETT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/13/automobiles/13VETT1/13VETT1-thumbSt