ions serving the elderly are struggling as nurses, home health aides and family members fall ill with the flu.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/11/as-flu-rages-caregiving-suffers/', 'snippet': 'Institutions serving the elderly are struggling as nurses, home health aides and family members fall ill with the flu.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The flu started in the personal care center at Masonic Village in Elizabethtown, Pa., then moved to the nursing home. Within a few days, seven older adults had taken ill. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Flu Rages, Caregiving Suffers', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Postings | Recent Entries From Our Blogs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elder Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Influenza', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nursing Homes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Centers for Disease Control and Prevention', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mayo Clinic', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Montefiore Medical Center', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mount Sinai Medical Center', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-11T23:02:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judith Graham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Graham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b227425-32eb-5d7c-976d-91d43b0af5ae', 'word_count': 1116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b227425-32eb-5d7c-976d-91d43b0af5ae'}, {'abstract': 'An Arizona resort attributes the initial yellowish cast to a rusty residue in its snow-making equipment, not the material’s wastewater origins.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/11/discolored-slopes-mar-debut-of-snow-making-effort/', 'snippet': 'An Arizona resort attributes the initial yellowish cast to a rusty residue in its snow-making equipment, not the material’s wastewater origins.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After a decade of legal battles, a ski resort in Northern Arizona recently became the first in the world to make artificial snow totally out of sewage effluent. On Dec. 24, Arizona Snowbowl fired up its snow guns for the first time, and to everyone’s surprise, the snow that blasted onto the mountain was yellow.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Discolored Slopes Mar Debut of Snow-Making Effort', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recycling of Waste Materials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skiing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snow and Snowstorms', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Center for Biological Diversity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-11T23:02:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Leslie Macmillan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Leslie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macmillan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/091bcccf-4ee8-58a1-b0e7-c5c1f2080802', 'word_count': 817, 'uri': 'nyt://article/091bcccf-4ee8-58a1-b0e7-c5c1f2080802'}, {'abstract': 'What’s happening to Democrats?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/11/is-that-a-backbone-i-see/', 'snippet': 'What’s happening to Democrats?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Senate Democrats give Obama full backing in any unilateral action he might take on the debt ceiling. Reports say that Harry Reid is still partial to the 14th amendment; but there’s also the coin and the coupons.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is That A Backbone I See?', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-11T23:04:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c7ce5e3-34bb-5fac-898e-9f1ad03e8c72', 'word_count': 172, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c7ce5e3-34bb-5fac-898e-9f1ad03e8c72'}, {'abstract': 'A guide to cultural and recreational events in the Hudson Valley.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/13/nyregion/events-in-westchester.html', 'snippet': 'A guide to cultural and recreational events in the Hudson Valley.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A guide to cultural and recreational events in the Hudson Valley. Items for the calendar should be sent at least three weeks in advance to westweek@nytimes.com.', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Events in Westchester', 'kicker': 'Calendar', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Westchester', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 2, 'maj