zfest, Bryan and the Aardvarks, led by the bassist Bryan Copeland, sounded ready for a bigger stage, or at least an indie film soundtrack.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bryan and the Aardvarks, led by the bassist Bryan Copeland, specializes in an unabashedly pretty strain of postbop, chamberlike and euphonious. At the Culture Project theater on Bleecker Street, early in the going at Winter Jazzfest on Friday night, they sounded ready for a bigger stage, or at least an indie film soundtrack.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Winter Jazzfest: Pretty Postbop From a Comfy Seat', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Winter Jazzfest', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Culture Project', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-12T01:17:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06673b1b-5d7e-5d48-9541-69c21eb4b2df', 'word_count': 247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06673b1b-5d7e-5d48-9541-69c21eb4b2df'}, {'abstract': 'Bistro Etcetera in Port Washington has a menu and décor as diverse as its name suggests.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/13/nyregion/a-review-of-bistro-etcetera-in-port-washington.html', 'snippet': 'Bistro Etcetera in Port Washington has a menu and décor as diverse as its name suggests.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Both the food and the décor at Bistro Etcetera, on Main Street in Port Washington, are as eclectic as the name suggests. There is nothing haphazard about the cooking, though: the chef and owner, Karen Melanie LaRocco, clearly knows what she is doing.', 'print_section'