983-94 Rangers cause in a suburban hotel for a few months? The answer is plenty.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/12/sports/hockey/when-rangers-roamed-the-hotel-halls.html', 'snippet': 'How much trouble could the 1983-94 Rangers cause in a suburban hotel for a few months? The answer is plenty.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Barry Beck’s tomato-red perm stopped me in my tracks as I rounded the corner on the second floor of the Ramada Inn in Armonk, N.Y. It was mid-September 1983, and I had been in the hotel’s employ for two weeks. It was only then that I noticed the squirming mummy being carried by Beck, the Rangers’ captain, and Nick Fotiu, the team’s resident brawler.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/12/sports/12rangers1/12rangers1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/12/sports/12rangers1/12rangers1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1135, 'width': 1135, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When Rangers Roamed the Halls', 'kicker': 'Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Rangers Roamed the Halls', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gervino, Tony', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Rangers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hotels and Travel Lodgings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Building Service Employees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-12T01:34:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tony Gervino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gervino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f2466fd5-ec80-5528-9025-97794da38984', 'word_count': 807, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f2466fd5-ec80-5528-9025-97794da38984'}, {'abstract': 'A minor Shakespearean character comes to the fore in Tim Crouch’s “I, Malvolio,” at the Duke on 42nd Street.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/12/theater/tim-crouch-on-i-malvolio-his-one-man-show-at-the-duke.html', 'snippet': 'A minor Shakespearean character comes to the fore in Tim Crouch’s “I, Malvolio,” at the Duke on 42nd Street.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even the most audacious actors rarely play a suicide attempt for laughs. But in his acclaimed one-man show “I, Malvolio,” the British performer Tim Crouch flings a noose over a ceiling pipe, slides a chair underneath and blames everyone for his lot in life — audience members included. So will they muster compassion for this character, a puritanical blowhard who has just spent 30 minutes attacking them for a variety of sins, or will they indulge baser instincts and mock him in kind?', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/12/theater/12crouch/12crouch-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/12/theater/12crouch/12crouch-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/12/theater/12crouch/12crouch-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'ca