g to open doorknobs with their elbows. “Epidemic spurs rush to hospitals,” announced The New York Post under a “Flu York” front-page headline. A financial Web site offered a list of undervalued stocks in the funeral service industry. The mayor of Boston declared a public health emergency. Google Flu Trends painted a map of the country in deep red and inspired a raft of terrifying predictions. (“Outbreak could be the worst on record.”)', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Flu. Who Knew?', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Flu. Who Knew?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Influenza', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Collins, Gail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epidemics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-12T01:39:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gail Collins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a20862c-0734-531b-a364-dcac90d565f5', 'word_count': 823, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a20862c-0734-531b-a364-dcac90d565f5'}, {'abstract': 'A rescue operation was under way in a rural part of western China after a landslide buried a village in Yunnan Province, killing at least 42 people and injuring two others.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/12/world/asia/china-landslide-buries-a-rural-village.html', 'snippet': 'A rescue operation was under way in a rural part of western China after a landslide buried a village in Yunnan Province, killing at least 42 people and injuring two others.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A rescue operation was under way in a rural part of western China after a landslide buried a village in Yunnan Province, killing at least 42 people and injuring two others, the authorities said Friday. Officials in Beijing ordered an “all-out rescue” effort to search for survivors after reports said that 19 children were among the missing, according to Xinhua, the official state news agency. The landslide, which took place in a mountainous region about 340 miles northeast of Kunming, the provincial capital, was said to have been set off by heavy rain and snow. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China: Landslide Buries a Rural Village', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: Landslide Buries a Rural Village', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Landslides and Mudslides', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barboza, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yunnan Province (China)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rescues', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-12T01:39:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Barboza', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barboza', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/43e4797b-9a43-5221-83ef-3d7a6d92e3b4', 'word_count': 95, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43e4797b-9a43-5221-83ef-3d7a6d92e3b4'}, {'abstract': 'An Academy member who declared he wouldn’t vote for “Zero Dark Thirty” for any Oscar drew a public response from a high-ranking Sony executive, a rare step in Hollywood.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/11/sony-defends-zero-dark-thirty-after-oscar-voter-speaks-out/', 'snippet': 'An Academy member who declared he wouldn’t vote for “Zero Dark Thirty” for any Oscar drew a public response from a high-ranking Sony executive, a rare step in Hollywood.', 'lead_paragraph': ' LOS ANGELES — It’s official: “Zero Dark Thirty” is now a political football not just in the United States Senate, where several senators have been challenging its portrayal of torture in the hunt for Osama bin Laden, but also within the voting ranks of the Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sony Defends ‘Zero Dark Thirty’ After Oscar Voter Speaks Out', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ACADEMY OF MOTION PICTURE ARTS AND SCIENCES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sony Pictures Entertainment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-12T01:40:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cieply', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cieply', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1238d08e-c3d2-5b85-9c2a-e79a37e13eb6', 'word_count': 394, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1238d08e-c3d2-5b85-9c2a-e79a37e13eb6'}, {'abstract': 'Traditional uses of the coca leaf in Bolivia will no longer be considered illegal under a United Nations antidrug convention, the organization said Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/12/world/americas/bolivia-morales-wins-victory-as-un-agrees-to-define-some-coca-use-as-legal.html', 'snippet': 'Traditional uses of the coca leaf in Bolivia will no longer be considered illegal under a United Nations antidrug convention, the organization said Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Traditional uses of the coca leaf in Bolivia will no longer be considered illegal under a United Nations antidrug convention, the organization said Friday. Coca is the plant used to make cocaine, but many people in Bolivia, which has a majority indigenous population, chew it as a mild stimulant, a use that has continued since pre-Colombian times. Bolivians also use the plant as a tea, in medicines and in religious or social rituals. The government of President Evo Morales withdrew from the international agreement a year ago as it sought an exception for traditional uses of the plant within its borders. The change was a diplomatic victory for Mr. Morales, above. To block the change, 62 United Nations members would have had to object; only 15 did, including the United States. Bolivia will now rejoin the convention, which could help it receive aid in fighting drug trafficking. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/12/world/briefs-morales/briefs-morales-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 918, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/12/world/briefs-morales/briefs-morales-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 918}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/12/world/briefs-morales/briefs-morales-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 670, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/12/world/briefs-morales/briefs-morales-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1175, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/12/world/briefs-morales/briefs-morales-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/12/world/briefs-morales/briefs-morales-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/12/world/briefs-morales/briefs-morales-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bolivia: Morales Wins Victory as U.N. Agrees to Define Some Coca Use as Legal', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bolivia: Morales Wins Victory as U.N. Agrees to Define Some Coca Use as Legal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coca (Plant)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morales, Evo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bolivia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-12T01:42:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Neuman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Neuman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c670b31-f7bb-59a5-8e08-a94bc1c44380', 'word_count': 147, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c670b31-f7bb-59a5-8e08-a94bc1c44380'}, {'abstract': 'State investigators on Friday accused the former defense minister, Anatoly E. Serdyukov, of obstructing a corruption investigation into real estate dealings by the Defense Ministry.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/12/world/europe/russia-ex-defense-chief-faces-accusers.html', 'snippet': 'State investigators on Friday accused the former defense minister, Anatoly E. Serdyukov, of obstructing a corruption investigation into real estate dealings by the Defense Ministry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'State investigators on Friday accused the former defense minister, Anatoly E. Serdyukov, of obstructing a corruption investigation into real estate dealings by the Defense Ministry, and suggested that he might soon face criminal charges. Mr. Serdyukov, who was dismissed by President Vladimir V. Putin in November, invoked his constitutional right not to incriminate himself during an interrogation, a spokesman for the state Investigative Committee said. Several of his former aides have already been charged in the case. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia: Ex-Defense Chief Faces Accusers', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia: Ex-Defense Chief Faces Accusers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roth, Andrew', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Investigative Committee', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Serdyukov, Anatoly E', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-12T01:44:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Roth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/245c4a72-44c2-5ea1-bc7c-d64af5570bb7', 'word_count': 77, 'uri': 'nyt://article/245c4a72-44c2-5ea1-bc7c-d64af5570bb7'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama nominated Jacob J. Lew to be the Treasury se