pigeons from the air — but also invited Wayne LaPierre, chief executive officer of the National Rifle Association, as his guest for the opening of a new shooting range in Searchlight, Nev. Mr. Reid, a former policeman, eagerly displayed his sportsman’s enthusiasm to the voters. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Senator Reid Takes Fresh Aim', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Senator Reid Takes Fresh Aim', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reid, Harry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newtown, Conn, Shooting (2012)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Rifle Assn', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'LaPierre, Wayne', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-12T01:46:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/1aa4158f-af44-5ba7-941d-7856819b482c', 'word_count': 420, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1aa4158f-af44-5ba7-941d-7856819b482c'}, {'abstract': 'After four fatalities at Aqueduct’s meet, which opened Dec. 12, the New York State Racing and Wagering Board said necropsies would be performed on all horses that sustain deadly racing injuries.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/12/sports/aqueduct-breakdowns-lead-to-order-for-necropsies.html', 'snippet': 'After four fatalities at Aqueduct’s meet, which opened Dec. 12, the New York State Racing and Wagering Board said necropsies would be performed on all horses that sustain deadly racing injuries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York State Racing and Wagering Board announced Friday that it would order necropsies for all horses that sustain deadly racing injuries on Aqueduct’s inner dirt track after four fatalities at the racetrack’s meet, which opened Dec. 12.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Horse Deaths at Aqueduct Stir Action by State Board', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Horse Deaths at Aqueduct Stir Action by State Board', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York State Racing and Wagering Board', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Aqueduct Racetrack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Racing Assn', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horses', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doping (Sports)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-12T01:47:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Drape', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Drape', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c60fee4-d40d-5c9a-8113-256fe2aeaffd', 'word_count': 500, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c60fee4-d40d-5c9a-8113-256fe2aeaffd'}, {'abstract': 'The top United Nations nuclear monitoring official expressed renewed pessimism on Friday about negotiations with Iran, set for next week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/12/world/middleeast/little-hope-seen-for-iran-nuclear-talks.html', 'snippet': 'The top United Nations nuclear monitoring official expressed renewed pessimism on Friday about negotiations with Iran, set for next week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The top United Nations nuclear monitoring official expressed renewed pessimism on Friday about negotiations with Iran, set for next week. The talks are aimed at gaining access to a restricted military area, which his inspectors suspect may have been used for atomic bomb-trigger testing work. The official, Yukiya Amano, director general of the International Atomic Energy Agency, said that “the outlook is not bright” for obtaining permission from Iran to visit the site, Parchin, which is about 20 miles south of Tehran. Mr. Amano’s remarks contrasted with a more optimistic tone from the agency less than a month ago, when his deputy, Herman Nackaerts, expressed hope that the negotiations this Wednesday would lead to final agreement on an inspection plan. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Little Hope Seen for Iran Nuclear Talks', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | United Nations', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Little Hope Seen for Iran Nuclear Talks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Atomic Energy Agency', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Amano, Yukiya', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-12T01:48:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 