ippet': 'A movie-spawned fascination with Lugers bumps up against the reality of today’s assault weapons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I know what it feels like to be a gun lover.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Back When I Was Packing', 'kicker': 'Dick Cavett', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Belcher, Jovan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Costas, Bob', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Imus, Don', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Rifle Assn', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-12T02:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dick Cavett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cavett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/996ad789-0cfc-550e-bb00-f6c32443d0e6', 'word_count': 1069, 'uri': 'nyt://article/996ad789-0cfc-550e-bb00-f6c32443d0e6'}, {'abstract': 'At last, the first vivid display of the giant squid’s living beauty.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/12/opinion/squidolatry.html', 'snippet': 'At last, the first vivid display of the giant squid’s living beauty.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two points about the giant squid, Architeuthis dux, recently caught on video by Japanese scientists and now writhing all over the Internet. It is not a colossal squid, Mesonychoteuthis hamiltoni, which is even larger. And this is not the first deep-water image of a giant squid. In 2004, Japanese scientists photographed one taking their bait nearly 3,000 feet underwater in roughly the same location, some 600 miles south of Japan. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Squidolatry', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Squidolatry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Squid', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-12T02:01:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e14721c-e52e-5cfd-8dfd-38bbba43e616', 'word_count': 296, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e14721c-e52e-5cfd-8dfd-38bbba43e616'}, {'abstract': 'In 1964 General Motors engineers built an experimental Corvette called the XP-819. Now it is being restored by a team of automotive craftsmen in Valley Stream, N.Y.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/automobiles/100000002000122/the-corvette-xp-819.html', 'snippet': 'In 1964 General Motors engineers built an experimental Corvette called the XP-819. Now it is being restored by a team of automotive craftsmen in Valley Stream, N.Y.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1964 General Motors engineers built an experimental Corvette called the XP-819. Now it is being restored by a team of automotive craftsmen in Valley Stream, N.Y.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/12/automobiles/video-corvette/video-corvette-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/12/automobiles/video-corvette/video-corvette-articleLarge