rst season tickets in 1946.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/12/sports/hockey/12hershey3-img/12hershey3-img-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/12/sports/hockey/12hershey3-img/12hershey3-img-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/12/sports/hockey/12hershey3-img/12hershey3-img-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 729, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/12/sports/hockey/12hershey3-img/12hershey3-img-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1457, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Hershey, an Original A.H.L. Team Plays On Uninterrupted', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Hershey, an Original A.H.L. Team Plays On Uninterrupted', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hershey Bears', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN HOCKEY LEAGUE', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-12T02:58:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Caldwell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caldwell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c735b04e-76e1-5b3b-acd9-a043e3930d62', 'word_count': 1007, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c735b04e-76e1-5b3b-acd9-a043e3930d62'}, {'abstract': 'The trombonist Jacob Garchik and his Atheist Trombone Gospel Choir brought his themes vividly to life at Bowery Electric.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/11/winter-jazzfest-nine-man-band-fleshes-out-a-one-man-show/', 'snippet': 'The trombonist Jacob Garchik and his Atheist Trombone Gospel Choir brought his themes vividly to life at Bowery Electric.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The trombonist and composer-arranger Jacob Garchik released one of the odder (and better) jazz recordings of last year: “The Heavens: The Atheist Gospel Trombone Album.” The ethical/religious connotations of the album are probably best left to another forum; what’s germane here is the fact that the Heavens, on record, is a one-man show, a product of shrewd overdubbing and self-sufficient conviction.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Winter Jazzfest: Nine-Man Band Fleshes Out a One-Man Show', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Winter Jazzfest', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garchik, Jacob', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-12T03:00:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f6f3549-6150-51cb-bb5f-6c0aa8769e91', 'word_count': 279, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f6f3549-6150-51cb-bb5f-6c0aa8769e91'}, {'abstract': 'Friendly beatings from Doug Peterson and Brad Wilber.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/11/in-the-wrong-business/', 'snippet': 'Friendly beatings from Doug Peterson and Brad Wilber.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SATURDAY’S PUZZLE — Doug Peterson and Brad Wilber are two of the nicest people I know in the field of crossword puzzle construction. Lovely men they both are, with an air of gentility about them, and decent table manners for the most part. So I don’t understand why they insist on beating me silly with their crosswords.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In the Wrong Business', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-12T03:00:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2488b979-51bb-5bde-bdc4-ea752c82d8e0', 'word_count': 326, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2488b979-51bb-5bde-bdc4-ea752c82d8e0'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on January 12, 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/12/pageoneplus/corrections-january-12-2013.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on January 12, 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': 'INTERNATIONAL', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: January 12, 2013', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-12T03:00:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/4bb6cfe6-59c0-502b-a076-8ec6d46cba0b', 'word_count': 490, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4bb6cfe6-59c0-502b-a076-8ec6d46cba0b'}, {'abstract': 'Gilberto Valle’s lawyer complained to a judge that moving her client to a Brooklyn detention center and exposing him to other prisoners would put him in danger.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/12/nyregion/gilberto-valle-officer-held-in-kidnapping-plot-balks-at-jail-transfer.html', 'snippet': 'Gilberto Valle’s lawyer complained to a judge that moving her client to a Brooklyn detention center and exposing him to other prisoners would put him in danger.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gilberto Valle, the New York police officer charged with plotting to kidnap, kill and eat women, had been held in a special unit of the Metropolitan Correctional Center in Manhattan, separated from other prisoners, apparently for his own protection.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Officer Held in Plot to Kidnap Women Balks at Jail Transfer', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Police Officer Detained in a Scheme To Kidnap Women Balks at a Transfer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Valle, Gilberto', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cannibalism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kidnapping', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Prisons', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Correctional Center (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-12T03:06:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Weiser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weiser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2b98c47-e3b8-5fa1-93ba-64b77b644ea4', 'word_count': 386, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2b98c47-e3b8-5fa1-93ba-64b77b644ea4'}, {'abstract': '“Once Removed: Sculpture’s Changing Frame of Reference” relies slavishly on the collectible and the concept of the collection, rather than exploring the deviating path of contemporary sculpture.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/13/nyregion/a-review-of-once-removed-sculptures-changing-frame-of-reference-at-yale-university-art-gallery.html', 'snippet': '“Once Removed: Sculpture’s Changing Frame of Reference” relies slavishly on the collectible and the concept of the collection, rather than exploring the deviating path of contemporary sculpture.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A hundred years after Pablo Picasso shaped a guitar from cardboard, and nearly a century since Marcel Duchamp signed a urinal and called it art, it’s easy to forget that these were huge transgressions against the lineage of Western sculpture. Previously, sculpture consisted of objects in stone, bronze or wood. But as “Once Removed: Sculpture’s Changing Frame of Reference” at the Yale University Art Gallery shows, sculpture can be made of anything now, from feathers and video to Vaseline.', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/nyregion/13ARTSCT1_SPAN/13ARTSCT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/13/nyregion/13ARTSCT1_SPAN/13ARTSCT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subty