anthropy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Community Services', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bedford-Stuyvesant (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-12T04:46:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Otis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Otis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca82656e-bd69-533e-9840-b2b29b3b0d4a', 'word_count': 686, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca82656e-bd69-533e-9840-b2b29b3b0d4a'}, {'abstract': 'A new generation concerned with ethical cleanliness, environmental sensitivity and expensive, curated victuals is spending much more to eat than it probably should.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/13/nyregion/new-generation-confronts-unaffordable-luxury-of-food.html', 'snippet': 'A new generation concerned with ethical cleanliness, environmental sensitivity and expensive, curated victuals is spending much more to eat than it probably should.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sometime around 1990 and not too long out of college, I held what memory tells me was my first true dinner party, in a three-bedroom brownstone duplex in Brooklyn, where the rent was approximately $1,200 a month. The menu revolved around a pork loin stuffed with sausage and dried apricots, a recipe that came from “The New Basics,” which along with “The Silver Palate Cookbook,” its predecessor, and the various musings of Laurie E. Colwin would have made up the near entirety of any young aspiring cook’s kitchen library. That evening, we were paying tribute to a friend who had recently begun working as a writer for David Letterman, and in that spirit my roommate and I purchased several bottles of Kendall-Jackson chardonnay for $11 each, feeling very grand about it.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/nyregion/13BIGCITY_SPAN/13BIGCITY_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/13/nyregion/13BIGCITY_SPAN/13BIGCITY_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/nyregion/13BIGCITY_SPAN/13BIGCITY_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/nyregion/13BIGCITY_SPAN/13BIGCITY_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/nyregion/13BIGCITY_SPAN/13BIGCITY_SPAN-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/13/nyregion/13BIGCITY_SPAN/13BIGCITY_SPAN-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/nyregion/13BIGCITY_SPAN/13BIGCITY_SPAN-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Unaffordable Luxury of Food', 'kicker': 'Big City', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Unaffordable Luxury of Food', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Youth', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-12T04:49:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ginia Bellafante', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ginia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bellafante', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c67d5329-fd38-5809-8274-147e9fe3a900', 'word_count': 910, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c67d5329-fd38-5809-8274-147e9fe3a900'}, {'abstract': 'The Bulls ran pick-and-roll plays to perfection, displayed terrific ball movement and harassed Carmelo Anthony to hand the Knicks their third straight loss.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/12/sports/basketball/knicks-fall-to-the-bulls.html', 'snippet': 'The Bulls ran pick-and-roll plays to perfection, displayed terrific ball movement and harassed Carmelo Anthony to hand the Knicks their third straight loss.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Chicago Bulls did not need to bully the Knicks. They did not need to slow the game down, either. In the third meeting of the season between the teams, the Bulls were dominant.\xa0', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/12/sports/basketball/12knicks-anthony-img/12knicks-anthony-img-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 822, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/12/sports/basketball/12knicks-anthony-img/12knicks-anthony-img-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1643, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype