icle', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b037abd-8864-5487-bd69-36d7006b49c9', 'word_count': 320, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b037abd-8864-5487-bd69-36d7006b49c9'}, {'abstract': 'Some unfinished sagas are idling as the car-racing winter off-season reaches its midpoint.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/12/as-formula-one-hibernates-some-puzzlers-to-ponder/', 'snippet': 'Some unfinished sagas are idling as the car-racing winter off-season reaches its midpoint.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS— It’s the winter season, when nothing happens in Formula One. The last race of 2012 was on Nov. 25, in Brazil, and the first race of the 2013 season will take place on March 17, in Australia. But the presentation of the new cars starts later this month. Winter testing starts on Feb. 5 in Spain. And actually, a lot has been happening, some of it puzzling, or open to interpretation. I’d like to take a break from the break and make short list of the principal such head-scratchers, and ask readers what they make of it all. In most cases, I am not quite sure what I make of it, but have some ideas, too.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/10/blogs/Ferrari10/Ferrari10-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 512, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/10/blogs/Ferrari10/Ferrari10-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 512, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/10/blogs/Ferrari10/Ferrari10-thumbStandard.jpg',