t: “THE MUSIC OF CHANCE,” by PAUL AUSTER, a novel about the supposed meaninglessness of the universe. Published in 1990, it has since become a film starring Mandy Patinkin and James Spader, but Mr. Auster’s writing is so charming, you’ll want to read the book. Here is the New York Times review of the novel.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Variety: An Acrostic With Personality', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Acrostic Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-12T17:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f406e939-01fe-5e45-bec5-42932a5d6ed4', 'word_count': 224, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f406e939-01fe-5e45-bec5-42932a5d6ed4'}, {'abstract': 'French airstrikes overnight in Mali pushed back Islamist rebels from a key village and destroyed a rebel command center, France said, as West African nations promised a fast deployment of troops to Mali.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/13/world/africa/french-airstrikes-push-back-islamist-rebels-in-mali.html', 'snippet': 'French airstrikes overnight in Mali pushed back Islamist rebels from a key village and destroyed a rebel command center, France said, as West African nations promised a fast deployment of troops to Mali.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — French airstrikes in Mali appeared to halt an Islamist rebel advance, France said Saturday, as West African nations authorized what they said would be a fast deployment of troops in support of the weak Ma