', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Supreme Court this week will consider whether to reverse a troubling 2002 decision that allowed judges greater sentencing power in certain circumstances. For the sake of fairness and consistency, it should overturn that 10-year-old ruling. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Restoring Due Process', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Restoring Due Process', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alleyne, Allen Ryan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sixth Amendment (US Constitution)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitution (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jury System', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mandatory Sentencing', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-12T18:30:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/b51c11c9-22c9-5b70-b61d-2cd439564b1c', 'word_count': 416, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b51c11c9-22c9-5b70-b61d-2cd439564b1c'}, {'abstract': 'The administration mistakenly buys into a Republican plan to cut cost-of-living increases.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/13/opinion/sunday/misguided-social-security-reform.html', 'snippet': 'The administration mistakenly buys into a Republican plan to cut cost-of-living increases.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the end of last year, just shy of the 11th hour in the fiscal cliff negotiations, President Obama made an offer that included a Republican-backed idea to cut spending by lowering the cost-of-living adjustment for Social Security benefits. The move shocked Congressional Democrats and dismayed Mr. Obama’s liberal base. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Misguided Social Security ‘Reform’', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Misguided Social Security ‘Reform’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Security (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inflation (Economics)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Price Index', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-12T18:31:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/2cfaaf8a-7edc-5b24-98d1-e7f5c44f5b93', 'word_count': 792, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2cfaaf8a-7edc-5b24-98d1-e7f5c44f5b93'}, {'abstract': 'Between Harry Reid’s inflations and President Obama’s nominations, Democrats are playing a game of arrogance and needless errors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/13/opinion/sunday/bruni-democrats-behaving-badly.html', 'snippet': 'Between Harry Reid’s inflations and President Obama’s nominations, Democrats are playing a game of arrogance and needless errors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOR the textbook definition of not knowing enough to quit while you’re ahead, please turn your attention to Harry Reid, he of the scabrous tongue and rotten temper, a boxer in his youth and a pu