artial-menswear/', 'snippet': 'The changing demands of war — or the military, anyway — have generated almost all the major evolution in menswear.', 'lead_paragraph': '“War, huh, yeah, what is it good for?” asked the lyrics to a 1970s hit by Edwin Starr. The answer: “Absolutely nothing, uh huh!” That’s not entirely true, though. The changing demands of war — or the military, anyway — have generated almost all the major evolution in menswear, particularly when it comes to the longest and most successful of male uniforms, the suit.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Burberry’s Martial Menswear', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Milan Fashion Week', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bailey, Christopher', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Burberry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-12T18:54:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Guy Trebay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Guy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Trebay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3a1e18b-b4a1-5a6e-a2bb-4dc9c284f746', 'word_count': 189, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3a1e18b-b4a1-5a6e-a2bb-4dc9c284f746'}, {'abstract': 'Television shows provide a kind of through-line that’s missing from most of our lives.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/13/opinion/sunday/tv-the-thinking-persons-entertainment-of-choice.html', 'snippet': 'Television shows provide a kind of through-line that’s missing from most of our lives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SOME of television’s most compelling shows start up again this month — and thank heaven for that. “Downton Abbey,” “The Good Wife” and “Girls” will happily draw viewers — like me — back into their characters and their plot-heavy story lines. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/sunday-review/13QUART/13QUART-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 425, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/13/sunday-review/13QUART/13QUART-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 425}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/sunday-review/13QUART/13QUART-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 726, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/sunday-review/13QUART/13QUART-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1451, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/sunday-review/13QUART/13QUART-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/13/sunday-review/13QUART/13QUART-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/sunday-review/13QUART/13QUART-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Thinking Person’s Entertainment', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Thinking Person’s Entertainment', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 