ank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4ce464c-21ae-528b-8a0f-1e1347ef46ca', 'word_count': 984, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4ce464c-21ae-528b-8a0f-1e1347ef46ca'}, {'abstract': 'Friends, colleagues and admirers of Aaron Swartz, a digital activist and innovator, posted tributes to him online on Saturday, following reports of his death.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/12/tributes-to-a-digital-pioneer-follow-reports-of-his-death/', 'snippet': 'Friends, colleagues and admirers of Aaron Swartz, a digital activist and innovator, posted tributes to him online on Saturday, following reports of his death.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last Updated, 9:02 p.m. Friends, colleagues and admirers of Aaron Swartz, a digital activist and innovator, posted tributes to him online on Saturday, after an early-morning report of his death by The Tech, the Massachusetts Institute of Technology student newspaper. An uncle, Michael Wolf, told The Times that Mr. Swartz, 26, had apparently committed suicide in New York on Friday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Remembering Aaron Swartz', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Copyrights and Copyright Violations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Swartz, Aaron', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Creative Commons', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Demand Progress', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jstor', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Massachusetts Institute of Technology', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-12T18:59:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Schwartz and Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwartz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8684a3d-358f-59d4-a786-366a22344ec0', 'word_count': 1198, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8684a3d-358f-59d4-a786-366a22344ec0'}, {'abstract': 'A success at every level, the Lakers’ Kobe Bryant has had little experience with struggling on the basketball court.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/12/bryant-now-deals-with-mediocrity/', 'snippet': 'A success at every level, the Lakers’ Kobe Bryant has had little experience with struggling on the basketball court.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Albert Camus once wrote, “There is scarcely any passion without struggle.” Anyone who has watched Kobe Bryant play basketball might beg to differ.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bryant Now Deals With Mediocrity', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bryant Now Deals With Mediocrity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bryant, Kobe', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Lakers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-12T19:07:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Hoffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/166e646d-39e9-5bd2-b67b-292864bc02a9', 'word_count': 812, 'uri': 'nyt://article/166e646d-39e9-5bd2-b67b-292864bc02a9'}, {'abstract': 'In Los Angeles, storefront doctors’ offices are servicing mostly uninsured Latinos, leaving officials to examine the clinics’ place in the nation’s health system.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/13/health/bodega-clinicas-draw-interest-of-health-officials.html', 'snippet': 'In Los Angeles, storefront doctors’ offices are servicing mostly uninsured Latinos, leaving officials to examine the clinics’ place in the nation’s health system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HUNTINGTON PARK, Calif. — The “bodega clinicas” that line the bustling commercial streets of immigrant neighborhoods around Los Angeles are wedged between money order kiosks and pawnshops. These storefront offices, staffed with Spanish-speaking medical providers, treat ailments for cash: a doctor’s visit is $20 to $40; a cardiology exam is $120; and at one bustling clinic, a colonoscopy is advertised on an erasable board for $700.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/us/CLINICAS-2/CLINICAS-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/13/us/CLINICAS-2/CLINICAS-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/us/CLINICAS-2/CLINICAS-2-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 666, 'width': 999, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/us/CLINICAS-2/CLINICAS-2-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 666, 'width': 999, 'subType': 'superJum