ings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-12T19:41:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Helaine Olen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Helaine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Olen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/e14cd914-e421-501c-83cd-42801b31f7fb', 'word_count': 550, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e14cd914-e421-501c-83cd-42801b31f7fb'}, {'abstract': 'Zero bound economics in action.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/12/japans-teachable-moment/', 'snippet': 'Zero bound economics in action.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Whatever else you can say about the new turn in Japanese policy, it’s offering a great demonstration of the peculiarities of zero-lower-bound economics. (JGBs meet the ZLB, OK!)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Japan’s Teachable Moment', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-12T19:44:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68f38929-510c-540e-a6de-b1ce079888ea', 'word_count': 235, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68f38929-510c-540e-a6de-b1ce079888ea'}, {'abstract': 'Precious Perry, 23, survived a difficult upbringing to become a kind of surrogate mother to her two siblings. She expects to graduate with a bachelor’s degree in May.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/13/nyregion/after-foster-care-becoming-a-role-model-for-her-sisters.html'