8-3166-5940-b359-4a35f92d2043', 'word_count': 1144, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b44750e8-3166-5940-b359-4a35f92d2043'}, {'abstract': 'I’ve been trying to lie about this story for years.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/12/writing-about-what-haunts-us/', 'snippet': 'I’ve been trying to lie about this story for years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve been trying to lie about this story for years. As a fiction writer, I feel an almost righteous obligation to the untruth. Fabrication is my livelihood, and so telling something straight, for me, is the mark of failure. Yet in many attempts over the years I’ve not been able to make out of this tiny — but weirdly soul-defining — episode in my life anything more than a plain recounting of the facts, as best as I can remember them. Dressing them up into fiction, in this case, wrecked what is essentially a long overdue confession. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Writing About What Haunts Us', 'kicker': 'Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Writing About What Haunts Us', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-12T19:49:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Orner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Orner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c71aee2f-575e-5f94-899e-64f18b4170b7', 'word_count': 1229, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c71aee2f-575e-5f94-899e-64f18b4170b7'}, {'abstract': 'As part of the 2012-13 Neediest Cases campaign, The New York Times is catching up with some of the people who were profiled in recent campaigns.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/01/12/nyregion/neediest-oneyearlater-moms.html', 'snippet': 'As part of the 2012-13 Neediest Cases campaign, The New York Times is catching up with some of the people who were profiled in recent campaigns.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As part of the 2012-13 Neediest Cases campaign, The New York Times is catching up with some of the people who were profiled in recent campaigns.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pressing On for the Children', 'kicker': 'The Neediest Cases | One Year Later', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times Neediest Cases Fund', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-12T19:56:24+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'New York', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/59ce018c-7348-59e9-bba6-9022328d3c61', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/59ce018c-7348-59e9-bba6-9022328d3c61'}, {'abstract': 'Two films depicting men who shed modern society’s constraints — Richard Fleischer’s “Ashanti” (1979) and Ted Kotcheff’s “Wake in Fright” (1971) — have surfaced on DVD.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/13/movies/homevideo/new-on-dvd-ashanti-and-wake-in-fright.html', 'snippet': 'Two films depicting men who shed modern society’s constraints — Richard Fleischer’s “Ashanti” (1979) and Ted Kotcheff’s “Wake in Fright” (1971) — have surfaced on DVD.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SURPRISINGLY, Joseph Conrad’s novella “Heart of Darkness” has only been filmed once under its own name — as a 1993 made-for-television movie directed by Nicolas Roeg. But with its richly metaphorical plot and tight dramatic structure — leaving the trappings of Western civilization behind, a cultured man embarks on a journey into a strange territory, where he is forced to confront the savagery (“the horror, the horror”) that survives beneath the surface of polite human behavior — the tale has served as a template for countless works of art (William Faulkner’s “Sanctuary,” for example), and perhaps even greater quantities of schlock (Ruggero Deodato’s “Cannibal Holocaust”).', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/arts/13KEHR_SPAN/13KEHR_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/13/arts/13KEHR_SPAN/13KEHR_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/arts/13KEHR_SPAN/13KEHR_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/arts/13KEHR_SPAN/13KEHR_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/arts/13KEHR_SPAN/13KEHR_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/13/arts/13KEHR_SPAN/13KEHR_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/arts/13KEHR_SPAN/13KEHR_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Descending Into a State of Nature', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Descending Into A State of Nature', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kehr, Dave', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DVD (Digital Versatile Disc)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fleischer, Richard', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kotcheff, Ted', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Ashanti (Movie)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-12T20:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'subsection_name': 'DVD', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Kehr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kehr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/316a91a0-50d7-5995-b036-467f7c3c302c', 'word_count': 1392, 'uri': 'nyt://article/316a91a0-50d7-5995-b036-467f7c3c302c'}, {'abstract': 'A Hungarian novelist awaits a visit from hate and violence personified.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/12/someones-knocking-at-my-door/', 'snippet': 'A Hungarian novelist awaits a visit from hate and violence personified.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The editors of Anxiety recently asked the Hungarian novelist Laszlo Krasznahorkai to contribute to the series. Below, in the author’s words, is “a lyrical essay about the terrible meeting between boorishness and aggressiveness,” a meditation on a type of violent person who produces in him “the deepest personal anxiety.” It was translated by George Szirtes from the Hungarian.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headlin