d', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9c981b3-a508-5df8-874a-b0e6999df9bf', 'word_count': 851, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9c981b3-a508-5df8-874a-b0e6999df9bf'}, {'abstract': 'Is there any sort of plan?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/12/so-what-will-you-do-mr-president/', 'snippet': 'Is there any sort of plan?', 'lead_paragraph': 'If I’d spent the past five years living in a monastery or something, I would take the Treasury Department’s declaration that the coin option is out as a sign that there’s some other plan ready to go. Maybe 14th Amendment, maybe moral obligation coupons or some other form of scrip, something.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'So What Will You Do, Mr. President?', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-12T21:29:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ab852b4-aa03-52b2-8e0d-bd3b70034772', 'word_count': 264, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ab852b4-aa03-52b2-8e0d-bd3b70034772'}, {'abstract': 'Donatella Versace offered a delirious and invigorating show in Milan.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/12/a-show-that-only-versace-could-give/', 'snippet': 'Donatella Versace offered a delirious and invigorating show in Milan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MILAN — There were suits in steroidal Al Capone proportions (and accessories: spectator shoes!). There was graffiti print double-denim. There were wide ties lopped so short Emmett Kelly could have worn them. There were studded Stormtrooper boots 