ork Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Treasury Won’t Mint Coin to Defy Debt Ceiling', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Treasury Won’t Mint Coin to Defy Debt Ceiling', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lowrey, Annie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Treasury Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Mint', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Currency', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-13T01:18:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annie Lowrey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lowrey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f4aa103-27e5-533b-afb8-e6d7b5abc5d0', 'word_count': 431, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f4aa103-27e5-533b-afb8-e6d7b5abc5d0'}, {'abstract': 'An air-quality monitor atop the United States Embassy recently measured an air quality index well above 500, which is supposed to be the top of the scale.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/13/science/earth/beijing-air-pollution-off-the-charts.html', 'snippet': 'An air-quality monitor atop the United States Embassy recently measured an air quality index well above 500, which is supposed to be the top of the scale.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — One Friday more than two years ago, an air-quality monitoring device atop the United States Embassy in Beijing recorded data so horrifying that someone in the embassy called the level of pollution “Crazy Bad” in an infamous Twitter post. That day the Air Quality Index, which uses standards set by the United States Environmental Protection Agency, had crept above 500, which was supposed to be the top of the scale.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/world/china/china-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/13/world/china/china-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/world/china/china-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/world/china/china-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/world/china/china-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/13/world/china/china-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/world/china/china-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'On Scale of 0 to 500, Beijing’s Air Quality Tops ‘Crazy Bad’ at 755', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On Scale of 0 to 500, Beijing’s Air Quality Tops ‘Crazy Bad’ at 755', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beijing (China)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-13T01:24:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1027e184-a72a-5929-9e24-2a5427672b85', 'word_count': 819, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1027e184-a72a-5929-9e24-2a5427672b85'}, {'abstract': 'Readers comment on my column about gender violence as a global human rights challenge, from India to America.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/12/taking-violence-against-women-seriously/', 'snippet': 'Readers comment on my column about gender violence as a global human rights challenge, from India to America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My Sunday column grew out of the rape/murder in Delhi. At the time I was in China, reporting there, and so I didn’t weigh in. But this is of course an issue that I’ve covered in one way or another for decades and that Sheryl and I tried to call attention to in Half the Sky, and friends began emailing me about other incidents of sexual violence or gender violence that deserved attention. An American woman raped in India, whom the authorities weren’t interested in. A 13-year-old girl dying of injuries caused by rape in Liberia. A separate incident in which an 8-year-old girl is kidnapped by a pimp in Liberia. A woman in San Francisco allegedly doused with gasoline by her boyfriend and set on fire. A girl in Nepal burned alive because she refused a marriage offer. And so on and so on.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Taking Violence Against Women Seriously….', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-13T01:35:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/20ac9e4b-f813-5142-a5aa-71581ee81c99', 'word_count': 264, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20ac9e4b-f813-5142-a5aa-71581ee81c99'}, {'abstract': 'The campaign now being waged against Senator Chuck Hagel’s nomination as secretary of defense echoes his dispute with fellow Republicans over the invasion of Iraq in 2003.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/13/us/old-foes-lead-charge-against-chuck-hagel.html', 'snippet': 'The campaign now being waged against Senator Chuck Hagel’s nomination as secretary of defense echoes his dispute with fellow Republicans over the invasion of Iraq in 2003.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the bitter debate that led up to the American invasion of Iraq in 2003, Senator Chuck Hagel of Nebraska said that some of his fellow Republicans, in their zest for war, lacked the perspective of veterans like him, who have “sat in jungles or foxholes and watched their friends get their heads blown off.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/us/HAGEL/HAGEL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/13/us/HAGEL/HAGEL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 480}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/us/HAGEL/HAGEL-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/us/HAGEL/HAGEL-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1639, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/us/HAGEL/HAGEL-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/13/us/HAGEL/HAGEL-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/us/HAGEL/HAGEL-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hawks on Iraq Prepare for War Again, Against Hagel', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hawks on Iraq At War Again, Against Hagel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rutenberg, Jim', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hagel, Chuck', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003-11)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-13T01:43:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Rutenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rutenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/baa2a822-b8de-5b35-8e1f-512cbef337a2', 'word_count': 1506, 'uri': 'nyt://article/baa2a822-b8de-5b35-8e1f-512cbef337a2'}, {'abstract': 'Claudia Acuña’s set was propulsive and polished, and the strongest creative force in the band was the guitarist Mike Moreno, who fashioned a fluent solo.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/12/winter-jazzfest-a-new-world-meshing-of-pop-and-folk/', 'snippet': 'Claudia Acuña’s set was propulsive and polished, and the strongest creative force in the band was the guitarist Mike Moreno, who fashioned a fluent solo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Day 2 of Winter Jazzfest began, for me, with Claudia Acuña at the Bitter End, reharmonizing “You Are My Sunshine” for a standing-room crowd. I feel as if I’m still digesting last night’s offerings, including a brilliantly indeterminate set by the bassist Eric Revis, the pianist Kris Davis and the drummer Andrew Cyrille; and a midnight set by Nasheet Waits’s Equality, featuring the pianist Vijay Iyer. I tumbled into bed this morning at 3:30, and spent most of the day looking forward to more of the same.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Winter Jazzfest: A New-World Meshing of Pop and Folk', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Winter Jazzfest', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-13T01:46:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f4280ef-6193-55e7-bb52-9b8dd15aa241', 'word_count': 228, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f4280ef-6193-55e7-bb52-9b8dd15aa241'}, {'abstract': 'Few tourist destinations are as exotic and unsafe as Afghanistan, where people still visit in dwindling numbers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/13/world/asia/taliban-targets-tourists-but-some-still-visit-afghanistan.html', 'snippet': 'Few tourist destinations are as exotic and unsafe as Afghanistan, where people still visit in dwindling numbers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — The Taliban have a message for foreign tourists who come to Afghanistan, especially if they are from any of the 50 countries that are part of the NATO-led coalition supporting the government: Big mistake.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/world/AFGHANISTAN-2/AFGHANISTAN-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 156, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/world/AFGHANISTAN-2/AFGHANISTAN-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 156, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Despite Taliban Threat, Afghanistan Manages to Entice Some Tourists', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Despite Taliban Threat, Afghanistan Manages To Entice Some Tourists', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nordland, Rod', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hotels and Travel Lodgings', 'rank