'nyt://article/f92078e5-95ea-57d1-a3d8-b739673f690d', 'word_count': 702, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f92078e5-95ea-57d1-a3d8-b739673f690d'}, {'abstract': 'A version of “The Play of Daniel” has returned to the Fuentidueña Chapel at the Cloisters in honor of the 75th anniversary of the museum’s opening.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/14/arts/music/the-play-of-daniel-at-the-cloisters.html', 'snippet': 'A version of “The Play of Daniel” has returned to the Fuentidueña Chapel at the Cloisters in honor of the 75th anniversary of the museum’s opening.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The point of opera’s origins, the moment when various age-old combinations of music and drama came together in a newly integrated way, keeps being pushed further back.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/14/arts/DANIEL/DANIEL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/14/arts/DANIEL/DANIEL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/14/arts/DANIEL/DANIEL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/14/arts/DANIEL/DANIEL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/14/arts/DANIEL/DANIEL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In a Work From the Dawn of Opera, Daniel Avoids Becoming Some Lions’ Lunch', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In a Work From the Dawn of Opera, Daniel Avoids Becoming Some Lions’ Lunch', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cloisters, The', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gotham Early Music Scene', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-13T21:22:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zachary Woolfe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zachary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Woolfe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/761bc122-796f-57bf-a5be-e2b48cb9deeb', 'word_count': 516, 'uri': 'nyt://article/761bc122-796f-57bf-a5be-e2b48cb9deeb'}, {'abstract': 'In “The Men Dancers: From the Horse’s Mouth ” dancers of varying ages and genres gather for an intimate showcase of talking and dancing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/14/arts/dance/the-men-dancers-from-the-horses-mouth-at-14th-street-y.html', 'snippet': 'In “The Men Dancers: From the Horse’s Mouth ” dancers of varying ages and genres gather for an intimate showcase of talking and dancing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dance is an oral tradition in which roles and works are passed one from one generation to the next. But what happens to the personal stories? On Thursday evening at the Theater at the 14th Street Y the dancer Todd Allen shared a good one in honor of “The Men Dancers: From the Horse’s Mouth.” At the age of 5, while growing up in Salt Lake City, he planted a tree with Martha Graham, who was traveling through the city. As the only boy in his dance program, Mr. Allen was chosen to appear at the ceremony. Graham was “a pyramid of purple with a head in a bun,” as he put it. “I don’t remember any arms.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/14/arts/DANCERS/DANCERS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 844, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/14/arts/DANCERS/DANCERS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1689, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/14/arts/DANCERS/DANCERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/14/arts/DANCERS/DANCERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/14/arts/DANCERS/DANCERS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'To Tell a Story, You Have to Have the Right Moves', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Tell a Story, You Have to Have the Right Moves', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-13T21:23:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7481652-c7b9-523e-8819-8bb99c9b28ae', 'word_count': 511, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7481652-c7b9-523e-8819-8bb99c9b28ae'}, {'abstract': 'In “Ruff” Peggy Shaw ruminates on the workings of her mind and memory in an impressionistic monologue that’s admirably unsentimental.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/14/theater/reviews/ruff-peggy-shaws-new-solo-show-at-performance-space-122.html', 'snippet': 'In “Ruff” Peggy Shaw ruminates on the workings of her mind and memory in an impressionistic monologue that’s admirably unsentimental.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I found myself praying,” Peggy Shaw says in her new solo show “Ruff,” recalling the day she suffered a stroke. It seemed the natural thing to do, since she had already fallen to her knees. “If you get me through this I will stop wearing suits,” she remembers thinking. “I will get married. I will pay market rent in Manhattan. I will not wear skinny jeans. I’ll take antidepressants.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/14/arts/RUFF/RUFF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/14/arts/RUFF/RUFF-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/14/arts/RUFF/RUFF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/14/arts/RUFF/RUFF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2