s, accurate speed guns, a better antidoping program, and breakthroughs for Chinese men and South American women. He would also like to see players take a break from towel breaks: ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Is On Your Tennis Wish List for 2013?', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-13T21:56:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By THE NEW YORK TIMES', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f04324d7-3488-5560-a851-5d6604bc922b', 'word_count': 165, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f04324d7-3488-5560-a851-5d6604bc922b'}, {'abstract': 'Matt Bryant’s 49-yard field goal with eight seconds left proved the difference as the Falcons rallied past the Seahawks after they had blown a 20-point lead.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/14/sports/football/falcons-escape-against-seahawks.html', 'snippet': 'Matt Bryant’s 49-yard field goal with eight seconds left proved the difference as the Falcons rallied past the Seahawks after they had blown a 20-point lead.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATLANTA — Through more than 250 games with two teams in 16 N.F.L. seasons, Tony Gonzalez never cried tears of joy. He saw players on other teams do it, of course, watching with envy as his opponents were so overwhelmed by the emotion of a victory that they wept on their shoulder pads. But for Gonzalez, those tears never came. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/14/sports/NFC/NFC-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 369, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/14/sports/NFC/N