a4b-19a0-58c6-ae44-037feb4332a0'}, {'abstract': 'Senator Lisa Murkowski broke through the partisan wall in support of more transparency in campaign financing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/14/opinion/one-republican-steps-forward.html', 'snippet': 'Senator Lisa Murkowski broke through the partisan wall in support of more transparency in campaign financing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Until now, the Senate minority leader, Mitch McConnell, has not seen a single member of his caucus dare to buck his fierce opposition to a law requiring fuller disclosure of campaign contributions. But last month, Senator Lisa Murkowski, Republican of Alaska, broke through the partisan wall to propose a badly needed mandate for transparency by the growing army of unrestricted, unidentified donors who underwrite attack ads and other stealth tactics that have so disfigured American politics. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'One Republican Steps Forward', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'One Republican Steps Forward', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murkowski, Lisa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Crossroads Grassroots Policy Strategies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-14T01:39:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c2dc2f5-1078-5dd2-a643-332330f015da', 'word_count': 338, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c2dc2f5-1078-5dd2-a643-332330f015da'}, {'abstract': 'Readers respond to