omic-transfusion.html', 'snippet': 'A new stimulus package could help jump-start Japan’s moribund economy, but structural reforms are needed for long-term revival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The $116 billion stimulus package unveiled Friday by Japan’s new prime minister, Shinzo Abe, is a step in the right direction for the world’s third-largest economy and America’s fourth-largest trading partner. Mr. Abe’s predecessors in the center-left Democratic Party unwisely followed a course of fiscal austerity, and paid the price for it last month at the polls. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Japan’s Latest Economic Transfusion', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Japan’s Latest Economic Transfusion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABE, SHINZO', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-14T01:52:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/3cbf733b-f9a0-5354-8f93-b063c750cdf0', 'word_count': 384, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3cbf733b-f9a0-5354-8f93-b063c750cdf0'}, {'abstract': 'The fiscal cliff agreement did not fully reform the alternative minimum tax.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/14/opinion/an-incomplete-fix.html', 'snippet': 'The fiscal cliff agreement did not fully reform the alternative minimum tax.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thanks to the fiscal cliff deal, the alternative minimum tax will not ensnare tens of millions of middle-class Americans for whom it was never intended. The deal raised the income thresholds before the A.M.T. kicks in and indexes them for inflation going forward. As a practical matter, this means that 28 million filers who would have had to pay the tax on their 2012 returns have been spared and are much less likely to have to pay the tax in the future. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Incomplete Fix', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Incomplete Fix', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALTERNATIVE MINIMUM TAX', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-14T01:57:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e00f343-3094-5549-a4bf-345226c4ad03', 'word_count': 539, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e00f343-3094-5549-a4bf-345226c4ad03'}, {'abstract': 'Seattle quarterback Russell Wilson was 31 seconds from an N.F.C. championship game after engineering a come-from-behind touchdown against Atlanta.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/14/sports/football/russell-wilson-of-seahawks-shows-talent-and-poise-in-loss.html', 'snippet': 'Seattle quarterback Russell Wilson was 31 seconds from an N.F.C. championship game after engineering a come-from-behind touchdown against Atlanta.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATLANTA — In the morgue silence of the Seattle locker room, several Seahawks sat frozen on folding chairs, staring straight ahead at nothing. A few heads were hidden beneath white towels. One player sniffled.', 'print_section': 'D', '