The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71565722-2b6c-59aa-8ea9-344396fabf61', 'word_count': 166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71565722-2b6c-59aa-8ea9-344396fabf61'}, {'abstract': 'A university achieves elite status in Dresden. And in the small city of Frankfurt an der Oder, a school reaches across the Polish border to engage with Eastern Europe.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/14/university-life-in-the-former-east-germany/', 'snippet': 'A university achieves elite status in Dresden. And in the small city of Frankfurt an der Oder, a school reaches across the Polish border to engage with Eastern Europe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With more than 2.2 million students\xa0studying\xa0in its universities and other post-secondary institutions, the German higher education system is one of Europe’s biggest. It is also unique in that it continues to be\xa0comparatively\xa0well funded, despite Europe’s financial troubles. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/education/EducLede/EducLede-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 372, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/13/education/EducLede/EducLede-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 372}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/education/EducLede/EducLede-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/education/EducLede/EducLede-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/13/education/E