eur’s future earnings — irrespective of what company the entrepreneur ends up building or working for.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/14/a-modest-proposal-to-open-up-small-business-credit/', 'snippet': 'Suppose we were to allow lenders to be paid back with a percentage of an entrepreneur’s future earnings — irrespective of what company the entrepreneur ends up building or working for.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In my last post about the state of small-business lending, I discussed the need to find a way to break through the gridlock in order to open up access to reasonably priced capital for small-business owners and entrepreneurs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Modest Proposal to Open Up Small-Business Credit', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-14T16:00:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ami Kassar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ami', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kassar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d43c557a-b757-5dec-a2b4-bd08852537c2', 'word_count': 547, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d43c557a-b757-5dec-a2b4-bd08852537c2'}, {'abstract': 'The wide coverage of Beijing’s air, which has been rated “hazardous” or even worse since last week, was the most open display of coverage on the issue in recent memory.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/15/world/asia/china-allows-media-to-report-alarming-air-pollution-crisis.html', 'snippet': 'The wide coverage of Beijing’s air, which has been rated “hazardous” or even worse since last week, was the most open display of coverage on the issue in recent memory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — The Chinese state news media on Monday published aggressive reports on what they described as the sickening and dangerous air pollution in Beijing and other parts of northern China, indicating that popular anger over air quality had reached a level where Communist Party propaganda officials felt that they had to allow the officially sanctioned press to address the growing concerns of ordinary citizens.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/15/world/CHINA-1/CHINA-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/15/world/CHINA-1/CHINA-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/15/world/CHINA-1/CHINA-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/15/world/CHINA-1/CHINA-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1311, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/15/world/CHINA-1/CHINA-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/15/world/CHINA-1/CHINA-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/15/world/CHINA-1/CHINA-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, '