acting. Her Wikipedia page was briefly updated to say so, though backstage in the press room, Ms. Foster denied that she would ever stop performing – “you couldn’t drag me away” — while adding that she would like be to directing “tomorrow.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Parsing What Jodie Foster Did (and Didn’t) Say', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golden Globes (Awards)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Foster, Jodie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-14T17:40:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/90a035b0-3bf8-5b86-b1c5-0785b3288c7e', 'word_count': 509, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90a035b0-3bf8-5b86-b1c5-0785b3288c7e'}, {'abstract': 'The Metropolitan Museum of Art held a formal ground-breaking on Monday morning for the $65 million makeover of its plaza and fountains, a project that has been under construction since October.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/14/ground-is-officially-broken-on-met-museums-david-h-koch-plaza/', 'snippet': 'The Metropolitan Museum of Art held a formal ground-breaking on Monday morning for the $65 million makeover of its plaza and fountains, a project that has been under construction since October.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Metropolitan Museum of Art held a formal ground-breaking on Monday morning for the $65 million makeover of its plaza and fountains, a project that has been under construction since October. Wearing hard hats and brandishing shovels – both bearing the Met’s logo – museum and city officials ceremoniously dug into the dirt on the plaza. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ground Is Officially Broken on Met Museum’s ‘David H. Koch Plaza’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ground Is Broken For New Met Plaza', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fountains', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Campbell, Thomas P', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koch, David H', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Museum of Art', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-14T17:41:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Vogel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vogel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bcc5166a-cded-535e-a7ca-190da638714d', 'word_count': 304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bcc5166a-cded-535e-a7ca-190da638714d'}, {'abstract': 'Best N.B.A. games this week pit the Lakers and Bucks, the Rockets and Pacers and the Warriors vs. the Spurs.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/14/best-n-b-a-games-of-the-week/', 'snippet': 'Best N.B.A. games this week pit the Lakers and Bucks, the Rockets and Pacers and the Warriors vs. the Spurs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Off the Dribble will highlight three essential games to watch each week, featuring hot teams, winning and losing streaks, and intriguing matchups from every corner of the league. (All times eastern.