: 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-14T17:44:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonah Bromwich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bromwich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0407c510-6993-55b2-a5f3-ca63e47847d7', 'word_count': 631, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0407c510-6993-55b2-a5f3-ca63e47847d7'}, {'abstract': 'The platinum coin, the debt ceiling, and how technical victories are swamped by political defeats.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/14/how-to-lose-at-american-politics/', 'snippet': 'The platinum coin, the debt ceiling, and how technical victories are swamped by political defeats.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No doubt thanks to my timely intervention in the great $1 trillion coin debate, the Treasury Department explicitly rejected the possibility that the White House would mint a platinum “solution” to the debt ceiling debate this weekend. I put the word “solution” in quotation marks because I’m confident that the coin gambit would have solved exactly none of the problems that its supporters claimed it was designed to address. No matter how many clever arguments exist to justify the maneuver, the politics of coin minting would have been just terrible for the White House — and because public opinion would have shaped how both the markets and the other branches of government would have responded to the move, those terrible politics would have ultimately produced exactly the kind of long-run outcomes (from swifter spending cuts to a stronger and more radicalized G.O.P.) that most of the coin-minters wanted to avoid.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How To Lose At American Politics', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-14T17:45:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9489d9cc-5878-501b-a472-d10fbc24feeb', 'word_count': 802, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9489d9cc-5878-501b-a472-d10fbc24feeb'}, {'abstract': 'Old Hollywood glamour met high fashion’s forwardness last night on the red carpet.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/14/look-of-the-moment-the-golden-globes-2/', 'snippet': 'Old Hollywood glamour met high fashion’s forwardness last night on the red carpet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Look of The Moment | The Golden Globes', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golden Globes (Awards)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-14T17:47:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/475ac212-740a-5811-b1f4-4577aca47cfd', 'word_count': 318, 'uri': 'nyt://article/475ac212-740a-5811-b1f4-4577aca47cfd'}, {'abstract': 'The following is the complete transcript from President Obama’s final press conference of his first term.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/14/us/politics/full-transcript-of-president-obamas-press-conference.html', 'snippet': 'The following is the complete transcript from President Obama’s final press conference of his first term.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The following is the complete transcript of President Obama’s press conference on Monday in Washington. (Transcript courtesy of Federal News Service.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Full Transcript of President Obama’s Press Conference', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-14T17:50:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Text', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e137f13-9b15-5072-9aec-e29373435c51', 'word_count': 8106, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e137f13-9b15-5072-9aec-e29373435c51'}, {'abstract': 'Things Serious people believe for no reason.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/14/on-the-unbearable-self-indulgence-of-centrist-economics/', 'snippet': 'Things Serious people believe for no reason.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ed Kilgore is deeply annoyed, as he should be, at the “No Labels” people promulgating the notion that all we need to do to solve our problems is transcend our petty partisanship. As he points out, even their diagnosis of what our problems are — specifically, that budget uncertainty is keeping our economy depressed — is something that, as it happens, neither Democrats nor Republicans accept.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On the Unbearable Self-Indulgence of Centrist Economics', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-14T17:58:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4eb325ac-279d-5636-be22-dbdd81a1b3a7', 'word_count': 381, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4eb325ac-279d-5636-be22-dbdd81a1b3a7'}, {'abstract': 'The writer Sohaila Abdulali, who was gang-raped as a teenager in India, discusses overcoming the trauma of sexual assaults.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/world/asia/100000002003829/moving-past-the-trauma-of-sexual-assault.html', 'snippet': 'The writer Sohaila Abdulali, who was gang-raped as a teenager in India, discusses overcoming the trauma of sexual assaults.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The writer Sohaila Abdulali, who was gang-raped as a teenager in India, discusses overcoming the trauma of sexual assaults.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/14/world/video-tc10-130114-writer/video-tc10-130114-writer-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/14/world/video-tc10-130114-writer/video-tc10-130114-writer-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight'