u-harris-to-perform-at-fund-raiser-for-county-music-hall-of-fame/', 'snippet': 'It will be the first time since 2008 that the event is being held in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Vince Gill and Emmylou Harris will perform next month at a fund-raiser in New York for the Country Music Hall of Fame and Museum, the first time since 2008 that the hall has held its annual “All for the Hall” gala in the city. The event will take place on Feb. 26 at the Best Buy Theater. Mr. Gill and Ms. Harris will anchor the show, inviting several special guests onto the stage to swap songs and stories in an informal format known in Nashville as a guitar pull. The other performers have yet to be announced. Tickets are $1,000 and the proceeds from the event go to support the museum in Nashville. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vince Gill and Emmylou Harris to Perform at Fund-raiser for County Music Hall of Fame', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gill and Harris to Perform At Country Music Fund-Raiser', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gill, Vince', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harris, Emmylou', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nashville (Tenn)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-14T18:01:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8cef8f41-7425-54f5-80e2-9acb848885a8', 'word_count': 120, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8cef8f41-7425-54f5-80e2-9acb848885a8'}, {'abstract': 'A reader criticizes the Time Warner Cable spot that refers to “Shameless,” the cable series on Showtime.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/14/business/media/q-and-a-with-stuart-elliott.html', 'snippet': 'A reader criticizes the Time Warner Cable spot that refers to “Shameless,” the cable series on Showtime.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stuart Elliott, the advertising columnist, answers questions from readers each week. Questions can be sent to stuarte@nytimes.com.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/05/27/business/media/stuart-elliott-headshot/stuart-elliott-headshot-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 234, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/05/27/business/media/stuart-elliott-headshot/stuart-elliott-headshot-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 234, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/05/27/business/media/stuart-elliott-headshot/stuart-elliott-headshot-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/05/27/business/media/stuart-elliott-headshot/stuart-elliott-headshot-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/05/27/business/media/stuart-elliott-headshot/stuart-elliott-headshot-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Q. and A. With Stuart Elliott', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Q. and A. With Stuart Elliott', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-14T18:06:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/d708b91e-41e7-536c-9578-d0bc6bd26cf2', 'word_count': 655, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d708b91e-41e7-536c-9578-d0bc6bd26cf2'}, {'abstract': 'Hester Bloch joined Isobar, London, in a new post, global chief marketing officer. She had been global marketing director at AKQA, part of WPP.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/14/business/media/webdenda.html', 'snippet': 'Hester Bloch joined Isobar, London, in a new post, global chief marketing officer. She had been global marketing director at AKQA, part of WPP.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Linda Bailey and Stacey Davis joined the Cadient Group, King of Prussia, Pa. Ms. Bailey becomes senior copywriter; she had been a lead writer at the Newtown, Pa., office of InVentiv Health. Ms. Davis becomes creative director for copy; she has worked as a freelance creative director, copywriter and marketing consultant for the last decade.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Accounts and People of Note in the Advertising Industry', 'kicker': 'Webdenda', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Webdenda', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Relations and Publicity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-14T18:12:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e01dd41-d21d-550b-accc-adb45ab1c535', 'word_count': 1351, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e01dd41-d21d-550b-accc-adb45ab1c535'}, {'abstract': 'Greg Sandoval, a senior writer for CNET, resigned on Monday, less than an hour after a report suggested that CNET was barred from presenting an award to a company being sued by CBS, which owns the Web site.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/14/resignation-suggests-rift-between-cnet-and-cbs/', 'snippet': 'Greg Sandoval, a senior writer for CNET, resigned on Monday, less than an hour after a report suggested that CNET was barred from presenting an award to a company being sued by CBS, which owns the Web site.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are companies with divisions that spend billions of dollars on entertainment. There are also companies with divisions that review new gadgets and sometimes champion the spectacular ones — even those that challenge the status quo.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Resignation Suggests Rift Between CNET and CBS', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'CNET Clashes With Its Owner, and a Reporter Resigns', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dish Network', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Las Vegas (Nev)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-14T18:12:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Busi