in Kaepernick has a chance to be the first quarterback known at least as much for his running as for his passing to win a Super Bowl.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/14/keeping-score-a-quarterback-who-can-run-away-with-the-title/', 'snippet': 'San Francisco quarterback Colin Kaepernick has a chance to be the first quarterback known at least as much for his running as for his passing to win a Super Bowl.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Colin Kaepernick rushed for 181 yards in San Francisco’s playoff victory over Green Bay on Saturday night, setting the single-game rushing record for a quarterback, it was immediately declared that he was reinventing the way the position was played.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Keeping Score: A Quarterback Who Can Run Away With the Title', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Using His Legs, When Arms Always Win Out', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaepernick, Colin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco 49ers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-14T21:23:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Hoffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ebc70c1-3a2c-5228-9f64-218f94c0c50b', 'word_count': 833, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ebc70c1-3a2c-5228-9f64-218f94c0c50b'}, {'abstract': 'Letters to the Editor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/15/science/dangers-of-marijuana-2-letters.html', 'snippet': 'Letters to the Editor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Dangers’ of Marijuana? (2 Letters)', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Dangers’ of Marijuana?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marijuana', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-14T21:24:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/09a139fc-4ce5-517e-9f17-269e4c46617d', 'word_count': 272, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09a139fc-4ce5-517e-9f17-269e4c46617d'}, {'abstract': 'A letter to the Editor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/15/science/when-parents-tease-1-letter.html', 'snippet': 'A letter to the Editor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Parents Tease (1 Letter)', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Parents Tease', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-14T21:24:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc1fab8b-8b38-5e0d-9c4a-1790a9fd4647', 'word_count': 133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc1fab8b-8b38-5e0d-9c4a-1790a9fd4647'}, {'abstract': 'Lyn Elizabeth Paolo, the costume designer of ABC’s television show starring Kerry Washington, tells T about creating a realistic but stylized version of Washington, D.C.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/14/gladiators-in-suits-the-fashion-of-scandal/', 'snippet': 'Lyn Elizabeth Paolo, the costume designer of ABC’s television show starring Kerry Washington, tells T about creating a realistic but stylized version of Washington, D.C.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The costume designer Lyn Elizabeth Paolo’s work on ABC’s Washington, D.C., drama “Scandal” has garnered a lot of buzz of late, particularly regarding the way she outfits the show’s lead character Olivia Pope, a high-power “fixer,” or crisis-management professional (played by Kerry Washington). Though viewers may not have guessed, the show is shot entirely in Los Angeles, where Paolo also creates the wardrobe for TNT’s “Southland” and Showtime’s dark comedy “Shameless.” But Paolo has worked in Washington before, editing the looks for “The West Wing,” which, along with extensive research, informs her portrayal of the political characters on “Scandal,” from the president and his cabinet to the politicians whose dilemmas Pope and Associates is charged with resolving. Here, Paolo tells T about creating a realistic but stylized version of the nation’s capital.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': "‘Gladiators in Suits': The Fashion of ‘Scandal’", 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dressing D.C.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Washington, Kerry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC INC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-14T21:30:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erika Allen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erika', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Allen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f59fc2d-e643-5eba-aa0f-ead0928ba962', 'word_count': 1013, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f59fc2d-e643-5eba-aa0f-ead0928ba962'}, {'abstract': 'Fan behavior in San Francisco has led to an increased police presence at 49ers games; 92 people were ejected from the game against the Packers on Saturday.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/14/cracking-down-on-malevolence-at-candlestick/', 'snippet': 'Fan behavior in San Francisco has led to an increased police presence at 49ers games; 92 people were ejected from the game against the Packers on Saturday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a city, San Francisco has an image of the laid-back hippie Mecca, populated by the live-and-let-live crowd. That image, however, does not extend to 49ers fans and how they behave at Candlestick Park. In fact, that behavior has so degenerated over the past few seasons that police are doubling down on trying to restore something resembling civility.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cracking Down on Malevolence at Candlestick', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Candlestick Park', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco 49ers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-14T21:33:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8bd094fe-da48-5aae-a89a-45310a85c9f3', 'word_count': 377, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8bd094fe-da48-5aae-a89a-45310a85c9f3'}, {'abstract': '“Hamlet, Prince of Grief,” in the Under the Radar Festival at the Public Theater, is a 30-minute, one-person version of “Hamlet” presented by the Leev Theater Group of Iran.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/15/theater/reviews/hamlet-prince-of-grief-at-the-public-theater.html', 'snippet': '“Hamlet, Prince of Grief,” in the Under the Radar Festival at the Public Theater, is a 30-minute, one-person version of “Hamlet” presented by the Leev Theater Group of Iran.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s easy to think of activities that could reasonably be completed in a half-hour. You could cook a pasta puttanesca, get a solid workout on the treadmill, buy a tube of toothpaste at Duane Reade.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/15/arts/15HAMLET/15HAMLET-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/15/arts/15HAMLET/15HAMLET-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/15/arts/15HAMLET/15HAMLET-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 614, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/15/arts/15HAMLET/15HAMLET-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1229, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'su