.nytimes.com/2013/01/14/a-parade-of-floats-for-obamas-inaugural/', 'snippet': 'The president’s inaugural parade next Monday will feature eight floats.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It won’t be Macy’s on Thanksgiving Day, but President Obama’s inaugural parade next Monday will feature eight floats, made by a company that has been building presidential floats since the 1949 inauguration of Harry Truman.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Parade of Floats for Obama’s Inaugural', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inaugurations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parades', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-14T21:38:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sheryl Gay Stolberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sheryl', 'middlename': 'Gay', 'lastname': 'Stolberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/88f61396-c5d4-5de5-b8e4-110ef237d38d', 'word_count': 362, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88f61396-c5d4-5de5-b8e4-110ef237d38d'}, {'abstract': 'A $10 million American expedition is close to beginning work to drill through to a subglacial lake in Antarctica, looking for signs of microbial life and insight on glaciers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/15/science/wissard-project-seeks-signs-of-life-under-antarctica.html', 'snippet': 'A $10 million American expedition is close to beginning work to drill through to a subglacial lake in Antarctica, looking for signs of microbial life and insight on glaciers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Three major scientific projects set out this season to seek evidence of life in lakes deep under the Antarctic ice — evidence that could provide clues in the search for evidence of life elsewhere in the solar system, perhaps in Mars’s past, or even now under the surface of Enceladus, one of Saturn’s moons. But only one of the projects, a $10 million expedition from the United States, has a chance of identifying long-hidden microbes before the weather on the frigid continent puts an end to drilling in about a month. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/15/science/15ICE_SPAN/15ICE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/15/science/15ICE_SPAN/15ICE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/15/science/15ICE_SPAN/15ICE_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/15/science/15ICE_SPAN/15ICE_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2040, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/15/science/15ICE_SPAN/15ICE_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/15/science/15ICE_SPAN/15ICE_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/15/science/15ICE_SPAN/15ICE_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Deep Under Antarctica, Looking for Signs of Life', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Deep Under Antarctica, Looking for Signs of Life', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ANTARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gorman, James', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Microbiology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wissard (Whillans Ice Stream Subglacial Access Research Drilling)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ice', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Glaciers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-14T21:39:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Gorman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gorman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e01151c-4252-532c-b4f8-018da6fb8a3e', 'word_count': 1215, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e01151c-4252-532c-b4f8-018da6fb8a3e'}, {'abstract': 'BMW introduces an entry-level 3 Series, the 320i, a model designation from the company’s past.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/14/a-bmw-for-the-masses-kind-of/', 'snippet': 'BMW introduces an entry-level 3 Series, the 320i, a model designation from the company’s past.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Introduced on Monday, Jan. 14: 2013 BMW 320i', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A BMW for the Masses, Kind of', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bayerische Motorenwerke AG', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-14T21:39:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lawrence Ulrich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lawrence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ulrich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/358b4a17-9d31-59e3-9202-a7e6334eff7b', 'word_count': 273, 'uri': 'nyt://article/358b4a17-9d31-59e3-9202-a7e6334eff7b'}, {'abstract': 'Databases offer a trove of medical information, without the cost of clinical research trials.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/15/health/mining-electronic-records-for-revealing-health-data.html', 'snippet': 'Databases offer a trove of medical information, without the cost of clinical research trials.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the past decade, nudged by new federal regulations, hospitals and medical offices around the country have been converting scribbled doctors’ notes to electronic records. Although the chief goal has been to improve efficiency and cut costs, a disappointing report published last week by the RAND Corp. found that electronic health records actually may be raising the nation’s medical bills.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mining Electronic Records for Revealing Health Data', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mining Electronic Records for Revealing Health Data', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electronic Health Records', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Data-Mining and Database Marketing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-14T21:48:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Jaret', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jaret', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/40399538-1bda-5a2f-a617-aeb10e2a13f8', 'word_count': 1216, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40399538-1bda-5a2f-a617-aeb10e2a13f8'}, {'abstract': 'Ken Austin is the founder and chairman of Avión Tequila, a maker of the beverage. He has loved flying since he was a child growing up near Kennedy Airport, and named his company for it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/15/business/met-by-coyotes-on-the-runway.html', 'snippet': 'Ken Austin is the founder and chairman of Avión Tequila, a maker of the beverage. He has loved flying since he was a child growing up near Kennedy Airport, and named his company for it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I GREW up near Kennedy Airport, right on the border of Queens. Sometimes the approaching planes were so loud that I thought they were landing in our yard. I used to get a flashlight and go to my bedroom window and turn the thing on and off. I thought I was signaling the pilots. That’s when I fell in love with aviation. I was president of a private jet company. Now, I’m in the tequila business, mostly flying to meet clients, find new clients and check on production. I even named the brand Avión, the Spanish word for plane.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/15/business/Flier/Flier-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 724, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/15/business/Flier/Flier-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1449, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Law on Board, and Coyotes on the Runway', 'kicker': 'Frequent Flier', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Law on Board, and Coyotes on the Runway', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Business Travel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guadalajara (Mexico)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Austin, Ken', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Avion Tequila', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-14T21:54:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Austin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0362bdb0-777d-5ad4-ad37-37d31ab88312', 'word_count': 602, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0362bdb0-777d-5ad4-ad37-37d31ab88312'}, {'abstract': 'As more Americans take up yoga, hotel companies, and even some airports, are beginning to cater to avid practitioners.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/15/business/some-hotel-companies-and-airports-start-to-offer-yoga.html', 'snippet': 'As more Americans take up yoga, hotel companies, and even some airports, are beginning to cater to avid practitioners.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ed Michael Reggie, a health care executive from New York, is even more devoted to his yoga practice on the road than he is at home.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 