ation': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/449cd7dd-a6f8-5a93-b11c-f40c98c97ee1', 'word_count': 929, 'uri': 'nyt://article/449cd7dd-a6f8-5a93-b11c-f40c98c97ee1'}, {'abstract': 'Twitter lights up over the actress’ rambling, riveting speech at the Golden Globe Awards.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/17/fashion/wow-whatever-it-was-jodie-foster-said.html', 'snippet': 'Twitter lights up over the actress’ rambling, riveting speech at the Golden Globe Awards.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE Golden Globe Awards started out being all about Tina Fey and Amy Poehler — perhaps the best award-show hosts ever — but by evening’s end most of the talk was of Jodie Foster and the rambling, riveting speech (watched by her date, a stone-faced Mel Gibson) in which she seemed to simultaneously come out of the closet and announce her retirement from acting. On Twitter, Ms. Foster’s speech brought praise for its bravery as well as derision for not being brave enough.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/fashion/17zHASHTAG/17zHASHTAG-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/17/fashion/17zHASHTAG/17zHASHTAG-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/fashion/17zHASHTAG/17zHASHTAG-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 802, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/fashion/17zHASHTAG/17zHASHTAG-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1443, 'width': 1130, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'th