ient and urged users to disable the software on their Web browsers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even after Oracle fixed a serious security flaw in its Java software on Sunday, the Department of Homeland Security warned that the fix was not sufficient and urged users to disable Java on their Web browsers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Department of Homeland Security: Disable Java ‘Unless It Is Absolutely Necessary’', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-14T23:48:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicole Perlroth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicole', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perlroth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a20f446f-3b74-5339-ad42-8eee91f9e59a', 'word_count': 436, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a20f446f-3b74-5339-ad42-8eee91f9e59a'}, {'abstract': 'Unlike during the 2011 debt ceiling negotiations, this time it is only members of Congress who will come before voters again.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/14/why-obama-may-drive-a-hard-bargain/', 'snippet': 'Unlike during the 2011 debt ceiling negotiations, this time it is only members of Congress who will come before voters again.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama has repeatedly stated that he will not negotiate over the federal debt ceiling, which must be raised soon to avoid a default.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Obama May Drive a Hard Bargain', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, House of Representatives', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'va