an To Improve Risk Controls', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dimon, James', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JPMorgan Chase & Company', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-15T00:16:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jessica Silver-Greenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jessica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver-Greenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b1de04c-90a2-51cb-ac6c-ed31e185a893', 'word_count': 875, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b1de04c-90a2-51cb-ac6c-ed31e185a893'}, {'abstract': 'The Coast Guard said it had hoped to find the plane, which was carrying three service members, before the men’s closest relatives died.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/15/us/world-war-ii-plane-that-crashed-in-greenland-in-1942-is-found.html', 'snippet': 'The Coast Guard said it had hoped to find the plane, which was carrying three service members, before the men’s closest relatives died.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Coast Guard said Monday that a private team had located a World War II rescue plane that crashed on the southeast coast of Greenland 70 years ago with three service members on board.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Search Crew Finds World War II Plane That Crashed in Greenland', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'World War II Plane Found in Glacier', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Coast Guard', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greenland', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aviation Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-15T00:17:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Southall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Southall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c4fa8d7-ddf4-5a22-84c3-3f0719a828b1', 'word_count': 511, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c4fa8d7-ddf4-5a22-84c3-3f0719a828b1'}, {'abstract': 'A draft report from a federal committee warns that if humanity fails to get a handle on emissions, climate change is likely to accelerate and threaten human welfare in many ways.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/14/an-alarm-in-the-offing-on-climate-change/', 'snippet': 'A draft report from a federal committee warns that if humanity fails to get a handle on emissions, climate change is likely to accelerate and threaten human welfare in many ways.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The natural conservatism of science has often led climatologists to be cautious in their pronouncements about global warming. More than once they have drawn criticism for burying their fundamental message – that society is running some huge risks — in caveats and cavils.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Alarm in the Offing on Climate Change', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drought', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wildfires', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Marine Biological Laboratory', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-15T00:18:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Justin Gillis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gillis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6cb1676-6891-515f-a667-38e6e91b9e4c', 'word_count': 600, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6cb1676-6891-515f-a667-38e6e91b9e4c'}, {'abstract': 'Palestinian medical officials accused Israeli soldiers of killing the farmer, Mustafa Abu Jarad, 21, but a military spokeswoman denied any Israeli involvement.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/15/world/middleeast/gaza-farmer-killed-at-border.html', 'snippet': 'Palestinian medical officials accused Israeli soldiers of killing the farmer, Mustafa Abu Jarad, 21, but a military spokeswoman denied any Israeli involvement.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A Palestinian farmer died Monday hours after he was shot in the northern Gaza Strip. Palestinian medical officials accused Israeli soldiers of killing the farmer, Mustafa Abu Jarad, 21, but a military spokeswoman denied any Israeli involvement. Since November, when a cease-fire between Hamas, the militant group that runs Gaza, and Israel was brokered by Egypt, Israeli troops have killed three Palestinians near the restricted border area. Also on Monday, rescue workers recovered the body of a Palestinian who had been trapped in a smuggling tunnel under Gaza’s border with Egypt. The man, Ali al-Qadi, was in the tunnel with two other people on Saturday when it collapsed after a period of heavy rain. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gaza: Farmer Killed at Border', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gaza: Farmer Killed at Border', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Akram, Fares', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gaza Strip', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hamas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-15T00:18:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fares Akram', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fares', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Akram', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa5984b5-17fc-5a63-848f-022eaea49158', 'word_count': 114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa5984b5-17fc-5a63-848f-022eaea49158'}, {'abstract': 'As he escorted stars from the stage to the red carpet last night, Ryan Seacrest, a host on the E! Entertainment Golden Globes broadcast, was compelled to exhort repeatedly, “Be careful getting down.” So awash was the scene in lavish trains, fishtail hems and trailing skirts that quite a few nominees risked a nasty tumble.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/14/trendspotting-taffeta-and-tulle-at-the-golden-globes/', 'snippet': 'As he 