ce.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/14/kerdiles-keeps-commitment-and-powers-wisconsin/', 'snippet': 'Nic Kerdiles made his college debut in late November, delayed nearly two months because of an N.C.A.A. suspension, and the Badgers have not lost since.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Unlike many North American sports, hockey players can choose to develop outside of an educational setting, in the Canadian Hockey League, though some contend that the on- and off-ice value of a college experience makes it the clear choice for most players.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kerdiles Keeps Commitment and Powers Wisconsin', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Wisconsin-Madison', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-15T04:53:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Snee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Snee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93040e9f-3a05-5c13-b7c7-e8bb334c30e0', 'word_count': 335, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93040e9f-3a05-5c13-b7c7-e8bb334c30e0'}, {'abstract': 'About a third of Americans say they have used the Internet to diagnose a medical condition for themselves or someone else, according to a new study from the Pew Research Center.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/15/turning-to-the-web-for-a-medical-diagnosis/', 'snippet': 'About a third of Americans say they have used the Internet to diagnose a medical condition for themselves or someone else, according to a new study from the Pew Research Center.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thirty-five percent of American adults said they had used the Internet to diagnose a medical condition for themselves or someone else, according to a new Pew Research Center study. Women are more likely than men to turn to the Internet for diagnoses. Other groups more likely to do so are younger people, white adults, people with college degrees and those who live in households with income above $75,000.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/15/health/15typing/15typing-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 565, 'width': 849, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/15/health/15typing/15typing-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 565, 'width': 849, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/15/health/15typing/15typing-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/15/health/15typing/15typing-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/15/health/15typing/15typing-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Turning to the Web for a Medical Diagnosis', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Awareness: Turning to Web for Diagnosis', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value':