cle/b966972d-2f5a-5da6-9af2-b1d59b4aa193', 'word_count': 1836, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b966972d-2f5a-5da6-9af2-b1d59b4aa193'}, {'abstract': 'Michael E. Mann, a climatologist at Penn State, promotes passage of a Pennsylvania bill that would subsidize energy retrofits and strengthen the state’s renewable energy standard.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/15/climate-scientist-backs-bill-to-curb-emissions/', 'snippet': 'Michael E. Mann, a climatologist at Penn State, promotes passage of a Pennsylvania bill that would subsidize energy retrofits and strengthen the state’s renewable energy standard.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Michael E. Mann, a prominent climatologist at Penn State, has thrown his support behind an effort to get Pennsylvania to do more to reduce its carbon dioxide emissions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Climate Scientist Backs Bill to Curb Emissions', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alternative and Renewable Energy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carbon Dioxide', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fuel Efficiency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mid-Atlantic States (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Natural Gas', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Corbett, Thomas W', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mann, Michael E', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania State University', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-15T12:54:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Hurdle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hurdle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/48326b4e-c2cc-5667-92ba-3127564dc486', 'word_count': 635, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48326b4e-c2cc-5667-92ba-3127564dc486'}, {'abstract': 'Years pass, and without warning, a glance in the mirror reveals the mother you wished you’d known better, and engaged more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/15/booming/face-to-face-with-mom-in-the-mirror.html', 'snippet': 'Years pass, and without warning, a glance in the mirror reveals the mother you wished you’d known better, and engaged more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It happens when you least expect it. You look into the mirror just as you’ve done every other day since Year Zero, but today your mother is staring back at you. The face you didn’t intend to inherit, the waist you would never allow to be altered by time, the expression of the lip or eye that echoes a familiar face, not yours, is right there in front of you.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/15/booming/15mystory-booming-mirror3/15mystory-booming-mirror3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/15/booming/15mystory-booming-mirror3/15mystory-booming-mirror3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 390}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/15/booming/15mystory-booming-mirror3/15mystory-booming-mirror3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 666, 'width'