.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/15/updates-on-the-gun-violence-debate-4/', 'snippet': 'The Lede is following the debate on gun violence in the wake of the shootings in Newtown, Conn., with reports from our correspondents and from around the Web.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Lede is following the debate on gun violence in the wake of the shootings in Newtown, Conn., with reports from our correspondents and from around the Web. On Tuesday, New York lawmakers voted voting on changes to gun laws that would expand the state’s ban on assault weapons and limit access to guns by the mentally ill. Vice President Joseph R. Biden Jr.’s recommendations include multiple steps that President Obama can take without legislative action. And religious leaders, including the United States Conference of Catholic Bishops, is expected to weigh in on the debate. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jan. 15 Updates on the Gun Violence Debate', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newtown, Conn, Shooting (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Conference of Catholic Bishops', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-15T15:14:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ef3d137-f1d2-56ec-a678-423e0a77445c', 'word_count': 1650, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ef3d137-f1d2-56ec-a678-423e0a77445c'}, {'abstract': 'Nissan shows a replacement for the Versa hatchback at the Detroit auto show.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/15/the-nissan-versa-note-sure-looks-like-a-hatchback/', 'snippet': 'Nissan shows a replacement for the Versa hatchback at the Detroit auto show.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Introduced on Tuesday, Jan. 15 Nissan Versa Note', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Nissan Versa Note Sure Looks Like a Hatchback', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'North American International Auto Show', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nissan Motor Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-15T15:17:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7889e5d7-1ec6-5d54-95ae-be3493a8e1ba', 'word_count': 326, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7889e5d7-1ec6-5d54-95ae-be3493a8e1ba'}, {'abstract': 'France’s labor unions and businesses reached an agreement to significantly reform the country’s labor laws.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/15/a-french-grand-bargain/', 'snippet': 'France’s labor unions and businesses reached an agreement to significantly reform the country’s labor laws.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even as Gérard Depardieu drew the world’s attention to France’s high marginal tax rates by taking up Russian citizenship, French labor unions and businesses reached an agreement late Friday night on significant reform of the country’s labor laws. The deal should help create new jobs while protecting workers, and should also help stabilize the government of President François Hollande, which has been struggling to reenergize the economy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A French Grand Bargain', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Working Hours', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hollande, Francois', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-15T15:28:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vikas Bajaj', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vikas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bajaj', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/26e7a6aa-6e1b-5bd3-9503-132e6f65df69', 'word_count': 427, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26e7a6aa-6e1b-5bd3-9503-132e6f65df69'}, {'abstract': 'John Cale, the experimental-rock pioneer, is presiding over two programs at the Brooklyn Academy of Music: one a tribute to Nico, one a performance of his album “Paris 1919.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/16/arts/music/with-john-cale-in-paris-and-along-the-borderline.html', 'snippet': 'John Cale, the experimental-rock pioneer, is presiding over two programs at the Brooklyn Academy of Music: one a tribute to Nico, one a performance of his album “Paris 1919.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Musicians often lead eventful lives with changes of direction that reflect their shifting interests and their responses to the musical landscape. But few have covered as much of the waterfront as John Cale, the Welsh rocker who performs three shows at the Brooklyn Academy of Music this week.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subty