0-9fd154996ac5', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/e18e2b1d-b539-5e5e-b710-9fd154996ac5'}, {'abstract': 'The Ford Edge SE tops Insure.com’s list of least-expensive cars to insure.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/15/the-least-and-most-expensive-cars-to-insure/', 'snippet': 'The Ford Edge SE tops Insure.com’s list of least-expensive cars to insure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not many people consider insurance when they go car shopping, but your premiums can vary a fair bit depending on the type of car you buy. Insure.com each year compiles a list of the 20 least (and most) expensive cars to insure, and a number of S.U.V.’s and crossover vehicles are among the cheapest for the 2013 model year.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Least (and Most) Expensive Cars to Insure', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Cheapest Cars to Insure', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ford Motor Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-15T16:32:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2723473a-15e2-5cd3-9c37-b5b746789985', 'word_count': 496, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2723473a-15e2-5cd3-9c37-b5b746789985'}, {'abstract': 'An 18th-century Chinese vase that sold for a record-setting $83 million at auction in 2010 but never paid for has now been sold for less than half that amount, according to Bloomberg.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/15/chinese-vase-said-to-sell-for-less-than-half-its-record-setting-price/', 'snippet': 'An 18th-century Chinese vase that sold for a record-setting $83 million at auction in 2010 but never paid for has now been sold for less than half that amount, according to Bloomberg.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When an 18th-century Chinese vase made for the Qianlong emperor sold for a record $83 million at a West London auction more than two years ago, it seemed like one of those rag-to-riches stories that was almost too good to be true. The price was more than 50 times the auction estimate and a record for any Asian work of art ever sold at auction. The bid was made by an agent on behalf of the Beijing-based collector Wang Yaohui, according to a Bloomberg report  posted on Monday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chinese Vase Said to Sell for Less Than Half Its Record-Setting Price', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Records and Achievements', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Tony', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-15T16:34:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Vogel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vogel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3156b8e5-d4ce-5df9-b665-a8e842b5f816', 'word_count': 191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3156b8e5-d4ce-5df9-b665-a8e842b5f816'}, {'abstract': 'A photographer captured images of the South Bronx in the 1980s that belie the grim stereotype of a crime-ridden, burning borough. Read more on the Lens blog.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/15/lens-ricky-floress-portraits-of-the-south-bronx/', 'snippet': 'A photographer captured images of the South Bronx in the 1980s that belie the grim stereotype of a crime-ridden, burning borough. Read more on the Lens blog.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ricky Flores’s photos of the South Bronx in the 1980s belie the grim stereotype of a crime-ridden, burning borough. The stripped cars, hip-hop culture and the buildings aflame are there, but so is the full range of human experience and emotion. The photographer’s images from that era, along with those of five others, will be displayed in a new exhibition opening this weekend at the Bronx Documentary Center. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lens: Ricky Flores’s Portraits of the South Bronx', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Bronx (Bronx, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-15T16:35:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0d6859f-3f74-5dd4-b45e-694bb0898924', 'word_count': 75, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0d6859f-3f74-5dd4-b45e-694bb0898924'}, {'abstract': 'Goldman Sachs decided Tuesday it would not delay the payment of bonuses to its staff in Britain, a move that would have helped investment bankers and other top employees to benefit from a lower income tax rate.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/01/15/goldman-retreats-from-plan-to-award-bonuses-later-in-britain/', 'snippet': 'Goldman Sachs decided Tuesday it would not delay the payment of bonuses to its staff in Britain, a move that would have helped investment bankers and other top employees to benefit from a lower income tax rate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – Goldman Sachs decided on Tuesday that it would not delay the payment of bonuses to its staff in Britain, a move that would have helped investment bankers and other highly paid employees benefit from a lower income tax rate.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Goldman Retreats From Plan to Award Bonuses Later in Britain', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Goldman Bonuses Won’t Be Timed to Ease a Tax', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bonuses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Compensation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-15T16:47:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Werdigier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werdigier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c25561f-1b09-57b6-bb87-e504d5e8c57c', 'word_count': 507, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c25561f-1b09-57b6-bb87-e504d5e8c57c'}, {'abstract': 'Seeking to increase the awards’ relevance and profile, the National Book Foundation is adding to the number of finalists and expanding the list of judges beyond writers, to potentially include critics, librarians and booksellers.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/15/national-book-awards-to-diversify-judging-pool/', 'snippet': 'Seeking to increase the awards’ relevance and profile, the National Book Foundation is adding to the number of finalists and expanding the list of judges beyond writers, to potentially include critics, librarians and booksellers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Looking to broaden its appeal to the public and increase its impact on sales, The National Book Foundation, which presents The National Book Awards, announced Tuesday that it would increase the number of finalists and diversify the judging pool.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'National Book Awards to Diversify Judging Pool', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'National Book Awards To Diversify Judging Pool', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Book Trade and Publishing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Man Booker Prize', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Book Awards', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Entrekin, Morgan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Book Foundation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-15T16:51:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Leslie Kaufman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Leslie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaufman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b45466fa-30d1-54c2-819a-45cf7f25f18a', 'word_count': 376, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b45466fa-30d1-54c2-819a-45cf7f25f18a'}, {'abstract': 'Children are less likely to develop bad reactions to the DTaP vaccine, a routine immunization shot, if they get it in their thigh instead of in their arm, a new study shows.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/15/thigh-beats-arm-for-childhood-vaccine/', 'snippet': 'Children are less likely to develop bad reactions to the DTaP vaccine, a routine immunization shot, if they get it in their thigh instead of in their arm, a new study shows.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Children are less likely to develop bad reactions to the DTaP vaccine, a routine immunization shot that protects against diphtheria, tetanus and pertussis, or whooping cough, if they get it in their thigh instead of in their arm, a new study shows. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/16/health/16well_injection/16well_injection-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 596, 'width': 805, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/16/health/16well_injection/16well_injection-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 596, 'width': 805, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/16/health/16well_injection/16well_injection-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/16/health/16well_injection/16well_injection-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/16/health/16well_injection/16well_injection-th