tion_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hwaida Saad and Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hwaida', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saad', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8524b54-a3b2-590e-b605-f4f16a00c243', 'word_count': 1116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8524b54-a3b2-590e-b605-f4f16a00c243'}, {'abstract': 'Jori Lehtera scores a great penalty shot goal in the K.H.L. All-Star game on Sunday.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/15/coming-soon-to-north-america-penalty-shot-fever/', 'snippet': 'Jori Lehtera scores a great penalty shot goal in the K.H.L. All-Star game on Sunday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What with that soul-smothering N.H.L. lockout lasting so long, it might take a little something to get hockey fans back into the swing, or nudge casual sports fans toward remembering hockey is a sport. (Hint: Played on ice, very entertaining until ambulances are required.) To help, we bring you the best of a wacky penalty shot contest at the K.H.L. All-Star game in Chelyabinsk on Sunday, courtesy of Jori Lehtera, an East team all-star who plays for Sibir Novosibirsk. Lehtera was a 2008 draft pick by the St. Louis Blues, who could use this kind of inventiveness.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Coming Soon to North America: Penalty Shot Fever', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-15T17:00:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3740d4b2-010e-53e2-af7f-4206c5995e68', 'word_count': 174, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3740d4b2-010e-53e2-af7f-4206c5995e68'}, {'abstract': 'A documentary featuring the birds and bird watchers of Central Park makes its theatrical debut this Friday in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/15/the-birds-and-birders-of-central-park/', 'snippet': 'A documentary featuring the birds and bird watchers of Central Park makes its theatrical debut this Friday in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like many visitors to Central Park, the author Jonathan Franzen thought for years that only gray pigeons and brown sparrows could be seen in the man-made space at the center of Manhattan. It wasn’t until the day he went deeper into the Ramble with birder friends that he saw feathers with bright yellows, blues and blacks flitting from branch to branch.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Birds and Birders of Central Park', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birdwatching', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Franzen, Jonathan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-15T17:01:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily S. Rueb', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Rueb', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec1cf92b-5083-5538-90d9-b38d30a4a4aa', 'word_count': 269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec1cf92b-5083-5538-90d9-b38d30a4a4aa'}, {'abstract': 'Jari Lindholm, a reporter in Syria, describes the scene at a mass grave in Aleppo on Jan.9', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/15/mass-grave-found-in-aleppo-amid-fierce-fighting/', 'snippet': 'Jari Lindholm, a reporter in Syria, describes the scene at a mass grave in Aleppo on Jan.9', 'lead_paragraph': 'The bodies lay pell-mell under sticky, red earth at Al Islamiah, a sprawling cemetery in Aleppo. Here and there, a limb or a strip of clothing was visible: the tip of a rubber sandal, a clump of curled-up toes, shoeless feet in blue socks. And then there was the face: a prominent nose, a half-open mouth framed by gray stubble, eyes covered with a blindfold. Whatever had happened to the others, there seemed little doubt as to how this man had met his end.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mass Grave Found in Aleppo Amid Fierce Fighting', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Free Syrian Army', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALEPPO (SYRIA)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-15T17:03:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jari Lindholm', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jari', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lindholm', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f2d0eb1-5a5a-565e-9065-2bb73b3e0d30', 'word_count': 612, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f2d0eb1-5a5a-565e-9065-2bb73b3e0d30'}, {'abstract': 'The concept design is a preview of the redesigned 2015 version of America’s best-selling vehicle.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/15/a-ford-f-150-concept-larger-than-life/', 'snippet': 'The concept design is a preview of the redesigned 2015 version of America’s best-selling vehicle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Introduced on Tuesday, Jan. 15: Ford F-150 Atlas Concept', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Ford F-150 Concept, Larger Than Life', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'North American International Auto Show', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ford Motor Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-15T17:05:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jerry Garrett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jerry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garrett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25ff8c1e-77dd-5df3-8eb3-85b92b57bc8e', 'word_count': 262, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25ff8c1e-77dd-5df3-8eb3-85b92b57bc8e'}, {'abstract': 'Millet can be tricky to cook, but if you are careful, you will be rewarded with a fluffy and delicious salad.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/16/health/warm-millet-carrot-and-kale-salad-recipes-for-health.html', 'snippet': 'Millet can be tricky to cook, but if you are careful, you will be rewarded with a fluffy and delicious salad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I love millet but it is tricky to cook; it can easily turn to mush. I have found that cooking more than 2/3 cup at a time can be problematic because the millet at the bottom of the pot becomes gummy by the time all of the millet is cooked. But the tiny, nutritious seeds of grain expand so much during cooking that you don’t need more than 2/3 of a cup for this recipe, and if you toast the seeds in a little oil first and take care not to stir the millet once you’ve added the water you will get a fluffy result.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/15/science/16recipehealth/16recipehealth-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 368, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/15/science/16recipehealth/16recipehealth-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 368}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/15/science/16recipehealth/16recipehealth-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 629, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/15/science/16recipehealth/16recipehealth-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1257, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/15/science/16recipehealth/16recipehealth-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/15/science/16recipehealth/16recipehealth-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url