its original bus...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Juniper Networks is in a tough place. It has long been a distant second to Cisco Systems in the business of computer networking. It now faces the same industry shifts bedeviling Cisco, primarily a change from running networks with high-margin hardware to deploying cheap commodity computers and fancy software.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Juniper Jumps Into Software Networks', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cloud Computing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Enterprise Computing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Software', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Juniper Networks Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-15T17:15:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Hardy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hardy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8bdf3b1a-63b3-51cf-a093-5206887867d6', 'word_count': 744, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8bdf3b1a-63b3-51cf-a093-5206887867d6'}, {'abstract': 'The nutty flavor of buckwheat soba noodles makes for a delicious salad.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/17/health/skillet-soba-baked-tofu-and-green-bean-salad-recipes-for-health.html', 'snippet': 'The nutty flavor of buckwheat soba noodles makes for a delicious salad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You can make this salad with wide rice noodles, but I love the nutty flavor and wholesomeness of buckwheat soba.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/15/science/17recipehealth/17recipehealth-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 368, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/15/science/17recipehealth/17recipehealth-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 368}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/15/science/17recipehealth/17recipehealth-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 628, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/15/science/17recipehealth/17recipehealth-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1256, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/15/science/17recipehealth/17recipehealth-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/15/science/17recipehealth/17recipehealth-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/15/science/17recipehealth/17recipehealth-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Skillet Soba, Baked Tofu and Green Bean Salad With Spicy Dressing', 'kicker': 'Recipes for Health', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Salads', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-15T17:16:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Rose Shulman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': 'Rose', 'lastname': 'Shulman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'recipe', '_id': 'nyt://article/95cf6c25-72a6-564e-9913-8e2be5b1474f', 'word_count': 599, 'uri': 'nyt://article/95cf6c25-72a6-564e-9913-8e2be5b1474f'}, {'abstract': 'Triticale is a hybrid grain made from wheat and rye, but any hearty grain would work in this salad.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/18/health/skillet-brown-rice-barley-or-triticale-salad-recipes-for-health.html', 'snippet': 'Triticale is a hybrid grain made from wheat and rye, but any hearty grain would work in this salad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Triticale is a hybrid grain made from wheat and rye, which farmers and health food stores alike had high hopes for in the 1970s. It is a good source of phosphorus and a very good source of magnesium, but apparently the yields were disappointing to farmers and it never really caught on among consumers. I had sort of forgotten about it until I came across it again recently at Bob’s Red Mill. I like its chewy texture and earthy flavor, both very similar to farro or wheatberries. Any hearty, toothsome grain works well in this salad, so I’ve given you a choice.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/15/science/18recipehealth/18recipehealth-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/15/science/18recipehealth/18recipehealth-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth':