ertised as being for ages 4 and up. I suggested that this was, even by NRA standards, so tasteless that it must be a hoax.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'PS: A Little NRA Mystery', 'kicker': 'Bill Keller', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hoaxes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'iTunes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Rifle Assn', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-15T18:32:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Keller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/02e00c27-9ebf-5055-ad61-0bca0e0dbab6', 'word_count': 298, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02e00c27-9ebf-5055-ad61-0bca0e0dbab6'}, {'abstract': 'The violinist Itzhak Perlman and Yitzchak Meir Helfgot, the cantor from the Park East Synagogue in Manhattan, have scheduled a show for Feb. 28.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/15/another-first-for-barclays-center-a-concert-of-jewish-music/', 'snippet': 'The violinist Itzhak Perlman and Yitzchak Meir Helfgot, the cantor from the Park East Synagogue in Manhattan, have scheduled a show for Feb. 28.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The arena he built in Brooklyn has hosted concerts of hip-hop, Latin salsa and reggae, not to mention performances by Dylan, Streisand and the Rolling Stones, but when the genre chosen was Jewish music, Bruce C. Ratner decided to take charge himself.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/15/nyregion/15cityroom-concert/15cityroom-concert-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 933, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/15/nyregion/15cityroom-concert/15cityroom-concert-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1866, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/15/nyregion/15cityroom-concert/15cityroom-concert-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/15/nyregion/15cityroom-concert/15cityroom-concert-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/15/nyregion/15cityroom-concert/15cityroom-concert-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Another First for Barclays Center: A Concert of Jewish Music', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perlman, Itzhak', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ratner, Bruce', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Barclays Center (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-15T18:32:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph Berger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Berger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dce749bb-2a2e-5243-ad2b-484deeb3cb17', 'word_count': 595, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dce749bb-2a2e-5243-ad2b-484deeb3cb17'}, {'abstract': 'Wheels of sheep’s milk cheese are coated with herbs, including rosemary, lemon thyme, marjoram, elderberries and hop flowers, then aged.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/16/dining/hudson-valley-cheese-with-a-corsican-touch.html', 'snippet': 'Wheels of sheep’s milk cheese are coated with herbs, including rosemary, lemon thyme, marjoram, elderberries and hop flowers, then aged.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fleur du Maquis, better known as Brin d’Amour, is a popular Corsican sheep milk cheese with great character, thanks to its generous coating of brambly dried herbs, notably rosemary. Now, Murray’s Cheese is taking young, fat wheels of sheep’s milk cheese from Old Chatham Sheepherding in the Hudson Valley and giving them a Corsican accent, with a coating of rosemary, lemon thyme, marjoram, elderberries and hop flowers. The cheeses, called Hudson Flower, then age for about a month in Murray’s caves. The smooth, tangy interior acquires a mellow, satiny rim, which is flattered by the edible, fragrantly piney herb-dusted rind. And just as the Hudson Valley is a gentler place than volcanic Corsica, the herbs are not quite as aggressive as on the original. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/16/dining/16STUFF_CHEESE/16STUFF_CHEESE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/16/dining/16STUFF_CHEESE/16STUFF_CHEESE-superJumbo.jpg', '