 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Morgan Stanley', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-15T20:30:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susanne Craig', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Craig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6caeb90d-30a1-55a9-9ceb-303795af2326', 'word_count': 583, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6caeb90d-30a1-55a9-9ceb-303795af2326'}, {'abstract': 'My music had always been deeply informed by my depression. Listen to what happened when it finally began to lift.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/15/the-music-of-depression/', 'snippet': 'My music had always been deeply informed by my depression. Listen to what happened when it finally began to lift.', 'lead_paragraph': '“A grief without a pang, void, dark, and drear,” wrote Coleridge in “Dejection: An Ode,” a poem about the paralyzing melancholy he suffered most of his life, which might be diagnosed today as depression. “A stifled, drowsy, unimpassioned grief,/Which finds no natural outlet, no relief,/In word, or sigh, or tear….” The irony of these lines about a poet who is too unhappy to write is, of course, that we find them in a long, sustained poem. A friend shared these lines with me because a similar paradox is at play in many of my compositions, distant as they are from the work of the Romantics. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'My Dark Materials: The Music of Depression', 'kicker': 'The Score', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Depression (Mental)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Meditation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-15T20:45:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By keeril makan', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/27d30d98-7050-519b-b244-8a062ed81b3e', 'word_count': 1484, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27d30d98-7050-519b-b244-8a062ed81b3e'}, {'abstract': 'What’s the best way to avoid a sore back from sitting at a computer all day? What are some good exercises for the deskbound? Tara Parker-Pope responds to reader questions.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/15/ask-well-help-for-the-deskbound/', 'snippet': 'What’s the best way to avoid a sore back from sitting at a computer all day? What are some good exercises for the deskbound? Tara Parker-Pope responds to reader questions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Question:', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/12/health/12well_chair/12well_chair-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 703, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/12/health/12well_chair/12well_chair-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1406, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/12/health/12well_chair/12well_chair-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/12/health/12well_chair/12well_chair-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': 