': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/16/business/walmart-to-offer-more-us-made-goods.html', 'snippet': 'The retailer’s 10-year commitment, totaling $50 billion, comes as it is under pressure over its overseas sourcing following a deadly fire in November in Bangladesh.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The manufacturer 1888 Mills produces most of its sheets and towels overseas, in part to keep costs low for retailers like Walmart. But after Walmart gave 1888 Mills a long-term contract for towels made in the United States, 1888’s chief executive said the company expected to produce more goods here.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/16/business/WALMART/WALMART-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 930, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/16/business/WALMART/WALMART-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1859, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Walmart Plans to Buy American More Often', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Walmart Plans to Buy American More Often', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wal-Mart Stores Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clifford, Stephanie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bangladesh', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-16T00:29:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Clifford', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clifford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/57934392-ebaa-585b-b208-a7661bbdc098', 'word_count': 902, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57934392-ebaa-585b-b208-a7661bbdc098'}, {'abstract': 'Religious leaders, scientists and civil rights workers seized on Martin Luther King Jr.’s birthday to protest government inaction on climate change.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/15/at-a-protest-science-and-religion-team-up/', 'snippet': 'Religious leaders, scientists and civil rights workers seized on Martin Luther King Jr.’s birthday to protest government inaction on climate change.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Science and religion went hand-in-hand on Tuesday as leaders from both worlds gathered in front of the White House to protest what they cast as government inaction on climate change.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At a Climate Protest, Science and Religion', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion-State Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Martin Luther Jr', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-16T00:42:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jada F. Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jada', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93b7e7e6-dcbc-5b0d-a250-025cafa16917', 'word_count': 720, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93b7e7e6-dcbc-5b0d-a250-025cafa16917'}, {'abstract': 'Adrian Rodriguez was accused of stealing thousands of cartridges of copy machine toner from a law firm’s office in Manhattan and selling them on the black market.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/16/nyregion/man-charged-in-theft-of-copy-toner-worth-over-376000.html', 'snippet': 'Adrian Rodriguez was accused of stealing thousands of cartridges of copy machine toner from a law firm’s office in Manhattan and selling them on the black market.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In just about any office in the city, it is not uncommon for everyday items to disappear from the supply cabinet. Most of the time, it is relatively harmless — a pen here or a notepad there, tucked into a backpack and taken home. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For a Thief in This Office, Paper Clips Wouldn’t Do', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For a Thief In This Office, Paper Clips Wouldn’t Do', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black Markets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Office Supplies and Equipment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Printers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodriguez, Adrian', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-16T00:47:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marc Santora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d55b1176-1c5c-59fc-b49d-30301de2881e', 'word_count': 480, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d55b1176-1c5c-59fc-b49d-30301de2881e'}, {'abstract': 'Germany’s economic decline late last year and a flurry of disappointing results recently in other major economies raised questions about Europe’s ability to escape recession.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/16/world/europe/slowdown-in-germany-worries-euro-zone.html', 'snippet': 'Germany’s economic decline late last year and a flurry of disappointing results recently in other major economies raised questions about Europe’s ability to escape recession.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — Despite a drumbeat of optimistic forecasts from economists and upbeat statements from various European leaders, the actual news on the economy continues to be grim, with figures released Tuesday showing that Germany, the Continent’s flagship economy, contracted by about 0.5 percent in the final months of last year. Combined with a flurry of disappointing results recently in other major economies, the stumble raised questions about Europe’s ability to escape recession.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Slowdown in Germany Worries Euro Zone', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Slowdown In Germany Worries Euro Zone', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kulish, Nicholas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Monetary Union', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-16T00:48:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kulish and Jack Ewing', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kulish', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ewing', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d52c9758-8ee0-59b7-8c1f-e3367e8820a7', 'word_count': 640, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d52c9758-8ee0-59b7-8c1f-e3367e8820a7'}, {'abstract': 'As government seeks ways to save cash by outsourcing services, it might keep in mind that private efforts need clear goals and close monitoring, lest they veer in unintended directions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/16/business/when-privatization-works-and-why-it-doesnt-always.html', 'snippet': 'As government seeks ways to save cash by outsourcing services, it might keep in mind that private efforts need clear goals and close monitoring, lest they veer in unintended directions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Few corporate sagas capture the virtues and vices of state-owned companies and private enterprise better than the drama of BP’s roller-coaster ride between failure and success.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/02/29/business/eduardo-porter/eduardo-porter-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/02/29/business/eduardo-porter