e seen a thin, neatly dressed young man at the defense table who sometimes quietly confers with his lawyers. But on Tuesday they got a drastically different view as video and audiotapes secretly recorded by the F.B.I. in 2010 revealed a sometimes bombastic, sometimes swaggering religious militant who said repeatedly he was willing to kill and die as a martyr if need be.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/16/us/TERROR-2/TERROR-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 546, 'width': 445, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/16/us/TERROR-2/TERROR-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 546, 'width': 445, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/16/us/TERROR-2/TERROR-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/16/us/TERROR-2/TERROR-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/16/us/TERROR-2/TERROR-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Harsher View of Bombing Suspect Is Revealed on Tapes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Harsher View of Bombing Suspect Is Revealed on Tapes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mohamud, Mohamed Osman', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Kirk', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Portland (Ore)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-16T05:08:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kirk Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kirk', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c3d9a95-8ce8-501e-bafe-6e7c740cd0d6', 'word_count': 649, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c3d9a95-8ce8-501e-bafe-6e7c740cd0d6'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/16/arts/television/whats-on-wednesday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8 P.M. (Sundance) MONSOON WEDDING (2002) An extended Punjabi family works through its issues as it prepares to celebrate the arranged marriage of a daughter (Vasundhara Das, above left, with Shefali Shetty) — who has been carrying on an affair with a television host — and her betrothed (Parvin Dabas), who lives in Houston, in this film directed by Mira Nair. Naseeruddin Shah plays the father determined to pull off a wedding he cannot afford. Vijay Raaz is the wedding planner, who nervously eats marigolds. “\xa0‘Wedding’ often has the energy of a Bollywood spectacle, with its ingratiatingly incongruous shuffles of genres; we even get a handful of musical numbers, including a warm, offhanded song on the pleasures of married life performed by a group of women,” Elvis Mitchell wrote in The New York Times. “The agile handling of the soap opera elements — conventional plotting at best — finally makes ‘Wedding’ a pop, facile take on Capulet versus Montague stuff, likable but square.” He added: “Like the monsoon rains that temper Delhi’s summer heat, this movie offers subtle surprises. When ‘Wedding’ captures the small, hilarious skirmishes of a culture at war with itself, and the families trying to hold their ground against change, it is enchanting.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Wednesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-16T06:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/55141c4f-897a-5d6c-95a2-0ada0b25332f', 'word_count': 734, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55141c4f-897a-5d6c-95a2-0ada0b25332f'}, {'abstract': 'A profile of the lawyer defending one of the six accused, who blames the victim and her male companion.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/16/in-delhi-gang-rape-case-a-controversial-outspoken-lawyer-for-the-defense/', 'snippet': 'A profile of the lawyer defending one of the six accused, who blames the victim and her male companion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI: When Manohar Lal Sharma heard that the defendants in one of the most high-profile rape cases in recent years were about to be tried, he was the first to rush to court so he could offer to represent them pro bono.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Delhi Gang Rape Case, a Controversial, Outspoken Lawyer for the Defense', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mukherjee, Pranab', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strauss-Kahn, Dominique', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'},