ts at Studio 54 ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Selling Some Old Sparkle From Nights at Studio 54', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rubell, Steve', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Studio 54', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Memorabilia and Souvenirs', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hamilton, Bill', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-16T13:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9da3083d-2484-528c-8a4a-6d0b9d5b1522', 'word_count': 887, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9da3083d-2484-528c-8a4a-6d0b9d5b1522'}, {'abstract': 'Blending the humanist principles of an Indian mystic and the management style of McDonald’s, Aravind Eye Care System has become a global success.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/16/in-india-leading-a-hospital-franchise-with-vision/', 'snippet': 'Blending the humanist principles of an Indian mystic and the management style of McDonald’s, Aravind Eye Care System has become a global success.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the United States struggles to find new business models for health care, some innovators are looking to other industries, ones that provide high-quality services for low prices. In a recent article in The New Yorker, for example, Atul Gawande suggests that the Cheesecake Factory restaurant chain — with its size, central control and accountability for the customer experience — could be a model of sorts for health care. That’s not as outlandish as it seems. The world’s largest provider of eye care has found success by directly adapting the management practices of another big-box food brand, one that is not often associated with good health: McDonald’s.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Hospital Network With a Vision', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blindness', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cataracts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Eyes and Eyesight', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "McDonald's Corporation", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tamil Nadu (India)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-16T13:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tina Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97639321-5a98-5997-b709-3048d8de454f', 'word_count': 2040, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97639321-5a98-5997-b709-3048d8de454f'}, {'abstract': 'Interior Secretary Ken Salazar will leave President Obama’s cabinet by March, creating another opening for the president to fill as he begins his second term.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/17/us/politics/salazar-to-leave-interior-department.html', 'snippet': 'Interior Secretary Ken Salazar will leave President Obama’s cabinet by March, creating another opening for the president to fill as he begins his second term.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Ken Salazar, the blunt-spoken lawyer and rancher who took over the scandal-ridden Interior Department at the outset of the Obama administration, said Wednesday that he would step down  in March to return to his home in Colorado.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/us/SALAZAR/SALAZAR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 921, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/us/SALAZAR/SALAZAR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1454, 'width': 1308, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/us/SALAZAR/SALAZAR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/17/us/SALAZAR/SALAZAR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/us/SALAZAR/SALAZAR-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Interior Secretary to Step Down in March', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Interior Secretary to Step Down in March', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Interior Department', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Broder, John M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Salazar, Ken', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-16T13:01:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By John M. Broder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5684f8b0-768a-59c2-b4c9-595a5b650263', 'word_count': 940, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5684f8b0-768a-59c2-b4c9-595a5b650263'}, {'abstract': 'The French intervene to push back jihadis in Mali — to their credit and at others’ peril.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/16/the-risks-of-the-french-intervention-in-mali/', 'snippet': 'The French intervene to push back jihadis in Mali — to their credit and at others’ peril.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BAMAKO, Mali — Mamadou Doumbia was so thrilled that France intervened this weekend to beat back a jihadi offensive in Mali that on Monday he took me to buy a French flag to mount next to the Malian flag on the dashboard in his taxi.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Road to Bamako', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Coups D'Etat and Attempted Coups D'Etat", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tuareg (Ethnic Group)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mali', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-16T13:02:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hannah Armstrong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hannah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Armstrong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a495993-075e-5f98-a7be-ddbef2edc61d', 'word_count': 687, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a495993-075e-5f98-a7be-ddbef2edc61d'}, {'abstract': 'A summary of what’s on today’s editorial page.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/16/opinion-report-jobs-for-vets/', 'snippet': 'A summary of what’s on today’s editorial page.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From the editorial page', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Opinion Report: Jobs for Vets', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-16T13:07:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f153ad0a-8e11-5601-80e3-eb7aa540b2f4', 'word_count': 101, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f153ad0a-8e11-5601-80e3-eb7aa540b2f4'}, {'abstract': 'Metropolitan Diary: A poem captures the stillness of the park, with ducks busying themselves beside the pond.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/16/the-central-park-ducks-in-winter/', 'snippet': 'Metropolitan Diary: A poem captures the stillness of the park, with ducks busying themselves beside the pond.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dear Diary:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Central Park Ducks in Winter', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ducks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Winter (Season)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Central Park (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-16T13:30:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Goldfarb', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldfarb', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/612d9ac1-bdb6-58fc-9bf3-0f9cd659bd03', 'word_count': 59, 'uri': 'nyt://article/612d9ac1-bdb6-58fc-9bf3-0f9cd659bd03'}, {'abstract': 'In this week’s links: how online-dating sites tear us apart; what free will does not require; and more.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/16/stone-links-matchmaking-made-easy-all-too-easy/', 'snippet': 'In this week’s links: how online-dating sites tear us apart; what free will does not require; and more.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Taking off from Dan Slater’s essay in The Atlantic, the philosopher and Stone contributor Peter Ludlow pinpoints the source of the trouble with online dating. In the language of economics (which is probably apt), the most basic cost, of which the ones Slater identifies are just consequences, is that it creates a near frictionless market where transaction costs are all but eliminated. But it is friction, the complications it introduces, Ludlow thinks, that is exactly what we need in love–even if it’s not what we want.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stone Links: Dating Made Easy (All Too Easy)', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dating and Courtship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Online Dating', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harris, Sam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-16T13:30:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark de Silva', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'de Silva', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d56cd412-45cc-5214-b2ec-3a79431c5243', 'word_count': 680, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d56cd412-45cc-5214-b2ec-3a79431c5243'}, {'abstract': 'The New England tight end is a versatile offensive threat. He’s also a rugged presence who can clear a path for other receivers.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/16/how-aaron-hernandez-opened-a-throwing-window-for-tom-brady/', 'snippet': 'The New England tight end is a versatile offensive threat. He’s also a rugged presence who can clear a path for other receivers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Aaron Hernandez did it all for the Patriots in their 41-28 victory over Houston on Sunday. With tight end Rob Gronkowski out of the game, Hernandez was targeted nine times, finishing with six receptions for 85 yards.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Aaron Hernandez Opened a Throwing Window for Tom Brady', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hernandez, Aaron', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Patriots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-16T13:30:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Bretherton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bretherton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ecd9ea1d-dff2-559e-be06-e47a4a30b30a', 'word_count': 549, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ecd9ea1d-dff2-559e-be06-e47a4a30b30a'}, {'abstract': 'On what is likely his last trip as defense secretary, Leon E. Panetta had an audience on Wednesday morning at the Vatican with Pope Benedict XVI.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/17/world/europe/defense-secretary-leon-panetta-meets-pope.html', 'snippet': 'On what is likely his last trip as defense secretary, Leon E. Panetta had an audience on Wednesday morning at the Vatican with Pope Benedict XVI.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — On what is probably his last trip as defense secretary, Leon E. Panetta had an audience on Wednesday morning at the Vatican with Pope Benedict XVI, who told him, Mr. Panetta said, “Thank you for helping to protect the world.” Mr. Panetta said he replied, “Pray for me.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/world/europe/17military/17military-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/17/world/europe/17military/17military-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 403}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/world/europe/17military/17military-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/world/europe/17military/17military-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1371, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/world/europe/17military/17military-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/17/world/europe/17military/17military-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/world/europe/17military/17military-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Panetta, at Vatican, Says Pope Thanks Him for Service', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Panetta, at Vatican, Says Pope Thanks Him for Service', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Panetta, Leon E', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Benedict XVI', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-16T13:31:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Bumiller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bumiller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/61781789-9c1e-5d51-91ea-654c1de98f85', 'word_count': 540, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61781789-9c1e-5d51-91ea-654c1de98f85'}, {'abstract': 'Also, The Atlantic apologizes for an ad on its Web site that looked like a real article, and Facebook makes a stab at the Web search business ruled by its chief rival, Google.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/16/the-breakfast-meeting-disney-mixes-and-matches-characters-and-the-atlantic-apologizes/', 'snippet': 'Also, The Atlantic apologizes for an ad on its Web site that looked like a real article, and Facebook makes a stab at the Web search business ruled by its chief rival, Google.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York’s new gun law has a provision that restricts access to data about gun owners in the state, Christine Haughney writes in The Times. That component was included in the legislation in response to the publication of names and addresses of gun permit holders in two suburban New York counties by The Journal News, a newspaper based in White Plains, N.Y. The decision to print that information with an accompanying map outraged gun owners across the nation and prompted a backlash against the paper’s employees. Now some journalists are lamenting the loss of data previously available as a reporting tool. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: Gun Data Under Wraps, and Mixing and Matching Disney Characters', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-16T13:36:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editors', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editors'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2adbc612-e6eb-526a-b5a5-5b765e57b8b8', 'word_count': 376, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2adbc612-e6eb-526a-b5a5-5b765e57b8b8'}, {'abstract': 'Exercise can improve your flu shot’s potency, confusion and clarity from tuition calculators, a new awards program for Amtrak riders and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/16/wednesday-reading-improve-your-flu-shots-potency-with-exercise/', 'snippet': 'Exercise can improve your flu shot’s potency, confusion and clarity from tuition calculators, a new awards program for Amtrak riders and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wednesday Reading: Improve Your Flu Shot’s Potency With Exercise', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-16T13:43:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/79cb2529-eee5-5435-8f29-f4c2cdc52074', 'word_count': 113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79cb2529-eee5-5435-8f29-f4c2cdc52074'}, {'abstract': 'Goldman Sachs posts fourth-quarter profit of $2.89 billion. | JPMorgan Chase reports a record profit of $5.7 billion for the fourth quarter. | Goldman’s results may translate into higher bonuses for its employees, but the mood is more dour at Morgan Stanley. | Momentum seems to be growing for a leveraged buyout of Dell.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/01/16/goldman-profit-blows-through-expectations/', 'snippet': 'Goldman Sachs posts fourth-quarter profit of $2.89 billion. | JPMorgan Chase reports a record profit of $5.7 billion for the fourth quarter. | Goldman’s results may translate into higher bonuses for its employees, but the mood is more dour at Morg...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Goldman Sachs on Wednesday reported a fourth-quarter profit of $2.89 billion, or $5.60 a share, well above results in the period a year earlier and handily beating analysts’ expectations of $3.78 a share. The results were buoyed by strong trading and investment banking results. The firm’s conference call is at 10:30 a.m.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Goldman Profit Blows Through Expectations', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-16T13:50:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/43949c56-db98-535a-a7ef-2cfcc4881c58', 'word_count': 1756, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43949c56-db98-535a-a7ef-2cfcc4881c58'}, {'abstract': 'The change calls for deleting the identity numbers and addresses of directors from Hong Kong’s corporate registry starting next year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/17/business/global/hong-kong-takes-a-second-look-at-changes-to-corporate-database.html', 'snippet': 'The change calls for deleting the identity numbers and addresses of directors from Hong Kong’s corporate registry starting next year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — The second-highest official in Hong Kong said Wednesday that the government was reviewing a proposed rule change that had prompted a groundswell of worry among global banks, accounting firms, investors and media companies who fear the loss of a powerful tool against corruption in China.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hong Kong Reconsiders Changes to Corporate Database', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hong Kong Reconsiders Changes to Corporate Database', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hong Kong', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boards of Directors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-16T13:58:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Keith Bradsher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Keith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bradsher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6daa7fda-9ab4-5ff0-8bf8-b1c59cfb741e', 'word_count': 624, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6daa7fda-9ab4-5ff0-8bf8-b1c59cfb741e'}, {'abstract': 'Facebook has spent eight years nudging its users to share everything they like and everything they do, reports Somini Sengupta in Wednesday’s New York Times. Now, the company has unveiled a new tool to help people dig through all that data to find the information they want.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/16/daily-report-facebook-introduces-a-new-search-tool/', 'snippet': 'Facebook has spent eight years nudging its users to share everything they like and everything they do, reports Somini Sengupta in Wednesday’s New York Times. Now, the company has unveiled a new tool to help people dig through all that data to find...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Facebook has spent eight years nudging its users to share everything they like and everything they do, reports Somini Sengupta in Wednesday’s New York Times. Now, the company is betting it has enough data so that people can find whatever they want on Facebook. And on Tuesday, it unveiled an ambitious new tool to help them dig for it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-jumbo-v6.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-superJumbo-v3.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbLarge-v5.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Daily Report: Facebook Introduces a New Search Tool', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search Engines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-16T13:59:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b39938fb-6b2a-5193-945e-f1bd33fc3d8d', 'word_count': 317, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b39938fb-6b2a-5193-945e-f1bd33fc3d8d'}, {'abstract': 'If we’re the same age, why do you look so old?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/16/booming/sexual-myopia-if-youre-my-age-why-do-you-look-so-old.html', 'snippet': 'If we’re the same age, why do you look so old?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every once in a while a male friend in his 60s tells me that try as he might, he just cannot get turned on by women his own age and naturally I channel Cher in “Moonstruck” and let him have it: Snap out of it, I say! Look in the mirror! We all age! What’s more important to you, a woman 30 years younger whom you can show off on the beach or someone who doesn’t draw a blank when you talk about Bullwinkle and Boris Badenov? Not that I have that many conversations in which I need to reference Bullwinkle and Boris Badenov, but when I do I don’t want to have to get bogged down in the whole back story. This is why I know this whole cougar thing is a myth. I do not know any women in their 60s who want a 30-year-old boyfriend because what would they talk about?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/16/booming/16wadler-booming-dybbuk/16wadler-booming-dybbuk-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 682, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/16/booming/16wadler-booming-dybbuk/16wadler-booming-dybbuk-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1365, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/16/booming/16wadler-booming-dybbuk/16wadler-booming-dybbuk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/16/booming/16wadler-booming-dybbuk/16wadler-booming-dybbuk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/16/booming/16wadler-booming-dybbuk/16wadler-booming-dybbuk-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sexual Myopia', 'kicker': 'I Was Misinformed', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Boomers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dating and Courtship', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Age, Chronological', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-16T14:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Booming', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joyce Wadler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joyce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wadler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f2b5c7cf-e19e-529a-80e2-3ff7d2dbebd3', 'word_count': 1186, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f2b5c7cf-e19e-529a-80e2-3ff7d2dbebd3'}, {'abstract': 'The French version of the “Fifty Shades of Grey” trilogy should have flopped. But it hasn’t. Why?', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/16/lumiere-the-french-fifty-shades/', 'snippet': 'The French version of the “Fifty Shades of Grey” trilogy should have flopped. But it hasn’t. Why?', 'lead_paragraph': 'When it comes to erotica and pornography, whether hard, soft, sadomasochistic or merely steamy, the French believe they have done it first, done it better and done it all. So the French version of the “Fifty Shades of Grey” trilogy should have flopped.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lumière | The French Fifty Shades', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Fifty Shades of Grey (Book)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-16T14:00:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elaine Sciolino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elaine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sciolino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f10fba5b-a99a-5a22-b175-fd6e69664545', 'word_count': 1013, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f10fba5b-a99a-5a22-b175-fd6e69664545'}, {'abstract': 'Alison R. Byerly will succeed Daniel H. Weiss as the new president of Lafayette College, a liberal arts institution that was founded in 1826.', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/16/lafayette-selects-its-first-female-president/', 'snippet': 'Alison R. Byerly will succeed Daniel H. Weiss as the new president of Lafayette College, a liberal arts institution that was founded in 1826.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lafayette College has named Alison R. Byerly as its 17th president, making her the first woman to lead the liberal arts institution in Easton, Pa.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/16/education/16thechoice-lafayette/16thechoice-lafayette-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/16/education/16thechoice-lafayette/16thechoice-lafayette-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/16/education/16thechoice-lafayette/16thechoice-lafayette-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/16/education/16thechoice-lafayette/16thechoice-lafayette-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/16/education/16thechoice-lafayette/16thechoice-lafayette-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lafayette Selects Its First Female President', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weiss, Daniel H', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Haverford College', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lafayette College', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Middlebury College', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-16T14:01:16+0000', 'document_type':