thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/16/blogs/16rdv-planes/16rdv-planes-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/16/blogs/16rdv-planes/16rdv-planes-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Will Boeing’s Problems Benefit Its European Rival?', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AIRBUS INDUSTRIE', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boeing Company', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Toulouse (France)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-16T14:16:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Morris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/60552c77-0f01-55ce-81e7-17dd9d46d10d', 'word_count': 453, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60552c77-0f01-55ce-81e7-17dd9d46d10d'}, {'abstract': 'The leader in handing out nifty stuff at the Detroit auto show is usually Scion, which in the past has offered hats, sunglasses and key chains. This year it had cloth sleeves for your gadgets and a Scion-branded baseball cap.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/16/trinkets-and-doodads-for-those-who-are-just-looking/', 'snippet': 'The leader in handing out nifty stuff at the Detroit auto show is usually Scion, which in the past has offered hats, sunglasses and key chains. This year it had cloth sleeves for your gadgets and a Scion-branded baseball cap.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Seeing all the new cars may be the reason automotive journalists from all over the world gather at the Detroit auto show during press days at the Cobo Center, but part of the fun is also seeing what tchotchkes the automakers hand out on the show floor. The new Corvette Stingray is important and all, but wasn’t that a really cool paperweight Chevy handed out along with the press materials about the car? They went fast.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trinkets and Doodads for Those Who Are Just Looking', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'North American International Auto Show', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chevrolet Division of General Motors Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'eBay Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jeep Division of Chrysler', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-16T14:21:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Schembari', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schembari', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1b48a88-174d-5ba7-8103-6a82f1f4f2ab', 'word_count': 260, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1b48a88-174d-5ba7-8103-6a82f1f4f2ab'}, {'abstract': 'Sportswriters ponder the possibilities of Lance Armstrong’s confessional interview with Oprah Winfrey.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/17/sports/channeling-lance-armstrong-leading-off.html', 'snippet': 'Sportswriters ponder the possibilities of Lance Armstrong’s confessional interview with Oprah Winfrey.', 'lead_paragraph': 'O.K., so you find yourself with another day to kill while frantically searching your on-screen cable TV guide looking for the Oprah Winfrey Network — Honey, you sure it isn’t the Alerta TV network? I found that in the 400s. Halogen TV, maybe? — and you’ve decided to wonder whether you will be sick of Lance Armstrong’s big staged confession before it even starts. This is a distinct possibility. After all, Winfrey has already done interviews about the interview (sigh), let people know Armstrong will not come off as contrite (eye roll) and will quite likely try to paint cycling’s leadership as the truly bad guys (stomach churn). Winfrey’s network helped exactly nothing by deciding to drag the thing over two nights, so you can be doubly preannoyed at the whole sideshow.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Channeling Armstrong', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ARMSTRONG, LANCE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winfrey, Oprah', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Francona, Terry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zetterberg, Henrik', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bicycles and Bicycling', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-16T14:28:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b08839da-0c07-5976-bd52-99ebb9a09f0d', 'word_count': 682, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b08839da-0c07-5976-bd52-99ebb9a09f0d'}, {'abstract': 'In a 129-page report attached to its quarterly earnings on Wednesday, JPMorgan Chase dissected the trading loss of more than $6 billion at its chief investment office, outlining a breakdown at the highest levels of management and “remedial” steps it has since taken.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/01/16/jpmorgan-report-on-trading-loss-takes-aim-at-top-executives/', 'snippet': 'In a 129-page report attached to its quarterly earnings on Wednesday, JPMorgan Chase dissected the trading loss of more than $6 billion at its chief investment office, outlining a breakdown at the highest levels of management and “remedial” steps ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The bad bet that cost JPMorgan Chase more than $6 billion has already provoked scrutiny from regulators and federal agents. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'JPMorgan Report on Trading Loss Takes Aim at Top Executives', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-16T14:37:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8581a26a-aa5f-5a00-9795-e9ca4fe547a5', 'word_count': 1064, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8581a26a-aa5f-5a00-9795-e9ca4fe547a5'}, {'abstract': 'Lower costs helped the airline, which is operating under bankruptcy court protection, post a profit, compared with a loss a year ago.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/17/business/american-air-reports-a-profit.html', 'snippet': 'Lower costs helped the airline, which is operating under bankruptcy court protection, post a profit, compared with a loss a year ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'American Airlines, which is in the final stages of bankruptcy and under pressure from US Airways to merge, on Wednesday reported a fourth-quarter profit mostly because of lower costs and some reorganization credits.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/business/American/American-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/business/American/American-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'American Airlines Reports a Thin Profit', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'American Airlines Reports a Thin Profit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN AIRLINES', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMR CORP', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-16T14:41:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jad Mouawad', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mouawad', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/87489845-827c-5c1d-9027-cb1665af3a65', 'word_count': 427, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87489845-827c-5c1d-9027-cb1665af3a65'}, {'abstract': 'The job action stems from an attempt by New York City to reform one of the most inefficient transportation systems in the country, which costs almost $7,000 a year for each passenger.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/17/nyregion/new-york-school-bus-drivers-go-on-strike.html', 'snippet': 'The job action stems from an attempt by New York City to reform one of the most inefficient transportation systems in the country, which costs almost $7,000 a year for each passenger.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The day before the start of New York City’s first school bus strike in 34 years, a long yellow bus pulled up at Public School 282 in Park Slope, Brooklyn, and the little bodies that popped out could be counted on one hand: Three. The big bus had dropped off part of its cargo earlier, at another school, but in all, 10 children had ridden on a bus fit for about 60.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/nyregion/STRIKE1/STRIKE1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/17/nyregion/STRIKE1/STRIKE1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/nyregion/STRIKE1/STRIKE1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 687, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/nyregion/STRIKE1/STRIKE1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1373, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/nyregion/STRIKE1/STRIKE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/17/nyregion/STRIKE1/STRIKE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/nyregion/STRIKE1/STRIKE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At Strike’s Root, Runaway Costs In Busing Pupils', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At Strike&#8217;s Root, Runaway Costs In Busing Pupils', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Strikes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buses', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Department (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMALGAMATED TRANSIT UNION', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-16T14:44:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Al Baker and Marc Santora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Al', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99252527-6a22-52cd-9dd1-31cc7c94dca6', 'word_count': 1565, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99252527-6a22-52cd-9dd1-31cc7c94dca6'}, {'abstract': 'A new change in rules for the best documentary Oscar may dramatically affect the outcome.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/16/another-change-in-the-documentary-oscar-rules/', 'snippet': 'A new change in rules for the best documentary Oscar may dramatically affect the outcome.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While everyone was busy prepartying and donating money, the Academy quietly announced a major rule change to its members. As GoldDerby.com reports, an e-mail\xa0 on Saturday informed voters that choosing the best documentary, best animated short and best live-action short would no longer be such exclusive affairs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Change in the Oscar Rules for Documentaries', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-16T15:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/087976f6-0a98-5c40-8501-eec5ef76ac5f', 'word_count': 206, 'uri': 'nyt://article/087976f6-0a98-5c40-8501-eec5ef76ac5f'}, {'abstract': 'A once-forlorn zone near the Berlin Wall holds the promise of Germany’s tech industry.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/16/tech-innovation-in-berlin/', 'snippet': 'A once-forlorn zone near the Berlin Wall holds the promise of Germany’s tech industry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — Travis Todd, an American tech entrepreneur, pointed at the snow-covered construction site behind his shared office. Twenty-five years ago, East German border guards would have gunned down anyone caught in the restricted zone along the Berlin Wall. Today, Google and other investors are turning an abandoned brewery in the “death strip” into a technology campus.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From Death Strip to Tech Campus', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venture Capital', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Berlin (Germany)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-16T15:03:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lucian Kim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lucian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6f38f6a-34a5-5f68-a7cf-5a4bf50053e4', 'word_count': 612, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6f38f6a-34a5-5f68-a7cf-5a4bf50053e4'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/16/what-were-reading-608/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Food & Wine: Scarlett Johansson wishes she could have raw oysters with Bette Davis. — Jeff Gordinier ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-16T15:16:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a550712a-8be9-5378-9580-77fd8ebbadf3', 'word_count': 451, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a550712a-8be9-5378-9580-77fd8ebbadf3'}, {'abstract': 'The Lede is following the debate on gun violence in the wake of the shootings in Newtown, Conn., with reports from our correspondents and from around the Web.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/16/updates-on-the-gun-violence-debate-5/', 'snippet': 'The Lede is following the debate on gun violence in the wake of the shootings in Newtown, Conn., with reports from our correspondents and from around the Web.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Lede is following the debate on gun violence in the wake of the shootings in Newtown, Conn., with reports from our correspondents and from around the Web. On Wednesday, President Obama announced a push for new laws to restrict the availability of guns and to embrace a series of executive actions that he can take without seeking congressional approval.  ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jan. 16 Updates on the Gun Violence Debate', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newtown, Conn, Shooting (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-16T15:35:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f6470a5-ed6c-5060-9266-a98474535056', 'word_count': 6649, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f6470a5-ed6c-5060-9266-a98474535056'}, {'abstract': 'Some of those arrested, on charges including racketeering and extortion, had ties to the Genovese, Gambino and Luchese crime families, an official said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/17/nyregion/fbi-arrests-nearly-30-with-ties-to-waste-industry.html', 'snippet': 'Some of those arrested, on charges including racketeering and extortion, had ties to the Genovese, Gambino and Luchese crime families, an official said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the annals of organized crime and extortion, there is no end to the victims and their suffering, from movie stars and Wall Street brokers to truck drivers and small businessmen.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/nyregion/CARTING/CARTING-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/17/nyregion/CARTING/CARTING-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/nyregion/CARTING/CARTING-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/nyregion/CARTING/CARTING-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/nyregion/CARTING/CARTING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/17/nyregion/CARTING/CARTING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/nyregion/CARTING/CARTING-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150