h': 'ROME — The dark, double-breasted suits have long been a mainstay, but now former Prime Minister Silvio Berlusconi has taken to wearing the occasional fedora. It lends him a rakish, retro air as he embarks on what many Italians, foreign investors and no doubt Chancellor Angela Merkel of Germany hoped would never happen: another election campaign. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/world/berlusconi/berlusconi-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 658, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/world/berlusconi/berlusconi-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1315, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/world/berlusconi/berlusconi-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/17/world/berlusconi/berlusconi-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/world/berlusconi/berlusconi-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Insider’s Insider Returns to Politics, This Time as an Outsider', 'kicker': 'Memo from Rome', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Insider’s Insider Returns to Politics, This Time as an Outsider', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Donadio, Rachel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berlusconi, Silvio', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merkel, Angela', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-16T15:53:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Donadio', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Donadio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf1fc8b5-ad9e-59ca-afa4-47822d78637b', 'word_count': 1118, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf1fc8b5-ad9e-59ca-afa4-47822d78637b'}, {'abstract': 'The musical satire about reality television and its shameless contestants is set at a dating competition show also called “Nobody Loves You.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/16/second-stage-theater-adds-nobody-loves-you/', 'snippet': 'The musical satire about reality television and its shameless contestants is set at a dating competition show also called “Nobody Loves You.”', 'lead_paragraph': '“Nobody Loves You,” a musical satire about reality television and its shameless contestants, will be the final production in the 2012-13 season at Second Stage Theater, the company said on Wednesday. The musical — which features a book by Itamar Moses (the playwright of “The Four of Us” and a writer for television’s “Boardwalk Empire”), music by Gaby Alter, lyrics by Mr. Moses and Mr. Alter and choreography by Mandy Moore (of television’s “So You Think You Can Dance”) — chronicles a young man who competes on a fictional reality show (also called “Nobody Loves You”) in hopes of regaining a lost girlfriend and of exposing the contrivances of the show.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'cr