'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Solomon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Solomon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/01abee45-24d7-57ba-90e6-b1c30dc6c9c2', 'word_count': 1179, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01abee45-24d7-57ba-90e6-b1c30dc6c9c2'}, {'abstract': 'If the four North American premieres that made up this year’s Contemporary Dance Showcase at Japan Society had anything in common, it was highly active lighting design.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/17/arts/dance/contemporary-dance-showcase-at-japan-society.html', 'snippet': 'If the four North American premieres that made up this year’s Contemporary Dance Showcase at Japan Society had anything in common, it was highly active lighting design.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last weekend Japan Society presented its 15th annual contemporary dance showcase and once again opened a window onto the East Asian scene. The series’s artistic director, Yoko Shioya, remarked that the Internet has made that scene more easily accessible. She also said that her focus has shifted from new companies to new works, since so many dancers and choreographers are now freelancers and eager to collaborate with artists outside dance. Sounds like New York.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/16/arts/showcase/showcase-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/16/arts/showcase/showcase-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/16/arts/showcase/showcase-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 667, 'wi