 their annual retreat this week. As a sign of my good intentions, I am not going to make any jokes involving Custer and Little Bighorn.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Latest in Anti-Politics', 'kicker': 'The Conversation', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'York, Byron', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-16T18:05:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Brooks and Gail Collins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Gail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/40c8e470-e89a-51c5-8737-dba1f179c88e', 'word_count': 1114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40c8e470-e89a-51c5-8737-dba1f179c88e'}, {'abstract': 'A closer look at social insurance and entitlement programs reveals some surprises about where government spending is —\xa0and isn’t — increasing.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/16/what-is-driving-growth-in-government-spending/', 'snippet': 'A closer look at social insurance and entitlement programs reveals some surprises about where government spending is —\xa0and isn’t — increasing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s one of the most fundamental political questions of our time: What’s driving the growth in government spending? And it has a relatively straightforward answer: first and foremost, spending on health care through Medicare and Medicaid, and other major social insurance and entitlement programs.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Is Driving Growth in Government Spending?', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Health Care Drives Increase in Government Spending', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-16T18:06:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/abe250ae-f4f0-5941-a5a8-3949e11450d9', 'word_count': 2137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/abe250ae-f4f0-5941-a5a8-3949e11450d9'}, {'abstract': 'Howard Beck, the N.B.A. reporter for The Times, will answer questions from readers.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/16/have-an-n-b-a-question-howard-beck-has-answers/', 'snippet': 'Howard Beck, the N.B.A. reporter for The Times, will answer questions from readers.', 'lead_paragraph': '3:56 p.m. | Updated What has happened to the Mavericks? Are the Nets good enough to go beyond the first round of the playoffs? Can the Lakers be repaired? Howard Beck, the N.B.A. reporter for The Times, will answer questions from readers about the season. Use the comment field below for your questions. Answers will appear next week on Off the Dribble.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Have an N.B.A. Question? Howard Beck Has Answers', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beck, Howard', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-16T18:06:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5bc784be-7bb5-5a3c-b078-e461bf7d2bea', 'word_count': 68, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5bc784be-7bb5-5a3c-b078-e461bf7d2bea'}, {'abstract': 'Idina Menzel performed at Carnegie Hall on Sunday night, accompanied by the Orchestra of St. Lukes under the direction of Rod Mounsey.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/17/arts/music/idina-menzel-at-carnegie-hall.html', 'snippet': 'Idina Menzel performed at Carnegie Hall on Sunday night, accompanied by the Orchestra of St. Lukes under the direction of Rod Mounsey.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nearly a decade has passed since Idina Menzel introduced her signature song, the Stephen Schwartz anthem “Defying Gravity” in the 2003 Broadway smash “Wicked.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/16/arts/idina/idina-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/16/arts/idina/idina-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type':