rticle', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judy Battista', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Battista', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e18f5779-98a9-50d3-a5b8-8d57bd24d4cd', 'word_count': 648, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e18f5779-98a9-50d3-a5b8-8d57bd24d4cd'}, {'abstract': 'An iPhone app, “Banker’s Bonus 2013,” allows a banker (or really anyone) to enter a bonus amount and see how it ranks among others around the world.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/01/16/comparing-wall-st-bonuses-theres-an-app-for-that/', 'snippet': 'An iPhone app, “Banker’s Bonus 2013,” allows a banker (or really anyone) to enter a bonus amount and see how it ranks among others around the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s a ritual as old as Wall Street. Come bonus time, employees furtively compare their pay to see how they measure up.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Comparing Wall St. Bonuses? There’s an App for That', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bonuses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-16T18:21:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/264bd97e-5115-57ba-ab3e-0e0e8af5f88d', 'word_count': 220, 'uri': 'nyt://article/264bd97e-5115-57ba-ab3e-0e0e8af5f88d'}, {'abstract': 'The cable channel scrapped the show, which was in development, after the promotion of an online petition that condemned Oxygen, accusing it of exploiting and stereotyping black children and families.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/16/oxygen-drops-plans-for-all-my-babies-mamas/', 'snippet': 'The cable channel scrapped the show, which was in development, after the promotion of an online petition that condemned Oxygen, accusing it of exploiting and stereotyping black children and families.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The cable channel Oxygen has scrapped a show in development called “All My Babies’ Mamas” after the promotion of an online petition that condemned the channel, accusing it of exploiting and stereotyping black children and families.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Oxygen Drops Plans for ‘All My Babies’ Mamas’', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Oxygen Kills a Show After Racism Criticism', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cable Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oxygen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Comcast Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philadelphia (Pa)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-16T18:23:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c213f684-df96-5b00-b007-0c6e8f4fd632', 'word_count': 421, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c213f684-df96-5b00-b007-0c6e8f4fd632'}, {'abstract': 'An analysis of the incoming freshman class of the 113th Congress belies the Little Guy image. The 94 new lawmakers boast a median net worth of $1,066,515 — almost exactly $1 million more than the wealth of a typical American household.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/16/incoming-members-of-congress-not-exactly-average-joes/', 'snippet': 'An analysis of the incoming freshman class of the 113th Congress belies the Little Guy image. The 94 new lawmakers boast a median net worth of $1,066,515 — almost exactly $1 million more than the wealth of a typical American household.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the rise of the Tea Party movement, the image of Average Joe Citizen taking over Congress has captured the media’s imagination, from rural northern Florida, which sent a large-animal veterinarian, Ted Yoho, to the House, to eastern Michigan, which elected a reindeer farmer and Santa Claus impersonator, Kerry Bentivolio.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Incoming Members of Congress Not Exactly Average Joes', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tea Party Movement', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Delaney, John', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Issa, Darrell E', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kerry, John', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Polis, Jared', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Warner, Mark R', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yoho, Ted', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-16T18:38:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Weisman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weisman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5c48118-4170-5441-87ce-85c130e5db81', 'word_count': 398, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5c48118-4170-5441-87ce-85c130e5db81'}, {'abstract': 'The Presidential Inaugural Committee held a news conference at the National Press Club Wednesday to preview this weekend’s festivities.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/16/inaugural-committee-previews-weekends-festivities/', 'snippet': 'The Presidential Inaugural Committee held a news conference at the National Press Club Wednesday to preview this weekend’s festivities.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I love the idea of any show that begins with Chuck Schumer and ends with Beyoncé.” — Brent Colburn, communications director for President Obama’s inaugural committee, describing Monday’s swearing in ceremony on the west front of the Capitol. Senator Charles E. Schumer, the New York Democrat, will make remarks opening the ceremony and Beyoncé will sing the national anthem at the end. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Inaugural Committee Previews Weekend’s Festivities', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-16T18:46:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sheryl Gay Stolberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sheryl', 'middlename': 'Gay', 'lastname': 'Stolberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0fe7eef6-9cbb-5ca6-ad59-8169f21b5195', 'word_count': 246, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0fe7eef6-9cbb-5ca6-ad59-8169f21b5195'}, {'abstract': 'The Colombian-born Andrés Orozco-Estrada, 35, will become music director of the Houston Symphony in 2014.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/16/south-american-maestro-to-the-houston-symphony/', 'snippet': 'The Colombian-born Andrés Orozco-Estrada, 35, will become music director of the Houston Symphony in 2014.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Houston Symphony on Wednesday named the Colombian-born Andrés Orozco-Estrada as its next music director. Mr. Orozco-Estrada, 35, will begin conducting the orchestra regularly next season and take over officially with a five-year contract in the 2014-15 season.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Houston Symphony Chooses New Maestro', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Graf, Hans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Orozco-Estrada, Andres', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Houston Symphony Orchestra', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-16T18:48:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/793473d6-1d47-56a2-8172-d8de26617ec2', 'word_count': 89, 'uri': 'nyt://article/793473d6-1d47-56a2-8172-d8de26617ec2'}, {'abstract': 'Parsons Dance presented works by David Parsons, the company’s artistic director, and Katarzyna Skarpetowska at the Joyce Theater.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/17/arts/dance/works-by-david-parsons-and-katarzyna-skarpetowska.html', 'snippet': 'Parsons Dance presented works by David Parsons, the company’s artistic director, and Katarzyna Skarpetowska at the Joyce Theater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Parsons Dance returned to the Joyce Theater on Tuesday with works by the choreographer David Parsons, including his new “Dawn to Dusk,” as well as a commission by a former company member, Katarzyna Skarpetowska. Each serve watered-down versions of dances by master choreographers: Mr. Parsons, as usual, draws from Paul Taylor, with whom he danced. Ms. Skarpetowska, at least in her new “Black Flowers,” channels Martha Graham.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Breath of Florida, Alligators Included', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Breath of Florida, Alligators Included', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Joyce Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parsons, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-16T18:51:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5fa2a581-b971-53a2-92d1-52a4dde33ef1', 'word_count': 474, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5fa2a581-b971-53a2-92d1-52a4dde33ef1'}, {'abstract': '“It’s not necessarily about one person and four wheels being bad,” said the show’s curator, Christina de Roos of Spread Art. “It’s about the environmental consequences of the automobile and the things that come from a heavy car culture.”', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/16/anti-auto-show-focusing-on-alternative-transportation/', 'snippet': '“It’s not necessarily about one person and four wheels being bad,” said the show’s curator, Christina de Roos of Spread Art. “It’s about the environmental consequences of the automobile and the things that come from a heavy car culture.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'DETROIT — The North American International Anti-Auto Show, an art exhibition timed around the show at the Cobo Center, opens Friday night with a black-tie preview at the Contemporary Art Institute of Detroit. Admission is $1 to the green carpet event, where anti-auto show girls will unveil some of the artwork from 14 artists highlighting alternative transportation-based themes. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Anti-Auto Show Focusing on Alternative Transportation', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'North American International Auto Show', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-16T18:57:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tamara Warren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tamara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Warren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/da294916-ebfd-5ff2-ad35-b11a4e507444', 'word_count': 441, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da294916-ebfd-5ff2-ad35-b11a4e507444'}, {'abstract': 'Dieter Roth’s works live on as a family business.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2013/01/20/arts/d