ling” closed after four performances, leaving behind a memorable pan from Clive Barnes of The New York Times. “There is nothing much wrong” with the show, he wrote, “that a new book, new music, new lyrics, new settings, new direction, new choreography and a partially new cast would not quite possibly put right.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/theater/17fig-web/17fig-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 240, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/17/theater/17fig-web/17fig-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 240}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/theater/17fig-web/17fig-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 409, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/theater/17fig-web/17fig-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/theater/17fig-web/17fig-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/17/theater/17fig-web/17fig-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/theater/17fig-web/17fig-web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'By the Fadduh of ’60s Parodies', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None,