On Snowy Slopes, Fingers Glide Down the Touch Screen', 'kicker': 'App Smart', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On Snowy Slopes, Fingers Glide Down the Touch Screen', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skiing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eaton, Kit', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALPINE SKIING', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-16T22:34:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kit Eaton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kit', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eaton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/58e882c9-56fc-5bfa-9c31-c49b9b334cd3', 'word_count': 760, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58e882c9-56fc-5bfa-9c31-c49b9b334cd3'}, {'abstract': '“Seagull (Thinking of you)” is a play that blurs boundaries: between actors and their roles, male and female, fiction and reality, past and present, parody and sincerity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/17/theater/reviews/seagull-thinking-of-you-at-new-ohio-theater.html', 'snippet': '“Seagull (Thinking of you)” is a play that blurs boundaries: between actors and their roles, male and female, fiction and reality, past and present, parody and sincerity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Remember those much-parodied Calvin Klein fragrance commercials that Richard Avedon did in the mid-1980s? The ones with glamorous, sexually ambiguous young creatures in stark rooms, striking languorous poses and speaking enigmatic nonsense? Well, that’s kind of what Tina Satter’s “Seagull (Thinking of you),” part of Performance Space 122’s Coil Festival, feels like, at least at first.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5'