], 'headline': {'main': 'A Snub by Oscars? Affleck Has an Answer', 'kicker': 'The Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Snub By Oscars? Affleck Has An Answer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'AFFLECK, BEN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Argo (Movie)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-16T22:39:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'subsection_name': 'Awards Season', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a5eb179-d650-50c1-98b8-3bbff05a7e40', 'word_count': 1123, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a5eb179-d650-50c1-98b8-3bbff05a7e40'}, {'abstract': 'The New York City Ballet opened its winter season on Tuesday night with a Balanchine-Tchaikovsky triple bill.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/17/arts/dance/new-york-city-ballet-at-the-koch-theater.html', 'snippet': 'The New York City Ballet opened its winter season on Tuesday night with a Balanchine-Tchaikovsky triple bill.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Peter Martins will soon reach his 30th anniversary as ballet master in chief of New York City Ballet. The company’s schedule for the whole 2012-13 season reads as a statement of what Mr. Martins believes matters most to its identity. The fall season concentrated on the series of Stravinsky ballets that was the most celebrated and radical part of the founder and choreographer George Balanchine’s work; the current season, through Feb. 24, celebrates Balanchine’s no less important Tchaikovsky ballets (following the six-week season of “George Balanchine’s The Nutcracker,” a core ballet for reasons apart from its popularity). And the spring season will focus on Mr. Martins’s own ballets. Premieres by both Justin Peck and Christopher Wheeldon are spaced over months. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/arts/SERANADE/SERANADE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/17/arts/SERANADE/SERANADE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/arts/SERANADE/SERANADE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/arts/SERANADE/SERANADE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1153, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/arts/SERANADE/SERANADE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/17/arts/SERANADE/SERANADE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/arts/SERANADE/SERANADE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Letting Dance Carry Music: Balanchine Put Tchaikovsky in Perspective', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Letting Dance Carry Music: Balanchine Put Tchaikovsky in Per