'nyt://article/f0b0bdba-390c-5e06-9f41-3d970f954182', 'word_count': 484, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0b0bdba-390c-5e06-9f41-3d970f954182'}, {'abstract': 'A show of stained glass by Brian Clarke opens this week at Pace in Chelsea.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/17/garden/qa-with-brian-clarke-stained-glass-artist.html', 'snippet': 'A show of stained glass by Brian Clarke opens this week at Pace in Chelsea.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Brian Clarke, 59, a stained-glass artist, will present more than 50 works in “Between Extremities,” a show that opens Thursday at one of the Pace galleries in Chelsea. Mr. Clarke’s glass can be found in chapels, mosques and synagogues, but also in corporate headquarters and shopping centers. He has collaborated with architects including Renzo Piano, Zaha Hadid and Norman Foster. Born in the north of England to a coal miner father and a mother who worked in a cotton mill, he lives in London.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/garden/17QNA1_SPAN/17QNA1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/17/garden/17QNA1_SPAN/17QNA1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/garden/17QNA1_SPAN/17QNA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 745, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/garden/17QNA1_SPAN/17QNA1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1490, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/garde