he Jewish terrorist,” Yaakov (Jack) Teitel was also convicted of other crimes, including bombings in 2008 that wounded a leftist Israeli professor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Jerusalem court on Wednesday convicted an American immigrant who lived in a West Bank settlement of killing two Palestinians in 1997. Known as “the Jewish terrorist,” Yaakov (Jack) Teitel was also convicted of other crimes, including bombings in 2008 that wounded a leftist Israeli professor and a teenage boy belonging to a community of Jews who believe in Jesus. Sentencing is planned for February. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Israel: U.S. Immigrant Convicted in Palestinian Deaths', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Israel: U.S. Immigrant Convicted in Palestinian Deaths', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Teitel, Yaakov', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-17T03:29:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Kershner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/49761c24-4ba6-5d35-b9f1-8e09c015ceec', 'word_count': 65, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49761c24-4ba6-5d35-b9f1-8e09c015ceec'}, {'abstract': 'The Nets, winners of seven straight games, were red hot, and the Hawks, playing without their leading scorer, were stone cold, but Wednesday’s game in Atlanta saw a reversal of fortune.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/17/sports/basketball/nets-fall-to-hawks-in-atlanta.html', 'snippet': 'The Nets, winners of seven straight games, were red hot, and the Hawks, playing without their leading scorer, were stone cold, but Wednesday’s game in Atlanta saw a reversal of fortune.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATLANTA — The Nets’ seven-game winning streak came to a thudding end Wednesday night when they were run off the Philips Arena floor, 109-95, by an energetic Hawks team missing its best player.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/sports/SUB-NETS/SUB-NETS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 811, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/sports/SUB-NETS/SUB-NETS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1621, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/sports/SUB-NETS/SUB-NETS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/17/sports/SUB-NETS/SUB-NETS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/sports/SUB-NETS/SUB-NETS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'About-Face as Slumping Hawks Crush Sizzling Nets', 'kicker': 'Hawks 109, Nets 95', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'About-Face as Slumping Hawks Crush Sizzling Nets'