cle/b3243f6d-b278-5ad1-a008-f10b7da957c3', 'word_count': 533, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3243f6d-b278-5ad1-a008-f10b7da957c3'}, {'abstract': 'Contradicting early French reports, officials said French forces had been involved in direct ground combat since just after landing last week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/18/world/africa/france-mali-intervention.html', 'snippet': 'Contradicting early French reports, officials said French forces had been involved in direct ground combat since just after landing last week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BAMAKO, Mali — French soldiers have battled Islamist militants in direct clashes on the ground in central Mali since just after landing last week, according to officials, and fighting continued\xa0on Thursday as hundreds of French reinforcements arrived. The ground battles expanded the campaign against the militants, who have seized much of the nation, beyond the airstrikes used initially.\xa0', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/18/world/18mali_image/18mali_image-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/18/world/18mali_image/18mali_image-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/18/world/18mali_image/18mali_image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/18/world/18mali_image/18mali_image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/18/world/18mali_image/18mali_image-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'France Sends Reinforcements to Confront Islamist Forces in Mali', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On the Ground in Mali, France Sends Reinforcements to Confront Islamist Forces', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mali', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-17T11:32:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Nossiter, Neil MacFarquhar and Alan Cowell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nossiter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacFarquhar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/53fbf9be-9a46-5670-bf06-c913bee8ca26', 'word_count': 711, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53fbf9be-9a46-5670-bf06-c913bee8ca26'}, {'abstract': 'A defendant accused of insulting Thailand’s king was punished not only for what he said during a speech, but also for making a gesture of being muzzled.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/18/world/asia/in-thailand-a-broader-definition-of-insulting-royalty.html', 'snippet': 'A defendant accused of insulting Thailand’s king was punished not only for what he said during a speech, but also for making a gesture of being muzzled.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BANGKOK — It has become almost routine in Thailand for judges to hand down jail sentences to those convicted of offending the country’s king. But an unusual ruling issued on Thursday appears to considerably broaden the interpretation of Thailand’s already restrictive lèse-majesté law.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Thailand, a Broader Definition of Insulting Royalty', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Thai’s Gesture Spoke Volumes Against King, Court Rules', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fuller, Thomas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Royal Family', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Thailand', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bhumibol Adulyadej', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chuklom, Yossawarit', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-17T11:42:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Fuller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fuller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b71a9df-1fb8-56d4-a71b-3a763ba5e087', 'word_count': 611, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b71a9df-1fb8-56d4-a71b-3a763ba5e087'}, {'abstract': 'Portland’s karaoke scene includes strippers, muppets and every song you can dream of. Can a city be having a pop-music moment if all everyone’s doing is singing along?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/20/magazine/portland-karaoke-scene.html', 'snippet': 'Portland’s karaoke scene includes strippers, muppets and every song you can dream of. Can a city be having a pop-music moment if all everyone’s doing is singing along?', 'lead_paragraph': 'John Brophy, the mastermind of America’s greatest karaoke night, lives in a well-kept bungalow in a neighborhood of small homes in southeast Portland, Ore. When I visited on a weekday afternoon last spring, Brophy, then 36, wore a ringer T-shirt and dark jeans. His wrist was encircled by a half-dozen bracelets, and his dark hair swooped in front of his face. Like many Portlanders, he’s in a band, called Gingerbread Patriots, although currently the band is on hiatus — the “Shows” section of the Gingerbread Patriots Web site is empty but for the words “2009 will bring shows shows and more shows!”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/magazine/20Karaoke1/20Karaoke1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/20/magazine/20Karaoke1/20Karaoke1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/magazine/20Karaoke1/20Karaoke1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/magazine/20Karaoke1/20Karaoke1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/magazine/20Karaoke1/20Karaoke1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/20/magazine/20Karaoke1/20Karaoke1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/magazine/20Karaoke1/20Karaoke1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Good Does Karaoke Have to Be to Qualify as Art?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Karaokia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Karaoke', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kois, Dan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Portland (Ore)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baby Ketten Karaoke', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-17T12:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Kois', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kois', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb7e2ddd-5949-52e5-91a4-4d23f35bd456', 'word_count': 3718, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb7e2ddd-5949-52e5-91a4-4d23f35bd456'}, {'abstract': 'In Portland, I visited karaoke nights at tiki bars, strip clubs, comedy clubs, honky-tonks and pizza places. These are the songs I sang.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/17/what-i-sang-on-my-epic-karaoke-odyssey/', 'snippet': 'In Portland, I visited karaoke nights at tiki bars, strip clubs, comedy clubs, honky-tonks and pizza places. These are the songs I sang.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For this weekend’s magazine, I wrote about my epic six-day karaoke odyssey in Portland, Ore., hoping to figure out why this city’s karaoke scene is so ridiculously vibrant. I visited karaoke nights at tiki bars, strip clubs, comedy clubs, honky-tonks and pizza places, interviewing K.J.s (karaoke jocks), fans, strippers and Portland’s mayor. But I also, of course, sang. A lot.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What I Sang on My Epic Karaoke Odyssey', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Karaoke', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Portland (Ore)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-17T12:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Kois', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kois', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b46ee10-4b28-5b6f-a709-f66c609645cb', 'word_count': 169, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b46ee10-4b28-5b6f-a709-f66c609645cb'}, {'abstract': 'A commercial on ABC would have cost TerraCycle hundreds of thousands of dollars and only given it 30 seconds of exposure. Instead, the company got more than three minutes, twice in one month. But at what cost?', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/17/maybe-there-is-such-a-thing-as-bad-publicity/', 'snippet': 'A commercial on ABC would have cost TerraCycle hundreds of thousands of dollars and only given it 30 seconds of exposure. Instead, the company got more than three minutes, twice in one month. But at what cost?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In part because we are a social enterprise with a mission that most people support\xa0— keeping waste out of landfills and incinerators\xa0— TerraCycle has been blessed with a lot of good publicity. In fact, we talk about having what we call a “negative-cost” media department that in 2012 generated more than 4,500 articles around the world. That’s more than 12 articles per day! (You can see an example of this coverage here.) We call the department negative-cost because we have been able to produce marketing\xa0— books, TV shows\xa0— that earns us money while also promoting the company.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Maybe There Is Such a Thing as Bad Publicity', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Relations and Publicity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TerraCycle', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-17T12:00:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Szaky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Szaky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5dfa5470-4dc8-5341-b404-b44e8ca20b32', 'word_count': 555, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5dfa5470-4dc8-5341-b404-b44e8ca20b32'}, {'abstract': 'A tender, rosy roast beef — a good excuse for more Henry Bain sauce.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/20/magazine/when-the-steak-sauce-makes-the-meat.html', 'snippet': 'A tender, rosy roast beef — a good excuse for more Henry Bain sauce.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Pendennis Club in Louisville, Ky., is a big Georgian pile that might have appeared in the Thackeray novel it was named for, full of wealthy afternoon nappers and drawling black-tie gentry. In the early part of the last century, the club’s headwaiter was a black man named Henry Bain. His contribution to the world was at least as important as the newspapers and racehorses, banks and bridges sired by the white club members he 