sion from the occupation, or any other body.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Countersettlement', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Israeli Settlements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Palestinian Authority', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Bank', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-17T12:12:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Raja Shehadeh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Raja', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shehadeh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/322f8f79-a609-5c14-a1fe-c4958afffd3c', 'word_count': 712, 'uri': 'nyt://article/322f8f79-a609-5c14-a1fe-c4958afffd3c'}, {'abstract': 'Does interest on reserves change anything fundamental?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/17/all-your-base-are-belong-to-us-what-is-the-question/', 'snippet': 'Does interest on reserves change anything fundamental?', 'lead_paragraph': 'OK, we are indeed, as Steve Randy Waldman says, all dorks, and so are you if you are reading this. What’s more, we’re inarticulate dorks, or so it seems.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'All Your Base Are Belong To Us: What Is the Question?', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-17T12:12:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', '