arter profit. | The move by JPMorgan’s board to cut Jamie Dimon’s pay was intended as a message for regulators and investors. | Rio Tinto takes a $14 billion write-down and its chief steps down. | A group weighing a buyout of Dell is said to be approaching a financing goal.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/01/17/mortgage-woes-weigh-on-bank-of-america/', 'snippet': 'Bank of America posts a 63 percent drop in fourth-quarter profit. | The move by JPMorgan’s board to cut Jamie Dimon’s pay was intended as a message for regulators and investors. | Rio Tinto takes a $14 billion write-down and its chief steps down. ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bank of America continues to work through mortgage woes stemming from its acquisition of Countrywide Financial. The bank reported a widely expected 63 percent drop in fourth-quarter profit after settling claims over its mortgage business. The earnings of $732 million amounted to 3 cents a share, narrowly beating estimates of 2 cents a share, based on analysts surveyed by Thomson Reuters. The bank’s quarterly revenue was down about 25 percent, to $18.7 billion. The conference call is scheduled for 8:30 a.m.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mortgage Woes Weigh on Bank of America', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-17T13:54:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d757809-dcae-501d-b7b6-6edcc044facf', 'word_count': 1842, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d757809-dcae-501d-b7b6-6edcc044facf'}, {'abstract': 'Kuwata brings a distinctive style to tea ceremony ceramics, by creating bowls and cups that look surreal, even psychedelic.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/17/breaking-the-mold-takuro-kuwata/', 'snippet': 'Kuwata brings a distinctive style to tea ceremony ceramics, by creating bowls and cups that look surreal, even psychedelic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Takuro Kuwata’s gem-studded vessels, in vivid Pop Art reds and blues, appear far removed from traditional Japanese tea ceremony ware. Similarly, the artist’s sherbet-hued bowls — malleable-looking structures with cracked, milk-white armors of glaze — could only be surreal, even psychedelic renderings of tea ceremony ceramics.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Breaking the Mold | Takuro Kuwata', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ceramics and Pottery', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-17T14:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erica Bellman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bellman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3a1bb77-5bc1-5528-81a4-224a77ccdff2', 'word_count': 338, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3a1bb77-5bc1-5528-81a4-224a77ccdff2'}, {'abstract': 'Massive open online courses, or MOOCs, tend to have low completion rates, some with 10 percent or fewer students actually finishing. But because they are computerized, the courses offer an ideal medium for quantifying what works and what doesn’t, and researchers are paying attention.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/17/measuring-the-success-of-online-education/', 'snippet': 'Massive open online courses, or MOOCs, tend to have low completion rates, some with 10 percent or fewer students actually finishing. But because they are computerized, the courses offer an ideal medium for quantifying what works and what doesn’t, ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the dirty secrets about MOOCs — massive open online courses — is that they are not very effective, at least if you measure effectiveness in terms of completion rates. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Measuring the Success of Online Education', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Learning', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carnegie Mellon University', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Duolingo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Udacity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-17T14:07:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Markoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Markoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aed41f66-10da-5256-9380-5dd82fabf7f5', 'word_count': 735, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aed41f66-10da-5256-9380-5dd82fabf7f5'}, {'abstract': 'The man thought to be behind the kidnapping of foreign hostages in Algeria is a well-known kingpin of the jihadist movement in Saharan Africa. He recently split from Al Qaeda and is now running his own operations from Islamist-controlled northern Mali.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/17/algerian-jihadist-kingpin-behind-hostage-seizure/', 'snippet': 'The man thought to be behind the kidnapping of foreign hostages in Algeria is a well-known kingpin of the jihadist movement in Saharan Africa. He recently spl