ngnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/17/ken-salazars-legacy/', 'snippet': 'The interior secretary set aside hundreds of thousands of acres of Western lands for the future development of solar and wind power.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Obama administration will soon lose three of its most public-spirited and progressive players on environmental policy. Lisa Jackson made great strides on climate and clean air issues as head of the Environmental Protection Agency. Jane Lubchenco worked tirelessly and creatively to resist the decline in threatened fish populations as boss of the National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration. Both announced their wish to return to private life last month. The latest departure is Ken Salazar, who said Wednesday that he will leave his post as interior secretary in a few weeks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ken Salazar’s Legacy', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hydraulic Fracturing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Offshore Drilling and Exploration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wind Power', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jackson, Lisa P', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Salazar, Ken', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-17T14:55:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert B. Semple Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7915553b-0ded-5502-9618-28052d6563f7', 'word_count': 542, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7915553b-0ded-5502-9618-28052d6563f7'}, {'abstract': 'Pakistan’s newest ramble-rouser is fomenting revolution –- from a bulletproof container on the doorstep of Parliament.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/17/muhammad-tahir-ul-qadri-the-cleric-in-the-container/', 'snippet': 'Pakistan’s newest ramble-rouser is fomenting revolution –- from a bulletproof container on the doorstep of Parliament.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Between 25,000 and 50,000 people marched on Islamabad this week to demand the resignation of the government and electoral reforms. At the head of the movement is Muhammad Tahir-ul Qadri, a cleric who recently returned to Pakistan from Canada.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Cleric in the Container', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qadri, Muhammad Tahir-ul', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-17T14:57:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Huma Yusuf', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Huma', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yusuf', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b93f33cc-8de7-597f-94d6-7197ea10bdb8', 'word_count': 487, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b93f33cc-8de7-597f-94d6-7197ea10bdb8'}, {'abstract': 'House Republicans, at a two-day retreat in Virginia, were considering allowing an extension of a month or so to foster more discussion about spending cuts.', 'web_url':