le', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c64eae6-f61a-5184-8c07-9898029791e4', 'word_count': 431, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c64eae6-f61a-5184-8c07-9898029791e4'}, {'abstract': 'This week we pair “Pentatina for Five Vowels,” a poem by Campbell McGrath, with “Why You Won’t Be the Person You Expect to Be” by John Tierney.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/17/poetry-pairing-pentatina-for-five-vowels/', 'snippet': 'This week we pair “Pentatina for Five Vowels,” a poem by Campbell McGrath, with “Why You Won’t Be the Person You Expect to Be” by John Tierney.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week’s Poetry Pairing matches “Pentatina for Five Vowels,” a poem by Campbell McGrath with an article, “Why You Won’t Be the Person You Expect to Be” by John Tierney, and the related video, above.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Poetry Pairing | ‘Pentatina for Five Vowels’', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-17T15:04:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9481c9e-a877-525b-b15c-38295f039cac', 'word_count': 549, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9481c9e-a877-525b-b15c-38295f039cac'}, {'abstract': 'The director Allen Hughes paints New York a darker shade of noir in “Broken City,” which traces the moral education of a cop who has shot a man dead and is forced to turn in his badge.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/18/movies/broken-city-directed-by-allen-hughes.html', 'snippet': 'The director Allen Hughes paints New York a darker shade of noir in “Broken City,” which traces the moral education of a cop who has shot a man dead and is forced to turn in his badge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After sundown the familiar, big, beautiful, soul-dirty town in “Broken City” looks as if it were built from shattered glass. That’s especially true from the air, where the director, Allen Hughes, likes to take a god’s-eye measure of what’s below, the camera gliding over the glittering lights and shadows as black as the abyss. This is a place so ominous that the sun never seems to shine, leaving the gray streets and people washed in an icy blue light. One glance and it’s obvious that this is New York, though it’s a city Mr. Hughes has painted a darker shade of noir. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fighting for Light Amid Urban Noir', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fighting for Light Amid Urban Noir', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hughes, Allen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wahlberg, Mark', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zeta-Jones, Catherine', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pepper, Barry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Broken City (Movie)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-17T15:07:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/89d671a