sick, but don’t just blame influenza.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The flu comes every year and this year’s strain has hit early and hard. The Times’s Donald G. McNeil Jr. says plenty of people are sick, but don’t just blame influenza.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/science/video-tc10-flu/video-tc10-flu-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/17/science/video-tc10-flu/video-tc10-flu-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/science/video-tc10-flu/video-tc10-flu-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/17/science/video-tc10-flu/video-tc10-flu-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Flu Season Strikes Again ... and Again', 'kicker': 'HEALTH', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Influenza', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-17T16:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/cc075efc-f535-5e06-b4a9-1f30716c4aba', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/cc075efc-f535-5e06-b4a9-1f30716c4aba'}, {'abstract': 'Ben Affleck has had a roller coaster career in Hollywood, so he’s at peace with being overlooked in the Oscar nominations.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/17/ben-affleck-resurgent-yet-again/', 'snippet': 'Ben Affleck has had a roller coaster career in Hollywood, so he’s at peace with being overlooked in the Oscar nominations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Early on, “Argo” was seen as a front-runner for awards this season: in August it was shown in a sneak preview at the Telluride Film Festival, where “The King’s Speech” started its journey to best picture, and in September it received a standing ovation at the Toronto International Film Festival, the same response that “Slumdog Millionaire,” another best picture winner, received. But as late arrivals like “Lincoln,” “Les Misérables” and “Zero Dark Thirty” picked up steam, “Argo” began to seem like an underdog, a status more or less solidified when the film received seven Oscar nominations but not one for its director, Ben Affleck, a nod usually necessary for a best-picture win.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ben Affleck, Resurgent Yet Again', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'AFFLECK, BEN', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-17T16:00:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4c3c52b-0b19-55cb-be9c-5d0048d8ec27', 'word_count': 290, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4c3c52b-0b19-55cb-be9c-5d0048d8ec27'}, {'abstract': 'The author of “The World Until Yesterday” says that if he had to recommend one book of geography to children, he would suggest his own “Guns, Germs, and Steel.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/20/books/review/jared-diamond-by-the-book.html', 'snippet': 'The author of “The World Until Yesterday” says that if he had to recommend one book of geography to children, he would suggest his own “Guns, Germs, and Steel.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The author of “The World Until Yesterday” says that if he had to recommend one book of geography to children, he would suggest his own “Guns, Germs, and Steel.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/books/review/0120-BTB/0120-BTB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 701, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/books/review/0120-BTB/0120-BTB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2021, 'width': 1384, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/books/review/0120-BTB/0120-BTB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/20/books/review/0120-BTB/0120-BTB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/books/review/0120-BTB/0120-BTB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jared Diamond: By the Book', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jared Diamond', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Diamond, Jared', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-17T16:14:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/600d824f-ec2e-504b-8f16-6b89d56f4ac8', 'word_count': 1845, 'uri': 'nyt://article/600d824f-ec2e-504b-8f16-6b89d56f4ac8'}, {'abstract': 'A small mass was “incidentally noted” on my patient’s chart. But once the incidentaloma had been given life, so to speak, it was no longer incidental. We were now obliged to run some highly complicated — and expensive — lab tests.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/17/the-fallout-of-a-chance-medical-finding/', 'snippet': 'A small mass was “incidentally noted” on my patient’s chart. But once the incidentaloma had been given life, so to speak, it was no longer incidental. We were now obliged to run some highly complicated — and expensive — lab tests.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An incidental finding — I was convinced of it. My patient had undergone a CT scan of the abdomen at another hospital because of stomach pains and “incidentally noted” was a 2-centimeter mass in her adrenal gland. She brought in the report for me to see, nervous that she might have cancer. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/health/17well_ofri/17well_ofri-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/health/17well_ofri/17well_ofri-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/health/17well_ofri/17well_ofri-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/17/health/17well_ofri/17well_ofri-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'r