54-5e69-976d-74d5ea49d299', 'word_count': 234, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f598ad73-1554-5e69-976d-74d5ea49d299'}, {'abstract': 'Where I saw Paris in D.C., my French in-laws saw neo-Classical run wild.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/17/monument-to-a-city/', 'snippet': 'Where I saw Paris in D.C., my French in-laws saw neo-Classical run wild.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My wife and I began to unconsciously prepare ourselves for living in Washington, D.C., long before we actually moved to the city. Over the course of three years and half a dozen trips from our apartment in Paris to my parents’ home deep in the Virginia suburbs, we imagined hypothetical versions of our life there. We wandered through Georgetown and pictured ourselves living in a colonial-style mansion on a cobblestone road. We went out to eat in Columbia Heights and imagined life on a not-too-quiet street near our favorite strip of restaurants and bars. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Monument to a City', 'kicker': 'Townies', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monuments and Memorials (Structures)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mengestu, Dinaw', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-17T17:00:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dinaw Mengestu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dinaw', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mengestu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1457cea-8a7a-5c37-88c3-ddc9d19619b3', 'word_count': 1094, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1457cea-8a7a-5c37-88c3-ddc9d19619b3'}, {'abstract': 'Younger Americans are taking on debt at a higher rate, and paying it off more slowly, than previous generations, a study finds.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/17/young-people-paying-off-card-debt-more-slowly/', 'snippet': 'Younger Americans are taking on debt at a higher rate, and paying it off more slowly, than previous generations, a study finds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Younger Americans not only borrow heavily on their credit cards, but they repay the debt at slower rates than previous generations, new research from Ohio State University finds.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Young People Paying Off Card Debt More Slowly', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Cards', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Bankruptcies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ohio State University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-17T17:04:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d51762af-b5a8-506a-869d-e2f0ce6e477d', 'word_count': 502, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d51762af-b5a8-506a-869d-e2f0ce6e477d'}, {'abstract': 'Labor leaders say an episode involving a Quaker meeting house has no connection with any work dispute.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/18/us/philadelphia-vandalism-seen-by-some-as-union-intimidation.html', 'snippet': 'Labor leaders say an episode involving a Quaker meeting house has no connection with any work dispute.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHILADELPHIA — It was several weeks ago when vandals struck the building site, setting fire to a crane, cutting deep gashes in steel columns and loosening the bolts that anchored them. The episode resulted in about $500,000 in damage and was, the authorities believe, apparently an attempt to halt the construction of a Quaker meeting house.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/18/us/QUAKER/QUAKER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/18/us/QUAKER/QUAKER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/18/us/QUAKER/QUAKER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/18/us/QUAKER/QUAKER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Philadelphia Vandalism of Quaker Building Is Seen by Some as Union Intimidation', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Philadelphia Vandalism of Quaker Building Is Seen by Some as Union Intimidation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hurdle, Jon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quakers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vandalism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philadelphia (Pa)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-17T17:05:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Hurdle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hurdle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1c52c8a-8a36-5b32-bd6d-b3a5c8967026', 'word_count': 853, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1c52c8a-8a36-5b32-bd6d-b3a5c8967026'}, {'abstract': 'A new Broadway production of “Cat on a Hot Tin Roof”\xa0reminds Jeb Brown of the summer 39 years ago when he was cast as one of the kids in “Cat.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/20/theater/cat-on-a-hot-tin-roof-was-my-introduction-to-acting.html', 'snippet': 'A new Broadway production of “Cat on a Hot Tin Roof”\xa0reminds Jeb Brown of the summer 39 years ago when he was cast as one of the kids in “Cat.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'A NEW Broadway production of “Cat on a Hot Tin Roof,”\xa0like the one scheduled to open on Jan. 17, will always ring with a certain importance in the theater world, but for me it brings on an additional spell of nostalgia. In 1974, at 10 years old, I landed a thrill of a summer job as one of the kids in “Cat” — those “no-neck monsters” as Tennessee Williams so memorably called them. My parents had responded to an ad for open auditions at the American Shakespeare Theater\xa0in Stratford, Conn. I was offered the role, the production turned out to be a hit, and we transferred to New York the following fall.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/arts/20JEB1_SPAN/20JEB1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 375, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/20/arts/20JEB1_SPAN/20JEB1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 375}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'capti