 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gretchen Reynolds', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gretchen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reynolds', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e694c5a6-6bfd-591b-81d3-fd0ca6ed1596', 'word_count': 498, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e694c5a6-6bfd-591b-81d3-fd0ca6ed1596'}, {'abstract': 'Checking out “Newsreaders,” from the people responsible for “Children’s Hospital.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/17/channel-surfing-faking-it-with-newsreaders/', 'snippet': 'Checking out “Newsreaders,” from the people responsible for “Children’s Hospital.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the narrow programming niche of 15-minute late-night television comedies, there is a handful of auteurs: Seth Green (“Robot Chicken”), Jon Glaser (“Delocated”) and Rob Corddry (“Children’s Hospital”). Their faces pop up before midnight — Mr. Corddry on “Ben and Kate,” Mr. Glaser on “Parks and Recreation,” Mr. Green, reunited with his “Buffy the Vampire Slayer” co-star Alyson Hannigan, on a recent episode of “How I Met Your Mother” — but in the wee hours they’re nobody’s guest star.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Channel Surfing: Faking It With ‘Newsreaders’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-17T19:35:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Hale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09a06839-5abf-5b19-afaf-385d9a51bbaa', 'word_count': 476, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09a06839-5abf-5b19-afaf-385d9a51bbaa'}, {'abstract': 'The city’s Board of Elections has been consistently criticized for the manner in which it runs elections even as its budget has soared.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/17/new-york-city-elections-are-becoming-ever-more-costly/', 'snippet': 'The city’s Board of Elections has been consistently criticized for the manner in which it runs elections even as its budget has soared.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s often been said that democracy can be messy. In New York City, it’s also increasingly expensive, especially the way the Board of Elections operates. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York City Elections Are Becoming Ever More Costly', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Board of Elections (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-17T19:36:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Roberts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roberts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf7d4a84-9ca3-579b-81cc-9b1d7d1a22a2', 'word_count': 374, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf7d4a84-9ca3-579b-81cc-9b1d7d1a22a2'}, {'abstract': 'The list of coaches who made it — win or lose — to the Super Bowl with more than one team remains shorter than the similar list in the other sports.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/17/quirks-of-the-game-for-coaches-a-tough-road-back-to-super-bowl/', 'snippet': 'The list of coaches who made it — win or lose — to the Super Bowl with more than one team remains shorter than the similar list in the other sports.', 'lead_paragraph': 'First, Robert Griffin III’s knee buckled and took the Washington Redskins’ season down with it, then Peyton Manning took a knee and down went the Denver Broncos’ season. Both Mike Shanahan and John Fox are being questioned for their coaching decisions, but these were more than typical playoff losses — both men lost out on a chance to make history.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/18/sports/basketball/18walsh/18walsh-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 742, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/18/sports/basketball/18walsh/18walsh-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1484, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/18/sports/basketball/18walsh/18walsh-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/18/sports/basketball/18walsh/18walsh-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/18/sports/basketball/18walsh/18walsh-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Quirks of the Game: For Coaches, a Tough Road Back to Super Bowl', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coaches and Managers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': '