computer companies in the world. In the 1990s, its share price tripled in each of three consecutive years. But after the bubble burst, it resorted to accounting fraud to persuade investors it was doing better than it really was.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/19/business/norris-75-standardinline/norris-75-standardinline-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/04/19/business/norris-75-standardinline/norris-75-standardinline-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dell’s Ups and Downs With Options', 'kicker': 'High & Low Finance', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dell’s Ups and Downs With Options', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stock Options and Purchase Plans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Compensation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dell Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACCOUNTING AND ACCOUNTANTS', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-17T19:38:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Floyd Norris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Norris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebcb272c-c8d9-5b2b-befc-52cef640b69c', 'word_count': 1476, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebcb272c-c8d9-5b2b-befc-52cef640b69c'}, {'abstract': 'Here are three completely overlooked features in Windows 8, discovered while mucking around in the operating system’s deepest, darkest corners.', 'web_url': 'https://pogue.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/17/three-windows-8-features-worth-celebrating/', 'snippet': 'Here are three completely overlooked features in Windows 8, discovered while mucking around in the operating system’s deepest, darkest corners.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You already know my overall opinion of Windows 8: that it’s two very good operating systems — one for touch screens, one for mouse and keyboard — idiotically superimposed on each other. You wind up with duplicate everything: two Web browsers, two help systems, two search features, two control panels (actually three, but never mind). It’s very confusing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Three Windows 8 Features Worth Celebrating', 'kicker': 'Pogue&#039;s Posts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Windows (Operating System)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-17T19:44:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Pogue', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogue', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3df0bcd1-75c0-53e8-b293-8ba0f69bb8dd', 'word_count': 959, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3df0bcd1-75c0-53e8-b293-8ba0f69bb8dd'}, {'abstract': 'The United Federation of Teachers and the Bloomberg administration blamed each other for talks breaking down even as a midnight deadline approached.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/18/nyregion/new-york-city-talks-on-teacher-evaluations.html', 'snippet': 'The United Federation of Teachers and the Bloomberg administration blamed each other for talks breaking down even as a midnight deadline approached.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Bloomberg administration and New York City’s teachers’ union said Thursday that they had failed to reach a deal on a new system for evaluating 75,000 public school teachers, putting the city into immediate danger of losing out on up to $450 million in state and federal money and raising the possibility of cuts to staff and programs.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/18/nyregion/EVAL1/EVAL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/18/nyregion/EVAL1/EVAL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/18/nyregion/EVAL1/EVAL1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/18/nyregion/EVAL1/EVAL1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'No Deal on Teacher Evaluations; City Risks Losing $450 Million', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Deal on Teacher Evaluations; City Risks Losing $450 Million', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Performance Evaluations (Labor)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Department (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Federation of Teachers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mulgrew, Michael', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations',