istance. | Business groups want restraint on debt ceiling threats. | The White House readies a new team of advisors.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'TimesCast Politics: Gun Debate Moves to Capitol Hill', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-17T21:31:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f5836de-6b58-5d0e-b1b8-2af81bbea065', 'word_count': 60, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f5836de-6b58-5d0e-b1b8-2af81bbea065'}, {'abstract': 'The tabletop guitarist Keith Rowe improvised in duets with Graham Lambkin and Michael Pisaro as part of the Amplify 2013: Rotation festival at the Temp art space.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/18/arts/music/keith-rowe-with-graham-lambkin-and-michael-pisaro-at-temp.html', 'snippet': 'The tabletop guitarist Keith Rowe improvised in duets with Graham Lambkin and Michael Pisaro as part of the Amplify 2013: Rotation festival at the Temp art space.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Keith Rowe is 72, and the instrument he’s been associated with for nearly 50 years is an electric guitar, laid flat on a table. Near the guitar are the things he uses for manipulating the sound of the guitar or interacting with it: flat objects of various weights and hardnesses, a couple of effects pedals, a small electric fan, a wad of steel wool, a small radio, an iPod, a sound mixer. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/18/arts/ROWE/ROWE-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 376, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'artic