eum coke, a highly carbon-rich byproduct, one report argues.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/17/2-reports-on-oil-sands-paint-a-dire-picture/', 'snippet': 'Emissions from mining, transporting and refining the oil fail to factor in the impact of petroleum coke, a highly carbon-rich byproduct, one report argues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Opponents of the Keystone XL pipeline and the heavy Canadian crude oil that it would carry released two reports on Thursday asserting that the environmental impacts of the project are worse than previously estimated, and urged the Obama administration to veto it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '2 Reports on Oil Sands Paint a Dire Picture', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Keystone Pipeline System', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil Sands', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TransCanada Corporation', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALBERTA (CANADA)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nebraska', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-17T21:34:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By John M. Broder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/10e6031c-26f6-539c-8241-2252931ec153', 'word_count': 562, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10e6031c-26f6-539c-8241-2252931ec153'}, {'abstract': 'Lorin Maazel led the Philharmonic on Wednesday in Sibelius’s Second Symphony and Brahms’s Piano Concerto No. 1, with the soloist Yefim Bronfman.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/18/arts/music/lorin-maazel-leads-philharmonic-in-sibelius-and-brahms.html', 'snippet': 'Lorin Maazel led the Philharmonic on Wednesday in Sibelius’s Second Symphony and Brahms’s Piano Concerto No. 1, with the soloist Yefim Bronfman.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many oppressive regimes have tried to manipulate the role of music in their citizens’ lives. The Taliban banned it almost entirely, and the Nazis prohibited performances of works by “degenerate” composers. The Soviets branded as “formalist” scores that didn’t meet the requirements of Socialist Realism, demanding patriotic and folk-tinged pieces. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/18/arts/18PHIL_SPAN/18PHIL_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/18/arts/18PHIL_SPAN/18PHIL_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/18/arts/18PHIL_SPAN/PHIL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 874, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/18/arts/18PHIL_SPAN/PHIL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1748, 'width': 2048, 'subTy