ns', 'value': 'Kachin Independence Army', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-17T23:19:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Fuller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fuller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/744a3492-4788-5027-adb2-2a5a379ea688', 'word_count': 498, 'uri': 'nyt://article/744a3492-4788-5027-adb2-2a5a379ea688'}, {'abstract': 'The State Labor Department reported that more than half of the jobs lost in November were added back in New York City, and unemployment remained at 8.8 percent.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/17/city-jobs-lost-in-storm-are-returning-but-unemployment-rate-is-flat/', 'snippet': 'The State Labor Department reported that more than half of the jobs lost in November were added back in New York City, and unemployment remained at 8.8 percent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York City’s job market started to shrug off the effects of Hurricane Sandy at the end of the year, new employment statistics showed on Thursday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'City Jobs Lost in Storm Are Returning, but Unemployment Rate Is Flat', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-17T23:20:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_d