ons', 'value': 'Citigroup Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-18T02:03:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess and Jessica Silver-Greenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jessica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver-Greenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd46691c-ef38-5e38-b68d-ed793b6cddaa', 'word_count': 1007, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd46691c-ef38-5e38-b68d-ed793b6cddaa'}, {'abstract': 'Members of the United States Conference of Mayors, at their winter meeting in Washington, said they were heartened by President Obama’s call for new laws to curb gun violence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/18/us/politics/recalling-pain-of-guns-toll-mayors-urge-bills-passage.html', 'snippet': 'Members of the United States Conference of Mayors, at their winter meeting in Washington, said they were heartened by President Obama’s call for new laws to curb gun violence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Some mayors spoke about the bad feeling they got with each call that there had been another shooting in their city. Others described the pain of burying police officers who had worked for them. Many recalled their attempts to console grieving families.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/18/us/JP-MAYORS/JP-MAYORS-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/18/us/JP-MAYORS/JP-MAYORS-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400