 New Jersey appointed the panel after opponents criticized him for not mentioning gun violence in his State of the State address.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After facing sharp criticism for not mentioning gun violence in his State of the State speech, Gov. Chris Christie of New Jersey appointed a task force on Thursday to examine gun control measures and school safety, as well as look at some of the underlying problems behind gun violence, including addiction and mental illness.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/18/nyregion/CHRISTIE-sub2/CHRISTIE-sub2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/18/nyregion/CHRISTIE-sub2/CHRISTIE-sub2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/18/nyregion/CHRISTIE-sub2/CHRISTIE-sub2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/18/nyregion/CHRISTIE-sub2/CHRISTIE-sub2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/18/nyregion/CHRISTIE-sub2/CHRISTIE-sub2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Christie Forms Panel on Firearms and School Safety', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Christie Forms Panel on Firearms and School Safety', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the State Message (NJ)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Preston, Jennifer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-18T03:49:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1ae46a4-fb6d-5c39-bf2f-2bd0cd4d9a69', 'word_count': 506, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1ae46a4-fb6d-5c39-bf2f-2bd0cd4d9a69'}, {'abstract': 'The overall increase was 9 percent over the last decade, and two-thirds of that rise came from two Orthodox Jewish neighborhoods in Brooklyn that have high birthrates.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/18/nyregion/reversing-past-trend-new-yorks-jewish-population-rises.html', 'snippet': 'The overall increase was 9 percent over the last decade, and two-thirds of that rise came from two Orthodox Jewish neighborhoods in Brooklyn that have high birthrates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Borough Park in Brooklyn, with its preponderance of Orthodox synagogues and kosher restaurants, is the most Jewish area in the New York City region, with 78 percent of households there identifying as Jewish. Close behind is Great Neck, Long Island, with its thriving enclave of Persian Jews, and then the Five Towns, also on Long Island, where a higher percentage of Jews identify as modern Orthodox than anywhere else in the region, according to a Jewish demographic study released Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jewish Population Is Up in the New York Region', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jewish Population Is Up In the New York Region', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Population', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'UJA-Federation of New York', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York Metropolitan Area', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-18T03:51:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sharon Otterman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sharon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Otterman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e8c2163-716c-5c03-b66d-3ee8a7613216', 'word_count': 646, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e8c2163-716c-5c03-b66d-3ee8a7613216'}, {'abstract': 'Though there was improvement, economic data also underlined the view that the pace of future growth is likely to remain well below that seen in recent years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/19/business/global/chinese-economy-picks-up-steam-in-last-quarter.html', 'snippet': 'Though there was improvement, economic data also underlined the view that the pace of future growth is likely to remain well below that seen in recent years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — The giant Chinese economy picked up steam during the last few months of 2012, closely watched data from Beijing on Friday confirmed. But at the same time the figures underlined the view that the pace of future growth is likely to remain well below that seen in recent years.', 'print_section':