nces at the Met” presentation, which Anthony Tommasini, writing in The New York Times, called handsome and insightful. “The production’s contemporary element comes from showing the main characters engaged in a triangle of desire, distrust and gamesmanship,” he said, adding: “In her village Adina is like a prima donna, something Ms. Netrebko easily conveys.” And Mr. Polenzani “is coming into his prime.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Friday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-18T06:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f6558ba-0ace-5746-8b51-5f6bfc634e60', 'word_count': 695, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f6558ba-0ace-5746-8b51-5f6bfc634e60'}, {'abstract': 'Why France’s intervention in Mali is necessary, despite the risks for France, the region and the West.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/18/mali-need-not-be-frances-afghanistan/', 'snippet': 'Why France’s intervention in Mali is necessary, despite the risks for France, the region and the West.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A colleague’s question could have come from anyone in the United States.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/18/world/africa/18mali/18mali-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/18/world/africa/18