fier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ab3d73c-5520-5a0e-82c7-dd5bdf3c843a', 'word_count': 894, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ab3d73c-5520-5a0e-82c7-dd5bdf3c843a'}, {'abstract': 'Tomas Berdych shows his passion for tennis and his passion for watches, a love inspired by a childhood shortcoming.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/18/for-berdych-trophies-are-worn-on-the-wrist/', 'snippet': 'Tomas Berdych shows his passion for tennis and his passion for watches, a love inspired by a childhood shortcoming.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MELBOURNE, Australia — Nearly all top tennis players have some public social media presence, with many of them on multiple networks. Maria Sharapova, who has long maintained an active Facebook page, joined Twitter this week, and has accumulated more than 60,000 followers in just a few days. Roger Federer sticks exclusively to Facebook, while Serena Williams was an early adapter of Twitter, and often tweets product endorsements and occasionally opaque allusions to her personal life.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Berdych, Trophies are Worn on the Wrist', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-18T06:06:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By BEN ROTHENBERG', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'ROTHENBERG', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5689bd00-7a7d-52d6-aac2-e4fae252ea3f', 'word_count': 580, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5689bd00-7a7d-52d6-aac2-e4fae252ea3f'}, {'abstract': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/18/news-quiz-january-18-2013/', 'snippet': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'See what you know about the news below. To prepare, you might scan the articles or summaries on today’s paper. Good luck!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Quiz | January 18, 2013', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-18T06:30:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anastasia Economides', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anastasia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Economides', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65848803-c2d8-54e5-b700-ad68c76bfbb1', 'word_count': 22, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65848803-c2d8-54e5-b700-ad68c76bfbb1'}, {'abstract': 'Lawmakers voted early Friday to investigate former Finance Minister George Papaconstantinou over his handling of a list of wealthy Greeks with Swiss bank accounts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/18/world/europe/greece-ex-official-to-be-investigated.html', 'snippet': 'Lawmakers voted early Friday to investigate former Finance Minister George Papaconstantinou over his handling of a list of wealthy Greeks with Swiss bank accounts.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Lawmakers voted early Friday to investigate former Finance Minister George Papaconstantinou over his handling of a list of wealthy Greeks with Swiss bank accounts, a potential source of tax revenue that was never used by the authorities, stirring public outrage in the debt-racked country. After several hours of heated debate, 265 members of the 300-seat Parliament voted to set up a committee to determine whether Mr. Papaconstantinou should face criminal charges for tampering with the list or breach of duty. A 12-member committee of lawmakers has until Feb. 25 to submit its proposal to Parliament, which will then vote on whether to indict the former minister. Mr. Papaconstantinou has denied accusations that he removed the names of relatives from the list. Proposals to broaden the investigation to include other politicians were rejected. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Greece: Ex-Official to Be Investigated', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Greece: Ex-Official to Be Investigated', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kitsantonis, Niki', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Switzerland', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Papaconstantinou, George', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-18T06:35:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Niki Kitsantonis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Niki', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kitsantonis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/783a124a-8efa-5b16-aec0-05b4f167cb14', 'word_count': 132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/783a124a-8efa-5b16-aec0-05b4f167cb14'}, {'abstract': 'One of the world’s most closely watched elephant populations has been heavily hit by ivory poachers, scientists in Kenya said this week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/18/world/africa/kenya-study-details-poachers-toll.html', 'snippet': 'One of the world’s most closely watched elephant populations has been heavily hit by ivory poachers, scientists in Kenya said this week.', 'lead_paragraph': ' One of the world’s most closely watched elephant populations has been heavily hit by ivory poachers, scientists in Kenya said this week. In a study published Wednesday, scientists with the group Save the Elephants said that the proportion of illegally killed elephants in the Samburu area of northern Kenya had risen to more than 50 percent of all deaths and that the number of older elephants (which usually have the biggest tusks) declined drastically. “Ivory demand and prices have reached a point at which poachers are willing to target well-protected, closely monitored populations,” said Iain Douglas-Hamilton, founder of Save the Elephants. “This is now being replicated in other protected areas across Africa.” Scientists estimate that tens of thousands of African elephants are being slaughtered each year, more than at any time in decades, to meet the rising demand for ivory in Asia’s rapidly growing economies. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kenya: Study Details Poachers’ Toll', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Africa', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Kenya: Study Details Poachers’ Toll', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gettleman, Jeffrey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elephants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poaching (Wildlife)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ivory', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kenya', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-18T06:39:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeffrey Gettleman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeffrey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gettleman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/1435c487-655b-5ddd-a082-e785d501899d', 'word_count': 145, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1435c487-655b-5ddd-a082-e785d501899d'}, {'abstract': 'Muhammad Tahir-ul Qadri, a Pakistani preacher, emerged on the country’s political scene, leading huge protests in Islamabad. After days of standoffs, he reached a symbolic deal with the government.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/world/middleeast/100000002012141/defusing-a-crisis-in-pakistan.html', 'snippet': 'Muhammad Tahir-ul Qadri, a Pakistani preacher, emerged on the country’s political scene, leading huge protests in Islamabad. After days of standoffs, he reached a symbolic deal with the government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Muhammad Tahir-ul Qadri, a Pakistani preacher, emerged on the country’s political scene, leading huge protests in Islamabad. After days of standoffs, he reached a symbolic deal with the government.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/world/video-qadri-supporters/video-qadri-supporters-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/17/world/video-qadri-supporters/video-qadri-supporters-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/world/video-qadri-supporters/video-qadri-supporters-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/17/world/video-qadri-supporters/video-qadri-supporters-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Defusing a Crisis in Pakistan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-18T07:05:08+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'Mac William Bishop and Michelle Stockman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mac', 'middlename': 'William', 'lastname': 'Bishop', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michelle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stockman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/2afa8d95-cc67-53b4-af79-4d0bf1aca4d5', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/2afa8d95-cc67-53b4-af79-4d0bf1aca4d5'}, {'abstract': 'Hostage watch in Algeria; mourning in Turkey; Depardieu as national image shaper; “Fifty Shades” in French; Armstrong’s confession.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/18/iht-quick-read-jan-18/', 'snippet': 'Hostage watch in Algeria; mourning in Turkey; Depardieu as national image shaper; “Fifty Shades” in French; Armstrong’s confession.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEWS Hours after Algerian forces raided a gas facility, there was still no official word on the number of hostages freed, killed or still held by their Islamist kidnappers. Adam Nossiter reported from Bamako, Mali, and Rick Gladstone from New York.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/18/world/turkey1/turkey1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/18/world/turkey1/turkey1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/18/world/turkey1/turkey1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/18/world/turkey1/turkey1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/18/world/turkey1/turkey1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'IHT Quick Read: Jan. 18', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-18T07:45:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By The International Herald Tribune', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The International Herald Tribune'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc14faaf-3123-56b7-b803-b01b2dda6a91', 'word_count': 336, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc14faaf-3123-56b7-b803-b01b2dda6a91'}, {'abstract': 'Prime Minister David Cameron postponed a speech in Amsterdam on Britain’s future in Europe, citing the need to stay in London for developments in the hostage crisis in Algeria.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/19/world/europe/david-cameron-delays-talk-on-new-role-in-europe.html', 'snippet': 'Prime Minister David Cameron postponed a speech in Amsterdam on Britain’s future in Europe, citing the need to stay in London for developments in the hostage crisis in Algeria.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Prime Minister David Cameron, who canceled a long-anticipated speech because of a hostage crisis in Algeria involving Britons, planned to deliver an explicit warning that Britain might leave the European Union if changes in its administration were not made, according to excerpts from the speech released Thursday and embargoed until Friday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cameron Warns That Britain Could Leave European Union', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cameron Warns That Britain Could Leave European Union', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cameron, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burns, John F', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speeches and Statements', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALGERIA', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-18T07:51:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By John F. Burns and Alan Cowell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Burns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d09df0e-18f5-5292-bcff-11a0a268ea8e', 'word_count': 587, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d09df0e-18f5-5292-bcff-11a0a268ea8e'}, {'abstract': 'Defying the Algerian Army’s demands to give up, kidnappers still held at least 10 hostages. The United States said that American citizens were still being held and one was killed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/19/world/africa/algeria-militants-hostages.html', 'snippet': 'Defying the Algerian Army’s demands to give up, kidnappers still held at least 10 hostages. The United States said that American citizens were still being held and one was killed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BAMAKO, Mali — Defying the Algerian Army’s demands to give up, the band of Islamist militant kidnappers who terrorized a remote Saharan gas field complex still held at least 10 and possibly dozens of foreign hostages on Friday, and a senior Algerian government official said there were no talks planned to end the standoff.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/world/algeria/algeria-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 412, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/19/world/algeria/algeria-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 412}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/world/algeria/algeria-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 703, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/world/algeria/algeria-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1407, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/world/algeria/algeria-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/19/world/algeria/algeria-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/world/algeria/algeria-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'As Algeria Hostage\r\nCrisis Goes On, U.S.\r\nSays American Died', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Militants in Algeria Refuse to Surrender and Continue to Hold Hostages', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALGERIA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hostages', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Al Mulathameen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mali', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-18T08:00:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Nossiter and Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nossiter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ee08dcc-62c1-5515-88d2-2479f2cea912', 'word_count': 1546, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ee08dcc-62c1-5515-88d2-2479f2cea912'}, {'abstract': 'Players at the Australian Open note the lack of drug scandals afflicting professional tennis.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/18/at-australian-open-tough-talk-about-armstrong/', 'snippet': 'Players at the Australian Open note the lack of drug scandals afflicting professional tennis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MELBOURNE, Australia — A world away from the leather-cushioned chairs which held Lance Armstrong and Oprah Winfrey in their interview Thursday, third-round tennis opponents Novak Djokovic and Radek Stepanek sat in their own wooden swivel chairs behind podiums under Rod Laver Arena, and discussed Armstrong’s revelations. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Australian Open, Tough Talk About Armstrong', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-18T08:18:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By BEN ROTHENBERG', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'ROTHENBERG', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed69fbaf-4be2-5cf4-9f98-4fc9622767b8', 'word_count': 654, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed69fbaf-4be2-5cf4-9f98-4fc9622767b8'}, {'abstract': 'Photographer Sephi Bergerson has documented a wide variety of marriage ceremonies.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/18/weddings-across-india-in-photograph/', 'snippet': 'Photographer Sephi Bergerson has documented a wide variety of marriage ceremonies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the last five years, in the course of working on a photography book “Just Another Indian Wedding,” I may have witnessed and documented a greater variety of Indian weddings than any other person on earth.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From Tamil Brahmin to Kashmiri Pandit: Weddings Across India', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mumbai (India)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-18T08:35:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sephi Bergerson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sephi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bergerson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eba462e2-ae4b-51f6-ba1b-5ebaa9900e62', 'word_count': 184, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eba462e2-ae4b-51f6-ba1b-5ebaa9900e62'}, {'abstract': 'Betsy Andreu watched Lance Armstrong’s interview with Oprah Winfrey, waiting in vain for Armstrong to say that she and her husband were not liars.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/19/sports/cycling/in-armstrong-interview-no-closure-for-andreus.html', 'snippet': 'Betsy Andreu watched Lance Armstrong’s interview with Oprah Winfrey, waiting in vain for Armstrong to say that she and her husband were not liars.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Betsy Andreu, the stay-at-home mother of three who for years was among Lance Armstrong’s greatest foes, on Friday finally let the whirlwind of the past 24 hours sink in. She thought this moment would never come.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/sports/19cycling2/19cycling2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo',