': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Astrology', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fortune Telling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Superstitions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indian National Congress', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-18T09:30:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hartosh Singh Bal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hartosh', 'middlename': 'Singh', 'lastname': 'Bal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4232294b-fc20-54d8-a2c9-a2808ccaad21', 'word_count': 489, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4232294b-fc20-54d8-a2c9-a2808ccaad21'}, {'abstract': 'What are some of the causes of the slowdown in the snowboarding industry, according to the article?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/18/interest-in-snowboarding-on-the-decline/', 'snippet': 'What are some of the causes of the slowdown in the snowboarding industry, according to the article?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In “Has Snowboarding Lost Its Edge?” Christopher Solomon reports on the snowboarding industry.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/travel/20UPDATE_SPAN-LN/20UPDATE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/20/travel/20UPDATE_SPAN-LN/20UPDATE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/travel/20UPDATE_SPAN-LN/20UPDATE_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 691, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/travel/20UPDATE_SPAN-LN/20UPDATE_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1382, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/travel/20UPDATE_SPAN-LN/20UPDATE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/20/travel/20UPDATE_SPAN-LN/20UPDATE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/travel/20UPDATE_SPAN-LN/20UPDATE_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Interest in Snowboarding on the Decline', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-18T09:30:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Gonchar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonchar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/269b9816-55a6-51bf-9048-bad0471875db', 'word_count': 120, 'uri': 'nyt://article/269b9816-55a6-51bf-9048-bad0471875db'}, {'abstract': 'To capture Russia’s rapid changes and vast territory, Rafal Milach went small, delving into the lives of seven people reconciling their country’s past with its ever-evolving future.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/18/russia-in-three-cities-and-7-rooms/', 'snippet': 'To capture Russia’s rapid changes and vast territory, Rafal Milach went small, delving into the lives of seven people reconciling their country’s past with its ever-evolving future.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Contradictions lie at the heart of Rafal Milach’s “7 Rooms,” a project that took Mr. Milach, a Warsaw-based photographer, to Russia in search of insights through the ordinary. Though he wanted to avoid clichés — vodka drinking, prisons, cadet schools, ballets — some pictures reflect their Soviet legacy. And although he traveled widely through three cities – Moscow, Yekaterinburg and Krasnoyarsk – his project didn’t make sense to him until he narrowed his focus to seven individuals.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia, in Three Cities and ‘7 Rooms’', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-18T10:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt McCann', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McCann', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a0bc4d57-b301-5346-8ddd-43d3bc65bd47', 'word_count': 588, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a0bc4d57-b301-5346-8ddd-43d3bc65bd47'}, {'abstract': 'What do you like about this idea? What concerns do you have?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/18/would-you-feel-safer-with-armed-guards-patrolling-your-school/', 'snippet': 'What do you like about this idea? What concerns do you have?', 'lead_paragraph': 'After the shooting at Sandy Hook Elementary School in Newtown, Conn., that killed 26 people, the National Rifle Association recommended that armed guards should be stationed at every school to prevent similar episodes. This week the N.R.A. released an ad criticizing President Obama for having Secret Service protection at his daughters’ school, but not promoting armed protection at every American school.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/us/POSSE-2-LN/POSSE-2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/17/us/POSSE-2-LN/POSSE-2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/us/POSSE-2-LN/POSSE-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 668, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/us/POSSE-2-LN/POSSE-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1335, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/us/POSSE-2-LN/POSSE-2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/17/us/POSSE-2-LN/POSSE-2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/us/POSSE-2-LN/POSSE-2-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Would You Feel Safer With Armed Guards Patrolling Your School?', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-18T10:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Gonchar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonchar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8accbf2-03f7-5153-b61f-d2a3d75dcbd8', 'word_count': 516, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8accbf2-03f7-5153-b61f-d2a3d75dcbd8'}, {'abstract': 'In addition to the cease-fire, to start Saturday, the Myanmar government said it would pursue peace talks, but it was unclear how the rebels would react to the government’s overtures.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/19/world/asia/kachin-refugees-reported-to-flee-myanmar-to-china.html', 'snippet': 'In addition to the cease-fire, to start Saturday, the Myanmar government said it would pursue peace talks, but it was unclear how the rebels would react to the government’s overtures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BANGKOK — After weeks of intense fighting near the border with China, the Myanmar government on Friday announced what appeared to be a unilateral cease-fire in its offensive against ethnic Kachin rebels. The government also said it would pursue peace talks, but it was unclear how the rebels would react to the government’s overtures.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/world/jp-myanmar/jp-myanmar-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/19/world/jp-myanmar/jp-myanmar-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/world/jp-myanmar/jp-myanmar-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo'