nd Budgeting', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-18T15:24:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By James B. Stewart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0f4801c-9fcd-515a-9e27-f789442b7038', 'word_count': 1330, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0f4801c-9fcd-515a-9e27-f789442b7038'}, {'abstract': 'In remembrance and defiance, hundreds went to the movie theater in Aurora, Colo., on Thursday where a gunman killed 12 people.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/19/us/six-months-after-carnage-a-theater-reopens.html', 'snippet': 'In remembrance and defiance, hundreds went to the movie theater in Aurora, Colo., on Thursday where a gunman killed 12 people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AURORA, Colo. — Some came to the movies limping and on crutches, still hobbled from the fusillade of bullets that cut through bodies and chairs and walls that night in July. They came holding hands and snapping photos, dressed up in blazers to meet the governor or wearing T-shirts emblazoned with the face of a fallen friend.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/us/19aurora-cnd/19aurora-cnd-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/19/us/19aurora-cnd/19aurora-cnd-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/us/19aurora-cnd/19aurora-cnd-jumbo-v2.jpg', '