lliams, whose course was set in England under the influence of Francis Bacon, Edward Coke, Oliver Cromwell and John Milton.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paperback Row', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Paperback Row', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-18T15:41:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ihsan Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ihsan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/53c81e21-5aa2-5aad-90a7-5b9b1c7a16e1', 'word_count': 496, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53c81e21-5aa2-5aad-90a7-5b9b1c7a16e1'}, {'abstract': 'Recently reviewed books of particular interest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/20/books/review/editors-choice.html', 'snippet': 'Recently reviewed books of particular interest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE WORLD UNTIL YESTERDAY: What Can We Learn From Traditional Societies?,  by Jared Diamond. (Viking, $36.) To answer his subtitle, the “Guns, Germs, and Steel” author cites child rearing, dispute resolution and the treatment of the elderly.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Editors’ Choice', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Editors’ Choice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-18T15:41:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/042d5d02-bf1a-5456-a398-eee3a09458ea', 'word_count': 279, 'uri': 'nyt://article/042d5d02-bf1a-5456-a398-eee3a09458ea'}, {'abstract': 'Sonia Sotomayor recalls her early life and the road toward the court.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/20/books/review/my-beloved-world-by-sonia-sotomayor.html', 'snippet': 'Sonia Sotomayor recalls her early life and the road toward the court.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Sonia Sotomayor was 7 years old and hospitalized with diabetes, she learned to give herself insulin shots by practicing on an orange. At home, her mother showed her how to light a burner on the stove with a match, and together they would fill a pot with water to cover the syringe and needle. Sonia was taught to wait for a boil and then to wait five minutes more. The daily shots became her way of fending off conflict between her parents: Her father’s hands trembled because of his alcoholism, and her mother, a nurse who worked long hours, would get angry when she couldn’t rely on him. “The last thing I wanted was for them to fight about me,” Sotomayor relates in her new memoir. “It then dawned on me: If I needed to have these shots every day for the rest of my life, the only way I’d survive was to do it myself.” ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/books/review/20BAZELON/20BAZELON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 962, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/books/review/20BAZELON/20BAZELON-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1935, 'width': 1818, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/books/review/20BAZELON/20BAZELON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/20/books/review/20BAZELON/20BAZELON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/books/review/20BAZELON/20BAZELON-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Making of a Justice', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Making of a Justice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bazelon, Emily', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'My Beloved World (Book)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sotomayor, Sonia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-18T15:42:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily Bazelon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bazelon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/94bedcc3-627b-5260-9d40-58eb6ef181fb', 'word_count': 1223, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94bedcc3-627b-5260-9d40-58eb6ef181fb'}, {'abstract': 'The mission: Improve the Wikipedia presence of the Ford Presidential Library and Museum.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/18/gerald-ford-library-hires-wikipedian-in-residence/', 'snippet': 'The mission: Improve the Wikipedia presence of the