er fiction list, says he envies the time when he was writing “in my little cubbyhole with nobody knocking on my door.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/27/books/review/inside-the-list.html', 'snippet': 'David Baldacci, whose latest novel is at No. 12 on the hardcover fiction list, says he envies the time when he was writing “in my little cubbyhole with nobody knocking on my door.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE MOTIVE: David Baldacci’s latest novel, “The Forgotten,” is at No. 12 in its eighth week on the hardcover fiction list. It’s hard to imagine Baldacci’s fans looking up from the book’s breathy sentences — “The smell of sex was all over her. He wondered if she realized that” — to ask themselves what compels Baldacci to face the blank page every day; really, isn’t the smell of sex enough? Be that as it may, anybody curious can find Baldacci’s thoughts on the matter in “Why We Write,” a new collection of interviews edited by Meredith Maran, in which 20 well-known authors try to analyze what, exactly, keeps them at it.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/books/review/20list-img/20list-img-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 298, 'width': 294, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/books/review/20list-img/20list-img-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 298, 'width': 294, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/books/review/20list-img/20list-img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/20/books/review/20list-img/20list-img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth':