', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-18T17:58:14+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/829495f0-c50d-54fa-8cea-bb566560a801', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/829495f0-c50d-54fa-8cea-bb566560a801'}, {'abstract': 'Life with baby: The pros and cons of being the new parent trailblazers in your circle of friends.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/18/when-old-friends-meet-the-new-baby/', 'snippet': 'Life with baby: The pros and cons of being the new parent trailblazers in your circle of friends.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My daughter celebrated one month on this planet just last week. She is a glorious little babe, happy and chubby and sleeping and eating like a champ. We feel especially lucky that she’s doing so well, because as first-time parents, my husband and I still feel like we’re so green, we glow like a neon sign. We regularly consult Google to make sure that nothing bad will happen to our girl after hearing her grunt while breathing on the baby monitor. I’m no teenage mom — I got pregnant a week shy of my 30th birthday — but we’re the first in our close circle to have children, so to our childless pals, we are fonts of superior pregnancy and baby knowledge. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/style/motherlode-jess-grose/motherlode-jess-grose-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 833, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/style/motherlode-jess-grose/motherlode-jess-grose-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1229, 'width': 1510, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/style/motherlode-jess-grose/motherlode-jess-grose-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/17/style/motherlode-jess-grose/motherlode-jess-grose-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/17/style/motherlode-jess-grose/motherlode-jess-grose-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When Old Friends Meet the New Baby', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Friendship', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Childbirth', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-18T17:58:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jessica Grose', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jessica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grose', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9cc433c2-e86d-5289-88d3-0130648e1429', 'word_count': 827, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9cc433c2-e86d-5289-88d3-0130648e1429'}, {'abstract': 'Peter Liguori, named Thursday as chief executive of the reconstituted Tribune Company, said that managing the company’s newspapers well is crucial but that he would also explore acquiring more television stations.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/18/new-tribune-chief-signals-greater-television-focus/', 'snippet': 'Peter Liguori, named Thursday as chief executive of the reconstituted Tribune Company, said that managing the company’s newspapers well is crucial but that he would also explore acquiring more television stations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two-thirds of the Tribune Company’s revenues currently come from the newspapers it owns. But that most likely won’t be true a year from now.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Tribune Chief Signals Greater Television Focus', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Liguori, Peter', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Tribune', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Times', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tribune Co', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-18T18:03:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/40611e7e-5f41-5a13-9896-cefd5457bf1d', 'word_count': 469, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40611e7e-5f41-5a13-9896-cefd5457bf1d'}, {'abstract': 'It’s possible that members of the “Les Miz” cast will sing at the Oscars, though given his reviews, Russell Crowe probably won’t be among them.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/18/a-les-miz-medley-at-the-oscars-possibly-but-count-out-russell-crowe/', 'snippet': 'It’s possible that members of the “Les Miz” cast will sing at the Oscars, though given his reviews, Russell Crowe probably won’t be among them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Will the Oscars put to the test all those tales of the “Les Misérables” stars singing live? The Daily Mail in “Les Miz”-mad England reports that Samantha Barks, who made a rare stage-to-screen transition as Eponine, is in talks to perform on the telecast with her co-stars. Possibilities include group numbers like “One Day More” or “Do You Hear the People Sing” with Amanda Seyfried and Eddie Redmayne, or a medley with Anne Hathaway’s show-stopping “I Dreamed a Dream” and Hugh Jackman’s “Who Am I?” (or, more likely, “Suddenly,” an Oscar nominee for best song). ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A ‘Les Miz’ Medley at the Oscars? Possibly (But Count Out Russell Crowe)', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barks, Samantha', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crowe, Russell', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-18T18:04:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3a4ceac-9380-5d94-9a82-9611a20194d4', 'word_count': 166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3a4ceac-9380-5d94-9a82-9611a20194d4'}, {'abstract': 'After helping President Obama win re-election, his action group, renamed Organizing for Action, will raise money and rally support for his agenda.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/19/us/politics/obamas-campaign-machinery-turns-to-promoting-policy.html', 'snippet': 'After helping President Obama win re-election, his action group, renamed Organizing for Action, will raise money and rally support for his agenda.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — A new political operation created to advance President Obama’s agenda in his second term will be allowed to raise unlimited money and accept corporate contributions, but officials said Friday the donations will be disclosed.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama to Turn Campaign Machinery to Promoting Policy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama Campaign Team\r\nTo Promote His Agenda', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zeleny, Jeff', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Messina, Jim (1969- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Organizing for Action', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-18T18:05:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Zeleny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zeleny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ba5e5e5-20f2-501f-8b90-870ddfdd9a24', 'word_count': 581, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ba5e5e5-20f2-501f-8b90-870ddfdd9a24'}, {'abstract': 'Paris', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2013/01/18/fashion/runway-mens/comme-des-garcons-fall-2013-menswear.ht