eported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/27309a0c-3c42-52d7-b938-3c9ae9ce7dcf', 'word_count': 2638, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27309a0c-3c42-52d7-b938-3c9ae9ce7dcf'}, {'abstract': 'The White House has released the new official portrait of President Obama.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/18/for-obama-second-term-brings-a-new-look/', 'snippet': 'The White House has released the new official portrait of President Obama.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The White House has released the new official portrait of President Obama. Shot on Dec. 6, by White House photographer Pete Souza, the portrait features Mr. Obama, smiling broadly, standing in the Oval Office. The portrait is a slight departure from the 2009 version, which featured a close-up shot of then President-elect Obama, with a solemn expression and a blander background. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Obama, Second Term Brings a New Look', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-18T18:25:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Corasaniti', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Corasaniti', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/69bd6bf9-ed21-5942-9391-00f0f1c1db61', 'word_count': 63, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69bd6bf9-ed21-5942-9391-00f0f1c1db61'}, {'abstract': 'Amid tiny towns and deserted dwellings sits a world-class birding site, the Sax-Zim Bog, where people from around the world travel to glimpse hard-to-spot species.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/20/travel/in-a-minnesota-bog-a-festival-of-birds.html', 'snippet': 'Amid tiny towns and deserted dwellings sits a world-class birding site, the Sax-Zim Bog, where people from around the world travel to glimpse hard-to-spot species.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ON an early winter’s evening in northern Minnesota, a convoy of five snappy yellow school buses rolled out into the dusk. From the windows, the distant horizon of pointy evergreens and wide-open expanses of frosted wetlands looked like a frozen dead zone. But we were on a tour to see life — bird life.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/travel/20EXPLORER1/20EXPLORER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/20/travel/20EXPLORER1/20EXPLORER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/travel/20EXPLORER1/20EXPLORER1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/travel/20EXPLORER1/20EXPLORER1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/travel/20EXPLORER1/20EXPLORER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/20/travel/20EXPLORER1/20EXPLORER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/travel/20EXPLORER1/20EXPLORER1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height'