Stephen A. Schwarzman’s penguins.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Private Equity’s Penguins on Parade', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Penguins', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rubio, Marco', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schwarzman, Stephen A', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SeaWorld Adventure Parks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'The Blackstone Group', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-18T18:35:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/262d3f52-31e2-5de2-89c8-6e5d3d88d2b8', 'word_count': 168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/262d3f52-31e2-5de2-89c8-6e5d3d88d2b8'}, {'abstract': 'Republicans said they would back down on the borrowing limit to open a window for Congress to pass a budget and begin talks on long-term deficit reduction.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/19/us/politics/house-gop-agrees-to-lift-debt-ceiling-for-3-months.html', 'snippet': 'Republicans said they would back down on the borrowing limit to open a window for Congress to pass a budget and begin talks on long-term deficit reduction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Backing down from their hard-line stance, House Republicans said Friday that they would agree to lift the federal government’s statutory borrowing limit for three months, with a requirement that both chambers of Congress pass a budget in that time to clear the way for negotiations on long-term deficit reduction. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Reversal, House G.O.P. Agrees to Lift Debt Limit', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Reversal, House G.O.P. Agrees to Lift Debt Limit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-18T18:42:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Weisman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weisman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f90b4e9-5ec4-51d3-a91a-d220c59018dd', 'word_count': 1050, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f90b4e9-5ec4-51d3-a91a-d220c59018dd'}, {'abstract': 'This week, Lawrence Wright discusses Scientology; Leslie Kaufman has notes from the field; Emily Bazelon talks about Sonia Sotomayor’s new memoir; and Gregory Cowles has best-seller news. Sam Tanenhaus is the host.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2013/01/18/books/review/20books_pod.html', 'snippet': 'This week, Lawrence Wright discusses Scientology; Leslie Kaufman has notes from the field; Emily Bazelon talks about Sonia Sotomayor’s new memoir; and Gregory Cowles has best-seller news. Sam Tanenhaus is the host.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week, Lawrence Wright discusses Scientology; Leslie Kaufman has notes from the field; Emily Bazelon talks about Sonia Sotomayor’s new memoir; and Gregory Cowles has best-seller news. Sam Tanenhaus is the host.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Book Review Podcast', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Podcasts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-18T18:52:28+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/ab1c3081-009c-5a5a-8a56-0e404c148870', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/ab1c3081-009c-5a5a-8a56-0e404c148870'}, {'abstract': 'If the Mississippi River got so low that navigation had to stop, grain exports and the other commodities could get a lot more expensive very quickly.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/18/drought-points-up-critical-role-of-u-s-waterways/', 'snippet': 'If the Mississippi River got so low that navigation had to stop, grain exports and the other commodities could get a lot more expensive very quickly.', 'lead_paragraph': ' When people think of the Mississippi River, they might have visions of Mark Twain and old steamboats. But few Americans understand the vast amounts of shipping traffic that still makes its way up and down the river, part of the world’s largest navigable inland waterway.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Drought Points Up Critical Role of Waterways', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infrastructure (Public Works)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subj