has returned to 2006 levels, car sales — a sensitive economic indicator — have not. In Europe, sales continue to fall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE United States’ industrial economy has finally returned to where it was in 2006, something that few other major developed countries have accomplished. But car sales, a sign of consumer economic health and confidence, remain well below the level of six years ago across the spectrum of countries. In Europe, car sales fell last year to the lowest level since 1995.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Car Sales Worldwide Are Slow to Rebound', 'kicker': 'Off the Charts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Car Sales Worldwide Are Slow To Rebound', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-18T19:16:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Floyd Norris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Norris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6f88124-e168-533d-a4b2-e6d808ca566d', 'word_count': 558, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6f88124-e168-533d-a4b2-e6d808ca566d'}, {'abstract': 'The season has been particularly bad for older people, but appears to have peaked, with reports of new cases declining in most of the nation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.n