ponse;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Photos of The Moment | Louis Vuitton', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paris Fashion Week', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vuitton, Louis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-18T19:50:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Schohaja', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Schohaja', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/997327d4-fb9c-5965-95f1-c1a29391c37b', 'word_count': 35, 'uri': 'nyt://article/997327d4-fb9c-5965-95f1-c1a29391c37b'}, {'abstract': 'Marriage-role terminology carried too much baggage of a history I didn’t want. Until my gay friends began using the words.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/20/fashion/labels-of-married-life-in-a-new-light-modern-love.html', 'snippet': 'Marriage-role terminology carried too much baggage of a history I didn’t want. Until my gay friends began using the words.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I NOW pronounce you husband and wife,” the minister said to Anthony and me 22 years ago. Although I was thrilled about what we were undertaking, I cringed. Being pronounced a “wife” felt archaic and just plain weird. I went with it, squeamish but thankful that at least we’d gotten past the days of “man” and wife.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/fashion/20MODERNLOVE_SPAN/20MODERNLOVE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/20/fashion/20MODERNLOVE_SPAN/20MODERNLOVE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/fashion/20MODERNLOVE_SPAN/20MODERNLOVE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 664, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/fashion/20MODERNLOVE_SPAN/20MODERNLOVE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1328, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/fashion/20MODERNLOVE_SPAN/20MODERNLOVE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/20/fashion/20MODERNLOVE_SPAN/20MODERNLOVE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/fashion/20MODERNLOVE_SPAN/20MODERNLOVE_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Labels of Married Life, in a New Light', 'kicker': 'Modern Love', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Labels of Married Life, in a New Light', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Language and Languages', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Modern Love (Times Column)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-18T19:53:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margot Page', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margot', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Page', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b5333aa-a54f-5069-b3c6-c3ada2b581be', 'word_count': 1489, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b5333aa-a54f-5069-b3c6-c3ada2b581be'}, {'abstract': 'Debt limit crisis, over (we think).', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/18/not-with-a-bang-but-with-a-whimper/', 'snippet': 'Debt limit crisis, over (we think).', 'lead_paragraph': 'When you’re wrong, you’re wrong. I thought that by ruling out any way to bypass the debt limit, the White House was setting itself up, at least potentially, for an ignominious cave-in. But it appears that the strategy has worked, and it’s the Republicans giving up. I’m happy to concede that the president and team called this one right.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Not With A Bang But With A Whimper', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-18T20:06:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eda779b4-566b-55b6-a398-6fc790e91ece', 'word_count': 191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eda779b4-566b-55b6-a398-6fc790e91ece'}, {'abstract': 'Fashion has turned decidedly away from the corporate world this Paris men’s fashion season.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/18/down-and-out-in-paris/', 'snippet': 'Fashion has turned decidedly away from the corporate world this Paris men’s fashion season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fashion has turned decidedly away from the corporate world this season. It wasn’t that long ago that Raf Simons and Kim Jones of Louis Vuitton were making elite power statements; during the recession, Mr. Simons predicted that young men, concerned about jobs, would want tailored clothes. Other designers didn’t stint on the polish.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Down and Out in Paris', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Down and Out in Paris', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Kim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Simons, Raf', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'van Noten, Dries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vuitton, Louis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Watanabe, Junya', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-18T20:07:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b9fe0ad-9b29-5e7c-b28c-de4c3fd241a8', 'word_count': 533, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b9fe0ad-9b29-5e7c-b28c-de4c3fd241a8'}, {'abstract': 'Rangers defenseman Michael Sauer still has not returned to the ice 13 months after sustaining a concussion.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/18/sauers-return-from-concussion-still-uncertain/', 'snippet': 'Rangers defenseman Michael Sauer still has not returned to the ice 13 months after sustaining a concussion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GREENBURGH — The one injury blemish on an otherwise healthy Rangers roster heading into the abbreviated 2013 N.H.L. season is defenseman Michael Sauer, who is still out indefinitely after the concussion he suffered more than 13 months ago.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/sports/hockey/19sauer/19sauer-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 725, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/sports/hockey/19sauer/19sauer-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1451, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/sports/hockey/19sauer/19sauer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/19/sports/hockey/19sauer/19sauer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/sports/hockey/19sauer/19sauer-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sauer’s Return from Concussion Still Uncertain', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Rangers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-18T20:07:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a562b763-e49a-553c-9059-0104e6eaeb5d', 'word_count': 301, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a562b763-e49a-553c-9059-0104e6eaeb5d'}, {'abstract': 'The country’s working-age population is on the decline.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/18/will-china-have-to-abandon-its-one-child-rule/', 'snippet': 'The country’s working-age population is on the decline.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chinese officials released data on Friday showing that the country’s economy grew faster than previously anticipated at the end of last year. Investors greeted that news enthusiastically while virtually ignoring another, more worrying development: The country’s working age population has officially started declining. In 2012, for the first time in recent memory, the number of Chinese between the ages of 15 and 59 fell — by 3.45 million to 937.27 million.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Will China Have to Abandon Its One-Child Rule?', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Population', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xi Jinping', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-18T20:08:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vikas Bajaj', 'person': [{'firstname