d and Times reporters in Washington will be providing live updates and analysis starting at 9 a.m. on Monday and running through the inaugural ceremony.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/18/live-coverage-of-obamas-second-inaugural/', 'snippet': 'President Obama begins his second term in office this weekend and Times reporters in Washington will be providing live updates and analysis starting at 9 a.m. on Monday and running through the inaugural ceremony.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As President Obama begins his second term in office, Times reporters in Washington are providing live updates and analysis. Mr. Obama declared that the country was “made for this moment,” but said that the nation must confront the needs of a rising middle class.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Live Coverage of Obama’s Second Inauguration', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inaugurations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-18T21:47:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ecce895-9292-5885-b53f-fa0b6d8cc6ae', 'word_count': 10341, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ecce895-9292-5885-b53f-fa0b6d8cc6ae'}, {'abstract': 'The Philadelphia Orchestra, conducted by its music director, Yannick Nézet-Séguin, performed a concert of works by Ravel, Szymanowski and Shostakovich at Carnegie Hall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/19/arts/music/philadelphia-orchestra-with-nezet-seguin-at-carnegie-hall.html', 'snippet': 'The Philadelphia Orchestra, conducted by its music director, Yannick Nézet-Séguin, performed a concert of works by Ravel, Szymanowski and Shostakovich at Carnegie Hall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the players of an excellent student orchestra want to pay special tribute to an inspiring conductor at the end of a concert, they stomp and shuffle their feet during ovations. On Thursday night at Carnegie Hall it was not a bunch of exuberant students but the veteran players of the great Philadelphia Orchestra who stomped their feet for Yannick Nézet-Séguin, the 37-year-old Canadian conductor now in his first season as the orchestra’s music director. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/arts/19YANNICK/19YANNICK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 275, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/19/arts/19YANNICK/19YANNICK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 275}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/arts/19YANNICK/19YANNICK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 470, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/arts/19YANNICK/19YANNICK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 940, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/arts/19YANNICK/19YANNICK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/19/arts/19YANNICK/19YANNICK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/arts/19YANNICK/19YANNICK-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Foot-Stomping Night at Carnegie Hall', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Foot-Stomping Night at Carnegie Hall', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tommasini, Anthony', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Philadelphia Orchestra', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carnegie Hall', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nezet-Seguin, Yannick', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-18T21:50:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Tommasini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tommasini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/2dafb3d5-6916-5eb0-bebd-14800f8a2882', 'word_count': 584, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2dafb3d5-6916-5eb0-bebd-14800f8a2882'}, {'abstract': 'A 15-room Carnegie Hill town house, 25 feet wide, was given an external face-lift in 1921 by Cass Gilbert, whose most famous creation was the Woolworth Building.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/18/big-ticket-sold-for-24912140/', 'snippet': 'A 15-room Carnegie Hill town house, 25 feet wide, was given an external face-lift in 1921 by Cass Gilbert, whose most famous creation was the Woolworth Building.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An unusual Carnegie Hill mansion of majestic proportions — it is 25 feet wide — and distinguished by the ultimate in urban convenience items, an en-suite garage offering direct and discreet entry into the home, sold for $24,912,140 and was the most expensive sale of t