er is being offered in connection with this singular touring production, which runs in New York through Feb. 3. And the experience of that meal may come closer to admitting you to the world of this play’s performers than anything you will subsequently see onstage. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/arts/19BREAD/19BREAD-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 333, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/19/arts/19BREAD/19BREAD-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 333}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/arts/19BREAD/19BREAD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 568, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/arts/19BREAD/19BREAD-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1136, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/arts/19BREAD/19BREAD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/19/arts/19BREAD/19BREAD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/arts/19BREAD/19BREAD-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nourished by Language That Is Based on Touching', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nourished By Language That Is Based On Touching', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nalagaat', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disabilities', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deafness', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blindness', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Senses and Sensation', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tel Aviv (Israel)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bread', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-18T23:21:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff565004-53ad-59c3-8771-98433b2b33b6', 'word_count': 497, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff565004-53ad-59c3-8771-98433b2b33b6'}, {'abstract': 'In “Magical,” at New York Live Arts, the director Annie Dorsen and the choreographer Anne Juren tease and challenge feminist performance art of the 1960s and ’70s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/19/arts/dance/magical-by-annie-dorsen-and-anne-juren-at-new-york-live-arts.html', 'snippet': 'In “Magical,” at New York Live Arts, the director Annie Dorsen and the choreographer Anne Juren tease and challenge feminist performance art of the 1960s and ’70s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Marina Abramovic once danced naked in public for six hours, with a piece of fabric covering her face. Yoko Ono let audience members snip away her clothing and underwear. Carolee Schneemann pulled the text of her performance out of her own vagina. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/arts/19MAGICAL/19MAGICAL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 968, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/arts/19MAGICAL/19MAGICAL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1937, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/arts/19MAGICAL/19MAGICAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/19/arts/19MAGICAL/19MAGICAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/arts/19MAGICAL/19MAGICAL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Now You See Her, and Now You See More of Her', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Now You See Her, and Now You See More of Her', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dorsen, Annie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Live Arts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coil Festival', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-18T23:28:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Seibert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seibert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/398abbc5-a52c-5614-b2df-944de64ba2f7', 'word_count': 554, 'uri': 'nyt://article/398abbc5-a52c-5614-b2df-944de64ba2f7'}, {'abstract': 'Unique, a restaurant that opened in Oceanside two months ago, serves lobster tacos, creamy mushroom soup and sushi rolls from a varied menu of small plates.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/20/nyregion/a-review-of-unique-in-oceanside.html', 'snippet': 'Unique, a restaurant that opened in Oceanside two months ago, serves lobster tacos, creamy mushroom soup and sushi rolls from a varied menu of small plates.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Unusual” might be a better name for Unique, a restaurant that opened in Oceanside two months ago. It is hardly the only place around that mixes sushi and Japanese standards with Western dishes, adding cross-cultural creations like a crispy lobster wrap in phyllo dough. But Unique does it very well.', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/nyregion/20DINELI3/20DINELI3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/20/nyregion/20DINELI3/20DINELI3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/nyregion/20DINELI3/20DINELI3-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/nyr