', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/01/19/us/politics/new-york-times-cbs-poll-obama.html', 'snippet': 'The latest polling measured American attitudes toward President Obama at the beginning of his second term.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The latest polling measured American attitudes toward President Obama at the beginning of his second term.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Latest New York Times/CBS News Polling Results', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-18T23:30:50+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/c4fc9dd8-27bb-55a5-b680-801913e3eb14', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/c4fc9dd8-27bb-55a5-b680-801913e3eb14'}, {'abstract': 'As the president begins his second term, he holds the approval of 51 percent of Americans, according to a poll by The New York Times and CBS News.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/19/us/politics/entering-2nd-term-obama-has-51-percent-approval-rating.html', 'snippet': 'As the president begins his second term, he holds the approval of 51 percent of Americans, according to a poll by The New York Times and CBS News.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama begins his second term on Sunday with Americans cautiously optimistic about both the years ahead and his stewardship, but more polarized politically than four years ago and with less lofty hopes.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Poll Finds Most Back Obama, With a Split on Party Lines', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Poll Finds Most Back Obama, With a Split On Party Lines', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Calmes, Jackie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thee-Brenan, Megan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-18T23:31:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jackie Calmes and Megan Thee-Brenan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jackie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Calmes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Megan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thee-Brenan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/50ab5a75-bdd8-5cdc-9524-c9d0ee9365c8', 'word_count': 1151, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50ab5a75-bdd8-5cdc-9524-c9d0ee9365c8'}, {'abstract': 'Horror series are multiplying on television, with “Do No Harm” and “The Following” among the latest, but the medium imposes special challenges for creators.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/20/arts/television/do-no-harm-the-walking-dead-and-other-tv-horror.html', 'snippet': 'Horror series are multiplying on television, with “Do No Harm” and “The Following” among the latest, but the medium imposes special challenges for creators.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TELEVISION, long the home of monstrous behavior, has never seemed like the ideal medium for actual monsters. TV has tried to generate chills over the years, but for every occasional success like “The Twilight Zone” or “The X-Files,” there’s a “Kolchak: The Night Stalker” or “666 Park Avenue” that was quickly killed off. If you’re looking for legitimate, jump-from-your-chair scares, the conventional wisdom goes, you’re usually better off in a theater. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/arts/20HARM2_SPAN/20HARM2_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/20/arts/20HARM2_SPAN/20HARM2_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/arts/20HARM2_SPAN/20HARM2_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/arts/20HARM2_SPAN/20HARM2_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/arts/20HARM2_SPAN/20HARM2_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/20/arts/20HARM2_SPAN/20HARM2_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/arts/20HARM2_SPAN/20HARM2_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Helpful Hints for Household Horror', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Helpful Hints for Household Horror', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-18T23:36:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Craig Tomashoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Craig', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tomashoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6fcb97c1-e60e-5a5f-8c19-82aae01e29cb', 'word_count': 998, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6fcb97c1-e60e-5a5f-8c19-82aae01e29cb'}, {'abstract': 'In New York City Ballet’s “Swan Lake,” “Allegro Brillante” and “Tschaikovsky Suite No. 3,” you can feel the many ways in which Balanchine choreography intensifies the Tchaikovsky experience.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/19/arts/dance/new-york-city-ballet-at-koch-theater.html', 'snippet': 'In New York City Ballet’s “Swan Lake,” “Allegro Brillante” and “Tschaikovsky Suite No. 3,” you can feel the many ways in which Balanchine choreography intensifies the Tchaikovsky experience.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Deeper into Tchaikovsky! Four weeks of New York City Ballet’s current season are devoted to music by this composer, and much of the programming consists of works by George Balanchine. In each of the three ballets in Thursday’s program — the one-act “Swan Lake,” “Allegro Brillante” and “Tschaikovsky Suite No. 3” — you could feel the many ways Balanchine choreography intensifies the Tchaikovsky experience. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/arts/19BRILLANTE/19BRILLANTE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/19/arts/1