Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f15dc02-22a4-5d31-b07b-33826da96ec5', 'word_count': 854, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f15dc02-22a4-5d31-b07b-33826da96ec5'}, {'abstract': 'José James has followed a winding road, through Europe, two record labels and many musical idioms, to arrive at his album “No Beginning No End.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/20/arts/music/jose-jamess-no-beginning-no-end.html', 'snippet': 'José James has followed a winding road, through Europe, two record labels and many musical idioms, to arrive at his album “No Beginning No End.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE singer José James’s cool and confident new album, “No Beginning No End,” to be released by Blue Note next week, sounds like the result of the black-pop continuum, jazz and soul and hip-hop and R&B, slow-cooked for more than 50 years. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/arts/20JAMES_SPAN/20JAMES_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/20/arts/20JAMES_SPAN/20JAMES_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/arts/20JAMES_SPAN/20JAMES_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/arts/20JAMES_SPAN/20JAMES_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'heigh