on': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/world/briefs-pillay/briefs-pillay-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 670, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/world/briefs-pillay/briefs-pillay-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1529, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Commissioner Urges Action on Syria', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | United Nations', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Commissioner Urges Action on Syria', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pillay, Navi', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-19T00:42:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil MacFarquhar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacFarquhar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d15d57ac-e49d-5487-ae18-71d93f5ef0d4', 'word_count': 135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d15d57ac-e49d-5487-ae18-71d93f5ef0d4'}, {'abstract': 'The executive chef at BUtterfield 8, in White Plains, wants the restaurant to be known for more than the drinks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/20/nyregion/a-review-of-butterfield-8-in-white-plains.html', 'snippet': 'The executive chef at BUtterfield 8, in White Plains, wants the restaurant to be known for more than the drinks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You might enter BUtterfield 8, a four-month-old restaurant in White Plains, look around, and expect it to offer typical pub fare: nachos, burgers, maybe a pasta dish. The front room is taken up by a massive, four-sided bar and there are at least six wide-screen TVs, all showing sports. The dining room is a handsome, wood-paneled space with an open kitchen, but it is down several steps from the bar area, making the drinking scene appear to be BUtterfield 8’s focus.', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/nyregion/20DINEWE1/20DINEWE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/20/nyregion/20DINEWE1/20DINEWE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/nyregion/20DINEWE1/20DINEWE1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/nyregion/20DINEWE1/20DINEWE1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/nyregion/20DINEWE1/20DINEWE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/20/nyregion/20DINEWE1/20DINEWE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/nyregion/20DINEWE1/20DINEWE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'More Than Pub Fare on an Ambitious Menu', 'kicker': 'Westchester Dining | White Plains', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'More Than Pub Fare On an Ambitious Menu', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'White Plains (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BUtterfield 8 (White Plains, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-19T00:43:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily DeNitto', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'DeNitto', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c34fd96-4ee8-5cf0-a65d-bd4473e9471d', 'word_count': 830, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c34fd96-4ee8-5cf0-a65d-bd4473e9471d'}, {'abstract': 'President François Hollande called the killing of a French journalist in Syria an “odious act” and paid tribute to “all the journalists who pay with their lives for their commitment to freedom of the press.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/19/world/europe/france-a-tribute-to-a-fallen-journalist.html', 'snippet': 'President François Hollande called the killing of a French journalist in Syria an “odious act” and paid tribute to “all the journalists who pay with their lives for their commitment to freedom of the press.”', 'lead_paragraph': ' President François Hollande on Friday called the killing of a French journalist in Syria an “odious act” and paid tribute to “all the journalists who pay with their lives for their commitment to freedom of the press.” The journalist, Yves Debay, 58, was killed Thursday in Aleppo, apparently by sniper fire, though the circumstances of his death remain unclear. In Syria on Friday, another journalist, a correspondent for Al Jazeera, Mohamed al-Massalma, was shot to death by a sniper while covering the fighting near Dara’a in the south, The Associated Press reported. Also, two car bombs exploded in Dara’a and a rocket slammed into a building in Aleppo, killing at least 12 people, The A.P. said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France: A Tribute to a Fallen Journalist', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France: A Tribute to a Fallen Journalist', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Debay, Yves', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hollande, Francois', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-19T00:50:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maïa de la Baume', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maïa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'de la Baume', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e6ce22e-d419-5216-8805-0dd55b553b6e', 'word_count': 116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e6ce22e-d419-5216-8805-0dd55b553b6e'}, {'abstract': 'A senior Pakistani diplomat said Friday that his government would release all Afghan Taliban prisoners in its custody, bolstering hopes for peace negotiations with the insurgents.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/19/world/asia/pakistan-taliban-prisoners-to-be-freed.html', 'snippet': 'A senior Pakistani diplomat said Friday that his government would release all Afghan Taliban prisoners in its custody, bolstering hopes for peace negotiations with the insurgents.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A senior Pakistani diplomat said Friday that his government would release all Afghan Taliban prisoners in its custody, bolstering hopes for peace negotiations with the insurgents. But the diplomat, Jalil Jilani, a high-ranking Foreign Ministry official, did not specify when the detainees would be released, and a Western diplomat in Islamabad, speaking on the customary condition of anonymity, noted that Pakistan had previously stated its intention to eventually release all Afghan Taliban detainees. Mr. Jilani declined to specify whether Abdul Ghani Baradar, a former Taliban deputy leader who was captured in Pakistan with American help, would be among those released, saying only that all prisoners would be freed and that “2013 will see concrete outcomes in the peace process.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pakistan: Taliban Prisoners to Be Freed', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pakistan: Taliban Prisoners to Be Freed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-19T00:51:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Declan Walsh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Declan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Walsh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/f44e5633-c1be-5bb8-9b15-f8168e81db39', 'word_count': 119, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f44e5633-c1be-5bb8-9b15-f8168e81db39'}, {'abstract': 'Barack Obama should examine the setbacks faced by presidents who served before him.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/19/opinion/how-obama-can-learn-from-failure.html', 'snippet': 'Barack Obama should examine the setbacks faced by presidents who served before him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHAPEL HILL, N.C. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Obama Can Learn From Failure', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How Obama Can Learn From Failure', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carter, Jimmy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Monroe, James', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cleveland, Grover', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coolidge, Calvin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidents and Presidency (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-19T00:54:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. Gerhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Gerhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/d62618b0-eddd-53eb-81de-ae25167e409a', 'word_count': 1079, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d62618b0-eddd-53eb-81de-ae25167e409a'}, {'abstract': 'C. Ray Nagin was indicted by a federal grand jury on Friday on 21 counts including conspiracy, bribery and money laundering.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/19/us/c-ray-nagin-former-mayor-of-new-orleans-indicted-on-corruption-charges.html', 'snippet': 'C. Ray Nagin was indicted by a federal grand jury on Friday on 21 counts including conspiracy, bribery and money laundering.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW ORLEANS — C. Ray Nagin, the former mayor of this city who fulminated against the federal government’s response to Hurricane Katrina but became for many a symbol of the shortcomings of government himself, was indicted by a federal grand jury on Friday on 21 counts including conspiracy, bribery and money laundering.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/us/NAGIN/NAGIN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 807, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/us/NAGIN/NAGIN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1942, 'width': 1530, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/us/NAGIN/NAGIN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/19/us/NAGIN/NAGIN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/us/NAGIN/NAGIN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Former Mayor of New Orleans Is Charged in Sweeping Corruption Case', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Former Mayor of New Orleans Is Charged in Sweeping Corruption Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nagin, C Ray', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Orleans (La)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Money Laundering', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Katrina (2005)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-19T00:57:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Campbell Robertson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Campbell', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robertson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8de4f73d-b099-5e2a-af3a-7ecb19b04645', 'word_count': 1167, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8de4f73d-b099-5e2a-af3a-7ecb19b04645'}, {'abstract': 'People like me who suffer from depression need to be kept safe from ourselves. I don’t want a gun in my house.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/19/opinion/please-take-away-my-right-to-a-gun.html', 'snippet': 'People like me who suffer from depression need to be kept safe from ourselves. I don’t want a gun in my house.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A FEW years ago, I awoke at 2:30 a.m. to more than a “rapping, rapping at my chamber door.” It was a full-force pounding of a body trying to break into my little house in Washington, D.C. It was the sound and scenario that, as a single woman living alone, I feared more than spiders in the house.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Please Take Away My Right to a Gun', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Please Take Away My Right to a Gun', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Button, Wendy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newtown, Conn, Shooting (2012)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Depression (Mental)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suicides and Suicide Attempts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-19T01:03:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Wendy Button', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Wendy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Button', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7987fac-7762-5de3-98f2-55b8e4174909', 'word_count': 983, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7987fac-7762-5de3-98f2-55b8e4174909'}, {'abstract': 'Dozens of plays will be staged in New Jersey in coming months, and sometimes cooperation between theater companies helps to transform an idea into a reality.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/20/nyregion/to-raise-the-curtain-new-jersey-theaters-are-pulling-together.html', 'snippet': 'Dozens of plays will be staged in New Jersey in coming months, and sometimes cooperation between theater companies helps to transform an idea into a reality.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New Jersey theaters are lighting up again this month and next after a post-holiday lull. In the months ahead, they will be producing more than a dozen plays that are new to local stages. And to make those plays happen, a certain amount of cooperation is often involved.', 'print_section': 'NJ', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/nyregion/20ARTSNJ1_SPAN/20ARTSNJ1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/20/nyregion/20ARTSNJ1_SPAN/20ARTSNJ1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/nyregion/20ARTSNJ1_SPAN/20ARTSNJ1_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/nyregion/20ARTSNJ1_SPAN/20ARTSNJ1_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1360, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/nyregion/20ARTSNJ1_SPAN/20ARTSNJ1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/20/nyregion/20ARTSNJ1_SPAN/20ARTSNJ1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/nyregion/20ARTSNJ1_SPAN/20ARTSNJ1_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'To Raise the Curtain, Pulling Together', 'kicker': 'Arts | New Jersey', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Raise the Curtain, Pulling Together', 'nam