ian-and-ronald-perelman-in-a-new-legal-clash.html', 'snippet': 'Ronald O. Perelman and Larry Gagosian, friends for years as well as business partners, are now enemies in court.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After failing to persuade the billionaire collector Ronald O. Perelman to drop his lawsuit over an art deal gone sour, the powerhouse gallery mogul Larry Gagosian switched to attack mode on Friday. He described Mr. Perelman — his longtime friend, client and business partner — as a “deadbeat” and “bully” in court papers, saying he should be sanctioned by the judge for bringing the “frivolous” action. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/arts/19LAWSUIT1/19LAWSUIT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 495, 'width': 421, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/arts/19LAWSUIT1/19LAWSUIT1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 495, 'width': 421, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/arts/19LAWSUIT1/19LAWSUIT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/19/arts/19LAWSUIT1/19LAWSUIT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/arts/19LAWSUIT1/19LAWSUIT1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Blow in Art Clash of Titans', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Blow In Art Clash Of Titans', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gagosian, Larry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perelman, Ronald O', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-19T01:24:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e42fbcd-3458-546f-a57e-8b6d1ee8eefe', 'word_count': 1011, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e42fbcd-3458-546f-a57e-8b6d1ee8eefe'}, {'abstract': 'More than 40 days of violence have shown the fragility of the hopes generated from the Good Friday agreement, the blueprint for the power-sharing government in Northern Ireland.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/19/world/europe/new-northern-ireland-violence-may-be-about-more-than-the-british-flag.html', 'snippet': 'More than 40 days of violence have shown the fragility of the hopes generated from the Good Friday agreement, the blueprint for the power-sharing government in Northern Ireland.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BELFAST, Northern Ireland — For more than six weeks, it has been a dismal case of back-to-the-future, a crudely sectarian upheaval that has defied all attempts at peacemaking.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/world/ulster1/ulster1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/19/world/ulster1/ulster1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/world/ulster1/ulster1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/world/ulster1/ulster1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1362, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/world/ulster1/ulster1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/19/world/ulster1/ulster1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/world/ulster1/ulster1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Violence in Belfast May Be About More Than the Flag', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Violence in Belfast May Be About More Than the Flag', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burns, John F', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flags, Emblems and Insignia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Belfast (Northern Ireland)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Northern Ireland', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-19T01:27:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By John F. Burns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Burns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/896b46a2-ce07-542d-818e-4c18848592c6', 'word_count': 1329, 'uri': 'nyt://article/896b46a2-ce07-542d-818e-4c18848592c6'}, {'abstract': 'Sandburg scholars think the poem, “The Revolver,” dates to the 1920s, or perhaps earlier.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/19/books/carl-sandburg-poem-discovered.html', 'snippet': 'Sandburg scholars think the poem, “The Revolver,” dates to the 1920s, or perhaps earlier.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Except for the smudgy typewriter strokes, it reads like up-to-date social commentary: a poem on the fearsome power of a gun. But the brief work was composed some nine decades ago by a literary giant, Carl Sandburg, and until days ago, scholars had no idea it existed. For years Ernie Gullerud, a volunteer helping to create a digital archive of Sandburg’s voluminous output at the University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign, has pulled a poem from a folder, recorded its title and first and last lines, and then moved on to the next page. But last week, a short poem, “The Revolver,” caught his attention. “I said, ‘Hey, this is as pertinent today as it was then,’ so I brought it to the librarians,” said Mr. Gullerud, 83. After consulting with experts, the staff of the university’s Rare Book and Manuscript Library concluded that it was a genuine, unpublished and unknown work. “The paper is his paper, and the typewriter is his typewriter,” Valerie Hotchkiss, the library’s director, said. Sandburg scholars think the poem dates to the 1920s, or perhaps earlier.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Carl Sandburg Poem Discovered', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Carl Sandburg Poem Discovered', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sandburg, Carl', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Illinois', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-19T01:29:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Pérez-Peña', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pérez-Peña', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d82c94b3-f469-56d5-abb4-5cc8d9f9065a', 'word_count': 180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d82c94b3-f469-56d5-abb4-5cc8d9f9065a'}, {'abstract': 'Citing health reasons, the president of the University of California, Mark Yudof, said Friday that he would step down at the end of August.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/19/education/california-university-president-to-quit.html', 'snippet': 'Citing health reasons, the president of the University of California, Mark Yudof, said Friday that he would step down at the end of August.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Citing health reasons, the president of the University of California, Mark Yudof, said Friday that he would step down at the end of August. Mr. Yudof, who has overseen the 10-college system for five years, said he would teach law at the University of California, Berkeley. Mr. Yudof said that the series of budget cuts the system had faced seemed to be ending. “We are not fully in the clear, but we are much closer than we were even a few months ago,” he said. In the state budget proposed last week, the system received $250 million more than last year. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California: University President to Quit', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | West', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'California: University President To Quit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yudof, Mark G', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of California', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-19T01:30:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Medina', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Medina', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/6480976f-580e-5dea-a453-4538d779bbae', 'word_count': 101, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6480976f-580e-5dea-a453-4538d779bbae'}, {'abstract': 'A show at the Heckscher Museum of Art commemorates the centennial of Manhattan’s 1913 Armory Show that introduced European modernism to the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/20/nyregion/a-review-of-modernizing-america-at-the-heckscher-museum-of-art.html', 'snippet': 'A show at the Heckscher Museum of Art commemorates the centennial of Manhattan’s 1913 Armory Show that introduced European modernism to the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A hundred years ago next month, a group of progressive artists who opposed the ideas and exhibition practices of the National Academy of Design organized a show titled simply “International Exhibition of Modern Art.” Composed of more than 1,300 works of art, it became famous for introducing European modernism to the United States and is remembered by the name of its locale: the 69th Regiment Armory on Lexington Avenue in Manhattan. This winter, the Heckscher Museum of Art in Huntington has mounted a show commemorating the Armory Show’s centennial.', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/nyregion/20ARTSLI4/20ARTSLI4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1119, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/20/nyregion/20ARTSLI4/20ARTSLI4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1119}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/nyregion/20ARTSLI4/20ARTSLI4-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 550, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/nyregion/20ARTSLI4/20ARTSLI4-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1099, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/nyregion/20ARTSLI4/20ARTSLI4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/20/nyregion/20ARTSLI4/20ARTSLI4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/nyregion/20ARTSLI4/20ARTSLI4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'European Modernism, as Told by Americans', 'kicker': 'Arts | Long Island', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'European Modernism, as Told by Americans', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Huntington (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Heckscher Museum of Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARMORY SHOW, THE INTERNATIONAL FAIR OF NEW ART (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sculpture', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-19T01:31:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Schwendener', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwendener', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f58fc795-9f16-59fd-adb1-76a635c8c131', 'word_count': 931, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f58fc795-9f16-59fd-adb1-76a635c8c131'}, {'abstract': 'The Interior Department will issue revised rules on the use of hydraulic fracturing to drill for oil and gas on public lands, officials said Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/19/us/regulations-on-fracking-are-revised.html', 'snippet': 'The Interior Department will issue revised rules on the use of hydraulic fracturing to drill for oil and gas on public lands, officials said Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': '\xa0 \xa0The Interior Department will issue revised rules on the use of hydraulic fracturing to drill for oil and gas on public lands, officials said Friday. The rules will replace a proposal released last May that was opposed by oil companies and state officials, who said they conflict with regulations in use on private lands and will add cost to drilling operations.\xa0Details of the revised proposal were not disclosed, but an Interior Department official said it would require disclosure of chemicals used in the process, control of methane emissions and careful management of drilling wastewater. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Regulations on Fracking Are Revised', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Environment', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Regulations On Fracking Are Revised', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hydraulic Fracturing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Interior Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-19T01:31:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By John M. Broder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/885e4b32-6e0f-5956-9b04-b2dfed009b0a', 'word_count': 95, 'uri': 'nyt://article/885e4b32-6e0f-5956-9b04-b2dfed009b0a'}, {'abstract': 'As the second part of Lance Armstrong’s televised confession that he doped and lied his way to seven Tour de France titles is broadcast on Friday, The Lede will round up reaction and provide real-time fact-checking and analysis.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/18/live-updates-on-armstrongs-confession/', 'snippet': 'As the second part of Lance Armstrong’s televised confession that he doped and lied his way to seven Tour de France titles is broadcast on Friday, The Lede will round up reaction and provide real-time fact-checking and analysis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the second part of Lance Armstrong’s televised confession that he doped and lied his way to seven Tour de France titles is broadcast on the Oprah Winfrey Network Friday night, The Lede will have real-time fact-checking and analysis from New York Times reporters, including Juliet Macur and Naila-Jean Meyers. We will also round up reactions from fans, bloggers, journalists and fellow riders once the broadcast and live stream gets underway, at 9 p.m. Eastern Time. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/10/10/us/10lede_onion/10lede_onion-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/10/10/us/10lede_onion/10lede_onion-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/10/10/us/10lede_onion/10lede_onion-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/10/10/us/10lede_onion/10lede_onion-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/10/10/us/10lede_onion/10lede_onion-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Live Updates on Armstrong’s Confession', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bicycles and Bicycling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doping (Sports)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tour de France (Bicycle Race)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ARMSTRONG, LANCE', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-19T01:35:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/729ea92d-6ccd-58b0-90a8-d656aa3857ab', 'word_count': 3624, 'uri': 'nyt://article/729ea92d-6ccd-58b0-90a8-d656aa3857ab'}, {'abstract': 'Galileo’s achievement was the end of geocentrism, but ignorance and magical thinking continue to this day.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/19/opinion/galileo-the-starry-messenger.html', 'snippet': 'Galileo’s achievement was the end of geocentrism, but ignorance and magical thinking continue to this day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is a month when anyone with a telescope or good binoculars can gaze up at one of the brightest objects in the night sky and revisit a staggering achievement in astronomy: Galileo’s discovery, over several January days in 1610, of Jupiter’s four largest moons.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/opinion/19galileo/19galileo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 733, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/opinion/19galileo/19galileo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1466, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJu