a-to-remove-invasive-body-scanners.html', 'snippet': 'The Transportation Security Administration said the maker of the scanners failed to meet a deadline for new software that protected passengers’ privacy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — After years of complaints by passengers and members of Congress, the Transportation Security Administration said Friday that it would begin removing the controversial full-body scanners that produce revealing images of airline travelers beginning this summer.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Unpopular Full-Body Scanners to Be Removed From Airports', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Unpopular Full-Body Scanners To Be Removed From Airports', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nixon, Ron', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Airport Security', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Scanning Devices', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transportation Security Administration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-19T01:57:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Nixon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nixon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a587c092-8dc5-5947-a053-5cf77e6ecc5a', 'word_count': 286, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a587c092-8dc5-5947-a053-5cf77e6ecc5a'}, {'abstract': 'When I called Thomas DiNapoli, the New York State Comptroller, about a pension fund’s investment in gun manufacturers, I got a surprising reply.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/18/and-then-theres-new-york/', 'snippet': 'When I called Thomas DiNapoli, the New York State Comptroller, about a pension fund’s investment in gun manufacturers, I got a surprising reply.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is one response to my queries about investors and Cerberus that I was unable to fit into my column. But I would like to dwell here for a moment on the response of the New York State Common Retirement Fund to the Newtown massacre. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'And Then There’s New York…', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Firearms', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newtown, Conn, Shooting (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DiNapoli, Thomas P', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Freedom Group Family of Cos', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York State Common Retirement Fund', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Office of the Comptroller (NYS)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Smith & Wesson', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wedgwood Baptist Church', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Newtown (Conn)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Norway', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oregon', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-19T02:02:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Nocera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nocera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'N