r the city’s schools.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/19/opinion/the-teacher-evaluation-fight-in-new-york-city.html', 'snippet': 'Failure to reach agreement might mean the loss of hundreds of millions of dollars in state and federal money for the city’s schools.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Bloomberg administration’s failure to reach an agreement with the New York City teachers’ union on the details of a state-mandated teacher evaluation system by the Thursday deadline has cost the city hundreds of millions of dollars in state money. The State Education Department notified the city on Friday that it would face even harsher penalties if it failed to promptly establish a timeline and budget for complying with the law. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Teacher Evaluation Fight', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Teacher Evaluation Fight', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Performance Evaluations (Labor)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Race to the Top Fund', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Department (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Federation of Teachers', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-19T02:14:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/1bef1d95-b517-55ba-82ed-0fdb21ad7401', 'word_count': 584, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1bef1d95-b517-55ba-82ed-0fdb21ad7401'}, {'abstract': 'The release of minutes from Fed policy meetings before the financial storm have revived a standoff from when the Treasury secretary was head of the New York Fed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/19/business/transcripts-revive-a-tiff-of-two-fed-presidents.html', 'snippet': 'The release of minutes from Fed policy meetings before the financial storm have revived a standoff from when the Treasury secretary was head of the New York Fed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the financial crisis gathered strength in the summer of 2007, two regional Federal Reserve presidents had a curt exchange over whether one of them — Timothy F. Geithner, now the Treasury secretary — might have shared too much information with bankers.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Transcripts Revive a Tiff of Two Fed Presidents', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Transcripts Revive a Tiff Of Two Fed Presidents', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schwartz, Nelson D', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Geithner, Timothy F', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lacker, Jeffrey M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interest Rates', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-19T02:21:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nelson D. Schwartz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nelson', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0ab0e50-848e-5492-84db-bfab67064cb9', 'word_count': 489, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0ab0e50-848e-5492-84db-bfab67064cb9'}, {'abstract': 'In spite of Newtown and all the other mass shootings, a look at one Cerberus investment fund would suggest that it’s still all about making money, not saving lives.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/19/opinion/nocera-investing-in-guns.html', 'snippet': 'In spite of Newtown and all the other mass shootings, a look at one Cerberus investment fund would suggest that it’s still all about making money, not saving lives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2006, Cerberus Capital Management, the private equity firm run by the secretive financier Steven Feinberg, set out to raise $6.5 billion in a new fund called Cerberus Institutional Partners Series IV. Feinberg’s reputation for extracting value from troubled companies — by replacing management, shuttering facilities and creating “efficiencies” — was such that by May 2007, when the fund was finally closed, it had gotten commitments for nearly $1 billion more than it had sought.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-ci