alue': 'Lazarenko, Pavlo', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-19T02:38:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By David M. Herszenhorn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e5b3860-9f77-5083-af29-7f74581bbc5b', 'word_count': 504, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e5b3860-9f77-5083-af29-7f74581bbc5b'}, {'abstract': 'The stock market often rises at the start of the new year — but beware the temptation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/20/opinion/sunday/check-the-calendar-before-you-buy-that-stock.html', 'snippet': 'The stock market often rises at the start of the new year — but beware the temptation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN the first three weeks or so of trading this year, the Standard & Poor’s 500-stock index, a measure of the broad market, has climbed more than 4 percent — and on Jan. 18, in fact, closed at its highest level since December 2007. Last January, the S.&P. 500 rose 4.4 percent — a blistering pace that, if kept up for the rest of 2012, would have translated into a compound annual return of nearly 67 percent. (Alas, it did not.) January 2011 was also a hot one for stocks, its monthly return translating into an annualized gain of 31 percent.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/sunday-review/20GRAY/20GRAY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 767, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo',