1853-417e-5bcf-ae7d-f87a2884aedb'}, {'abstract': 'Three pallets of floor tile, ordered by a man using someone else’s credit card, were delivered in front of a Brooklyn building and haven’t been seen since.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/19/nyregion/an-unwitting-buyer-and-8500-pounds-of-italian-tile-that-vanished.html', 'snippet': 'Three pallets of floor tile, ordered by a man using someone else’s credit card, were delivered in front of a Brooklyn building and haven’t been seen since.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The porcelain tile, about 8,500 pounds of it, was imported from Modena, Italy, by a family-owned tile store in Brooklyn. What happened to that load of tile one afternoon in November is anyone’s guess. In a carefully orchestrated caper, with a buyer who did not know he had bought anything and a trucking company delivering the load to a home that was not expecting it, the tile vanished on a busy Brooklyn avenue. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/nyregion/CRIMESCENE1/CRIMESCENE1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 382, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/19/nyregion/CRIMESCENE1/CRIMESCENE1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 382}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/nyregion/CRIMESCENE1/CRIMESCENE1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 651, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/nyregion/CRIMESCENE1/CRIMESCENE1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1303, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'ima