 York State', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-19T03:46:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Kaplan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/acb0847a-e714-58f3-b07b-805a219bd79b', 'word_count': 425, 'uri': 'nyt://article/acb0847a-e714-58f3-b07b-805a219bd79b'}, {'abstract': 'Two days after a one-sided defeat in Atlanta, the Nets won a back-and-forth game against the same bruising opponent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/19/sports/basketball/nets-hold-off-hawks-in-rematch.html', 'snippet': 'Two days after a one-sided defeat in Atlanta, the Nets won a back-and-forth game against the same bruising opponent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Nets have three stars in the conversation for All-Star Game nominations, and they would not have beaten the Atlanta Hawks on Friday without Deron Williams, Joe Johnson and Brook Lopez. But, crucially, the Nets withstood Atlanta’s rough, battering style by taking cues from their two less-heralded starters: forwards Reggie Evans and Gerald Wallace, who heave their bodies around with the best of them.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/sports/nets/nets-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 803, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/sports/nets/nets-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1606, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/sports/nets/nets-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/19/sports/nets/nets-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/sports/nets/nets-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nets Pull a Reversal in Win vs. Atlanta', 'kicker': 'Nets 94, Hawks 89', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nets Pull Reversal on Atlanta With a Win at Home', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Nets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Atlanta Hawks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-19T03:49:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zach Schonbrun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zach', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schonbrun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f3658ee-3793-52d1-a3e4-147f8ff091bc', 'word_count': 730, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f3658ee-3793-52d1-a3e4-147f8ff091bc'}, {'abstract': 'The state education commissioner threatened to withhold federal funds if new plans for a teacher evaluation system for New York City weren’t submitted by Feb. 15.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/19/nyregion/more-money-at-risk-over-teacher-evaluations.html', 'snippet': 'The state education commissioner threatened to withhold federal funds if new plans for a teacher evaluation system for New York City weren’t submitted by Feb. 15.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A day after New York City’s failure to create a new teacher evaluation system cost it hundreds of millions of dollars in state aid, an exasperated state education official on Friday threatened to withhold more than $1 billion more from the city, including its share of federal Race to the Top grants.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Money at Risk on Teacher Evaluations', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'More Money at Risk On Teacher Evaluations', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Performance Evaluations (Labor)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Aid (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Race to the Top Fund', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, John B Jr', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-19T03:52:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Al Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Al', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03365bb6-11de-5598-b98e-52c401241154', 'word_count': 896, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03365bb6-11de-5598-b98e-52c401241154'}, {'abstract': 'History has inadequately afforded Edward I. Koch, who served as New York mayor as the AIDS crisis worsened, a judgment of his responses to it that is divorced from questions about his sexuality.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/20/nyregion/judging-mayor-kochs-aids-record-without-the-whispers.html', 'snippet': 'History has inadequately afforded Edward I. Koch, who served as New York mayor as the AIDS crisis worsened, a judgment of his responses to it that is divorced from questions about his sexuality.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s a moment toward the end of “Koch,” a soon-to-be released documentary by Neil Barsky on the extended political career of the city’s 105th mayor, in which Edward I. Koch, eternally single, is asked to address questions surrounding the longstanding interest in his sexuality. He responds as he has done for a long time now, declaring that it is no one’s business. He argues that his engagement with the issue would set a precedent for gross intrusions into the personal lives of political candidates, a bit of narcissistic posturing that seems to ignore the extent to which that field has already been trampled by mad dogs and wild horses. ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/nyregion/20BIGCITY2/20BIGCITY2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 404, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/20/nyregion/20BIGCITY2/20BIGCITY2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 404}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/nyregion/20BIGCITY2/20BIGCITY2-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 689, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/nyregion/20BIGCITY2/20BIGCITY2-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1378, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None