 the 2008 killing, and why he remains convinced of her guilt. “Beyond the Headlines: Prosecuting Casey Anthony,” at 10, introduces the actual people in the case.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Saturday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-19T06:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/af4268cc-55de-5672-a1e3-a606a847e152', 'word_count': 713, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af4268cc-55de-5672-a1e3-a606a847e152'}, {'abstract': 'Goaltender Martin Brodeur, who said he began pondering retirement two years ago, agreed to a two-year deal in July after his team’s run to the Stanley Cup finals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/19/sports/hockey/martin-brodeur-of-devils-eager-to-lead-team-again.html', 'snippet': 'Goaltender Martin Brodeur, who said he began pondering retirement two years ago, agreed to a two-year deal in July after his team’s run to the Stanley Cup finals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEWARK — When the Devils made a stunning march to the Stanley Cup finals last season after finishing sixth in the Eastern Conference, they inadvertently breathed new life into the career of goaltender Martin Brodeur.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/19/sports/brodeur/brodeur-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 664, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'ju