icker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Carolina', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-19T19:30:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Beard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8cf22047-77a4-5b2f-b93d-c95911648b9f', 'word_count': 1611, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8cf22047-77a4-5b2f-b93d-c95911648b9f'}, {'abstract': 'A venerable game company picks a champion before the first puck is dropped in the lockout-delayed N.H.L. season.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/19/rangers-will-win-cup-according-to-strat-o-matic/', 'snippet': 'A venerable game company picks a champion before the first puck is dropped in the lockout-delayed N.H.L. season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In what is either an astounding piece of forecasting or the equivalent of acknowledging a no-hitter in the eighth inning, Strat-O-Matic announced Saturday that the Rangers had won the Stanley Cup in a simulated 2013 season it had conducted.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rangers Will Win Cup, According to Strat-O-Matic', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Callahan, Ryan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Rangers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-19T19:32:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/63842f49-4c2f-5462-ae17-0cf765024087', 'word_count': 264, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63842f49-4c2f-5462-ae17-0cf765024087'}, {'abstract': 'Statements made by President Obama while campaigning for his first term.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/01/20/us/politics/first-term-promises-made-kept-and-broken.html', 'snippet': 'Statements made by President Obama while campaigning for his first term.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Statements made by President Obama while campaigning for his first term.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'First-Term Promises Made, Kept and Broken', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inaugurations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidents and Presidency (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-19T19:33:59+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/3fd328d4-93c0-52bc-8491-036cd3490588', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/3fd328d4-93c0-52bc-8491-036cd3490588'}, {'abstract': 'Readers comment on my column about the need for tighter regulation of endocrine-disrupting chemicals, some of which may be linked to obesity.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/19/the-all-new-non-obesogen-diet-plan/', 'snippet': 'Readers comment on my column about the need for tighter regulation of endocrine-disrupting chemicals, some of which may be linked to obesity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hm. I figured if I could get the word “diet” in the headline, that might improve readership. But the point of my Sunday column isn’t precisely how individuals can lose weight — although more exercise, fewer sugars/carbohydrates and fewer endocrine-disrupting chemicals might be a plan — but more broadly a call for tighter regulation of those endocrine-disruptors. It’s a theme I’ve written about periodically, and one that I once talked about with Stephen Colbert. To me, the chemical industry seems to be following the strategy of Big Tobacco, except that it’s getting away with it. And because these issues seem wonkish and obscure, they don’t get a lot of media attention.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The All-New Non-Obesogen Diet Plan!!!', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-19T19:34:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/85a25c04-fc1c-5a50-9724-7d317889e640', 'word_count': 240, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85a25c04-fc1c-5a50-9724-7d317889e640'}, {'abstract': 'Lindsey Vonn won a World Cup downhill race Saturday, her first victory in more than five weeks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/20/sports/vonn-takes-downhill-and-is-back-to-her-winning-ways.html', 'snippet': 'Lindsey Vonn won a World Cup downhill race Saturday, her first victory in more than five weeks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CORTINA D’AMPEZZO, Italy — Under the pale spires of the Dolomite mountains, Lindsey Vonn reclaimed her title as ski racing’s speed queen in the downhill Saturday, posting her first victory since a nearly monthlong absence from the World Cup tour. It was Vonn’s seventh win in Cortina and the 58th victory of her World Cup career.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/sports/YSKI1/YSKI1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 738, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/sports/YSKI1/YSKI1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1169, 'width': 842, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/sports/YSKI1/YSKI1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/20/sports/YSKI1/YSKI1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/sports/YSKI1/YSKI1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Vonn Takes Downhill and Is Back to Winning Ways', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Vonn, Looking Back in Top Form, Takes the Downhill', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vonn, Lindsey', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Cup (Skiing)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skiing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-19T19:51:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kelley McMillan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kelley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McMillan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/60fa972b-fa56-5f9b-8f5a-e92aee661da2', 'word_count': 599, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60fa972b-fa56-5f9b-8f5a-e92aee661da2'}, {'abstract': 'The screenwriter and actress Halley Feiffer writes about her experiences in the shadow of Sundance, beginning with a strange flight to Park City, Utah.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/19/slamdance-dispatch-a-long-um-productive-night/', 'snippet': 'The screenwriter and actress Halley Feiffer writes about her experiences in the shadow of Sundance, beginning with a strange flight to Park City, Utah.', 'lead_paragraph': 'All eyes are on Sundance right now, and the long shadow it casts can make it difficult for filmmakers at the “other” Park City, Utah, festival, Slamdance, to get their projects seen. The Carpetbagger blog asked Halley Feiffer, co-writer and star of “He’s Way More Famous Than You,” directed by Michael Urie, to share her experiences at Slamdance. Here is her first dispatch, en route from New York to the festival. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Slamdance Dispatch: A Long, Um, Productive Night', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Slamdance Film Festival', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feiffer, Halley', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Park City (Utah)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-19T20:05:25+0000', 'document_type':