ization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a772d108-5d7c-55b9-bf5d-e60339e14830', 'word_count': 742, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a772d108-5d7c-55b9-bf5d-e60339e14830'}, {'abstract': 'About 60 percent of Gov. Rick Perry’s 256 office employees, as well as two-third’s of his most senior staff members, are women.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/20/us/women-are-a-majority-on-gov-rick-perrys-staff.html', 'snippet': 'About 60 percent of Gov. Rick Perry’s 256 office employees, as well as two-third’s of his most senior staff members, are women.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Gov. Rick Perry looks up from his desk these days, more often than not he is surrounded by women. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/us/20-TTWOMEN/20-TTWOMEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/20/us/20-TTWOMEN/20-TTWOMEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/us/20-TTWOMEN/20-TTWOMEN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/us/20-TTWOMEN/20-TTWOMEN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/us/20-TTWOMEN/20-TTWOMEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/20/us/20-TTWOMEN/20-TTWOMEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/us/20-TTWOMEN/20-TTWOMEN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Women Are Majority on Governor’s Staff', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Women Are Majority on Governor’s Staff', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-19T23:42:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily Ramshaw', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ramshaw', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ee9abb1-14f9-543d-9b5e-5656e4f25fb3', 'word_count': 548, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ee9abb1-14f9-543d-9b5e-5656e4f25fb3'}, {'abstract': 'Our economy won’t come back strong unless it also becomes more fair.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/19/inequality-is-holding-back-the-recovery/', 'snippet': 'Our economy won’t come back strong unless it also becomes more fair.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The re-election of President Obama was like a Rorschach test, subject to many interpretations. In this election, each side debated issues that deeply worry me: the long malaise into which the economy seems to be settling, and the growing divide between the 1 percent and the rest — an inequality not only of outcomes but also of opportunity. To me, these problems are two sides of the same coin: with inequality at its highest level since before the Depression, a robust recovery will be difficult in the short term, and the American dream — a good life in exchange for hard work — is slowly dying.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Inequality Is Holding Back the Recovery', 'kicker': 'The Great Divide', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Inequality Is Holding Back The Recovery', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-19T23:47:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph E. Stiglitz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Stiglitz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e999d7b7-fb62-5269-919d-25a8d5323594', 'word_count': 1750, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e999d7b7-fb62-5269-919d-25a8d5323594'}, {'abstract': 'Some people had hoped the recent debate about stricter gun control might help reduce the smuggling of weapons across the border and into Mexico’s drug war, but many Texas officials oppose the plans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/20/us/texas-officials-oppose-new-controls-despite-gun-smuggling-to-mexico.html', 'snippet': 'Some people had 