trong said in an e-mail that he would be spending quiet time with his family before deciding what will be next on his to-do list, which antidoping officials hope is testifying.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/20/sports/cycling/antidoping-agencies-wait-as-lance-armstrong-decides-next-move.html', 'snippet': 'Lance Armstrong said in an e-mail that he would be spending quiet time with his family before deciding what will be next on his to-do list, which antidoping officials hope is testifying.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The long wait for Lance Armstrong to admit his doping and deceit ended last week when he came clean, at least partly, in an interview with Oprah Winfrey.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Armstrong Decides Next Move, Agencies Are Watching', 'kicker': 'Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Armstrong Decides Next Move, Agencies Are Watching', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Macur, Juliet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ARMSTRONG, LANCE', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doping (Sports)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Anti-Doping Agency', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Anti-Doping Agency', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cycling, Road', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bicycles and Bicycling', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-20T01:32:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Cycling', 'byline': {'original': 'By Juliet Macur', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Juliet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macur', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/781e54a9-30fa-5310-a1c4-f73e9c4f1844', 'word_count': 849, 'uri': 'nyt://article/781e54a9-30fa-5310-a1c4-f73e9c4f1844'}, {'abstract': 'It used to be that presidents enjoyed a “honeymoon period” at the beginning of their second term, with a large number of Americans who had failed to vote for them nevertheless expressing their best wishes. Not anymore.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/19/for-second-term-presidents-a-shorter-honeymoon/', 'snippet': 'It used to be that presidents enjoyed a “honeymoon period” at the beginning of their second term, with a large number of Americans who had failed to vote for them nevertheless expressing their best wishes. Not anymore.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama will begin his second term more popular than he has been for most of the past three years. His approval rating is 52 percent, according to the RealClearPolitics average, against 43 percent who disapprove of his performance. (Mr. Obama’s numbers in the latest New York Times/CBS News poll are similar: 51 percent approval and 41 percent disapproval.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Second-Term Presidents, a Shorter Honeymoon', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-20T01:34:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1585525c-858a-5ed4-9a64-a69cc84cee42', 'word_count': 616, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1585525c-858a-5ed4-9a64-a69cc84cee42'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Musial, who played his entire career in St. Louis, won seven batting titles, hit 475 home runs, amassed 3,630 hits and was voted into the Hall of Fame in his first year of eligibility.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/20/sports/baseball/baseball-great-stan-musial-dies-at-92.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Musial, who played his entire career in St. Louis, won seven batting titles, hit 475 home runs, amassed 3,630 hits and was voted into the Hall of Fame in his first year of eligibility.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stan Musial, one of baseball’s greatest hitters and a revered figure in the storied history of the St. Louis Cardinals — \xa0the player they called Stan the Man — died Saturday. He was 92.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/sports/baseball/20musial-1/20musial-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 597, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/20/sports/baseball/20musial-1/20musial-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 597}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/sports/baseball/20musial-1/20musial-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1018, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/sports/baseball/20musial-1/20musial-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2036, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/20/sports/baseball/20musial-1/20musial-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/20/sports/baseball/20musial-1/20musial-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbna