talking points will be whether they can trade for Seattle quarterback Matt Flynn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It wasn’t that long ago that the Jets were part of conference championship day.\xa0On Friday, they made two moves to try to get back there, hiring John Idzik as general manager and Marty Mornhinweg as offensive coordinator.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The New Jets: A Pass-Happy Team?', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mornhinweg, Marty', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-20T13:06:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2f99ee9-7d45-5b97-8318-1588936ab3cd', 'word_count': 546, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2f99ee9-7d45-5b97-8318-1588936ab3cd'}, {'abstract': 'The quiet ceremony before Monday’s public pomp, forced by a quirk of the constitutional calendar, started President Obama’s second term with a divided government at home and persistent threats abroad.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/21/us/politics/president-obama-inauguration.html', 'snippet': 'The quiet ceremony before Monday’s public pomp, forced by a quirk of the constitutional calendar, started President Obama’s second term with a divided government at home and persistent threats abroad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — With only his family beside him, Barack Hussein Obama was sworn into office for a second term on Sunday in advance of Monday’s public pomp, facing a bitterly divided government at home and persistent threats abroad that inhibit his effort to redefine America’s use of power.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/21/us/politics/21inaugural_7/21inaugural_7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/21/us/politics/21inaugural_7/21inaugural_7-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1354, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/21/us/politics/21inaugural_7/21inaugural_7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/21/us/politics/21inaugural_7/21inaugural_7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Sworn In for 2nd Term, This Time Quietly', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama Takes Oath, Beginning 2nd Term: An Intimate White House Ceremony —\r\nTraditional Pomp Is Set for Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Calmes, Jackie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inaugurations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-20T13:17:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jackie Calmes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jackie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Calmes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7701e61-5972-5fc2-870b-eafaa5f04f50', 'word_count': 1333, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7701e61-5972-5fc2-870b-eafaa5f04f50'}, {'abstract': 'The one place that many Republicans say they will not be during the long weekend, if they can help it, is anywhere near the nation’s capital.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/21/us/politics/as-washington-draws-inaugural-crowds-republicans-leave.html', 'snippet': 'The one place that many Republicans say they will not be during the long weekend, if they can help it, is anywhere near the nation’s capital.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some were heading out West to hit the slopes. Some were traveling south for warmer climes. Others were merely popping across the river for a boozy night with friends.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/21/us/politics/21congress_web1/21congress_web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/21/us/politics/21congress_web1/21congress_web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/21/us/politics/21congress_web1/21congress_web1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/21/us/politics/21congress_web1/21congress_web1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo',