hion week photo diary of Kevin Tachman.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Photos of The Moment | Lanvin', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-20T20:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin Tachman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tachman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f3062b2a-3e41-559d-85d9-cc3fc07e6c61', 'word_count': 36, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f3062b2a-3e41-559d-85d9-cc3fc07e6c61'}, {'abstract': '“Broadway Romance,” a program of theater songs performed by Howard McGillin, Rebecca Luker and Ted Sperling, brings nostalgia to the Café Carlyle.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/21/arts/music/broadway-romance-at-cafe-carlyle.html', 'snippet': '“Broadway Romance,” a program of theater songs performed by Howard McGillin, Rebecca Luker and Ted Sperling, brings nostalgia to the Café Carlyle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The very title of the winter-season opening show at the Café Carlyle, “Broadway Romance,” promises cuddly nostalgia with minimal anxiety and hysteria. Three reliable Broadway hands — the singers Howard McGillin and Rebecca Luker, with the musical director and occasional vocalist Ted Sperling on piano — deliver on that promise. The sequence of mostly well-known theater songs offers a sophisticated variation on an old story: boy meets girl, boy loses girl, boy gets girl back, with marriage and children added.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Boy Meets Girl, Song Ensues', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Boy Meets Girl, Song Ensues', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cafe Carlyle', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGillin, Howard', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Luker, Rebecca', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sperling, Ted', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-20T20:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/6528c7ac-f98b-5204-98ef-cbce47ce9394', 'word_count': 297, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6528c7ac-f98b-5204-98ef-cbce47ce9394'}, {'abstract': 'Each of the four works performed in the American Composers Orchestra program “Time Travels” used music to examine the very concept of time.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/21/arts/music/the-american-composers-orchestra-at-zankel-hall.html', 'snippet': 'Each of the four works performed in the American Composers Orchestra program “Time Travels” used music to examine the very concept of time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In some sense every piece of music involves an exploration of time, whether Gregorian chant, a Haydn symphony or Messiaen’s “Quartet for the End of Time.” The American Composers Orchestra made this issue the focus of a program at Zankel Hall on Friday night, “Time Travels,” part of the ensemble’s innovative Orchestra Underground series. Each of the four works performed uses music to examine the very concept of time. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/21/arts/21composer/21composer-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/21/arts/21composer/21composer-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/21/arts/21composer/21composer-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/21/arts/21composer/21composer-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/21/arts/21composer/21composer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/21/arts/21composer/21composer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/21/arts/21composer/21composer-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hitting Start, Stop and Pause on the Long Arc of Time', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hitting Start, Stop and Pause on the Long Arc of Time', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'per