an ambivalent position in our world.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Way of the Agnostic', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christians and Christianity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-20T22:30:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gary Gutting', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gutting', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8caa932f-e8dd-5fcd-9d90-14ce165ef752', 'word_count': 1790, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8caa932f-e8dd-5fcd-9d90-14ce165ef752'}, {'abstract': 'Since the 1970s Camilo José Vergara has been photographing murals of the Rev. Dr. Martin Luther King Jr. painted on walls in cities across the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/21/arts/design/murals-of-the-rev-dr-martin-luther-king-jr.html', 'snippet': 'Since the 1970s Camilo José Vergara has been photographing murals of the Rev. Dr. Martin Luther King Jr. painted on walls in cities across the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since the 1970s Camilo José Vergara has been photographing murals of the Rev. Dr. Martin Luther King Jr. painted on walls in cities across the United States. Through them, he has documented social and political changes in the country itself. On a wall in the Callowhill section of Philadelphia, above, Dr. King is the potent orator of the Washington marches; on Frederick Douglass Boulevard in Harlem he’s a solitary, anxious visionary. In Los Angeles his figure is all but buried under fresh graffiti; in the South Bronx, the site of turf wars between blacks and Latinos in the 1970s, his face is scratched out.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/21/arts/KINGFLOATER/KINGFLOATER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/21/arts/KINGFLOATER/KINGFLOATER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/21/arts/KINGFLOATER/KINGFLOATER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 665, 'width': 994, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/21/arts/KINGFLOATER/KINGFLOATER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 665, 'width': 994, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/21/arts/KINGFLOATER/KINGFLOATER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/21/arts/KINGFLOATER/KINGFLOATER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/21/arts/KINGFLOATER/KINGFLOATER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Eyes on a Prized and Ubiquitous Face', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Eyes on a Prized and Ubiquitous Face', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cotter, Holland', '