'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb972720-ad03-51d1-9858-1f3b8a9e51f3', 'word_count': 190, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb972720-ad03-51d1-9858-1f3b8a9e51f3'}, {'abstract': 'When thousands of rape kits sit untested, victims are denied justice while the perpetrators remain free to attack.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/21/opinion/untested-rape-kits-delay-justice.html', 'snippet': 'When thousands of rape kits sit untested, victims are denied justice while the perpetrators remain free to attack.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the final hours of the last Congress, the Senate approved action against an intolerable failure of criminal justice — the backlog of scores of thousands of rape test kits allowed to sit untested for years in police custody. Victims are denied justice while the perpetrators remain free to rape again.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Evidence of Rape Ignored', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Evidence of Rape Ignored', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forensic Science', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-21T01:27:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8c6e318-cf0c-5588-941d-825dde74c5da', 'word_count': 304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8c6e318-cf0c-5588-941d-825dde74c5da'}, {'abstract': 'The Supreme Court wisely ended a destructive lawsuit to prevent the federal government from financing this promising area of research.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/21/opinion/embryonic-stem-cell-research-gets-a-reprieve.html', 'snippet': 'The Supreme Court wisely ended a destructive lawsuit to prevent the federal government from financing this promising area of research.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Supreme Court has wisely ended a bizarre and destructive lawsuit to prevent the federal government from financing embryonic stem cell research. By refusing to hear the case, the court put a halt to more than three years of turmoil that drove some scientists away from such research because of uncertainty about its legality and questions about continued federal funding.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stem Cell Research Gets a Reprieve', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stem Cell Research Gets a Reprieve', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stem Cells (Embryonic)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stem Cells', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-21T01:27:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/40b5401a-5f60-50d5-8778-bb027cefa590', 'word_count': 335, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40b5401a-5f60-50d5-8778-bb027cefa590'}, {'abstract': 'Will Republicans work with Democrats in the new session, or remain hijacked by the party’s most extreme minority?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/21/opinion/a-choice-for-republican-leaders.html', 'snippet': 'Will Republicans work with Democrats in the new session, or remain hijacked by the party’s most extreme minority?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ted Cruz, the newly elected Tea Party senator from Texas, embodies the rigidity the public grew to loathe in Congress’s last term. He is bursting with fervor to fight compromise and consensus-building in Washington wherever it is found. Unlike 85 percent of the Republicans in the Senate, he would have voted against the fiscal cliff deal. He says gun control is unconstitutional. Breaking even with conservative business leaders, he would have no qualms about using the debt ceiling as a hostage because he believes (falsely) that it would produce only a partial government shutdown and not default.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Choice for Republican Leaders', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Choice for Republican Leaders', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cruz, Ted', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-21T01:27:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c3fe975-0a92-5810-b6