ions', 'value': 'Coalition of the Radical Left (Greece)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-21T01:50:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Alderman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alderman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a8d799a-5910-5d3b-975e-4682758c5a82', 'word_count': 1390, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a8d799a-5910-5d3b-975e-4682758c5a82'}, {'abstract': 'After winning an Olympic gold medal, the coach of the UConn women’s basketball team, Geno Auriemma, has returned to a changing college landscape.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/20/geno-auriemma-on-rivals-old-and-new/', 'snippet': 'After winning an Olympic gold medal, the coach of the UConn women’s basketball team, Geno Auriemma, has returned to a changing college landscape.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Having returned from the London Olympics as a gold medal-winning coach, Geno Auriemma resumed his familiar perch with his Connecticut women’s basketball team in hard pursuit of a national championship. His next title would be his eighth, equaling his longtime rival, Pat Summitt at Tennessee.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Geno Auriemma on Rivals, Old and New', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Facing a Changing Landscape', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Auriemma, Geno', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Connecticut', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-21T01:53:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Araton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Araton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/719bd37d-a00e-5527-b292-94b30d0cf557', 'word_count': 1056, 'uri': 'nyt://article/719bd37d-a00e-5527-b292-94b30d0cf557'}, {'abstract': 'The ads, which come as Time Warner Cable faces stiff competition, will say that the company’s service has improved, and will offer former subscribers a money-back guarantee.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/21/business/media/time-warner-cable-ad-campaign-aims-at-regaining-customers.html', 'snippet': 'The ads, which come as Time Warner Cable faces stiff competition, will say that the company’s service has improved, and will offer former subscribers a money-back guarantee.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cable companies big and small have been losing television subscribers — millions of them — to satellite and telecommunications competitors for years. But Time Warner Cable says it is ready to claw some of them back. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/21/business/21television1/21television1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 290, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/21/business/21television1/21television1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 290}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/21/business/21television1/21television1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 495, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/21/business/21television1/21television1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 991, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Time Warner Cable Tries to Win Back Ex-Subscribers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Time Warner Cable Tries to Win Back Ex-Subscribers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stelter, Brian', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Time Warner Cable Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Verizon Communications Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AT&T Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Comcast Corporation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-21T01:59:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb99e430-e3a8-5b0c-a683-38cddc065062', 'word_count': 675, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb99e430-e3a8-5b0c-a683-38cddc065062'}, {'abstract': 'When we put the old and the sick out of sight, we enable a baseless fantasy of eternal health and youth. What is it doing to us?', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/20/you-are-going-to-die/', 'snippet': 'When we put the old and the sick out of sight, we enable a baseless fantasy of eternal health and youth. What is it doing to us?', 'lead_paragraph': 'My sister and I recently toured the retirement community where my mother has announced she’ll be moving. I have been in some bleak clinical facilities for the elderly where not one person was compos mentis and I had to politely suppress the urge to flee, but this was nothing like that. It was a very cushy modern complex housed in what used to be a seminary, with individual condominiums with big kitchens and sun rooms, equipped with fancy restaurants, grills and snack bars, a fitness center, a concert hall, a library, an art room, a couple of beauty salons, a bank and an ornate chapel of Italian marble. You could walk from any building in the complex to another without ever going outside, through underground corridors and glass-enclosed walkways through the woods. Mom described it as “like a college dorm, except the boys aren’t as good-looking.” Nonetheless I spent much of my day trying not to cry.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'You Are Going to Die', 'kicker': 'Anxiety', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Longevity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Retirement Communities and Assisted Living', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-21T02:00:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Kreider', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kreider', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1c94043-146a-5f38-90b4-a3d3572f814b', 'word_count': 1506, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1c94043-146a-5f38-90b