ing numbers of Syrians to relocate within the country or flee across the border, creating a disaster that is threatening to destabilize the region. The international community has an obligation to do more to ease the suffering.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Syrian Refugee Crisis', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Syrian Refugee Crisis', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Aid', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-21T02:16:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/b56f1835-d996-5906-8749-22d79fae3578', 'word_count': 434, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b56f1835-d996-5906-8749-22d79fae3578'}, {'abstract': 'Some beer halls across the country are opening with the goal of selling alcohol and donating the profits to charities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/21/us/new-pubs-send-profits-to-charity.html', 'snippet': 'Some beer halls across the country are opening with the goal of selling alcohol and donating the profits to charities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PORTLAND, Ore. — Ask a bartender exactly how much profit was collected from that pint of beer you just drank, and the answer is likely to be as murky as a barrel-aged bourbon stout. The economics of alcohol, like the calorie count, are usually about the last things pu