pet': 'Corey Arnold is a fisherman, photographer and photographer of fishermen. In frigid Alaska, he documents the rugged lives of those who make their living from the water.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Near the mouth of the Kvichak River in southwestern Alaska, there is a knob of tundra reaching into the water that locals call Graveyard Point. Atop a small bluff lie the dilapidated remains of an abandoned fish cannery, and below is a vast, swampy delta.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Eat, Sleep, Fish, Click', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-21T10:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jesse Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jesse', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f721610-7f00-5026-bfc3-59a0c52d2db4', 'word_count': 1159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f721610-7f00-5026-bfc3-59a0c52d2db4'}, {'abstract': 'Five Taliban suicide bombers stormed the headquarters of the traffic police early on Monday, setting off a battle that killed at least three officers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/22/world/asia/insurgents-attack-police-unit-in-kabul.html', 'snippet': 'Five Taliban suicide bombers stormed the headquarters of the traffic police early on Monday, setting off a battle that killed at least three officers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — In the second brazen attack on the capital in less than a week, five Taliban suicide bombers stormed the headquarters of the traffic police early on Monday, setting off a fierce nine-hour gun battle that raged into the afternoon and claimed the lives of at least three traffic officers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimed