el is dead.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/21/the-prime-minister-of-israel-will-win-again/', 'snippet': 'With Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu almost certain to win Tuesday’s election, competitive democracy in Israel is dead.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — Eight years ago, writing about the popularity of Kadima, the centrist party of then-Prime Minister Ariel Sharon, I argued that maybe it was attractive but it “has no grass-roots activists, no organization, no history — and no future.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bibi Forever', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netanyahu, Benjamin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kadima Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Likud Party (Israel)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-21T14:45:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shmuel Rosner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shmuel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3e85557-b005-515d-8c05-312dfff3fe16', 'word_count': 598, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3e85557-b005-515d-8c05-312dfff3fe16'}, {'abstract': 'The all-star game in Mobile, Ala., is a chance to watch players on a theoretically even playing field — one big step on the road to the N.F.L. draft.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/21/2013-senior-bowl-preview/', 'snippet': 'The all-star game in Mobile, Ala., is a chance to watch players on a theoretically even playing field — one big step on the road to the N.F.L. draft.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When you study college football players year-round, the Senior Bowl is not the introduction to pro prospects that it is for many fans. The all-star game in Mobile, Ala., is a chance to watch players on a theoretically even playing field: the teams will play in a vanilla scheme; the players are all processing new information; and the prospects get an even number of repetitions against top competition in practice. It’s a chance to watch how players react to coaching, improve the fine points of their craft, and handle the scrutiny while competing against some of the best college football has to offer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/22/sports/football/22nassib/22nassib-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 712, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/22/sports/football/22nassib/22nassib-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1423, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/22/sports/football/22nassib/22nassib-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/22/sports/football/22nassib/22nassib-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/22/sports/football/22nassib/22nassib-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '2013 Senior Bowl Preview', '