bout security threats.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TIANJIN, China — When Airbus executives arrived here seven years ago scouting for a location to assemble passenger jets, the broad, flat expanse next to Tianjin Binhai International Airport was a grassy field.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China’s Focus on Aerospace Raises Security Questions', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China Looks to the Sky', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Investments', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Military Aircraft', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AIRBUS INDUSTRIE', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN INTERNATIONAL GROUP INC', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Aviation Industry Corporation of China (AVIC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Lease Finance Corp', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-21T22:41:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Keith Bradsher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Keith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bradsher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d104f0f5-2f01-5d17-babd-f37bc9dcfc73', 'word_count': 1464, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d104f0f5-2f01-5d17-babd-f37bc9dcfc73'}, {'abstract': 'Researchers have found a possible explanation for the pain and stomach cramping in infants: the kinds of microbes that inhabit their intestines.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/21/microbes-linked-to-colic-in-babies/', 'snippet': 'Researchers have found a possible explanation for the pain and stomach cramping in infants: the kinds of microbes that inhabit their intestines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No one knows what causes colic, the intense pain and stomach cramping that commonly begins in otherwise healthy infants at about a month and disappears a few months later. But now researchers have found a possible explanation: the kinds of microbes that inhabit babies’ intestines.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/25/health/well_childhood/well_childhood-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 219, 'width': 225, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/25/health/well_childhood/well_childhood-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 219, 'width': 225, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/25/health/well_childhood/well_childhood-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/25/health/well_childhood/well_childhood-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/25/health/well_childhood/well_childhood-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 149, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Microbes Linked to Colic in Babies', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Childhood: Microbes Linked to Colic', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Intestinal Tract', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Microbiology', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-21T22:44:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Bakalar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakalar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b04cfdb0-cba5-54de-9a55-9d9bffa12cdf', 'word_count': 192, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b04cfdb0-cba5-54de-9a55-9d9bffa12cdf'}, {'abstract': 'It’s not unusual to fret over big decisions, but suppressing lingering doubts can cause regret, and in the case of marriages, higher divorce rates among women who ignored cold feet.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/21/avoiding-cold-feet-down-the-aisle/', 'snippet': 'It’s not unusual to fret over big decisions, but suppressing lingering doubts can cause regret, and in the case of marriages, higher divorce rates among women who ignored cold feet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'His charisma was big enough to make his bad habits seem small, more like quirks than flaws. The cigarettes on his breath; the extra weight around the middle; the indifference to clothing and appearances — surely these were minor things, correctable in time.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/22/science/22JPMIND/22JPMIND-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'ju