bffe-a89a-53d6-901b-e28cd5fa5de3'}, {'abstract': 'A Human Rights Watch report says Italian authorities are not following international standards on how to treat asylum seekers and unaccompanied migrant children who arrive illegally.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/22/world/europe/italy-said-to-turn-back-asylum-seekers-from-greece.html', 'snippet': 'A Human Rights Watch report says Italian authorities are not following international standards on how to treat asylum seekers and unaccompanied migrant children who arrive illegally.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — Instead of following international standards on how to treat asylum seekers and unaccompanied migrant children who arrive illegally from Greece, the Italian authorities have been summarily returning them, according to a report by Human Rights Watch scheduled to be published Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Italy Often Turns Back Asylum Seekers Arriving Illegally From Greece, Report Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Italy Often Turns Back Asylum Seekers Arriving Illegally From Greece, Report Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Asylum, Right of', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Human Rights Watch', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-22T01:03:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elis