k Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘We Are Made for This Moment, and We Will Seize It’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘We Are Made for This Moment, and We Will Seize It’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inaugurations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speeches and Statements', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-22T01:30:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Text', '_id': 'nyt://article/75d8914e-02f8-5170-adac-ba762ee9f8f8', 'word_count': 765, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75d8914e-02f8-5170-adac-ba762ee9f8f8'}, {'abstract': 'On Tuesday, the Democrats can use a simple majority to end the routine abuse of the filibuster.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/22/opinion/a-chance-for-the-senate-to-fix-the-filibuster.html', 'snippet': 'On Tuesday, the Democrats can use a simple majority to end the routine abuse of the filibuster.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For six years, Democrats in the Senate have chafed at an unprecedented abuse of the filibuster by Republicans, who have used the practice to hold up nominees high and low and require a supermajority for virtually every bill. But now that they finally have an opportunity to end much of this delay and abuse, Democrats are instead considering only a few half-measures.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Chance to Fix the Senate', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Chance to Fix the Senate', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Filibusters and Debate Curbs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organization