 {'abstract': 'In Springfield, Ill., the state capital where President Obama served as a legislator, residents looked to his second term with a mixture of anxiety, uncertainty and a muted hopefulness.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/22/us/politics/in-springfield-ill-applause-for-obama-is-muted.html', 'snippet': 'In Springfield, Ill., the state capital where President Obama served as a legislator, residents looked to his second term with a mixture of anxiety, uncertainty and a muted hopefulness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SPRINGFIELD, Ill. — Harvey Nelson glanced around a diner here on Monday, then dropped his voice to a hush to talk about politics. Yes, he said, looking around again at nearby tables, he voted for President Obama, and yes, he said, some signs seem to be emerging of an improving economy. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/22/us/MOOD/MOOD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 714, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/22/us/MOOD/MOOD-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1429, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Applause Is Muted in City With Role in President’s Rise', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Applause Is Muted in City With Role in President’s Rise', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Springfield (Ill)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Illin