 African immigrants have gone from looking for a new start in an unwelcoming Europe to, more recently, Yemen, where their basic needs are met.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trapped Between Africa and Saudi Arabia', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Aranda, Samuel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Saudi Arabia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-22T10:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Gonzalez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonzalez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b44b643-6f87-5f75-8bad-e17ad683fbfc', 'word_count': 890, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b44b643-6f87-5f75-8bad-e17ad683fbfc'}, {'abstract': 'Should family members of very famous people have the right to privacy?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/22/would-you-want-to-grow-up-in-the-public-eye/', 'snippet': 'Should family members of very famous people have the right to privacy?', 'lead_paragraph': 'During Monday’s presidential inauguration coverage, every commentator seemed to remark on how Malia and Sasha Obama are growing up before our eyes. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/22/us/22girls1-LN/22girls1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 651, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'im