te': '2013-01-22T11:52:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/63c4e76b-3865-5958-9470-0b860789d82b', 'word_count': 321, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63c4e76b-3865-5958-9470-0b860789d82b'}, {'abstract': 'The pain inherent in an N.F.L. playing career can be so severe and constant that it may be hard for the average fan to comprehend.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/22/the-agony-of-the-n-f-l/', 'snippet': 'The pain inherent in an N.F.L. playing career can be so severe and constant that it may be hard for the average fan to comprehend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two writers recently shed light on a darkness that is enveloping the N.F.L. Consider it a reality check for the drama and enjoyment of the last three weekends of playoff football.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Agony of the N.F.L.', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-22T11:57:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa667f00-ee0f-564d-b8b7-c4db71fb31f4', 'word_count': 653, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa667f00-ee0f-564d-b8b7-c4db71fb31f4'}, {'abstract': 'The week in Mobile, Ala., is an important marker on the road to the N.F.L. draft, but the caliber of competition has suffered because 24 players chose not to participate.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/22/how-relevant-is-the-senior-bowl/', 'snippet': 'The week in Mobile, Ala., is an important marker on the road to the N.F.L. draft, but the caliber of competition has suffered because 24 players chose not to participate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOBILE, Ala. — Many football fans openly question the value of college all-star games in pre-draft evaluation. Some writers who cover the event every year have similar questions. As it often does, Monday morning’s weigh-in prompted a tangential discussion among those in attendance and those readers following on Twitter.\xa0 Setting aside the indignity of a process in which over 100 players parade across a stage in their underwear in the football community’s perverse version of Fashion Week, there are valid questions about just how relevant the Senior Bowl is.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Relevant Is the Senior Bowl?', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-22T12:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jene Bramel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bramel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5d91bad-8a2c-5706-b08e-f864b083eaaf', 'word_count': 708, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5d91bad-8a2c-5706-b08e-f864b083eaaf'}, {'abstract': 'Smart entrepreneurs want to take over the world and prove everyone wrong, but employees want stability and a good job where they can live a good life. They become risk averse.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/22/when-a-fast-growth-entrepreneur-is-too-fast-for-his-own-company/', 'snippet': 'Smart entrepreneurs want to take over the world and prove everyone wrong, but employees want stability and a good job where they can live a good life. They become risk averse.', 'lead_paragraph': '“They will carry him out of the company in a body bag” is the first thing I ever heard about David Deeter. I had asked about him because the accounting firm that carries his name, Frazier & Deeter, is one of the fastest-growing firms in America and yet he works in the tax department. It didn’t add up.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When a Fast-Growth Entrepreneur is Too Fast for His Own Company', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACCOUNTING AND ACCOUNTANTS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-22T12:00:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cliff Oxford', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cliff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Oxford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a580a0a1-7842-589a-bd8c-32cc0c4f4a6f', 'word_count': 1532, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a580a0a1-7842-589a-bd8c-32cc0c4f4a6f'}, {'abstract': 'The Bolshoi Ballet has made Galina Stepanenko, a former principal dancer, its acting artistic director. She takes over for Sergei Filin, who after suffering an acid attack, said that he regretted not accepting protection.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/23/world/europe/bolshoi-theater-director-acid-attack.html', 'snippet': 'The Bolshoi Ballet has made Galina Stepanenko, a former principal dancer, its acting artistic director. She takes over for Sergei Filin, who after suffering an acid attack, said that he regretted not accepting protection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — Galina Stepanenko, a former principal dancer with the Bolshoi Ballet, was named the company’s acting artistic director on Tuesday, taking over for Sergei Filin, who was severely burned last week when a masked man threw acid in his face. In an interview published on Tuesday, Mr. Filin said he regretted not accepting protection after receiving threats in mid-December.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/23/arts/23BOLSHOI/23BOLSHOI-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/23/arts/23BOLSHOI/23BOLSHOI-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 677}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/23/arts/23BOLSHOI/23BOLSHOI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 908, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/23/arts/23BOLSHOI/23BOLSHOI-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1997, 'width': 1770, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/23/arts/23BOLSHOI/23BOLSHOI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/23/arts/23BOLSHOI/23BOLSHOI-thu