imes.com/2013/01/22/what-were-reading-612/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'National Geographic: “The Kyrgyz also eat yak-milk yogurt, fizzy and thick, and a hard cheese called kurut,which you soften in your mouth for several minutes before chewing,” Michael Finkel writes of the struggling nomads who occupy the Wakhan corridor of Afghanistan. “Also unleavened rounds of bread the size of pizzas. Meat is reserved for special gatherings. The closest to a vegetable is a tiny wild onion, no bigger than a pea.” — Jeff Gordinier', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-22T15:01:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/76b713c2-a7b2-5fc3-8c8b-dcbceb26ced7', 'word_count': 389, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76b713c2-a7b2-5fc3-8c8b-dcbceb26ced7'}, {'abstract': 'N.F.L. fans can expect a lot of articles about the Harbaughs, Ray Lewis and Colin Kaepernick before the big game.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/23/sports/two-long-weeks-to-the-super-bowl-leading-off.html', 'snippet': 'N.F.L. fans can expect a lot of articles about the Harbaughs, Ray Lewis and Colin Kaepernick before the big game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In case you have forgotten since last year, let’s refresh what happens in the usual two-week pre-Super Bowl media arc. Today, you still have a lot of people coming to grips with the whole Harbaugh Bowl thing, including the Harbaughs, who are trying to deadpan their way out of this altogether. But, as Judy Battista writes in The New York Times, these would be your typical ferociously competitive brothers — not as dissimilar as they seem, Steve Serby writes in The New York Post, if they weren’t the first pair to coach against each other in the Super Bowl. Oh yeah, there is that.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Longest 2 Weeks', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Super Bowl', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaepernick, Colin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lewis, Ray', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Flacco, Joe', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Radwanska, Agnieszka', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goodell, Roger', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-22T15:01:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/01de5dd7-b100-57c1-8d95-7f769c48e85f', 'word_count': 623, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01de5dd7-b100-57c1-8d95-7f769c48e85f'}, {'abstract': 'CNN viewers may have noticed over the weekend the distinctive James Earl Jones refrain “This is CNN,” part of an effort by Jeff Zucker, the new chief executive of CNN Worldwide, to acknowledge the channel’s legacy.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/22/as-zucker-starts-at-cnn-a-familiar-and-deep-voice-is-heard/', 'snippet': 'CNN viewers may have noticed over the weekend the distinctive James Earl Jones refrain “This is CNN,” part of an effort by Jeff Zucker, the new chief executive of CNN Worldwide, to acknowledge the channel’s le