nd its regulators to the possibility that operators at plants with more than one reactor might have to deal with more than one meltdown at a time in a flood, earthquake or other catastrophe. Officials are now working to assure that they could master that situation. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Early Nuclear Warning: Was It for Naught?', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fukushima Daiichi Nuclear Power Plant (Japan)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Japan Earthquake and Tsunami (2011)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Energy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nuclear Regulatory Commission', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Union of Concerned Scientists', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-22T16:08:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37fb3416-9a8d-5914-b165-f22d007b8e95', 'word_count': 577, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37fb3416-9a8d-5914-b165-f22d007b8e95'}, {'abstract': 'Scenes from the spring 2013 couture photo diary of Schohaja.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/22/photos-of-the-moment-christian-dior-6/', 'snippet': 'Scenes from the spring 2013 couture photo diary of Schohaja.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NY