nservative Group Pastes Liberal Stamp on Obama', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inaugurations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Crossroads Grassroots Policy Strategies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-22T16:31:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ea1624e-f94d-5343-b143-44c74fefa4ea', 'word_count': 223, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ea1624e-f94d-5343-b143-44c74fefa4ea'}, {'abstract': 'Venus and Serena Williams, favorites to win the doubles title at the Australian Open, were defeated by Sara Errani and Roberta Vinci on Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/22/venus-and-serena-williams-lose-in-doubles/', 'snippet': 'Venus and Serena Williams, favorites to win the doubles title at the Australian Open, were defeated by Sara Errani and Roberta Vinci on Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MELBOURNE, Australia — As heavily favored as Serena Williams is to win the women’s singles title at the 2013 Australian Open, she was an even heavier favorite to win with her sister Venus at her side.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Williams Sisters Lose in Doubles', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-22T16:35:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By BEN ROTHENBERG', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'ROTHENBERG', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/abe21f00-dd1f-5eab-9854-de2306cbda79', 'word_count': 481, 'uri': 'nyt://article/abe21f00-dd1f-5eab-9854-de2306cbda79'}, {'abstract': 'The court did not have sufficient time Tuesday to take up the petition to move the case outside Delhi.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/22/supreme-court-to-hear-petition-of-gang-rape-accused-on-wednesday/', 'snippet': 'The court did not have sufficient time Tuesday to take up the petition to move the case outside Delhi.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Supreme Court has delayed until Wednesday a hearing on a petition to move the gang rape trial from New Delhi.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Supreme Court to Consider Moving Delhi Gang Rape Trial on Wednesday', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-22T16:36:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Niharika Mandhana', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Niharika', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mandhana', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/95e86670-201e-5944-9645-11f0d1b99f88', 'word_count': 319, 'uri': 'nyt://article/95e86670-201e-5944-9645-11f0d1b99f88'}, {'abstract': 'The question is whether this will lead to greater political openness, an authoritarian clampdown to restore the veneer of stability, or social turmoil.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/01/22/appearance-of-consensus-is-breaking-down-in-china/', 'snippet': 'The question is whether this will lead to greater political openness, an authoritarian clampdown to restore the veneer of stability, or social turmoil.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GUANGZHOU, China — For two decades after the Tiananmen Square crackdown in 1989, China seemed on the surface like a country where free-market and even laissez-faire principles prevailed. It looked as if a consensus had been reached on putting economic policy and the headlong pursuit of affluence ahead of ideology and politics.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In China, the Appearance of Consensus Is Breaking Down', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In China, Veneer of Consensus Is Breaking Down', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-22T16:37:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Keith Bradsher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Keith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bradsher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f84ed5a-c87a-5439-b52c-42f843e6750a', 'word_count': 1136, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f84ed5a-c87a-5439-b52c-42f843e6750a'}, {'abstract': 'Novak Djokovic exposed Tomas Berdych’s lack of technical and tactical flexibility in the Australian Open quarterfinals.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/22/djokovics-complete-game-overcomes-berdychs-power/', 'snippet': 'Novak Djokovic exposed Tomas Berdych’s lack of technical and tactical flexibility in the Australian Open quarterfinals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The rap on Tomas Berdych is that he has no Plan B, that he can play tennis only one way: with blistering pace and power. It is a formula that has taken Berdych, a 6-foot-5 player from the Czech Republic, close to the pinnacle of the men’s game.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Djokovic’s Complete Game Beats Berdych’s Power', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-22T16:44:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By GEOFF MACDONALD', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Geoff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MACDONALD', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0872cca-7cc5-5f6d-80c1-3ee36019134f', 'word_count': 439, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0872cca-7cc5-5f6d-80c1-3ee36019134f'}, {'abstract': 'A Taliban spokesman said that Prince Harry must have “mental problems,” after the royal said that killing militants from an Apache helicopter was similar to playing video games.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/22/prince-harry-compares-war-to-playstation-and-taliban-is-not-amused/', 'snippet': 'A Taliban spokesman said that Prince Harry must have “mental problems,” after the royal said that killing militants from an Apache helicopter was similar to playing video games.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Taliban spokesman said on Tuesday that Prince Harry must have “mental problems,” following the broadcast of remarks by the royal in which he said that killing militants from an Apache helicopter was similar to playing video games.', 'sourc