hotographs of their meals, the chef David Bouley has seen it all. There are the foreign tourists who, despite their big cameras, tend to be very discreet. There are those who use a flash and annoy everyone around them. There are those who come equipped with gorillapods — those small, flexible tripods to use on their tables. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/23/dining/23PHOTOGRAPHY_SPAN/23PHOTOGRAPHY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 219, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/23/dining/23PHOTOGRAPHY_SPAN/23PHOTOGRAPHY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 219}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/23/dining/23PHOTOGRAPHY_SPAN/23PHOTOGRAPHY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 374, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/23/dining/23PHOTOGRAPHY_SPAN/23PHOTOGRAPHY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 408, 'width': 1116, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/23/dining/23PHOTOGRAPHY_SPAN/23PHOTOGRAPHY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/23/dining/23PHOTOGRAPHY_SPAN/23PHOTOGRAPHY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/23/dining/23PHOTOGRAPHY_SPAN/23PHOTOGRAPHY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Restaurants Turn Camera Shy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Restaurants Turn Camera Shy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stapinski, Helene', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chefs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-22T21:59:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Helene Stapinski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Helene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stapinski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8704b9c5-976e-5137-b7a7-3a8f0f824e86', 'word_count': 1128, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8704b9c5-976e-5137-b7a7-3a8f0f824e86'}, {'abstract': 'Keep your eye on the business cycle.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/22/the-non-surge-in-government-spending/', 'snippet': 'Keep your eye on the business cycle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The fiscal debate in Washington is dominated by things everyone knows that happen not to be true. One of those things is the notion that we have a fiscal crisis, an assertion belied both by the low interest rates at which the Feds can borrow and by the fact that medium-term deficit projections really aren’t that alarming. Another is the notion that our current deficit is driven by a surge in government spending.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Non-Surge in Government Spending', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-22T22:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original':