bers Don’t Say So', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Verizon Communications Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-22T23:28:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian X. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b52ed13d-d2ee-50b7-b50d-8cd409036635', 'word_count': 306, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b52ed13d-d2ee-50b7-b50d-8cd409036635'}, {'abstract': '“The Pirogue” is the story of 30 men and one woman who set off in a long, brightly painted wooden canoe on a voyage from Africa to Spain.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/23/movies/the-pirogue-directed-by-moussa-toure.html', 'snippet': '“The Pirogue” is the story of 30 men and one woman who set off in a long, brightly painted wooden canoe on a voyage from Africa to Spain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Europe as in the United States, immigration is a politically contentious issue most often addressed in abstract demographic and ideological terms. There have been movies that try to give the problem a human face, focusing on the struggles of families and individuals, frequently with well-meaning sentimentality.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/23/arts/23PIROGUE/23PIROGUE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'art