 'nyt://article/569e4fe1-ce90-5c6b-b866-18226d684ea4'}, {'abstract': 'An internal analysis conducted by Johnson & Johnson in 2011 after it recalled a troubled hip implant projected that the all-metal device would fail within five years in nearly 40 percent of patients who received it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/01/23/business/23hip-docs.html', 'snippet': 'An internal analysis conducted by Johnson & Johnson in 2011 after it recalled a troubled hip implant projected that the all-metal device would fail within five years in nearly 40 percent of patients who received it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An internal analysis conducted by Johnson & Johnson in 2011 after it recalled a troubled hip implant projected that the all-metal device would fail within five years in nearly 40 percent of patients who received it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Projection of Hip Implant Failure Rate', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hips', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Johnson & Johnson', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-22T23:28:47+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/2308cb0b-8aaf-526f-a888-7ce5cf61913d', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/2308cb0b-8aaf-526f-a888-7ce5cf61913d'}, {'abstract': 'Three reasons why an ascendant President Obama might not prove to be the “liberal Reagan.”', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/22/the-liberal-hour/', 'snippet': 'Three reasons why an ascendant President Obama might not prove to be the “liberal Reagan.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'I naturally preferred my own version of President Obama’s second inaugural to the speech he actually delivered yesterday, but the substance of the two was roughly similar. The president clearly feels that his re-election both reflects and ratifies a larger leftward shift in American politics: His address reached backward to ground this new progressive era in the American past, offered explicit nods to the demographic groups and constituencies whose present-day growth has made it possible, and then sketched out an agenda suited to a more left-of-center future — climate change legislation and green industrial policy, a pathway to citizenship for illegal immigrants, the universalization of gay marriage, new gun control laws, etc. It was not a speech designed to co-opt opponents of this agenda, to put it mildly — particularly\xa0those opponents whose control of the House of Representatives will make this agenda difficult to implement. But those of us who watched his negative, joyless re-election campaign and assumed that this president would begin his second term as a lame duck were only half-right. While there’s still good reason to think that Obama’s biggest legislative accomplishments are in the rearview mirror, the fact that he could win a clean victory despite the grim economic backdrop seems to have given him more confidence in the staying power of his coalition, and the continuing short-term impediments to his agenda in Washington seem to have liberated him to play for the longer term instead.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Liberal Hour', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-22T23:34:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/32fbb4d7-8048-5ad1-beca-84b2a5658676', 'word_count': 1494, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32fbb4d7-8048-5ad1-beca-84b2a5658676'}, {'abstract': 'Celgene’s drug Abraxane prolonged the lives of patients with advanced pancreatic cancer by almost two months in a clinical trial, but the gains were not as big as expected.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/23/business/pancreatic-cancer-drug-found-to-extend-life.html', 'snippet': 'Celgene’s drug Abraxane prolonged the lives of patients with advanced pancreatic cancer by almost two months in a clinical trial, but the gains were not as big as expected.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Celgene’s drug Abraxane prolonged the lives of patients with advanced pancreatic cancer by almost two months in a clinical trial, researchers reported Tuesday, signifying an advance in treating a notoriously difficult disease but not as big a leap as some doctors and investors had hoped.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Drug Is Shown to Help Pancreatic Cancer Cases ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Drug Is Shown to Help Pancreatic Cancer Cases', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pollack, Andrew', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pancreatic Cancer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Clinical Trials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Celgene Corporation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-22T23:37:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Pollack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pollack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank'