 '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Uganda', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-23T01:09:27+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Opinion', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'Roger Ross Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roger', 'middlename': 'Ross', 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/e6c373be-703f-5af5-be8a-9c4e8c385ff2', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/e6c373be-703f-5af5-be8a-9c4e8c385ff2'}, {'abstract': 'The filmmaker Roger Ross Williams reveals how money donated by\xa0American evangelicals helps finance a violent antigay movement in\xa0Uganda.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/23/opinion/gospel-of-intolerance.html', 'snippet': 'The filmmaker Roger Ross Williams reveals how money donated by\xa0American evangelicals helps finance a violent antigay movement in\xa0Uganda.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Raised in Pennsylvania, I grew up in the black church. My father was a religious leader in the community, and my sister is a pastor. I went to church every Sunday and sang in the choir. But for all that the church gave me — for all that it represented belonging, love and community — it also shut its doors to me as a gay person. That experience left me with the lifelong desire to explore the power of religion to transform lives or destroy them. I became interested in Uganda, an intensely religious country that attracts many American missionaries and much funding from United States faith-based organizations. The American evangelical movement in Africa does valuable work in helping the poor. But as you’ll see in this Op-Doc video, some of their efforts and money feed a dangerous ideology that seeks to demonize L.G.B.T. people and intensifies religious rhetoric until it results in violence. It is important for American congregations to hold their churches accountable for what their money does in Africa. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/23/opinion/video-opdoc-uganda/video-opdoc-uganda-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/23/opinion/video-opdoc-uganda/video-opdoc-uganda-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/23/opinion/video-opdoc-uganda/video-opdoc-uganda-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 507, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/23/opinion/video-opdoc-uganda/video-opdoc-uganda-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 507, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/23/opinion/video-opdoc-uganda/video-opdoc-uganda-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/23/opinion/video-opdoc-uganda/video-opdoc-uganda-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/23/opinion/video-opdoc-uganda/video-opdoc-uganda-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Gospel of Intolerance’', 'kicker': 'Op-Docs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Gospel of Intolerance’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Uganda', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evangelical Movement', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Faith-Based Initiatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-23T01:11:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roger Ross Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roger', 'middlename': 'Ross', 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/e3d4db66-5c5b-5a8a-b6f7-1e3053e1d3e7', 'word_count': 210, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3d4db66-5c5b-5a8a-b6f7-1e3053e1d3e7'}, {'abstract': 'Six automakers are expected to advertise eight car brands during the game, while six other companies are to advertise eight beverages.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/23/business/media/super-bowl-ads-will-be-heavy-on-colas-beers-and-cars.html', 'snippet': 'Six automakers are expected to advertise eight car brands during the game, while six other companies are to advertise eight beverages.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EACH year within the Super Bowl, Madison Avenue plays an Ad Bowl, as marketers spend large amounts of time and treasure to create commercials that will, they hope, win plaudits and move merchandise. And within each Ad Bowl, two categories of consumer products usually account for a supersize amount of spots: automobiles and beverages.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/23/business/ADCO-1/ADCO-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 251, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/23/business/ADCO-1/ADCO-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 251}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/23/business/ADCO-1/ADCO-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/23/business/ADCO-1/ADCO-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 783, 'width': 1871, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/23/business/ADCO-1/ADCO-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/23/business/ADCO-1/ADCO-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/23/business/ADCO-1/ADCO-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Super Bowl Ads Will Be Heavy on Colas, Beers and Cars', 'kicker': 'Advertising', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Super Bowl Ads Will Be Heavy On Colas, Beers And Cars', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Elliott, Stuart', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Super Bowl', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beverages', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-23T01:14:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/43728ea7-8b08-5337-91ea-9c6122e6922d', 'word_count': 870, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43728ea7-8b08-5337-91ea-9c6122e6922d'}, {'abstract': 'Eritrea appeared calm on Tuesday, a day after soldiers stormed a government ministry and briefly took over the state-run airwaves, according to capital residents.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/23/world/africa/eritrea-calm-after-coup-attempt.html', 'snippet': 'Eritrea appeared calm on Tuesday, a day after soldiers stormed a government ministry and briefly took over the state-run airwaves, according to capital residents.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Eritrea appeared calm on Tuesday, a day after renegade soldiers stormed a government ministry and briefly took over the state-run airwaves, according to capital residents. “Shops, offices, banks, schools are all open,” a resident wrote by e-mail. “And cars and buses and taxis seem to be running normally.” The writer added: “The situation is murky. Nobody seems to know whether there was a coup attempt, or the whole thing was staged for some sinister purpose.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Eritrea: Calm After Coup Attempt', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Africa', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Eritrea: Calm After Coup Attempt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gettleman, Jeffrey', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Eritrea', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Coups D'Etat and Attempted Coups D'Etat", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-23T01:18:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeffrey Gettleman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeffrey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gettleman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9a90266-18f6-52a7-aca1-65ecde6fa775', 'word_count': 75, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9a90266-18f6-52a7-aca1-65ecde6fa775'}, {'abstract': 'Millions of low-income people could be required to pay more for health care under a proposed federal policy that would give states more freedom to impose additional charges on Medicaid patients.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/23/health/medicaid-patients-could-face-higher-fees-under-a-proposed-federal-policy.html', 'snippet': 'Millions of low-income people could be required to pay more for health care under a proposed federal policy that would give states more freedom to impose additional charges on Medicaid patients.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Millions of low-income people could be required to pay more for health care under a proposed federal policy that would give states more freedom to impose co-payments and other charges on Medicaid patients.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Many Medicaid Patients Could Face Higher Fees Under a Proposed Federal Policy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Many Medicaid Patients Could Face Higher Fees Under a Proposed Federal Policy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pear, Robert', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 's