n and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-23T11:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Casey B. Mulligan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Casey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb23c6f0-6475-5533-b03e-4a50b5cfde63', 'word_count': 643, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb23c6f0-6475-5533-b03e-4a50b5cfde63'}, {'abstract': 'The all-star game is lacking the talent of previous editions, but there are still a number of good prospects to evaluate.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/23/day-two-highlights-from-the-senior-bowl/', 'snippet': 'The all-star game is lacking the talent of previous editions, but there are still a number of good prospects to evaluate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOBILE, Ala. — The second day of practices Tuesday continued to reinforce the sense of urgency that the Senior Bowl director Phil Savage must be feeling to improve the direction of the all-star game. While most writers would agree – including the two of us – that the Senior Bowl has a lot to offer its players, scouts and news media, the fact that 25 percent of the players initially invited to the event turned down the chance to participate isn’t a point that is going to disappear this week when more players disappear from practices. The Clemson big-play back Andre Ellington withdrew. The Texas A&M slot man Ryan Swope was watching on the sidelines without pads. So were linebackers John Simon and Trevardo Williams.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Day Two Highlights From the Senior Bowl', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': 