rted', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/19a108ce-083d-5fe2-8142-e601a539fae6', 'word_count': 979, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19a108ce-083d-5fe2-8142-e601a539fae6'}, {'abstract': 'Italian prosecutors continue to investigate suspected Mafia involvement in renewable energy projects from Sardinia to Apulia.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/23/on-our-radar-clean-energy-sullied/', 'snippet': 'Italian prosecutors continue to investigate suspected Mafia involvement in renewable energy projects from Sardinia to Apulia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The ongoing discovery of links between the Mafia and Italy’s once-booming wind and solar industries raises questions about the use of government subsidies for renewable energy. [The Washington Post]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Our Radar: Clean Energy, Sullied', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-23T12:41:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/be116520-c4d8-5ab0-8fa4-79bc0f20c0de', 'word_count': 132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be116520-c4d8-5ab0-8fa4-79bc0f20c0de'}, {'abstract': 'A massive Kurdish funeral procession in eastern Turkey was a well-ordered, dignified display of grief, but the Turkish media wouldn’t show it.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/23/turkish-media-wont-report-good-news-about-the-kurds/', 'snippet': 'A massive Kurdish funeral procession in eastern Turkey was a well-ordered, dignified display of grief, but the Turkish media wouldn’t show it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISTANBUL — Last Thursday was a major news day in Turkey, and part of the story was that the Turkish media failed to report a major event in the Kurdish southeast of the country.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The News They Carried', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Funerals and Memorials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kurds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Kurdistan Workers' Party", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-23T12:48:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Finkel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Finkel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1dfe8e1-1924-5890-8f7f-599bb796d283', 'word_count': 735, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1dfe8e1-1924-5890-8f7f-599bb796d283'}, {'abstract': 'During an often contentious panel discussion in Davos, Switzerland, Jamie Dimon of JPMorgan Chase defended the banking industry’s changes since the financial crisis as Axel Weber, the chairman of UBS, criticized central bankers.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/01/23/at-davos-financial-leaders-debate-reform-and-monetary-policy/', 'snippet': 'During an often contentious panel discussion in Davos, Switzerland, Jamie Dimon of JPMorgan Chase defended the banking industry’s changes since the financial crisis as Axel Weber, the chairman of UBS, criticized central bankers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DAVOS, Switzerland — Jamie Dimon, the chief executive of JPMorgan Chase, apologized again for the bank’s recent $6 billion trading loss, this time in front of an audience that included the elite of the financial world. But in keeping with his confident demeanor, it was a diet portion of humble pie.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Davos, Financial Leaders Debate Reform and Monetary Policy', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dimon, James', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weber, Axel A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Economic Forum', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Davos (Switzerland)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-23T12:49:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Ewing', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ewing', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5fe3815-1620-5d5f-bcbf-5e0d22097ddf', 'word_count': 613, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5fe3815-1620-5d5f-bcbf-5e0d22097ddf'}, {'abstract': 'The former Raiders coach said he was shocked and saddened by accusations from Tim Brown and Jerry Rice that he tried to lose the 2003 Super Bowl to Tampa Bay.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/23/bill-callahans-statement-denying-super-bowl-sabotage/', 'snippet': 'The former Raiders coach said he was shocked and saddened by accusations from Tim Brown and Jerry Rice that he tried to lose the 2003 Super Bowl to Tampa Bay.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The former Raiders coach Bill Callahan released a statement Tuesday night denying accusations that he tried to lose the 2003 Super Bowl against Tampa Bay.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bill Callahan’s Statement Denying Super Bowl ‘Sabotage’