pub_date': '2013-01-23T13:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Streitfeld', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Streitfeld', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/116ffc74-e0d4-52d6-a91a-2a10786297b8', 'word_count': 472, 'uri': 'nyt://article/116ffc74-e0d4-52d6-a91a-2a10786297b8'}, {'abstract': 'A back-and-forth about SSI, my reporting and how best to make progress on poverty.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/23/chipping-away-at-poverty-an-exchange/', 'snippet': 'A back-and-forth about SSI, my reporting and how best to make progress on poverty.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Advocates of Supplemental Security Income, or SSI, have been steaming at a December column that I wrote from Kentucky, arguing that it unfairly maligns a program that is a lifeline to the disabled. Here’s one criticism , here’s another, and here are letters we published. I’ve tweeted some of the criticisms and responded with tweets, but I haven’t really engaged in a broader discussion, so that’s what I’d like to do here. First, you’ll see below a memo from two attorneys from Community Legal Services in Philadelphia to the Times’s Public Editor (they’ve agreed to make the memo public), and then (after their footnotes) a response by me to the points they raise.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chipping Away at Poverty — an Exchange', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illiteracy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Welfare (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Social Security Administration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kentucky', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-23T13:08:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/90297cb7-a2ef-55fb-aaea-f4a36f7ab51a', 'word_count': 3960, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90297cb7-a2ef-55fb-aaea-f4a36f7ab51a'}, {'abstract': 'A summary of what’s on today’s editorial page.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/23/opinion-report-the-school-bus-strike/', 'snippet': 'A summary of what’s on today’s editorial page.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From the editorial page', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Opinion Report: The School Bus Strike', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-23T13:15:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a3b204d-7569-555d-8ce9-afe6a4731e23', 'word_count': 66, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a3b204d-7569-555d-8ce9-afe6a4731e23'}, {'abstract': 'In Microsoft, Silver Lake may have found a major ally for a takeover effort for Dell. | The Davos agenda has few meetings on financial risk, creating the impression that the world’s leaders have other priorities. | Should bankers have faced criminal action over the financial crisis? | Morgan Stanley is pushing bills into the future by deferring compensation for its employees.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/01/23/for-dell-deal-silver-lake-may-find-a-partner-in-microsoft/', 'snippet': 'In Microsoft, Silver Lake may have found a major ally for a takeover effort for Dell. | The Davos agenda has few meetings on financial risk, creating the impression that the world’s leaders have other priorities. | Should bankers have faced crimin...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Silver Lake may have found a deep-pocketed investor to join a takeover effort for Dell. Microsoft, Dell’s longtime ally, is in talks to contribute up to several billion dollars to a potential bid, which could exceed $20 billion, a person briefed on the matter tells DealBook’s Michael J. de la Merced. Microsoft, which has not yet made a commitment, has more than $66 billion in cash on hand. The company has done business with Silver Lake in the past, including when Microsoft acquired Skype in 2011.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Dell Deal, Silver Lake May Find a Partner in Microsoft', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-23T13:18:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf320534-cd1c-586c-8476-d9e675d21c8a', 'word_count': 1881, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf320534-cd1c-586c-8476-d9e675d21c8a'}, {'abstract': 'In Tainan, a city in Taiwan’s south, two new museums show the depth of cultural and historical diversity on the island.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/23/taiwans-diverse-literature-and-history-on-show-in-two-new-museums/', 'snippet': 'In Tainan, a city in Taiwan’s south, two new museums show the depth of cultural and historical diversity on the island.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAINAN — Two new museums in Tainan, a city in Taiwan’s south, say much about how the island’s people have worked in recent years to build an unusually inclusive cultural identity, a model for Chinese-speaking societies, as I write in my Letter from Taiwan this week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Taiwan’s Diverse Literature and History on Show in Two New Museums', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collectors and Collections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tainan (Taiwan)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Taiwan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-23T13:21:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Didi Kirsten Tatlow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Didi', 'middlename': 'Kirsten', 'lastname': 'Tatlow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/66c61b60-3a0b-5086-8000-b3a8498ab0fc', 'word_count': 353, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66c61b60-3a0b-5086-8000-b3a8498ab0fc'}, {'abstract': 'As Research in Motion prepares to introduce the BlackBerry 10, the company has been very cagey about the fees it will charge corporations for using the device’s network. The fees have been an important part of RIM’s profits and analysts are concerned about a possible decline in revenue.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/23/rim-still-unable-to-clarify-its-fee-structure/', 'snippet': 'As Research in Motion prepares to introduce the BlackBerry 10, the company has been very cagey about the fees it will charge corporations for using the device’s network. The fees have been an important part of RIM’s profits and analysts are concer...', 'lead_paragraph': 'For their maker, Research in Motion, BlackBerrys have always been the gift that keeps on giving. Until now, every BlackBerry handset has continued to generate monthly service fees for the company until it falls apart or is stuck in a drawer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'RIM Still Unable to Clarify Its Fee Structure', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'BlackBerry (Handheld Device)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Research In Motion Ltd', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-23T13:24:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18a06a6d-e98a-5c0f-81f6-fbb339d7a5bf', 'word_count': 598, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18a06a6d-e98a-5c0f-81f6-fbb339d7a5bf'}, {'abstract': 'Metropolitan Diary: A couple having a special dinner at an expensive restaurant hears how to make a glass of iced tea go farther.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/23/overheard-at-le-bernardin/', 'snippet': 'Metropolitan Diary: A couple having a special dinner at an expensive restaurant hears how to make a glass of iced tea go farther.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Dear Dia