 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d32b17e-d6d9-5fad-9594-efe4747a595d'}, {'abstract': 'The protests two years ago shook the rule of King Abdullah II, and he is relying on the results to quiet his critics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/24/world/middleeast/jordanians-vote-in-first-parliament-elections-since-protests.html', 'snippet': 'The protests two years ago shook the rule of King Abdullah II, and he is relying on the results to quiet his critics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MULEIH, Jordan — Two years ago, Mohamed al-Snaid organized laborers to demonstrate against poor working conditions, helping to start a movement that spread throughout the country and gave voice to a festering anger that has shaken the rule of King Abdullah II. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Despite Boycott, More Than Half of Voters Are Said to Turn Out in Jordan Election', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Despite Boycott, More Than Half of Voters Are Said to Turn Out in Jordan Election', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fahim, Kareem', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jordan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-23T13:36:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kareem Fahim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kareem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fahim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/75dbd44e-5ccc-56c0-8df4-fc1cb3d27fa5', 'word_count': 559, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75dbd44e-5ccc-56c0-8df4-fc1cb3d27fa5'}, {'abstract': 'I like the newer, blunter me. I sense a whole new world opening up.', 'web_url': 'https://