gacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Courtesy Control Malfunctions', 'kicker': 'I Was Misinformed', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Boomers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs, Etiquette and Manners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-23T14:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Booming', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joyce Wadler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joyce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wadler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1060e0c3-fb2f-5b14-9011-ba65e5eb7f07', 'word_count': 888, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1060e0c3-fb2f-5b14-9011-ba65e5eb7f07'}, {'abstract': 'Social programs are often the target of conservative budget cuts, but they often save us money. Investing in the best of them will save even more.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/23/when-paying-it-forward-pays-us-back/', 'snippet': 'Social programs are often the target of conservative budget cuts, but they often save us money. Investing in the best of them will save even more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you’ve listened to the debate on how the United States should avoid going over the “fiscal cliff” over the past months, you might believe that the government has only two options to address its budget woes — either slash social programs, as conservatives favor, or the liberal tack, raise taxes. That’s a myopic view, one that actually distorts the relationship between social programs and society at large. Many of the most effective ones are not a mere expense to be trimmed off a budget; they often can and do save considerable money for society. And they’d be even more economical in this regard if the government invested in their widespread adoption.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Paying It Forward Pays Us Back', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nursing and Nurses', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-23T14:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Bornstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bornstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5bf952ac-85ba-562d-8a51-94305c00ce00', 'word_count': 1367, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5bf952ac-85ba-562d-8a51-94305c00ce00'}, {'abstract': 'Gary Clark Jr. is also on the bill for the ceremony on April 18 in Los Angeles.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/23/mayer-hudson-and-aguilera-among-performers-for-rock-hall-ceremony/', 'snippet': 'Gary Clark Jr. is also on the bill for the ceremony on April 18 in Los Angeles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'John Mayer, Jennifer Hudson and Christina Aguilera are among the musicians who will perform at the induction ceremony in April for the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame and Museum.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mayer, Hudson and Aguilera Among Performers for Rock Hall Ceremony', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mayer and Hudson To Sing at Rock Hall', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject'