}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Boeing’s Battery Problems Cast Doubt on Appraisal of New Technologies', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Boeing Battery Problems Cast Doubt on Technology Appraisals', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Batteries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Drew, Christopher', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boeing Company', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aviation Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lithium (Metal)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Aviation Administration', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-23T14:20:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jad Mouawad and Christopher Drew', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mouawad', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Drew', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/38360481-54e3-50f0-b980-9fd410608fe2', 'word_count': 1358, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38360481-54e3-50f0-b980-9fd410608fe2'}, {'abstract': 'Secretary of State Hillary Rodham Clinton asserted that she had moved quickly to improve the security of American diplomats after the September attack in Benghazi that killed four Americans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/24/us/testifying-on-benghazi-clinton-cites-new-security-steps.html', 'snippet': 'Secretary of State Hillary Rodham Clinton asserted that she had moved quickly to improve the security of American diplomats after the September attack in Benghazi that killed four Americans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — In one of her final appearances as secretary of state, Hillary Rodham Clinton on Wednesday vigorously defended her handling of last September’s attack on the United States diplomatic compound in Benghazi, Libya, which killed four Americans and prompted a scathing review of State Department procedures.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/24/us/politics/24clinton2/24clinton2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/24/us/politics/24clinton2/24clinton2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/24/us/politics/24clinton2/24clinton2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/24/us/politics/24clinton2/24clinton2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/24/us/politics/24clinton2/24clinton2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/24/us/politics/24clinton2/24clinton2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/24/us/politics/24clinton2/24clinton2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Facing Congress, Clinton Defends Her Actions Before and After Libya Attack', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Facing Congress, Clinton Defends Her Actions Before and After Libya Attack', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gordon, Michael R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Benghazi (Libya)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Benghazi Attack (2012)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-23T14:24:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael R. Gordon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Gordon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8bc167a1-5c01-5390-82a7-4718a7a21c3e', 'word_count': 1181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8bc167a1-5c01-5390-82a7-4718a7a21c3e'}, {'abstract': 'The last concert will offer works in which death plays a prominent role.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/23/carnegie-halls-spring-for-music-will-expire-on-fitting-notes/', 'snippet': 'The last concert will offer works in which death plays a prominent role.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The final performance of the final season of “Spring for Music,” an orchestra festival at Carnegie Hall, will have a fittingly morbid theme, according to programming announced on Tuesday. The Pittsburgh Symphony Orchestra, on May 10, 2014, will present the last scene of Poulenc’s opera “Dialogues of the Carmelites,” in which a group of nuns are serially guillotined; the first New York performance of James MacMillan’s “Woman of the Apocalypse,” based on the Book of Revelation; and a mélange of Mozart music — titled “Requiem and Death in Words and Music” — centered around his completed sections of the “Requiem.” Pittsburgh’s music director, Manfred Honeck, will conduct.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Carnegie Hall’s ‘Spring for Music’ Will Expire on Fitting Notes', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Fitting Ending For Carnegie Festival', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Spring for Music Festival (Carnegie Hall)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Honeck, Manfred', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mozart, Wolfgang Amadeus', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Poulenc, Francis', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carnegie Hall', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cincinnati Symphony Orchestra', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Philharmonic', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pittsburgh Symphony Orchestra', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rochester Philharmonic', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Seattle Symphony', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pittsburgh (Pa)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-23T14:30:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7457975a-50de-59fc-8e87-8b54a0a329be', 'word_count': 159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7457975a-50de-59fc-8e87-8b54a0a329be'}, {'abstract': 'There is a saying in France: vivre cachée, vivre heureux: live hidden, live happily. A winemaker in a region steeped in tradition takes the opposite view.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/23/in-saint-milion-rich-and-proud-of-it/', 'snippet': 'There is a saying in France: vivre cachée, vivre heureux: live hidden, live happily. A winemaker in a region steeped in tradition takes the opposite view.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAINT-ÉMILION, France—There is a saying in France: Vivre cachée, vivre heureux; “live hidden, live happily.” It applies especially to the country’s rich people. Not only do public displays of wealth draw the covetous gaze of tax collectors, they are frowned on by a culture that values solidarity. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/23/arts/23RDV-WINE/23RDV-WINE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/23/arts/23RDV-WINE/23RDV-WINE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/23/arts/23RDV-WINE/23RDV-WINE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/23/arts/23RDV-WINE/23RDV-WINE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None,