iginal': 'By Christopher F. Schuetze', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Schuetze', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ba18c81-d363-5387-b410-31db3d8fe5bb', 'word_count': 297, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ba18c81-d363-5387-b410-31db3d8fe5bb'}, {'abstract': 'Also, country music radio returns to New York, and a big premiere for Fox’s “The Following.”', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/23/the-breakfast-meeting-how-espn-missed-the-hoax-story-and-hard-times-at-sundance/', 'snippet': 'Also, country music radio returns to New York, and a big premiere for Fox’s “The Following.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'ESPN had been trying to confirm the story that Manti Te’o’s girlfriend – whose apparent death from leukemia became a rallying cry for Notre Dame football and a selling-point for the linebacker’s Heisman candidacy – was a hoax. But the network was hoping for an interview with Mr. Te’o and lost the story to Deadspin.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: How ESPN Missed the Hoax Story and Hard Times at Sundance', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-23T14:50:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editors', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editors'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b39b545-502f-5d7b-9e32-8a8b38496161', 'word_count': 273, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b39b545-502f-5d7b-9e32-8a8b38496161'}, {'abstract': 'David Cameron, the British prime minister, has pledged a referendum on the country’s place in Europe if he is re-elected. Older voters should be forgiven for thinking they’ve been here before.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/23/britons-promised-vote-on-europe-again/', 'snippet': 'David Cameron, the British prime minister, has pledged a referendum on the country’s place in Europe if he is re-elected. Older voters should be forgiven for thinking they’ve been here before.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — A British political leader faces dissent within his own party over the country’s membership in Europe. He promises to renegotiate the terms and to hold a referendum on the issue if he wins the next election.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/23/blogs/23rdv-referendum/23rdv-referendum-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/23/blogs/23rdv-referendum/23rdv-referendum-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/23/blogs/23rdv-referendum/23rdv-referendum-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/23/blogs/23rdv-referendum/23rdv-referendum-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/23/blogs/23rdv-referendum/23rdv-referendum-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/23/blogs/23rdv-referendum/23rdv-referendum-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/