o criticizing the Syrian opposition, Russia’s foreign minister said the decision to remove 77 Russians from Syria did not signal the start of an evacuation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — Russia’s foreign minister, Sergey V. Lavrov, said on Wednesday that the main obstacle to peace in Syria was the opposition’s “obsession with the idea of toppling the Bashar al-Assad regime.” He also said that the Kremlin’s Emergency Ministry flights that removed 77 Russians from the war zone early on Wednesday had not signaled the start of an evacuation.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/24/world/24russia_span2/24russia_span2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/24/world/24russia_span2/24russia_span2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/24/world/24russia_span2/24russia_span2-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/24/world/24russia_span2/24russia_span2-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1361, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/24/world/24russia_span2/24russia_span2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/24/world/24russia_span2/24russia_span2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, '