p-the-bodies/', 'snippet': 'The plays, adapted by Mike Boulton from Hilary Mantel’s prize-winning novels, will begin in repertory in December.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Wolf Hall” and “Bring Up the Bodies,” Hilary Mantel’s pair of Man Booker Prize-winning novels about Tudor England, are coming to the stage. The Royal Shakespeare Company announced on Wednesday that Mike Poulton, known for his theatrical versions of classic works like “The Canterbury Tales” and “Le Morte d’Arthur,” is adapting both books for the company, and that the stage versions, directed by Jeremy Herrin, will appear in repertory starting in December.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Royal Shakespeare Company to Stage ‘Wolf Hall’ and ‘Bring Up the Bodies’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'British Troupe to Stage Two Hilary Mantel Works', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Man Booker Prize', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cromwell, Thomas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Doran, Gregory', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Herrin, Jeremy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mantel, Hilary', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Poulton, Mike', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tennant, David', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-23T17:39:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles McGrath', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGrath', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c5ddcf2-6ee5-509f-a7f2-46fbe82c3af1', 'word_count': 214, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c5ddcf2-6ee5-509f-a7f2-46fbe82c3af1'}, {'abstract': 'Federal authorities charged three Eastern European men with using a computer virus, nicknamed Gozi, that surreptitiously infected over a million computers worldwide, including at NASA, to steal what prosecutors said was at least tens of millions of dollars from personal bank accounts.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/23/u-s-charges-three-with-hacking/', 'snippet': 'Federal authorities charged three Eastern European men with using a computer virus, nicknamed Gozi, that surreptitiously infected over a million computers worldwide, including at NASA, to steal what prosecutors said was at least tens of millions o...', 'lead_paragraph': '3:22 p.m. | Updated to change name of one of the people indicted. He is Mihai Ionut Paunescu, not Ionut Paunescu. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Charges Three With Hacking', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Malware', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Aeronautics and Space Administration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-23T17:57:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Somini Sengupta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Somini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sengupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d67e62e-61ac-5ba1-912d-1cb7493929bf', 'word_count': 236, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d67e62e-61ac-5ba1-912d-1cb7493929bf'}, {'abstract': 'Although President Obama barely touched on gun control in his Inaugural Address, he infuriated the ever-vigilant executive vice president of the National Rifle Association.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/23/wayne-lapierre-strikes-again/', 'snippet': 'Although President Obama barely touched on gun control in his Inaugural Address, he infuriated the ever-vigilant executive vice president of the National Rifle Association.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama made only glancing reference to gun control in his Inaugural Address, merely saying that we need to keep our children safe “from the streets of Detroit to the hills of Appalachia to the quiet lanes of Newtown.” But he didn’t fool Wayne LaPierre, the ever-vigilant executive vice president of the National Rifle Association.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wayne LaPierre Strikes Again', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'LaPierre, Wayne', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Rifle Assn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-23T18:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2bf91a03-acf4-504a-bd0b-949287dfb3d9', 'word_count': 519, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2bf91a03-acf4-504a-bd0b-949287dfb3d9'}, {'abstract': 'Colleen Atwood, a three-time Oscar winner for her costume design and nominee for “Snow White and the Huntsman,” discusses her work.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/23/below-the-line-dressing-snow-white/', 'snippet': 'Colleen Atwood, a three-time Oscar winner for her costume design and nominee for “Snow White and the Huntsman,” discusses her work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Colleen Atwood is no stranger to the Oscars. The much sought-after costume designer has been nominated for 10 Academy Awards and has won three for her work on “Chicago” (2002), “Memoirs of a Geisha” (2006) and “Alice in Wonderland” (2010).', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Below the Line: Dressing ‘Snow White’', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Veil Fit For a Queen', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Costumes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Atwood, Colleen', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hemsworth, Chris', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanders, Rupert', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stewart, Kristen', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Theron, Charlize', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-23T18:00:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9bd1ba7-3253-5ad9-9035-f40a44957c8d', 'word_count': 760, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9bd1ba7-3253-5ad9-9035-f40a44957c8d'}, {'abstract': 'The cruise industry has instituted 10 new safety policies in response to the Costa Concordia crash that killed 32 people a year ago.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/23/before-setting-off-a-drill/', 'snippet': 'The cruise industry has instituted 10 new safety policies in response to the Costa Concordia crash that killed 32 people a year ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The cruise industry has instituted 10 new safety policies in response to the Costa Concordia crash that killed 32 people a year ago. The Cruise Lines International Association, the trade group that represents major cruise lines globally, has developed requirements over the last year that muster drills, passenger emergency drills, be conducted before departing from port rather than within 24 hours of sailing, and that the crew receives more mandatory lifeboat training, among other measures. The International Maritime Organization, a United Nations agency that oversees maritime safety, said it expects to make muster drills before departure mandatory.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Before Setting Off, a Drill', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cruises: Before Setting Off, a Drill', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cruises', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cruise Lines International Assn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Maritime Organization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-23T18:00:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tanya Mohn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tanya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55c3fbdf-0d7