rge W. Bush’s second inauguration in 2005.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/23/more-than-20-million-viewers-watched-coverage-of-inauguration/', 'snippet': 'The total was down sharply from four years ago for President Obama’s first inauguration, but higher than George W. Bush’s second inauguration in 2005.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A total of 20.552 million viewers tuned in on 18 separate television networks to watch coverage of the second inauguration of President Obama, the Nielsen Company reported Wednesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Than 20 Million Viewers Watched Coverage of Inauguration', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cable Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inaugurations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reagan, Ronald Wilson', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nielsen Media Research', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-23T18:16:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/44d55086-b356-579a-9302-879bc1af244d', 'word_count': 237, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44d55086-b356-579a-9302-879bc1af244d'}, {'abstract': 'Three suspects in the theft of seven masterpieces from the Kunsthal Museum in Rotterdam in October have been arrested in Romania, but there is still no word on where the stolen art might be.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/23/suspects-in-dutch-art-heist-if-not-the-art-itself-in-custody/', 'snippet': 'Three suspects in the theft of seven masterpieces from the Kunsthal Museum in Rotterdam in October have been arrested in Romania, but there is still no word on where the stolen art might be.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Three suspects in the theft of seven masterpieces from the Kunsthal Museum in Rotterdam, the Netherlands, have been arrested in Romania, but there is still no word on where the stolen art might be, the BBC reported. The paintings, which include works by Monet, Picasso, Matisse and Lucien Freud, were taken from the gallery on Oct. 16. A spokeswoman for the Rotterdam police, Yvette van den Heerik, said that the suspects’ involvement was still being investigated.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Suspects in Dutch Art Heist (if Not the Art Itself) in Custody', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Matisse, Henri', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Monet, Claude', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Picasso, Pablo', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kunsthal Museum (Rotterdam, Netherlands)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Caracas (Venezuela)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Miami (Fla)', 'rank': 10, 'ma