ps://publiceditor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/23/the-raging-debate-over-objectivity-and-transparency/', 'snippet': 'Is the concept outdated or even more important in the new media era?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The objectivity argument I wrote about this month continues to simmer. In the interests of making this blog a continuing conversation about journalism issues, large and small, I’m posting a few of the most substantial pieces on this subject that I’ve seen in recent weeks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Raging Debate Over Objectivity and Transparency', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-23T18:29:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d881464a-56ea-5d31-a834-4e8b47180e68', 'word_count': 431, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d881464a-56ea-5d31-a834-4e8b47180e68'}, {'abstract': 'Saying “torture is reprehensible,” Kathryn Bigelow defends “Zero Dark Thirty” on “The Colbert Report.”', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/23/kathryn-bigelow-speaks-out/', 'snippet': 'Saying “torture is reprehensible,” Kathryn Bigelow defends “Zero Dark Thirty” on “The Colbert Report.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Colbert Report Get More: Colbert Report Full Episodes,Political Humor & Satire Blog,Video Archive', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kathryn Bigelow Speaks Out', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bigelow, Kathryn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Colbert, Stephen', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-23T18:30:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e97c29c-b5a1-5c6e-86ef-e46c305d1beb', 'word_count': 93, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e97c29c-b5a1-5c6e-86ef-e46c305d1beb'}, {'abstract': 'Print, dress: a new company lets the consumer turn a photograph into a custom-fit, ready-to-wear design.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/23/site-to-be-seen-constrvt-com/', 'snippet': 'Print, dress: a new company lets the consumer turn a photograph into a custom-fit, ready-to-wear design.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To established fashion designers, Mary Huang and Jenna Fizel may well appear as the Visigoths did to the Romans: outsiders bent on cheerfully upending civilization as they know it. Interaction designers by training and novices to the fashion world, the two have started a clothing label that essentially eliminates the need for the creative vision of one person. Instead, they’ve created software that puts that power in the hands of consumers, a process Huang calls “fashion design for the Instagram generation.” Shoppers logging on to constrvct.com can upload a photograph that will later be translated into a print, choose from a variety of basic silhouettes (the sheath dress is currently the most popular), then plug in their measurements. Three weeks later, a dress arrives in the mail, a time scale Huang estimate will be cut by two-thirds once the partners raise the funds to bring production in-house. Soon, pre-existing images will be available for selection, with royalties going to the artists who created them. And plans are afoot to add further customizing options like neckline, sleeve and hemline choices. “We don’t even need to make a pattern,” Huang says. “We can make the dress directly from the 3-D model. It’s basically you press the button, we make the dress. If we can do this at scale, it could change the way the whole industry works.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Site to Be Seen | constrvct.com', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-23T18:30:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nancy MacDonell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nancy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacDonell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0145e792-b70a-592f-abb8-1c24e4ade859', 'word_count': 225, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0145e792-b70a-592f-abb8-1c24e4ade859'}, {'abstract': 'Brooks and Collins on all the good inauguration-sequestration gossip.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/23/hats-off-to-president-obama/', 'snippet': 'Brooks and Collins on all the good inauguration-sequestration gossip.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David Brooks: Let’s get to the big news of the week first, at least to me. Did you know that Jimmy Carter once allegedly went after a dog with a saw because it ate some of 