om/2013/01/24/arts/music/jeff-harnar-cabaret-at-laurie-beechman-theater.html', 'snippet': 'In Jeff Harnar’s cabaret show “Does This Song Make Me Look Fat?” his comedic special material had an extra edge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sooner or later the eternal boy becomes a man. It happened to Robert Morse, once the embodiment of a juvenile male lead in Broadway musicals who eventually turned into Bertram Cooper, the crabby senior ad executive in “Mad Men.” And it has happened to Jeff Harnar, the ingenuous cabaret crooner who in the 1980s and ’90s might have played the same chirpy eager-beaver roles associated with Mr. Morse had they been created. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/24/arts/HARNAR/HARNAR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 391, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/24/arts/HARNAR/HARNAR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 391}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/24/arts/HARNAR/HARNAR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 667, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/24/arts/HARNAR/HARNAR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1334, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/24/arts/HARNAR/HARNAR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/24/arts/HARNAR/HARNAR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'i