me': 'Crawford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9f49a50-731e-54cd-b945-ea0a05b607b0', 'word_count': 797, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9f49a50-731e-54cd-b945-ea0a05b607b0'}, {'abstract': 'The war in Mali is not just about preventing terrorism; it’s a fight to defend a secular, tolerant society.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/24/opinion/the-taliban-of-timbuktu.html', 'snippet': 'The war in Mali is not just about preventing terrorism; it’s a fight to defend a secular, tolerant society.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEFORE the recent French intervention in Mali began, 412,000 people had already left their homes in the country’s north, fleeing torture, summary executions, recruitment of child soldiers and sexual violence against women at the hands of fundamentalist militants. Late last year, in Algeria and southern Mali, I interviewed dozens of Malians from the north, including many who had recently fled. Their testimonies confirmed the horrors that radical Islamists, self-proclaimed warriors of God, have inflicted on their communities.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Taliban of Timbuktu', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Taliban of Timbuktu', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mali', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shariah (Islamic Law)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mujao (Movement for Oneness and Jihad in West Africa)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-24T01:23:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karima Bennoune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karima', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bennoune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b61ff7d-0c7e-5a7c-8770-f4d7dfed994b', 'word_count': 928, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b61ff7d-0c7e-5a7c-8770-f4d7dfed994b'}, {'abstract': 'Supporters say that if the gay marriage bill gets to the Senate, it would pass, but opponents are skeptical and state senators are being lobbied heavily by both sides.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/24/us/politics/rhode-island-weighs-gay-marriage-as-the-last-holdout-in-new-england.html', 'snippet': 'Supporters say that if the gay marriage bill gets to the Senate, it would pass, but opponents are skeptical and state senators are being lobbied heavily by both sides.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PROVIDENCE, R.I. — Rhode Island, the only state in New England that has not legalized gay marriage, began taking up the matter this week. The State House is expected to pass a bill Thursday that would allow anyone to marry “any eligible person regardless of gender.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/24/us/RHODE-ISLAND/RHODE-ISLAND-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 362, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/24/us/RHODE-ISLAND/RHODE-ISLAND-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 362}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/24/us/RHODE-ISLAND/RHODE-ISLAND-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 619, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/24/us/RHODE-ISLAND/RHODE-ISLAND-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1237, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/24/us/RHODE-ISLAND/RHODE-ISLAND-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/24/us/RHODE-ISLAND/RHODE-ISLAND-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/24/us/RHODE-ISLAND/RHODE-ISLAND-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Last Holdout in New England, Rhode Island Weighs Gay Marriage', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Last Holdout in New England, Rhode Island Weighs Gay Marriage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rhode Island', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-24T01:30:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katharine Q. Seelye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katharine', 'middlename': 'Q.', 'lastname': 'Seelye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b99f6eae-230e-54ec-8228-43654816ab56', 'word_count': 923, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b99f6eae-230e-54ec-8228-43654816ab56'}, {'abstract': 'The president said equality for all is a main goal of his second term. He could begin by helping to make sure a child’s potential for success isn’t limited by a ZIP code.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/24/opinion/kristof-for-obamas-new-term-start-here.html', 'snippet': 'The president said equality for all is a main goal of his second term. He could begin by helping to make sure a child’s potential for success isn’t limited by a ZIP code.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Point to a group of toddlers in an upper-middle-class neighborhood in America, and it’s a good bet that they will go to college, buy nice houses and enjoy white-collar careers.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/nicholas-kristof/nicholas-kristof-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/nicholas-kristof/nicholas-kristof-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/nicholas-kristof/nicholas-kristof-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/nicholas-kristof/nicholas-kristof-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/nicholas-kristof/nicholas-kristof-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/nicho