ship with President Obama as he navigates Israel’s new political landscape.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/24/world/middleeast/netanyahu-obama-ties-may-thaw-after-israel-election.html', 'snippet': 'Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu’s weakened position could set the stage for an improvement in his relationship with President Obama as he navigates Israel’s new political landscape.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — For President Obama, whose relationship with Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu of Israel has often resembled that of a couple trapped in a loveless marriage, the last three months must have offered some grim satisfaction.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Netanyahu-Obama Ties May Thaw After Israel Election', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Netanyahu, Weakened by Election, May Mend Ties to Obama', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Landler, Mark', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netanyahu, Benjamin', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yesh Atid', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-24T01:42:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/94ff77a4-0cbd-5ab2-b0e3-5700f5e79712', 'word_count': 1016, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94ff77a4-0cbd-5ab2-b0e3-5700f5e79712'}, {'abstract': 'The filmmaker follows Travis Williams, a young public defender in the Deep South, who struggles against long hours, low pay and staggering caseloads to bring justice to all.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/24/opinion/true-believers-in-justice.html', 'snippet': 'The filmmaker follows Travis Williams, a young public defender in the Deep South, who struggles against long hours, low pay and staggering caseloads to bring justice to all.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’d always wanted to be a lawyer, but unlike Travis Williams — the subject of this Op-Doc video — I never wanted to be a public defender. I didn’t understand how anyone could represent people who did terrible things. “Criminals” were not people I wanted to help. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/24/opinion/video-opdoc-gideon/video-opdoc-gideon-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/24/opinion/video-opdoc-gideon/video-opdoc-gideon-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/24/opinion/video-opdoc-gideon/video-opdoc-gideon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/24/opinion/video-opdoc-gideon/video-opdoc-gideon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘True Believers in Justice’', 'kicker': 'Op-Docs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘True Believers in Justice’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Defenders and Court-Appointed Lawyers (Criminal)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-24T01:43:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dawn Porter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dawn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Porter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/fdb7f4bb-fa57-561a-9626-2019d5549c3c', 'word_count': 413, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fdb7f4bb-fa57-561a-9626-2019d5549c3c'}, {'abstract': 'Yair Lapid’s party shocked the political establishment by winning 19 of Parliament’s 120 seats, becoming Israel’s second-largest faction and a crucial partner for Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/24/world/middleeast/the-making-of-yair-lapid-israels-new-power-broker.html', 'snippet': 'Yair Lapid’s party shocked the political establishment by winning 19 of Parliament’s 120 seats, becoming Israel’s second-largest faction and a crucial partner for Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TEL AVIV — They pitched tents along Rothschild Boulevard and took to the streets in unprecedented numbers, hundreds of thousands demonstrating against the rising costs of gas, apartments, even cottage cheese.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/24/world/israel1/israel1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/24/world/israel1/israel1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/24/world/israel1/israel1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumb