rgues for more efforts to increase the rate of students finishing a degree — not just getting more of them into college.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/23/helping-degree-seekers-finish-what-they-start/', 'snippet': 'A report argues for more efforts to increase the rate of students finishing a degree — not just getting more of them into college.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is a paradox in American higher education: of the millions of students who apply to and enter postsecondary degree programs, only about half end up graduating within six years.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Helping Degree Seekers Finish What They Start', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Graduation Rates', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-24T02:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annie Lowrey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lowrey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/81a8b682-394e-56f1-88ea-ba9c53631399', 'word_count': 502, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81a8b682-394e-56f1-88ea-ba9c53631399'}, {'abstract': 'Roe V. Wade, decided 40 years ago was not about women’s rights. It was about doctors who faced criminal prosecution for acting in what they thought was the best interests of their patients.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/23/misconceptions/', 'snippet': 'Roe V. Wade, decided 40 years ago was not about women’s rights. It was about doctors who faced criminal prosecution for acting in what they thought was the best interests of their patients.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Francis Lorson, the longtime chief deputy clerk of the Supreme Court, once told me the following story. On a January day in the mid-1970s, he and Justice Potter Stewart were in an official car traveling from the court to the White House, where the justice was to preside at a swearing-in ceremony. As they rode along Pennsylvania Avenue, they saw a crowd heading in the opposite direction, up Capitol Hill toward the court.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Misconceptions', 'kicker': 'Opinionator', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roe v Wade (Supreme Court Decision)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Connor, Sandra Day", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stewart, Potter', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Planned Parenthood Federation of America', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-24T02:00:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Linda Greenhouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Linda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenhouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5d9b697-4575-5f30-9af7-111b0f261358', 'word_count': 1780, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5d9b697-4575-5f30-9af7-111b0f261358'}, {'abstract': 'With one Democratic senator absent, Republicans in the Virginia State Senate pushed through a redistricting bill by one vote that Democrats say dilutes blacks’ votes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/24/us/politics/virginia-senates-redistricting-is-protested.html', 'snippet': 'With one Democratic senator absent, Republicans in the Virginia State Senate pushed through a redistricting bill by one vote that Democrats say dilutes blacks’ votes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Monday, one of Virginia’s state senators attended the inauguration: Henry L. Marsh III, a longtime civil rights lawyer, who played hooky to witness a milestone for an African-American president.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Redistricting in Virginia Hurts Blacks, Democrats Say', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Redistricting In Virginia Hurts Blacks, Democrats Say', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Redistricting and Reapportionment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gabriel, Trip', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marsh, Henry L III', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-24T02:01:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Trip Gabriel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Trip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/135655b3-89d7-5b2c-837d-12000cf68c13', 'word_count': 702, 'uri': 'nyt://article/135655b3-89d7-5b2c-837d-12000cf68c13'}, {'abstract': 'A French lawyer working with Fl