me': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-24T03:31:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By John F. Burns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Burns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c625ca4-e597-5655-9693-799a8a0be640', 'word_count': 717, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c625ca4-e597-5655-9693-799a8a0be640'}, {'abstract': 'A vaccination drive is being planned for Feb. 25 and health workers are canvassing the neighborhoods where the sewage samples were taken.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/24/health/egypt-polio-virus-is-found-in-cairos-sewers.html', 'snippet': 'A vaccination drive is being planned for Feb. 25 and health workers are canvassing the neighborhoods where the sewage samples were taken.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The polio virus has been found in the sewers of Cairo, and it appears to have come from Pakistan, the World Health Organization said Wednesday. Egypt has not had a case of polio since 2004. A vaccination drive is being planned for Feb. 25, and health workers are canvassing the neighborhoods where the sewage samples were taken, looking for children or adults who may have recently been paralyzed, said Sona Bari, a spokeswoman for the W.H.O. \xa0Pakistan has said it will post teams at its international airports vaccinating all outward-bound passengers under age 5. Last month, at least nine Pakistani volunteers in an internationally supported polio vaccination drive were killed by militants across Pakistan in a campaign of intimidation that has hurt efforts to eradicate the disease there. Pakistan is one of the last three countries, with Afghanistan and Nigeria, with indigenous polio. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt: Polio Virus Is Found in Cairo’s Sewers', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Egypt: Polio Virus Is Found in Cairo’s Sewers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McNeil, Donald G Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poliomyelitis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Health Organization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-24T03:36:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Donald G. McNeil Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Donald', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'McNeil', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb6d9ece-3793-57dc-b14e-999b26ca88ba', 'word_count': 143, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb6d9ece-3793-57dc-b14e-999b26ca88ba'}, {'abstract': 'Justice Minister Néstor Reverol said “the Venezuelan ultraright in complicity with the ultraright outside the country” were behind a plot to kill Vice President Nicolás Maduro.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/24/world/americas/venezuela-officials-say-plot-targeted-vice-president.html', 'snippet': 'Justice Minister Néstor Reverol said “the Venezuelan ultraright in complicity with the ultraright outside the country” were behind a plot to kill Vice President Nicolás Maduro.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Officials said Wednesday that they had uncovered a plot to assassinate the top two government figures who have been running the country during the absence of the cancer-stricken President Hugo Chávez. Justice Minister Néstor Reverol said “the Venezuelan ultraright in complicity with the ultraright outside the country” were behind a plot to kill the two officials, Vice President Nicolás Maduro and the National Assembly president, Diosdado Cabello. Speaking later at a pro-government rally, Mr. Maduro mentioned the plot allegations and promised to use a “hard hand against the right-wing conspiracy.” Mr. Reverol said that security had been increased. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Venezuela: Officials Say Plot Targeted Vice President', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Venezuela: Officials Say Plot Targeted Vice President', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assassinations and Attempted Assassinations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maduro, Nicolas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venezuela', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-24T03:38:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Neuman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Neuman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/81e79326-4079-5c12-8730-a0af00ecf3a3', 'word_count': 98, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81e79326-4079-5c12-8730-a0af00ecf3a3'}, {'abstract': 'The golfer compared his comments over his rising taxes to a poor shot he made during the final round of the 2006 United States Open.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/24