 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Aviation Administration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aviation Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Batteries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lithium (Metal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-24T03:49:12+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/b8873498-1025-54e4-97a4-4d649594b382', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/b8873498-1025-54e4-97a4-4d649594b382'}, {'abstract': 'Employees at the office of two lawyers in Beijing said in telephone interviews that they have been hired to represent Bo Xilai, the former Communist Party chief of Chongqing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/24/world/asia/bo-xilai-former-communist-party-chief-hires-lawyers.html', 'snippet': 'Employees at the office of two lawyers in Beijing said in telephone interviews that they have been hired to represent Bo Xilai, the former Communist Party chief of Chongqing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Employees at the office of two lawyers in Beijing, Li Guifang and Wang Zhaofeng, have said in telephone interviews that the two have been hired to represent Bo Xilai, the former Communist Party chief of Chongqing who was felled by a scandal last year. Mr. Bo’s wife, Gu Kailai, was given a commuted life sentence last summer after she was found guilty of murdering Neil Heywood, a British businessman. The party announced last September that Mr. Bo, whose father was a Communist elder, would be tried on criminal charges including corruption and trying to cover up Mr. Heywood’s murder. Mr. Li and Mr. Wang were unavailable for comment on Tuesday, but their assistants at the law office, Deheng, said Mr. Bo, who has been detained since last spring, and his family had appointed them to represent him. The assistants said they had no information on any date or location for a trial. In early January, an official news media report said Mr. Bo’s case had been handed to “judicial organs,” which ignited speculation that Mr. Bo’s trial might take place soon.\xa0', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China: Former Powerful Official Hires Lawyers', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bo Xilai', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-24T03:51:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5d6ba08-14a1-542c-b74c-15a52ac28ccb', 'word_count': 181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5d6ba08-14a1-542c-b74c-15a52ac28ccb'}, {'abstract': 'Cardinal Glemp helped steer his nation through a historic and relatively peaceful transition from communism to democracy in 1989.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/24/world/europe/cardinal-jozef-glemp-of-poland-is-dead-at-83.html', 'snippet': 'Cardinal Glemp helped steer his nation through a historic and relatively peaceful transition from communism to democracy in 1989.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cardinal Jozef Glemp, the spiritual leader of Poland’s Roman Catholics for 25 years, who helped steer his nation through a historic and r