son) struggles to keep Darryl (Craig Robinson) from moving to Philadelphia, and Jim (John Krasinski) is forced to miss Cece’s first recital. On “1600 Penn,” at 9:30, President Gilchrist (Bill Pullman) uses his position to track down someone of importance to the family, while Emily (Jenna Elfman) is determined to defy protocol when the Austrian chancellor (David St. James) and his wife (Rebecca Wisocky) visit.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Thursday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-24T06:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/e83dc861-44d0-568a-8cf9-0309569cd762', 'word_count': 729, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e83dc861-44d0-568a-8cf9-0309569cd762'}, {'abstract': 'China’s animal lovers are increasingly staging “rescues” of cats and dogs headed for the dinner table. In one rescue, following the crash of a truck in Changsha, over 800 cats were saved but 200 died. according to Chinese media reports.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/24/cat-rescues-in-china-raise-host-of-new-questions/', 'snippet': 'China’s animal lovers are increasingly staging “rescues” of cats and dogs headed for the dinner table. In one rescue, following the crash of a truck in Changsha, over 800 cats were saved but 200 died. according to Chinese media reports.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — The crazy meowing from a truck crashed on a highway outside Changsha, in central China, told rescuers this was n