inst the government, a court filing shows. | Court documents shed new light on what bankers knew at the height of the housing bubble. | Goldman Sachs won a legal fight ove...', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was not just lawmakers and taxpayers who expressed concern when the board of the American International Group met this month to consider joining a lawsuit against the government agencies that rescued the insurer during the financial crisis. The company’s lawyers, too, delivered a stark warning to the board, with one saying the lawsuit had only a 20 percent chance of success, according to a letter filed on Wednesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside A.I.G.’s Decision Not to Sue', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-24T13:22:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5bba96e-1321-53d5-b263-8984bb92a116', 'word_count': 1706, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5bba96e-1321-53d5-b263-8984bb92a116'}, {'abstract': 'As a closely watched trial gets under way, a judge warns lawyers against speaking to the media.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/24/india-rape-trial-starts-with-renewed-ban-on-media-coverage/', 'snippet': 'As a closely watched trial gets under way, a judge warns lawyers against speaking to the media.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The trial of five men accused in the gang rape of a 23-year-old woman in a moving bus in New Delhi is being watched closely as a symbol of India’s commitment to justice for women, but information about the ongoing court proceedings may be scarce.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'India Rape Trial Starts With Renewed Ban on Media Coverage', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'India: Rape Suspects’ Trial Begins', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Juvenile Delinquency', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Delhi (India)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-24T13:27:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Niharika Mandhana and Heather Timmons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Niharika', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mandhana', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Heather', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Timmons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/995b7ea7-9f04-557e-8623-253c010e5b5c', 'word_count': 731, 'uri': 'nyt://article/995b7ea7-9f04-557e-8623-253c010e5b5c'}, {'abstract': 'Also, Apple disappoints and some longtime employees are laid off at Rolling Stone.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/24/the-breakfast-meeting-assange-assails-propaganda-film-and-netflix-surges/', 'snippet': 'Also, Apple disappoints and some longtime employees are laid off at Rolling Stone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Netflix surprised Wall Street with a fourth-quarter profit of $8 million and a customer base of more than 27 million American households, causing one analyst to say the company has “risen from the ashes” of its disastrous 2011. Shares jumped 30 percent in after-hours trading. Apple reported a profit of $13.1 billion and a 28 percent increase in the sale of iPhones but that still wasn’t enough for investors, who pounded the stock down 11 percent in after-hours trading.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: Assange Assails ‘Propaganda’ Film, and Netflix Surges', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reality Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assange, Julian P', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Condon, Bill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Netflix Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rolling Stone', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wenner Media', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WikiLeaks', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-24T13:29:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editors', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editors'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/835ed0de-a679-50c7-92b4-c12d430c96cf', 'word_count': 298, 'uri': 'nyt://article/835ed0de-a679-50c7-92b4-c12d430c96cf'}, {'abstract': 'Metropolitan Diary: During a cab ride, a driver and a passenger bond over the Concert for Bangladesh.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/24/a-memorable-concert/', 'snippet': 'Metropolitan Diary: During a cab ride, a driver and a passenger bond over 