t speech that set the tone for the sixth Jaipur Literature Festival, which opened Thursday to the sounds of chanting Buddhist monks, beating drums called nagadas and India’s national anthem.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Octogenarian Opens Jaipur Lit Fest With Rousing Speech', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hanif, Mohammed', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kapoor, Anish', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jaipur (India)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Bengal (India)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-24T15:21:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pamposh Raina', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pamposh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Raina', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2329f4c6-0187-5d66-a969-858792430a3b', 'word_count': 335, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2329f4c6-0187-5d66-a969-858792430a3b'}, {'abstract': 'Senator John Kerry returns to the Senate Foreign Relations Committee to answer questions at his confirmation hearing as secretary of state.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/24/live-video-kerrys-confirmation-hearing/', 'snippet': 'Senator John Kerry returns to the Senate Foreign Relations Committee to answer questions at his confirmation hearing as secretary of state.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Senator John Kerry, a Democrat from Massachusetts, returns Thursday morning to the Senate Foreign Relations Committee, of which he was once the chairman, to answer questions at his confirmation hearing as secretary of state.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video of Kerry’s Confirmation Hearing', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kerry, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate Committee on Foreign Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-24T15:22:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/450b4c90-a1bf-5534-bbf8-8225b350d5c2', 'word_count': 188, 'uri': 'nyt://article/450b4c90-a1bf-5534-bbf8-8225b350d5c2'}, {'abstract': 'Doctors appeal to the authorities to lower the speed limit in the region and cut back on industrial activity.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/24/on-our-radar-salt-lake-smog/', 'snippet': 'Doctors appeal to the authorities to lower the speed limit in the region and cut back on industrial activity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Environmental Protection Agency has singled out the Salt Lake region as having the nation’s worst air for much of January, when an icy fog smothers valleys and traps soot for days or weeks at a time. The air is so tainted that more than 100 Utah doctors are pressing the authorities to lower highway speed limits, curb industrial activity and make mass transit free for the rest of the winter. [Associated Press]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Our Radar: Salt Lake Smog', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-24T15:24:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f282c16c-7edd-5b76-8516-234738c61843', 'word_count': 240, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f282c16c-7edd-5b76-8516-234738c61843'}, {'abstract': 'Did the Venezuelan government really just censor the broadcast of the country’s Constitution — which was drafted by Chávez supporters, with his wholehearted support?', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/24/when-the-venezuelan-government-bans-broadcasts-of-its-own-constitution/', 'snippet': 'Did the Venezuelan government really just censor the broadcast of the country’s Constitution — which was drafted by Chávez supporters, with his wholehearted support?', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s been two weeks now since Venezuela’s telecom regulator served a cease-and-desist order on Venezuela’s last free-to-air opposition broadcaster, Globovision. Some recent content, the station was told, broke the law by “inciting hate, panic or disturbing public order.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Chávez Constitutional', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Censorship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of the Press', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chavez, Hugo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venezuela', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-24T15:26:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Francisco Toro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Francisco', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Toro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/27ae79fc-e4e5-51cf-9fbe-578f60dd7c7b', 'word_count': 327, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27ae79fc-e4e5-51cf-9fbe-578f60dd7c7b'}, {'abstract': 'The Jaipur Literature Festival focuses on Buddhism this year.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/24/dalai-lama-stresses-science-and-secularism-in-jaipur/', 'snippet': 'The Jaipur Literature Festival focuses on Buddhism this year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As an eager audience settled into their seats on a chilly Thursday morning, the first day of the Jaipur Literature Festival, six monks from the Drepung Loseling monastery, clad in orange robes, sat on the stage with their legs crossed and hands pressed together as in prayer. A calm settled over the audience as the monks’ deep, throaty chants echoed across the front lawns.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dalai Lama Stresses Science and Secularism in Jaipur', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buddhism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dalai Lama', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jaipur (India)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tibet', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-24T15:27:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neha Thirani Bagri', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neha', 'middlename': 'Thirani', 'lastname': 'Bagri', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/794ec82e-d5e7-57c1-9dd7-5bc05182fa12', 'word_count': 627, 'uri': 'nyt://article/794ec82e-d5e7-57c1-9dd7-5bc05182fa12'}, {'abstract': 'Being a submissive or dutiful patient doesn’t always pay off. Who exactly was I being good for? Sometimes it’s good to be bad.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/24/living-with-cancer-the-good-patient-syndrome/', 'snippet': 'Being a submissive or dutiful patient doesn’t always pay off. Who exactly was I being good for? Sometimes it’s good to be bad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I remember when being good seemed strategic. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/24/health/24well_gubar/24well_gubar-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 415, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/24/health/24well_gubar/24well_gubar-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 415}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/24/health/24well_gubar/24well_gubar-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 708, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/24/health/24well_gubar/24well_gubar-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1417, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/24/health/24well_gubar/24well_gubar-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/24/health/24well_gubar/24well_gubar-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, '