ations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Netherlands', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-24T15:38:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Cowell and Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7fd7efcc-98d3-5a5a-ac0c-292a86ac89fd', 'word_count': 892, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7fd7efcc-98d3-5a5a-ac0c-292a86ac89fd'}, {'abstract': 'Duke loses. Azarenka’s timeout is criticized. And the N.C.A.A. finds itself in fiasco territory.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/25/sports/surprises-slip-ups-and-questionable-strategy-leading-off.html', 'snippet': 'Duke loses. Azarenka’s timeout is criticized. And the N.C.A.A. finds itself in fiasco territory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you like your college sports served with a side of chaos, this is a great day for you. Because not only did we have a nutty night of college basketball upsets, with No. 1 Duke being shellacked by Miami and Butler falling victim to a buzzer-beater by LaSalle, the N.C.A.A. was trying (and failing) to make sense of the utter fiasco it had made out of its investigation of Miami. This was not, mind you, a terribly complicated investigation, as these things go, with the booster Nevin Shapiro spilling the beans from a prison cell about the thousands of impermissible benefits he provided Miami players.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/25/sports/ncaafootball/25leadingpic/