4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shapiro, Nevin', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sharapova, Maria', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Li Na', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stephens, Sloane', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "Te'o, Manti", 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Azarenka, Victoria', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Australian Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-24T15:38:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/949bea79-dac7-5155-96bd-6c2f885fbcfc', 'word_count': 565, 'uri': 'nyt://article/949bea79-dac7-5155-96bd-6c2f885fbcfc'}, {'abstract': 'San Francisco’s wealthy neighbor to the north, Marin boasts oyster bars, a famous farmers’ market, cultural spots and a bounty of optical treats.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/27/travel/36-hours-in-marin-county-calif.html', 'snippet': 'San Francisco’s wealthy neighbor to the north, Marin boasts oyster bars, a famous farmers’ market, cultural spots and a bounty of optical treats.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Crossing the Golden Gate Bridge from San Francisco, you arrive in Marin even before landing on solid ground. The county line hangs above the water’s edge, which is fitting, since the county itself feels suspended — ethereal, privileged, a place apart from the rest of the Bay Area. Fearing the perils of suburban sprawl, Marin invested early and often in conservation. Outside of a handful of small cities (San Rafael and Novato the largest among them), Marin is a surprisingly rural landscape of cattle ranches, rolling hills, redwood groves, houseboat communities and roadhouses. Among the wealthiest counties in the country, Marin’s affluence is apparent in towns like Mill Valley. But Marin, one of the state’s smallest counties, also has small towns, like Bolinas and Fairfax, that retain an endearing Northern California eccentricity.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/travel/27HOURS_SPAN-sf/27HOURS_SPAN-sf-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 490, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/27/travel/27HOURS_SPAN-sf/27HOURS_SPAN-sf-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 490}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/travel/27HOURS_SPAN-sf/27HOURS_SPAN-sf-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 837, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/travel/27HOURS_SPAN-sf/27HOURS_SPAN-sf-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1674, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/travel/27HOURS_SPAN-sf/27HOURS_SPAN-sf-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/27/travel/27HOURS_SPAN-sf/27HOURS_SPAN-sf-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'im