e': None, 'lastname': 'Piola', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/75d6698d-aca1-578e-86bc-86f02da73ded', 'word_count': 36, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75d6698d-aca1-578e-86bc-86f02da73ded'}, {'abstract': 'I worried about health care and women’s rights, but I also worried about having to move away from D.C.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/24/the-personal-side-of-a-presidential-election/', 'snippet': 'I worried about health care and women’s rights, but I also worried about having to move away from D.C.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It wasn’t my choice to move to D.C. When people ask (as they always do), “What brought you here?” my response is the same. I shake my head, roll my eyes, and say, “my husband’s job.” If Tim is standing next to me, I’ll point at him, or pat his back and smile, to remind him how lucky he is that I followed him here. The message I’m trying to get across is clear: if it weren’t for my husband, I’d leave in a heartbeat.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Personal Side of a Presidential Election', 'kicker': 'Townies', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sleep', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-24T17:20:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Close', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Close', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8605acc1-4f0a-5289-a798-ed7be441490c', 'word_count': 916, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8605acc1-4f0a-5289-a798-ed7be441490c'}, {'abstract': 'Doctors on average spend more than four years of their careers embroiled in lawsuits, and certain specialists, like neurosurgeons, average well over 10 years, according to a new report.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/24/the-drawn-out-process-of-the-medical-lawsuit/', 'snippet': 'Doctors on average spend more than four years of their careers embroiled in lawsuits, and certain specialists, like neurosurgeons, average well over 10 years, according to a new report.', 'lead_paragraph': 'She was one of the most highly sought radiologists in her hospital, a doctor with the uncanny ability to divine the source of maladies from the shadows of black and white X-ray films. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/24/health/24chen/24chen-articleLarge.jpeg', 'height': 378, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/24/health/24chen/24chen-articleLarge.jpeg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 378}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/24/health/24chen/24chen-jumbo.jpeg', 'height': 646, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/24/health/24chen/24chen-superJumbo.jpeg', 'height': 1292, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/24/health/24chen/24chen-thumbStandard.jpeg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/24/health/24chen/24chen-thumbStandard.jpeg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/24/health/24chen/24chen-thumbLarge.jpeg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Drawn Out Process of the Medical Lawsuit', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Cost of Malpractice Claims', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Malpractice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-24T17:23:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pauline W. Chen, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pauline', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d24f5e73-1b7c-5724-9473-ef32d2c97551', 'word_count': 731, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d24f5e73-1b7c-5724-9473-ef32d2c97551'}, {'abstract': 'The creative forces behind the stage version of “Once” are reimagining “The Glass Menagerie” for a run at the American Repertory Theater.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/27/theater/reviving-the-glass-menagerie.html', 'snippet': 'The creative forces behind the stage version of “Once” are reimagining “The Glass Menagerie” for a run at the American Repertory Theater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAMBRIDGE, MASS. — Last June, two weeks after winning Tony Awards for their hit Broadway musical, “Once,” the director John Tiffany and the set designer Bob Crowley boarded a train in New York with only a few hours to accomplish a