b6a7-56be-9bd0-fbe82800b64e'}, {'abstract': 'Some theater companies performing Off Broadway are using disabled actors, sometimes deliberately making a point of their disabilities.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/24/theater-talkback-defying-expectations-off-broadway/', 'snippet': 'Some theater companies performing Off Broadway are using disabled actors, sometimes deliberately making a point of their disabilities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Theatergoers generally expect actors to abide by certain longstanding conventions, and if actors fail to oblige, it usually isn’t intentional. We assume, for starters, that people portraying other people are going to speak so we don’t have to strain to understand them. Emotions, even mixed emotions, should be rendered with comparable accessibility and with a flow that passes for a smoother, larger version of the real thing.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Theater Talkback: Defying Expectations Off Broadway', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Defying Expectations Off Broadway', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Inflatable Frankenstein (Play)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blindness', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coil Festival', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deafness', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disabilities', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Under the Radar Festival', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crouch, Tim', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Satter, Tina', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Half Straddle', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nalagaat', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Public Theater', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Radiohole', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-24T17:37:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93586dab-2a1d-5624-80e9-2746a41c50be', 'word_count': 1266, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93586dab-2a1d-5624-80e9-2746a41c50be'}, {'abstract': 'The American statesman made clear that while Davos Man and Woman are concerned about global economic gyrations, political problems most threaten the world.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/24/kissinger-political-threats-to-global-economy-abound/', 'snippet': 'The American statesman made clear that while Davos Man and Woman are concerned about global economic gyrations, political problems most threaten the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DAVOS, Switzerland — Henry A. Kissinger has never shied from unvarnished political assessments and during an hour-long address to the World Economic Forum on Thursday, the former American secretary of state delivered a list of sober warnings about rising threats on the world stage.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/24/blogs/24rdv-kissinger-davos/24rdv-kissinger-davos-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/24/blogs/24rdv-kissinger-davos/24rdv-kissinger-davos-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 