yn Bigelow says, in response to critics,that it’s “a movie, not a documentary.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kathryn Bigelow continues her “Zero Dark Thirty” tour of duty, defending and explicating the film, which is now No. 2 at the box office. On “CBS This Morning,” she told Charlie Rose that it’s “a movie, not a documentary.” John Miller, a senior CBS correspondent and former F.B.I. intelligence official, sitting with her, added that he found it to be accurate in representing the search for Osama bin Laden. “The part of the story I thought it really captured was this incredible effort,” he said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bigelow on the Offensive', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bigelow, Kathryn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-24T18:02:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc0d2d2b-3dd9-51d8-b3e8-ed8102c9d00a', 'word_count': 198, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc0d2d2b-3dd9-51d8-b3e8-ed8102c9d00a'}, {'abstract': 'A retrospective at the International Center of Photography on the photojournalist Chim shows his eye lingering on children caught in grown-up battles.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/27/arts/design/a-retrospective-on-the-war-photographer-chim.html', 'snippet': 'A retrospective at the International Center of Photography on the photojournalist Chim shows his eye lingering on children caught in grown-up battles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chim, a k a David Seymour, was one of the stars of the heroic mid-20th-century golden age of photojournalism, the time before television, when the news of the day was conveyed with unprecedented immediacy in black-and-white images in the pages of Life and other magazines. He covered the hot spots of Europe and the Middle East from the Spanish Civil War in the 1930s to the Suez crisis, in which he was killed by gunfire in 1956. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/arts/27CHIM1_SPAN/27CHIM1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/27/arts/27CHIM1_SPAN/27CHIM1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/arts/27CHIM1_SPAN/27CHIM1_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/arts/27CHIM1_SPAN/27CHIM1_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/arts/27CHIM1_SPAN/27CHIM1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/27/arts/27CHIM1_SPAN/27CHIM1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/arts/27CHIM1_SPAN/27CHIM1_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thum