e having an identity crisis. On the one hand, the Grizzlies are one of the best teams in the league, with the fifth highest schedule-adjusted margin of victory. On the other hand, Memphis traded two key reserves on Tuesday to the Cleveland Cavaliers to get below the luxury tax threshold. (Although that trade was said to allow them to keep Rudy Gay — the team’s leading scorer — for the remainder of the season.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Keeping Score: Tough Conference May Keep Grizzlies Down', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gay, Rudy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Memphis Grizzlies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-24T19:41:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Justin Kubatko', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kubatko', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ded98b95-6695-5e42-b110-6961d8559b72', 'word_count': 477, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ded98b95-6695-5e42-b110-6961d8559b72'}, {'abstract': 'When day care is consistently good, and consistently used, any negative effect on children’s behavior disappears.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/24/day-care-and-behavior-problems-unlinked/', 'snippet': 'When day care is consistently good, and consistently used, any negative effect on children’s behavior disappears.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Time spent in day care doesn’t link to problems for older children — at least, not when that day-care time is separated from the socio-political context in which the care is provided. A team of researchers from Norway, Harvard and Boston College, examining the varied research that sporadically associates an increase in hours in day care with increased behavior problems, noted that the work was all based on child-care studies done in the United States. And the United States, they argue, is a lousy place to study the impact of early child care on children.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Day Care and Behavior Problems, Unlinked', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Day Care Centers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Work-Life Balance', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bazelon, Emily', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-24T19:42:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d624f80b-c964-5c88-ad11-89037fda277c', 'word_count': 853, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d624f80b-c964-5c88-ad11-89037fda277c'}, {'abstract': 'Out front is ASAP Rocky, the Harlem hip-hop star. Behind the scenes is ASAP Yams, his longtime friend and collaborator, who serves as something of a spirit guide, helping to shape Rocky’s sonic style.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/multimed