 wrong on the politics.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/24/tim-geithner-is-wrong-2/', 'snippet': 'Right on the debt, wrong on the politics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'But he’s right, too.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tim Geithner Is Wrong', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-24T19:46:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4af8ad1-3f0d-56c9-827a-fb3866ff8ddc', 'word_count': 402, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4af8ad1-3f0d-56c9-827a-fb3866ff8ddc'}, {'abstract': 'When Brigitte Lefèvre retires in 2014, tradition will be in the hands of Mr. Millepied, the 35-year old choreographer and former New York City Ballet principal dancer.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/24/at-press-conference-benjamin-millepied-responds-to-questions-about-new-paris-opera-ballet-post/', 'snippet': 'When Brigitte Lefèvre retires in 2014, tradition will be in the hands of Mr. Millepied, the 35-year old choreographer and former New York City Ballet principal dancer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — The journalists who arrived this morning at the Palais Garnier for the news conference introducing Benjamin Millepied as the new director of dance at the Paris Opera were ushered into the grandly proportioned office of its general director, Nicolas Joel. “I am sure that Serge Lifar came in frequently through this door to demand more for his ballet company,” he said. Then he looked at Brigitte Lefèvre, who has directed the Paris Opera Ballet since 1995. “It’s a tradition that has continued.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Benjamin Millepied Answers Questions About His New Post With Paris Opera Ballet', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-24T19:49:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roslyn Suclas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roslyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Suclas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34664dab-8e48-571f-a85f-0b14861b7dd6', 'word_count': 582, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34664dab-8e48-571f-a85f-0b14861b7dd6'}, {'abstract': 'With few outside pressures, an older couple has nothing to do but love each other, be happy and go running.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/27/style/modern-love-the-race-grows-sweeter-near-its-final-lap.html', 'snippet': 'With few outside pressures, an older couple has nothing to do but love each other, be happy and go running.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sam and I dated for two years. Then, when I turned 70 and he 80, we had a joint 150th birthday party and announced our engagement. We married a year later.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/29/fashion/27MODERNLOVE/27MODERNLOVE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 725, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/29/fashion/27MODERNLOVE/27MODERNLOVE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 725}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/29/fashion/27MODERNLOVE/27MODERNLOVE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 848, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/29/fashion/27MODERNLOVE/27MODERNLOVE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1696, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/29/fashion/27MODERNLOVE/27MODERNLOVE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/29/fashion/27MODERNLOVE/27MODERNLOVE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/29/fashion/27MODERNLOVE/27MODERNLOVE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Race Grows Sweeter Near Its Final Lap', 'kicker': 'Modern Love', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Race Grows Sweeter Near Its Final Lap', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Love (Emotion)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dating and Courtship', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Modern Love (Times Column)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-24T19:53:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eve Pell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/02fa464e-78ec-5d61-9399-513b4c586364', 'word_count': 1506, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02fa464e-78ec-5d61-9399-513b4c586364'}, {'abstract': 'The Lede is watching Katie Couric’s interview Thursday with Manti Te’o, the Notre Dame football star who said he was tricked into believing first that he had a girlfriend and then that the girlfriend died of leukemia.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/24/updates-on-the-katie-couric-interview-with-manti-teo/', 'snippet': 'The Lede is watching Katie Couric’s interview Thursday with Manti Te’o, the Notre Dame football star who said he was tricked into believing first that he had a girlfriend and then that the girlfriend died of leukemia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Lede watched Katie Couric’s interview Thursday with Manti Te’o, the Notre Dame football star who said he was tricked into believing first that he had a girlfriend and then that the girlfriend died of leukemia. Excerpts from the interview have been published on the “Katie” show’s Web site.  ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Updates on the Katie Couric Interview With Manti Te’o', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Te’o Messages Played', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Couric, Katie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "Te'o, Manti", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deadspin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Notre Dame', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-24T19:53:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/be69fa2b-ad8f-510c-b0b5-27190160dd59', 'word_count': 2083, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be69fa2b-ad8f-510c-b0b5-27190160dd59'}, {'abstract': 'Frequent urination for people as they get older may be attributed to a number of reasons including normal changes in the body.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/24/booming/why-am-i-making-so-many-pit-stops.html', 'snippet': 'Frequent urination for people as they get older may be attributed to a number of reasons including normal changes in the body.', 'lead_paragraph': "There are those who have suggested that this feature appears to take an unseemly delight in the decline of the human body: ears that don't hear as well, spines that compress and curve, nose sensors that fade. And did we mention those hairs that start growing out of places other than the head? So we are happy to report on one thing baby boomers may find they do as well as well as ever: urinating. In fact, not only are they still doing it, they may well be doing it more often than ever. A lot more often.", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/24/booming/24question-booming-relieve/24question-booming-relieve-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 869, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/24/booming/24question-booming-relieve/24question-booming-relieve-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 869}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/24/booming/24question-booming-relieve/24question-booming-relieve-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 708, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/24/booming/24question-booming-relieve/24question-booming-relieve-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1415, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/