332914611d'}, {'abstract': 'The governor wants New Yorkers to sell their waterfront homes to the state.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/24/cuomo-bows-to-mother-nature/', 'snippet': 'The governor wants New Yorkers to sell their waterfront homes to the state.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York has yet to receive an estimated $30 billion from Washington for Hurricane Sandy relief, but Governor Andrew Cuomo already knows one way he plans to spend it.\xa0 He said in a meeting with The Times editorial board on Wednesday that he wants the state to discourage the building and rebuilding, and then rebuilding, of unsafe houses on New York’s vast and vulnerable shoreline.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cuomo Bows to Mother Nature', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-24T20:32:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eleanor Randolph', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eleanor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Randolph', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/984b6247-b0b2-549c-ae30-8cde4a4de9c1', 'word_count': 306, 'uri': 'nyt://article/984b6247-b0b2-549c-ae30-8cde4a4de9c1'}, {'abstract': '“Working on a Special Day,” about the friendship between a homemaker and her neighbor in 1938 Rome, is a stage adaptation of a 1977 film.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/25/theater/reviews/working-on-a-special-day-at-59e59-theaters.html', 'snippet': '“Working on a Special Day,” about the friendship between a homemaker and her neighbor in 1938 Rome, is a stage adaptation of a 1977 film.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The house lights still on, a man and a woman begin to undress on a black-walled stage. Carefully, modestly, they trade their street clothes for costumes: a dingy housedress and stockings for her, natty slacks and a crisp white shirt for him. Transformed, they go about creating a world for themselves. They pull props from a shopping cart and start to draw on the walls with chalk — windows appear, a hanging lamp, a portrait. Voilà: a Roman apartment in 1938. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/25/arts/25WORKING/0125WORKING-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/25/arts/25WORKING/0125WORKING-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/25/arts/25WORKING/0125WORKING-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/25/arts/25WORKING/0125WORKING-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/25/arts/25WORKING/25WORKING-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/25/arts/25WORKING/25WORKING-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/25/arts/25WORKING/25WORKING-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 15