'abstract': 'A look back at TimesOpen 2012: some changes we made in our approach, some risks we took, and how they worked out.', 'web_url': 'https://open.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/24/timesopen-2012-behind-the-music/', 'snippet': 'A look back at TimesOpen 2012: some changes we made in our approach, some risks we took, and how they worked out.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We’re now far enough into 2013 that I’ve stopped mistakenly typing “2012.” That means the TimesOpen team is busy working on this year’s slate of events, plus some other plots and schemes you’ll be hearing about in due course. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'TimesOpen 2012: Behind the Music', 'kicker': 'Open', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-24T21:03:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andre Behrens', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andre', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Behrens', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5190a1e0-4757-5653-a708-9e05622e6662', 'word_count': 1010, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5190a1e0-4757-5653-a708-9e05622e6662'}, {'abstract': 'Toyota and BMW announced on Thursday that they have reached a deal for joint research on a lithium-air battery and a fuel-cell vehicle system.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/24/wheelies-the-global-collaboration-edition/', 'snippet': 'Toyota and BMW announced on Thursday that they have reached a deal for joint research on a lithium-air battery and a fuel-cell vehicle system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In which we bring you motoring news from around the Web:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wheelies: The Global Collaboration Edition', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric and Hybrid Vehicles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bayerische Motorenwerke AG', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toyota Motor Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-24T21:04:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/85395045-6d59-5427-a2ac-5731fc411aac', 'word_count': 324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85395045-6d59-5427-a2ac-5731fc411aac'}, {'abstract': 'Thomas Schütte’s “United Enemies” is coming to Central Park; Alexandre Arrechea’s “No Limit” architectural sculpture will line Park Avenue; and Gagosian Gallery is taking Jeff Koons’s “Metallic Venus” to the European Fine Art Fair.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/25/arts/design/schutte-in-central-park-arrechea-on-park-avenue.html', 'snippet': 'Thomas Schütte’s “United Enemies” is coming to Central Park; Alexandre Arrechea’s “No Limit” architectural sculpture will line Park Avenue; and Gagosian Gallery is taking Jeff Koons’s “Metallic Venus” to the European Fine Art Fair.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two pairs of cast bronze male figures, bound together with rope and balancing on a tripod of sticks, were a bizarre sight on the grounds of Kensington Gardens in London last fall. Their faces were gnarled and grimacing, their heads facing different directions, as if they were fighting to break free from each other. The sculptures are from the “United Enemies” series by the German artist Thomas Schütte. He started the series in the early 1990s, and this installation was part of a larger exhibition at the Serpentine Gallery.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 