://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/24/anita-hill-sundance-star/', 'snippet': 'Though film-industry celebrities are plentiful at Sundance, it has been Anita Hill drawing the attention of festival-goers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARK CITY, Utah – Celebrity-spotting is a parlor game here at the Sundance Film Festival, with sightings up and down Main Street of everyone from Paris Hilton and James Franco to Anita Hill. Yes, that Anita Hill: the lawyer and academic whose testimony at the 1991 confirmation hearings of the Supreme Court nominee Clarence Thomas became a flashpoint in political and gender history. She is the subject of the documentary “Anita,” from the Oscar-winning filmmaker Freida Mock (“Maya Lin: A Strong Vision”), and Ms. Hill’s presence around town has caused a stir.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Anita Hill, Sundance Star', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sundance Film Festival (Park City, Utah)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hill, Anita', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-24T21:27:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9ba5e3b-7468-5d42-ae0e-db0cf198b872', 'word_count': 332, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9ba5e3b-7468-5d42-ae0e-db0cf198b872'}, {'abstract': 'On Thursday, Twitter introduced Vine, a new video sharing service for the iPhone and iPod touch, but it came with a few privacy snags. Vine lets users create and share bite-size, looping video clips that are six seconds long or shorter.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/24/twitter-introduces-vine-a-new-video-feature-but-with-privacy-snags/', 'snippet': 'On Thursday, Twitter introduced Vine, a new video sharing service for the iPhone and iPod touch, but it came with a few privacy snags. Vine lets users create and share bite-size, looping video clips that are six seconds long or shorter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Thursday, Twitter introduced Vine, a new video sharing service, albeit with a few serious privacy hiccups.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Twitter Introduces Vine, a New Video Feature, but With Privacy Snags', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Privacy Snags\r\nImpair Twitter’s\r\nNew Video Feature', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-24T21:28:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicole Perlroth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicole', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perlroth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d06c0e75-36f2-5c06-bfe1-43a1489acf3f', 'word_count': 543, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d06c0e75-36f2-5c06-bfe1-43a1489acf3f'}, {'abstract': 'Who knew a how-to book by an unknown writer from 1938 would be such a powerful read?', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/24/how-to-read-like-a-blog-boss/', 'snippet': 'Who knew a how-to book by an unknown writer from 1938 would be such a powerful read?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Edith Zimmerman\xa0is the founder and editor of the Web site\xa0The Hairpin. Her most recent articles for the magazine were about\xa0Candace Bushnell and Joseph P. Kennedy III.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/24/magazine/24-if-you-want-to-write-book/24-if-you-want-to-write-book-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 475, 'width': 306, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/24/magazine/24-if-you-want-to-write-book/24-if-you-want-to-write-book-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 475, 'width': 306, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/24/magazine/24-if-you-want-to-write-book/24-if-you-want-to-write-book-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/24/magazine/24-if-you-want-to-write-book/24-if-you-want-to-write-book-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/24/magazine/24-if-you-want-to-write-book/24-if-you-want-to-write-book-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Read Like a Blog Boss', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-24T21:32:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edith Zimmerman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zimmerman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c06d63b8-2187-5b6b-b8a7-546a7d47f16d', 'word_count': 318, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c06d63b8-2187-5b6b-b8a7-546a7d47f16d'}, {'abstract': 'Defense Secretary Leon E. Panetta and Gen. Martin E. Dempsey said that not every woman would become a combat soldier but that every woman deserved the chance to try.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/25/us/politics/formally-lifting-a-combat-ban-military-chiefs-stress-equal-opportunity.html', 'snippet': 'Defense Secretary Leon E. Panetta and Gen. Martin E. Dempsey said that not every woman would become a combat soldier but that every woman deserved the chance to try.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The historic decision to lift the military’s ban on women in combat had its roots in the personal experiences in war zones of Defense Secretary Leon E. Panetta and Gen. Martin E. Dempsey, the chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff, both men said on Thursday. For General Dempsey, it all began in Baghdad.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/25/us/SUB-MILITARY/SUB-MILITARY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 389, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/25/us/SUB-MILITARY/SUB-MILITARY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 389}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/25/us/SUB-MILITARY/SUB-MILITARY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 664, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/25/us/SUB-MILITARY/SUB-MILITARY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1328, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJum