tics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6605a72-f17f-5abe-9ced-6575a0a25f72', 'word_count': 620, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6605a72-f17f-5abe-9ced-6575a0a25f72'}, {'abstract': 'New Senate filibuster rules don’t do away with many of the old roadblocks that had ground the Senate almost to a halt, but they will make for easier clearance.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/24/new-senate-rules-designed-to-speed-things-up/', 'snippet': 'New Senate filibuster rules don’t do away with many of the old roadblocks that had ground the Senate almost to a halt, but they will make for easier clearance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New Senate rules on the filibuster, adopted Thursday after weeks of negotiations and the threat of a crisis in Congress’s upper chamber, don’t do away with many of the old roadblocks that had ground the Senate almost to a halt, but they will drastically shorten the distance between the hurdles and lower their height for easier clearance.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Senate Rules Designed to Speed Things Up', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Filibusters and Debate Curbs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McConnell, Mitch', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reid, Harry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-24T21:59:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politic