table, with a large tube coming out of his mouth. The caption identified him as Hugo Chávez, the cancer-stricken president of Venezuela, and said he was undergoing medical treatment in Cuba.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/25/world/25spain_image/25spain_image-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/25/world/25spain_image/25spain_image-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/25/world/25spain_image/25spain_image-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/25/world/25spain_image/25spain_image-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/25/world/25spain_image/25spain_image-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/25/world/25spain_image/25spain_image-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/25/world/25spain_image/25spain_image-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Spanish Newspaper Apologizes for Printing Fake Photo of Chávez', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spanish Newspaper Apologizes for Printing Fake Photo of Chávez', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chavez, Hugo', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'El Pais', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-24T22:16:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Neuman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Neuman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/253d3ef3-8861-5132-a948-9a2af3c3b663', 'word_count': 649, 'uri': 'nyt://article/253d3ef3-8861-5132-a948-9a2af3c3b663'}, {'abstract': 'As more financiers jump to the technology sector, some find that big investors are skeptical that they have what it takes to nurture a young company.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/01/24/moving-from-wall-street-to-the-tech-sector-proves-tricky/', 'snippet': 'As more financiers jump to the technology sector, some find that big investors are skeptical that they have what it takes to nurture a young company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Vinicius Vacanti set out to make a pitch for a local deals start-up to investors, he figured he understood the process given his four years on Wall Street.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Moving From Wall Street to the Tech Sector Proves Tricky', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Moving From Wall Street to the Tech Sector Proves Tricky', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Careers and Professions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venture Capital', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-24T22:18:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c9d4182-736d-5675-bfec-e1039f5a4909', 'word_count': 1056, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c9d4182-736d-5675-bfec-e1039f5a4909'}, {'abstract': 'Perhaps none of the former Communist countries have come quite so far as Slovenia in redeveloping a vibrant wine culture.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/30/dining/reviews/slovenias-vineyards-and-a-vibrant-wine-culture-rebound.html', 'snippet': 'Perhaps none of the former Communist countries have come quite so far as Slovenia in redeveloping a vibrant wine culture.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EASTERN EUROPE IS HOME to an ancient wine culture, though it’s not always obvious from the wines today. Just as Prohibition largely severed the modern American industry from its nascent origins, Communism separated countries from centuries of winemaking traditions. The post-Communist rejuvenation of these traditions, and their adaptation to the modern world, are among the most exciting stories in wine today.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/30/dining/30WINE_SPAN/30WINE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 420, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/30/dining/30WINE_SPAN/30WINE_SP