be making it harder to put them in new homes, officials say.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/25/world/us-adoptions-from-abroad-decline-sharply.html', 'snippet': 'Moves to limit adoptions by some countries and tougher standards intended to protect children may be making it harder to put them in new homes, officials say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The number of foreign children adopted by Americans has plunged to its lowest level in more than a decade as some countries have cut back on adoptions to the United States and others have struggled to meet stricter standards intended to combat corruption and child trafficking, government officials said Thursday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'American Adoptions From Abroad at Their Lowest Level in Years', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'American Adoptions From Abroad at Their Lowest Level in Years', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADOPTIONS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Swarns, Rachel L', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-25T02:31:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel L. Swarns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Swarns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d2ab50e-1f5d-5bd4-8665-620da857dfd1', 'word_count': 753, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d2ab50e-1f5d-5bd4-8665-620da857dfd1'}, {'abstract': 'After an easy 51-to-19 vote by representatives, the