jor': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-25T04:05:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Zeleny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zeleny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e26e988f-4777-591f-9b9a-4995225e0123', 'word_count': 878, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e26e988f-4777-591f-9b9a-4995225e0123'}, {'abstract': 'The vote was intended by King Abdullah II to quell the discontent that has posed a challenge to his rule, but the results make it unlikely that the protest movement will be appeased.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/25/world/middleeast/jordan-elections-favor-government-loyalists.html', 'snippet': 'The vote was intended by King Abdullah II to quell the discontent that has posed a challenge to his rule, but the results make it unlikely that the protest movement will be appeased.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AMMAN, Jordan — The new 150-seat Parliament here will include members arrested just days before the elections on charges of vote-buying, and a cast of government loyalists will dominate a body long seen by Jordanians as being as corrupt as it is inept. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Loyalists to Dominate Jordan’s New Parliament', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Loyalists to Dominate Jordan’s New Parliament', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fahim, Kareem', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABDULLAH II, KING OF JORDAN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jordan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-25T04:09:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kareem Fahim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kareem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fahim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/afbf2453-1723-52e7-8177-27b11fcae27a', 'word_count': 414, 'uri': 'nyt://article/afbf2453-1723-52e7-8177-27b11fcae27a'}, {'abstract': 'Said Ali al-Shihri died recently from wounds he received during a “counterterrorism operation” late last year, Yemen’s government announced Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/25/world/middleeast/said-ali-al-shihri-qaeda-leader-in-yemen-is-dead.html', 'snippet': 'Said Ali al-Shihri died recently from wounds he received during a “counterterrorism operation” late last year, Yemen’s government announced Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Said Ali al-Shihri, the second-ranking operative in Al Qaeda’s branch in Yemen, died recently from wounds he received during a “counterterrorism operation” late last year, Yemen’s government announced Thursday. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No. 2 Leader of Al Qaeda in Yemen Is Killed', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No. 2 Leader Of Al Qaeda In Yemen Is Killed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mazzetti, Mark', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shihri, Said Ali al-', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Al Qaeda in the Arabian Peninsula', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-25T04:10:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Mazzetti', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mazzetti', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6195970d-c33c-5e3a-be95-eeb4b099a4db', 'word_count': 342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6195970d-c33c-5e3a-be95-eeb4b099a4db'}, {'abstract': 'Dulce Vida Cafe, whose menu is filled with recipes from the owner’s mother, attracts expatriates from across the city.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/27/nyregion/dulce-vida-cafe-offers-colombian-expatriates-the-comforts-of-home.html', 'snippet': 'Dulce Vida Cafe, whose menu is filled with recipes from the owner’s mother, attracts expatriates from across the city.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Adiós, Queens!” said the squat, burly man to Maria Marquez-Hass, the owner of Dulce Vida Cafe on Lexington Avenue and 82nd\xa0Street, on a recent Saturday. He wasn’t talking about an impending move. He meant that her Colombian food was so good that he would no longer have to traipse from his home in the Bronx out to Jackson Heights, where many of the city’s Colombian restaurants are found, to get his fix.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/nyregion/27JOINT2/27JOINT2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/27/nyregion/27JOINT2/27JOINT2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/nyregion/27JOINT2/27JOINT2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/nyregion/27JOINT2/27JOINT2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/nyregion/27JOINT2/27JOINT2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/27/nyregion/27JOINT2/27JOINT2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/nyregion/27JOINT2/27JOINT2-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Savoring Culinary Secrets From Colombia', 'kicker': 'Neighborhood Joint', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Savoring Culinary Secrets From Colombia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Upper East Side (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dulce Vida Cafe (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-25T04:12:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sylvie Bigar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sylvie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bigar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2faa986b-e534-58bd-8e25-907d35d8070e', 'word_count': 599, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2faa986b-e534-58bd-8e25-907d35d8070e'}, {'abstract': 'Officials said that they had uncovered evidence that leaders of the Joint Fruit Company had used falsified contracts with fictitious businesses to obtain large loans from major banks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/25/world/europe/russia-police-search-offices-of-fruit-importer.html', 'snippet': 'Officials said that they had uncovered evidence that leaders of the Joint Fruit Company had used falsified contracts with fictitious businesses to obtain large loans from major banks.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Law enforcement officials on Thursday searched the offices of Vladimir Kekhman, the general director of the Mikhailovsky Theater in St. Petersburg, as part of a widening fraud investigation into the Joint Fruit Company, of which Mr. Kekhman is a major owner. Known as “the Banana King,” because of the wealth he earned as a fruit importer, Mr. Kekhman in recent years has seemed to focus more on the arts than on business. Officials with the Interior Ministry told the news agency Interfax that it had uncovered evidence that between 2010 and 2012 leaders of the Joint Fruit Company had used falsified contracts with fictitious businesses to obtain large loans from major banks. Investigators said Mr. Kekhman was not a target of the investigation. The Joint Fruit Company filed for bankruptcy last year after creditors sought repayment of the loans. Mr. Kekhman issued a statement saying that he was “outraged” by the fraud allegations against company officials and that he was cooperating with law enforcement. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Police Search Offices of Fruit Importer in Russia', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia: Police Search Offices of Fruit Importer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kekhman, Vladimir', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mikhailovsky Opera and Ballet Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-25T04:13:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By David M. Herszenhorn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/8431a7d8-0842-5843-bd12-a8f464a2bbd0', 'word_count': 164, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8431a7d8-0842-5843-bd12-a8f464a2bbd0'}, {'abstract': 'A coalition of opposition groups has called for a major rally in Tahrir Square to voice opposition to the new Islamist-backed Constitution and President Mohamed Morsi.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/25/world/middleeast/egypt-protesters-clash-with-police-in-cairo.html', 'snippet': 'A coalition of opposition groups has called for a major rally in Tahrir Square to voice opposition to the new Islamist-backed Constitution and President Mohamed Morsi.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Protesters clashed with the police on Thursday in Cairo near Tahrir Square on the eve of the second anniversary of the uprising that toppled President Hosni Mubarak. Three police officers and dozens of protesters were injured in skirmishes after protesters tried to dismantle concrete barriers that had been set up around the Interior Ministry after previous demonstrations. A coalition of opposition groups has called for a major rally in Tahrir Square, the center of the 2011 uprising, to voice opposition to the new Islamist-backed Constitution and President Mohamed Morsi. The Muslim Brotherhood, the Islamist group allied with Mr. Morsi, has asked its supporters to observe the anniversary by taking part in community service projects far from the square, a plea aimed at preventing renewed fighting between the factions. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/25/world/egypt-floater/egypt-floater-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/25/world/egypt-floater/egypt-floater-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/25/world/egypt-floater/egypt-floater-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 676, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/25/world/egypt-floater/egypt-floater-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1351, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/25/world/egypt-floater/egypt-floater-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/25/world/egypt-floater/egypt-floater-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/25/world/egypt-floater/egypt-floater-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Protesters Clash With Police in Cairo', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Egypt: Protesters Clash With Police in Cairo', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Egypt)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-25T04:15:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By David D. Kirkpatrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/5792e9ca-25d8-5726-bcfc-a9343fd1c514', 'word_count': 128, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5792e9ca-25d8-5726-bcfc-a9343fd1c514'}, {'abstract': 'For a tennis fanatic in the United States, managing the time difference between the U.S. and Australia is one of the most difficult tasks of the year.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/24/the-perils-of-dvring-the-australian-open/', 'snippet': 'For a tennis fanatic in the United States, managing the time difference between the U.S. and Australia is one of the most difficult tasks of the year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'How does one fit eight hours of tennis viewing into a workday without getting fired or divorced? That’s the question I face four times every year when my life revolves around tennis’s major tournaments to the detriment of work and family life. Twice in the past five years, I made the mistake of booking trips to Latin America during the Australian Open and found myself up in the middle of the night, watching grainy images of barely recognizable figures on dodgy Web sites that infected my laptop with viruses. Never again.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Perils of DVR’ing the Australian Open', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-25T04:26:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By DAVE SEMINARA', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'SEMINARA', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a1afc3d-63a8-5a06-bd0e-a5545520e414', 'word_count': 731, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a1afc3d-63a8-5a06-bd0e-a5545520e414'}, {'abstract': 'As a result of property damage, localities across the New York region that are reeling from Hurricane Sandy cannot expect to reap the same property taxes from homeowners.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/25/nyregion/storm-damaged-homes-mean-lower-property-tax-revenues-in-new-york-region.html', 'snippet': 'As a result of property damage, localities across the New York region that are reeling from Hurricane Sandy cannot expect to reap the same property taxes from homeowners.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Localities across the New York region, already reeling from the cost of cleaning up from Hurricane Sandy, are confronting the prospect of an even bigger blow to their finances: a precipitous decline in property tax revenues.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/25/nyregion/JP-SANDY/JP-SANDY-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/25/nyregion/JP-SANDY/JP-SANDY-articleLarge-v2.jpg', '