e crowd was restrained, at least by Boston standards.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON — Max Goldstein of Manhattan dutifully paid more than $100 for his upper-bowl seat at TD Garden on Thursday night. To him, it was money well spent.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Boston Crowd Boos Anthony, but Bitterness Is Left Behind ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Boston Crowd Boos Anthony, but Bitterness Is Left Behind', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'May, Peter', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Celtics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANTHONY, CARMELO', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garnett, Kevin', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-25T05:04:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter May', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'May', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ff4feca-7cc0-5943-8f5e-2eff1de15eab', 'word_count': 416, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ff4feca-7cc0-5943-8f5e-2eff1de15eab'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/25/arts/television/whats-on-friday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '1:30 P.M. (IFC) ABOUT A BOY (2002) In Paul and Chris Weitz’s adaptation of Nick Hornby’s novel Hugh Grant plays Will, a London Lothario with a Peter Pan complex who must face up to his irresponsible ways when Marcus (Nicholas Hoult), the socially inept 12-year-old son of a hippie-dippy single mother (Toni Collette, above, with Mr. Grant, right, and Mr. Hoult), begins to stalk him. Rachel Weisz is the artist on whom Will fixes his sights; he uses Marcus to help seduce her. Writing in The New York Times, A. O. Scott said that “Mr. Grant, leaning on his mumbling charm until it turns into its opposite, is an ideal cad.” Like “High Fidelity,” another of Mr. Hornby’s works, “\xa0‘About a Boy’ finds redemption in a stale, gooey pop song, in this case Roberta Flack’s ‘Killing Me Softly,’\xa0” Mr. Scott added. “It’s a cheap trick, but one that’s guaranteed to work every time. You succumb to the movie’s warmth and bonhomie because the alternative is to remain in the isolating, self-protective cynicism from which Will has been lucky to escape.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Friday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-25T06:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/97ee0f04-1cd5-50c1-b38f-adf8a46a2e9a', 'word_count': 748, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97ee0f04-1cd5-50c1-b38f-adf8a46a2e9a'}, {'abstract': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/25/news-quiz-january-25-2013/', 'snippet': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'See what you know about the news below. To prepare, you might scan the articles or summaries on today’s paper. Good luck!', 'source': 'The New Yo