ions are realistic and whether she is offering the contractor the proper incentives to sell sponsorships of YogaFit’s conferences and its branded merchandise.\xa0She asked the group how quickly they expected new sales representatives to sell and what type of learning curve they expected.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Getting Sales Representatives to Sell', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-25T12:00:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adriana Gardella', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adriana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gardella', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f662b490-4fc5-57d9-b9e8-99cfb6364c96', 'word_count': 897, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f662b490-4fc5-57d9-b9e8-99cfb6364c96'}, {'abstract': 'The author of “The Gurkha’s Daughter,” on why the Jaipur Literature festival is important for him and why you should read his book.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/25/five-questions-for-prajwal-parajuly/', 'snippet': 'The author of “The Gurkha’s Daughter,” on why the Jaipur Literature festival is important for him and why you should read his book.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Prajwal Parajuly is an Indian writer whose first book “The Gurkha’s Daughter,” a collection of short stories on Nepalese-speaking people, was recently released in India. He spoke to India Ink from the Jaipur Literature Festival. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Five Questions for: Prajwal Parajuly'