ace to start when assessing whether banks release sufficient information about their financial results.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/01/25/making-sense-of-wall-streets-trading-revenue/', 'snippet': 'Trading results are good place to start when assessing whether banks release sufficient information about their financial results.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Traders at the top Wall Street firms racked up nearly $80 billion of revenue last year. But understanding how they produced all that money is far from simple. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Making Sense of Wall Street’s Trading Revenue', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bank of America Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citigroup Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JPMorgan Chase & Company', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Morgan Stanley', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-25T15:12:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Eavis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eavis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce5fbc27-56ad-55d3-adb4-669ab9956c96', 'word_count': 807, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce5fbc27-56ad-55d3-adb4-669ab9956c96'}, {'abstract': 'Senate Republicans are delaying hearings for an exceptional, and moderate, appeals court nominee.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/25/yet-more-g-o-p-obstruction/', 'snippet': 'Senate Republicans are delaying hearings for an exceptional, and moderate, appeals court nominee.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In his first term, President Obama tried to fill two vacancies on the U.S. Court of Appeals for the District of Columbia. No luck: Senate Republicans blocked both of his nominees. Unsurprisingly, they’re showing no signs of letting up. As Legal Times reported on Wednesday, they’re delaying hearings for Srikanth Srinivasan, an exceptional and moderate candidate.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yet More G.O.P. Obstruction', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-25T15:17:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lincoln Caplan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lincoln', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/38d6bca0-83b9-5e8d-bb99-2ac7752d6926', 'word_count': 501, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38d6bca0-83b9-5e8d-bb99-2ac7752d6926'}, {'abstract': 'The judge in the case expressed the view that that punishment was “way too light” for the former agent John C. Kiriakou.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/26/us/ex-officer-for-cia-is-sentenced-in-leak-case.html', 'snippet': 'The judge in the case expressed the view that that punishment was “way too light” for the former agent John C. Kiriakou.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALEXANDRIA, Va. — A former Central Intelligence Agency officer was sentenced on Friday to 30 months in prison for disclosing the identity of a covert agency officer to a freelance writer, representing the first time that a C.I.A. officer will serve prison time for disclosing clas