s-and-quality-of-care/', 'snippet': 'A new study makes it even more difficult to draw firm conclusions on whether Medicare Advantage patients get better or worse care than those with traditional Medicare.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Uwe E. Reinhardt is an economics professor at Princeton. He has some financial interests in the health care field.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reader Response: Medicare Options and Quality of Care', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-25T16:17:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Uwe E. Reinhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Uwe', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Reinhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c677cc2-4185-5747-a742-b373c39c33a7', 'word_count': 1070, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c677cc2-4185-5747-a742-b373c39c33a7'}, {'abstract': 'Senator Saxby Chambliss, Republican of Georgia, said he would retire at the end of 2014, a decision likely to set off a battle on the Republican Party’s right flank.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/26/us/politics/senator-saxby-chambliss-to-announce-retirement.html', 'snippet': 'Senator Saxby Chambliss, Republican of Georgia, said he would retire at the end of 2014, a decision likely to set off a battle on the Republican Party’s right flank.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Senator Saxby Chambliss, the Georgia Republican who helped lead efforts to find a bipartisan deficit reduction compromise, announced on Friday that he would retire at the end of 2014, a decision likely to set off a battle on the Republican Party’s right flank for a successor.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/26/us/politics/26chambliss_image1/26chambliss_image1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 552, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/26/us/politics/26chambliss_image1/26chambliss_image1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 552}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/26/us/politics/26chambliss_image1/26chambliss_image1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 941, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/26/us/politics/26chambliss_image1/26chambliss_image1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1883, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/26/us/politics/26chambliss_image1/26chambliss_image1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/26/us/politics/26chambliss_image1/26chambliss_image1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/26/us/politics/26chambliss_image1/26chambliss_image1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chambliss Announces Retirement From Senate', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chambliss Announces Retirement From Senate', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chambliss, Saxby', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-25T16:19:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Weisman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weisman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e070ad25-688f-5f37-a8fa-c514101f17f5', 'word_count': 505, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e070ad25-688f-5f37-a8fa-c514101f17f5'}, {'abstract': 'Times critics on “Parker,” “Yossi” and “The Taste of Money.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/25/this-weeks-movies-jan-25/', 'snippet': 'Times critics on “Parker,” “Yossi” and “The Taste of Money.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this week’s video, Times critics offer their thoughts on the action film “Parker” with Jason Statham, the Israeli drama “Yossi” and Im Sang-soo’s “Taste of Money.” Find all of this week’s reviews here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'This Week’s Movies: Jan. 25', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Im Sang-soo', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Statham, Jason', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-25T16:20:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8860b503-e093-5aaa-bea5-d0a0df0187fd', 'word_count': 34, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8860b503-e093-5aaa-bea5-d0a0df0187fd'}, {'abstract': 'A path to a career is paved with the sometimes-painful experiences we make our own.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/27/books/review/the-accidental-writer.html', 'snippet': 'A path to a career is paved with the sometimes-painful experiences we make our own.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I became a writer when I was hit on the head with a rock. It was 1969, I was 6 years old and my mother had dropped me off at a friend’s birthday party. It was June, and I remember the backyard of that house, in Mandeville Canyon, the hot California sun on my hair, the screams of the children as they ran around the yard. The partygoers had assembled into a big and rowdy gang, chasing the birthday boy, trying to get him to crawl through the spanking machine (a joyful and sadistic enterprise in which the children stood in a row and the birthday boy crawled through their legs, getting whacked along the way). The adults gathered inside, trying to ignore us. Then the birthday boy picked up a big rock. And he threw it. ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/books/review/0127-Bender-1357936385328/0127-Bender-1357936385328-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/27/books/review/0127-Bender-1357936385328/0127-Bender-1357936385328-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 682}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/books/review/0127-Bender-1357936385328/0127-Bender-1357936385328-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 902, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo',