rld/middleeast/tens-of-thousands-fill-tahrir-square-on-anniversary-of-egyptian-revolt.html', 'snippet': 'Egyptians in Tahrir Square protested against the Muslim Brotherhood, and the military is said to have deployed armored vehicles in Suez on Saturday to restore security.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — Violence erupted across Egypt on Friday as tens of thousands of demonstrators filled Tahrir Square to mark the second anniversary of the country’s revolution with an outpouring of rage against the rise to power of the Muslim Brotherhood. At least seven protesters and two police officers were killed in clashes in Suez, the state news media said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Deadly Riots Erupt Across Egypt on Anniversary of Revolution', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Deadly Riots Erupt Across Egypt on Anniversary of Revolution', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kirkpatrick, David D', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Egypt)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mubarak, Hosni', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tahrir Square (Cairo)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-25T17:03:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By David D. Kirkpatrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe0fc197-ea07-55cb-88f4-c00f5433564c', 'word_count': 1040, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe0fc197-ea07-55cb-88f4-c00f5433564c'}, {'abstract': 'Even parents who are convinced we don’t hover may not be stepping back to allow children to step up.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/25/helicopter-parents-make-children-miss-milestones/', 'snippet': 'Even parents who are convinced we don’t hover may not be stepping back to allow children to step up.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yet another account of educators describing wild instances of helicopter parenting is making the rounds, this time from Australia. The Sydney Morning Herald reports that two-thirds of school psychologists, counselors, teachers and mental health workers who responded to a survey by the Queensland University of Technology reported seeing some instances of “overparenting” while more than a quarter said they’d seen many.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Helicopter Parents Make Children Miss Milestones', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-25T17:04:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea586575-731f-5fc2-9b6f-a73d47ea8e7f', 'word_count': 564, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea586575-731f-5fc2-9b6f-a73d47ea8e7f'}, {'abstract': 'New-home sales rose at a faster rate in 2012 than in any year since 1983. But 2012 was still one of the worst years ever.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/25/new-home-sales-soar-and-remain-low/', 'snippet': 'New-home sales rose at a faster rate in 2012 than in any year since 1983. But 2012 was still one of the worst years ever.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New-home sales rose 20 percent in 2012, the government said Friday. That is the largest annual gain since 1983.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New-Home Sales Soar — and Remain Low', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-25T17:04:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Floyd Norris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Norris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/256d5f46-e519-5b7d-9c27-cd56c77de39f', 'word_count': 251, 'uri': 'nyt://article/256d5f46-e519-5b7d-9c27-cd56c77de39f'}, {'abstract': 'Paperback books of particular interest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/27/books/review/paperback-row.html', 'snippet': 'Paperback books of particular interest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HOPE: A Tragedy,  by Shalom Auslander. (Riverhead, $16.) Auslander’s previous books — the story collection “Beware of God” and the memoir “Foreskin’s Lament” — are propelled by the author’s struggle with the constraints of his Orthodox Jewish background. In “Hope: A Tragedy,” his first novel, hilarity alternates with pain as a doleful family man in upstate New York finds a prickly geriatric squatter in his attic: she claims to be Anne Frank and is working on a novel to eclipse her girlhood diary.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paperback Row', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Paperback Row', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-25T17:05:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ihsan Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ihsan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a9629d2-3ca4-5874-a14e-3c598209a813', 'word_count': 514, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a9629d2-3ca4-5874-a14e-3c598209a813'}, {'abstract': 'AT&T has agreed to buy some spectrum — the radio waves that carry wireless calls and data — from its main competitor, Verizon Wireless. It will pay $1.9 billion for spectrum licenses that would cover 42 million people across 18 states.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/25/att-will-buy-some-verizon-spectrum-for-1-9-billion/', 'snippet': 'AT&T has agreed to buy some spectrum — the radio waves that carry wireless calls and data — from its main competitor, Verizon Wireless. It will pay $1.9 billion for spectrum licenses that would cover 42 million people across 18 states.', 'lead_paragraph': ' AT&T said on Friday that it had agreed to buy some spectrum — the radio waves that carry wireless calls and data — from its main competitor, Verizon Wireless.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'AT&T Will Buy Some Verizon Spectrum for $1.9 Billion', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radio Spectrum', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AT&T Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Verizon Communications Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-25T17:06:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian X. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd6492f1-5cc9-5867-bbb2-7a5c15bfa5e5', 'word_count': 266, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd6492f1-5cc9-5867-bbb2-7a5c15bfa5e5'}, {'abstract': 'The United Nations opens a campaign to reduce waste, noting just one-quarter of what is lost or discarded each year would feel the world’s hungry.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/25/the-conundrum-of-food-waste/', 'snippet': 'The United Nations opens a campaign to reduce waste, noting just one-quarter of what is lost or discarded each year would feel the world’s hungry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Each year, 1.3 billion tons of food — about one third of all the food produced globally –- ends up wasted even as hundreds of millions of people go hungry. This week, two United Nations agencies opened a global campaign to address that conundrum, calling for changes in the way that food is harvested, transported, processed, sold and consumed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Conundrum of Food Waste', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-25T17:09:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emma Bryce', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emma', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bryce', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6139eae4-0d8a-530a-ab49-6f8bdf26f9ed', 'word_count': 678, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6139eae4-0d8a-530a-ab49-6f8bdf26f9ed'}, {'abstract': 'Food-related events around New York.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/25/weekend-fare-126/', 'snippet': 'Food-related events around New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A festival of beer, bourbon and barbecue will feature two tasting sessions on Saturday at The Tunnel, 608 West 28th Street, in Chelsea. From noon to 4 p.m., the focus is on bacon, and from 5:30 to 8:30 p.m., a barbecue plate is included with the unlimited samplings of beer and bourbon. Limited tickets are available only at the door, at $135 for the first session and $120 in the evening.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Weekend Fare', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-25T17:11:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bao Ong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bao', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/51cc3912-89a7-54e0-8703-7bc5eecb0472', 'word_count': 244, 'uri': 'nyt://article/51cc3912-89a7-54e0-8703-7bc5eecb0472'}, {'abstract': 'Ben Ratliff and Jon Caramanica discuss ASAP Rocky and his “spirit guide,” ASAP Yams.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/25/popcast-asap-rocky-arrives/', 'snippet': 'Ben Ratliff and Jon Caramanica discuss ASAP Rocky and his “spirit guide,” ASAP Yams.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The young Harlem rapper ASAP Rocky recently topped the Billboard album chart with the release of his major label debut album, “Long.Live.ASAP.” On this week’s Popcast, the host Ben Ratliff talks to Jon Caramanica, a pop music critic for The Times, about the album, what it means to be post-regional in a genre so obsessed with place, and what trends in hip-hop Rocky’s success might augur.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/25/arts/asap-popcast/asap-popcast-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 367, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/25/arts/asap-popcast/asap-popcast-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 367}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/25/arts/asap-popcast/asap-popcast-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 627, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/25/arts/asap-popcast/asap-popcast-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1253, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/25/arts/asap-popcast/asap-popcast-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/25/arts/asap-popcast/asap-popcast-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/25/arts/asap-popcast/asap-popcast-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Popcast: ASAP Rocky Arrives', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline'