m Apple and other companies. That finding was included in Apple’s 2013 report on labor conditions at its suppliers, where more t...', 'lead_paragraph': ' Labor recruiters in China last year knowingly provided underage workers to a supplier that built parts for products from Apple and other companies. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Apple Takes Aim at Providers of Underage Laborers', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Foxconn Technology', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-25T18:34:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Wingfield', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wingfield', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3b770b6-89c5-5539-9ca6-315f1672d7a5', 'word_count': 306, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3b770b6-89c5-5539-9ca6-315f1672d7a5'}, {'abstract': 'Roger Federer’s facade of cool crumbled in his loss to Andy Murray in the semifinals of the Australian Open, his rare expletives even prompting the BBC to apologize for them.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/25/federer-loses-cool-as-he-loses-match-to-murray/', 'snippet': 'Roger Federer’s facade of cool crumbled in his loss to Andy Murray in the semifinals of the Australian Open, his rare expletives even prompting the BBC to apologize for them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MELBOURNE, Australia — Calling Roger Federer unflappable is normally as bold a statement as calling Shaquille O’Neal tall.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Federer Loses Cool as He Loses Match to Murray', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-25T18:37:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By BEN ROTHENBERG', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'ROTHENBERG', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a039a12-a1ca-5060-8fea-ea57e04b1429', 'word_count': 545, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a039a12-a1ca-5060-8fea-ea57e04b1429'}, {'abstract': 'Lena Dunham, the much-discussed actor, director, writer and creator of “Girls,” won a Golden Globe award earlier this month for her lead performance on the show, and “Girls” won the Golden Globe for best comedy series.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/25/hbo-orders-third-season-of-girls/', 'snippet': 'Lena Dunham, the much-discussed actor, director, writer and creator of “Girls,” won a Golden Globe award earlier this month for her lead performance on the show, and “Girls” won the Golden Globe for best comedy series.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Girls run the world — not only in Beyoncé’s song lyrics but on HBO’s schedule, too. The cable channel announced on Friday that it was picking up a third season of “Girls,” its hit comedy created by Lena Dunham and starring her as the foremost of a group of Brooklyn-based friends learning to navigate their young lives. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/25/arts/girls/girls-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/25/arts/girls/girls-articleLa