}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df081032-4ca5-557e-b2d8-42ebe4546cb3', 'word_count': 453, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df081032-4ca5-557e-b2d8-42ebe4546cb3'}, {'abstract': 'The Weinsteins are trying to position Robert De Niro as this year’s Meryl Streep: a living legend who hasn’t won an Oscar in years.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/25/a-de-niro-campaign-that-takes-a-page-from-the-streep-playbook/', 'snippet': 'The Weinsteins are trying to position Robert De Niro as this year’s Meryl Streep: a living legend who hasn’t won an Oscar in years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES – With less than a month to go before the Oscars, studios are putting their muscle into campaigns on all platforms. The Weinstein Company, a master of the form, has made a TV spot to show viewers – and Oscar voters – the many facets of Robert De Niro’s best supporting actor-nominated performance in “Silver Linings Playbook.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A De Niro Campaign That Takes a Page From the Streep Playbook', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'De Niro, Robert', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Weinstein Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-25T19:27:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2b477c9-f03c-51cd-97e9-bc1ffd80e6f0', 'word_count': 236, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2b477c9-f03c-51cd-97e9-bc1ffd80e6f0'}, {'abstract': 'Discussing the city’s contest to pick a developer for a new “micro-apartment” building on his Friday radio show, the mayor fondly recalled his own humble start in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/25/living-in-his-own-tiny-home-before-he-was-a-billionaire-mayor/', 'snippet': 'Discussing the city’s contest to pick a developer for a new “micro-apartment” building on his Friday radio show, the mayor fondly recalled his own humble start in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg may now be one of the wealthiest men in the world, with gracious estates scattered across the globe from Bermuda to London, but it was not always so.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/26/nyregion/cityroom-shoebox/cityroom-shoebox-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 422, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/26/nyregion/cityroom-shoebox/cityroom-shoebox-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 422}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/26/nyregion/cityroom-shoebox/cityroom-shoebox-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 720, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/26/nyregion/cityroom-shoebox/cityroom-shoebox-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1257, 'width': 1788, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/26/nyregion/cityroom-shoebox/cityroom-shoebox-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/26/nyregion/cityroom-shoebox/cityroom-shoebox-th