A Study in Contrasts in Australian Open Final', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-25T20:29:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By BEN ROTHENBERG', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'ROTHENBERG', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/006121a9-5c2f-5e3a-884d-8b1261ea47b1', 'word_count': 503, 'uri': 'nyt://article/006121a9-5c2f-5e3a-884d-8b1261ea47b1'}, {'abstract': 'Marjane Satrapi’s memoir is No. 1 on the paperback list.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/25/graphic-books-best-sellers-persepolis-tops-the-paperback-list/', 'snippet': 'Marjane Satrapi’s memoir is No. 1 on the paperback list.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is activity on each of our graphic books best-seller lists this week. At No. 1 on the manga list is Vol. 2 of “Missions of Love,” a romance series. On the hardcover list, at No. 3, is “Dark Tower: The Gunslinger — The Man in Black,” the latest adaption of Stephen King’s epic, published by Marvel Entertainment. At No. 4 is Vol. 2 of “Wonder Woman,” part of the “New 52” initiative by DC Comics that reintroduced all the company’s heroes. Wonder Woman has always been tied to Greek mythology and this version is making great use of those mischievous gods and goddesses.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/25/books/25graphicbooks/25graphicbooks-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 786, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/25/books/25graphicbooks/25graphicbooks-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheig