ustines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72b8a42c-e892-5def-892d-4a67b6a5bd6f', 'word_count': 216, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72b8a42c-e892-5def-892d-4a67b6a5bd6f'}, {'abstract': 'A look back at the allure of a Ken Griffey Jr. rookie card and an 11-year-old on a mission.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/25/the-card-of-my-dreams-always-elusive/', 'snippet': 'A look back at the allure of a Ken Griffey Jr. rookie card and an 11-year-old on a mission.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was a spring day in 1998, and my best friend’s mother was on the other end of the phone. The news wasn’t good: her nephew wanted his baseball card back, despite the deal his younger brother had made to sell it to me for $2.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/24/sports/baseball/24griffey/24griffey-articleLarge.png', 'height': 445, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/24/sports/baseball/24griffey/24griffey-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 445}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/24/sports/baseball/24griffey/24griffey-jumbo.png', 'height': 451, 'width': 608, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/24/sports/baseball/24griffey/24griffey-superJumbo.png', 'height': 451, 'width': 608, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/24/sports/baseball/24griffey/24griffey-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/24/sports/baseball/24griffey/24griffey-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/24/sports/baseball/24griffey/24griffey-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Card of My Dreams, Always Elusive', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Card', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trading Cards', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Griffey, Ken Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McWilliam, Richard P (1953-2013)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Topps Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-25T20:41:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph Burgess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burgess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/847a9ecd-92b4-594b-98fc-f2bef368e977', 'word_count': 1084, 'uri': 'nyt://article/847a9ecd-92b4-594b-98fc-f2bef368e977'}, {'abstract': 'Consumers and merchants share war stories from their own attempts to dispute debit or credit card purchases or defend against these complaints.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/25/reports-from-your-own-credit-card-disputes/', 'snippet': 'Consumers and merchants share war stories from their own attempts to dispute debit or credit card purchases or defend against these complaints.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this weekend’s Your Money column, I tried to give people a user’s guide to disputing credit and debit card purchases. The ability to turn problems over to your card issuer is one of the most powerful weapons in a consumer’s arsenal, but you don’t want to be wielding it constantly. Merchants are people, too, and disputing a charge causes them real hassle and expense.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reports From Your Own Credit Card Disputes', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Cards', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN EXPRESS COMPANY', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Discover Financial Services', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MasterCard Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Visa Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-25T20:47:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Lieber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lieber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f900fe6-7b0a-5d8a-88fd-c69eedf2c25b', 'word_count': 297, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f900fe6-7b0a-5d8a-88fd-c69eedf2c25b'}, {'abstract': '“The Future Is Not What It Was,” by Michael Rabe, playing at Walkerspace, refers to the future but is set “in a world not unlike our own, where society’s moral compasses have been broken.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/26/theater/reviews/the-future-is-not-what-it-was-at-walkerspace.html', 'snippet': '“The Future Is Not What It Was,” by Michael Rabe, playing at Walkerspace, refers to the future but is set “in a world not unlike our own, where society’s moral compasses have been broken.”', 'lead_paragraph': '“Everybody’s last night on earth is a sick joke,” Sean, a single young New Yorker, says defensively. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/26/arts/26FUTURE/26FUTURE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 384, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/26/arts/26FUTURE/26FUTURE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 384}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/26/arts/26FUTURE/26FUTURE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/26/arts/26FUTURE/26FUTURE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1311, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/26/arts/26FUTURE/26FUTURE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/26/arts/26FUTURE/26FUTURE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/26/arts/26FUTURE/26FUTURE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Dead Date: That’ll Kill a Romance', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Dead Date: That’ll Kill A Romance', 'name': None, '