 [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pentagon Reverses Some of Its Censoring of a War Book', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pentagon Reverses Some of Its Censoring of a War Book', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classified Information and State Secrets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shaffer, Anthony A', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bagram Air Base (Afghanistan)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-25T20:51:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Shane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1831d174-f713-5910-bd2a-c404470cb95f', 'word_count': 425, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1831d174-f713-5910-bd2a-c404470cb95f'}, {'abstract': 'Bucks readers who own small businesses discuss their experiences in lobbying state and local government officials.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/25/wielding-influence-even-if-youre-small/', 'snippet': 'Bucks readers who own small businesses discuss their experiences in lobbying state and local government officials.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Paul Sullivan, in his Wealth Matters column this week, writes about one of small businesses’ disadvantages — they do not have the resources that the big companies do to wield political influence. But, as Paul points out, that does not mean they can’t wield any influence.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wielding Influence, Even if You’re Small', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lobbying and Lobbyists', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-25T20:53:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bucks Editors', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bucks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Editors', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9db00f80-0e87-5b26-8df5-32d3aab8b0e2', 'word_count': 167, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9db00f80-0e87-5b26-8df5-32d3aab8b0e2'}, {'abstract': 'Years of bad blood between the two hedge fund magnates spilled publicly onto CNBC’s airwaves on Friday, as Mr. Icahn derided his younger counterpart as a “crybaby,” and Mr. Ackman declared the veteran investor a “bully.”', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/01/25/rumble-on-basic-cable-as-ackman-takes-on-icahn-live/', 'snippet': 'Years of bad blood between the two hedge fund magnates spilled publicly onto CNBC’s airwaves on Friday, as Mr. Icahn derided his younger counterpart as a “crybaby,” and Mr. Ackman declared the veteran investor a “bully.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a half-hour on Friday afternoon, the eyes of Wall Street were not on the usual fixations, like the fiscal talks in Washington, or Apple’s earnings or a potential takeover of Dell.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Hedge Fund Dogfight, Live, Mesmerizes Wall Street', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Hedge Fund Dogfight, Live, Mesmerizes Wall St.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hedge Funds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ackman, William A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Icahn, Carl C', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CNBC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Herbalife Ltd', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-25T20:53:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf398ec1-ac1a-551c-b116-9c25e52d0d78', 'word_count': 765, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf398ec1-ac1a-551c-b116-9c25e52d0d78'}, {'abstract': 'Hedge fund magnates take their feud to CNBC. | A sign to Wall St. in Obama’s picks for regulators. | Goldman overcomes its latest headache. | Jesse Eisinger of ProPublica on a suit that hints at behavior by bankers in a bubble. | A look back on our reporting of the past week’s highs and lows in finance.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/01/25/week-in-review-rumble-on-basic-cable/', 'snippet': 'Hedge fund magnates take their feud to CNBC. | A sign to Wall St. in Obama’s picks for regulators. | Goldman overcomes its latest headache. | Jesse Eisinger of ProPublica on a suit that hints at behavior by bankers in a bubble. | A look back on ou...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hedge fund magnates take their feud to CNBC. | A sign to Wall Street in Obama’s picks for regulators. | Goldman overcomes its latest headache. | Jesse Eisinger of ProPublica on a suit that hints at behavior by bankers in a bubble. | Microsoft may back a Dell buyout. | Andrew Ross Sorkin says that prophecies made in Davos don’t always come true. | Its tax edge on thin ice, private equity is regrouping. | Looking skyward in Asia.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Week in Review: Rumble on Basic Cable', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-25T20:54:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Owles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Owles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/80c54b0f-58b2-5794-8d04-ca595d8c159d', 'word_count': 1044, 'uri': 'nyt://article/80c54b0f-58b2-5794-8d04-ca595d8c159d'}, {'abstract': 'Fans who woke up at 3:30 this morning to watch Andy Murray play Roger Federer got an extra treat.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/25/jim-courier-wins-australian-open-again/', 'snippet': 'Fans who woke up at 3:30 this morning to watch Andy Murray play Roger Federer got an extra treat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As if the gutty, four-hour, five-set Australian Open semifinal today between Andy Murray and Roger Federer weren’t enough to make East Coast tennis fans glad they woke up at 3:30 a.m. to watch it live, viewers who hung on to see Jim Courier’s interview with Murray (scroll toward end of video) after his victory got an extra treat. Courier, who won the last of his four Grand Slam titles in Australia exactly 20 years ago, was a power baseliner as a player. As an interviewer, though, he’s a crisp serve-and-volley man. His questions are brief and informed, and they encourage his subjects to actually say something, as opposed to the all-too-common inane sportscaster queries like “How big was that . . . ?” and “What does it mean to have . . . ?” Courier was overshadowed during his fine playing career by contemporaries like Pete Sampras and Andre Agassi, but as an on-court interviewer, he’s almost unbeatable.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/25/magazine/25-andy-murray-interview-2/25-andy-murray-interview-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 289, 'width': 480, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/25/magazine/25-andy-murray-interview-2/25-andy-murray-interview-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 289, 'width': 480, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/25/magazine/25-andy-murray-interview-2/25-andy-murray-interview-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/25/magazine/25-andy-murray-interview-2/25-andy-murray-interview-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/25/magazine/25-andy-murray-interview-2/25-andy-murray-interview-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jim Courier Wins Australian Open Again', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-25T20:56:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Hoerburger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoerburger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News',