 {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Denver Nuggets', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Lakers', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-25T21:06:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Howard Beck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Howard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/76874500-0d86-550e-b68e-caeb486147dc', 'word_count': 3320, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76874500-0d86-550e-b68e-caeb486147dc'}, {'abstract': 'An economic renaissance in Mexico, Chile, Colombia, Panama and Peru has become the focus in Latin America, and sub-Saharan Africa has also flashed signs of promise.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/01/25/in-davos-the-search-for-new-nations-driven-by-economic-growth/', 'snippet': 'An economic renaissance in Mexico, Chile, Colombia, Panama and Peru has become the focus in Latin America, and sub-Saharan Africa has also flashed signs of promise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DAVOS, Switzerland — With Europe in a sharp slowdown and the United States forging only a slow recovery, the business and academic elites gathering here are scouring the global landscape for any new economic success story. And a number of countries are stepping forward here at the World Economic Forum to peddle their tales — even if the smart money knows that betting on emerging markets continues to be\xa0risky.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Lookout in Davos for Next Growth Story in Emerging Markets', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On Lookout in Davos For Next Growth Story In Emerging Markets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Latin America', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-25T21:06:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Alderman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alderman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d14dbc3a-1a84-579c-9d8c-448c751e9501', 'word_count': 1127, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d14dbc3a-1a84-579c-9d8c-448c751e9501'}, {'abstract': 'Trisha Brown, a leading choreographer for more than 50 years, will present her last two dances at the Brooklyn Academy of Music this week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/27/arts/dance/trisha-browns-long-career-and-last-dances.html', 'snippet': 'Trisha Brown, a leading choreographer for more than 50 years, will present her last two dances at the Brooklyn Academy of Music this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE CHOREOGRAPHER TRISHA BROWN has made dances worth arguing about for more than 50 years, and for at least 30 years her dances have been loved across the world. Many of today’s best-known choreographers — including David Gordon, Mark Morris and Stephen Petronio — have cited her influence, whether for the poetic fluidity of her movement or for the steely, analytical methods of her choreographic structures. A pioneer of the pure-dance experimentalists of the 1960s and ’70s, she challenged and changed the way we define dance performance. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/arts/27TRISHA_SPAN/27TRISHA_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/27/arts/27TRISHA_SPAN/27TRISHA_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/arts/27TRISHA_SPAN/27TRISHA_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/arts/27TRISHA_SPAN/27TRISHA_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/arts/27TRISHA_SPAN/27TRISHA_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/27/arts/27TRISHA_SPAN/27TRISHA_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/arts/27TRISHA_SPAN/27TRISHA_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pure Dance, Pure Finale', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pure Dance, Pure Finale', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brown, Trisha, Dance Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Trisha',