nst another, the goliath European leagues have been rubbing shoulders and stepping over each other for some time now, carving out the modern world of soccer one television deal or coefficient at a time.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bundesliga: Best-Run League in the World', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'German Bundesliga', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-25T21:30:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stefan Bienkowski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stefan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bienkowski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a8f10f9-903b-50e0-a655-1ab4ad194e06', 'word_count': 956, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a8f10f9-903b-50e0-a655-1ab4ad194e06'}, {'abstract': 'The gas facility in Algeria was cordoned off during the hostage crisis, but two little-known news agencies from Mauritania published updates on the attack and even cited the attackers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/26/world/africa/2-mauritanian-agencies-get-scoops-in-algeria-siege.html', 'snippet': 'The gas facility in Algeria was cordoned off during the hostage crisis, but two little-known news agencies from Mauritania published updates on the attack and even cited the attackers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — There were no reporters on hand when Islamist militants emerged from the sands of eastern Algeria last week to storm a gas facility full of international workers, and Algerian security forces cordoned off the site during the hostage crisis that ensued,