9f'}, {'abstract': 'Despite the claim, residents of the city of Ismayilli said it remained on the brink of martial law after two days of protests, a rare explosion of uncontrolled frustration in the country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/26/world/asia/officials-in-azerbaijan-claim-to-restore-order-to-rioting-city.html', 'snippet': 'Despite the claim, residents of the city of Ismayilli said it remained on the brink of martial law after two days of protests, a rare explosion of uncontrolled frustration in the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — Officials of the ruling party in Azerbaijan said on Friday that the police had restored order in the city of Ismayilli after two days of rioting and calls for the local governor to resign. Local residents, however, said the police were still making arrests and the city remained on the brink of martial law.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Officials in Azerbaijan Claim to Restore Order to Rioting City', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Azerbaijan: Riot Quelled, Officials Say', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Azerbaijan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Aliyev, Ilham H', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Martial Law', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-25T22:25:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Roth and Shahla Sultanova', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Shahla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sultanova', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 