e60', 'word_count': 810, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86fac2f2-cc4a-528a-a78a-448432d81e60'}, {'abstract': 'In Beijing, it costs 22.3 times the typical household income to buy a home. The most comparable number for New York is 6.2.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/25/a-place-that-makes-new-york-real-estate-look-cheap/', 'snippet': 'In Beijing, it costs 22.3 times the typical household income to buy a home. The most comparable number for New York is 6.2.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Think it’s expensive to buy a home in New York? Try moving to China.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Place That Makes New York Real Estate Look Cheap', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-25T22:26:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf660e74-3f13-5820-a56a-a4ede656f391', 'word_count': 300, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf660e74-3f13-5820-a56a-a4ede656f391'}, {'abstract': 'A selection of cultural events this week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/27/arts/jan-27-feb-2.html', 'snippet': 'A selection of cultural events this week.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The rain in Spain stays mainly in the plain” has been replaced by “pahk yah cah in Hahvahd Yahd.” And a gender switch has rendered Henry Higgins a Hannah and Eliza Doolittle an Elliot. But “The Makeover,” a “Hallmark Hall of Fame” production on Sunday at 9 p.m. on ABC, retains the bone structure of George Bernard Shaw’s “Pygmalion,” in which a professor of phonetics wagers that he can train a Cockney flower girl to pass as a duchess by way of proper speech and manners. Set in contemporary Boston, “The Makeover” updates the tale, with Higgins (played by Julia Stiles) as an educational consultant and grammar stickler who decides, after a failed run for Congress, to transform an unkempt beer salesman (David Walton) into the perfect candidate. But she has to subdue that South Side accent before Washington can be conquered — or love pursued. KATHRYN SHATTUCK', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/arts/27GUIDE8/27GUIDE8-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 253, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/27/arts/27GUIDE8/27GUIDE8-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 253}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/arts/27GUIDE8/27GUIDE8-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 433, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/arts/27GUIDE8/27GUIDE8-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 811, 'width': 1920, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/arts/27GUIDE8/27GUIDE8-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/27/arts/27GUIDE8/27GUIDE8-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None,