of the global elite gathered at Davos this year are draping South African scarves on their shoulders and wrapping their iPads with cozies provided by businesses in Peru. It was hardly a new fashion trend, but it was a sign of the latest wave of up-and-coming, fast-growing countries determined to show the world that they have arrived — or badly want to.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Davos, Hunting for the Next Big Thing….uh, Country', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Davos (Switzerland)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-26T00:14:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Alderman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alderman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1343282-ac44-59d2-8418-d41142d80565', 'word_count': 179, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1343282-ac44-59d2-8418-d41142d80565'}, {'abstract': 'Nancy and Steve Potter met on a commune and now live on their own farm, where they enjoy the hard work. And each other.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/25/booming/30-years-sweet-as-a-jar-of-jam.html', 'snippet': 'Nancy and Steve Potter met on a commune and now live on their own farm, where they enjoy the hard work. And each other.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Booming’s “Making It Last” column profiles baby boomer couples who have been together 25 years or more. Send us your story and photos through our submission form.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/25/boomi