their childhood, use their fury against their captor to help others.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/26/movies/hansel-gretel-witch-hunters.html', 'snippet': 'Hansel and Gretel, all grown up and perhaps traumatized by their childhood, use their fury against their captor to help others.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Between the vampire fad and the zombie fad, we haven’t been giving nearly enough attention lately to this planet’s witch problem, so it’s good to see the Norwegian director Tommy Wirkola put the issue back in the public eye with “Hansel & Gretel: Witch Hunters.” It may not stay in the public eye long because this movie is probably not going to put up “Twilight”-like numbers, but, hey, you have to admire the against-the-grain effort.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/26/arts/26FILMROUNDUP/26FILMROUNDUP-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 320, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/26/arts/26FILMROUNDUP/26FILMROUNDUP-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 320}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/26/arts/26FILMROUNDUP/26FILMROUNDUP-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 546, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/26/arts/26FILMROUNDUP/26FILMROUNDUP-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1093, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/26/arts/26FILMROUNDUP/26FILMROUNDUP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/26/arts/26FILMROUNDUP/26FILMROUNDUP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/26/arts/26FILMROUNDUP/26FILMROUNDUP-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Twist on Grimm: It’s the Witches Who are Hunted', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fairy Tales', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Arterton, Gemma', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Renner, Jeremy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-26T00:28:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/621d0ade-3372-57d3-b3d5-1f96a637552f', 'word_count': 270, 'uri': 'nyt://article/621d0ade-3372-57d3-b3d5-1f96a637552f'}, {'abstract': 'In a rare joint interview on “60 Minutes,” President Obama lavishly praised his departing secretary of state. Some saw it as a thumb on the scales of the 2016 presidential campaign.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/25/obama-heaps-praise-on-hillary-clinton-in-joint-appearance/', 'snippet': 'In a rare joint interview on “60 Minutes,” President Obama lavishly praised his departing secretary of state. Some saw it as a thumb on the scales of the 2016 presidential campaign.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama said in an interview shown Friday night that Hillary Rodham Clinton, his bitter rival for the Democratic nomination five years ago, “will go down as one of the finest secretary of states we’ve had” and added that he would “miss her” once she steps down in the coming days.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Heaps Praise on Hillary Clinton in Joint Appearance', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-26T00:29:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c26d0c71-90a5-566f-bb9c-1b7ca683bfe7', 'word_count': 485, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c26d0c71-90a5-566f-bb9c-1b7ca683bfe7'}, {'abstract': 'The men in the Bollywood “Race 2” are toned, dressed-up blanks, pulled out of the drawer marked International Man of Mystery.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/26/movies/race-2-a-bollywood-sequel-from-abbas-mastan.html', 'snippet': 'The men in the Bollywood “Race 2” are toned, dressed-up blanks, pulled out of the drawer marked International Man of Mystery.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Race 2,” a Bollywood thriller set mostly in Turkey, has so much plot that it takes time out at the beginning to sketch in some details. As a portentous voice-over intones, we watch images of the characters on their yachts and in their fancy cars, their beautifully tailored suits straining to contain their meaty gym bodies.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ogling Two International Men of Mystery', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-26T00:31:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Saltz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saltz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/904e9698-6214-5e2a-890b-0972ed28b486', 'word_count': 240, 'uri': 'nyt://article/904e9698-6214-5e2a-890b-0972ed28b486'}, {'abstract': 'Over the years, Alfa Romeo has said it was returning to the United States, but it never did. This time the company seems to mean it, with plans to sell the 4C sports coupe here in the fall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/27/automobiles/alfa-anticipation-once-again.html', 'snippet': 'Over the years, Alfa Romeo has said it was returning to the United States, but it never did. This time the company seems to mean it, with plans to sell the 4C sports coupe here in the fall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alfa Romeo’s ever-shifting plans for a return to the North American market, which it left in 1995 after decades of pitiful sales, poor reliability and strained dealer relations, form a boulevard of broken dreams. The latest blueprint for Alfa’s American resurrection calls for sales of the coming 4C sports coupe, a 2014 model, to begin here in the fall.', 'print_section': 'AU', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/automobiles/27ALFA/27ALFA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 258, 'width':