', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Hale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/53020807-7f13-5abe-8c31-accf662a4953', 'word_count': 825, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53020807-7f13-5abe-8c31-accf662a4953'}, {'abstract': 'Japan said it would inject trillions of yen by buying government bonds, the percentage of American workers in labor unions fell sharply and President Obama nominated two former prosecutors to financial regulatory posts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2013/01/26/business/Bizday-Week-in-Pictures.html', 'snippet': 'Japan said it would inject trillions of yen by buying government bonds, the percentage of American workers in labor unions fell sharply and President Obama nominated two former prosecutors to financial regulatory posts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Japan said it would inject trillions of yen by buying government bonds, the percentage of American workers in labor unions fell sharply and President Obama nominated two former prosecutors to financial regulatory posts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/26/business/Bizday-Week-in-Pictures-slide-NLF9/Bizday-Week-in-Pictures-slide-NLF9-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/26/business/Bizday-Week-in-Pictures-slide-NLF9/Bizday-Week-in-Pictures-slide-NLF9-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/26/business/Bizday-Week-in-Pictures-slide-NLF9/Bizday-Week-in-Pictures-slide-NLF9-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}