896-5fa5-9209-0d9be106c70d'}, {'abstract': 'The Arts Exchange presents a multimedia exploration of the construction of watercraft along the Hudson River and the north and south shores of Long Island Sound.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/27/nyregion/in-white-plains-from-shore-to-shore-an-exhibition-on-boat-building.html', 'snippet': 'The Arts Exchange presents a multimedia exploration of the construction of watercraft along the Hudson River and the north and south shores of Long Island Sound.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHITE PLAINS — It is easy to imagine a brisk breeze blowing and lapping water buoying the wooden boats that fill the gallery of ArtsWestchester’s Arts Exchange as part of “From Shore to Shore: Boat Builders and Boatyards of Westchester and Long Island.” The exhibition presents a multimedia exploration of boat building in the region. It includes a 15-foot-long illustrated timeline, graphic panels, videos, models and half-models and a selection of well-worn tools. Interspersed are actual boats — a flat-bottom fishing skiff, a couple of rowing boats, six handcrafted kayaks and a 16-foot melonseed catboat, its single gaff-rigged sail unfurled.', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/nyregion/27ARTSWE1_SPAN/27ARTSWE1_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 374, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/27/nyregion/27ARTSWE1_SPAN/27ARTSWE1_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 374}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/nyregion/27ARTSWE1_SPAN/27ARTSWE1_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 639, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image',