tion': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/893a8e58-7757-550d-893c-1213dd8f330b', 'word_count': 927, 'uri': 'nyt://article/893a8e58-7757-550d-893c-1213dd8f330b'}, {'abstract': 'A musical at Hartford Stage tells the story of the tenor Roland Hayes, the first African-American vocalist to receive international acclaim.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/27/nyregion/a-review-of-breath-and-imagination-at-hartford-stage.html', 'snippet': 'A musical at Hartford Stage tells the story of the tenor Roland Hayes, the first African-American vocalist to receive international acclaim.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE HEADLINE ON an unsigned music review from 1929 in The New York Times was unequivocal: “Roland Hayes, Tenor, Delights a Throng: Carnegie Hall Audience Hears Him in Meticulous Refinement of Style.” The critic praised the program of arias, art songs and spirituals and compared Hayes’s phrasing to “the delicacy of a cameo”; what’s more, the singer was so famous that the reviewer did not feel it necessary to mention the most extraordinary aspect of the concert: Roland Hayes, tenor, who had toured Europe and sung for royalty, was a black man, born in rural Georgia to a former slave.', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/nyregion/27ARTSCT1_SPAN/27ARTSCT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/27/nyregion/27ARTSCT1_SPAN/27ARTSCT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/nyregion/27ARTSCT1_SPAN/27ARTSCT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/nyregion/27ARTSCT1_SPAN/27ARTSCT1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/nyregion/27ARTSCT1_SPAN/27ARTSCT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/27/nyregion/27ARTSCT1_SPAN/27ARTSCT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/nyregion/27ARTSCT1_SPAN/27ARTSCT1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Tenor With ‘Breath and Imagination’', 'kicker': 'Arts | Connecticut', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Tenor With ‘Breath and Imagination’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hartford (Conn)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hartford Stage Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tresnjak, Darko', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beaty, Daniel', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sykes, Jubilant', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-26T01:23:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sylviane Gold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sylviane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/74ae6f24-8786-528b-afbf-a05c82cf2f87', 'word_count': 737, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74ae6f24-8786-528b-afbf-a05c82cf2f87'}, {'abstract': 'Death rates from flu and pneumonia have soared well above those of the last few years, confirming that this will be a fairly severe flu season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/26/health/more-evidence-of-a-severe-flu-season.html', 'snippet': 'Death rates from flu and pneumonia have soared well above those of the last few years, confirming that this will be a fairly severe flu season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Death rates from flu and pneumonia have soared well above those of the last few years, confirming that this will be a fairly severe flu season, figures released Friday by federal health officials show. At the same time, new infections with influenza continued to fall, suggesting that the season has peaked almost everywhere in the country except in the far West. Because so many of those hospitalized and dying from the flu are geriatric patients, the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention issued guidelines to doctors who care for older patients, suggesting giving high-dose flu shots to the elderly and starting antiflu drugs as soon as an infection is suspected. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Evidence of a Severe Flu Season', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Health', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'More Evidence of a Severe Flu Season', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McNeil, Donald G Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Influenza', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-26T01:25:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Donald G. McNeil Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Donald', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'McNeil', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d51fcc75-61f4-5fdf-8265-24cb1307ea7e', 'word_count': 110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d51fcc75-61f4-5fdf-8265-24cb1307ea7e'}, {'abstract': 'The relationship between Danica Patrick, 30, and Ricky Stenhouse, 25, is likely to shine a brighter spotlight on their performances this season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/26/sports/autoracing/danica-patrick-and-ricky-stenhouse-dating.html', 'snippet': 'The relationship between Danica Patrick, 30, and Ricky Stenhouse, 25, is likely to shine a brighter spotlight on their performances this season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CONCORD, N.C. — Danica Patrick’s arrival as a full-time driver in Nascar’s Sprint Cup series has gone from sideshow to spectacle even before the first green flag of the season.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/26/sports/autoracing/26couples2-img/26couples2-img-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 508, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/26/sports/autoracing/26couples2-img/26couples2-img-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 508}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/26/sports/autoracing/26couples2-img/26couples2-img-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 868, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/26/sports/autoracing/26couples2-img/26couples2-img-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1525, 'width': 1800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/26/sports/autoracing/26couples2-img/26couples2-img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/26/sports/autoracing/26couples2-img/26couples2-img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/26/sports/autoracing/26couples2-img/26couples2-img-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Patrick and Stenhouse, Fellow Sprint Cup Rookies, Are Also a Couple', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Patrick and Stenhouse, Fellow Sprint Cup Rookies, Are Now Also a Couple', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dating and Courtship', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Patrick, Danica', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stenhouse, Ricky Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nascar Sprint Cup Series', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-26T01:25:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Auto Racing', 'byline': {'original': 'By Viv Bernstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Viv', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bernstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c83ccd5c-e89c-5dc6-a248-131f79b4508e', 'word_count': 591, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c83ccd5c-e89c-5dc6-a248-131f79b4508e'}, {'abstract': 'Justice Sonia Sotomayor recalled a lesson that she learned, painfully, at Blessed Sacrament School on the obligation to think about people in need.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/26/nyregion/with-her-old-school-set-to-close-a-justice-reminisces.html', 'snippet': 'Justice Sonia Sotomayor recalled a lesson that she learned, painfully, at Blessed Sacrament School on the obligation to think about people in need.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The planned closing of Blessed Sacrament School in the Bronx — a haven amid the housing projects in the Soundview neighborhood — has left many parents and graduates upset. That includes the valedictorian of the class of 1968, who grew up in the projects that now bear her name: Sonia Sotomayor, associate justice of the United States Supreme Court.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/26/nyregion/SCHOOL1-city/SCHOOL1-city-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/26/nyregion/SCHOOL1-city/SCHOOL1-city-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/26/nyregion/SCHOOL1-city/SCHOOL1-city-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/26/nyregion/SCHOOL1-city/SCHOOL1-city-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1323, 'width': 1986, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/26/nyregion/SCHOOL1-city/SCHOOL1-city-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/26/nyregion/SCHOOL1-city/SCHOOL1-city-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/26/nyregion/SCHOOL1-city/SCHOOL1-city-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'As Her Old School Faces the End, a Justice Reminisces', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Her Old School Faces the End, a Justice Reminisces', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gonzalez, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Blessed Sacrament School (Bronx, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private and Sectarian Schools', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sotomayor, Sonia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-26T01:25:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Gonzalez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonzalez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9209c02c-9a0f-5276-8586-810533c6eca7', 'word_count': 743, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9209c02c-9a0f-5276-8586-810533c6eca7'}, {'abstract': 'Using phony Senate sessions, lawmakers tried to keep two federal agencies from operating.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/26/opinion/a-court-upholds-republican-chicanery.html', 'snippet': 'Using phony Senate sessions, lawmakers tried to keep two federal agencies from operating.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For most of President Obama’s first term, Republicans used legislative trickery to try to prevent the functioning of two federal agencies they hate, the National Labor Relations Board and the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau. First they would filibuster the president’s nominees to the agencies, knowing that neither agency could operate without board members or a director. Then they would create fake legislative sessions for the Senate during its recess, intended solely to prevent Mr. Obama from making recess appointments as an end run.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Court Upholds Republican Chicanery', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Court Upholds Republican Chicanery', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Financial Protection Bureau', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Labor Relations Board', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cordray, Richard', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidents and Presidency (US)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-26T01:27:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3e75135-9ed8-5d31-9526-f026d4fcbf89', 'word_count': 588, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3e75135-9ed8-5d31-9526-f026d4fcbf89'}, {'abstract': 'To some observers, Victoria Azarenka’s injury timeout at a pivotal point in her match against Sloane Stephens was an unusual and troubling tactic.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/25/in-tennis-gamesmanship-is-the-norm/', 'snippet': 'To some observers, Victoria Azarenka’s injury timeout at a pivotal point in her match against Sloane Stephens was an unusual and troubling tactic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gardnar Mulloy could hardly believe his eyes. Watching the Australian Open semifinal between Victoria Azarenka and Sloane Stephens on television, the 99-year-old Mulloy suddenly found himself screaming at what he described as “an atrocity, the worst thing I’ve ever seen” in a tennis match.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Tennis, Gamesmanship Is the Norm', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-26T01:30:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By NEIL AMDUR', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'AMDUR', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aef3fc99-f381-56f4-97b6-6dd6abbd5513', 'word_count': 722, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aef3fc99-f381-56f4-97b6-6dd6abbd5513'}, {'abstract': 'A federal judge assails the New York City Police Department’s stop-and-frisk program for its flagrant indifference to the Fourth Amendment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/26/opinion/when-police-violate-the-constitution.html', 'snippet': 'A federal judge assails the New York City Police Department’s stop-and-frisk program for its flagrant indifference to the Fourth Amendment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The federal courts are bearing down on the New York City Police Department’s constitutionally suspect stop-and-frisk program, under which hundreds of thousands of citizens are stopped on the streets each year, often illegally and for no discernible reason. Earlier this month, the federal judge who is presiding over three lawsuits that challenge different parts of the program issued her harshest ruling yet, putting the city on notice that some aspects of stop and frisk are clearly unconstitutional.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Police Violate the Constitution', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Police Violate the Constitution', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search and Seizure', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scheindlin, Shira A', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fourth Amendment (US Constitution)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-26T01:30:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/90146efb-075d-5297-9534-4c9963885cf1', 'word_count': 588, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90146efb-075d-5297-9534-4c9963885cf1'}, {'abstract': 'Sheriff David A. Clarke Jr. of Milwaukee County issued a radio message suggesting that residents consider how to protect themselves from crime, including firearm training.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/26/us/wisconsin-sheriff-makes-a-pitch-for-gun-training.html', 'snippet': 'Sheriff David A. Clarke Jr. of Milwaukee County issued a radio message suggesting that residents consider how to protect themselves from crime, including firearm training.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sheriff David A. Clarke Jr. of Milwaukee County has issued a radio message suggesting that residents consider how to protect themselves from crime, including, perhaps, firearm training. “With officers laid off and furloughed, simply calling 911 and waiting is no longer your best option,” the sheriff said in the recording, one installment in the periodic public service messages he issues. “You could beg for mercy from a violent criminal, hide under the bed, or you can fight back,” he said, later suggesting that residents consider taking a certified course in firearm safety. Sheriff Clarke said in an interview that his office has faced budget cuts in recent years and that he meant his message merely to encourage safety and personal responsibility. “I wouldn’t tell people to go get a gun,” Sheriff Clarke said. “I wouldn’t tell them not to go get a gun.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wisconsin: Sheriff Makes a Pitch for Gun Training', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Midwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wisconsin: Sheriff Makes a Pitch For Gun Training', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Firearms', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wisconsin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clarke, David A Jr', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-26T01:33:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Monica Davey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Monica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d92f9ae7-360c-5b59-bf05-7a9d1e504d22', 'word_count': 143, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d92f9ae7-360c-5b59-bf05-7a9d1e504d22'}, {'abstract': 'A federal judge in Dallas ruled that a group of federal immigration agents can proceed with a lawsuit that seeks to halt an Obama administration program.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/26/us/texas-lawsuit-permitted-over-immigration-policy.html', 'snippet': 'A federal judge in Dallas ruled that a group of federal immigration agents can proceed with a lawsuit that seeks to halt an Obama administration program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A federal judge in Dallas has ruled that a group of federal immigration agents can proceed with a lawsuit that seeks to halt an Obama administration program granting reprieves from deportation to young illegal immigrants. In a suit filed in August, several Immigration and Customs Enforcement agents argued that the administration had exceeded its constitutional authority in granting the reprieves, and said they were being forced to violate the law by obeying instructions to refrain from deporting the young immigrants. Judge Reed O’Connor rejected a Justice Department request to dismiss the case. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Texas: Lawsuit Permitted Over Immigration Policy', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Southwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Texas: Lawsuit Permitted Over Immigration Policy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Preston, Julia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deportation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dallas (Tex)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigrants', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Immigration and Customs Enforcement (US)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-26T01:33:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c9f85ae-0457-5e8a-b1f0-84a5b78fe356', 'word_count': 92, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c9f85ae-0457-5e8a-b1f0-84a5b78fe356'}, {'abstract': '“In the Company of Women: Prints by Mary Cassatt,” an exhibition at the Jane Voorhees Zimmerli Art Museum in New Brunswick, runs through March 3.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/27/nyregion/a-review-of-prints-by-mary-cassatt-at-the-jane-voorhees-zimmerli-art-museum.html', 'snippet': '“In the Company of Women: Prints by Mary Cassatt,” an exhibition at the Jane Voorhees Zimmerli Art Museum in New Brunswick, runs through March 3.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW BRUNSWICK, N.J. — In an 1890 letter famous among scholars of the period, Mary Cassatt urged the painter Berthe Morisot, her friend, “You must see the Japanese — come as soon as you can.” The Japanese she was referring to was an exhibition of 725 woodblock prints and albums at the École des Beaux-Arts in Paris. But Cassatt was writing from a particular perspective: she was obsessed with prints and printmaking. “In the Company of Women: Prints by Mary Cassatt,” an exhibition of 23 prints at the Jane Voorhees Zimmerli Art Museum here, offers a snapshot of Cassatt’s engagement with the medium.', 'print_section': 'NJ', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/201