e to the abuse of power.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/26/world/africa/ali-laarayedh-leads-the-tunisian-agency-that-once-jailed-him.html', 'snippet': 'Ali Laarayedh, now the interior minister of Tunisia, said that his prison experiences as a political activist make him sensitive to the abuse of power.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TUNIS — It was the first time Ali Laarayedh had inspected a prison cell, but even then, as the interior minister, his old instincts kicked in.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/26/world/tunisia/tunisia-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/26/world/tunisia/tunisia-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/26/world/tunisia/tunisia-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/26/world/tunisia/tunisia-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/26/world/tunisia/tunisia-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/26/world/tunisia/tunisia-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/26/world/tunisia/tunisia-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Leading the Tunisian Agency That Once Jailed Him', 'kicker': 'The Saturday Profile', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Leading the Tunisian Agency That Once Jailed Him', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tunisia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Torture', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Laarayedh, Ali', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-26T01:39:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil MacFarquhar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacFarquhar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Biography', '_id': 'nyt://article/24e54e51-cd77-5fb7-b180-b2baeaa6dbc1', 'word_count': 1127, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24e54e51-cd77-5fb7-b180-b2baeaa6dbc1'}, {'abstract': 'Investigators said that for three years, a team of employees of the Long Island Rail Road participated in stealing copper wire and selling it for cash to a local scrap metal company.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/26/nyregion/15-lirr-employees-arrested-in-copper-wire-theft.html', 'snippet': 'Investigators said that for three years, a team of employees of the Long Island Rail Road participated in stealing copper wire and selling it for cash to a local scrap metal company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MINEOLA, N.Y. — Investigators say the scheme spanned three years, uncoiling months before a blizzard whipped the region’s transit systems and continuing until two weeks ago, with the Metropolitan Transportation Authority still reeling from Hurricane Sandy.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/26/nyregion/COPPER/COPPER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 407, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/26/nyregion/COPPER/COPPER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 407}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/26/nyregion/COPPER/COPPER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 695, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/26/nyregion/COPPER/COPPER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1200, 'width': 1767, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/26/nyregion/COPPER/COPPER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/26/nyregion/COPPER/COPPER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/26/nyregion/COPPER/COPPER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'L.I.R.R. Employees Accused of Netting $250,000 From Copper Wire Stolen at Work', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'L.I.R.R. Employees Accused of Netting $250,000 From Copper Wire Stolen at Work', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Copper, Brass and Bronze', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Long Island Rail Road Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Transportation Authority', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nassau County (NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Railroads', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-26T01:44:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Flegenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flegenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c04a08f1-e8ad-5aa3-8fac-73a65c17da01', 'word_count': 598, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c04a08f1-e8ad-5aa3-8fac-73a65c17da01'}, {'abstract': 'Some Republicans have proposed switching the way their states award Electoral College votes from winner-take-all to a proportional system based on Congressional districts. Democrats should be glad none of those plans have moved forward.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/25/electoral-college-changes-would-pose-danger-for-democrats/', 'snippet': 'Some Republicans have proposed switching the way their states award Electoral College votes from winner-take-all to a proportional system based on Congressional districts. Democrats should be glad none of those plans have moved forward.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Republican state senators in Virginia, as well as the state’s Republican governor, Bob McDonnell, announced Friday that they would oppose a bill to change how the state awards its electoral votes in presidential elections. The proposed legislation would have moved the state from awarding its electors on a winner-take-all basis to a proportional system based on Congressional districts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Electoral College Cha