 United States on the matter of airlines’ carbon emissions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAST fall, when Democrats and Republicans seemed unable to agree on anything, one bill glided through Congress with broad bipartisan support and won a quick signature from President Obama: the European Union Emissions Trading Scheme Prohibition Act of 2011.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Your Biggest Carbon Sin May Be Air Travel', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Your Biggest Carbon Sin May Be Air Travel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosenthal, Elisabeth', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Civil Aviation Organization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carbon Dioxide', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-26T18:31:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b5110a2-3db5-5a8f-b303-3270c7491984', 'word_count': 1024, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b5110a2-3db5-5a8f-b303-3270c7491984'}, {'abstract': 'Videos show reaction in Cairo and another Egyptian city, Port Said, to death sentences handed down in a deadly soccer riot case.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/26/egypts-soccer-riots-a-view-from-the-ground/', 'snippet': 'Videos show reaction in Cairo and another Egyptian city, Port Said, to death sentences handed down in a deadly soccer riot case.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was one of the world’s deadliest episodes of soccer violence — a clash between fans of the Egyptian team Al Masry, of Port Said, and players and fans from Al Ahly, of Cairo, a year ago that killed 74 and wounded over 1,000. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt’s Soccer Riots, a View From the Ground', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cairo (Egypt)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-26T18:32:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ravi Somaiya', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ravi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Somaiya', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06f40e4b-78ac-5be8-a5d0-5e407a49cdc4', 'word_count': 292, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06f40e4b-78ac-5be8-a5d0-5e407a49cdc4'}, {'abstract': 'Tim Flannery, the Giants’ third-base coach, is performing to raise money for Bryan Stow, the Giants fan who was beaten outside Dodger Stadium in 2011.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/27/sports/giants-tim-flannery-has-gift-for-coaching-and-carrying-a-tune.html', 'snippet': 'Tim Flannery, the Giants’ third-base coach, is performing to raise money for Bryan Stow, the Giants fan who was beaten outside Dodger Stadium in 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The back-spinning, bases-clearing grounder that Hunter Pence and his broken bat cued past the St. Louis Cardinals’ infield in October sent the San Francisco Giants’ third-base coach, Tim Flannery, to work. Frantically windmilling his arm, Flannery sent Buster Posey all the way home from first base to complete the three-run double and propel the Giants toward victory in Game 7 of the National League Championship Series.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/sports/dogYFLANNERY2/dogYFLANNERY2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 537, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/27/sports/dogYFLANNERY2/dogYFLANNERY2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 537}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/sports/dogYFLANNERY2/dogYFLANNERY2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 916, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/sports/dogYFLANNERY2/dogYFLANNERY2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1831, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/sports/dogYFLANNERY2/dogYFLANNERY2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/27/sports/dogYFLANNERY2/dogYFLANNERY2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/sports/dogYFLANNERY2/dogYFLANNERY2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Giants’ Flannery Has Gift for Coaching and Carrying a Tune', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Journeyman And a Music Man', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Flannery, Tim', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco Giants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-26T18:33:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hillel Kuttler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hillel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kuttler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0a9efe5-e8ab-5da6-b964-84be371a950d', 'word_count': 967, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0a9efe5-e8ab-5da6-b964-84be371a950d'}, {'abstract': 'Roman Catholic leaders pay too much heed to insulating, justifying and protecting their priesthood and themselves.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/27/opinion/sunday/bruni-catholicisms-curse.html', 'snippet': 'Roman Catholic leaders pay too much heed to insulating, justifying and protecting their priesthood and themselves.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I HAVE nothing against priests,” writes Garry Wills in his provocative new book, “Why Priests? A Failed Tradition,” and I’d like at the outset to say the same. During a career that has included no small number of formal interviews and informal conversations with them, I’ve met many I admire, men of genuine compassion and remarkable altruism, more dedicated to humanity than to any dogma or selective tradition.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/frank-bruni/frank-bruni-a