www.nytimes.com/2013/01/27/opinion/sunday/the-bird-flu-experiments.html', 'snippet': 'Research on the deadly bird flu virus is to resume, but have all earlier concerns been adequately addressed?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scientists who had stopped research during the past year on a newly created bird flu virus because of safety and terrorism concerns have announced plans to resume their work. We wish we could be as sanguine as they are that all the earlier concerns have been dealt with.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Bird Flu Experiments', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Bird Flu Experiments', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Avian Influenza', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Institutes of Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-26T18:39:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/2837f37c-85cb-55be-a22f-fd038b077d73', 'word_count': 350, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2837f37c-85cb-55be-a22f-fd038b077d73'}, {'abstract': 'A dispute is testing the clout of jihadist fighters and the ability of civilian opposition groups to stand up to them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/27/world/middleeast/syria-war-developments.html', 'snippet': 'A dispute is testing the clout of jihadist fighters and the ability of civilian opposition groups to stand up to them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — The tensions had been simmering for months in the northern Syrian town of Saraqib. Civilian antigovernment activists had complained of rebel fighters who needlessly destroyed a milk factory and treated residents disrespectfully. A growing contingent of jihadist fighters from the ideologically extreme and militarily formidable Nusra Front was suspicious of the activists’ secular, nonviolent agenda.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jihadists and Secular Activists Clash in Syria', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jihadists and Secular Activists Clash in Syria', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mourtada, Hania', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-26T18:39:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hania Mourtada and Anne Barnard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hania', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mourtada', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Anne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e24d8dd8-b771-5a22-ade3-aaa61b3a126e', 'word_count': 1028, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e24d8dd8-b771-5a22-ade3-aaa61b3a126e'}, {'abstract': 'Scientists warn that future winters may be less white.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/27/opinion/sunday/enjoying-snow-while-we-still-have-it.html', 'snippet': 'Scientists warn that future winters may be less white.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SNOW was my first love. From November’s first flakes and the season’s first blizzard, to unexpected midnight dustings and late March blasts, snow fell frequently and happily on my childhood in western Massachusetts. I never complained about the unshoveled, post-blizzard darkness of my paper route, nor about scrambling over icy drifts en route to school. In the evenings I read in front of our wood stove, captivated by thoughts of Narnia’s endless winter. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/sunday-review/27SNOW/27SNOW-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 433, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/27/sunday-review/27SNOW/27SNOW-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 433}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/sunday-review/27SNOW/27SNOW-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 739, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/sunday-review/27SNOW/27SNOW-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1478, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/sunday-review/27SNOW/27SNOW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/27/sunday-review/27SNOW/27SNOW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/sunday-review/27SNOW/27SNOW-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Enjoying Snow, While We Still Have It', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Enjoying Snow, While We Still Have It', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snow and Snowstorms', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vanhoenacker, Mark', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-26T18:41:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Vanhoenacker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vanhoenacker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/d170de2b-8501-5c05-a184-e12546796cf3', 'word_count': 923, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d170de2b-8501-5c05-a184-e12546796cf3'}, {'abstract': 'Fans at the New Year Grand Sumo Tournament were hopeful that 2013 might bring an end to the protracted losing streak by Japanese wrestlers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/27/sports/in-sumos-birthplace-a-drought-of-champions.html', 'snippet': 'Fans at the New Year Grand Sumo Tournament were hopeful that 2013 might bring an end to the protracted losing streak by Japanese wrestlers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — On the first day of the New Year Grand Sumo Tournament last Sunday, fans here were hopeful that 2013 might bring change: an end to the protracted losing streak by Japanese wrestlers. But the only reminders anyone needed of that unlikelihood were the giant portraits of the winners of the last 32 Japanese tournaments that were hanging at Ryogoku Kokugikan arena.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/sports/dogYSUMO/dogYSUMO-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 555, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/27/sports/dogYSUMO/dogYSUMO-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 555}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/sports/dogYSUMO/dogYSUMO-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 944, 'width': 1021, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/sports/dogYSUMO/dogYSUMO-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 944, 'width': 1021, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/sports/dogYSUMO/dogYSUMO-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/27/sports/dogYSUMO/dogYSUMO-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/sports/dogYSUMO/dogYSUMO-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Sumo’s Birthplace, a Drought of Champions', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Sumo&#8217;s Birthplace, a Drought of Champions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sumo Wrestling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tokyo (Japan)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-26T18:41:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel Krieger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krieger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6d88d15-aba5-5939-b436-d2fd17c20c04', 'word_count': 1051, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6d88d15-aba5-5939-b436-d2fd17c20c04'}, {'abstract': 'By Oklahoma, we felt as if we had approached some metaphysical border.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/27/opinion/sunday/driving-with-moby-dick.html', 'snippet': 'By Oklahoma, we felt as if we had approached some metaphysical border.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Is there a stranger figure in American literature than the narrator of “Moby-Dick”? He says, “Call me Ishmael” — the very first words of the book — but that isn’t exactly the same as saying “My name is Ishmael.” He could be anyone, of any name, but Ishmael is what the reader must agree to call him before the book can get under way. I recently drove with a friend from my farm in New York State to Southern California, and Ishmael was our companion. We picked him up, so to speak, on the dark, icy streets of New Bedford, round about 1851, and delivered him within sight of what he calls “your contemplative Pacific,” ageless as always.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/sunday-review/27editorial/27editorial-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/27/sunday-review/27editorial/27editorial-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/27/sunday-review/27editoria