organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4714d176-57ef-517c-a029-d612fc990849', 'word_count': 1128, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4714d176-57ef-517c-a029-d612fc990849'}, {'abstract': 'A fresh study paid for by Norway’s science agency examines temperature changes in the oceans and atmosphere and concludes that global warming will be on the low side.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/26/weaker-global-warming-seen-in-study-promoted-by-norways-research-council/', 'snippet': 'A fresh study paid for by Norway’s science agency examines temperature changes in the oceans and atmosphere and concludes that global warming will be on the low side.', 'lead_paragraph': '| Updates below |Purveyors of climate doubt have seized on a news release from the Research Council of Norway with this provocative title: “Global warming less extreme than feared?” The release describes new research finding that global warming from the buildup of greenhouse gases will be on the low end of the persistently wide spread of projections by other research groups. (There’s a presentation describing the work below.) \xa0[A sentence here has been moved to the bottom.]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Weaker Global Warming Seen in Study Promoted by Norway’s Research Council', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hansen, James E', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Muller, Richard', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Aeronautics and Space Administration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Norway', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-26T21:01:19+0000', 'document_ty