, 'pub_date': '2013-01-27T05:15:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Society', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': 'Weddings', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4166f6c6-f051-5ab7-8ccd-14ee4f454b86', 'word_count': 249, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4166f6c6-f051-5ab7-8ccd-14ee4f454b86'}, {'abstract': 'The Inferno, one of the world’s oldest and longest downhill races, has grown from 12 competitors to 1,850 ski racers, but many of the rituals remain.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/27/sports/skiing/at-inferno-downhill-growing-size-of-event-hasnt-spoiled-its-charm.html', 'snippet': 'The Inferno, one of the world’s oldest and longest downhill races, has grown from 12 competitors to 1,850 ski racers, but many of the rituals remain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MÜRREN, Switzerland — On a sun-drenched hill overlooking the Eiger, Monch and Jungfrau peaks, 1,850 ski racers prepared Saturday to compete in the Inferno, one of the world’s oldest and longest downhill races. As they shuffled through the start house perched at 9,720 feet in the Bernese Oberland, a bottle of homemade schnapps hung in the entryway, a traditional elixir to quell prerace jitters.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Inferno Downhill, Growing Size of Event Hasn’t Spoiled Its Charm', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At Inferno Downhill, Growing Size of Event Hasn’t Spoiled Its Charm', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALPINE SKIING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Switzerland', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-27T05:42:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Skiing', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kelley McMillan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kelley', 'middlename': None, 'lastna