: 'My husband and I adopted our three children, now ages 11, 10 and 7, in October 2010 (we had to wait another nine months for our oldest daughter, the eldest of three biological siblings). We hadn’t intended to adopt this many, but we did not know how to answer the questions of desired age, sex, race and quantity on our paperwork so we left it blank, which the social workers took to mean, “We have a blank, load them up!” During our last training, we got a call that the current foster parents wanted to hand them over A.S.A.P., and we had to leave early to pick them up. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Foster Parenting Creates a Future, Without Erasing the Past', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADOPTIONS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foster Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Love (Emotion)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-27T14:41:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brittney Dalton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brittney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dalton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/710a7234-aaab-5b5c-a461-b573665525af', 'word_count': 769, 'uri': 'nyt://article/710a7234-aaab-5b5c-a461-b573665525af'}, {'abstract': 'Residents of Gao, who had been under occupation for nearly a year by Islamist fighters, celebrated the arrival of Malian and French troops.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/28/world/africa/france-mali-conflict.html', 'snippet': 'Residents of Gao, who had been under occupation for nearly a year by Islamist fighters, celebrated the arrival of Malian and French troops.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SÉVARÉ, Mali — Residents of northern Mali’s largest city poured out of their homes to celebrate the expulsion of Islamist fighters who had held their town for months, playing the music that had been forbidden under the militants’ harsh interpretation of Islamic rule and dancing in the streets.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/28/world/MALI/MALI-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/28/world/MALI/MALI-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 345}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/28/world/MALI/MALI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 589, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/28/world/MALI/MALI-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1179, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/28/world/MALI/MALI-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/28/world/MALI/MALI-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/28/world/MALI/MALI-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'With Fighters Gone, Malians Welcome Normal Days', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Fighters Gone, Malians Welcome Normal Days', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Polgreen, Lydia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tuareg (Ethnic Group)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mali', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Al Qaeda in the Islamic Maghreb', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mujao (Movement for Oneness and Jihad in West Africa)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Timbuktu (Mali)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-27T14:48:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lydia Polgreen and Peter Tinti', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lydia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Polgreen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tinti', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d7ee95a-a1e7-5766-a99d-3c0cb6b19647', 'word_count': 999, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d7ee95a-a1e7-5766-a99d-3c0cb6b19647'}, {'abstract': 'The right loses its resonance.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/27/from-welfare-queens-to-disabled-deadbeats/', 'snippet': 'The right loses its resonance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you want to understand the trouble Republicans are in, one good place to start is with the obsession the right has lately developed with the rising disability rolls. The growing number of Americans receiving disability payments has, for many on the right, become a symbol of our economic and moral decay; we’re becoming a nation of malingerers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From Welfare Queens to Disabled Deadbeats', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-27T15:06:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6397d882-f1d8-5240-a0be-79961c7ce4c4', 'word_count': 582, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6397d882-f1d8-5240-a0be-79961c7ce4c4'}, {'abstract': 'The company’s offerings have been certified by the Marine Stewardship Council as responsibly harvested.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/27/an-ecolabel-for-mcdonalds-fish-fare/', 'snippet': 'The company’s offerings have been certified by the Marine Stewardship Council as responsibly harvested.', 'lead_paragraph': ' McDonald’s has signed on with the Marine Stewardship Council to show that the fish it serves is caught in an environmentally responsible manner. While the fish is not changing, the deal will make the council’s distinctive blue logo familiar to tens of millions of Americans for the first time.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/28/blogs/msc/msc-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 807, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/28/blogs/msc/msc-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 807}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/28/blogs/msc/msc-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1009, 'width': 750, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/28/blogs/msc/msc-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1009, 'width': 750, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/28/blogs/msc/msc-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/28/blogs/msc/msc-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/28/blogs/msc/msc-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Ecolabel for McDonald’s Fish Fare', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACCREDITATION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fast Food Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish Farming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fishing, Commercial', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labeling and Labels', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pollock (Fish)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "McDonald's Corporation", 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-27T15:35:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Jolly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jolly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1b45ac7-4c9e-57ba-a809-ffd0d9f6f9b0', 'word_count': 744, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1b45ac7-4c9e-57ba-a809-ffd0d9f6f9b0'}, {'abstract': 'Scenes from an intense fire that ripped through a nightclub crowded with university students in southern Brazil early on Sunday morning.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/27/fire-at-a-nightclub-in-southern-brazil/', 'snippet': 'Scenes from an intense fire that ripped through a nightclub crowded with university students in southern Brazil early on Sunday morning.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last Updated, Monday, 3:36 p.m. An intense fire ripped through a nightclub crowded with university students in southern Brazil early on Sunday morning, leaving behind a scene of horror, with bodies piled in the club’s bathrooms and on the street. At least 233 people were killed, many of them students in the agronomy and veterinary medicine programs at a local university, police officials said. By Sunday evening, the authorities had released a preliminary list of the dead.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fire at a Nightclub in Southern Brazil', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bars and Nightclubs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-27T15:56:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Schwirtz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwirtz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/485bfd9a-8d59-5447-a254-f6b56eeea4d7', 'word_count': 499, 'uri': 'nyt://article/485bfd9a-8d59-5447-a254-f6b56eeea4d7'}, {'abstract': 'A journey of just a couple of hundred feet took many more years than expected for a Jewish congregation on the West Side.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/27/at-last-a-new-lincoln-square-synagogue/', 'snippet': 'A journey of just a couple of hundred feet took many more years than expected for a Jewish congregation on the West Side.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Torah scrolls had only 250 feet to travel from the old Lincoln Square Synagogue to the new Lincoln Square Synagogue.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Last, a New Lincoln Square Synagogue', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Eye on Tradition, A Synagogue Opens', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Synagogues', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CetraRuddy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Square', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Square Synagogue', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Upper West Side (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-27T16:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Dunlap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Dunlap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c904368-251b-5ee2-ae34-4bb59a0c1bac', 'word_count': 800, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c904368-251b-5ee2-ae34-4bb59a0c1bac'}, {'abstract': 'To many people who understand computers and the law, there is a danger in lumping people who have not sought financial gain with armed robbers. Where people should receive slaps on the wrist, they face decades in jail.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/27/disruptions-a-fuzzy-and-shifting-line-between-hacker-and-criminal/', 'snippet': 'To many people who understand computers and the law, there is a danger in lumping people who have not sought financial gain with armed robbers. Where people should receive slaps on the wrist, they face decades in jail.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In January 2011, I was assigned to cover a hearing in Newark, where Daniel Spitler, then 26, stood accused of breaching AT&T’s servers and stealing 114,000 e-mail addresses.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/28/technology/28disrupt-web/28disrupt-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 351, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/28/technology/28disrupt-web/28disrupt-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 351}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/28/technology/28disrupt-web/28disrupt-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/28/technology/28disrupt-web/28disrupt-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1198, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/28/technology/28disrupt-web/28disrupt-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/28/technology/28disrupt-web/28disrupt-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/28/technology/28disrupt-web/28disrupt-web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Disruptions: A Fuzzy and Shifting Line Between Hacker and Criminal', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Fuzzy Line Separates Hacker and Criminal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberattacks and Hackers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spitler, Daniel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Swartz, Aaron (1986-2013)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AT&T Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-27T16:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6577e1e5-0f77-5f8d-8faf-94cd4b62bd18', 'word_count': 586, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6577e1e5-0f77-5f8d-8faf-94cd4b62bd18'}, {'abstract': 'Ron Kirk, the United States trade representative, says President Obama is committed to an agreement to smooth trade with the European Union, but only if it can overcome objections from farm groups and win Congressional approval.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/01/27/trade-official-says-u-s-wants-deal-with-europe/', 'snippet': 'Ron Kirk, the United States trade representative, says President Obama is committed to an agreement to smooth trade with the European Union, but only if it can overcome objections from farm groups and win Congressional approval.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DAVOS, Switzerland — America’s top trade negotiator said late on Saturday that President Obama was committed to reaching an agreement to smooth trade with the European Union, but only if it was written in a way that would overcome objections from farm groups and that could win Congressional approval.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trade Official Says U.S. Wants Deal With Europe', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kirk, Ron', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-27T16:15:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Ewing', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ewing', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1eaafe0a-fa50-5108-99da-b1d4b2db0094', 'word_count': 1008, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1eaafe0a-fa50-5108-99da-b1d4b2db0094'}, {'abstract': 'The film, starring Jeremy Renner and Gemma Arterton as the title characters, took in an estimated $19 million at North American movie theaters over the weekend.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/27/hansel-and-gretel-witch-hunters-leads-at-the-box-office/', 'snippet': 'The film, starring Jeremy Renner and Gemma Arterton as the title characters, took in an estimated $19 million at North American movie theaters over the weekend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Armed with machine guns and other over-the-top weaponry, Hansel and Gretel took in an estimated $19 million at North American movie theaters over the weekend — a total that, while strong enough for No. 1, represented far from a fairy-tale finish. Based on prerelease audience surveys, some analysts had predicted that “Hansel and Gretel: Witch Hunters” (featuring Jeremy Renner and Gemma Arterton as the title characters) could take in as much as $30 million.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Hansel and Gretel: Witch Hunters’ Leads at the Box Office', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Hansel and Gretel’ Leads at Box Office', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Arterton, Gemma', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Renner, Jeremy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hollywood.com', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-27T17:50:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25d03d9f-6acc-5b16-9d90-5cca3af904b8', 'word_count': 228, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25d03d9f-6acc-5b16-9d90-5cca3af904b8'}, {'abstract': 'Bill de Blasio, the city’s public advocate, promised to focus on education as well as neighborhood and pocketbook issues that he said had not been addressed by Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/28/nyregion/bill-de-blasio-kicks-off-campaign-for-mayor.html', 'snippet': 'Bill de Blasio, the city’s public advocate, promised to focus on education as well as neighborhood and pocketbook issues that he said had not been addressed by Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pledging to “leave no New Yor