ssional approval.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Reassures an Impatient Europe on Trade', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Reassures an Impatient Europe on Trade', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs (Tariff)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kirk, Ron', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-27T23:14:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Ewing', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ewing', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/317f30e4-abb4-5bbd-aef5-37bb5e406b26', 'word_count': 1087, 'uri': 'nyt://article/317f30e4-abb4-5bbd-aef5-37bb5e406b26'}, {'abstract': '“A Rite” is a collaboration by dancers and actors to celebrate the centenary of Stravinsky’s “Rite of Spring,” at the University of North Carolina, Chapel Hill.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/28/arts/dance/a-rite-riffs-on-stravinsky-at-chapel-hill-nc.html', 'snippet': '“A Rite” is a collaboration by dancers and actors to celebrate the centenary of Stravinsky’s “Rite of Spring,” at the University of North Carolina, Chapel Hill.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHAPEL HILL, N.C. — A hundred years on “The Rite of Spring” has become a popular commodity: not just Stravinsky’s score but the whole idea of its neobarbaric modernism and the myths surrounding its scandalous premiere. Like most dance critics, I’m all too used to seeing stagings of “The Rite” that trivialize its complexity: they coast on its music’s force without investigating its ingredients.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/28/arts/0128ZANE01/0128ZANE01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 321, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/28/arts/0128ZANE01/0128ZANE01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 321}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/28/arts/0128ZANE01/0128ZANE01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 547, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/28/arts/0128ZANE01/0128ZANE01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1095, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/28/arts/0128ZANE01/0128ZANE01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/28/arts/0128ZANE01/0128ZANE01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/28/arts/0128ZANE01/0128ZANE01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bodies and Voices Riff on ‘Rite of Spring’', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_he