rents, victims and the public, brandishing endless litigation and fatuous claims of confidentiality. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Cardinal and the Truth', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Cardinal and the Truth', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mahony, Roger M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Priests', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Curry, Thomas John (1943- )', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-28T02:03:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/8532b982-04bc-5274-879c-2fad4947f330', 'word_count': 354, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8532b982-04bc-5274-879c-2fad4947f330'}, {'abstract': 'New York City’s public hospital system is moving away from cost-of-living increases.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/28/opinion/paying-doctors-for-performance.html', 'snippet': 'New York City’s public hospital system is moving away from cost-of-living increases.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In line with the goals of national health care reform, New York City’s public hospital system has embarked on a radical change in the way it will pay doctors. Instead of granting automatic pay increases, it will pay them based on how well they reduce costs, increase patient satisfaction and improve the quality of care. The Health and Hospitals Corporation, which runs the city’s 11 public hospitals, deserves praise for an ambitious proposal that will need to be refined as it is put into practice. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paying Doctors for Performance', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Paying Doctors for Performance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Health and Hospitals Corp', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-28T02:05:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/5aa0ce40-02cd-57af-960c-ca0cdcf84c06', 'word_count': 441, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5aa0ce40-02cd-57af-960c-ca0cdcf84c06'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Andrew Cuomo should keep pressing for statewide standards on false confessions and witness misidentification.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/28/opinion/mr-cuomos-plan-on-wrongful-convictions.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Andrew Cuomo should keep pressing for statewide standards on false confessions and witness misidentification.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Andrew Cuomo negotiated a package of criminal justice changes with the Legislature last winter that broadly expanded New York State’s DNA database by requiring all convicts to submit a DNA sample. Disappointingly, the measure did not include other important fixes that would further strengthen law enforcement’s ability to exonerate the innocent and convict the guilty. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mr. Cuomo’s Plan on Wrongful Convictions', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mr. Cuomo’s Plan on Wrongful Convictions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'False Arrests, Convictions and Imprisonments', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-28T02:07:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a07e15d6-eb33-5da9-b653-84d311bb25b0', 'word_count': 251, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a07e15d6-eb33-5da9-b653-84d311bb25b0'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama’s elevating inaugural message on gay rights needs legal follow-through.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/28/opinion/beyond-mr-obamas-inaugural-message-on-gay-rights.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama’s elevating inaugural message on gay rights needs legal follow-through.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By including gay rights in the arc of the struggle for civil rights — the road “through Seneca Falls and Selma and Stonewall” — President Obama linked his presidency to ending antigay discrimination and underscored the legal wrong of denying gay people the freedom to marry.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multi