creasingly absurd and aggressive laws?', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/28/is-moscow-setting-the-russian-oppositions-agenda/', 'snippet': 'Has Putin’s regime hijacked the Russian opposition’s agenda by provoking it to protest increasingly absurd and aggressive laws?', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — After a ghastly week during which gay activists faced violence in the streets of Moscow and Voronezh and Parliament voted for a law banning “homosexual propaganda,” I was surprised to hear a sudden chorus of pro-opposition voices calling on the Russian opposition to stop paying attention to the homophobic law in particular and other new repressive Russian laws in general.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Diversionary Politics', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Assembly', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-28T13:40:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Masha Gessen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Masha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gessen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e06da67e-e5a1-5cd6-a5d1-23d81d9a4b89', 'word_count': 429, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e06da67e-e5a1-5cd6-a5d1-23d81d9a4b89'}, {'abstract': 'Iceland won a landmark court case on Monday over its refusal to immediately cover the losses of British and Dutch depositors who lost money in Icesave, a failed Icelandic bank.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/01/28/iceland-wins-major-case-over-failed-bank/', 'snippet': 'Iceland won a landmark court case on Monday over its refusal to immediately cover the losses of British and Dutch depositors who lost money in Icesave, a failed Icelandic bank.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRUSSELS — Iceland won a landmark case at a European court, ending an acrimonious legacy from the collapse of its banking system more than four years ago.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iceland Wins Major Case Over Failed Bank', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iceland Wins a European Court Victory in a Banking Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Landsbanki', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iceland', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Netherlands', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-28T13:50:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Higgins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Higgins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/880253bd-ad3e-5f68-871d-cdef7ee2d87c', 'word_count': 743, 'uri': 'nyt://article/880253bd-ad3e-5f68-871d-cdef7ee2d87c'}, {'abstract': 'Baghramian brings “Retainer,” a system of sculptures, to one of New York City’s oldest artist-founded institutions.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/28/nairy-baghramian-at-sculpturecenter/', 'snippet': 'Baghramian brings “Retainer,” a system of sculptures, to one of New York City’s oldest artist-founded institutions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Located in a Maya Lin-rehabbed former trolley repair shop around the corner from MoMA PS1 in Long Island City, Queens, SculptureCenter is one of New York City’s oldest artist-founded institutions at 85 years of age. The main gallery is a towering, slightly dilapidated room, and taking residence there this winter is “Retainer,” a sculpture by the Iranian-born, Berlin-based artist Nairy Baghramian. This commission is her first exhibition in the United States, though in Europe she’s well known for her manually and mechanically manipulated forms that are by turns delicate and inscrutable.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nairy Baghramian at SculptureCenter', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sculpture', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SculptureCenter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island City (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-28T14:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin McGarry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGarry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/847c1892-3b1f-57d3-8d05-36f1ba881972', 'word_count': 479, 'uri': 'nyt://article/847c1892-3b1f-57d3-8d05-36f1ba881972'}, {'abstract': 'In an effort to raise awareness, the former Saint Steve Gleason and N.F.L. players and coaches will unveil a public service announcement explaining the gradual physical failure that results from the disease.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/28/in-starkest-terms-players-share-message-about-a-l-s/', 'snippet': 'In an effort to raise awareness, the former Saint Steve Gleason and N.F.L. players and coaches will unveil a public service announcement explaining the gradual physical failure that results from the disease.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW ORLEANS — Outside the Superdome is a statue depicting one of the seminal moments in the history of the Saints and this revived city. Named “Rebirth,” the statue shows the moment the former Saints player Steve Gleason blocked a punt in the Saints’ first game back in the Superdome in 2006, the first game they played in New Orleans after Hurricane Katrina. That blocked punt led to the first score in the Saints’ victory over the Atlanta Falcons that night.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Starkest Terms, Players Share Message About A.L.S.', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AMYOTROPHIC LATERAL SCLEROSIS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Orleans Saints', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-28T14:00:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judy Battista', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Battista', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ebbb769-8fad-5781-b070-2b9e36929081', 'word_count': 474, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ebbb769-8fad-5781-b070-2b9e36929081'}, {'abstract': 'The Hess Corporation plans to sell 19 fuel terminals as part of a plan to refocus on higher-growth exploration and production. It also disclosed having received a letter from the hedge fund Elliott Management, which is seeking a big stake in Hess and a potential board fight.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/01/28/hess-weighs-sale-of-terminal-network/', 'snippet': 'The Hess Corporation plans to sell 19 fuel terminals as part of a plan to refocus on higher-growth exploration and production. It also disclosed having received a letter from the hedge fund Elliott Management, which is seeking a big stake in Hess ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Hess Corporation said on Monday that it planned to sell its network of terminals, as the oil company began to focus on finding and producing new sources of petroleum.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hess Weighs Sale of Terminal Network', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hedge Funds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refineries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Elliott Management Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hess Corporation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-28T14:14:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5156a51-46f9-58df-a21e-0dbbd