: 'nyt://article/a4d40b9d-eea6-5006-aa32-bbf76b012335'}, {'abstract': 'Union ranks are down over all, but they have risen in California, and among Latinos and Asian-Americans.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/28/labor-sees-bright-spots-in-membership-trends/', 'snippet': 'Union ranks are down over all, but they have risen in California, and among Latinos and Asian-Americans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The American labor movement received some bitter news last week when the Bureau of Labor Statistics released its annual report on union membership – it showed a 398,000 overall decline in union membership, with the percentage of workers in unions dropping to 11.3 percent, the lowest rate in nearly a century. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Labor Sees Bright Spots in Membership Trends', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bureau of Labor Statistics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-28T15:51:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Greenhouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenhouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36a4002f-44fa-5f41-9877-917bf3aa3664', 'word_count': 886, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36a4002f-44fa-5f41-9877-917bf3aa3664'}, {'abstract': 'An employer of more than 100 people, this owner finds dealing with the question of raises a constant challenge, one fraught with more negatives than positives.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/28/trying-to-answer-the-inevitable-question-can-i-have-a-raise/', 'snippet': 'An employer of more than 100 people, this owner finds dealing with the question of raises a constant challenge, one fraught with more negatives than positives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On an almost weekly basis, someone on my team of employees walks into my office and asks for a raise. It doesn’t seem to matter that we have a clearly communicated policy, and the question often comes with the same assertion — these employees believe they are worth more to the organization than they are being paid. Or perhaps, these employees point out, they work in one of the company’s more profitable business units. The list of potential reasons is quite long.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trying to Answer the Inevitable Question: Can I Have a Raise?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TerraCycle', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-28T16:00:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Szaky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Szaky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f3ebc5f1-4551-59fa-b9bc-68cedbd4dfed', 'word_count': 695, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f3ebc5f1-4551-59fa-b9bc-68cedbd4dfed'}, {'abstract': 'Financial planner Carl Richards explains through a sketch that the 2012 economy was better than it felt.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/vi