s network, called SportsNetLA, in a deal with Time Warner Cable that is worth $7 billion to $8 billion.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/28/dodgers-signing-lucrative-tv-deal-plan-to-start-regional-sports-network/', 'snippet': 'The baseball team said it would start its own sports network, called SportsNetLA, in a deal with Time Warner Cable that is worth $7 billion to $8 billion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The owners of the Los Angeles Dodgers said Monday that they intended to start a regional sports network in southern California, confirming weeks of reports about the team’s plans.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dodgers, Signing Lucrative TV Deal, Plan to Start Regional Sports Network', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox Sports', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Dodgers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Time Warner Cable Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-28T16:04:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/17f85004-0057-5d9a-90aa-5f16ad58f598', 'word_count': 652, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17f85004-0057-5d9a-90aa-5f16ad58f598'}, {'abstract': 'Juan-Pablo Montoya takes the checkered flag in the Rolex 24 Hours of Daytona.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/28/monday-motorsports-close-finish-caps-wild-24-hour-race-at-daytona/', 'snippet': 'Juan-Pablo Montoya takes the checkered flag in the Rolex 24 Hours of Daytona.', 'lead_paragraph': '2:06 p.m. | Updated A margin of just 22 seconds, after racing twice around the clock, decided the season-opening Rolex 24 Hours of Daytona race.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Monday Motorsports: Close Finish Caps Wild 24-Hour Race at Daytona', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nascar Sprint Cup Series', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Allmendinger, A J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ambrose, Marcos', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bowyer, Clint', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ecclestone, Bernie', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ganassi, Chip', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hunter-Reay, Ryan', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Montoya, Juan Pablo', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Patrick, Danica', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pruett, Scott', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stenhouse, Ricky Jr', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bayerische Motorenwerke AG', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Formula One', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sochi (Russia)', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-28T16:05:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jerry Garrett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jerry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garrett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc9d39f5-b928-572d-b0f3-7895c97f3060', 'word_count': 600, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc9d39f5-b928-572d-b0f3-7895c97f3060'}, {'abstract': 'Japan’s move to ease restrictions on American beef imports will allow ranchers and meatpackers to move past a mad cow scare that led to a ban in 2003, and regain full access to what was once their most lucrative market.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/29/business/global/japan-to-ease-restrictions-on-us-beef.html', 'snippet': 'Japan’s move to ease restrictions on American beef imports will allow ranchers and meatpackers to move past a mad cow scare that led to a ban in 2003, and regain full access to what was once their most lucrative market.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Reflecting diminishing fears over mad cow disease, Japan eased its decade-old restriction on imports of American beef on Monday, but industry experts said beef producers faced many more challenges to reverse a prolonged slump that has pared the nation’s herd to its lowest level in 60 years and sent prices soaring.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/29/business/29beef1/29beef1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 384, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/29/business/29beef1/29beef1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 384}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/29/business/29beef1/29beef1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'sup