e winning book was inspired by a real-life tale of a gorilla who thrives after being moved from a small cage to a zoo.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The One and Only Ivan,” the story of a silverback gorilla who makes a new life for himself after being moved from a tiny cage in a mall to a zoo, won the John Newbery Medal on Monday for the year’s outstanding contribution to children’s literature.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tale of Gorilla’s Renewed Life Wins Newbery Award', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Newbery Medal Honors A Tale Told By a Gorilla', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Caldecott Medal', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Libraries and Librarians', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newbery Medal', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Applegate, Katherine', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Caldecott, Randolph', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grant, Michael', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN LIBRARY ASSN', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-28T18:08:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Leslie Kaufman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Leslie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaufman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a776888-71e3-54a0-aa27-bacc1948f404', 'word_count': 634, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a776888-71e3-54a0-aa27-bacc1948f404'}, {'abstract': 'Dante de Blasio’s Afro became the talk of Twitter after he appeared at the news conference of Bill de Blasio, who was saying he was running for mayor.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/28/de-blasios-announcement-is-upstaged-by-sons-hair/', 'snippet': 'Dante de Blasio’s Afro became the talk of Twitter after he appeared at the news conference of Bill de Blasio, who was saying he was running for mayor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 1:52 p.m. | The city’s public advocate, Bill de Blasio, threw his hat in the ring for mayor on Sunday. Rather than go the usual route of announcing his candidacy at City Hall, Mr. de Blasio, who has cast himself as a champion of the forgotten, held a news conference in front of his house in Park Slope, Brooklyn, accompanied by his wife, who introduced him as an “outer-borough working dad,” and their teenage son, who also gave a speech.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/29/nyregion/cityroom-diblasio/cityroom-diblasio-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/29/nyregion/cityroom-diblasio/cityroom-diblasio-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/29/nyregion/cityroom-diblasio/cityroom-diblasio-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/29/nyregion/cityroom-diblasio/cityroom-diblasio-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/29/nyregion/cityroom-diblasio/cityroom-diblasio-thumbS