what kills it off.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/28/safety-fines-continue-to-be-hot-topics/', 'snippet': 'While President Obama expressed doubts that he would let a son play football over concerns about how safe the game is, Bernard Pollard of the Ravens believes making the game safer may be what kills it off.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW ORLEANS — The news media covering the Super Bowl are often criticized for the lack of attention paid to the actual game of football. But as the Baltimore Ravens and the San Francisco 49ers get ready to play in Super Bowl XLVII, the talk has largely been about the game on the field, and how dangerous it can be.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/29/sports/football/29pollard/29pollard-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 388, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/29/sports/football/29pollard/29pollard-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 388}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/29/sports/football/29pollard/29pollard-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 663, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/29/sports/football/29pollard/29pollard-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1325, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/29/sports/football/29pollard/29pollard-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/29/sports/football/29pollard/29pollard-thumbStandard.jp