pet': 'Tommy Lee Jones’s SAG win gives him a leg up in the Oscar race for best supporting actor, but one observer says Phillip Seymour Hoffman is the most deserving. What do you think?', 'lead_paragraph': 'With his victory at the Screen Actors Guild, Tommy Lee Jones may have edged a little closer to an Oscar victory for best supporting actor. But the category is chock full of strong candidates, all of them previous Oscar winners. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Whom Would You Pick for Supporting Actor?', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hoffman, Philip Seymour', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Tommy Lee', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Waltz, Christoph', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fandor.com', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-28T20:00:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d52362ed-c438-53d2-8f78-d338d703eb00', 'word_count': 174, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d52362ed-c438-53d2-8f78-d338d703eb00'}, {'abstract': 'Teddy Wayne’s new novel, “The Love Song of Jonny Valentine,” follows the rising stardom, and daily pressures, of a young heartthrob right out of the Justin Bieber mold.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/29/books/the-love-song-of-jonny-valentine-by-teddy-wayne.html', 'snippet': 'Teddy Wayne’s new novel, “The Love Song of Jonny Valentine,” follows the rising stardom, and daily pressures, of a young heartthrob right out of the Justin Bieber mold.', 'lead_paragraph': '“An old soul is the last thing you would expect to find inside Justin Bieber,” an old entry on his Web site says. “But all it takes is one listen to the 15-year-old soul-singing phenomenon to realize that he is light years ahead of his manufactured pop peers.” Mr. Bieber, now 18 and as big a pop star as ever, is the model for the 11-year-old with an old soul in Teddy Wayne’s sad-funny, sometimes cutting new novel, “The Love Song of Jonny Valentine.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/29/arts/BOOK/BOOK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 986, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/29/arts/BOOK/BOOK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 986}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/29/arts/BOOK/BOOK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 624, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/29/arts/BOOK/BOOK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1247, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/29/arts/BOOK/BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/29/arts/BOOK/BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/29/arts/BOOK/BOOK-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'He’s Got Voice, Looks and Fans. And He’s 11.', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'He’s Got Voice, Looks And Fans. And He’s 11.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wayne, Teddy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-28T20:14:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michiko Kakutani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michiko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kakutani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f14abd2f-eb7d-5ca4-b325-826537502ea6', 'word_count': 1138, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f14abd2f-eb7d-5ca4-b325-826537502ea6'}, {'abstract': 'The announcement appeared to signal that the administration does not currently see the closing of the Guantánamo Bay prison as a realistic priority.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/29/us/politics/state-dept-closes-office-working-on-closing-guantanamo-prison.html', 'snippet': 'The announcement appeared to signal that the administration does not currently see the closing of the Guantánamo Bay prison as a realistic priority.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FORT MEADE, Md. — The State Department on Monday reassigned Daniel Fried, the special envoy for closing the prison at Guantánamo Bay, Cuba, and will not replace him, according to an internal personnel announcement. Mr. Fried’s office is being closed, and his former responsibilities will be “assumed” by the office of the department’s legal adviser, the notice said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Office Working to Close Guantánamo Is Shuttered', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Office Working to Close Guantánamo Is Shuttered', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Savage, Charlie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fried, Daniel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guantanamo Bay Naval Base (Cuba)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Military Tribunals', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-28T20:16:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/22435cf3-764b-5ca7-98e3-6baecbb73260', 'word_count': 860, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22435cf3-764b-5ca7-98e3-6baecbb73260'}, {'abstract': 'Why immigration reform will almost certainly hurt the G.O.P. politically.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/28/immigration-and-republican-self-interest/', 'snippet': 'Why immigration reform will almost certainly hurt the G.O.P. politically.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here is Ezra Klein, explaining why Republican are suddenly looking more, shall we say, transigent on immigration than they’ve been on taxes:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Immigration and Republican Self-Interest', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rubio, Marco', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-28T20:19:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/21613dbf-7707-5dca-98c8-91632ed07029', 'word_count': 843, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21613dbf-7707-5dca-98c8-91632ed07029'}, {'abstract': 'The American team drilled through a half-mile of ice to reach Lake Whillans, and retrieved water samples, according to the project’s Web site.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/29/science/american-team-reports-drilling-through-to-antarctic-lake.html', 'snippet': 'The American team drilled through a half-mile of ice to reach Lake Whillans, and retrieved water samples, according to the project’s Web site.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An American research team finished drilling through a half-mile of Antarctic ice on Monday, reaching the surface of subglacial Lake Whillans and retrieving water samples that will be studied for the presence of life, according to the team’s Web site.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Team Drills Through to Antarctic Lake', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Environment: U.S. Team Drills Through to Antarctic Lake', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ANTARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gorman, James', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lakes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ice', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Microbiology', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-28T20:30:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Gorman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gorman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/101ee924-c68f-52e1-a6b1-062028179235', 'word_count': 215, 'uri': 'nyt://article/101ee924-c68f-52e1-a6b1-062028179235'}, {'abstract': 'The new centerpiece of the Culinary Institute of America features white-oak walls, avant-garde lighting fixtures and ice cream hand-cranked tableside.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/28/starter-at-bocuse-recreating-the-classics/', 'snippet': 'The new centerpiece of the Culinary Institute of America features white-oak walls, avant-garde lighting fixtures and ice cream hand-cranked tableside.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Starter, an occasional column, takes a look at newly opened restaurants.Weather was hardly a deterrent to the diners. Though a deep freeze lingered Saturday night, customers eagerly fled the windy 19-degree temperature for the warmth and welcome of the new $3 million Bocuse Restaurant at the Culinary Institute of America in Hyde Park, N.Y.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Starter: At Bocuse, Recreating the Classics', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Classroom for New Classics', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bocuse Restaurant (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Culinary Institute of America', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Escoffier Restaurant (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-28T20:35:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Glenn Collins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Glenn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/654f7f3b-ebc9-5ccc-a37f-17bcf84fe5ed', 'word_count': 722, 'uri': 'nyt://article/654f7f3b-ebc9-5ccc-a37f-17bcf84fe5ed'}, {'abstract': 'The youth organization may lift its ban on gay members.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/28/boy-scouts-join-the-present/', 'snippet': 'The youth organization may lift its ban on gay members.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last July, the Boy Scouts of America were the target of richly deserved outrage when they announced that after two-years of soul searching, they had decided not to change their policy banning gay members and gay Scout leaders. The Supreme Court had said it was their right to do that — but what kind of post-19th century discussion could have led to that nonsensical decision? When President Obama publicly disagreed with the B.S.A.’s decision, the Scouts waved off his objections and said they would not reconsider.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Boy Scouts Join the Present', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boy Scouts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-28T20:36:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c87e929-29c3-5c92-8e9a-93a2fe921314', 'word_count': 482, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c87e929-29c3-5c92-8e9a-93a2fe921314'}, {'abstract': 'Under a new proposed policy, the Boy Scouts of America would allow local scouting groups to choose whether to allow gay members.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/29/us/boy-scouts-consider-lifting-ban-on-gay-leaders.html', 'snippet': 'Under a new proposed policy, the Boy Scouts of America would allow local scouting groups to choose whether to allow gay members.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Boy Scouts of America, with its traditions of youth in uniform and the character-building virtues of honor, has always looked back to an older, more structured image of America, when gay and lesbian people were invisible and silent. It was a view reaffirmed in Scout policy as recently as seven months ago. Openly gay scouts and scout leaders need not apply.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In a Quick Shift, Scouts Rethink a Ban on Gays', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Scouts Rethink A Ban on Gays In a Quick Shift', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Kirk', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boy Scouts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-28T20:38:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kirk Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kirk', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'repor