g is promoted before peer review.', 'lead_paragraph': ' | Updates below |Last year, after opponents of hydraulic fracturing made much of an unpublished paper by a doctoral candidate in economics who reported finding health impacts in infants from nearby gas drilling operations, I wrote a piece titled “When Publicity Precedes Peer Review in the Fight Over Gas Impacts.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Publicity Precedes Peer Review in Climate Science (Part One)', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academic and Scientific Journals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Relations and Publicity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Norway', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-28T20:56:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d46354b0-fa8b-59be-892d-64d89cf6b1d8', 'word_count': 1384, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d46354b0-fa8b-59be-892d-64d89cf6b1d8'}, {'abstract': 'A new restaurant by chef James Henry champions quality in-season ingredients, coupled with handmade in-house items such as bread, butter and charcuterie.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/28/table-talk-bones-in-paris/', 'snippet': 'A new restaurant by chef James Henry champions quality in-season ingredients, coupled with handmade in-house items such as bread, butter and charcuterie.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was at the helm of the much-acclaimed Au Passage restaurant that James Henry first made ripples in the Paris food scene. His delectable small plates were so well received that he decided to venture on his own. The result is Bones, which Henry unveiled earlier this month. The décor is spare with overhanging industrial light fixtures being the prominent design feature. The interior (an Irish pub in its former life) was deconstructed so that only the raw framework of bricks, wood and tiles remain — hence the skeletal name, Bones.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Table Talk | Bones in Paris', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-28T20:58:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Moroz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moroz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7705980a-4d28-54d4-bfbb-a9f79b8070b7', 'word_count': 337, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7705980a-4d28-54d4-bfbb-a9f79b8070b7'}, {'abstract': 'Ina Jang, the photographer behind our cover article on victims of child pornography, reveals the process behind her work.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/28/opening-a-sketchbook-and-finding-a-spark/', 'snippet': 'Ina Jang, the photographer behind our cover article on victims of child pornography, reveals the process behind her work.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit':