e', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Breastfeeding', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-28T21:09:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/582cc8e2-0e0c-5ebf-8ef9-23d40506f5d7', 'word_count': 911, 'uri': 'nyt://article/582cc8e2-0e0c-5ebf-8ef9-23d40506f5d7'}, {'abstract': 'The extraction of the substance from their gall bladders on makeshift farms causes deep suffering. And some bears’ organs are harvested through poaching.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/28/market-for-bear-bile-threatens-asian-population/', 'snippet': 'The extraction of the substance from their gall bladders on makeshift farms causes deep suffering. And some bears’ organs are harvested through poaching.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The six bears that arrived this month at Animals Asia, an animal rescue center in China, had the grisly symptoms of inhumane bile milking. Greenish bile dripped from open fistulas used to drain gall bladders; teeth were broken and rotted from gnawing on the bars of tiny cages. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Market for Bear Bile Threatens Asian Population', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMALS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bears', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bladder', 'rank