Instead of using powdered chile for a nacho recipe, think about using whole dried chiles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Making short ribs chili nachos is the subject of this week’s column and video, and I mention that the chili part of the dish was inspired by a recipe I learned from my friend Nick. Nick’s chili is an extremely complexly flavored dish because instead of chile powder, he uses a combination of whole dried chiles.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Toasted Chiles Add Complexity to a Dish', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chili (Food)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-28T21:12:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d5dade8-7510-50e7-a24e-66f57f94d7b9', 'word_count': 224, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d5dade8-7510-50e7-a24e-66f57f94d7b9'}, {'abstract': 'Most of the current 49ers are too young to have experienced the dominant San Francisco teams of the 1980s and ’90s.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/28/san-francisco-players-carry-on-legacy-they-know-little-about/', 'snippet': 'Most of the current 49ers are too young to have experienced the dominant San Francisco teams of the 1980s and ’90s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW ORLEANS — The San Francisco 49ers last won a Super Bowl on Jan. 29, 1995. Colin Kaepernick, the team’s current starting quarterback, was 7. The team may have five Super Bowl wins, but Joe Looney, San Francisco’s youngest player, was alive for just one of them. The same is true for three other members of the active roster.', 'print_sect