undreds of information requests from United States government agencies last year, and most came without search warrants to establish probable cause.', 'lead_paragraph': 'United States law-enforcement agencies by and large do not establish probable cause or obtain a search warrant from an impartial judge before they seek information about a Twitter user, the company said Monday in its second transparency report.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Law Enforcement Rarely Uses Search Warrants in Getting Twitter Data', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-28T22:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Somini Sengupta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Somini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sengupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3ab70e9-da2b-5ace-8d53-a9cef3f8c010', 'word_count': 294, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3ab70e9-da2b-5ace-8d53-a9cef3f8c010'}, {'abstract': 'What to drink with heavy beef nachos at that Super Bowl party? Eric Asimov tells you.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/28/a-rich-generous-wine-to-pair-with-short-rib-nachos/', 'snippet': 'What to drink with heavy beef nachos at that Super Bowl party? Eric Asimov tells you.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Melissa Clark shares her recipe for short rib chile nachos in her column, A Good Appetite, to prepare for the Super Bowl. Here are some thoughts on what to drink with them; share your suggestions in the comments section below.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Rich, Generous Wine to Pair With Short Rib Nachos', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_he