-583c-b4bf-6cbf1421a308'}, {'abstract': 'Queen Beatrix announced Monday that she would abdicate on April 30 after serving as the Netherlands’ head of state for 33 years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/29/world/europe/queen-beatrix-of-the-netherlands-says-she-will-step-down.html', 'snippet': 'Queen Beatrix announced Monday that she would abdicate on April 30 after serving as the Netherlands’ head of state for 33 years.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Queen Beatrix announced Monday that she would abdicate on April 30 after serving as the Netherlands’ head of state for 33 years. Her eldest son, Prince Willem-Alexander, 45, will succeed her in the largely ceremonial role. In a speech broadcast on Dutch state television, the queen said it was time for a new generation to take on the responsibility of leading the country. Prime Minister Mark Rutte thanked the queen, left, for her service, calling her “an icon.” Mr. Rutte added that Queen Beatrix, who turns 75 on Thursday, had “applied herself heart and soul for Dutch society,” according to The Associated Press. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Netherlands: Queen Says She Will Step Down', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Netherlands: Queen Says She Will Step Down', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beatrix, Queen of the Netherlands', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Netherlands', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Willem-Alexander, Prince', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-29T01:54:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Erdbrink', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erdbrink', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/f3b96996-c4ad-5972-9860-74d7f83ef191', 'word_count': 103, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f3b96996-c4ad-5972-9860-74d7f83ef191'}, {'abstract': 'House Republicans should stop playing ideological games and reach agreement with the Senate on extending a lifesaving law.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/29/opinion/violence-against-women-act-is-reintroduced.html', 'snippet': 'House Republicans should stop playing ideological games and reach agreement with the Senate on extending a lifesaving law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Turning to a critical piece of unfinished business, Patrick Leahy, the Democratic chairman of the Senate Judiciary Committee, joined last week with a Republican colleague, Michael Crapo of Idaho, to reintroduce legislation to reauthorize the Violence Against Women Act, the 1994 law central to the nation’s efforts to fight domestic violence, sexual assault and stalking. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Push on Domestic Violence', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A New Push on Domestic Violence', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Domestic Violence', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Visas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-29T01:56:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/76dacfff-2450-5f70-8f40-5b1310efc4a0', 'word_count': 351, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76dacfff-2450-5f70-8f40-5b1310efc4a0'}, {'abstract': 'A small sampling of news articles from around the country gives a sense of the Second Amendment’s toll.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/29/opinion/nocera-and-in-last-weeks-gun-news.html', 'snippet': 'A small sampling of news articles from around the country gives a sense of the Second Amendment’s toll.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Monday, Jan. 21:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbLarge-v4.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'And in Last Week’s Gun News ...', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'And in Last Week’s Gun News ...', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-29T01:57:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Nocera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nocera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a55a1ab-3641-581c-848d-ef8c4f96e52a', 'word_count': 729, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a55a1ab-3641-581c-848d-ef8c4f96e52a'}, {'abstract': 'Why the new film version of ‘Les Misérables’ has so upset the critics.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/28/les-miserables-and-irony/', 'snippet': 'Why the new film version of ‘Les Misérables’ has so upset the critics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I may have missed it, but I don’t recall USA Today devoting a full one and three-quarters pages to a movie, never mind a movie that’s been out for some time now. But there in the Life section of the Weekend edition was a lengthy discussion of “Les Misérables,” or, more precisely, a discussion of the furiously negative responses the musical epic has evoked from a gaggle of critics who simultaneously trash the film and express an incredulity verging on outrage at fellow moviegoers who don’t share their view. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Les Misérables’ and Irony', 'kicker': 'Stanley Fish', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hooper, Tom', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rothko, Mark', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wallace, David Foster', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-29T02:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stanley Fish', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stanley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fish', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5be0b73b-c85c-553a-81e9-b59f6288c56f', 'word_count': 1271, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5be0b73b-c85c-553a-81e9-b59f6288c56f'}, {'abstract': 'A translator learns that the law of karma can be unforgiving.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/28/the-treachery-of-translators/', 'snippet': 'A translator learns that the law of karma can be unforgiving.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The fact is, there were always going to be a lot of fish in “Vingt mille lieues sous les mers.” When a publishing house commissioned me to produce a new translation of Jules Verne’s 19th-century underwater epic, I was confident of bringing a degree of joyous panache to the story of Captain Nemo, his submarine, the Nautilus and that giant killer squid. But I had forgotten about its systematic taxonomy of all the inhabitants of the seven seas. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Treachery of Translators', 'kicker': 'Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Translation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-29T02:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6cb40bfc-cf56-52b2-ae01-b800de8678e0', 'word_count': 1136, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6cb40bfc-cf56-52b2-ae01-b800de8678e0'}, {'abstract': 'Tiger Woods, who won his PGA Tour season debut for the first time since 2008, stands seven victories short of tying Sam Snead’s career record after winning the Farmers Insurance Open in San Diego.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/29/sports/golf/tiger-woods-wins-75th-career-title-8th-at-torrey-pines.html', 'snippet': 'Tiger Woods, who won his PGA Tour season debut for the first time since 2008, stands seven victories short of tying Sam Snead’s career record after winning the Farmers Insurance Open in San Diego.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN DIEGO — There is a shop in the village of La Jolla, Second Act West, where people flock to find vintage clothing. Seven miles away, Tiger Woods rooted around in the past on Monday and dug up his designer game from a few years back, turning Torrey Pines into his second act, west.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/29/sports/subGOLFfloater/subGOLFfloater-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/29/sports/subGOLFfloater/subGOLFfloater-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/29/sports/subGOLFfloater/subGOLFfloater-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/29/sports/subGOLFfloater/subGOLFfloater-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width':