abstract': 'President Lee Myung-bak on Tuesday granted special pardons to a longtime friend, political allies and dozens of others convicted of corruption and other crimes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/30/world/asia/outgoing-south-korean-leader-creates-furor-with-pardons.html', 'snippet': 'President Lee Myung-bak on Tuesday granted special pardons to a longtime friend, political allies and dozens of others convicted of corruption and other crimes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — With less than one month left in office, the departing president of South Korea, Lee Myung-bak, granted special pardons on Tuesday to political allies, a longtime friend and dozens of others who have been convicted of corruption and other crimes. The pardons ignited a rare quarrel between him and the president-elect.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Departing South Korean Leader Creates Furor With Pardons', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'South Korea: President Is Assailed\r\nBy Successor for Granting Pardons', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee Myung-bak', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Amnesties, Commutations and Pardons', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Saenuri Party (South Korea)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic United Party (South Korea)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Park Geun-hye', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-29T09:12:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Choe Sang-Hun', 'person': [{'firstname'