agraph': 'New York: It’s the season for parsley root — that herby, aromatic old-world veggie – in soups and stews. So here’s a recipe for couscous tabbouleh with parsley root from Hugue Dufour of M. Wells Dinette. – Glenn Collins ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-29T15:05:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b04c0161-e12e-5769-b61a-79644887e30d', 'word_count': 406, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b04c0161-e12e-5769-b61a-79644887e30d'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Poehler, the “Saturday Night Live” alumna and star of “Parks and Recreation,” is writing a memoir in the form of “an illustrated, nonlinear diary” for the It Books imprint of HarperCollins.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/29/treat-yourself-to-a-new-book-by-amy-poehler/', 'snippet': 'Ms. Poehler, the “Saturday Night Live” alumna and star of “Parks and Recreation,” is writing a memoir in the form of “an illustrated, nonlinear diary” for the It Books imprint of HarperCollins.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When she’s not helping to govern the fictional city of Pawnee, Ind., or presiding over the Golden Globes ceremony with her pal Tina Fey, Amy Poehler, it seems, harbors literary aspirations: dreams that will be fulfilled in a new memoir she is writing for the It Books imprint of HarperCollins.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/29/arts/poehler/poehler-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 316, 'width': 467, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'r