advice to communicators aiming to engage the public on climate science.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first 15 years or so of my coverage of the greenhouse effect and global warming focused on geophysical and environmental questions, along with energy and forest policy. Around 2005 I started paying more attention to the internal climate — meaning, how human perception, or misperception, of climate science and environmental risk influences the decisions, or indecision, of individuals and societies in the face of climate change.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Other Voices: Can Climate Science Communication Matter?', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-29T15:39:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ddc5585b-2df0-592a-82b8-5cb6760c4b7f', 'word_count': 855, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ddc5585b-2df0-592a-82b8-5cb6760c4b7f'}, {'abstract': 'Violins.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2013/01/29/booming/29booming-strav.html', 'snippet': 'Violins.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Violins.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ms. Buechner performs \r\nStravinsky, Petroushka', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-29T15:39:17+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Booming', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/1f5a88cc-7c8f-596c-ad01-3ca29d352d12', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/1f5a88cc-7c8f-596c-ad01-3ca29d352d12'}, {'abstract': 'Ray LaHood, the former Republican congressman who has run the nation’s Transportation Department under President Obama, will not serve a second term, he told department employees in a letter on Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/29/lahood-to-leave-transportation-department/', 'snippet': 'Ray LaHood, the former Republican congressman who has run the nation’s Transportation Department under President Obama, will not serve a second term, he told department employees in a letter on Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ray LaHood, the former Republican congressman from Illinois who has run the nation’s Transportation Department under President Obama, will not serve a second term, he told department employees in a letter on Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'LaHood to Leave Transportation Department', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Transportation Secretary Is Stepping Down', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transportation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'LaHood, Ray', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transportation Department (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-29T15:42:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/76fca40c-f29f-57b1-9783-b8de845b2d55', 'word_count': 337, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76fca40c-f29f-57b1-9783-b8de845b2d55'}, {'abstract': 'The story of an American Girl doll on loan at a New York library branch elicited many offers, though library officials said they were so overwhelmed that they could not accept doll donations.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/29/at-a-library-an-outpouring-of-support-and-new-dolls/', 'snippet': 'The story of an American Girl doll on loan at a New York library branch elicited many offers, though library officials said they were so overwhelmed that they could not accept doll donations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thea Taube — much like the Ottendorfer library’s suddenly famous doll mascot — has been inundated with such an outpouring of love and appreciation lately that she is nearly coming apart at the seams.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At a Library, an Outpouring of Support, and New Dolls', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dolls', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Libraries and Librarians', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Girl Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Public Library', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Village (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-29T15:45:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Corey Kilgannon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Corey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kilgannon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/64f6dc8a-3e62-57c0-81f6-74c95c3124f1', 'word_count': 732, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64f6dc8a-3e62-57c0-81f6-74c95c3124f1'}, {'abstract': 'N.F.L. players and coaches walk the tightrope of hearing about the dangers of their sport and pretending they are not there.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/30/sports/in-discussion-of-sports-violence-players-keep-quiet-leading-off.html', 'snippet': 'N.F.L. players and coaches walk the tightrope of hearing about the dangers of their sport and pretending they are not there.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The players who have gathered in New Orleans for the Super Bowl took an array of talents with them — passing, running, chasing down quarterbacks — but little did they know that their most useful talent in the week leading up to the big game would be tightrope walking. Denial has come in handy, too. Head-faking the big issue in the room? Invaluable.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/30/sports/football/30leading-1/30leading-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/30/sports/football/30leading-1/30leading-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/30/sports/football/30leading-1/30leading-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/30/sports/football/30leading-1/30leading-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo',