 want a law against domestic violence, they also want to know exactly what’s going into it, in a new push for accountability from their opaque government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — Li Yan, a woman from Sichuan Province who was convicted of killing her abusive husband, faces execution. As activists in China fight to save her life, three women last week delivered a petition with more than 12,000 signatures to the National People’s Congress in Beijing, demanding transparency in the drafting of a planned national law against domestic violence.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chinese Activists Demand Clarity on Domestic Violence Law', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Domestic Violence', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-29T15:59:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Didi Kirsten Tatlow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Didi', 'middlename': 'Kirsten', 'lastname': 'Tatlow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1462a8d8-2d88-5b73-8e3b-ed2a8968c764', 'word_count': 322, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1462a8d8-2d88-5b73-8e3b-ed2a8968c764'}, {'abstract': 'After some early successes as a photographer, Matt Eich returned to his home in Virginia to raise his family and confront the realities of home and career.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/29/redefining-home-on-the-virginia-peninsula/', 'snippet': 'After some early successes as a photographer, Matt Eich returned to his home in Virginia to raise his family and confront the realities of home and career.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Matt Eich was raised in the tidewater area of Virginia, a series of seven cities and smaller shore communities separated by water yet connected by bridges, tunnels and the presence of many large United States military bases. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Redefining Home in Tidewater Virginia', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Careers and Professions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Press Photographers Assn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia Beach (Va)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Williamsburg (Va)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-29T16:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Estrin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Estrin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/21c6a51d-16cf-57da-a188-b7677943fe55', 'word_count': 745, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21c6a51d-16cf-57da-a188-b7677943fe55'}, {'abstract': 'The award gives $50,000 to the playwright and $100,000 toward the production of the play.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/29/laurentshatcher-award-goes-to-daniel-pearle-for-a-kid-like-jake/', 'snippet': 'The award gives $50,000 to the playwright and $100,000 toward the production of the play.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The new play “A Kid Like Jake,” about raising a child in the world of Manhattan privilege, has won the 2013 Laurents/Hatcher Foundation Award, an unusually structured prize that provides $50,000 to the writer and an additional $100,000 toward the production costs for the show’s premiere. The playwright is Daniel Pearle, and Lincoln Center Theater has already announced that it will mount “A Kid Like Jake” at the Claire Tow Theater in June through its LCT3 program, which provides tickets for $20.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Laurents/Hatcher Award Goes to Daniel Pearle for ‘A Kid Like Jake’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Laurents/Hatcher Award Goes to Daniel Pearle', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cabnet, Evan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hatcher, Tom', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kern, Jon', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Laurents, Arthur', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Talbott, Jeff', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Laurents/Hatcher Foundation Award', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center Theater', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MCC Theater', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Second Stage Theater', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-29T16:04:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9dc6ca5-538c-5cd3-8fad-8fdbb383d7f6', 'word_count': 216, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9dc6ca5-538c-5cd3-8fad-8fdbb383d7f6'}, {'abstract': 'A new assault charge could force a judicial review of Chris Brown’s probation.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/29/frank-ocean-wants-to-press-charges-against-chris-brown/', 'snippet': 'A new assault charge could force a judicial review of Chris Brown’s probation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Frank Ocean, the R&B singer and songwriter, wants to press charges against Chris Brown after the two were said to have fought over a parking spot near a Los Angeles recording studio, a move that could jeopardize Mr. Brown’s probation on a previous assault conviction, Reuters reported. Mr. Brown pleaded guilty to assaulting Rihanna in 2009.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Frank Ocean Wants to Press Charges Against Chris Brown', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assaults', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Chris', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ocean, Frank', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-29T16:06:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d229c7e3-d66e-56f5-ad78-1a342198f85f', 'word_count': 132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d229c7e3-d66e-56f5-ad78-1a342198f85f'}, {'abstract': 'A new report on companies’ opinions of social media advertising shows that companies are spending more on that strategy, though they are concerned with getting an accurate measurement of its effectiveness.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/29/report-gauges-companies-approach-to-advertising-on-social-media/', 'snippet': 'A new report on companies’ opinions of social media advertising shows that companies are spending more on that strategy, though they are concerned with getting an accurate measurement of its effectiveness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since the arrival of social media platforms, companies have tried to figure out how to best use them to get their messages to consumers, often with mixed results. Some brands have embraced the notion that social platforms like Twitter allow constant interaction, for better or worse, with their customers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Report Gauges Companies’ Approach to Advertising on Social Media', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Online Advertising', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pinterest', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-29T16:11:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tanzina Vega', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tanzina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vega', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/16168e96-b785-5d12-ad32-bc3e5c3c9d7e', 'word_count': 660, 'uri': 'nyt://article/16168e96-b785-5d12-ad32-bc3e5c3c9d7e'}, {'abstract': 'The Swedish model shares some of her thoughts on style, classic rock, her love of natural products, and food.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/29/face-time-elsa-hosk/', 'snippet': 'The Swedish model shares some of her thoughts on style, classic rock, her love of natural products, and food.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Elsa Anna Sophia Hosk, a very sweet and exceptionally beautiful model from Sweden, was recently named the face of Pink, a subdivision of Victoria’s Secret. Just 24, she’s already worked for Christian Dior, Dolce & Gabbana, Lilly Pulitzer, Ugg and Nine West. Here she shares some of her thoughts on style, classic rock, her love of natural products, and food.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Face Time | Elsa Hosk', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Models (Professional)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-29T16:14:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tina Turnbow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Turnbow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/621261aa-90b7-55b2-bc76-f298f67edc25', 'word_count': 849, 'uri': 'nyt://article/621261aa-90b7-55b2-bc76-f298f67edc25'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/29/arts/television/whats-on-wednesday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '9 P.M. (13, 49) HENRY FORD “American Experience” chronicles the life and times of Ford, from his childhood on a Michigan farm in the 1860s and his dream of becoming a machinist in Detroit to his pursuit of racecar driving, the winnings from which allowed him to incorporate his Ford Motor Company. The result was the revolutionary Model T, a lightweight, durable and fast automobile that cost $850 at a time when the average car sold for more than $2,000. Soon the company was producing 1,000 cars a day. Taking its cue from the meatpacking industry, the company established the first automobile assembly line and controlled nearly half of the American car market. Ford, above with the Model T, also paid a $5 daily wage to reduce turnover, with strings attached. Immigrant workers had to attend the company’s English-language schools, and inspectors from the “sociological department” would delve into their private lives. As Ford became one of the richest men in the world, he found his hatred for the wealthy elite increasing; he allied himself with the common people. But as his ego expanded, so did his anger. Ford blamed Jews for the country’s problems, bullied those who worked for him and displayed withering cruelty toward his only son, Edsel, who died at 49 — a death many blamed on the unrelenting stress of trying to please his father.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Tuesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-29T16:18:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb97fdff-31b2-54b7-aa09-2e377969edde', 'word_count': 738, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb97fdff-31b2-54b7-aa09-2e377969edde'}, {'abstract': 'A Consumer Federation of America analysis found that lower-income drivers with clean accident records often pay higher auto insurance premiums than higher-income drivers who have caused an accident.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/29/when-good-drivers-pay-more-for-insurance-than-bad-ones/', 'snippet': 'A Consumer Federation of America analysis found that lower-income drivers with clean accident records often pay higher auto insurance premiums than higher-income drivers who have caused an accident.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some big insurance companies charge higher auto rates for lower-income drivers, even if the drivers have safe driving records, an analysis from the Consumer Federation of America finds.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Good Drivers Pay More for Insurance Than Bad Ones', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Safe Driver,\r\nHigh Costs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Insurance and Liability', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hunter, Robert', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ALLSTATE CORP', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Federation of America', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Geico Corp', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Progressive Casualty Insurance Co', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Farm Insurance Cos', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-29T16:20:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b41d5ca-bf9d-5c9d-9f36-3bb182720882', 'word_count': 759, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b41d5ca-bf9d-5c9d-9f36-3bb182720882'}, {'abstract': 'A 