xt Senate race.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/29/will-mcconnell-hold-on/', 'snippet': 'He may face a right-wing primary challenger in his next Senate race.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s too early to say for sure, but it looks like the 2014 Kentucky Senate race might just borrow its storyline from 2012, when the far-right wing engineered the selection of Republican fringe candidates that could not win a general election.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Will McConnell Hold On?', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Senate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tea Party Movement', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McConnell, Mitch', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-29T18:45:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/678c24cd-faeb-5e8c-adfc-b16e28061a08', 'word_count': 656, 'uri': 'nyt://article/678c24cd-faeb-5e8c-adfc-b16e28061a08'}, {'abstract': 'A week in the life of armed America.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/29/go-ahead-google-shooting/', 'snippet': 'A week in the life of armed America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'That is what my assistant, Jennifer Mascia, and I did last week in compiling the stories for today’s column. The column gives only the smallest of hints as to how many shootings there are on any given day; my guess is that even Google doesn’t find them all. To give you a fuller picture, we’ve reconstructed the Google search for “shooting” from Monday to Saturday last we