a “Ripper Street.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tuesday was a good day for being bad, especially if you do so in the context of cable-TV comedy or drama. Showtime said that it had ordered new seasons of its dark comedies “Shameless” (about a Chicago family gone to seed); “Californication” (about an author struggling — and sometimes not struggling — with his sex life); and “House of Lies,” about a group of unscrupulous management consultants. All three series have seen their viewership grow over previous seasons, Showtime said, and will resume production later this year in Los Angeles to begin new seasons in 2014. Don Cheadle, a star of “House of Lies,” was a surprise winner of the Golden Globe for lead actor in a comedy or musical series earlier this month. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Good News for Bad People as Showtime, Cinemax and BBC America Renew Series', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Day of Good News For Bad People on TV', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cheadle, Don', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BBC America', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cinemax', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Showtime', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-29T19:22:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebf067d9-0cc7-5621-a1ed-3185553ea2b9', 'word_count': 198, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebf067d9-0cc7-5621-a1ed-3185553ea2b9'}, {'abstract': 'With a too cozy board, It’s no coincidence that the oil company has had 