, 'headline': {'main': 'A Room Fit for a Queen', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goring Hotel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-29T20:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3003859a-9f64-5bbb-92fb-ec4fa7205403', 'word_count': 44, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3003859a-9f64-5bbb-92fb-ec4fa7205403'}, {'abstract': 'Domestic cats in the United States kill billions of birds and mammals a year, according to a new report, a rate that is much higher than previous estimates.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/30/science/that-cuddly-kitty-of-yours-is-a-killer.html', 'snippet': 'Domestic cats in the United States kill billions of birds and mammals a year, according to a new report, a rate that is much higher than previous estimates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For all the adorable images of cats that play the piano, flush the toilet, mew melodiously and find their way back home over hundreds of miles, scientists have identified a shocking new truth: cats are far deadlier than anyone realized.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/30/science/30cats-span/30cats-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/30/science/30cats-span/30cats-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/30/science/30cats-span/30cats-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/30/science/30cats-span/30cats-span-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/30/science/30cats-span/30cats-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/30/science/30cats-span/30cats-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/30/science/30cats-span/30cats-span-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'That Cuddly Kitty Is Deadlier Than You Think', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From Cuddly Critter to Killing Machine: Cats Are Much Deadlier Than Once Thought', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cats', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Anger, Natalie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fish and Wildlife Service', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Smithsonian Conservation Biology Institute', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nature Communications', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mammals', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nature Communications (Journal)', 'rank': 8, 'major