illiard-trained theater actor, currently on hiatus from his role as Brick in Broadway’s “Cat on a Hot Tin Roof,” talks about what it’s like to work opposite Scarlett Johansson.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/29/talking-talent-benjamin-walker/', 'snippet': 'The Juilliard-trained theater actor, currently on hiatus from his role as Brick in Broadway’s “Cat on a Hot Tin Roof,” talks about what it’s like to work opposite Scarlett Johansson.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Juilliard-trained theater actor Benjamin Walker, who played the 16th president on the silver screen in “Abraham Lincoln: Vampire Hunter” and Andrew Jackson on Broadway, has taken a break from American politics to star as the booze-swilling Brick in “Cat on a Hot Tin Roof” at the Richard Rogers Theater through March 30. At a sculptured 6-foot-3, Walker successfully embodies Brick with bourbon-soaked vulnerability and plenty of southern charm. Thirty minutes before curtain, a cool and collected Walker answered T’s questions about crutches, lap dances and his almighty mother-in-law, Meryl Streep.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Talking Talent | Benjamin Walker', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Arena | Talking Talent: Benjamin Walker', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walker, Benjamin (1982- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Cat on a Hot Tin Roof (Play)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-29T21:30:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lauren Tabach-Bank', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lauren', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tabach-Bank', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organizat