s', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Catsimatidis Announces Bid for Mayor', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Catsimatidis Announces Republican Run for Mayor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Catsimatidis, John A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gristedes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-29T22:05:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael M. Grynbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cfd82f09-acb0-580f-91ae-cb7327591702', 'word_count': 599, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cfd82f09-acb0-580f-91ae-cb7327591702'}, {'abstract': 'New Orleans, where bakery loyalties run deep, has become a laboratory for desserts — especially when it comes to the popular king cake and its many variations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/30/dining/king-cakes-abound-in-new-orleans.html', 'snippet': 'New Orleans, where bakery loyalties run deep, has become a laboratory for desserts — especially when it comes to the popular king cake and its many variations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW ORLEANS — Other cities might be trudging through cabbage season at this point in winter, but New Orleans is eating cake. From Twelfth Night to Mardi Gras, which is Feb. 12 this year, daily consumption of king cake — a round of sweet dough glazed with purple, gold and green sugar — is more or less compulsory. It’s a clue that although this city’s rémoulades and gumbos and Sazeracs are renowned, there is also a world of sweet treats to explore.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/30/dining/30BAKERIES_SPAN/30BAKERIES_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 423, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/30/dining/30BAKERIES_SPAN/30BAKERIES_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 423}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/30/dining/30BAKERIES_SPAN/30BAKERIES_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 722, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/30/dining/30BAKERIES_SPAN/30BAKERIES_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 932, 'width': 1321, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/30/dining/30BAKERIES_SPAN/30BAKERIES_SPAN-thumbStandard-v6.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/30/dining/30BAKERIES_SPAN/30BAKERIES_SPAN-thumbStandard-v6.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/30/dining/30BAKERIES_SPAN/30BAKERIES_SPAN-thumbLarge-v6.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A City Drenched in Sugar', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A City Drenched in Sugar', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Orleans (La)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moskin, Julia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cakes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bakeries and Baked Products', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mardi Gras', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Henry, Dwight', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Desserts', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-29T22:05:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Moskin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moskin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0d799d7-3b7f-5822-bbc0-bac937add33b', 'word_count': 1461, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0d799d7-3b7f-5822-bbc0-bac937add33b'}, {'abstract': 'The producers of “Truman Capote’s ‘Breakfast at Tiffany’s’” are scrambling to raise $1 million after an investor pulled out of the $4 million show.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/29/producers-scramble-after-investor-withdraws-from-breakfast-at-tiffanys/', 'snippet': 'The producers of “Truman Capote’s ‘Breakfast at Tiffany’s’” are scrambling to raise $1 million after an investor pulled out of the $4 million show.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Broadway producers of “Truman Capote’s ‘Breakfast at Tiffany’s’” are scrambling to raise $1 million after an investor pulled out of the $4 million show, according to a spokesman for the production, which began rehearsals on Monday and is scheduled to begin performances on March 4. The cast, led by Emilia Clarke (HBO’s “Game of Thrones”) as Holly Golightly, have been told that the production would be in jeopardy if the money was not replaced quickly. The play’s spokesman, Rick Miramontez, declined to identify the investor who dropped out, but said some additional money had already been raised and the producers were working hard to find the rest. Another Broadway-bound show this season, “Rebecca,” fell apart because of money problems after four of its investors were revealed to be phantoms. The producers of “Breakfast at Tiffany’s” – Colin Ingram Productions Limited, Donovan Mannato and Dominic Ianno – are relative newcomers to Broadway.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Producers Scramble After Investor Withdraws From ‘Breakfast at Tiffany’s’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Investor Withdraws From Capote’s ‘Tiffany’s’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-29T22:13:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7e0a425-cd0d-59ad-8fe6-c0d685429c39', 'word_count': 152, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7e0a425-cd0d-59ad-8fe6-c0d685429c39'}, {'abstract': 'The debate over royalties has become especially heated over the last couple of years.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/29/streaming-and-micropennies-the-footnotes/', 'snippet': 'The debate over royalties has become especially heated over the last couple of years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Tuesday’s paper, I wrote about the royalties that musicians and record companies earn from online streaming companies like Spotify, Pandora and YouTube.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Streaming and Micropennies: The Footnotes', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Audio Recordings 