ters and editors of The New York Times scour the Web for important and peculiar items. For Tuesday, selections include Google Maps adding information on North Korea, a computer virus that has stolen thousands of Facebook log-in...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here are some of the more interesting items that the tech reporters and editors of The New York Times found on the Web recently. See more here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Today’s Scuttlebot: Stolen Facebook IDs and All About Zelda', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-29T22:45:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/31f6a9b5-f23c-504a-a477-c2fdf41a5d67', 'word_count': 133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31f6a9b5-f23c-504a-a477-c2fdf41a5d67'}, {'abstract': 'The Danish director and screenwriter Nikolaj Arcel talks about making “The Royal Affair” from a story every Dane knows (even if few outsiders do).', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/29/a-story-known-far-and-wide-in-denmark-at-least/', 'snippet': 'The Danish director and screenwriter Nikolaj Arcel talks about making “The Royal Affair” from a story every Dane knows (even if few outsiders do).', 'lead_paragraph': 'Until this month, if the Danish director and screenwriter Nikolaj Arcel was known at all in the English-speaking world, it was as the co-writer of the screenplay for the original version of “The Girl With the Dragon Tattoo.” But after winning two prizes at the Berlin Film Festival a year ago, the latest film he directed, “A Royal Affair,” is now getting attention in Hollywood as one of the five contenders nominated for the Academy Award for best foreign-language film.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/30/arts/royalaffair/royalaffair-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 361, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/30/arts/royalaffair/royalaffair-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 361}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/30/arts/royalaffair/royalaffair-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 617, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/30/arts/royalaffair/royalaffair-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1233, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/30/arts/royalaffair/royalaffair-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/30/arts/royalaffair/royalaffair-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/30/arts/royalaffair/royalaffair-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Story Known Far and Wide, in Denmark at Least', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nikolaj Arcel, ‘A Royal\r\nAffair,’ Denmark', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Arcel, Nikolaj', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Denmark', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-29T22:54:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Rohter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6460a40-0f3a-5d74-a924-53c13e484d0b', 'word_count': 1275, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6460a40-0f3a-5d74-a924-53c13e484d0b'}, {'abstract': 'Christine Andreas, in her cabaret show at 54 Below, is being allowed to fly as far and wide as she wishes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/30/arts/music/christine-andreas-in-bemused-at-54-below.html', 'snippet': 'Christine Andreas, in her cabaret show at 54 Below, is being allowed to fly as far and wide as she wishes.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Bemused,” the title of the singer Christine Andreas’s deliciously tangy show at 54 Below, is one of the most misused and hard-to-pin-down words in the English language. As Ms. Andreas reflected on its meanings at Sunday evening’s opening-night performance, one synonym, “thunderstruck,” stood out. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/30/arts/SUBANDREAS/SUBANDREAS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/30/arts/SUBANDREAS/SUBANDREAS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/30/arts/SUBANDREAS/SUBANDREAS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/30/arts/SUBANDREAS/SUBANDREAS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/30/arts/SUBANDREAS/SUBANDREAS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/30/arts/SUBANDREAS/SUBANDREAS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/30/arts/SUBANDREAS/SUBANDREAS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Right Tune, Right Singer: Pure Alchemy', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Right Tune, Right Singer: Pure Alchemy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': '54 Below (Manha