o-charms-the-host/', 'snippet': 'Senator Marco Rubio laid out his broad principles for immigration legislation, and by the end of the interview the radio show host Rush Limbaugh seemed downright smitten.', 'lead_paragraph': ' WASHINGTON — Senator Marco Rubio, Republican of Florida, continued his conservative media tour Tuesday with an afternoon telephone interview on Rush Limbaugh’s talk radio show. The back and forth went so well, from Mr. Rubio’s point of view, that at 6 p.m. his office was still tweeting out highlights from the exchange.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Limbaugh Interview, Rubio Charms the Host', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Limbaugh, Rush', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rubio, Marco', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-30T00:06:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff4d616b-93a4-5400-a3f1-3232c3b15ff1', 'word_count': 781, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff4d616b-93a4-5400-a3f1-3232c3b15ff1'}, {'abstract': 'Residents of Sapelo Island, many of whom are descendants of slaves, objected after their taxes rose by as much as 1,000 percent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/30/us/history-rich-georgia-island-wins-second-look-on-taxes.html', 'snippet': 'Residents of Sapelo Island, many of whom are descendants of slaves, objected after their 