fb647ea45a2'}, {'abstract': 'The organization’s plan to no longer “dictate” an antigay policy to local scouting groups does not go far enough in its renunciation of antigay bigotry.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/30/opinion/the-boy-scouts-fall-short-in-policy-on-gays.html', 'snippet': 'The organization’s plan to no longer “dictate” an antigay policy to local scouting groups does not go far enough in its renunciation of antigay bigotry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just a week after President Obama made ending antigay discrimination a central message of his Inaugural Address, the Boy Scouts of America provided more evidence that greater acceptance and inclusion is becoming a social norm. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Boy Scouts Fall Short', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Boy Scouts Fall Short', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boy Scouts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-30T02:11:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/71b2af4b-be77-550a-9856-35e1d4855ea1', 'word_count': 436, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71b2af4b-be77-550a-9856-35e1d4855ea1'}, {'abstract': 'There are many good proposals on gun control, which should be debated and voted on in full public view.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/30/opinion/congress-takes-up-gun-violence.html', 'snippet': 'There are many good proposals on gun control, which should be debated and voted on in full public view.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Senate hearings on stronger gun controls are scheduled to begin on Wednesday before a divided Congress and a nation agonizing over how to prevent more of the carnage that killed 20 schoolchildren and six adults last month at a Newtown, Conn., elementary school. The gun lobby’s opposition to reasonable controls is already fierce, and political courage is, as ever, wavering in Congress. But this singular opportunity to curb the gun violence must not be wasted in more of the posturing in Washington that tolerates 30,000 gun deaths a year.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Congress Takes Up Gun Violence', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Congress Takes Up Gun Violence', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Series', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-30T02:12:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7d1c814-f292-598c-b2ea-98d6e4d8d253', 'word_count': 640, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7d1c814-f292-598c-b2ea-98d6e4d8d253'}, {'abstract': 'The push to make MF Global customers nearly whole, a goal now surprisingly within reach, is a remarkable turnaround for the brokerage firm.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/01/29/mf-globals-bankruptcy-closes-in-on-a-happy-conclusion/', 'snippet': 'The push to make MF Global customers nearly whole, a goal now surprisingl