_paragraph': 'NEW ORLEANS — Baltimore quarterback Joe Flacco, one of the quietest and most polite players in the middle of two boisterous franchises in New Orleans for Super Bowl XLVII, made some waves Monday night when he was quoted as being critical of the decision to hold the Super Bowl at MetLife Stadium in East Rutherford, N.J., next year.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Flacco Not a Fan of Super Bowl in New Jersey', 'kicker': 'N.F.L. Roundup', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Flacco Makes Waves', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MetLife Stadium (NJ)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baltimore Ravens', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Flacco, Joe', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-30T05:15:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Hoffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e87e52d-8396-5e18-9522-aa4d75c88633', 'word_count': 370, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e87e52d-8396-5e18-9522-aa4d75c88633'}, {'abstract': 'One-day series win against England came as a relief for the captain of the Indian cricket team.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/30/sweet-taste-of-victory-for-dhoni-and-co/', 'snippet': 'One-day series win against England came as a relief for the captain of the Indian cricket team.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The one man who appears to be the most relieved after the 3-2 win in the five-match one-day cricket series against England is the Indian captain, Mahendra Singh Dhoni.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sweet Taste of Victory for Dhoni and Co.', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cricket (Game)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pujara, Cheteshwar', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tendulkar, Sachin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-30T05:58:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Haresh Pandya', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Haresh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pandya', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/73dc0296-a694-57c1-9124-c81af1f58496', 'word_count': 580, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73dc0296-a694-57c1-9124-c81af1f58496'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/30/arts/television/whats-on-wednesday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '9 P.M. (13, 49) WHO KILLED LINDBERGH’S BABY? On March 1, 1932, Charles and Anne Lindbergh’s 20-month-old son, above, was kidnapped from the family’s home near Hopewell, N.J. Negotiations stretched out for weeks, but the boy was never returned. His body was found two months later less than five miles from Hopewell, and, after a two-year investigation, Bruno Richard Hauptmann, a German immigrant living in the Bronx, was ultimately found guilty of extortion and murder. He was executed on April 3, 1936. This “Nova” episode reopens the case as investigators use contemporary forensic and behavioral-science techniques to determine what really happened to the child, and why.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page'