84f3-ed83443a2f82'}, {'abstract': 'For the Times staff photographer Andrea Mohin, taking dance pictures is “sports photography in the dark when you don’t know the game.”', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/30/on-assignment-the-joy-of-dance/', 'snippet': 'For the Times staff photographer Andrea Mohin, taking dance pictures is “sports photography in the dark when you don’t know the game.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some photographers live for the the thrill of the unexpected happening right in front of them. Others prefer a more ordered world, where each occurrence is telegraphed far in advance.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Assignment: The Joy of Dance', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-30T10:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a578a89-505a-5da6-9f4e-a07a97eb5ec6', 'word_count': 164, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a578a89-505a-5da6-9f4e-a07a97eb5ec6'}, {'abstract': 'The espionage thrillers of Gérard de Villiers have more than the ring of truth to them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/02/03/magazine/gerard-de-villiers-the-spy-novelist-who-knows-too-much.html', 'snippet': 'The espionage thrillers of Gérard de Villiers have more than the ring of truth to them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last June, a pulp-fiction thriller was published in Paris under the title “Le Chemin de Damas.” Its lurid green-and-black cover featured a busty woman clutching a pistol, and its plot included the requisite car chases, explosions and sexual conquests. Unlike most paperbacks, though, this one attracted the attention of intelligence officers and diplomats on three continents. Set in the midst of Syria’s civil war, the book offered vivid character sketches of that country’s embattled ruler, Bashar al-Assad, and his brother Maher, along with several little-known lieutenants and allies. It detailed a botched coup attempt secretly supported by the American and Israeli intelligence agencies. And most striking of all, it described an attack on one of the Syrian regime’s command centers, near the presidential palace in Damascus, a month before an attack in the same place killed several of the regime’s top figures. “It was prophetic,” I was told by one veteran Middle East analyst who knows Syria well and preferred to remain nameless. “It really gave you a sense of the atmosphere inside the regime, of the way these people operate, in a way I hadn’t seen before.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/02/03/magazine/03novelist1/03novelist1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/02/03/magazine/03novelist1/03novelist1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 750}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/02/03/magazine/03novelist1/03novelist1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 820, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/02/03/magazine/03novelist1/03novelist1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1500, 'width': 1200, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/02/03/magazine/03novelist1/03novelist1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/02/03/magazine/03novelist1/03novelist1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/02/03/magazine/03novelist1/03novelist1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Spy Novelist Who Knows Too Much', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Spy Novelist Who Knows Too Much', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Villiers, Gerard', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Worth, Robert F', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Directorate for External Security (DGSE)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-30T10:00:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert F. Worth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Worth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/206043fe-408f-57b0-bf56-789373132661', 'word_count': 4037, 'uri': 'nyt://article/206043fe-408f-57b0-bf56-789373132661'}, {'abstract': 'This is a special edition of our daily question. Answering it by Feb.13 will make students 13 to 19 years old eligible to have their responses posted elsewhere on NYTimes.com.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/30/student-challenge-what-tech-tools-play-the-biggest-role-in