blems', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Toyota Is Recalling\r\nOne Million Vehicles', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recalls and Bans of Products', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lexus Division of Toyota Motor Corp', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Highway Traffic Safety Administration', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toyota Motor Corporation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-30T16:11:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2eab18b-aa86-54d9-be3f-9cf2a0d69e02', 'word_count': 249, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2eab18b-aa86-54d9-be3f-9cf2a0d69e02'}, {'abstract': 'In this week’s links: Marxist admirers of a Pope conversant with the Frankfurt School; Jane Austen as moral philosopher; and more.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/30/stone-links-jane-austen-aristotelian-pope-benedict-marxist/', 'snippet': 'In this week’s links: Marxist admirers of a Pope conversant with the Frankfurt School; Jane Austen as moral philosopher; and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like his predecessor John Paul II, who wrote his doctoral dissertation on the German phenomenologist Max Scheler, and wove a keen understanding of philosophical history into encyclicals like “Fides et Ratio”, Pope Benedict XVI also seems quite comfortable engaging in philosophical debate. Judging by his interactions with Jürgen Habermas, among others, one might assume that the Pope stands for a political and theological conservatism quite at odds with Marxist tradition. Yet they, and indeed Benedict himself might be surprised to find that, as a post at First Things explains, he evidently has his admirers on the left. Four Italian “Ratzingerian Marxists” of the “Old Left” have issued a “manifesto” hoping to enlist the Pope in their fight against a “consumerist-inflected secularism.” Strange bedfellows? Maybe not, considering that a few close readers of Benedict’s 2007 encyclical “Spe Salvi” have noted that the Pope cites Max Horkheimer and Theodor Adorno to help refute the plausibility of the thesis that, with the waning of theistic belief, “man himself is now called to establish justice.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stone Links: Jane Austen, Ethicist? Pope Benedict, Marxist?', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Austen, Jane', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Benedict XVI', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McEwen, Ian', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-30T16:19:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.c. Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/141e46f8-d024-5087-a34a-c2fbfb556ede', 'word_count': 398, 'uri': 'nyt://article/141e46f8-d024-5087-a34a-c2fbfb556ede'}, {'abstract': 'Proenza Schouler has reworked its infamous PS11 bag, which graces the arms of every Hollywood starlet and Park Avenue socialite, into a must-have wallet in fluorescent pink.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/30/feeling-for-proenza-schoulers-ps11-wallet/', 'snippet': 'Proenza Schouler has reworked its infamous PS11 bag, which graces the arms of every Hollywood starlet and Park Avenue socialite, into a must-have wallet in fluorescent pink.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Proenza Schouler has reworked its infamous PS11 bag, which graces the arms of every Hollywood starlet and Park Avenue socialite, into a must-have wallet in fluorescent pink. With a bold hardware closure and ample room for cash, keys and lipstick, the PS11 doubles as a clutch for a night on the town. For those wanting to forgo the cliché dinner date and really make their special someone smile, this Valentine’s Day is in the bag.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Feeling For | Proenza Schouler’s PS11 Wallet', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Handbags and Purses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Proenza Schouler', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-30T16:30:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc7b850d-2744-5595-87a7-c47bf3c9fde1', 'word_count': 83, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc7b850d-2744-5595-87a7-c47bf3c9fde1'}, {'abstract': 'The season’s board books include “Good Night!” and “Spoonful!” by Benoit Marchon', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2013/01/30/bo