': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d99cd89b-af02-5e6e-8234-2d3ab1eeb4e5', 'word_count': 269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d99cd89b-af02-5e6e-8234-2d3ab1eeb4e5'}, {'abstract': 'A federal judge ruled that the class-action suit led by former U.C.L.A. basketball star Ed O’Bannon could proceed and be amended by the players to include live broadcast revenue.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/30/judge-allows-n-c-a-a-lawsuit-to-include-television-revenue/', 'snippet': 'A federal judge ruled that the class-action suit led by former U.C.L.A. basketball star Ed O’Bannon could proceed and be amended by the players to include live broadcast revenue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A federal judge on Tuesday rejected a motion by the N.C.A.A. to preclude live broadcast revenues from a lawsuit by men’s football and basketball players, which means college sports faces a much steeper paycheck should the players prevail in their class action lawsuit.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Judge Allows N.C.A.A. Lawsuit to Include Television Revenue', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Bannon, Ed", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Electronic Arts Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Collegiate Athletic Assn', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-30T20:19:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a74323ab-5589-54af-8cb5-676dd2accc42', 'word_count': 311, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a74323ab-5589-54af-8cb5-676dd2accc42'}, {'abstract': 'Sharón Clark, a jazz and soul diva, tears apart, peers inside and has fun with songs of her youth in her show at the Metropolitan Room.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/31/arts/music/sharon-clark-at-the-metropolitan-room.html', 'snippet': 'Sharón Clark, a jazz and soul diva, tears apart, peers inside and has fun with songs of her youth in her show at the Metropolitan Room.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You can’t underestimate the transformation of what seems like an ordinary song when an interpreter like Sharón Clark, a Washington-based jazz and soul diva, tears it apart and peers inside. A prime example in her show “Blame It on My Youth,” at the Metropolitan Room on Monday evening, was her ruminative interpretation of the old Carpenters’ hit, “Rainy Days and Mondays,” supported by Chris Grasso on piano, Tony Jefferson on drums and Neal Miner on bass. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/31/arts/SHARON/SHARON-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 373, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/31/arts/SHARON/SHARON-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 373}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/31/arts/SHARON/SHARON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 637, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/31/arts/SHARON/SHARON-s