enes at Super Bowl media day. David Pogue’s 60-second BlackBerry review.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A closer look at the reinvented BlackBerry. Behind the scenes at Super Bowl media day. David Pogue’s 60-second BlackBerry review. Go to the Bits blog to see the video.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'TimesCast Media+Tech: BlackBerry Has High Hopes for New Phones', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-30T20:46:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/27453d93-e635-56ca-9bbe-e879d1eb4f92', 'word_count': 29, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27453d93-e635-56ca-9bbe-e879d1eb4f92'}, {'abstract': 'Six months into our divorce, the kids’ mom moved back to Boston and I followed. In that tiny apartment, I unlearned everything I’d learned about how not to be a dad.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/30/when-a-divorce-makes-a-better-dad/', 'snippet': 'Six months into our divorce, the kids’ mom moved back to Boston and I followed. In that tiny apartment, I unlearned everything I’d learned about how not to be a dad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Divorce stinks. Don’t get me wrong. The excruciating pain of leaving your child on Mom’s doorstep, of missing holidays and first steps, of having to schedule visitation are nothing to sign up for unless there is no other choice. My divorce involved the kind of pain that makes you think walking in front of a train would be a piece of cake if not for your responsibilities. But buried deep within that pain is a silver lining — a motivation, an aspiration, a hands-on learning — that “normal” dads don’t get.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When a Divorce Makes a Better Dad