ersons', 'value': 'Molina, Alfred', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miranda, Lin-Manuel', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-30T22:51:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Hale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/485ddd65-b7df-58bf-be8b-38506babdde1', 'word_count': 901, 'uri': 'nyt://article/485ddd65-b7df-58bf-be8b-38506babdde1'}, {'abstract': 'The New York Philharmonic performed orchestral arrangements of suites from Sondheim musicals on Tuesday at Avery Fisher Hall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/31/arts/music/philharmonics-symphonic-sondheim-at-avery-fisher-hall.html', 'snippet': 'The New York Philharmonic performed orchestral arrangements of suites from Sondheim musicals on Tuesday at Avery Fisher Hall.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Attend the score of ‘Sweeney Todd,’\xa0” Nathan Lane said, tweaking the lyric to the ballad that opens the masterpiece musical by Stephen Sondheim and Hugh Wheeler. The occasion was a special New York Philharmonic program on Tuesday night at Avery Fisher Hall, titled “Symphonic Sondheim,” devoted to orchestral arrangements of suites from four of Mr. Sondheim’s musicals, along with incidental music to a play, “The Enclave,” and a suite from the film score for “Stavisky.” Mr. Lane was the droll host. On the podium was the great Sondheim maestro Paul Gemignani.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/31/arts/31SYMPHONIC/31SYMPHONIC-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 558, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'l