3a85-c94b-5ce5-aee1-6a11e19dec98', 'word_count': 768, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b273a85-c94b-5ce5-aee1-6a11e19dec98'}, {'abstract': 'The gross domestic product shrank last quarter for the first time since mid-2009, partly as a result of declines in military spending and exports. Private residential investment continued to grow, indicating that the housing market is still recovering.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/01/30/business/GDP-Shrinks.html', 'snippet': 'The gross domestic product shrank last quarter for the first time since mid-2009, partly as a result of declines in military spending and exports. Private residential investment continued to grow, indicating that the housing market is still recove...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The gross domestic product shrank last quarter for the first time since mid-2009, partly as a result of declines in military spending and exports. Private residential investment continued to grow, indicating that the housing market is still recovering.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'G.D.P. Shrinks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gross Domestic Product', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-30T23:29:37+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/c2d4eebf-1f4c-5068-b8ee-df1b46ce7bd6', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/c2d4eebf-1f4c-5068-b8ee-df1b46ce7bd6'}, {'abstract': 'A 30-year retrospective of Gene and Doug Meyer’s work will be exhibited at Longue Vue House & Gardens in New Orleans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/31/garden/in-new-orleans-a-retrospective-of-gene-and-doug-meyer.html', 'snippet': 'A 30-year retrospective of Gene and Doug Meyer’s work will be exhibited at Longue Vue House & Gardens in New Orleans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From Friday through March 31, Longue Vue House & Gardens, the eight-acre estate in New Orleans formerly owned by the philanthropists Edith and Edgar Stern, will host a 30-year retrospective of the work of the versatile designing brothers Gene and Doug Meyer. The show will permeate building and grounds with a panoply of the brothers’ creations that reveal their ebullient way with color and striking mixes of art and fashion. “Joe Baker, the director, has been calling it an intervention,” Doug Meyer said. Garments, pillows and fabrics will be presented on mannequins throughout the main house. A 10-foot-square mirrored Plexiglas box set inside the Whim House — a guest house that had previously been closed to the public — will be a showcase for rugs. The catalog is $12 from dougandgene.com. Information: (504) 488-5488 or longuevue.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/31/garden/31SHOWS/31CURR1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 940, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/31/garden/31SHOWS/31CURR1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 940}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/31/garden/31SHOWS/31CURR1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 985, 'width': 629, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/31/garden/31SHOWS/31CURR1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 985, 'width': 629, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/31/garden/31SHOWS/31CURR1-thumbStandard.