ers what led her to take a role in one of Broadway’s most famous flops.', 'lead_paragraph': '“From now on, there will always be two groups of theatergoers in this world: those who have seen ‘Moose Murders,’ and those who have not.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Remember ‘Moose Murders’? She Was There — Onstage', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bicknell, Arthur', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nagourney, Adam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rich, Frank', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Richards, Ann', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taylor, Holland', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-30T23:31:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Heller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Heller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f1fb768-e72b-5752-aca0-3af939f76acf', 'word_count': 322, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f1fb768-e72b-5752-aca0-3af939f76acf'}, {'abstract': 'With Fashion Weeks approaching in New York and in Europe, the fear over the flu epidemic is bordering on hysteria.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/31/fashion/illness-walks-the-runway.html', 'snippet': 'With Fashion Weeks approaching in New York and in Europe, the fear over the flu epidemic is bordering on hysteria.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A top fashion designer quarantines a sneezing underling, forcing her to work in a closet. An industry P.R. executive makes colleagues douse their hands with Purell. Germ-phobic magazine editors are powerblasting offices with antiseptic wipes and Lysol.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/31/fashion/31FLU_SPAN/31FLU_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/31/fashion/31FLU_SPAN/31FLU_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/31/fashion/31FLU_SPAN/31FLU_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/31/fashion/31FLU_SPAN/31FLU_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/31/fashion/31FLU_SPAN/31FLU_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/31/fashion/31FLU_SPAN/31FLU_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/31/fashion/31FLU_SPAN/31FLU_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Illness Walks the Runway', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Illness Walks the Runway', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Fashion Week', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Influenza', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hygiene and Cleanliness', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-30T23:32:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd050527-5086-5a21-90cf-a61cc8f587d4', 'word_count': 1596, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd050527-5086-5a21-90cf-a61cc8f587d4'}, {'abstract': 'Forrest Lesch-Middelton, a California potter, introduces a tile collection for Clé.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/31/garden/forrest-lesch-middeltons-tile-collection-for-cle.html', 'snippet': 'Forrest Lesch-Middelton, a California potter, introduces a tile collection for Clé.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Forrest Lesch-Middelton, a potter in Petaluma, Calif., makes ceramics that look like the products of an ancient civilization whose people proudly insisted on being buried with their dishware. The surfaces are mottled, the decorations irregular and the tones earthy siennas and fawns. Mr. Lesch-Middelton invented a technique for transferring Islamic starbursts, scrolls and flowers to the surfaces of his pots while they are still on the wheel, requiring him to shape the vessels from the inside. (He began this work in 2003, the year the United States invaded Iraq, saying he wanted to show off the artistic heritage of a culture he believed was misunderstood.)', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/31/garden/31TILE/31CURR4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 207, 'width': 600, 'subType'