of storms that tore across the Southeast, leaving at least two people dead.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At least two people were killed when a powerful line of storms in the Southeast spawned tornadoes, demolishing homes and businesses, downing trees and flipping more than 100 cars and several tractor-trailers on a major interstate in northern Georgia. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video: Tornadoes Rip Across Southeast', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tornadoes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-31T01:04:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/05316479-7835-5b53-9f35-bf116622f251', 'word_count': 297, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05316479-7835-5b53-9f35-bf116622f251'}, {'abstract': 'Versions of Super Bowl ads are already online, in stark contrast to a decades-old strategy of building anticipation by keeping them under wraps until the game.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/31/business/media/super-bowl-ad-previews-draw-online-attention-with-criticism.html', 'snippet': 'Versions of Super Bowl ads are already online, in stark contrast to a decades-old strategy of building anticipation by keeping them under wraps until the game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Don’t misunderstand John Norman, the chief creative officer at TBWA/Chiat/Day Los Angeles. He is excited to be working on a commercial, for Pepsi Next cola, that will appear during Super Bowl XLVII