/31/world/europe/russia-cancels-agreement-with-us.html', 'snippet': 'The cancellation of a decade-long agreement that called for cooperation on law enforcement efforts was the latest example of strained relations between the two countries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Prime Minister Dmitri A. Medvedev said Wednesday that Russia would cancel a decade-long agreement with the United States that called for cooperation on law enforcement efforts including drug control and combating human trafficking. Relations between the two countries have been particularly troubled since December, when the United States adopted a law aimed at punishing Russian human rights abusers. Aleksei Pushkov, a Parliament member, said that Russia could afford to fight crime on its own. Russian officials also announced that they would ban certain frozen meat and meat products from the United States because of evidence farmers were using an artificial growth stimulant called ractopamine. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia Cancels Agreement With U.S.', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia Cancels Agreement With U.S.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Trafficking', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Medvedev, Dmitri A', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-31T02:12:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By David M. Herszenhorn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/f304b960-ceae-5ceb-8caf-f8f11b6a35ea', 'word_count': 104, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f304b960-ceae-5ceb-8caf-f8f11b6a35ea'}, {'abstract': 'Senate Democrats could have the wind at their backs, if only they would act with resolve instead of fear.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/31/opinion/political-power-needs-to-be-used-in-washington.html', 'snippet': 'Senate Democrats could have the wind at their backs, if only they would act with resolve instead of fear.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If ever there were a moment for Democrats to press their political advantage, this is it. Their message on many of the biggest national issues — taxes, guns, education spending, financial regulation — has widespread support, and they have increased their numbers in both houses of Congress. But after years of being out-yelled by strident right-wing ideologues, too many in the Democratic Party still have a case of nerves, afraid of bold action and forthright principles.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Political Power Needs to Be Used', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Political Power Needs to Be Used', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Filibusters and Debate Curbs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baucus, Max', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manchin, Joe III', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-31T02:14:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/3119d7b5-83f7-5884-9d5d-04886363fac9', 'word_count': 588, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3119d7b5-83f7-5884-9d5d-04886363fac9'}, {'abstract': 'New England fishery management officials say the only way to save the centuries-old cod fishing industry is to sharply limit it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/31/us/officials-back-deep-cuts-in-atlantic-cod-harvest-to-save-industry.html', 'snippet': 'New England fishery management officials say the only way to save the centuries-old cod fishing industry is to sharply limit it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PORTSMOUTH, N.H. — Fishery management officials meeting here on Wednesday voted to impose drastic new cuts to the commercial harvest of cod along the Atlantic coast, arguing that the only way to save the centuries-old cod fishing industry was to sharply limit it.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/31/us/COD-3/COD-3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/31/us/COD-3/COD-3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 395}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/31/us/COD-3/COD-3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/31/us/COD-3/COD-3-superJumbo.j