ws', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1f46d10-09d3-57d9-9765-444216d560e3', 'word_count': 645, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1f46d10-09d3-57d9-9765-444216d560e3'}, {'abstract': 'Sharif Ahmed, chairman of Smart Export Garments, and his colleague, M. D. Zakir Ahmed, were arrested after a fire last week left seven workers dead.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/31/world/asia/factory-owners-arrested-in-bangladesh.html', 'snippet': 'Sharif Ahmed, chairman of Smart Export Garments, and his colleague, M. D. Zakir Ahmed, were arrested after a fire last week left seven workers dead.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Bangladeshi police have arrested two owners of a factory that caught fire last week, resulting in the deaths of seven workers, in the latest blaze to strike the country’s garment export industry. Late Tuesday night, the police arrested Sharif Ahmed, chairman of Smart Export Garments, and his colleague, M. D. Zakir Ahmed. The Smart Export factory was manufacturing clothing for several European clothing brands. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Factory Owners Arrested in Bangladesh', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bangladesh: Factory Owners Arrested', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manik, Julfikar Ali', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bangladesh', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-31T02:17:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julfikar Ali Manik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julfikar', 'middlename': 'Ali', 'lastname': 'Manik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/89de76ca-43dc-550e-97c7-3b86fd618755', 'word_count': 65, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89de76ca-43dc-550e-97c7-3b86fd618755'}, {'abstract': 'The timing of the attacks coincided with reporting for an investigation that found that the relatives of China’s prime minister had accumulated a fortune worth several billion dollars through business dealings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/31/technology/chinese-hackers-infiltrate-new-york-times-computers.html', 'snippet': 'The timing of the attacks coincided with reporting for an investigation that found that the relatives of China’s prime minister had accumulated a fortune worth several billion dollars through business dealings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — For the last four months, Chinese hackers have persistently attacked The New York Times, infiltrating its computer systems and getting passwords for its reporters and other employees.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/31/technology/31hack-web/31hack-web-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 422, 'width': 595, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/31/technology/31hack-web/31hack-web-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 422, 'width': 595, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/31/technology/31hack-web/31hack-web-thum