 None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lotteries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-31T04:15:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/f59acbbd-9947-5a90-8879-8c9e147e23b4', 'word_count': 165, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f59acbbd-9947-5a90-8879-8c9e147e23b4'}, {'abstract': 'A man who distrusted the government and was “a survivalist type” shot and killed a school bus driver on Tuesday in Midland City, then took a 6-year-old rider hostage, law enforcement officials said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/31/us/alabama-boy-6-is-held-hostage.html', 'snippet': 'A man who distrusted the government and was “a survivalist type” shot and killed a school bus driver on Tuesday in Midland City, then took a 6-year-old rider hostage, law enforcement officials said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A man who distrusted the government and was “a survivalist type” shot and killed a school bus driver on Tuesday in Midland City, then took a 6-year-old rider hostage, law enforcement officials said. After more than 24 hours, he was still holding the boy, who has a form of autism, in a well-supplied bunker buried on the man’s property while the F.B.I. tried to negotiate the boy’s release. The police delivered medication for the boy to the bunker, which was surrounded by SWAT teams. The Dale County Sheriff’s Department identified the suspect as Jimmy Lee Dykes, 65. It said the episode began when Mr. Dykes stopped the bus and demanded to be let on. The driver, Charles Albert Poland Jr., 66, refused. As children escaped, Mr. Dykes fired at least four shots at the driver and grabbed the boy, according to the police and parents. The standoff continued into the evening Wednesday. The police said Mr. Dykes had been scheduled to appear in court Wednesday to face charges of menacing. He is accused of shooting at neighbors in an altercation involving a neighbor’s driving on his property. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Alabama: Boy, 6, Is Held Hostage', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Alabama: Boy, 6, Is Held Hostage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALABAMA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dykes, Jimmy Lee', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hostages', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Midland City (Ala)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-31T04:20:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kim Severson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Severson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/5913f4b5-f902-5583-b64c-b01137bb10f0', 'word_count': 187, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5913f4b5-f902-5583-b64c-b01137bb10f0'}, {'abstract': 'Seven years after Hurricane Katrina, the New Orleans neighborhood where Marshall Faulk grew up lags behind the city’s recovery.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/31/sports/football/in-super-bowl-city-scars-remain-where-the-water-receded.html', 'snippet': 'Seven years after Hurricane Katrina, the New Orleans neighborhood where Marshall Faulk grew up lags behind the city’s recovery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW ORLEANS — Back in town for the Super Bowl, Marshall Fau