-forgetting-to-begin/', 'snippet': 'Using a jarred brain as a teaching tool, my dad showed my 8-year-old self how brains with Alzheimer’s disease become smaller. But only after his death — and my mother’s confession about whose brain occupied that jar — did I figure out that my fath...', 'lead_paragraph': 'My gray matter might be waning. Then again, it might not be. But I swear that I can feel memories — as I’m making them — slide off a neuron and into a tangle of plaque. I steel myself for those moments to come when I won’t remember what just went into my head. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/26/health/26well_alzheimersold/26well_alzheimersold-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 407, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/26/health/26well_alzheimersold/26well_alzheimersold-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 407}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/26/health/26well_alzheimersold/26well_alzheimersold-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 501, 'width': 738, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/26/health/26well_alzheimersold/26well_alzheimersold-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 501, 'width': 738, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/26/health/26well_alzheimersold/26well_alzheimersold-thumbStandard-v3.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/26/health/26well_alzheimersold/26well_alzheimersold-thumbStandard-v3.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'ran