biggest threat facing Facebook. But there are increasing signs that it is turning this into an even bigger opportunity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Facebook deserves the benefit of the doubt about its rocketing costs. The social network’s bills jumped about 80 percent in the fourth quarter. That’s worrying — it’s twice as much as the top line grew. But all-important mobile advertising revenue doubled in 90 days. The potential profit justifies heavy investment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Facebook Can Justify Its High Valuation', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-31T17:54:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Cyran', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cyran', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/11ed16fc-fbd8-5fff-b67b-f5bea915838b', 'word_count': 349, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11ed16fc-fbd8-5fff-b67b-f5bea915838b'}, {'abstract': 'Booking.com, a lodging Web site popular among European travelers, last month began its first ad campaign in the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/31/meet-booking-com/', 'snippet': 'Booking.com, a lodging Web site popular among European travelers, last month began its first ad campaign in the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Booking.com, a lodging Web site popular among European travelers, last month began its first ad campaign in the United States. Unlike Hotels.com and other sites, it makes bookings directly with properties rather than buying inventory from them. That means for its roughly 265,000 listings, the traveler pays upon checkout rather than in advance, and cancellation depends on the hotel’s policy.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Meet Booking.com', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Online: Meet Booking.com', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Booking.com', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-31T18:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily Brennan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brennan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34468271-8f50-5216-8a09-f0dfb2ade8b9', 'word_count': 60, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34468271-8f50-5216-8a09-f0dfb2ade8b9'}, {'abstract': 'The view from New Orleans: The actor Wendell Pierce, a Saints fan, talks about the Super Bowl, New Orleans and beignets.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/31/new-orleans-through-wendell-pierces-eyes/', 'snippet': 'The view from New Orleans: The actor Wendell Pierce, a Saints fan, talks about the Super Bowl, New Orleans and beignets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Brett Michael Dykes, a writer based in New Orleans, will be writing about the city and the Super Bowl for The Fifth Down throughout the week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/02/01/sports/pierce2/pierce2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy':