wn national attention outside the court, they have usually reinforced the impression of jurists as ideological warriors: there was Antonin Scalia, for example, jousting with a freshman at Princeton about whether sodomy is equivalent to murder.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sonia Sotomayor’s Best Seller', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sotomayor, Sonia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-31T18:18:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lincoln Caplan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lincoln', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/11b4111d-ea24-59fc-bfd8-be58eb2b07d6', 'word_count': 650, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11b4111d-ea24-59fc-bfd8-be58eb2b07d6'}, {'abstract': 'A father who doesn’t think the Boy Scouts’ proposed changes on accepting gays goes far enough asks if he should let his son join a troop.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/01/31/booming/should-i-let-my-son-join-the-boy-scouts.html', 'snippet': 'A father who doesn’t think the Boy Scouts’ proposed changes on accepting gays goes far enough asks if he should let his son join a troop.', 'lead_paragraph': " Steven Petrow, the author of “Steven Petrow’s Complete Gay & Lesbian Manners,” (Workman, 2011), addresses questions about gay and straight etiquette for a boomer-age audience.  [This week's question arose from a conversation with an acquaintance about the news on Monday that the Boy Scouts may eliminate its national ban on gays.] [UPDATE: On Feb. 6 the Scouts announced they are postponing the decision till May.] Send questions for Civil Behavior to stevenpetrow@earthlink.net.", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/31/booming/31civil-booming-scouts/31civil-booming-scouts-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 358, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/31/booming/31civil-booming-scouts/31civil-booming-scouts-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 358}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/31/booming/31civil-booming-scouts/31civil-booming-scouts-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 611, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/31/booming/31civil-booming-scouts/31civil-booming-scouts-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1221, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/31/booming/31civil-booming-scouts/31civil-booming-scouts-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/31/booming/31civil-booming-scouts/31civil-booming-scouts-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/31/booming/31civil-booming-scouts/31civil-booming-scouts-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Should I Let My Son Join the Boy Scouts if the Gay Ban Changes?', 'kicker': 'Civil Behavior', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'o