thing to do.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/02/03/fashion/a-question-of-sexuality.html', 'snippet': 'Is a new friend gay? Better not ask. When interviewing a job candidate, play by the rules. Backing out of a wedding party may be the right thing to do.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Is there any way to ask a potential boyfriend whether he’s gay? I am a woman and have just started seeing a guy my friends think is gay. He belongs to a religious community in which people his age are usually married, so something is up. I can’t yet say he’s not into women. But part of me worries that if I don’t clear this up explicitly, I will always feel insecure about his affection.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 599}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Zip Your Lip', 'kicker': 'Social Q’s', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Zip Your Lip', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Careers and Professions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs, Etiquette and Manners', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-31T21:09:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Philip Galanes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Philip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Galanes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5ad3cb7-cedc-5af0-a1c0-e3a0903a05b0', 'word_count': 783, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5ad3cb7-cedc-5af0-a1c0-e3a0903a05b0'}, {'abstract': 'Andrew Cuomo’s approval rating has dropped since he announced his gun control plan. But he doesn’t seem to mind.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/31/guns-and-approval-ratings/', 'snippet': 'Andrew Cuomo’s approval rating has dropped since he announced his gun control plan. But he doesn’t seem to mind.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the first rules of politics is that you’re supposed to pretend you don’t govern according to opinion polls — that you put the good of the country ahead of reelection. In D.C. they sometimes forget to even pay lip service to this idea. Compromise always comes before courage; legislators focus on what’s possible as an excuse not to try something bold.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Guns and Approval Ratings', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reid, Harry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-31T21:10:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1b48423-475e-5dd3-8350-1fb3c4c7fffb', 'word_count': 478, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1b48423-475e-5dd3-8350-1fb3c4c7fffb'}, {'abstract': 'Most of the men in Jess Walter’s short-story collection “We Live in Water” have a litany of demotions and setbacks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/02/01/books/we-live-in-water-by-jess-walter.html', 'snippet': 'Most of the men in Jess Walter’s short-story collection “We Live in Water” have a litany of demotions and setbacks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In thanking the agent responsible for his new short-story collection, “We Live in Water,” Jess Walter gives a shout-out to “the literary social worker who found homes for these troubled kids.” Not every writer thinks of his stories as troubled offspring, but in Mr. Walter’s case it’s a fair description. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/31/arts/01JPBOOK/01JPBOOK-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 837, 'width': 600,