'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Koch in Intensive Care', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Koch Is Moved to Intensive Care', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koch, Edward I', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-31T21:29:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6e02041-e7c6-523c-8749-d5792ba4e34a', 'word_count': 142, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6e02041-e7c6-523c-8749-d5792ba4e34a'}, {'abstract': '“The Last Gladiators,” a documentary by Alex Gibney about Chris Nilan and the life of a hockey enforcer, will open in New York on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/31/fighting-was-easy-hockey-was-the-hard-part/', 'snippet': '“The Last Gladiators,” a documentary by Alex Gibney about Chris Nilan and the life of a hockey enforcer, will open in New York on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chris Nilan, the well-known former N.H.L. enforcer, has battled substance abuse since his retirement in 1992 and was once arrested for shoplifting. But he does not blame his troubles on 13 years of fighting in professional hockey — quite the contrary.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fighting Was Easy. Hockey Was the Hard Part.', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gibney, Alex', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nilan, Chris', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-31T21:33:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c80c89d4-f0a3-56da-bd24-f1ffbc674a69', 'word_count': 875, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c80c89d4-f0a3-56da-bd24-f1ffbc674a69'}, {'abstract': 'The Broadway producers of “Truman Capote’s ‘Breakfast at Tiffany’s’” have sorted out money problems that had the potential to derail the show’s planned opening in March, a spokesman for the show said.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/31/after-reshuffling-funds-breakfast-at-tiffanys-producers-plan-to-proceed/', 'snippet': 'The Broadway producers of “Truman Capote’s ‘Breakfast at Tiffany’s’” have sorted out money problems that had the potential to derail the show’s planned opening in March, a spokesman for the show said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Broadway producers of “Truman Capote’s ‘Breakfast at Tiffany’s’” have sorted out money problems that had the potential to derail the planned opening in March, a spokesman for the show said on Thursday. One of the “Tiffany’s” investors, who had been responsible for about $1 million of the show’s $4 million budget, had told his partners that he was bowing out, and the show’s cast and creative team was notified on Sunday that the producers needed to replace the money quickly or the play might be canceled. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Reshuffling Funds, ‘Breakfast at Tiffany’s’ Producers Plan to Proceed', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Breakfast at Tiffany’s’  Finds Needed Cash', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-31T21:35:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb2626e9-e02b-5dfe-9f7f-306d583d5ece', 'word_count': 205, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb2626e9-e02b-5dfe-9f7f-306d583d5ece'}, {'abstract': '“I never said it,” Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg said about an ungentlemanly quotation attributed to him in a magazine’s profile of Speaker Christine C. Quinn.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/02/01/nyregion/bloomberg-denies-commenting-on-womans-derriere.html', 'snippet': '“I never said it,” Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg said about an ungentlemanly quotation attributed to him in a magazine’s profile of Speaker Christine C. Quinn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Monday, he did not meet with reporters after testifying before the Legislature in Albany. On Tuesday, he refused to take questions on anything but his budget proposal at City Hall. On Wednesday, he did not appear in public. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mayor Denies Commenting on Woman’s Derrière', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mayor Says He Uttered No Remark On a Derrière', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York (Magazine)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quinn, Christine C', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-31T21:39:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ed7a698-fc2e-5baf-904f-327b7dd07edd', 'word_count': 491, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ed7a698-fc2e-5baf-904f-327b7dd07edd'}, {'abstract': 'A naming app that gives you the most common professions and political parties associated with thousands of names, along with when and where they were most popular.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/31/an-app-to-help-you-choose-a-name-or-spend-hours-analyzing-the-possibilities/', 'snippet': 'A naming app that gives you the most common professions and political parties associated with thousands of names, along with when and where they were most popular.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I am all finished having babies — but if I did have another baby, it might just be so I could have the fun of naming it. I love names (what writer doesn’t?). I loved naming my children (even though, in retrospect, one of those names was more popular than I had hoped). I like reading about names. And if I had had this app when I was pregnant, I’d have been sunk. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An App to Help You Choose a Name (or Spend Hours Analyzing the Possibilities)', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Names, Personal', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-31T21:39:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': ''