', 'web_url': 'https://bittman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/31/links-if-youre-so-inclined/', 'snippet': 'Your reading roundup for the week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If new state “Ag-Gag” laws pass, reporting factory farm abuses would be deemed an “Act of Terrorism.” (More on whistleblower suppression efforts here and here.) Maryn McKenna writes that one of the potential consequences of animal production being hidden from view is the proliferation of multi-drug resistant bacteria in chicken due to the overuse of antibiotics. (One of the great takeaways from this piece: “If you grew as fast as a chicken, you’d weigh 349 pounds at age two.”)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Links, If You’re So Inclined', 'kicker': 'Mark Bittman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Clean Water Act', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factory Farming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shale', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soft Drinks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bell, Kristen', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Emanuel, Rahm', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nestle, Marion', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quinn, Christine C', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Coca-Cola Company', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Des Moines Register', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hispanic Federation', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Aeronautics and Space Administration', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Assn for the Advancement of Colored People', 'rank': 18, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Pork Producers Council', 'rank': 19, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 20, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 21, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East River (NYC)', 'rank': 22, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 23, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maine', 'rank': 24, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mississippi', 'rank': 25, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Dakota', 'rank': 26, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 27, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-31T21:39:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8318e40-2e53-5bc1-8628-e8e6b8c1c1d6', 'word_count': 877, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8318e40-2e53-5bc1-8628-e8e6b8c1c1d6'}, {'abstract': 'The novels “Sandalwood Death” and “Pow!,” by Nobel Prize winner Mo Yan, combine literary imagination with a peasant spirit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/02/03/books/review/sandalwood-death-and-pow-by-mo-yan.html', 'snippet': 'The novels “Sandalwood Death” and “Pow!,” by Nobel Prize winner Mo Yan, combine literary imagination with a peasant spirit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mo Yan, winner of the 2012 Nobel Prize in Literature, has a deft way with similes: salty, sometimes gross, usually unexpected. Comparing women’s breasts to “ripe mangoes” is almost a cliché, but to describe the nipples as “rising gracefully, like the captivating mouths of hedgehogs” is arresting. Passengers disembarking from a train do so “like beetles rolling their precious dung.” A rich meal of pork lies on a man’s stomach, “churning and grinding like a litter of soon-to-be-born piglets.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/02/03/books/review/0203-Buruma/0203-Buruma-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/02/03/books/review/0203-Buruma/0203-Buruma-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 923}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/02/03/books/review/0203-Buruma/0203-Buruma-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 666, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/02/03/books/review/0203-Buruma/0203-Buruma-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1332, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/02/03/books/review/0203-Buruma/0203-Buruma-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/02/03/books/review/0203-Buruma/0203-Buruma-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/02/03/books/review/0203-Buruma/0203-Buruma-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Folk Opera', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Folk Opera', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mo Yan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-31T21:41:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Buruma', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buruma', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/63fc651b-2e7f-535e-a10b-83f2e6948004', 'word_count': 1608, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63fc651b-2e7f-535e-a10b-83f2e6948004'}, {'abstract': 'As the government calls a program to buy mortgage-backed securities a success, a court case is a reminder of how much information is still not publicly available about that market.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/02/01/business/court-case-offers-a-peek-into-mortgage-security-pricing.html', 'snippet': 'As the government calls a program to buy mortgage-backed securities a success, a court case is a reminder of how much information is still not publicly available about that market.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The private mortgage-backed securities market grew to be a virtually inscrutable giant. Each securitization contained thousands of mortgages and as many as dozens of different securities, some of which could emerge unscathed even if others produced total losses for investors.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/19/business/norris-75-standardinline/norris-75-standardinline-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/04/19/business/norris-75-standardinline/norris-75-standardinline-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Case Offers Peek Behind the Curtain of a Security', 'kicker': 'High & Low Finance', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Case Offers Peek Behind The Curtain Of a Security', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgage-Backed Securities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Financial Industry Regulatory Authority', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Litvak, Jesse C', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Treasury Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-31T21:41:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Floyd Norris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Norris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3775600b-f316-5d15-9f9e-4517d7bee62a', 'word_count': 1450, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3775600b-f316-5d15-9f9e-4517d7bee62a'}, {'abstract': 'The nineties are back: DKNY is re-releasing its iconic logo tees, bodysuits and outerwear with the cool kids cult shop.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/31/now-collaborating-dkny-for-opening-ceremony/', 'snippet': 'The nineties are back: DKNY is re-releasing its iconic logo tees, bodysuits and outerwear with the cool kids cult shop.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The sportswear label DKNY has teamed up with the cool kids cult shop Opening Ceremony to reissue select styles from the 1990s. Available tomorrow, the 15-piece collection starts at $145 and includes logo tees, bodysuits and outerwear rife with street-style nostalgia. The standout of the lot is a cropped puffer jacket with an oversize logo, which was first released in 1991. However, don’t expect to pay the same price from two decades ago. As if.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Now Collaborating | DKNY for Opening Ceremony', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Opening Ceremony (Retail Store)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-31T21:43:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/80627062-1832-52fa-b8b6-994953c5d3c3', 'word_count': 82, 'uri': 'nyt://article/80627062-1832-52fa-b8b6-994953c5d3c3'}, {'abstract': 'The base salary for the Morgan Stanley chief executive almost doubled in 2012, but his overall pay package is down, according to a filing on Thursday with the Securities and Exchange Commission.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/01/31/gorman-gets-a-big-bump-in-base-salary/', 'snippet': 'The base salary for the Morgan Stanley chief executive almost doubled in 2012, but his overall pay package is down, according to a filing on Thursday with the Securities and Exchange Commission.', 'lead_paragraph': 'James P. Gorman, the chief executive of Morgan Stanley, will receive a huge raise in his base salary this year, but his overall pay package for 2012 was down from 2011, according to a filing Thursday with the Securities and Exchange Commission.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morgan Stanley’s Chief Gets a Base Salary Raise', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Morgan Stanley’s Chief Gets a Base Salary Raise', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bonuses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Compensation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fleming, Gregory J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gorman, James P', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Morgan Stanley', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-31T21:46:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susanne Craig', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Craig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b203109-17f6-541a-8c9d-4e8228be625c', 'word_count': 446, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b203109-17f6-541a-8c9d-4e8228be625c'}, {'abstract': 'In Zarina’s “Paper Like Skin” exhibition at the Guggenheim, paper is sculpture, poetry, currency and, above all, a kind of permanent home for a nomadic spirit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/02/01/arts/design/zarina-paper-like-skin-at-the-guggenheim-museum.html', 'snippet': 'In Zarina’s “Paper Like Skin” exhibition at the Guggenheim, paper is sculpture, poetry, currency and, above all, a kind of permanent home for a nomadic spirit.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Paper is an organic material, almost like human skin,” the artist Zarina Hashmi has said. “You can scratch it, you can mold it. It even ages.” In “Zarina: Paper Like Skin,” Ms. Hashmi’s exhibition at the Guggenheim, it’s that and more: paper is sculpture, poetry, currency and, above all, a kind of permanent home for a nomadic spirit.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/02/01/arts/01SUBJPZARINA1_SPAN/01SUBJPZARINA1_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/02/01/arts/01SUBJPZARINA1_SPAN/01SUBJPZARINA1_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/02/01/arts/01SUBJPZARINA1_SPAN/01SUBJPZARINA1_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/02/01/arts/01SUBJPZARINA1_SPAN/01SUBJPZARINA1_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/02/01/arts/01SUBJPZARINA1_SPAN/01SUBJPZARINA1_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/02/01/arts/01SUBJPZARINA1_SPAN/01SUBJPZARINA1_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/02/01/arts/01SUBJPZARINA1_SPAN/01SUBJPZARINA1_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Reveling in the Multicultural Possibilities