, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Today’s Scuttlebot: Google’s Grand Canyon and Crowdfunded Space Programs', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-01-31T22:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/279c6fa7-e229-57dd-bd20-521caedf597c', 'word_count': 154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/279c6fa7-e229-57dd-bd20-521caedf597c'}, {'abstract': 'The piece will be Mr. Taylor’s 139th work. Other artists are also scheduled to perform.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/31/new-paul-taylor-work-to-premiere-at-vail-international-dance-festival/', 'snippet': 'The piece will be Mr. Taylor’s 139th work. Other artists are also scheduled to perform.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The latest new work by Paul Taylor, 82, the modern dance choreographer, will see the light of day in Colorado. The Vail International Dance Festival said on Thursday that Mr. Taylor’s 139th work – so far unnamed and performed by the Paul Taylor Dance Company — will have its premiere on Aug. 5 at the festival, which runs from July 28 through Aug. 10 in Vail and Beaver Creek, Colo. Larry Keigwin, Brian Brooks and Charles Riley are other choreographers who will have new pieces on the program, the festival said. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Paul Taylor Work to Premiere at Vail International Dance Festival', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Vail International Dance Festival  To Offer a New Paul Taylor Work', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vail International Dance Festival', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taylor, Paul', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pacific Northwest Ballet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taylor, Paul, Dance Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-31T22:00:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd4841a9-0e29-5b05-b6d0-48ddaab87e39', 'word_count': 156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd4841a9-0e29-5b05-b6d0-48ddaab87e39'}, {'abstract': 'Nature Theater of Oklahoma’s “Life and Times” reminds one critic that verbatim conversation on stage can offer its own distinctive pleasures.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/01/31/theater-talkback-the-rough-beauty-of-everyday-speech/', 'snippet': 'Nature Theater of Oklahoma’s “Life and Times” reminds one critic that verbatim conversation on stage can offer its own distinctive pleasures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Generally speaking, we don’t go to the theater to listen to conversations that we might just as easily hear while waiting in line at the grocery store or commuting on the subway. Among the essential gifts most great playwrights possess is an ability to take the dross of humble human speech and give it a silvering polish.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/31/theater/31life/31life-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/31/theater/31life/31life-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/31/theater/31life/31life-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/31/theater/31life/31life-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1255, 'width': 1882, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/31/theater/31life/31life-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/31/theater/31life/31life-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/31/theater/31life/31life-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Theater Talkback: The Rough Beauty of Everyday Speech', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baker, Annie', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Copper, Kelly', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Herzog, Amy', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Liska, Pavol', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Civilians, The (Theater Co)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nature Theater of Oklahoma', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-31T22:05:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Isherwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isherwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c9f1b43-af90-5e91-86b3-3e9057c6c540', 'word_count': 1011, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c9f1b43-af90-5e91-86b3-3e9057c6c540'}, {'abstract': 'In his new book, “Inventing Wine,” Paul Lukacs makes the point that the idea of “tradition” in wine has been thoroughly mutable.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/02/06/dining/the-history-of-wine-drinking-from-a-chore-to-a-choice.html', 'snippet': 'In his new book, “Inventing Wine,” Paul Lukacs makes the point that the idea of “tradition” in wine has been thoroughly mutable.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wine is old, ancient, neolithic. It has been consumed throughout recorded history. Yet wine as we know it today is relatively new. Where it originated, what it tasted like and represented, and how it was transformed over time are explored in Paul Lukacs’s fascinating new book, “Inventing Wine: A New History of One of the World’s Most Ancient Pleasures,” published in December by W. W. Norton & Company.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/02/06/dining/06POUR_SPAN/06POUR_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'h