: 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c26ac83b-a701-5c24-aae8-c259473aa7f4', 'word_count': 422, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c26ac83b-a701-5c24-aae8-c259473aa7f4'}, {'abstract': 'The Federal Reserve has proposed rules aimed at making sure that the American operations of foreign banks have the financial strength to absorb losses. Deutsche Bank executives, however, apparently feel the rules are unnecessarily restrictive.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/01/31/deutsche-banks-lonely-fight-with-the-fed/', 'snippet': 'The Federal Reserve has proposed rules aimed at making sure that the American operations of foreign banks have the financial strength to absorb losses. Deutsche Bank executives, however, apparently feel the rules are unnecessarily restrictive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was supposed to be an uneventful conference call for senior executives at Deutsche Bank, one of Europe’s largest lenders. But a nerve was clearly struck as the executives took questions from analysts on Thursday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Deutsche Bank’s Lonely Fight With the Fed', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deutsche Bank AG', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-01-31T22:40:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Eavis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eavis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/05f26a26-2633-54bc-92e4-b23e5daf0ba6', 'word_count': 948, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05f26a26-2633-54bc-92e4-b23e5daf0ba6'}, {'abstract': 'Walter Hill’s action film “Bullet to the Head” stars Sylvester Stallone as a contract killer in New Orleans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/02/01/movies/bullet-to-the-head-stars-sylvester-stallone.html', 'snippet': 'Walter Hill’s action film “Bullet to the Head” stars Sylvester Stallone as a contract killer in New Orleans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The multiple bullets that pierce multiple brains in “Bullet to the Head” — boring holes into people as disposable as paper gun targets — suggest that the title refers to an ideal rather than being merely descriptive. It implies, in other words, an appreciation and awareness of the principles of contemporary action cinema, and perhaps even a sense of play in respect to the genre. And while the veteran action director Walter Hill hasn’t done much to enliven this dull, unmemorable material, with its mechanically moving parts and popping gunfire, its dull-red splatter and spray, he has brought a spark of wit to the proceedings, starting with the figure of Sylvester Stallone. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/02/01/arts/01BULLET_SPAN/BULLET-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/02/01/arts/01BULLET_SPAN/BULLET-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/02/01/arts/01BULLET_SPAN/BULLET-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype':