noa-eshkol-at-the-jewish-museum.html', 'snippet': '“Sharon Lockhart/Noa Eshkol,” at the Jewish Museum, introduces viewers to a “forgotten” artist, the Israeli choreographer Noa Eshkol, while creating a new body of artwork.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Museums have changed significantly over the last several decades, so that they showcase more contemporary art but also try to balance their budgets by bringing in larger audiences. This sets up a challenge for artists. who must operate on multiple registers, speaking to aficionados as well as to the uninitiated. Sharon Lockhart’s show at the Jewish Museum does this beautifully.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/02/01/arts/01LOCKHART_SPAN/LOCKHART-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 348, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/02/01/arts/01LOCKHART_SPAN/LOCKHART-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 348}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/02/01/arts/01LOCKHART_SPAN/LOCKHART-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 594, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/02/01/arts/01LOCKHART_SPAN/LOCKHART-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1189, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/02/01/arts/01LOCKHART_SPAN/LOCKHART-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/02/01/arts/01LOCKHART_SPAN/LOCKHART-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 